#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:347
msgid "BUILDING FROM GIT"
msgstr "BŪVĒŠANA NO GIT"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:349
msgid ""
"You will need to install additional dependencies C<autoconf>, C<automake>, "
"C<gettext>, OCaml findlib and po4a when building from git."
msgstr ""
"Būvējot no git, būs jāinstalē papildu atkarības C<autoconf>, C<automake>, "
"C<gettext>, OCaml findlib un po4a."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:353
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" git clone https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs\n"
" cd libguestfs\n"
" git submodule update --init\n"
" autoreconf -i\n"
" ./configure\n"
" make\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" git clone https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs\n"
" cd libguestfs\n"
" git submodule update --init\n"
" autoreconf -i\n"
" ./configure\n"
" make\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:360
msgid "BUILDING FROM TARBALLS"
msgstr "BŪVĒŠANA NO TAR ARHĪVIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:362
msgid ""
"Tarballs are downloaded from L<http://download.libguestfs.org/>.  Stable "
"tarballs are signed with the GnuPG key for C<rich@annexia.org>, see "
"L<https://pgp.mit.edu/pks/lookup?op=vindex&search=0x91738F73E1B768A0>.  The "
"fingerprint is C<F777 4FB1 AD07 4A7E 8C87 67EA 9173 8F73 E1B7 68A0>."
msgstr ""
"Tar arhīvi tiek lejupielādēti no L<http://download.libguestfs.org/>.  "
"Stabilie tar arhīvi ir parakstīti ar GnuPG atslēgu C<rich@annexia.org>, "
"skatiet L<https://pgp.mit.edu/pks/lookup?op=vindex&search=0x91738F73E1B768A0>"
".  Nospiedums ir C<F777 4FB1 AD07 4A7E 8C87 67EA 9173 8F73 E1B7 68A0>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:368
msgid "Download and unpack the tarball."
msgstr "Lejupielādējiet un izpakojiet tar arhīvu."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:370
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" cd libguestfs-1.xx.yy\n"
" ./configure\n"
" make\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" cd libguestfs-1.xx.yy\n"
" ./configure\n"
" make\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:374
msgid "RUNNING THE TESTS"
msgstr "TESTU IZPILDE"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:376
msgid ""
"B<DO NOT run the tests as root!> Libguestfs can be built and tested as "
"non-root.  Running the tests as root could even be dangerous, don't do it."
msgstr ""
"B<NEIZPILDIET testus kā root!> Libguestfs var uzbūvēt un testēt kā "
"lietotājs, kas nav root.  Testu izpilde kā root var būt pat bīstama, "
"nedariet to."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:380
msgid "To sanity check that the build worked, do:"
msgstr "Lai pārbaudītu, vai būvēšana izdevās, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:382
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" make quickcheck\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" make quickcheck\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:384
msgid "To run the basic tests, do:"
msgstr "Lai izpildītu pamata testus, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:386
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" make check\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" make check\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:388
msgid ""
"There are many more tests you can run.  See L<guestfs-hacking(1)> for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Ir daudz vairāk testu, ko var izpildīt.  Sīkāk skatiet L<guestfs-hacking(1)>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:391
msgid "INSTALLING"
msgstr "INSTALĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:393
msgid ""
"B<DO NOT use C<make install>!> You'll end up with conflicting versions of "
"libguestfs installed, and this causes constant headaches for users.  See the "
"next section for how to use the F<./run> script instead."
msgstr ""
"B<NEIZMANTOJIET C<make install>!> Rezultātā būs instalētas konfliktējošas "
"libguestfs versijas, un tas lietotājiem rada pastāvīgas galvassāpes.  Kā tā "
"vietā izmantot skriptu F<./run>, skatiet nākamo sadaļu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:397
msgid "Distro packagers can use:"
msgstr "Distribūciju pakotāji var izmantot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:399
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" make INSTALLDIRS=vendor DESTDIR=[temp-build-dir] install\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" make INSTALLDIRS=vendor DESTDIR=[temp-build-dir] install\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:401
msgid "THE ./run SCRIPT"
msgstr "SKRIPTS ./run"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:403
msgid ""
"You can run L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestmount(1)> and the virt tools without "
"needing to install them by using the F<./run> script in the top directory.  "
"This script works by setting several environment variables."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestmount(1)> un virt rīkus var izpildīt bez "
"instalēšanas, izmantojot augšējās direktorijas skriptu F<./run>.  Šis "
"skripts darbojas, iestatot vairākus vides mainīgos."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:410
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./run guestfish [usual guestfish args ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./run guestfish [usual guestfish args ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:412
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./run virt-inspector [usual virt-inspector args ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./run virt-inspector [usual virt-inspector args ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:414
msgid ""
"The F<./run> script adds every libguestfs binary to the C<$PATH>, so the "
"above examples run guestfish and virt-inspector from the build directory "
"(not the globally installed guestfish if there is one)."
msgstr ""
"Skripts F<./run> pievieno katru libguestfs bināro failu mainīgajam C<$PATH>, "
"tāpēc iepriekšējie piemēri izpilda guestfish un virt-inspector no būvēšanas "
"direktorijas (nevis globāli instalēto guestfish, ja tāds ir)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:418
msgid ""
"You can use the script from any directory.  If you wanted to run your own "
"libguestfs-using program, then the following command will also work:"
msgstr ""
"Skriptu var izmantot no jebkuras direktorijas.  Ja vēlaties izpildīt savu "
"programmu, kas izmanto libguestfs, darbosies arī šī komanda:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:422
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /path/to/libguestfs/run ./my_program [...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /path/to/libguestfs/run ./my_program [...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:424
msgid "You can also run the C programs under valgrind like this:"
msgstr "C programmas var izpildīt arī ar valgrind, šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:426
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./run valgrind [valgrind opts...] virt-cat [virt-cat opts...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./run valgrind [valgrind opts...] virt-cat [virt-cat opts...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:428
msgid "or under gdb:"
msgstr "vai ar gdb:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:430
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./run gdb --args virt-cat [virt-cat opts...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./run gdb --args virt-cat [virt-cat opts...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:432
msgid ""
"This also works with sudo (eg. if you need root access for libvirt or to "
"access a block device):"
msgstr ""
"Tas darbojas arī ar sudo (piem., ja libvirt vai piekļuvei bloku ierīcei "
"vajadzīga root piekļuve):"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:435
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sudo ./run virt-cat -d LinuxGuest /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sudo ./run virt-cat -d LinuxGuest /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:437
msgid "To set environment variables, you can either do:"
msgstr "Lai iestatītu vides mainīgos, varat vai nu izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:439
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" LIBGUESTFS_HV=/my/qemu ./run guestfish\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" LIBGUESTFS_HV=/my/qemu ./run guestfish\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:441 docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:491
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:76 docs/guestfs-testing.pod:138
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:245 docs/guestfs-testing.pod:258
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:322 fish/guestfish.pod:863 fish/guestfish.pod:1057
#: lua/examples/guestfs-lua.pod:64
msgid "or:"
msgstr "or:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:443
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./run env LIBGUESTFS_HV=/my/qemu guestfish\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./run env LIBGUESTFS_HV=/my/qemu guestfish\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:445
msgid "F<local*> FILES"
msgstr "F<local*> FAILI"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:447
msgid ""
"Files in the top source directory that begin with the prefix F<local*> are "
"ignored by git.  These files can contain local configuration or scripts that "
"you need to build libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Faili pirmkoda augšējā direktorijā, kas sākas ar priedēkli F<local*>, git "
"ignorē.  Šie faili var saturēt lokālu konfigurāciju vai skriptus, kas jums "
"vajadzīgi libguestfs būvēšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:451
msgid ""
"I have a file called F<localconfigure> which is a simple wrapper around "
"F<configure> containing local configure customizations that I need.  It "
"looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Man ir fails F<localconfigure>, kas ir vienkāršs ietinējs ap F<configure> ar "
"man vajadzīgajiem lokālajiem configure pielāgojumiem.  Tas izskatās šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:455
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" . localenv\n"
" ./configure.sh \\\n"
"     -C \\\n"
"     --enable-werror \\\n"
"     \"$@\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" . localenv\n"
" ./configure.sh \\\n"
"     -C \\\n"
"     --enable-werror \\\n"
"     \"$@\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:461
msgid "So I can use this to build libguestfs:"
msgstr "Tātad libguestfs būvēšanai varu izmantot šo:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:463
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./localconfigure && make\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./localconfigure && make\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:465
msgid ""
"If there is a file in the top build directory called F<localenv>, then it "
"will be sourced by C<make>.  This file can contain any local environment "
"variables needed, eg. for skipping tests:"
msgstr ""
"Ja augšējā būvēšanas direktorijā ir fails F<localenv>, C<make> to izpildīs "
"(source).  Šajā failā var būt jebkuri vajadzīgie lokālie vides mainīgie, "
"piem., testu izlaišanai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:469
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Skip this test, it is broken.\n"
" export SKIP_TEST_BTRFS_FSCK=1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # Skip this test, it is broken.\n"
" export SKIP_TEST_BTRFS_FSCK=1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:472
msgid ""
"Note that F<localenv> is included by the top Makefile (so it’s a Makefile "
"fragment).  But if it is also sourced by your F<localconfigure> script then "
"it is used as a shell script."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka F<localenv> iekļauj augšējais Makefile (tātad tas ir "
"Makefile fragments).  Taču, ja to izpilda (source) arī jūsu skripts "
"F<localconfigure>, tas tiek izmantots kā čaulas skripts."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:476
msgid "SELECTED ./configure SETTINGS"
msgstr "IZVĒLĒTI ./configure IESTATĪJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:478
msgid "There are many C<./configure> options.  Use:"
msgstr "Ir daudz C<./configure> opciju.  Izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:480
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./configure --help\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./configure --help\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:482
msgid "to list them all.  This section covers some of the more important ones."
msgstr "lai tās visas uzskaitītu.  Šī sadaļa aptver dažas svarīgākās."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:487
msgid "B<--disable-appliance --disable-daemon>"
msgstr "B<--disable-appliance --disable-daemon>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:489
msgid "See L</USING A PREBUILT BINARY APPLIANCE> below."
msgstr "Skatiet L</IEPRIEKŠ UZBŪVĒTAS BINĀRĀS PALĪGSISTĒMAS IZMANTOŠANA> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:491
msgid "B<--disable-erlang>"
msgstr "B<--disable-erlang>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:493
msgid "B<--disable-golang>"
msgstr "B<--disable-golang>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:495
msgid "B<--disable-haskell>"
msgstr "B<--disable-haskell>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:497
msgid "B<--disable-lua>"
msgstr "B<--disable-lua>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:499
msgid "B<--disable-ocaml>"
msgstr "B<--disable-ocaml>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:501
msgid "B<--disable-perl>"
msgstr "B<--disable-perl>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:503
msgid "B<--disable-php>"
msgstr "B<--disable-php>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:505
msgid "B<--disable-python>"
msgstr "B<--disable-python>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:507
msgid "B<--disable-ruby>"
msgstr "B<--disable-ruby>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:509
msgid ""
"Disable specific language bindings, even if C<./configure> finds all the "
"necessary libraries are installed so that they could be compiled."
msgstr ""
"Atspējot konkrētus valodu saistījumus, pat ja C<./configure> konstatē, ka "
"visas vajadzīgās bibliotēkas ir instalētas, lai tos varētu kompilēt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:512
msgid ""
"Note that disabling OCaml (bindings) or Perl will have the knock-on effect "
"of disabling parts of the test suite and some tools."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka OCaml (saistījumu) vai Perl atspējošanai ir blakusefekts — "
"tiek atspējotas testu komplekta daļas un daži rīki."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:515
msgid ""
"OCaml is required to build libguestfs and this requirement cannot be "
"removed.  Using I<--disable-ocaml> only disables the bindings."
msgstr ""
"OCaml ir nepieciešams libguestfs būvēšanai, un šo prasību nevar noņemt.  I<--"
"disable-ocaml> atspējo tikai saistījumus."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:518
msgid "B<--disable-fuse>"
msgstr "B<--disable-fuse>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:520
msgid "Disable FUSE support in the API and the L<guestmount(1)> tool."
msgstr "Atspējot FUSE atbalstu API un rīkā L<guestmount(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:522
msgid "B<--disable-static>"
msgstr "B<--disable-static>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:524
msgid "Don’t build a static linked version of the libguestfs library."
msgstr "Neveidot statiski saistītu libguestfs bibliotēkas versiju."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:526
msgid "B<--enable-install-daemon>"
msgstr "B<--enable-install-daemon>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:528
msgid ""
"Normally L<guestfsd(8)> is not installed by C<make install>, since that "
"wouldn't be useful (instead it is \"installed\" inside the supermin "
"appliance).  However if packagers are building \"libguestfs live\" then they "
"should use this option."
msgstr ""
"Parasti C<make install> neinstalē L<guestfsd(8)>, jo tas nebūtu noderīgi (tā "
"vietā tas tiek „instalēts” supermin palīgsistēmā).  Tomēr, ja pakotāji būvē „"
"libguestfs live”, viņiem jāizmanto šī opcija."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:533
msgid "B<--enable-werror>"
msgstr "B<--enable-werror>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:535
msgid ""
"This turns compiler warnings into errors (ie. C<-Werror>).  Use this for "
"development, especially when submitting patches.  It should generally I<not> "
"be used for production or distro builds."
msgstr ""
"Tas pārvērš kompilatora brīdinājumus kļūdās (t. i., C<-Werror>).  "
"Izmantojiet to izstrādei, it īpaši, iesniedzot ielāpus.  Ražošanas vai "
"distribūciju būvēm to parasti I<nevajadzētu> izmantot."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:539
msgid "B<--with-default-backend=libvirt>"
msgstr "B<--with-default-backend=libvirt>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:541
msgid ""
"This controls the default method that libguestfs uses to run qemu (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/BACKEND>).  If not specified, the default backend is C<direct>, "
"which means libguestfs runs qemu directly."
msgstr ""
"Tas nosaka noklusējuma metodi, ko libguestfs izmanto qemu izpildei (skatiet "
"L<guestfs(3)/AIZMUGURSISTĒMA>).  Ja nav norādīta, noklusējuma "
"aizmugursistēma ir C<direct>, kas nozīmē, ka libguestfs izpilda qemu tieši."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:545
msgid ""
"Fedora and Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) E<ge> 7 use this flag to change "
"the default backend to C<libvirt>, because (especially in RHEL)  the policy "
"is not to allow any program to run qemu except via libvirt."
msgstr ""
"Fedora un Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) E<ge> 7 izmanto šo karogu, lai "
"mainītu noklusējuma aizmugursistēmu uz C<libvirt>, jo (it īpaši RHEL) "
"politika ir neļaut nevienai programmai izpildīt qemu citādi kā caur libvirt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:549
msgid ""
"Note that despite this setting, all backends are built into libguestfs, and "
"you can override the backend at runtime by setting the "
"C<$LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND> environment variable (or using API methods)."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka neatkarīgi no šī iestatījuma visas aizmugursistēmas ir "
"iebūvētas libguestfs, un aizmugursistēmu izpildlaikā var pārdefinēt, "
"iestatot vides mainīgo C<$LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND> (vai izmantojot API metodes)."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:553
msgid "B<--with-distro=REDHAT|DEBIAN|...>"
msgstr "B<--with-distro=REDHAT|DEBIAN|...>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:555
msgid ""
"Libguestfs needs to know which Linux distro is in use so it can choose "
"package names for the appliance correctly (see for example "
"F<appliance/packagelist.in>).  It normally does this automatically."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs jāzina, kura Linux distribūcija tiek izmantota, lai tas varētu "
"pareizi izvēlēties palīgsistēmas pakotņu nosaukumus (skatiet, piemēram, "
"F<appliance/packagelist.in>).  Parasti tas to dara automātiski."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:559
msgid ""
"However if you can building or packaging libguestfs on a new distro then you "
"can use I<--with-distro> to specify that the distro is similar to an "
"existing one (eg. I<--with-distro=REDHAT> if the distro is a new Red Hat or "
"CentOS derivative)."
msgstr ""
"Tomēr, ja būvējat vai iepakojat libguestfs jaunā distribūcijā, varat "
"izmantot I<--with-distro>, lai norādītu, ka distribūcija ir līdzīga esošai "
"(piem., I<--with-distro=REDHAT>, ja distribūcija ir jauns Red Hat vai CentOS "
"atvasinājums)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:564
msgid ""
"Note that if your distro is completely new then it may still require "
"upstream modifications."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā: ja jūsu distribūcija ir pilnīgi jauna, tai joprojām var būt "
"vajadzīgas izmaiņas augštecē."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:567
msgid "B<--with-extra=\">I<distroname>=I<version>,libvirt,...B<\">"
msgstr "B<--with-extra=\">I<distroname>=I<version>,libvirt,...B<\">"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:569
msgid "B<--with-extra=\"local\">"
msgstr "B<--with-extra=\"local\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:571
msgid ""
"This option controls the \"extra\" field returned by "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_version> and also printed by virt tools' I<--version> "
"option.  It is a free text field, but a good idea is to encode a "
"comma-separated list of facts such as the distro name and version, whether "
"libvirt is the default backend, and anything else that may help with "
"debugging problems raised by users."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija nosaka „extra” lauku, ko atgriež L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_version> un "
"drukā arī virt rīku opcija I<--version>.  Tas ir brīva teksta lauks, taču "
"ieteicams tajā iekodēt ar komatiem atdalītu faktu sarakstu, piemēram, "
"distribūcijas nosaukumu un versiju, vai libvirt ir noklusējuma "
"aizmugursistēma, un jebko citu, kas var palīdzēt atkļūdot lietotāju ziņotās "
"problēmas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:578
msgid ""
"For custom and/or local builds, this can be set to C<local> to indicate this "
"is I<not> a distro build."
msgstr ""
"Pielāgotām un/vai lokālām būvēm to var iestatīt uz C<local>, lai norādītu, "
"ka tā I<nav> distribūcijas būve."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:581
msgid "B<--without-libvirt>"
msgstr "B<--without-libvirt>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:583
msgid ""
"Compile libguestfs without libvirt support, even if libvirt development "
"libraries are installed."
msgstr ""
"Kompilēt libguestfs bez libvirt atbalsta, pat ja ir instalētas libvirt "
"izstrādes bibliotēkas."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:586
msgid "B<--with-qemu=\">bin1 bin2 ...B<\">"
msgstr "B<--with-qemu=\">bin1 bin2 ...B<\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:588
msgid ""
"Provide an alternate qemu binary (or list of binaries).  This can be "
"overridden at runtime by setting the C<LIBGUESTFS_HV> environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt alternatīvu qemu bināro failu (vai bināro failu sarakstu).  To "
"izpildlaikā var pārdefinēt, iestatot vides mainīgo C<LIBGUESTFS_HV>."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:592
msgid "B<--with-supermin-packager-config=>I<yum.conf>"
msgstr "B<--with-supermin-packager-config=>I<yum.conf>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:594
msgid "This passes the I<--packager-config> option to L<supermin(1)>."
msgstr "Tas nodod L<supermin(1)> opciju I<--packager-config>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:596
msgid ""
"The most common use for this is to build the appliance using an alternate "
"repository (instead of using the installed yum/dnf/apt/etc configuration to "
"find and download packages).  You might need to use this if you want to "
"build libguestfs without having a network connection.  Examples of using "
"this can be found in the Fedora C<libguestfs.spec> file (see L</BUILDING A "
"PACKAGE FOR FEDORA> below for resources)."
msgstr ""
"Visbiežāk to izmanto, lai palīgsistēmu būvētu, izmantojot alternatīvu "
"repozitoriju (nevis instalēto yum/dnf/apt u. c. konfigurāciju pakotņu "
"atrašanai un lejupielādei).  Tas var būt vajadzīgs, ja vēlaties būvēt "
"libguestfs bez tīkla savienojuma.  Lietojuma piemēri atrodami Fedora failā "
"C<libguestfs.spec> (resursus skatiet L</PAKOTNES BŪVĒŠANA FEDORA> tālāk)."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:604
msgid "B<--with-supermin-extra-options=\">--opt1 --opt2 ...B<\">"
msgstr "B<--with-supermin-extra-options=\">--opt1 --opt2 ...B<\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:606
msgid ""
"Pass additional options to L<supermin(1)>.  See F<appliance/make.sh.in> to "
"understand precisely what this does."
msgstr ""
"Nodot papildu opcijas L<supermin(1)>.  Lai precīzi saprastu, ko tas dara, "
"skatiet F<appliance/make.sh.in>."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:609
msgid "B<PYTHON>"
msgstr "B<PYTHON>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:611
msgid ""
"This environment variable may be set to point to a python binary "
"(eg. C<python3>).  When C<./configure> runs, it inspects this python binary "
"to find the version of Python, the location of Python libraries and so on."
msgstr ""
"Šo vides mainīgo var iestatīt, lai norādītu uz python bināro failu (piem., "
"C<python3>).  Kad C<./configure> tiek izpildīts, tas pārbauda šo python "
"bināro failu, lai noskaidrotu Python versiju, Python bibliotēku atrašanās "
"vietu u. tml."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:616
msgid "B<SUPERMIN>"
msgstr "B<SUPERMIN>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:618
msgid ""
"This environment variable can be set to choose an alternative L<supermin(1)> "
"binary.  This might be used, for example, if you want to use a newer "
"upstream version of supermin than is packaged for your distro, or if "
"supermin is not packaged at all.  On RHEL 7, you must set "
"C<SUPERMIN=/usr/bin/supermin5> when compiling libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Šo vides mainīgo var iestatīt, lai izvēlētos alternatīvu L<supermin(1)> "
"bināro failu.  To var izmantot, piemēram, ja vēlaties izmantot jaunāku "
"augšteces supermin versiju, nekā iepakots jūsu distribūcijai, vai ja "
"supermin nav iepakots vispār.  RHEL 7, kompilējot libguestfs, jāiestata "
"C<SUPERMIN=/usr/bin/supermin5>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:626
msgid "NOTES ABOUT QEMU AND KVM"
msgstr "PIEZĪMES PAR QEMU UN KVM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:628
msgid "A common problem is with broken or incompatible qemu releases."
msgstr "Bieža problēma ir bojāti vai nesaderīgi qemu laidieni."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:630
msgid ""
"Different versions of qemu have problems booting the appliance for different "
"reasons.  This varies between versions of qemu, and Linux distributions "
"which add their own patches."
msgstr ""
"Dažādām qemu versijām ir problēmas ar palīgsistēmas sāknēšanu dažādu iemeslu "
"dēļ.  Tas atšķiras starp qemu versijām un Linux distribūcijām, kas pievieno "
"savus ielāpus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:634
msgid ""
"If you find a problem, you could try using your own qemu built from source "
"(qemu is very easy to build from source), with a \"qemu wrapper\".  See "
"L<guestfs(3)/QEMU WRAPPERS>."
msgstr ""
"Ja atrodat problēmu, varat mēģināt izmantot savu no pirmkoda uzbūvētu qemu "
"(qemu ir ļoti viegli uzbūvēt no pirmkoda) ar „qemu ietinēju”.  Skatiet "
"L<guestfs(3)/QEMU IETINĒJI>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:638
msgid ""
"By default the configure script will look for qemu-kvm (KVM support).  KVM "
"is much faster than using plain qemu."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma configure skripts meklēs qemu-kvm (KVM atbalstu).  KVM ir "
"daudz ātrāks nekā vienkāršs qemu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:641
msgid ""
"You may also need to enable KVM support for non-root users, by following "
"these instructions: "
"L<http://www.linux-kvm.org/page/FAQ#How_can_I_use_kvm_with_a_non-privileged_user.3F>"
msgstr ""
"Iespējams, būs jāiespējo arī KVM atbalsts lietotājiem, kas nav root, sekojot "
"šīm instrukcijām: L<http://www.linux-kvm.org/page/"
"FAQ#How_can_I_use_kvm_with_a_non-privileged_user.3F>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:645
msgid "On some systems, this will work too:"
msgstr "Dažās sistēmās darbosies arī šis:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:647
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" chmod 0666 /dev/kvm\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" chmod 0666 /dev/kvm\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:649
msgid ""
"On some systems, the chmod will not survive a reboot, and you will need to "
"make edits to the udev configuration."
msgstr ""
"Dažās sistēmās chmod nepārdzīvos pārstartēšanu, un būs jārediģē udev "
"konfigurācija."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:652
msgid "USING CLANG (LLVM) INSTEAD OF GCC"
msgstr "CLANG (LLVM) IZMANTOŠANA GCC VIETĀ"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:654
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export CC=clang\n"
" ./configure\n"
" make\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export CC=clang\n"
" ./configure\n"
" make\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:658
msgid "USING A PREBUILT BINARY APPLIANCE"
msgstr "IEPRIEKŠ UZBŪVĒTAS BINĀRĀS PALĪGSISTĒMAS IZMANTOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:660
msgid ""
"To understand what the libguestfs appliance means, see "
"L<guestfs-internals(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Lai saprastu, ko nozīmē libguestfs palīgsistēma, skatiet L<guestfs-internals"
"(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:663
msgid ""
"If you are using non-Linux, or a Linux distribution that does not have "
"L<supermin(1)> support, or simply if you don't want to build your own "
"libguestfs appliance, then you can use one of the prebuilt binary appliances "
"that we supply: L<http://libguestfs.org/download/binaries/appliance>"
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat ne-Linux sistēmu vai Linux distribūciju bez L<supermin(1)> "
"atbalsta vai vienkārši nevēlaties būvēt savu libguestfs palīgsistēmu, varat "
"izmantot kādu no mūsu nodrošinātajām iepriekš uzbūvētajām binārajām "
"palīgsistēmām: L<http://libguestfs.org/download/binaries/appliance>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:669
msgid "Build libguestfs like this:"
msgstr "Būvējiet libguestfs šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:671
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./configure --disable-appliance --disable-daemon\n"
" make\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./configure --disable-appliance --disable-daemon\n"
" make\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:674
msgid ""
"Set C<$LIBGUESTFS_PATH> to the path where you unpacked the appliance "
"tarball, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Iestatiet C<$LIBGUESTFS_PATH> uz ceļu, kur izpakojāt palīgsistēmas tar "
"arhīvu, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:677 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:566
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_PATH=/usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_PATH=/usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:679
msgid ""
"and run the libguestfs programs and virt tools in the normal way, eg. using "
"the F<./run> script (see above)."
msgstr ""
"un izpildiet libguestfs programmas un virt rīkus parastajā veidā, piem., "
"izmantojot skriptu F<./run> (skatiet iepriekš)."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:682
msgid "BUILDING A PACKAGE FOR FEDORA"
msgstr "PAKOTNES BŪVĒŠANA FEDORA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:684
msgid ""
"The Fedora spec file is stored under: "
"L<http://pkgs.fedoraproject.org/cgit/rpms/libguestfs.git/>"
msgstr ""
"Fedora spec fails tiek glabāts: L<http://pkgs.fedoraproject.org/cgit/rpms/"
"libguestfs.git/>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:687
msgid "Libguestfs is built in Fedora using the ordinary Fedora build system (Koji)."
msgstr ""
"Fedorā libguestfs tiek būvēts, izmantojot parasto Fedora būvēšanas sistēmu "
"(Koji)."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:690
msgid "BUILDING A PACKAGE FOR RED HAT ENTERPRISE LINUX"
msgstr "PAKOTNES BŪVĒŠANA RED HAT ENTERPRISE LINUX"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:692
msgid ""
"Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) builds of libguestfs are heavily patched.  "
"There are broadly two types of patches we apply:"
msgstr ""
"Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) libguestfs būves ir stipri ielāpotas.  "
"Pārsvarā lietojam divu veidu ielāpus:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:699
msgid ""
"We disable many features that we do not wish to support for RHEL customers.  "
"For example, the \"libguestfs live\" feature is disabled."
msgstr ""
"Atspējojam daudzus līdzekļus, kurus nevēlamies atbalstīt RHEL klientiem.  "
"Piemēram, līdzeklis „libguestfs live” ir atspējots."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:704
msgid "We backport upstream features."
msgstr "Pārnesam augšteces līdzekļus uz vecākām versijām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:708
msgid ""
"The patches we apply to RHEL releases are available publicly in the upstream "
"git repository, in a branch called C<rhel-x.y>"
msgstr ""
"RHEL laidieniem lietotie ielāpi ir publiski pieejami augšteces git "
"repozitorijā, zarā C<rhel-x.y>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:711
msgid ""
"For example, the RHEL 7.3 patches are available here: "
"L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs/commits/rhel-7.3>"
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, RHEL 7.3 ielāpi ir pieejami šeit: L<https://github.com/libguestfs/"
"libguestfs/commits/rhel-7.3>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:714
msgid ""
"The sources and spec files for RHEL versions of libguestfs are available on "
"L<https://git.centos.org/project/rpms>, and see also "
"L<https://wiki.centos.org/Sources>."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs RHEL versiju pirmkods un spec faili ir pieejami L<https://"
"git.centos.org/project/rpms>, skatiet arī L<https://wiki.centos.org/Sources>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-building.pod:720
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-hacking(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-internals(1)>, L<guestfs-performance(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-release-notes(1)>, L<guestfs-testing(1)>, "
"L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)>, L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-hacking(1)>, L<guestfs-"
"internals(1)>, L<guestfs-performance(1)>, L<guestfs-release-notes(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-testing(1)>, L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)>, L<libguestfs-make-fixed-"
"appliance(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-faq - libguestfs Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)"
msgstr "guestfs-faq - libguestfs biežāk uzdotie jautājumi (BUJ)"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:5
msgid "ABOUT LIBGUESTFS"
msgstr "PAR LIBGUESTFS"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:7
msgid "What is libguestfs?"
msgstr "Kas ir libguestfs?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:9
msgid ""
"libguestfs is a way to create, access and modify disk images.  You can look "
"inside disk images, modify the files they contain, create them from scratch, "
"resize them, and much more.  It’s especially useful from scripts and "
"programs and from the command line."
msgstr ""
"libguestfs ir veids, kā veidot disku attēlus, piekļūt tiem un tos mainīt.  "
"Varat ieskatīties disku attēlos, mainīt tajos esošos failus, izveidot tos no "
"nulles, mainīt to izmēru un daudz ko citu.  Tas ir īpaši noderīgs no "
"skriptiem un programmām un no komandrindas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:14
msgid ""
"libguestfs is a C library (hence \"lib-\"), and a set of tools built on this "
"library, and bindings for many common programming languages."
msgstr ""
"libguestfs ir C bibliotēka (tātad „lib-”), uz šīs bibliotēkas veidotu rīku "
"kopa un saistījumi daudzām izplatītām programmēšanas valodām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:17
msgid ""
"For more information about what libguestfs can do read the introduction on "
"the home page (L<http://libguestfs.org>)."
msgstr ""
"Plašāku informāciju par to, ko libguestfs var darīt, lasiet ievadā mājaslapā "
"(L<http://libguestfs.org>)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:20
msgid "What are the virt tools?"
msgstr "Kas ir virt rīki?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:22
msgid ""
"Virt tools (website: L<http://virt-tools.org>) are a whole set of "
"virtualization management tools aimed at system administrators.  Some of "
"them come from libguestfs, some from libvirt and many others from other open "
"source projects.  So virt tools is a superset of libguestfs.  However "
"libguestfs comes with many important tools.  See L<http://libguestfs.org> "
"for a full list."
msgstr ""
"Virt rīki (tīmekļa vietne: L<http://virt-tools.org>) ir vesela "
"virtualizācijas pārvaldības rīku kopa, kas paredzēta sistēmu "
"administratoriem.  Daži no tiem nāk no libguestfs, daži no libvirt un daudzi "
"citi no citiem atvērtā pirmkoda projektiem.  Tātad virt rīki ir libguestfs "
"virskopa.  Tomēr libguestfs ietver daudzus svarīgus rīkus.  Pilnu sarakstu "
"skatiet L<http://libguestfs.org>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:29
msgid "Does libguestfs need { libvirt / KVM / Red Hat / Fedora }?"
msgstr "Vai libguestfs vajag { libvirt / KVM / Red Hat / Fedora }?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:31
msgid "No!"
msgstr "Nē!"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:33
msgid "libvirt is not a requirement for libguestfs."
msgstr "libvirt nav libguestfs prasība."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:35
msgid ""
"libguestfs works with any disk image, including ones created in VMware, KVM, "
"qemu, VirtualBox, Xen, and many other hypervisors, and ones which you have "
"created from scratch."
msgstr ""
"libguestfs darbojas ar jebkuru diska attēlu, ieskaitot tos, kas izveidoti "
"VMware, KVM, qemu, VirtualBox, Xen un daudzos citos hipervizoros, un tos, "
"kas izveidoti no nulles."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:39
msgid ""
"S<Red Hat> sponsors (ie. pays for) development of libguestfs and a huge "
"number of other open source projects.  But you can run libguestfs and the "
"virt tools on many different Linux distros and Mac OS X.  We try our best to "
"support all Linux distros as first-class citizens.  Some virt tools have "
"been ported to Windows."
msgstr ""
"S<Red Hat> sponsorē (t. i., apmaksā) libguestfs un ļoti daudzu citu atvērtā "
"pirmkoda projektu izstrādi.  Taču libguestfs un virt rīkus var izpildīt "
"daudzās dažādās Linux distribūcijās un Mac OS X.  Mēs darām visu iespējamo, "
"lai atbalstītu visas Linux distribūcijas kā pilntiesīgas.  Daži virt rīki ir "
"pārnesti uz Windows."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:45
msgid "How does libguestfs compare to other tools?"
msgstr "Kā libguestfs salīdzināms ar citiem rīkiem?"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:49
msgid "I<vs. kpartx>"
msgstr "I<pret kpartx>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:51
msgid ""
"Libguestfs takes a different approach from kpartx.  kpartx needs root, and "
"mounts filesystems on the host kernel (which can be insecure - see "
"L<guestfs-security(1)>).  Libguestfs isolates your host kernel from guests, "
"is more flexible, scriptable, supports LVM, doesn't require root, is "
"isolated from other processes, and cleans up after itself.  Libguestfs is "
"more than just file access because you can use it to create images from "
"scratch."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs izmanto citu pieeju nekā kpartx.  kpartx vajag root, un tas montē "
"failu sistēmas resursdatora kodolā (kas var būt nedroši — skatiet L<guestfs-"
"security(1)>).  Libguestfs izolē resursdatora kodolu no viesiem, ir "
"elastīgāks, skriptojams, atbalsta LVM, neprasa root, ir izolēts no citiem "
"procesiem un sakopj pēc sevis.  Libguestfs ir vairāk nekā tikai piekļuve "
"failiem, jo ar to var veidot attēlus no nulles."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:59
msgid "I<vs. vdfuse>"
msgstr "I<pret vdfuse>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:61
msgid ""
"vdfuse is like kpartx but for VirtualBox images.  See the kpartx comparison "
"above.  You can use libguestfs on the partition files exposed by vdfuse, "
"although it’s not necessary since libguestfs can access VirtualBox images "
"directly."
msgstr ""
"vdfuse ir līdzīgs kpartx, bet VirtualBox attēliem.  Skatiet iepriekšējo "
"salīdzinājumu ar kpartx.  Libguestfs var izmantot ar vdfuse atklātajiem "
"nodalījumu failiem, lai gan tas nav nepieciešams, jo libguestfs var piekļūt "
"VirtualBox attēliem tieši."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:66
msgid "I<vs. qemu-nbd>"
msgstr "I<pret qemu-nbd>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:68
msgid ""
"NBD (Network Block Device) is a protocol for exporting block devices over "
"the network.  qemu-nbd is an NBD server which can handle any disk format "
"supported by qemu (eg. raw, qcow2).  You can use libguestfs and qemu-nbd or "
"nbdkit together to access block devices over the network, for example: "
"C<guestfish -a nbd://remote>"
msgstr ""
"NBD (Network Block Device) ir protokols bloku ierīču eksportēšanai pa "
"tīklu.  qemu-nbd ir NBD serveris, kas var apstrādāt jebkuru qemu atbalstītu "
"diska formātu (piem., raw, qcow2).  Libguestfs un qemu-nbd vai nbdkit var "
"izmantot kopā, lai piekļūtu bloku ierīcēm pa tīklu, piemēram: C<guestfish -a "
"nbd://remote>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:74
msgid "I<vs. mounting filesystems in the host>"
msgstr "I<pret failu sistēmu montēšanu resursdatorā>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:76
msgid ""
"Mounting guest filesystems in the host is insecure and should be avoided "
"completely for untrusted guests.  Use libguestfs to provide a layer of "
"protection against filesystem exploits.  See also L<guestmount(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Viesu failu sistēmu montēšana resursdatorā ir nedroša, un no tās pilnībā "
"jāizvairās neuzticamu viesu gadījumā.  Izmantojiet libguestfs, lai "
"nodrošinātu aizsardzības slāni pret failu sistēmu ļaunprātīgu izmantošanu.  "
"Skatīt arī L<guestmount(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:81
msgid "I<vs. parted>"
msgstr "I<pret parted>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:83
msgid ""
"Libguestfs supports LVM.  Libguestfs uses parted and provides most parted "
"features through the libguestfs API."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs atbalsta LVM.  Libguestfs izmanto parted un nodrošina lielāko "
"daļu parted līdzekļu caur libguestfs API."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:88
msgid "GETTING HELP AND REPORTING BUGS"
msgstr "PALĪDZĪBAS SAŅEMŠANA UN ZIŅOŠANA PAR KĻŪDĀM"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:90
msgid "How do I know what version I'm using?"
msgstr "Kā uzzināt, kuru versiju izmantoju?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:92
msgid "The simplest method is:"
msgstr "Vienkāršākā metode ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --version\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --version\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:96
msgid ""
"Libguestfs development happens along an unstable branch and we periodically "
"create a stable branch which we backport stable patches to.  To find out "
"more, read L<guestfs(3)/LIBGUESTFS VERSION NUMBERS>."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs izstrāde notiek nestabilā zarā, un periodiski veidojam stabilu "
"zaru, uz kuru pārnesam stabilos ielāpus.  Lai uzzinātu vairāk, lasiet "
"L<guestfs(3)/LIBGUESTFS VERSIJU NUMURI>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:100
msgid "How can I get help?"
msgstr "Kā saņemt palīdzību?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:102
msgid "What mailing lists or chat rooms are available?"
msgstr "Kādi ir pieejamie pasta saraksti vai tērzētavas?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:104
msgid ""
"If you are a S<Red Hat> customer using Red Hat Enterprise Linux, please "
"contact S<Red Hat Support>: L<http://redhat.com/support>"
msgstr ""
"Ja esat S<Red Hat> klients un izmantojat Red Hat Enterprise Linux, lūdzu, "
"sazinieties ar S<Red Hat atbalstu>: L<http://redhat.com/support>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:107
msgid ""
"There is a mailing list, mainly for development, but users are also welcome "
"to ask questions about libguestfs and the virt tools: "
"L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>"
msgstr ""
"Ir pasta saraksts, galvenokārt izstrādei, taču arī lietotāji ir aicināti "
"uzdot jautājumus par libguestfs un virt rīkiem: L<https://"
"lists.libguestfs.org>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:111
msgid ""
"You can also talk to us on IRC channel C<#guestfs> on Libera Chat.  We're "
"not always around, so please stay in the channel after asking your question "
"and someone will get back to you."
msgstr ""
"Ar mums var sazināties arī IRC kanālā C<#guestfs> tīklā Libera Chat.  Mēs ne "
"vienmēr esam klāt, tāpēc pēc jautājuma uzdošanas, lūdzu, palieciet kanālā, "
"un kāds jums atbildēs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:115
msgid ""
"For other virt tools (not ones supplied with libguestfs) there is a general "
"virt tools mailing list: "
"L<https://www.redhat.com/mailman/listinfo/virt-tools-list>"
msgstr ""
"Citiem virt rīkiem (ne tiem, kas nāk ar libguestfs) ir vispārīgs virt rīku "
"pasta saraksts: L<https://www.redhat.com/mailman/listinfo/virt-tools-list>"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:119
msgid "How do I report bugs?"
msgstr "Kā ziņot par kļūdām?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:121
msgid "Please use the following link to enter a bug in Bugzilla:"
msgstr "Lai Bugzilla ievadītu kļūdu, lūdzu, izmantojiet šo saiti:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:123 docs/guestfs-testing.pod:18
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/enter_bug.cgi?component=libguestfs&product=Virtualization+Tools>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/"
"enter_bug.cgi?component=libguestfs&product=Virtualization+Tools>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:125
msgid "Include as much detail as you can and a way to reproduce the problem."
msgstr ""
"Iekļaujiet pēc iespējas vairāk informācijas un veidu, kā problēmu atkārtot."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:127
msgid "Include the full output of L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)>."
msgstr "Iekļaujiet pilnu L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)> izvadi."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:129
msgid "COMMON PROBLEMS"
msgstr "BIEŽĀKĀS PROBLĒMAS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:131
msgid ""
"See also L<guestfs(3)/LIBGUESTFS GOTCHAS> for some \"gotchas\" with using "
"the libguestfs API."
msgstr ""
"Dažus „slazdus”, izmantojot libguestfs API, skatiet arī L<guestfs(3)/"
"LIBGUESTFS SLAZDI>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:134
msgid "\"Could not allocate dynamic translator buffer\""
msgstr "\"Could not allocate dynamic translator buffer\""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:136
msgid ""
"This obscure error is in fact an SELinux failure.  You have to enable the "
"following SELinux boolean:"
msgstr ""
"Šī neskaidrā kļūda patiesībā ir SELinux kļūme.  Jāiespējo šāda SELinux Būla "
"vērtība:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" setsebool -P virt_use_execmem=on\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" setsebool -P virt_use_execmem=on\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:141
msgid ""
"For more information see "
"L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=806106>."
msgstr ""
"Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/"
"show_bug.cgi?id=806106>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:144
msgid "\"child process died unexpectedly\""
msgstr "\"child process died unexpectedly\""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:146
msgid ""
"[This error message was changed in libguestfs 1.21.18 to something more "
"explanatory.]"
msgstr ""
"[Libguestfs 1.21.18 šis kļūdas ziņojums tika mainīts uz kaut ko "
"paskaidrojošāku.]"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:149
msgid ""
"This error indicates that qemu failed or the host kernel could not boot.  To "
"get further information about the failure, you have to run:"
msgstr ""
"Šī kļūda norāda, ka qemu neizdevās vai resursdatora kodolu nevarēja sāknēt.  "
"Lai iegūtu papildu informāciju par kļūmi, jāizpilda:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:152 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:919
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:32 test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:154
msgid ""
"If, after using this, you still don’t understand the failure, contact us "
"(see previous section)."
msgstr ""
"Ja pēc tā kļūme joprojām nav saprotama, sazinieties ar mums (skatiet "
"iepriekšējo sadaļu)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:157
msgid ""
"libguestfs: error: cannot find any suitable libguestfs supermin, fixed or "
"old-style appliance on LIBGUESTFS_PATH"
msgstr ""
"libguestfs: error: cannot find any suitable libguestfs supermin, fixed or "
"old-style appliance on LIBGUESTFS_PATH"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:159
msgid "febootstrap-supermin-helper: ext2: parent directory not found"
msgstr "febootstrap-supermin-helper: ext2: parent directory not found"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:161
msgid "supermin-helper: ext2: parent directory not found"
msgstr "supermin-helper: ext2: parent directory not found"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:163
msgid "[This issue is fixed permanently in libguestfs E<ge> 1.26.]"
msgstr "[Šī problēma ir neatgriezeniski labota libguestfs E<ge> 1.26.]"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:165
msgid ""
"If you see any of these errors on Debian/Ubuntu, you need to run the "
"following command:"
msgstr "Ja Debian/Ubuntu redzat kādu no šīm kļūdām, jāizpilda šī komanda:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:168 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:285 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:336
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sudo update-guestfs-appliance\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sudo update-guestfs-appliance\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:170
msgid "\"Permission denied\" when running libguestfs as root"
msgstr "„Permission denied”, izpildot libguestfs kā root"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:172
msgid ""
"You get a permission denied error when opening a disk image, even though you "
"are running libguestfs as root."
msgstr ""
"Atverot diska attēlu, saņemat kļūdu „permission denied”, lai gan izpildāt "
"libguestfs kā root."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:175
msgid ""
"This is caused by libvirt, and so only happens when using the libvirt "
"backend.  When run as root, libvirt decides to run the qemu appliance as "
"user C<qemu.qemu>.  Unfortunately this usually means that qemu cannot open "
"disk images, especially if those disk images are owned by root, or are "
"present in directories which require root access."
msgstr ""
"To izraisa libvirt, tāpēc tas notiek tikai, izmantojot libvirt "
"aizmugursistēmu.  Izpildot kā root, libvirt nolemj izpildīt qemu "
"palīgsistēmu kā lietotājs C<qemu.qemu>.  Diemžēl tas parasti nozīmē, ka qemu "
"nevar atvērt disku attēlus, it īpaši, ja šo disku attēlu īpašnieks ir root "
"vai tie atrodas direktorijās, kurām vajadzīga root piekļuve."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:181
msgid ""
"There is a bug open against libvirt to fix this: "
"L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1045069>"
msgstr ""
"Ir atvērta libvirt kļūda, lai to labotu: L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/"
"show_bug.cgi?id=1045069>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:184
msgid "You can work around this by one of the following methods:"
msgstr "To var apiet kādā no šiem veidiem:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:190
msgid "Switch to the direct backend:"
msgstr "Pārslēgties uz tiešo aizmugursistēmu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:192 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:547
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:116 test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=direct\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=direct\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:196
msgid "Don’t run libguestfs as root."
msgstr "Neizpildīt libguestfs kā root."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:200
msgid ""
"Chmod the disk image and any parent directories so that the qemu user can "
"access them."
msgstr ""
"Izpildīt chmod diska attēlam un visām vecākdirektorijām, lai qemu lietotājs "
"tām varētu piekļūt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:205
msgid "(Nasty) Edit F</etc/libvirt/qemu.conf> and change the C<user> setting."
msgstr ""
"(Neglīti) Rediģēt F</etc/libvirt/qemu.conf> un mainīt iestatījumu C<user>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:209
msgid "execl: /init: Permission denied"
msgstr "execl: /init: Permission denied"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:211
msgid ""
"B<Note:> If this error happens when you are using a distro package of "
"libguestfs (eg. from Fedora, Debian, etc) then file a bug against the "
"distro.  This is not an error which normal users should ever see if the "
"distro package has been prepared correctly."
msgstr ""
"B<Piezīme:> ja šī kļūda rodas, izmantojot libguestfs distribūcijas pakotni "
"(piem., no Fedoras, Debian u. c.), iesniedziet kļūdas ziņojumu "
"distribūcijai.  Šī nav kļūda, ko parastiem lietotājiem vajadzētu redzēt, ja "
"distribūcijas pakotne ir sagatavota pareizi."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:216
msgid "This error happens during the supermin boot phase of starting the appliance:"
msgstr "Šī kļūda rodas palīgsistēmas palaišanas supermin sāknēšanas fāzē:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:219
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" supermin: mounting new root on /root\n"
" supermin: chroot\n"
" execl: /init: Permission denied\n"
" supermin: debug: listing directory /\n"
" [...followed by a lot of debug output...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" supermin: mounting new root on /root\n"
" supermin: chroot\n"
" execl: /init: Permission denied\n"
" supermin: debug: listing directory /\n"
" [...followed by a lot of debug output...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:225
msgid ""
"This is a complicated bug related to L<supermin(1)> appliances.  The "
"appliance is constructed by copying files like F</bin/bash> and many "
"libraries from the host.  The file C<hostfiles> lists the files that should "
"be copied from the host into the appliance.  If some files don't exist on "
"the host then they are missed out, but if these files are needed in order to "
"(eg) run F</bin/bash> then you'll see the above error."
msgstr ""
"Šī ir sarežģīta kļūda, kas saistīta ar L<supermin(1)> palīgsistēmām.  "
"Palīgsistēma tiek veidota, kopējot failus, piemēram, F</bin/bash>, un "
"daudzas bibliotēkas no resursdatora.  Fails C<hostfiles> uzskaita failus, "
"kas jākopē no resursdatora palīgsistēmā.  Ja kādi faili resursdatorā "
"neeksistē, tie tiek izlaisti, bet, ja šie faili vajadzīgi, lai (piem.) "
"izpildītu F</bin/bash>, redzēsiet iepriekšējo kļūdu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:233
msgid ""
"Diagnosing the problem involves studying the libraries needed by "
"F</bin/bash>, ie:"
msgstr ""
"Problēmas diagnosticēšana ietver F</bin/bash> vajadzīgo bibliotēku izpēti, "
"t. i.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:236
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldd /bin/bash\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldd /bin/bash\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:238
msgid ""
"comparing that with C<hostfiles>, with the files actually available in the "
"host filesystem, and with the debug output printed in the error message.  "
"Once you've worked out which file is missing, install that file using your "
"package manager and try again."
msgstr ""
"salīdzinot to ar C<hostfiles>, ar resursdatora failu sistēmā faktiski "
"pieejamajiem failiem un ar kļūdas ziņojumā izdrukāto atkļūdošanas izvadi.  "
"Kad noskaidrots, kurš fails trūkst, instalējiet to ar pakotņu pārvaldnieku "
"un mēģiniet vēlreiz."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:243
msgid ""
"You should also check that files like F</init> and F</bin/bash> (in the "
"appliance) are executable.  The debug output shows file modes."
msgstr ""
"Pārbaudiet arī, vai tādi faili kā F</init> un F</bin/bash> (palīgsistēmā) ir "
"izpildāmi.  Atkļūdošanas izvade rāda failu režīmus."

