msgstr ""
"Hilko Bengen atbalsta libguestfs Debian.  Ir pieejamas oficiālas Debian "
"pakotnes: L<http://packages.debian.org/search?keywords=libguestfs>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:311
msgid "Ubuntu"
msgstr "Ubuntu"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:313
msgid ""
"We don’t have a full time Ubuntu maintainer, and the packages supplied by "
"Canonical (which are outside our control) are sometimes broken."
msgstr ""
"Mums nav pilna laika Ubuntu uzturētāja, un Canonical nodrošinātās pakotnes "
"(kas ir ārpus mūsu kontroles) dažreiz ir bojātas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:316
msgid ""
"Canonical decided to change the permissions on the kernel so that it's not "
"readable except by root.  This is completely stupid, but they won't change "
"it (L<https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/linux/+bug/759725>).  So "
"every user should do this:"
msgstr ""
"Canonical nolēma mainīt kodola atļaujas tā, lai to varētu nolasīt tikai "
"root.  Tas ir pilnīgi muļķīgi, taču viņi to nemainīs (L<https://"
"bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/linux/+bug/759725>).  Tāpēc katram "
"lietotājam jāizpilda šis:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:326
msgid "Ubuntu 12.04"
msgstr "Ubuntu 12.04"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:328
msgid ""
"libguestfs in this version of Ubuntu works, but you need to update "
"febootstrap and seabios to the latest versions."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs šajā Ubuntu versijā darbojas, taču febootstrap un seabios "
"jāatjaunina uz jaunākajām versijām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:331
msgid ""
"You need febootstrap E<ge> 3.14-2 from: "
"L<http://packages.ubuntu.com/precise/febootstrap>"
msgstr ""
"Vajadzīgs febootstrap E<ge> 3.14-2 no: L<http://packages.ubuntu.com/precise/"
"febootstrap>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:334
msgid "After installing or updating febootstrap, rebuild the appliance:"
msgstr ""
"Pēc febootstrap instalēšanas vai atjaunināšanas no jauna uzbūvējiet "
"palīgsistēmu:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:338
msgid ""
"You need seabios E<ge> 0.6.2-0ubuntu2.1 or E<ge> 0.6.2-0ubuntu3 from: "
"L<http://packages.ubuntu.com/precise-updates/seabios> or "
"L<http://packages.ubuntu.com/quantal/seabios>"
msgstr ""
"Vajadzīgs seabios E<ge> 0.6.2-0ubuntu2.1 vai E<ge> 0.6.2-0ubuntu3 no: "
"L<http://packages.ubuntu.com/precise-updates/seabios> vai L<http://"
"packages.ubuntu.com/quantal/seabios>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:343
msgid "Also you need to do (see above):"
msgstr "Jāizpilda arī (skatiet iepriekš):"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:351
msgid "Gentoo"
msgstr "Gentoo"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:353
msgid ""
"Libguestfs was added to Gentoo in 2012-07 by Andreis Vinogradovs "
"(libguestfs) and Maxim Koltsov (mainly hivex).  Do:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs Gentoo pievienoja 2012. gada jūlijā Andreis Vinogradovs "
"(libguestfs) un Maxim Koltsov (galvenokārt hivex).  Izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:356
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" emerge libguestfs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" emerge libguestfs\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:358
msgid "Mageia"
msgstr "Mageia"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:360
msgid "Libguestfs was added to Mageia in 2013-08. Do:"
msgstr "Libguestfs Mageia tika pievienots 2013. gada augustā. Izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" urpmi libguestfs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" urpmi libguestfs\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:364
msgid "SuSE"
msgstr "SuSE"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:366
msgid "Libguestfs was added to SuSE in 2012 by Olaf Hering."
msgstr "Libguestfs SuSE pievienoja 2012. gadā Olaf Hering."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:368
msgid "ArchLinux"
msgstr "ArchLinux"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:370
msgid "Libguestfs was added to the AUR in 2010."
msgstr "Libguestfs AUR tika pievienots 2010. gadā."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:372
msgid "Other Linux distro"
msgstr "Cita Linux distribūcija"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:374
msgid "Compile from source (next section)."
msgstr "Kompilējiet no pirmkoda (nākamā sadaļa)."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:376
msgid "Other non-Linux distro"
msgstr "Cita ne-Linux distribūcija"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:378
msgid "You'll have to compile from source, and port it."
msgstr "Būs jākompilē no pirmkoda un jāpārnes."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:382
msgid "How can I compile and install libguestfs from source?"
msgstr "Kā kompilēt un instalēt libguestfs no pirmkoda?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:384
msgid ""
"You can compile libguestfs from git or a source tarball.  Read the README "
"file before starting."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs var kompilēt no git vai pirmkoda tar arhīva.  Pirms sākšanas "
"izlasiet README failu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:387
msgid ""
"Git: L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs> Source tarballs: "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/download>"
msgstr ""
"Git: L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs> Pirmkoda tar arhīvi: "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/download>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:390 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:424
msgid "Don’t run C<make install>! Use the C<./run> script instead (see README)."
msgstr ""
"Neizpildiet C<make install>! Tā vietā izmantojiet skriptu C<./run> (skatiet "
"README)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:392
msgid ""
"How can I compile and install libguestfs if my distro doesn't have new "
"enough qemu/supermin/kernel?"
msgstr ""
"Kā kompilēt un instalēt libguestfs, ja manā distribūcijā nav pietiekami "
"jauna qemu/supermin/kodola?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:395
msgid ""
"Libguestfs needs supermin 5.  If supermin 5 hasn't been ported to your "
"distro, then see the question below."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs vajag supermin 5.  Ja supermin 5 nav pārnests uz jūsu "
"distribūciju, skatiet jautājumu tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:398
msgid ""
"First compile qemu, supermin and/or the kernel from source.  You do I<not> "
"need to C<make install> them."
msgstr ""
"Vispirms kompilējiet qemu, supermin un/vai kodolu no pirmkoda.  Tiem I<nav> "
"jāizpilda C<make install>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:401
msgid ""
"In the libguestfs source directory, create two files.  C<localconfigure> "
"should contain:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs pirmkoda direktorijā izveidojiet divus failus.  C<localconfigure> "
"jāsatur:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" source localenv\n"
" #export PATH=/tmp/qemu/x86_64-softmmu:$PATH\n"
" ./configure --prefix /usr \"$@\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" source localenv\n"
" #export PATH=/tmp/qemu/x86_64-softmmu:$PATH\n"
" ./configure --prefix /usr \"$@\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:408
msgid "Make C<localconfigure> executable."
msgstr "Padariet C<localconfigure> izpildāmu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:410
msgid "C<localenv> should contain:"
msgstr "C<localenv> jāsatur:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:412
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #export SUPERMIN=/tmp/supermin/src/supermin\n"
" #export LIBGUESTFS_HV=/tmp/qemu/x86_64-softmmu/qemu-system-x86_64\n"
" #export SUPERMIN_KERNEL=/tmp/linux/arch/x86/boot/bzImage\n"
" #export SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION=4.XX.0\n"
" #export SUPERMIN_MODULES=/tmp/lib/modules/4.XX.0\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #export SUPERMIN=/tmp/supermin/src/supermin\n"
" #export LIBGUESTFS_HV=/tmp/qemu/x86_64-softmmu/qemu-system-x86_64\n"
" #export SUPERMIN_KERNEL=/tmp/linux/arch/x86/boot/bzImage\n"
" #export SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION=4.XX.0\n"
" #export SUPERMIN_MODULES=/tmp/lib/modules/4.XX.0\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:418
msgid ""
"Uncomment and adjust these lines as required to use the alternate programs "
"you have compiled."
msgstr ""
"Atkomentējiet un pēc vajadzības pielāgojiet šīs rindas, lai izmantotu "
"kompilētās alternatīvās programmas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:421
msgid ""
"Use C<./localconfigure> instead of C<./configure>, but otherwise you compile "
"libguestfs as usual."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet C<./localconfigure>, nevis C<./configure>, bet citādi "
"kompilējiet libguestfs kā parasti."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:426
msgid "How can I compile and install libguestfs without supermin?"
msgstr "Kā kompilēt un instalēt libguestfs bez supermin?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:428
msgid ""
"If supermin 5 supports your distro, but you don’t happen to have a new "
"enough supermin installed, then see the previous question."
msgstr ""
"Ja supermin 5 atbalsta jūsu distribūciju, bet jums nav instalēta pietiekami "
"jauna supermin versija, skatiet iepriekšējo jautājumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:431
msgid ""
"If supermin 5 doesn't support your distro at all, you will need to use the "
"\"fixed appliance method\" where you use a pre-compiled binary appliance.  "
"To build libguestfs without supermin, you need to pass C<--disable-appliance "
"--disable-daemon> to either F<./configure> or F<./configure> (depending "
"whether you are building respectively from git or from tarballs).  Then, "
"when using libguestfs, you B<must> set the C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH> environment "
"variable to the directory of a pre-compiled appliance, as also described in "
"L<guestfs-internals(1)/FIXED APPLIANCE>."
msgstr ""
"Ja supermin 5 jūsu distribūciju neatbalsta vispār, būs jāizmanto „fiksētās "
"palīgsistēmas metode”, kurā tiek izmantota iepriekš kompilēta binārā "
"palīgsistēma.  Lai uzbūvētu libguestfs bez supermin, F<./configure> vai F<./"
"configure> (atkarībā no tā, vai būvējat attiecīgi no git vai tar arhīviem) "
"jānodod C<--disable-appliance --disable-daemon>.  Pēc tam, izmantojot "
"libguestfs, B<jāiestata> vides mainīgais C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH> uz iepriekš "
"kompilētas palīgsistēmas direktoriju, kā aprakstīts arī L<guestfs-internals"
"(1)/FIKSĒTA PALĪGSISTĒMA>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:441
msgid ""
"For pre-compiled appliances, see also: "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/download/binaries/appliance/>."
msgstr ""
"Iepriekš kompilētas palīgsistēmas skatiet arī: L<http://libguestfs.org/"
"download/binaries/appliance/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:444
msgid "Patches to port supermin to more Linux distros are welcome."
msgstr "Ielāpi supermin pārnešanai uz vairāk Linux distribūcijām ir gaidīti."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:446
msgid "How can I add support for sVirt?"
msgstr "Kā pievienot sVirt atbalstu?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:448
msgid ""
"B<Note for Fedora/RHEL users:> This configuration is the default starting "
"with S<Fedora 18> and S<RHEL 7>.  If you find any problems, please let us "
"know or file a bug."
msgstr ""
"B<Piezīme Fedora/RHEL lietotājiem:> sākot ar S<Fedora 18> un S<RHEL 7>, šī "
"konfigurācija ir noklusējums.  Ja atrodat problēmas, lūdzu, paziņojiet mums "
"vai iesniedziet kļūdas ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:452
msgid ""
"L<SVirt|http://selinuxproject.org/page/SVirt> provides a hardened appliance "
"using SELinux, making it very hard for a rogue disk image to \"escape\" from "
"the confinement of libguestfs and damage the host (it's fair to say that "
"even in standard libguestfs this would be hard, but sVirt provides an extra "
"layer of protection for the host and more importantly protects virtual "
"machines on the same host from each other)."
msgstr ""
"L<SVirt|http://selinuxproject.org/page/SVirt> nodrošina nostiprinātu "
"palīgsistēmu, izmantojot SELinux, kas ļoti apgrūtina ļaunprātīgam diska "
"attēlam „izbēgt” no libguestfs ierobežojuma un kaitēt resursdatoram (var "
"teikt, ka arī standarta libguestfs tas būtu grūti, taču sVirt nodrošina "
"papildu aizsardzības slāni resursdatoram un, kas vēl svarīgāk, aizsargā "
"vienā resursdatorā esošās virtuālās mašīnas vienu no otras)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:460
msgid ""
"Currently to enable sVirt you will need libvirt E<ge> 0.10.2 (1.0 or later "
"preferred), libguestfs E<ge> 1.20, and the SELinux policies from recent "
"Fedora.  If you are not running S<Fedora 18+>, you will need to make changes "
"to your SELinux policy - contact us on the mailing list."
msgstr ""
"Pašlaik sVirt iespējošanai vajadzīgs libvirt E<ge> 0.10.2 (vēlams 1.0 vai "
"jaunāks), libguestfs E<ge> 1.20 un SELinux politikas no jaunākās Fedora.  Ja "
"neizmantojat S<Fedora 18+>, būs jāmaina SELinux politika — sazinieties ar "
"mums pasta sarakstā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:465
msgid "Once you have the requirements, do:"
msgstr "Kad prasības ir izpildītas, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:467
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./configure --with-default-backend=libvirt       # libguestfs >= 1.22\n"
" ./configure --with-default-attach-method=libvirt # libguestfs <= 1.20\n"
" make\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./configure --with-default-backend=libvirt       # libguestfs >= 1.22\n"
" ./configure --with-default-attach-method=libvirt # libguestfs <= 1.20\n"
" make\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:471
msgid "Set SELinux to Enforcing mode, and sVirt should be used automatically."
msgstr ""
"Iestatiet SELinux režīmā Enforcing, un sVirt vajadzētu izmantot automātiski."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:473
msgid ""
"All, or almost all, features of libguestfs should work under sVirt.  There "
"is one known shortcoming: L<virt-rescue(1)> will not use libvirt (hence "
"sVirt), but falls back to direct launch of qemu.  So you won't currently get "
"the benefit of sVirt protection when using virt-rescue."
msgstr ""
"Visiem vai gandrīz visiem libguestfs līdzekļiem vajadzētu darboties ar "
"sVirt.  Ir viens zināms trūkums: L<virt-rescue(1)> neizmantos libvirt (un "
"līdz ar to sVirt), bet atkāpsies uz qemu tiešu palaišanu.  Tāpēc, izmantojot "
"virt-rescue, pašlaik sVirt aizsardzība nebūs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:478
msgid ""
"You can check if sVirt is being used by enabling libvirtd logging (see "
"F</etc/libvirt/libvirtd.log>), killing and restarting libvirtd, and checking "
"the log files for S<\"Setting SELinux context on ...\"> messages."
msgstr ""
"Varat pārbaudīt, vai sVirt tiek izmantots, iespējojot libvirtd žurnalēšanu "
"(skatiet F</etc/libvirt/libvirtd.log>), nobeidzot un restartējot libvirtd un "
"pārbaudot žurnālu failos ziņojumus S<„Setting SELinux context on ...”>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:482
msgid ""
"In theory sVirt should support AppArmor, but we have not tried it.  It will "
"almost certainly require patching libvirt and writing an AppArmor policy."
msgstr ""
"Teorētiski sVirt vajadzētu atbalstīt AppArmor, taču mēs to neesam "
"izmēģinājuši.  Gandrīz noteikti būs jāielāpo libvirt un jāuzraksta AppArmor "
"politika."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:486
msgid "Libguestfs has a really long list of dependencies!"
msgstr "Libguestfs ir ļoti garš atkarību saraksts!"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:488
msgid ""
"The base library doesn't depend on very much, but there are three causes of "
"the long list of other dependencies:"
msgstr ""
"Pamata bibliotēka nav atkarīga no daudz kā, taču garajam citu atkarību "
"sarakstam ir trīs iemesli:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:493 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:720 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:926
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:381 docs/guestfs-performance.pod:165
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:207 docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:455
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:177 docs/internal-documentation.pod:195
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:306 docs/internal-documentation.pod:1362
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1488 lib/guestfs.pod:1603
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1943 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:410
msgid "1."
msgstr "1."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:495
msgid ""
"Libguestfs has to be able to read and edit many different disk formats.  For "
"example, XFS support requires XFS tools."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs jāspēj lasīt un rediģēt daudzus dažādus disku formātus.  "
"Piemēram, XFS atbalstam vajadzīgi XFS rīki."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:498 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:730 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:930
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:407 docs/guestfs-performance.pod:171
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:214 docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:461
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:181 docs/internal-documentation.pod:200
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:313 docs/internal-documentation.pod:1367
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1494 lib/guestfs.pod:1607
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1947 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:418
msgid "2."
msgstr "2."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:500
msgid ""
"There are language bindings for many different languages, all requiring "
"their own development tools.  All language bindings (except C) are optional."
msgstr ""
"Ir valodu saistījumi daudzām dažādām valodām, un katrai vajadzīgi savi "
"izstrādes rīki.  Visi valodu saistījumi (izņemot C) nav obligāti."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:504 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:735 docs/guestfs-faq.pod:934
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:419 docs/guestfs-performance.pod:220
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:467 docs/internal-documentation.pod:205
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:323 docs/internal-documentation.pod:1372
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1502 lib/guestfs.pod:1611
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1953 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:427
msgid "3."
msgstr "3."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:506
msgid "There are some optional library features which can be disabled."
msgstr "Ir daži neobligāti bibliotēkas līdzekļi, kurus var atspējot."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:510
msgid ""
"Since libguestfs E<ge> 1.26 it is possible to split up the appliance "
"dependencies (item 1 in the list above) and thus have (eg)  "
"C<libguestfs-xfs> as a separate subpackage for processing XFS disk images.  "
"We encourage downstream packagers to start splitting the base libguestfs "
"package into smaller subpackages."
msgstr ""
"Kopš libguestfs E<ge> 1.26 ir iespējams sadalīt palīgsistēmas atkarības "
"(iepriekšējā saraksta 1. punkts) un tādējādi, piemēram, C<libguestfs-xfs> "
"izveidot kā atsevišķu apakšpakotni XFS disku attēlu apstrādei.  Mudinām "
"pakārtotos pakotājus sākt sadalīt pamata libguestfs pakotni mazākās "
"apakšpakotnēs."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:516
msgid "Errors during launch on Fedora E<ge> 18, RHEL E<ge> 7"
msgstr "Kļūdas palaišanas laikā Fedora E<ge> 18, RHEL E<ge> 7"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:518
msgid ""
"In Fedora E<ge> 18 and RHEL E<ge> 7, libguestfs uses libvirt to manage the "
"appliance.  Previously (and upstream) libguestfs runs qemu directly:"
msgstr ""
"Fedora E<ge> 18 un RHEL E<ge> 7 libguestfs palīgsistēmas pārvaldībai izmanto "
"libvirt.  Iepriekš (un augštecē) libguestfs izpilda qemu tieši:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:522
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n"
" │ libguestfs                       │\n"
" ├────────────────┬─────────────────┤\n"
" │ direct backend │ libvirt backend │\n"
" └────────────────┴─────────────────┘\n"
"        ↓                  ↓\n"
"    ┌───────┐         ┌──────────┐\n"
"    │ qemu  │         │ libvirtd │\n"
"    └───────┘         └──────────┘\n"
"                           ↓\n"
"                       ┌───────┐\n"
"                       │ qemu  │\n"
"                       └───────┘\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n"
" │ libguestfs                       │\n"
" ├────────────────┬─────────────────┤\n"
" │ direct backend │ libvirt backend │\n"
" └────────────────┴─────────────────┘\n"
"        ↓                  ↓\n"
"    ┌───────┐         ┌──────────┐\n"
"    │ qemu  │         │ libvirtd │\n"
"    └───────┘         └──────────┘\n"
"                           ↓\n"
"                       ┌───────┐\n"
"                       │ qemu  │\n"
"                       └───────┘\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:536
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    upstream          Fedora 18+\n"
"    non-Fedora         RHEL 7+\n"
"    non-RHEL\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"    upstream          Fedora 18+\n"
"    non-Fedora         RHEL 7+\n"
"    non-RHEL\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:540
msgid ""
"The libvirt backend is more sophisticated, supporting SELinux/sVirt (see "
"above) and more.  It is, however, more complex and so less robust."
msgstr ""
"Libvirt aizmugursistēma ir sarežģītāka, atbalsta SELinux/sVirt (skatiet "
"iepriekš) u. c.  Tomēr tā ir sarežģītāka un tāpēc mazāk noturīga."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:544
msgid ""
"If you have permissions problems using the libvirt backend, you can switch "
"to the direct backend by setting this environment variable:"
msgstr ""
"Ja, izmantojot libvirt aizmugursistēmu, rodas atļauju problēmas, varat "
"pārslēgties uz tiešo aizmugursistēmu, iestatot šo vides mainīgo:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:549
msgid "before running any libguestfs program or virt tool."
msgstr "pirms jebkuras libguestfs programmas vai virt rīka izpildes."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:551
msgid "How can I switch to a fixed / prebuilt appliance?"
msgstr "Kā pārslēgties uz fiksētu / iepriekš uzbūvētu palīgsistēmu?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:553
msgid ""
"This may improve the stability and performance of libguestfs on Fedora and "
"RHEL."
msgstr "Tas var uzlabot libguestfs stabilitāti un veiktspēju Fedorā un RHEL."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:556
msgid "Any time after installing libguestfs, run the following commands as root:"
msgstr ""
"Jebkurā laikā pēc libguestfs instalēšanas kā root izpildiet šīs komandas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:559
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkdir -p /usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
" libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance /usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
" ls -l /usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkdir -p /usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
" libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance /usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
" ls -l /usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:563
msgid ""
"Now set the following environment variable before using libguestfs or any "
"virt tool:"
msgstr ""
"Tagad pirms libguestfs vai jebkura virt rīka izmantošanas iestatiet šo vides "
"mainīgo:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:568
msgid ""
"Of course you can change the path to any directory you want.  You can share "
"the appliance across machines that have the same architecture (eg. all "
"x86-64), but note that libvirt will prevent you from sharing the appliance "
"across NFS because of permissions problems (so either switch to the direct "
"backend or don't use NFS)."
msgstr ""
"Protams, ceļu var mainīt uz jebkuru vēlamo direktoriju.  Palīgsistēmu var "
"koplietot starp datoriem ar vienādu arhitektūru (piem., visiem x86-64), taču "
"ņemiet vērā, ka libvirt atļauju problēmu dēļ neļaus palīgsistēmu koplietot "
"caur NFS (tāpēc vai nu pārslēdzieties uz tiešo aizmugursistēmu, vai "
"neizmantojiet NFS)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:574
msgid "How can I speed up libguestfs builds?"
msgstr "Kā paātrināt libguestfs būves?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:576
msgid ""
"By far the most important thing you can do is to install and properly "
"configure Squid.  Note that the default configuration that ships with Squid "
"is rubbish, so configuring it is not optional."
msgstr ""
"Neapšaubāmi svarīgākais, ko varat darīt, ir instalēt un pareizi konfigurēt "
"Squid.  Ņemiet vērā, ka Squid noklusējuma konfigurācija ir nekam nederīga, "
"tāpēc tā konfigurēšana nav neobligāta."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:580
msgid ""
"A very good place to start with Squid configuration is here: "
"L<https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Extras/MockTricks#Using_Squid_to_Speed_Up_Mock_package_downloads>"
msgstr ""
"Ļoti laba vieta, kur sākt Squid konfigurēšanu, ir šeit: L<https://"
"fedoraproject.org/wiki/Extras/"
"MockTricks#Using_Squid_to_Speed_Up_Mock_package_downloads>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:583
msgid ""
"Make sure Squid is running, and that the environment variables "
"C<$http_proxy> and C<$ftp_proxy> are pointing to it."
msgstr ""
"Pārliecinieties, ka Squid darbojas un vides mainīgie C<$http_proxy> un "
"C<$ftp_proxy> norāda uz to."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:586
msgid ""
"With Squid running and correctly configured, appliance builds should be "
"reduced to a few minutes."
msgstr ""
"Ar darbojošos un pareizi konfigurētu Squid palīgsistēmas būvēm vajadzētu "
"samazināties līdz dažām minūtēm."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:589
msgid "How can I speed up libguestfs builds (Debian)?"
msgstr "Kā paātrināt libguestfs būves (Debian)?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:591
msgid ""
"Hilko Bengen suggests using \"approx\" which is a Debian archive proxy "
"(L<http://packages.debian.org/approx>).  This tool is documented on Debian "
"in the approx(8) manual page."
msgstr ""
"Hilko Bengen iesaka izmantot „approx” — Debian arhīva starpniekserveri "
"(L<http://packages.debian.org/approx>).  Šis rīks Debian ir dokumentēts "
"rokasgrāmatas lapā approx(8)."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:595
msgid "SPEED, DISK SPACE USED BY LIBGUESTFS"
msgstr "ĀTRUMS, LIBGUESTFS IZMANTOTĀ DISKA VIETA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:597
msgid ""
"B<Note:> Most of the information in this section has moved: "
"L<guestfs-performance(1)>."
msgstr ""
"B<Piezīme:> lielākā daļa šīs sadaļas informācijas ir pārvietota: L<guestfs-"
"performance(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:600
msgid "Upload or write seem very slow."
msgstr "Augšupielāde vai rakstīšana šķiet ļoti lēna."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:602
msgid ""
"If the underlying disk is not fully allocated (eg. sparse raw or qcow2) then "
"writes can be slow because the host operating system has to do costly disk "
"allocations while you are writing. The solution is to use a fully allocated "
"format instead, ie. non-sparse raw, or qcow2 with the "
"C<preallocation=metadata> option."
msgstr ""
"Ja pamatā esošais disks nav pilnībā piešķirts (piem., retināts raw vai qcow2)"
", rakstīšana var būt lēna, jo resursdatora operētājsistēmai rakstīšanas "
"laikā jāveic dārga diska vietas piešķiršana. Risinājums ir tā vietā izmantot "
"pilnībā piešķirtu formātu, t. i., neretinātu raw vai qcow2 ar opciju "
"C<preallocation=metadata>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:608
msgid "Libguestfs uses too much disk space!"
msgstr "Libguestfs izmanto pārāk daudz diska vietas!"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:610
msgid "libguestfs caches a large-ish appliance in:"
msgstr "libguestfs kešo diezgan lielu palīgsistēmu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:612
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /var/tmp/.guestfs-<UID>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /var/tmp/.guestfs-<UID>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:614
msgid ""
"If the environment variable C<TMPDIR> is defined, then "
"F<$TMPDIR/.guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>> is used instead."
msgstr ""
"Ja vides mainīgais C<TMPDIR> ir definēts, tā vietā tiek izmantots F<$TMPDIR/"
".guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:617
msgid "It is safe to delete this directory when you are not using libguestfs."
msgstr "Šo direktoriju var droši izdzēst, kad neizmantojat libguestfs."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:619
msgid ""
"virt-sparsify seems to make the image grow to the full size of the virtual "
"disk"
msgstr ""
"virt-sparsify šķietami palielina attēlu līdz pilnam virtuālā diska izmēram"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:622
msgid ""
"If the input to L<virt-sparsify(1)> is raw, then the output will be raw "
"sparse.  Make sure you are measuring the output with a tool which "
"understands sparseness such as C<du -sh>.  It can make a huge difference:"
msgstr ""
"Ja L<virt-sparsify(1)> ievade ir raw, izvade būs retināts raw.  "
"Pārliecinieties, ka izvadi mērāt ar rīku, kas saprot retinātību, piemēram, "
"C<du -sh>.  Atšķirība var būt milzīga:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:626
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ ls -lh test1.img\n"
" -rw-rw-r--. 1 rjones rjones 100M Aug  8 08:08 test1.img\n"
" $ du -sh test1.img\n"
" 3.6M\ttest1.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ ls -lh test1.img\n"
" -rw-rw-r--. 1 rjones rjones 100M Aug  8 08:08 test1.img\n"
" $ du -sh test1.img\n"
" 3.6M\ttest1.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:631
msgid "(Compare the apparent size B<100M> vs the actual size B<3.6M>)"
msgstr "(Salīdziniet šķietamo izmēru B<100M> ar faktisko izmēru B<3.6M>)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:633
msgid ""
"If all this confuses you, use a non-sparse output format by specifying the "
"I<--convert> option, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Ja tas viss jūs mulsina, izmantojiet neretinātu izvades formātu, norādot "
"opciju I<--convert>, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:636
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify --convert qcow2 disk.raw disk.qcow2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify --convert qcow2 disk.raw disk.qcow2\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:638
msgid "Why doesn't virt-resize work on the disk image in-place?"
msgstr "Kāpēc virt-resize nedarbojas ar diska attēlu uz vietas?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:640
msgid ""
"Resizing a disk image is very tricky -- especially making sure that you "
"don't lose data or break the bootloader.  The current method effectively "
"creates a new disk image and copies the data plus bootloader from the old "
"one.  If something goes wrong, you can always go back to the original."
msgstr ""
"Diska attēla izmēra maiņa ir ļoti sarežģīta — it īpaši, lai nezaudētu datus "
"un nesabojātu sāknētāju.  Pašreizējā metode faktiski izveido jaunu diska "
"attēlu un nokopē datus un sāknētāju no vecā.  Ja kaut kas noiet greizi, "
"vienmēr var atgriezties pie oriģināla."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:646
msgid ""
"If we were to make virt-resize work in-place then there would have to be "
"limitations: for example, you wouldn't be allowed to move existing "
"partitions (because moving data across the same disk is most likely to "
"corrupt data in the event of a power failure or crash), and LVM would be "
"very difficult to support (because of the almost arbitrary mapping between "
"LV content and underlying disk blocks)."
msgstr ""
"Ja virt-resize darbotos uz vietas, būtu jābūt ierobežojumiem: piemēram, "
"nedrīkstētu pārvietot esošos nodalījumus (jo datu pārvietošana tajā pašā "
"diskā, visticamāk, sabojātu datus strāvas zuduma vai avārijas gadījumā), un "
"LVM būtu ļoti grūti atbalstīt (gandrīz patvaļīgā kartējuma starp LV saturu "
"un pamatā esošajiem diska blokiem dēļ)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:653
msgid ""
"Another method we have considered is to place a snapshot over the original "
"disk image, so that the original data is untouched and only differences are "
"recorded in the snapshot.  You can do this today using C<qemu-img create> + "
"C<virt-resize>, but qemu currently isn't smart enough to recognize when the "
"same block is written back to the snapshot as already exists in the backing "
"disk, so you will find that this doesn't save you any space or time."
msgstr ""
"Vēl viena metode, ko esam apsvēruši, ir novietot momentuzņēmumu virs "
"oriģinālā diska attēla, lai oriģinālie dati paliktu neskarti un "
"momentuzņēmumā tiktu fiksētas tikai atšķirības.  To var izdarīt jau šodien, "
"izmantojot C<qemu-img create> + C<virt-resize>, taču qemu pašlaik nav "
"pietiekami gudrs, lai atpazītu, kad momentuzņēmumā tiek ierakstīts tas pats "
"bloks, kas jau ir pamatdiskā, tāpēc redzēsiet, ka tas neietaupa ne vietu, ne "
"laiku."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:661
msgid ""
"In summary, this is a hard problem, and what we have now mostly works so we "
"are reluctant to change it."
msgstr ""
"Kopsavilkumā — šī ir sarežģīta problēma, un tas, kas mums ir tagad, pārsvarā "
"darbojas, tāpēc nelabprāt to mainām."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:664
msgid "Why doesn't virt-sparsify work on the disk image in-place?"
msgstr "Kāpēc virt-sparsify nedarbojas ar diska attēlu uz vietas?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:666
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.26, virt-sparsify can now work on disk images in "
"place.  Use:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.26 virt-sparsify tagad var strādāt ar disku attēliem uz "
"vietas.  Izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:669
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify --in-place disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify --in-place disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:671
msgid "But first you should read L<virt-sparsify(1)/IN-PLACE SPARSIFICATION>."
msgstr "Taču vispirms izlasiet L<virt-sparsify(1)/RETINĀŠANA UZ VIETAS>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:673
msgid "PROBLEMS OPENING DISK IMAGES"
msgstr "PROBLĒMAS, ATVEROT DISKU ATTĒLUS"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:675
msgid "Remote libvirt guests cannot be opened."
msgstr "Attālos libvirt viesus nevar atvērt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:677
msgid ""
"Opening remote libvirt guests is not supported at this time.  For example "
"this won't work:"
msgstr ""
"Attālu libvirt viesu atvēršana pašlaik netiek atbalstīta.  Piemēram, šis "
"nedarbosies:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:680
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -c qemu://remote/system -d Guest\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -c qemu://remote/system -d Guest\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:682
msgid ""
"To open remote disks you have to export them somehow, then connect to the "
"export.  For example if you decided to use NBD:"
msgstr ""
"Lai atvērtu attālus diskus, tie kaut kā jāeksportē un pēc tam jāsavienojas "
"ar eksportu.  Piemēram, ja nolēmāt izmantot NBD:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:685
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" remote$ qemu-nbd -t -p 10809 guest.img\n"
"  local$ guestfish -a nbd://remote:10809 -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" remote$ qemu-nbd -t -p 10809 guest.img\n"
"  local$ guestfish -a nbd://remote:10809 -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:688
msgid ""
"Other possibilities include ssh (if qemu is recent enough), NFS or iSCSI.  "
"See L<guestfs(3)/REMOTE STORAGE>."
msgstr ""
"Citas iespējas ietver ssh (ja qemu ir pietiekami jauns), NFS vai iSCSI.  "
"Skatiet L<guestfs(3)/ATTĀLĀ KRĀTUVE>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:691
msgid "How can I open this strange disk source?"
msgstr "Kā atvērt šo dīvaino diska avotu?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:693
msgid ""
"You have a disk image located inside another system that requires access via "
"a library / HTTP / REST / proprietary API, or is compressed or archived in "
"some way.  (One example would be remote access to OpenStack glance images "
"without actually downloading them.)"
msgstr ""
"Jums ir diska attēls citā sistēmā, kam piekļuvei vajadzīga bibliotēka / "
"HTTP / REST / patentēta API, vai kas ir kaut kā saspiests vai arhivēts.  "
"(Viens piemērs būtu attāla piekļuve OpenStack glance attēliem, tos faktiski "
"nelejupielādējot.)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:698
msgid ""
"We have a sister project called nbdkit "
"(L<https://github.com/libguestfs/nbdkit>).  This project lets you turn any "
"disk source into an NBD server.  Libguestfs can access NBD servers directly, "
"eg:"
msgstr ""
"Mums ir māsas projekts nbdkit (L<https://github.com/libguestfs/nbdkit>).  "
"Šis projekts ļauj jebkuru diska avotu pārvērst par NBD serveri.  Libguestfs "
"var piekļūt NBD serveriem tieši, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:703
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a nbd://remote\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a nbd://remote\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:705
msgid ""
"nbdkit is liberally licensed, so you can link it to or include it in "
"proprietary libraries and code.  It also has a simple, stable plugin API so "
"you can easily write plugins against the API which will continue to work in "
"future."
msgstr ""
"nbdkit ir licencēts liberāli, tāpēc to var saistīt ar patentētām bibliotēkām "
"un kodu vai iekļaut tajos.  Tam ir arī vienkārša, stabila spraudņu API, "
"tāpēc var viegli rakstīt spraudņus šai API, kas turpinās darboties arī "
"nākotnē."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:710
msgid ""
"Error opening VMDK disks: \"uses a vmdk feature which is not supported by "
"this qemu version: VMDK version 3\""
msgstr ""
"Kļūda, atverot VMDK diskus: „uses a vmdk feature which is not supported by "
"this qemu version: VMDK version 3”"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:712
msgid ""
"Qemu (and hence libguestfs) only supports certain VMDK disk images.  Others "
"won't work, giving this or similar errors."
msgstr ""
"Qemu (un līdz ar to libguestfs) atbalsta tikai noteiktus VMDK disku "
"attēlus.  Citi nedarbosies, izraisot šo vai līdzīgas kļūdas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:715
msgid ""
"Ideally someone would fix qemu to support the latest VMDK features, but in "
"the meantime you have three options:"
msgstr ""
"Ideālā gadījumā kāds izlabotu qemu, lai atbalstītu jaunākos VMDK līdzekļus, "
"bet pagaidām jums ir trīs iespējas:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:722
msgid ""
"If the guest is hosted on a live, reachable ESX server, then locate and "
"download the disk image called F<I<somename>-flat.vmdk>.  Despite the name, "
"this is a raw disk image, and can be opened by anything."
msgstr ""
"Ja viesis atrodas darbojošā, sasniedzamā ESX serverī, atrodiet un "
"lejupielādējiet diska attēlu ar nosaukumu F<I<somename>-flat.vmdk>.  "
"Neskatoties uz nosaukumu, tas ir raw diska attēls, un to var atvērt jebkas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:726
msgid ""
"If you have a recent enough version of qemu and libguestfs, then you may be "
"able to access this disk image remotely using either HTTPS or ssh.  See "
"L<guestfs(3)/REMOTE STORAGE>."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir pietiekami jauna qemu un libguestfs versija, šim diska attēlam, "
"iespējams, var piekļūt attāli caur HTTPS vai ssh.  Skatiet L<guestfs(3)/"
"ATTĀLĀ KRĀTUVE>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:732
msgid ""
"Use VMware’s proprietary vdiskmanager tool to convert the image to raw "
"format."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet VMware patentēto rīku vdiskmanager, lai pārveidotu attēlu raw "
"formātā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:737
msgid ""
"Use nbdkit with the proprietary VDDK plugin to live export the disk image as "
"an NBD source.  This should allow you to read and write the VMDK file."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet nbdkit ar patentēto VDDK spraudni, lai tiešsaistē eksportētu "
"diska attēlu kā NBD avotu.  Tam vajadzētu ļaut lasīt un rakstīt VMDK failu."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:743
msgid "UFS disks (as used by BSD) cannot be opened."
msgstr "UFS diskus (ko izmanto BSD) nevar atvērt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:745
msgid ""
"The UFS filesystem format has many variants, and these are not "
"self-identifying.  The Linux kernel has to be told which variant of UFS it "
"has to use, which libguestfs cannot know."
msgstr ""
"UFS failu sistēmas formātam ir daudz variantu, un tie sevi neidentificē.  "
"Linux kodolam jāpasaka, kuru UFS variantu izmantot, ko libguestfs nevar "
"zināt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:749
msgid ""
"You have to pass the right C<ufstype> mount option when mounting these "
"filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Montējot šīs failu sistēmas, jānodod pareizā montēšanas opcija C<ufstype>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:752
msgid "See L<https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/filesystems/ufs.txt>"
msgstr "Skatiet L<https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/filesystems/ufs.txt>"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:754
msgid "Windows ReFS"
msgstr "Windows ReFS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:756
msgid ""
"Windows ReFS is Microsoft’s ZFS/Btrfs copy.  This filesystem has not yet "
"been reverse engineered and implemented in the Linux kernel, and therefore "
"libguestfs doesn't support it.  At the moment it seems to be very rare \"in "
"the wild\"."
msgstr ""
"Windows ReFS ir Microsoft ZFS/Btrfs kopija.  Šī failu sistēma vēl nav "
"apgriezti izpētīta un realizēta Linux kodolā, tāpēc libguestfs to "
"neatbalsta.  Pašlaik šķiet, ka „savvaļā” tā ir ļoti reta."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:761
msgid "Non-ASCII characters don’t appear on VFAT filesystems."
msgstr "VFAT failu sistēmās neparādās ne-ASCII rakstzīmes."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:763
msgid "Typical symptoms of this problem:"
msgstr "Tipiski šīs problēmas simptomi:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:769
msgid ""
"You get an error when you create a file where the filename contains "
"non-ASCII characters, particularly non 8-bit characters from Asian languages "
"(Chinese, Japanese, etc).  The filesystem is VFAT."
msgstr ""
"Veidojot failu, kura nosaukums satur ne-ASCII rakstzīmes, it īpaši ne-8 bitu "
"rakstzīmes no Āzijas valodām (ķīniešu, japāņu u. c.), rodas kļūda.  Failu "
"sistēma ir VFAT."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:775
msgid ""
"When you list a directory from a VFAT filesystem, filenames appear as "
"question marks."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitot VFAT failu sistēmas direktoriju, failu nosaukumi parādās kā "
"jautājuma zīmes."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:780
msgid "This is a design flaw of the GNU/Linux system."
msgstr "Šī ir GNU/Linux sistēmas projektēšanas kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:782
msgid ""
"VFAT stores long filenames as UTF-16 characters.  When opening or returning "
"filenames, the Linux kernel has to translate these to some form of 8 bit "
"string.  UTF-8 would be the obvious choice, except for Linux users who "
"persist in using non-UTF-8 locales (the user’s locale is not known to the "
"kernel because it’s a function of libc)."
msgstr ""
"VFAT garos failu nosaukumus glabā kā UTF-16 rakstzīmes.  Atverot vai "
"atgriežot failu nosaukumus, Linux kodolam tie jāpārvērš kāda veida 8 bitu "
"virknē.  UTF-8 būtu acīmredzamā izvēle, ja ne Linux lietotāji, kas joprojām "
"izmanto ne-UTF-8 lokāles (lietotāja lokāle kodolam nav zināma, jo tā ir libc "
"funkcija)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:788
msgid ""
"Therefore you have to tell the kernel what translation you want done when "
"you mount the filesystem.  The two methods are the C<iocharset> parameter "
"(which is not relevant to libguestfs) and the C<utf8> flag."
msgstr ""
"Tāpēc, montējot failu sistēmu, kodolam jāpasaka, kādu pārveidojumu "
"vēlaties.  Divas metodes ir parametrs C<iocharset> (kas nav būtisks "
"libguestfs) un karogs C<utf8>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:792
msgid ""
"So to use a VFAT filesystem you must add the C<utf8> flag when mounting.  "
"From guestfish, use:"
msgstr ""
"Tātad, lai izmantotu VFAT failu sistēmu, montējot jāpievieno karogs C<utf8>"
".  No guestfish izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:795
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> mount-options utf8 /dev/sda1 /\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> mount-options utf8 /dev/sda1 /\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:797
msgid "or on the guestfish command line:"
msgstr "vai guestfish komandrindā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:799
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish [...] -m /dev/sda1:/:utf8\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish [...] -m /dev/sda1:/:utf8\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:801
msgid "or from the API:"
msgstr "vai no API:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:803
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_mount_options (g, \"utf8\", \"/dev/sda1\", \"/\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_mount_options (g, \"utf8\", \"/dev/sda1\", \"/\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:805
msgid "The kernel will then translate filenames to and from UTF-8 strings."
msgstr "Pēc tam kodols pārveidos failu nosaukumus uz UTF-8 virknēm un no tām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:807
msgid ""
"We considered adding this mount option transparently, but unfortunately "
"there are several problems with doing that:"
msgstr ""
"Mēs apsvērām šīs montēšanas opcijas pievienošanu pārredzami, taču diemžēl "
"tam ir vairākas problēmas:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:814
msgid ""
"On some Linux systems, the C<utf8> mount option doesn't work.  We don't "
"precisely understand what systems or why, but this was reliably reported by "
"one user."
msgstr ""
"Dažās Linux sistēmās montēšanas opcija C<utf8> nedarbojas.  Mēs precīzi "
"nesaprotam, kurās sistēmās un kāpēc, taču par to uzticami ziņoja viens "
"lietotājs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:820
msgid ""
"It would prevent you from using the C<iocharset> parameter because it is "
"incompatible with C<utf8>.  It is probably not a good idea to use this "
"parameter, but we don't want to prevent it."
msgstr ""
"Tas neļautu izmantot parametru C<iocharset>, jo tas nav saderīgs ar C<utf8>"
".  Šo parametru droši vien nav ieteicams izmantot, taču nevēlamies to liegt."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:826
msgid "Non-ASCII characters appear as underscore (_) on ISO9660 filesystems."
msgstr "ISO9660 failu sistēmās ne-ASCII rakstzīmes parādās kā pasvītra (_)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:828
msgid ""
"The filesystem was not prepared correctly with mkisofs or genisoimage.  Make "
"sure the filesystem was created using Joliet and/or Rock Ridge extensions.  "
"libguestfs does not require any special mount options to handle the "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēma nav pareizi sagatavota ar mkisofs vai genisoimage.  "
"Pārliecinieties, ka failu sistēma izveidota ar Joliet un/vai Rock Ridge "
"paplašinājumiem.  Libguestfs failu sistēmas apstrādei nav vajadzīgas nekādas "
"īpašas montēšanas opcijas."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:833
msgid "Cannot open Windows guests which use NTFS."
msgstr "Nevar atvērt Windows viesus, kas izmanto NTFS."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:835
msgid "You see errors like:"
msgstr "Redzat šādas kļūdas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:837
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount: unknown filesystem type 'ntfs'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount: unknown filesystem type 'ntfs'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:839
msgid ""
"On Red Hat Enterprise Linux or CentOS E<lt> 7.2, you have to install the "
"L<libguestfs-winsupport|https://people.redhat.com/~rjones/libguestfs-winsupport/> "
"package.  In RHEL E<ge> 7.2, C<libguestfs-winsupport> is part of the base "
"RHEL distribution, but see the next question."
msgstr ""
"Red Hat Enterprise Linux vai CentOS E<lt> 7.2 jāinstalē pakotne L<libguestfs-"
"winsupport|https://people.redhat.com/~rjones/libguestfs-winsupport/>.  RHEL "
"E<ge> 7.2 C<libguestfs-winsupport> ir daļa no pamata RHEL distribūcijas, "
"taču skatiet nākamo jautājumu."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:845
msgid "\"mount: unsupported filesystem type\" with NTFS in RHEL E<ge> 7.2"
msgstr "„mount: unsupported filesystem type” ar NTFS RHEL E<ge> 7.2"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:847
msgid ""
"In RHEL 7.2 we were able to add C<libguestfs-winsupport> to the base RHEL "
"distribution, but we had to disable the ability to use it for opening and "
"editing filesystems.  It is only supported when used with L<virt-v2v(1)>.  "
"If you try to use L<guestfish(1)> or L<guestmount(1)> or some other programs "
"on an NTFS filesystem, you will see the error:"
msgstr ""
"RHEL 7.2 mēs varējām pievienot C<libguestfs-winsupport> pamata RHEL "
"distribūcijai, taču nācās atspējot iespēju to izmantot failu sistēmu "
"atvēršanai un rediģēšanai.  Tas tiek atbalstīts tikai, izmantojot ar L<virt-"
"v2v(1)>.  Ja mēģināsiet izmantot L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestmount(1)> vai citas "
"programmas ar NTFS failu sistēmu, redzēsiet kļūdu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:853
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount: unsupported filesystem type\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount: unsupported filesystem type\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:855
msgid ""
"This is not a supported configuration, and it will not be made to work in "
"RHEL.  Don't bother to open a bug about it, as it will be immediately "
"C<CLOSED -E<gt> WONTFIX>."
msgstr ""
"Šī nav atbalstīta konfigurācija, un RHEL tā netiks padarīta darbspējīga.  "
"Neveidojiet par to kļūdas ziņojumu, jo tas uzreiz tiks slēgts kā C<CLOSED -"
"E<gt> WONTFIX>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:859
msgid ""
"You may L<compile your own libguestfs removing this "
"restriction|https://www.redhat.com/archives/libguestfs/2016-February/msg00145.html>, "
"but that won't be endorsed or supported by Red Hat."
msgstr ""
"Varat L<kompilēt savu libguestfs, noņemot šo ierobežojumu|https://"
"www.redhat.com/archives/libguestfs/2016-February/msg00145.html>, taču Red "
"Hat to neatbalstīs un neapstiprinās."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:863
msgid "Cannot open or inspect RHEL 7 guests."
msgstr "Nevar atvērt vai inspicēt RHEL 7 viesus."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:865
msgid "Cannot open Linux guests which use XFS."
msgstr "Nevar atvērt Linux viesus, kas izmanto XFS."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:867
msgid ""
"RHEL 7 guests, and any other guests that use XFS, can be opened by "
"libguestfs, but you have to install the C<libguestfs-xfs> package."
msgstr ""
"RHEL 7 viesus un jebkurus citus viesus, kas izmanto XFS, libguestfs var "
"atvērt, taču jāinstalē pakotne C<libguestfs-xfs>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:870
msgid "USING LIBGUESTFS IN YOUR OWN PROGRAMS"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS IZMANTOŠANA SAVĀS PROGRAMMĀS"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:872
msgid "The API has hundreds of methods, where do I start?"
msgstr "API ir simtiem metožu, ar ko sākt?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:874
msgid ""
"We recommend you start by reading the API overview: L<guestfs(3)/API "
"OVERVIEW>."
msgstr "Iesakām sākt ar API pārskata izlasīšanu: L<guestfs(3)/API PĀRSKATS>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:877
msgid ""
"Although the API overview covers the C API, it is still worth reading even "
"if you are going to use another programming language, because the API is the "
"same, just with simple logical changes to the names of the calls:"
msgstr ""
"Lai gan API pārskats aptver C API, to tomēr vērts izlasīt, pat ja "
"izmantosiet citu programmēšanas valodu, jo API ir tā pati, tikai ar "
"vienkāršām loģiskām izmaiņām izsaukumu nosaukumos:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:882
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                  C  guestfs_ln_sf (g, target, linkname);\n"
"             Python  g.ln_sf (target, linkname);\n"
"              OCaml  g#ln_sf target linkname;\n"
"               Perl  $g->ln_sf (target, linkname);\n"
"  Shell (guestfish)  ln-sf target linkname\n"
"                PHP  guestfs_ln_sf ($g, $target, $linkname);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"                  C  guestfs_ln_sf (g, target, linkname);\n"
"             Python  g.ln_sf (target, linkname);\n"
"              OCaml  g#ln_sf target linkname;\n"
"               Perl  $g->ln_sf (target, linkname);\n"
"  Shell (guestfish)  ln-sf target linkname\n"
"                PHP  guestfs_ln_sf ($g, $target, $linkname);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:889
msgid ""
"Once you're familiar with the API overview, you should look at this list of "
"starting points for other language bindings: L<guestfs(3)/USING LIBGUESTFS "
"WITH OTHER PROGRAMMING LANGUAGES>."
msgstr ""
"Kad API pārskats ir pazīstams, apskatiet šo citu valodu saistījumu "
"sākumpunktu sarakstu: L<guestfs(3)/LIBGUESTFS IZMANTOŠANA AR CITĀM "
"PROGRAMMĒŠANAS VALODĀM>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:893
msgid "Can I use libguestfs in my proprietary / closed source / commercial program?"
msgstr ""
"Vai varu izmantot libguestfs savā patentētajā / slēgtā pirmkoda / "
"komerciālajā programmā?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:896
msgid ""
"In general, yes.  However this is not legal advice - read the license that "
"comes with libguestfs, and if you have specific questions contact a lawyer."
msgstr ""
"Kopumā jā.  Tomēr šis nav juridisks padoms — izlasiet ar libguestfs "
"piegādāto licenci, un, ja jums ir konkrēti jautājumi, sazinieties ar juristu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:900
msgid ""
"In the source tree the license is in the file C<COPYING.LIB> (LGPLv2+ for "
"the library and bindings) and C<COPYING> (GPLv2+ for the standalone "
"programs)."
msgstr ""
"Pirmkoda kokā licence ir failā C<COPYING.LIB> (LGPLv2+ bibliotēkai un "
"saistījumiem) un C<COPYING> (GPLv2+ atsevišķajām programmām)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:906
msgid "<!-- old anchor for the next section --> <a name=\"debug\"/>"
msgstr "<!-- old anchor for the next section --> <a name=\"debug\"/>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:911
msgid "DEBUGGING LIBGUESTFS"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS ATKĻŪDOŠANA"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:913
msgid "Help, it’s not working!"
msgstr "Palīgā, tas nedarbojas!"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:915
msgid ""
"If no libguestfs program seems to work at all, run the program below and "
"paste the B<complete, unedited> output into an email to "
"C<guestfs@lists.libguestfs.org>:"
msgstr ""
"Ja šķiet, ka neviena libguestfs programma nedarbojas vispār, izpildiet tālāk "
"norādīto programmu un ielīmējiet B<pilnu, nerediģētu> izvadi e-pastā uz "
"C<guestfs@lists.libguestfs.org>:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:921
msgid ""
"If a particular operation fails, supply all the information in this "
"checklist, in an email to C<libguestfs> @ C<redhat.com>:"
msgstr ""
"Ja neizdodas konkrēta darbība, sniedziet visu šajā pārbaudes sarakstā minēto "
"informāciju e-pastā uz C<libguestfs> @ C<redhat.com>:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:928
msgid "What are you trying to do?"
msgstr "Ko mēģināt darīt?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:932
msgid "What exact command(s) did you run?"
msgstr "Kuru(-as) tieši komandu(-as) izpildījāt?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:936
msgid "What was the precise error or output of these commands?"
msgstr "Kāda bija šo komandu precīza kļūda vai izvade?"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:938 docs/internal-documentation.pod:209
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:333 docs/internal-documentation.pod:1512
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:436
msgid "4."
msgstr "4."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:940
msgid ""
"Enable debugging, run the commands again, and capture the B<complete> "
"output.  B<Do not edit the output.>"
msgstr ""
"Iespējojiet atkļūdošanu, izpildiet komandas vēlreiz un saglabājiet B<pilnu> "
"izvadi.  B<Nerediģējiet izvadi.>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:943
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1\n"
" export LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1\n"
" export LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:946 docs/internal-documentation.pod:338
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1522 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:444
msgid "5."
msgstr "5."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:948
msgid ""
"Include the version of libguestfs, the operating system version, and how you "
"installed libguestfs (eg. from source, C<yum install>, etc.)"
msgstr ""
"Norādiet libguestfs versiju, operētājsistēmas versiju un to, kā instalējāt "
"libguestfs (piem., no pirmkoda, C<yum install> u. c.)"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:953
msgid ""
"How do I debug when using any libguestfs program or tool (eg. virt-customize "
"or virt-df)?"
msgstr ""
"Kā atkļūdot, izmantojot jebkuru libguestfs programmu vai rīku (piem., virt-"
"customize vai virt-df)?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:956
msgid ""
"There are two C<LIBGUESTFS_*> environment variables you can set in order to "
"get more information from libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Ir divi C<LIBGUESTFS_*> vides mainīgie, ko var iestatīt, lai iegūtu vairāk "
"informācijas no libguestfs."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:961
msgid "C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE>"
msgstr "C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:963
msgid ""
"Set this to 1 and libguestfs will print out each command / API call in a "
"format which is similar to guestfish commands."
msgstr ""
"Iestatiet to uz 1, un libguestfs izdrukās katru komandu / API izsaukumu "
"formātā, kas līdzīgs guestfish komandām."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:966
msgid "C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG>"
msgstr "C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:968
msgid ""
"Set this to 1 in order to enable massive amounts of debug messages.  If you "
"think there is some problem inside the libguestfs appliance, then you should "
"use this option."
msgstr ""
"Iestatiet to uz 1, lai iespējotu milzīgu daudzumu atkļūdošanas ziņojumu.  Ja "
"domājat, ka problēma ir libguestfs palīgsistēmā, izmantojiet šo opciju."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:974
msgid "To set these from the shell, do this before running the program:"
msgstr "Lai tos iestatītu no čaulas, pirms programmas izpildes izpildiet šo:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:976
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1\n"
" export LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1\n"
" export LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:979
msgid "For csh/tcsh the equivalent commands would be:"
msgstr "csh/tcsh ekvivalentās komandas būtu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:981
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" setenv LIBGUESTFS_TRACE 1\n"
" setenv LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG 1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" setenv LIBGUESTFS_TRACE 1\n"
" setenv LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG 1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:984
msgid "For further information, see: L<guestfs(3)/ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES>."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju skatiet: L<guestfs(3)/VIDES MAINĪGIE>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:986
msgid "How do I debug when using guestfish?"
msgstr "Kā atkļūdot, izmantojot guestfish?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:988
msgid ""
"You can use the same environment variables above.  Alternatively use the "
"guestfish options -x (to trace commands) or -v (to get the full debug "
"output), or both."
msgstr ""
"Varat izmantot tos pašus iepriekš minētos vides mainīgos.  Vai arī "
"izmantojiet guestfish opcijas -x (komandu izsekošanai) vai -v (pilnas "
"atkļūdošanas izvades iegūšanai) vai abas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:992
msgid "For further information, see: L<guestfish(1)>."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju skatiet: L<guestfish(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:994
msgid "How do I debug when using the API?"
msgstr "Kā atkļūdot, izmantojot API?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:996
msgid ""
"Call L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_trace> to enable command traces, and/or "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_verbose> to enable debug messages."
msgstr ""
"Izsauciet L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_trace>, lai iespējotu komandu izsekošanu, "
"un/vai L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_verbose>, lai iespējotu atkļūdošanas "
"ziņojumus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:999
msgid ""
"For best results, call these functions as early as possible, just after "
"creating the guestfs handle if you can, and definitely before calling "
"launch."
msgstr ""
"Labākiem rezultātiem izsauciet šīs funkcijas pēc iespējas agrāk, ja "
"iespējams, tūlīt pēc guestfs roktura izveides, un noteikti pirms launch "
"izsaukšanas."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1003
msgid "How do I capture debug output and put it into my logging system?"
msgstr "Kā tvert atkļūdošanas izvadi un ievietot to savā žurnalēšanas sistēmā?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1005
msgid ""
"Use the event API.  For examples, see: L<guestfs(3)/SETTING CALLBACKS TO "
"HANDLE EVENTS> and the F<examples/debug-logging.c> program in the libguestfs "
"sources."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet notikumu API.  Piemērus skatiet: L<guestfs(3)/ATZVANU "
"IESTATĪŠANA NOTIKUMU APSTRĀDEI> un programmā F<examples/debug-logging.c> "
"libguestfs pirmkodā."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1009
msgid "Digging deeper into the appliance boot process."
msgstr "Dziļāka palīgsistēmas sāknēšanas procesa izpēte."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1011
msgid ""
"Enable debugging and then read this documentation on the appliance boot "
"process: L<guestfs-internals(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Iespējojiet atkļūdošanu un pēc tam izlasiet šo dokumentāciju par "
"palīgsistēmas sāknēšanas procesu: L<guestfs-internals(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1014
msgid "libguestfs hangs or fails during run/launch."
msgstr "libguestfs uzkaras vai neizdodas run/launch laikā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1016
msgid ""
"Enable debugging and look at the full output.  If you cannot work out what "
"is going on, file a bug report, including the I<complete> output of "
"L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Iespējojiet atkļūdošanu un apskatiet pilnu izvadi.  Ja nevarat saprast, kas "
"notiek, iesniedziet kļūdas ziņojumu, iekļaujot I<pilnu> L<libguestfs-test-"
"tool(1)> izvadi."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1020
msgid "Debugging libvirt"
msgstr "Libvirt atkļūdošana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1022
msgid ""
"If you are using the libvirt backend, and libvirt is failing, then you can "
"enable debugging by editing F</etc/libvirt/libvirtd.conf>."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat libvirt aizmugursistēmu un libvirt neizdodas, atkļūdošanu var "
"iespējot, rediģējot F</etc/libvirt/libvirtd.conf>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1025
msgid ""
"If you are running as non-root, then you have to edit a different file.  "
"Create F<~/.config/libvirt/libvirtd.conf> containing:"
msgstr ""
"Ja darbojaties ne kā root, jārediģē cits fails.  Izveidojiet F<~/.config/"
"libvirt/libvirtd.conf> ar šādu saturu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1028
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" log_level=1\n"
" log_outputs=\"1:file:/tmp/libvirtd.log\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" log_level=1\n"
" log_outputs=\"1:file:/tmp/libvirtd.log\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1031
msgid ""
"Kill any session (non-root) libvirtd that is running, and next time you run "
"the libguestfs command, you should see a large amount of useful debugging "
"information from libvirtd in F</tmp/libvirtd.log>"
msgstr ""
"Nobeidziet jebkuru darbojošos sesijas (ne-root) libvirtd, un nākamreiz, "
"izpildot libguestfs komandu, failā F</tmp/libvirtd.log> vajadzētu redzēt "
"daudz noderīgas atkļūdošanas informācijas no libvirtd"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1035
msgid "Broken kernel, or trying a different kernel."
msgstr "Bojāts kodols vai cita kodola izmēģināšana."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1037
msgid ""
"You can choose a different kernel for the appliance by setting some "
"L<supermin environment variables|supermin(8)/ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES>:"
msgstr ""
"Palīgsistēmai var izvēlēties citu kodolu, iestatot dažus L<supermin vides "
"mainīgos|supermin(8)/ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1040
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION=4.8.0-1.fc25.x86_64\n"
" export SUPERMIN_KERNEL=/boot/vmlinuz-$SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION\n"
" export SUPERMIN_MODULES=/lib/modules/$SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION\n"
" rm -rf /var/tmp/.guestfs-*\n"
" libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION=4.8.0-1.fc25.x86_64\n"
" export SUPERMIN_KERNEL=/boot/vmlinuz-$SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION\n"
" export SUPERMIN_MODULES=/lib/modules/$SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION\n"
" rm -rf /var/tmp/.guestfs-*\n"
" libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1046
msgid "Broken qemu, or trying a different qemu."
msgstr "Bojāts qemu vai cita qemu izmēģināšana."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1048
msgid ""
"You can choose a different qemu by setting the hypervisor L<environment "
"variable|guestfs(3)/ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES>:"
msgstr ""
"Citu qemu var izvēlēties, iestatot hipervizora L<vides mainīgo|guestfs(3)/"
"ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1051
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_HV=/path/to/qemu-system-x86_64\n"
" libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_HV=/path/to/qemu-system-x86_64\n"
" libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1054
msgid "DESIGN/INTERNALS OF LIBGUESTFS"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS UZBŪVE/IEKŠĒJĀ DARBĪBA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1056
msgid "See also L<guestfs-internals(1)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<guestfs-internals(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1058
msgid "Why don’t you do everything through the FUSE / filesystem interface?"
msgstr "Kāpēc jūs nedarāt visu caur FUSE / failu sistēmas saskarni?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1061
msgid ""
"We offer a command called L<guestmount(1)> which lets you mount guest "
"filesystems on the host.  This is implemented as a FUSE module.  Why don't "
"we just implement the whole of libguestfs using this mechanism, instead of "
"having the large and rather complicated API?"
msgstr ""
"Mēs piedāvājam komandu L<guestmount(1)>, kas ļauj montēt viesu failu "
"sistēmas resursdatorā.  Tā ir realizēta kā FUSE modulis.  Kāpēc nerealizējam "
"visu libguestfs ar šo mehānismu, nevis ar lielo un diezgan sarežģīto API?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1066
msgid ""
"The reasons are twofold.  Firstly, libguestfs offers API calls for doing "
"things like creating and deleting partitions and logical volumes, which "
"don't fit into a filesystem model very easily.  Or rather, you could fit "
"them in: for example, creating a partition could be mapped to C<mkdir "
"/fs/hda1> but then you'd have to specify some method to choose the size of "
"the partition (maybe C<echo 100M E<gt> /fs/hda1/.size>), and the partition "
"type, start and end sectors etc., but once you've done that the "
"filesystem-based API starts to look more complicated than the call-based API "
"we currently have."
msgstr ""
"Iemesli ir divējādi.  Pirmkārt, libguestfs piedāvā API izsaukumus tādām "
"darbībām kā nodalījumu un loģisko sējumu izveide un dzēšana, kas nav viegli "
"iekļaujamas failu sistēmas modelī.  Precīzāk, tās varētu iekļaut: piemēram, "
"nodalījuma izveidi varētu kartēt uz C<mkdir /fs/hda1>, taču tad būtu "
"jānorāda kāda metode nodalījuma izmēra izvēlei (varbūt C<echo 100M E<gt> /fs/"
"hda1/.size>), nodalījuma tipam, sākuma un beigu sektoriem u. c., bet, kad "
"tas izdarīts, uz failu sistēmu balstītā API sāk izskatīties sarežģītāka nekā "
"mūsu pašreizējā uz izsaukumiem balstītā API."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1076
msgid ""
"The second reason is for efficiency.  FUSE itself is reasonably efficient, "
"but it does make lots of small, independent calls into the FUSE module.  In "
"guestmount these have to be translated into messages to the libguestfs "
"appliance which has a big overhead (in time and round trips).  For example, "
"reading a file in 64 KB chunks is inefficient because each chunk would turn "
"into a single round trip.  In the libguestfs API it is much more efficient "
"to download an entire file or directory through one of the streaming calls "
"like C<guestfs_download> or C<guestfs_tar_out>."
msgstr ""
"Otrs iemesls ir efektivitāte.  FUSE pats par sevi ir pietiekami efektīvs, "
"taču tas veic daudz mazu, neatkarīgu izsaukumu FUSE modulī.  Guestmount tie "
"jāpārveido ziņojumos libguestfs palīgsistēmai, kam ir lielas papildizmaksas "
"(laikā un turp-atpakaļ apmaiņās).  Piemēram, faila lasīšana 64 KB gabalos ir "
"neefektīva, jo katrs gabals pārvērstos vienā turp-atpakaļ apmaiņā.  "
"Libguestfs API daudz efektīvāk ir lejupielādēt visu failu vai direktoriju ar "
"kādu no straumēšanas izsaukumiem, piemēram, C<guestfs_download> vai "
"C<guestfs_tar_out>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1086
msgid "Why don’t you do everything through GVFS?"
msgstr "Kāpēc jūs nedarāt visu caur GVFS?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1088
msgid "The problems are similar to the problems with FUSE."
msgstr "Problēmas ir līdzīgas FUSE problēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1090
msgid ""
"GVFS is a better abstraction than POSIX/FUSE.  There is an FTP backend for "
"GVFS, which is encouraging because FTP is conceptually similar to the "
"libguestfs API.  However the GVFS FTP backend makes multiple simultaneous "
"connections in order to keep interactivity, which we can't easily do with "
"libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"GVFS ir labāka abstrakcija nekā POSIX/FUSE.  GVFS ir FTP aizmugursistēma, "
"kas ir iepriecinoši, jo FTP konceptuāli ir līdzīgs libguestfs API.  Tomēr "
"GVFS FTP aizmugursistēma interaktivitātes saglabāšanai veido vairākus "
"vienlaicīgus savienojumus, ko ar libguestfs nevaram viegli izdarīt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1098
msgid "<!-- old anchor for the next section --> <a name=\"backup\"/>"
msgstr "<!-- old anchor for the next section --> <a name=\"backup\"/>"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1103
msgid "Why can I write to the disk, even though I added it read-only?"
msgstr "Kāpēc diskā var rakstīt, lai gan pievienoju to tikai lasīšanai?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1105
msgid "Why does C<--ro> appear to have no effect?"
msgstr "Kāpēc šķiet, ka C<--ro> neko neietekmē?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1107
msgid ""
"When you add a disk read-only, libguestfs places a writable overlay on top "
"of the underlying disk.  Writes go into this overlay, and are discarded when "
"the handle is closed (or C<guestfish> etc. exits)."
msgstr ""
"Kad disku pievienojat tikai lasīšanai, libguestfs virs pamata diska novieto "
"rakstāmu pārklājumu.  Rakstīšana notiek šajā pārklājumā un tiek atmesta, kad "
"rokturis tiek aizvērts (vai C<guestfish> u. c. iziet)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1111
msgid ""
"There are two reasons for doing it this way: Firstly read-only disks aren't "
"possible in many cases (eg. IDE simply doesn't support them, so you couldn't "
"have an IDE-emulated read-only disk, although this is not common in real "
"libguestfs installations)."
msgstr ""
"Tā tiek darīts divu iemeslu dēļ: pirmkārt, tikai lasāmi diski daudzos "
"gadījumos nav iespējami (piem., IDE tos vienkārši neatbalsta, tāpēc nevarētu "
"būt IDE emulēts tikai lasāms disks, lai gan reālās libguestfs instalācijās "
"tas nav izplatīti)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1116
msgid ""
"Secondly and more importantly, even if read-only disks were possible, you "
"wouldn't want them.  Mounting any filesystem that has a journal, even "
"C<mount -o ro>, causes writes to the filesystem because the journal has to "
"be replayed and metadata updated.  If the disk was truly read-only, you "
"wouldn't be able to mount a dirty filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Otrkārt, un vēl svarīgāk, pat ja tikai lasāmi diski būtu iespējami, jūs tos "
"nevēlētos.  Jebkuras failu sistēmas ar žurnālu montēšana, pat C<mount -o ro>"
", izraisa rakstīšanu failu sistēmā, jo žurnāls jāatskaņo un jāatjaunina "
"metadati.  Ja disks būtu patiesi tikai lasāms, netīru failu sistēmu nevarētu "
"montēt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1122
msgid ""
"To make it usable, we create the overlay as a place to temporarily store "
"these writes, and then we discard it afterwards.  This ensures that the "
"underlying disk is always untouched."
msgstr ""
"Lai to padarītu lietojamu, izveidojam pārklājumu kā vietu šo rakstījumu "
"pagaidu glabāšanai un pēc tam to atmetam.  Tas nodrošina, ka pamata disks "
"vienmēr paliek neskarts."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1126
msgid ""
"Note also that there is a regression test for this when building libguestfs "
"(in C<tests/qemu>).  This is one reason why it’s important for packagers to "
"run the test suite."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā arī, ka, būvējot libguestfs, tam ir regresijas tests (C<tests/"
"qemu>).  Tas ir viens no iemesliem, kāpēc pakotājiem ir svarīgi izpildīt "
"testu komplektu."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1130
msgid "Does C<--ro> make all disks read-only?"
msgstr "Vai C<--ro> padara visus diskus tikai lasāmus?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1132
msgid ""
"I<No!> The C<--ro> option only affects disks added on the command line, "
"ie. using C<-a> and C<-d> options."
msgstr ""
"I<Nē!> Opcija C<--ro> ietekmē tikai komandrindā pievienotos diskus, t. i., "
"izmantojot opcijas C<-a> un C<-d>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1135
msgid ""
"In guestfish, if you use the C<add> command, then disk is added read-write "
"(unless you specify the C<readonly:true> flag explicitly with the command)."
msgstr ""
"Guestfish, ja izmantojat komandu C<add>, disks tiek pievienots lasīšanai un "
"rakstīšanai (ja vien komandā eksplicīti nenorādāt karogu C<readonly:true>)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1139
msgid "Can I use C<guestfish --ro> as a way to backup my virtual machines?"
msgstr "Vai C<guestfish --ro> var izmantot kā veidu virtuālo mašīnu dublēšanai?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1141
msgid ""
"Usually this is I<not> a good idea.  The question is answered in more detail "
"in this mailing list posting: "
"L<https://www.redhat.com/archives/libguestfs/2010-August/msg00024.html>"
msgstr ""
"Parasti tā I<nav> laba doma.  Uz jautājumu sīkāk atbildēts šajā pasta "
"saraksta ierakstā: L<https://www.redhat.com/archives/libguestfs/2010-August/"
"msg00024.html>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1145
msgid "See also the next question."
msgstr "Skatīt arī nākamo jautājumu."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1147
msgid "Why can’t I run fsck on a live filesystem using C<guestfish --ro>?"
msgstr ""
"Kāpēc nevaru izpildīt fsck darbojošā failu sistēmā, izmantojot C<guestfish --"
"ro>?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1149
msgid "This command will usually I<not> work:"
msgstr "Šī komanda parasti I<nedarbosies>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1151
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a /dev/vg/my_root_fs run : fsck /dev/sda\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a /dev/vg/my_root_fs run : fsck /dev/sda\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1153
msgid ""
"The reason for this is that qemu creates a snapshot over the original "
"filesystem, but it doesn't create a strict point-in-time snapshot.  Blocks "
"of data on the underlying filesystem are read by qemu at different times as "
"the fsck operation progresses, with host writes in between.  The result is "
"that fsck sees massive corruption (imaginary, not real!) and fails."
msgstr ""
"Iemesls ir tāds, ka qemu izveido momentuzņēmumu virs oriģinālās failu "
"sistēmas, taču tas neizveido stingru noteikta brīža momentuzņēmumu.  Fsck "
"darbības gaitā qemu nolasa pamata failu sistēmas datu blokus dažādos laikos, "
"un starplaikos notiek resursdatora rakstīšana.  Rezultātā fsck redz milzīgus "
"bojājumus (iedomātus, nevis reālus!) un neizdodas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1160
msgid ""
"What you have to do is to create a point-in-time snapshot.  If it’s a "
"logical volume, use an LVM2 snapshot.  If the filesystem is located inside "
"something like a btrfs/ZFS file, use a btrfs/ZFS snapshot, and then run the "
"fsck on the snapshot.  In practice you don't need to use libguestfs for this "
"-- just run F</sbin/fsck> directly."
msgstr ""
"Jāizveido noteikta brīža momentuzņēmums.  Ja tas ir loģiskais sējums, "
"izmantojiet LVM2 momentuzņēmumu.  Ja failu sistēma atrodas, piemēram, btrfs/"
"ZFS failā, izmantojiet btrfs/ZFS momentuzņēmumu un tad izpildiet fsck "
"momentuzņēmumā.  Praksē libguestfs tam nav jāizmanto — vienkārši izpildiet "
"F</sbin/fsck> tieši."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1166
msgid ""
"Creating point-in-time snapshots of host devices and files is outside the "
"scope of libguestfs, although libguestfs can operate on them once they are "
"created."
msgstr ""
"Resursdatora ierīču un failu noteikta brīža momentuzņēmumu izveide ir ārpus "
"libguestfs darbības jomas, lai gan libguestfs var ar tiem strādāt, kad tie "
"ir izveidoti."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1170
msgid "What’s the difference between guestfish and virt-rescue?"
msgstr "Kāda ir atšķirība starp guestfish un virt-rescue?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1172
msgid ""
"A lot of people are confused by the two superficially similar tools we "
"provide:"
msgstr ""
"Daudzi cilvēki apjūk no mūsu nodrošinātajiem diviem virspusēji līdzīgajiem "
"rīkiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1175
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ guestfish --ro -a guest.img\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" ><fs> fsck /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ guestfish --ro -a guest.img\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" ><fs> fsck /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1179
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-rescue --ro guest.img\n"
" ><rescue> /sbin/fsck /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-rescue --ro guest.img\n"
" ><rescue> /sbin/fsck /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1182
msgid ""
"And the related question which then arises is why you can’t type in full "
"shell commands with all the --options in guestfish (but you can in "
"L<virt-rescue(1)>)."
msgstr ""
"Un saistītais jautājums, kas tad rodas, ir, kāpēc guestfish nevar ierakstīt "
"pilnas čaulas komandas ar visām --opcijām (bet L<virt-rescue(1)> var)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1186
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)> is a program providing structured access to the "
"L<guestfs(3)> API.  It happens to be a nice interactive shell too, but its "
"primary purpose is structured access from shell scripts.  Think of it more "
"like a language binding, like Python and other bindings, but for shell.  The "
"key differentiating factor of guestfish (and the libguestfs API in general) "
"is the ability to automate changes."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)> ir programma, kas nodrošina strukturētu piekļuvi L<guestfs"
"(3)> API.  Tā gadās būt arī jauka interaktīva čaula, taču tās galvenais "
"mērķis ir strukturēta piekļuve no čaulas skriptiem.  Uztveriet to vairāk kā "
"valodas saistījumu, līdzīgi Python un citiem saistījumiem, bet čaulai.  "
"Guestfish (un libguestfs API kopumā) galvenā atšķirīgā iezīme ir spēja "
"automatizēt izmaiņas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1193
msgid ""
"L<virt-rescue(1)> is a free-for-all freeform way to boot the libguestfs "
"appliance and make arbitrary changes to your VM. It’s not structured, you "
"can't automate it, but for making quick ad-hoc fixes to your guests, it can "
"be quite useful."
msgstr ""
"L<virt-rescue(1)> ir brīvs veids, kā sāknēt libguestfs palīgsistēmu un veikt "
"patvaļīgas izmaiņas jūsu VM. Tas nav strukturēts, to nevar automatizēt, taču "
"ātriem ad-hoc viesu labojumiem tas var būt ļoti noderīgs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1198
msgid ""
"But, libguestfs also has a \"backdoor\" into the appliance allowing you to "
"send arbitrary shell commands.  It’s not as flexible as virt-rescue, because "
"you can't interact with the shell commands, but here it is anyway:"
msgstr ""
"Taču libguestfs ir arī „sētas durvis” palīgsistēmā, kas ļauj sūtīt "
"patvaļīgas čaulas komandas.  Tas nav tik elastīgi kā virt-rescue, jo ar "
"čaulas komandām nevar mijiedarboties, bet lūk:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1203
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> debug sh \"cmd arg1 arg2 ...\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> debug sh \"cmd arg1 arg2 ...\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1205
msgid ""
"Note that you should B<not> rely on this.  It could be removed or changed in "
"future. If your program needs some operation, please add it to the "
"libguestfs API instead."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka uz to B<nevajadzētu> paļauties.  Nākotnē to var noņemt vai "
"mainīt. Ja jūsu programmai vajadzīga kāda darbība, lūdzu, tā vietā "
"pievienojiet to libguestfs API."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1209
msgid "What’s the deal with C<guestfish -i>?"
msgstr "Kas ir ar C<guestfish -i>?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1211
msgid ""
"Why does virt-cat only work on a real VM image, but virt-df works on any "
"disk image?"
msgstr ""
"Kāpēc virt-cat darbojas tikai ar īstu VM attēlu, bet virt-df darbojas ar "
"jebkuru diska attēlu?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1214
msgid "What does \"no root device found in this operating system image\" mean?"
msgstr "Ko nozīmē „no root device found in this operating system image”?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1217
msgid ""
"These questions are all related at a fundamental level which may not be "
"immediately obvious."
msgstr ""
"Visi šie jautājumi ir saistīti fundamentālā līmenī, kas var nebūt uzreiz "
"acīmredzams."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1220
msgid ""
"At the L<guestfs(3)> API level, a \"disk image\" is just a pile of "
"partitions and filesystems."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)> API līmenī „diska attēls” ir tikai nodalījumu un failu sistēmu "
"kaudze."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1223
msgid ""
"In contrast, when the virtual machine boots, it mounts those filesystems "
"into a consistent hierarchy such as:"
msgstr ""
"Turpretī, kad virtuālā mašīna sāknējas, tā montē šīs failu sistēmas "
"konsekventā hierarhijā, piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1226
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /          (/dev/sda2)\n"
" │\n"
" ├── /boot  (/dev/sda1)\n"
" │\n"
" ├── /home  (/dev/vg_external/Homes)\n"
" │\n"
" ├── /usr   (/dev/vg_os/lv_usr)\n"
" │\n"
" └── /var   (/dev/vg_os/lv_var)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /          (/dev/sda2)\n"
" │\n"
" ├── /boot  (/dev/sda1)\n"
" │\n"
" ├── /home  (/dev/vg_external/Homes)\n"
" │\n"
" ├── /usr   (/dev/vg_os/lv_usr)\n"
" │\n"
" └── /var   (/dev/vg_os/lv_var)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1236
msgid "(or drive letters on Windows)."
msgstr "(vai disku burtos Windows)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1238
msgid ""
"The API first of all sees the disk image at the \"pile of filesystems\" "
"level.  But it also has a way to inspect the disk image to see if it "
"contains an operating system, and how the disks are mounted when the "
"operating system boots: L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION>."
msgstr ""
"API vispirms redz diska attēlu „failu sistēmu kaudzes” līmenī.  Taču tai ir "
"arī veids, kā inspicēt diska attēlu, lai noskaidrotu, vai tajā ir "
"operētājsistēma un kā diski tiek montēti, kad operētājsistēma sāknējas: "
"L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1243
msgid "Users expect some tools (like L<virt-cat(1)>) to work with VM paths:"
msgstr ""
"Lietotāji sagaida, ka daži rīki (piemēram, L<virt-cat(1)>) strādās ar VM "
"ceļiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1245
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-cat fedora.img /var/log/messages\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-cat fedora.img /var/log/messages\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1247
msgid ""
"How does virt-cat know that F</var> is a separate partition? The trick is "
"that virt-cat performs inspection on the disk image, and uses that to "
"translate the path correctly."
msgstr ""
"Kā virt-cat zina, ka F</var> ir atsevišķs nodalījums? Triks ir tāds, ka virt-"
"cat veic diska attēla inspicēšanu un izmanto to, lai pareizi tulkotu ceļu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1251
msgid ""
"Some tools (including L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-ls(1)>)  use "
"inspection to map VM paths.  Other tools, such as L<virt-df(1)> and "
"L<virt-filesystems(1)> operate entirely at the raw \"big pile of "
"filesystems\" level of the libguestfs API, and don't use inspection."
msgstr ""
"Daži rīki (tostarp L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-ls(1)>) izmanto "
"inspicēšanu VM ceļu kartēšanai.  Citi rīki, piemēram, L<virt-df(1)> un "
"L<virt-filesystems(1)>, pilnībā darbojas libguestfs API neapstrādātajā „"
"lielās failu sistēmu kaudzes” līmenī un neizmanto inspicēšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1256
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)> is in an interesting middle ground.  If you use the I<-a> "
"and I<-m> command line options, then you have to tell guestfish exactly how "
"to add disk images and where to mount partitions. This is the raw API level."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)> atrodas interesantā vidusceļā.  Ja izmantojat komandrindas "
"opcijas I<-a> un I<-m>, guestfish precīzi jāpasaka, kā pievienot disku "
"attēlus un kur montēt nodalījumus. Tas ir neapstrādātās API līmenis."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1261
msgid ""
"If you use the I<-i> option, libguestfs performs inspection and mounts the "
"filesystems for you."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat opciju I<-i>, libguestfs veic inspicēšanu un montē failu "
"sistēmas jūsu vietā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1264
msgid ""
"The error C<no root device found in this operating system image> is related "
"to this.  It means inspection was unable to locate an operating system "
"within the disk image you gave it.  You might see this from programs like "
"virt-cat if you try to run them on something which is just a disk image, not "
"a virtual machine disk image."
msgstr ""
"Kļūda C<no root device found in this operating system image> ir saistīta ar "
"to.  Tā nozīmē, ka inspicēšana nespēja atrast operētājsistēmu norādītajā "
"diska attēlā.  To var redzēt no tādām programmām kā virt-cat, ja mēģināt tās "
"izpildīt ar kaut ko, kas ir tikai diska attēls, nevis virtuālās mašīnas "
"diska attēls."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1270
msgid "What do these C<debug*> and C<internal-*> functions do?"
msgstr "Ko dara šīs C<debug*> un C<internal-*> funkcijas?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1272
msgid ""
"There are some functions which are used for debugging and internal purposes "
"which are I<not> part of the stable API."
msgstr ""
"Ir dažas funkcijas, ko izmanto atkļūdošanai un iekšējiem nolūkiem un kas "
"I<nav> stabilās API daļa."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1275
msgid ""
"The C<debug*> (or C<guestfs_debug*>) functions, primarily "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_debug> and a handful of others, are used for debugging "
"libguestfs.  Although they are not part of the stable API and thus may "
"change or be removed at any time, some programs may want to call these while "
"waiting for features to be added to libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Funkcijas C<debug*> (vai C<guestfs_debug*>), galvenokārt L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_debug> un dažas citas, tiek izmantotas libguestfs atkļūdošanai.  Lai "
"gan tās nav stabilās API daļa un tāpēc jebkurā laikā var mainīties vai tikt "
"noņemtas, dažas programmas tās var vēlēties izsaukt, gaidot, kamēr "
"libguestfs tiek pievienoti līdzekļi."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1281
msgid ""
"The C<internal-*> (or C<guestfs_internal_*>) functions are purely to be used "
"by libguestfs itself.  There is no reason for programs to call them, and "
"programs should not try to use them.  Using them will often cause bad things "
"to happen, as well as not being part of the documented stable API."
msgstr ""
"Funkcijas C<internal-*> (vai C<guestfs_internal_*>) paredzētas tikai pašai "
"libguestfs.  Programmām nav iemesla tās izsaukt, un programmām nevajadzētu "
"mēģināt tās izmantot.  To izmantošana bieži izraisīs nepatīkamas sekas, "
"turklāt tās nav dokumentētās stabilās API daļa."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1287
msgid "DEVELOPERS"
msgstr "IZSTRĀDĀTĀJI"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1289
msgid "Where do I send patches?"
msgstr "Kur sūtīt ielāpus?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1291
msgid ""
"Please send patches to the libguestfs mailing list "
"L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>.  You don't have to be subscribed, but there "
"will be a delay until your posting is manually approved."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, sūtiet ielāpus libguestfs pasta sarakstam L<https://"
"lists.libguestfs.org>.  Jums nav jābūt abonentam, taču būs aizkave, kamēr "
"jūsu ieraksts tiks manuāli apstiprināts."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1296
msgid ""
"B<Please don’t use github pull requests - they will be ignored>.  The "
"reasons are (a) we want to discuss and dissect patches on the mailing list, "
"and (b) github pull requests turn into merge commits but we prefer to have a "
"linear history."
msgstr ""
"B<Lūdzu, neizmantojiet github izvilkšanas pieprasījumus — tie tiks ignorēti>"
".  Iemesli ir (a) mēs vēlamies apspriest un izanalizēt ielāpus pasta "
"sarakstā un (b) github izvilkšanas pieprasījumi pārvēršas sapludināšanas "
"iesūtījumos, bet mēs dodam priekšroku lineārai vēsturei."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1301
msgid "How do I propose a feature?"
msgstr "Kā ierosināt līdzekli?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1303
msgid ""
"Large new features that you intend to contribute should be discussed on the "
"mailing list first (L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>).  This avoids "
"disappointment and wasted work if we don't think the feature would fit into "
"the libguestfs project."
msgstr ""
"Lielus jaunus līdzekļus, ko plānojat iesniegt, vispirms jāapspriež pasta "
"sarakstā (L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>).  Tas novērš vilšanos un "
"izšķiestu darbu, ja uzskatām, ka līdzeklis neiederas libguestfs projektā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1309
msgid ""
"If you want to suggest a useful feature but don’t want to write the code, "
"you can file a bug (see L</GETTING HELP AND REPORTING BUGS>)  with C<\"RFE: "
"\"> at the beginning of the Summary line."
msgstr ""
"Ja vēlaties ieteikt noderīgu līdzekli, bet nevēlaties rakstīt kodu, varat "
"iesniegt kļūdas ziņojumu (skatiet L</PALĪDZĪBAS SAŅEMŠANA UN ZIŅOŠANA PAR "
"KĻŪDĀM>) ar C<\"RFE: \"> rindas Summary sākumā."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1313
msgid "Who can commit to libguestfs git?"
msgstr "Kas var iesūtīt libguestfs git?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1315
msgid ""
"About 5 people have commit access to github.  Patches should be posted on "
"the list first and ACKed.  The policy for ACKing and pushing patches is "
"outlined here:"
msgstr ""
"Aptuveni 5 cilvēkiem ir iesūtīšanas piekļuve github.  Ielāpi vispirms "
"jāpublicē sarakstā un jāapstiprina (ACK).  Ielāpu apstiprināšanas un "
"nosūtīšanas politika izklāstīta šeit:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1319
msgid "L<https://www.redhat.com/archives/libguestfs/2012-January/msg00023.html>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://www.redhat.com/archives/libguestfs/2012-January/msg00023.html>"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1321
msgid "Can I fork libguestfs?"
msgstr "Vai varu atzarot libguestfs?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1323
msgid ""
"Of course you can.  Git makes it easy to fork libguestfs.  Github makes it "
"even easier.  It’s nice if you tell us on the mailing list about forks and "
"the reasons for them."
msgstr ""
"Protams, varat.  Git atvieglo libguestfs atzarošanu.  Github to atvieglo vēl "
"vairāk.  Būtu jauki, ja pastāstītu mums pasta sarakstā par atzarojumiem un "
"to iemesliem."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1327
msgid "MISCELLANEOUS QUESTIONS"
msgstr "DAŽĀDI JAUTĀJUMI"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1329
msgid "Can I monitor the live disk activity of a virtual machine using libguestfs?"
msgstr ""
"Vai ar libguestfs var uzraudzīt virtuālās mašīnas tiešo diska aktivitāti?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1331
msgid ""
"A common request is to be able to use libguestfs to monitor the live disk "
"activity of a guest, for example, to get notified every time a guest creates "
"a new file.  Libguestfs does I<not> work in the way some people imagine, as "
"you can see from this diagram:"
msgstr ""
"Bieži tiek lūgts izmantot libguestfs, lai uzraudzītu viesa tiešo diska "
"aktivitāti, piemēram, lai saņemtu paziņojumu katru reizi, kad viesis izveido "
"jaunu failu.  Libguestfs I<nedarbojas> tā, kā daži iedomājas, kā redzams "
"šajā diagrammā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1336
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n"
"            │ monitoring program using libguestfs │\n"
"            └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n"
"                             ↓\n"
" ┌───────────┐    ┌──────────────────────┐\n"
" │ live VM   │    │ libguestfs appliance │\n"
" ├───────────┤    ├──────────────────────┤\n"
" │ kernel (1)│    │ appliance kernel (2) │\n"
" └───────────┘    └──────────────────────┘\n"
"      ↓                      ↓ (r/o connection)\n"
"      ┌──────────────────────┐\n"
"      |      disk image      |\n"
"      └──────────────────────┘\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"            ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n"
"            │ monitoring program using libguestfs │\n"
"            └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n"
"                             ↓\n"
" ┌───────────┐    ┌──────────────────────┐\n"
" │ live VM   │    │ libguestfs appliance │\n"
" ├───────────┤    ├──────────────────────┤\n"
" │ kernel (1)│    │ appliance kernel (2) │\n"
" └───────────┘    └──────────────────────┘\n"
"      ↓                      ↓ (r/o connection)\n"
"      ┌──────────────────────┐\n"
"      |      disk image      |\n"
"      └──────────────────────┘\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1350
msgid ""
"This scenario is safe (as long as you set the C<readonly> flag when adding "
"the drive).  However the libguestfs appliance kernel (2) does not see all "
"the changes made to the disk image, for two reasons:"
msgstr ""
"Šis scenārijs ir drošs (ja vien, pievienojot disku, iestatāt karogu "
"C<readonly>).  Tomēr libguestfs palīgsistēmas kodols (2) neredz visas diska "
"attēlā veiktās izmaiņas divu iemeslu dēļ:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1356
msgid "i."
msgstr "i."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1358
msgid ""
"The VM kernel (1) can cache data in memory, so it doesn't appear in the disk "
"image."
msgstr "VM kodols (1) var kešot datus atmiņā, tāpēc tie neparādās diska attēlā."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1361
msgid "ii."
msgstr "ii."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1363
msgid ""
"The libguestfs appliance kernel (2) doesn't expect that the disk image is "
"changing underneath it, so its own cache is not magically updated even when "
"the VM kernel (1) does update the disk image."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs palīgsistēmas kodols (2) negaida, ka diska attēls zem tā mainās, "
"tāpēc tā paša kešatmiņa netiek maģiski atjaunināta pat tad, ja VM kodols (1) "
"atjaunina diska attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1369
msgid ""
"The only supported solution is to restart the entire libguestfs appliance "
"whenever you want to look at changes in the disk image.  At the API level "
"that corresponds to calling C<guestfs_shutdown> followed by "
"C<guestfs_launch>, which is a heavyweight operation (see also "
"L<guestfs-performance(3)>)."
msgstr ""
"Vienīgais atbalstītais risinājums ir restartēt visu libguestfs palīgsistēmu "
"katru reizi, kad vēlaties apskatīt izmaiņas diska attēlā.  API līmenī tas "
"atbilst C<guestfs_shutdown> izsaukumam, kam seko C<guestfs_launch>, kas ir "
"smagsvara darbība (skatīt arī L<guestfs-performance(3)>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1375
msgid ""
"There are some unsupported hacks you can try if relaunching the appliance is "
"really too costly:"
msgstr ""
"Ir daži neatbalstīti triki, ko var izmēģināt, ja palīgsistēmas atkārtota "
"palaišana tiešām ir pārāk dārga:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1382
msgid ""
"Call C<guestfs_drop_caches (g, 3)>.  This causes all cached data help by the "
"libguestfs appliance kernel (2) to be discarded, so it goes back to the disk "
"image."
msgstr ""
"Izsauciet C<guestfs_drop_caches (g, 3)>.  Tas liek atmest visus libguestfs "
"palīgsistēmas kodola (2) kešotos datus, tāpēc tas atgriežas pie diska attēla."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1386
msgid ""
"However this on its own is not sufficient, because qemu also caches some "
"data.  You will also need to patch libguestfs to (re-)enable the "
"C<cache=none> mode.  See: "
"L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/09/02/new-in-libguestfs-allow-cache-mode-to-be-selected/>"
msgstr ""
"Tomēr ar to vien nepietiek, jo arī qemu kešo daļu datu.  Būs jāielāpo arī "
"libguestfs, lai (atkārtoti) iespējotu režīmu C<cache=none>.  Skatiet: "
"L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/09/02/new-in-libguestfs-allow-cache-mode-"
"to-be-selected/>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1393
msgid ""
"Use a tool like L<virt-bmap|http://git.annexia.org/?p=virt-bmap.git> "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Tā vietā izmantojiet tādu rīku kā L<virt-bmap|http://git.annexia.org/?p=virt-"
"bmap.git>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1398
msgid "Run an agent inside the guest."
msgstr "Izpildiet aģentu viesī."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1402
msgid ""
"Nothing helps if the guest is making more fundamental changes (eg.  deleting "
"filesystems).  For those kinds of things you must relaunch the appliance."
msgstr ""
"Nekas nepalīdz, ja viesis veic fundamentālākas izmaiņas (piem., dzēš failu "
"sistēmas).  Šādos gadījumos palīgsistēma jāpalaiž atkārtoti."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1406
msgid ""
"(Note there is a third problem that you need to use consistent snapshots to "
"really examine live disk images, but that’s a general problem with using "
"libguestfs against any live disk image.)"
msgstr ""
"(Ņemiet vērā, ka ir trešā problēma — lai patiesi pārbaudītu darbojošos disku "
"attēlus, jāizmanto konsekventi momentuzņēmumi, taču tā ir vispārīga "
"problēma, izmantojot libguestfs ar jebkuru darbojošos diska attēlu.)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1412
msgid "L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr "L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-faq.pod:1422 docs/guestfs-performance.pod:519
msgid "Copyright (C) 2012-2025 Red Hat Inc."
msgstr "Copyright (C) 2012-2025 Red Hat Inc."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-hacking - extending and contributing to libguestfs"
msgstr "guestfs-hacking - libguestfs paplašināšana un līdzdalība tā izstrādē"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:7
msgid "This manual page is for hackers who want to extend libguestfs itself."
msgstr ""
"Šī rokasgrāmatas lapa ir paredzēta izstrādātājiem, kas vēlas paplašināt pašu "
"libguestfs."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:9
msgid "THE SOURCE CODE"
msgstr "PIRMKODS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:11
msgid ""
"Libguestfs source is located in the github repository "
"L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs>"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs pirmkods atrodas github repozitorijā L<https://github.com/"
"libguestfs/libguestfs>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:14
msgid ""
"Large amounts of boilerplate code in libguestfs (RPC, bindings, "
"documentation) are generated.  This means that many source files will appear "
"to be missing from a straightforward git checkout.  You have to run the "
"generator (C<./configure && make -C generator>) in order to create those "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Liela daļa libguestfs šablonkoda (RPC, saistījumi, dokumentācija) tiek "
"ģenerēta.  Tas nozīmē, ka vienkāršā git izrakstā daudzi pirmkoda faili "
"šķitīs trūkstoši.  Lai tos izveidotu, jāizpilda ģenerators (C<./configure && "
"make -C generator>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:20
msgid ""
"Libguestfs uses an autotools-based build system, with the main files being "
"F<configure.ac> and F<Makefile.am>.  See L</THE BUILD SYSTEM>."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs izmanto uz autotools balstītu būvēšanas sistēmu, kuras galvenie "
"faili ir F<configure.ac> un F<Makefile.am>.  Skatiet L</BŪVĒŠANAS SISTĒMA>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:23
msgid ""
"The F<generator> subdirectory contains the generator, plus files describing "
"the API.  The F<lib> subdirectory contains source for the library.  The "
"F<appliance> and F<daemon> subdirectories contain the source for the code "
"that builds the appliance, and the code that runs in the appliance "
"respectively.  Other directories are covered in the section L<SOURCE CODE "
"SUBDIRECTORIES> below."
msgstr ""
"Apakšdirektorija F<generator> satur ģeneratoru un failus, kas apraksta API.  "
"Apakšdirektorija F<lib> satur bibliotēkas pirmkodu.  Apakšdirektorijas "
"F<appliance> un F<daemon> satur attiecīgi palīgsistēmu būvējošā koda un "
"palīgsistēmā izpildāmā koda pirmkodu.  Citas direktorijas aplūkotas sadaļā "
"L<SOURCE CODE SUBDIRECTORIES> tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:30
msgid ""
"Apart from the fact that all API entry points go via some generated code, "
"the library is straightforward.  (In fact, even the generated code is "
"designed to be readable, and should be read as ordinary code).  Some actions "
"run entirely in the library, and are written as C functions in files under "
"F<lib>.  Others are forwarded to the daemon where (after some generated RPC "
"marshalling) they appear as C functions in files under F<daemon>."
msgstr ""
"Izņemot to, ka visi API ieejas punkti iet caur ģenerētu kodu, bibliotēka ir "
"vienkārša.  (Patiesībā pat ģenerētais kods ir veidots lasāms un jālasa kā "
"parasts kods.)  Dažas darbības pilnībā izpildās bibliotēkā un ir rakstītas "
"kā C funkcijas failos zem F<lib>.  Citas tiek pārsūtītas dēmonam, kur (pēc "
"ģenerētas RPC serializācijas) tās parādās kā C funkcijas failos zem F<daemon>"
"."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:38
msgid "To build from source, first read the L<guestfs-building(1)>."
msgstr "Lai būvētu no pirmkoda, vispirms izlasiet L<guestfs-building(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:40
msgid "SOURCE CODE SUBDIRECTORIES"
msgstr "PIRMKODA APAKŠDIREKTORIJAS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:42
msgid ""
"There are a lot of subdirectories in the source tree! Which ones should you "
"concentrate on first? F<lib> and F<daemon> which contain the source code of "
"the core library.  F<generator> is the code generator described above, so "
"that is important.  The F<Makefile.am> in the root directory will tell you "
"in which order the subdirectories get built.  And then if you are looking at "
"a particular tool (eg. F<customize>) or language binding (eg. F<python>), go "
"straight to that subdirectory, but remember that if you didn't run the "
"generator yet, then you may find files which appear to be missing."
msgstr ""
"Pirmkoda kokā ir daudz apakšdirektoriju! Uz kurām vispirms koncentrēties? Uz "
"F<lib> un F<daemon>, kas satur pamata bibliotēkas pirmkodu.  F<generator> ir "
"iepriekš aprakstītais koda ģenerators, tāpēc tas ir svarīgs.  F<Makefile.am> "
"saknes direktorijā pateiks, kādā secībā tiek būvētas apakšdirektorijas.  Un, "
"ja aplūkojat konkrētu rīku (piem., F<customize>) vai valodas saistījumu "
"(piem., F<python>), dodieties tieši uz šo apakšdirektoriju, taču "
"atcerieties: ja ģenerators vēl nav izpildīts, var atrast failus, kas šķiet "
"trūkstoši."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:54
msgid "F<align>"
msgstr "F<align>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:56
msgid "L<virt-alignment-scan(1)> command and documentation."
msgstr "Komanda L<virt-alignment-scan(1)> un dokumentācija."

