"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:370
msgid "EXTENDING LIBGUESTFS"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS PAPLAŠINĀŠANA"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:372
msgid "ADDING A NEW API"
msgstr "JAUNAS API PIEVIENOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:374
msgid ""
"Because large amounts of boilerplate code in libguestfs are generated, this "
"makes it easy to extend the libguestfs API."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā liela daļa libguestfs šablonkoda tiek ģenerēta, libguestfs API ir "
"viegli paplašināt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:377
msgid "To add a new API action there are two changes:"
msgstr "Lai pievienotu jaunu API darbību, jāveic divas izmaiņas:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:383
msgid ""
"You need to add a description of the call (name, parameters, return type, "
"tests, documentation) to F<generator/actions_*.ml> and possibly "
"F<generator/proc_nr.ml>."
msgstr ""
"Jāpievieno izsaukuma apraksts (nosaukums, parametri, atgriešanas tips, "
"testi, dokumentācija) failā F<generator/actions_*.ml> un, iespējams, "
"F<generator/proc_nr.ml>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:387
msgid ""
"There are two sorts of API action, depending on whether the call goes "
"through to the daemon in the appliance, or is serviced entirely by the "
"library (see L<guestfs-internals(1)/ARCHITECTURE>).  "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_sync> is an example of the former, since the sync is "
"done in the appliance.  L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_trace> is an example of the "
"latter, since a trace flag is maintained in the handle and all tracing is "
"done on the library side."
msgstr ""
"Ir divu veidu API darbības atkarībā no tā, vai izsaukums nonāk līdz dēmonam "
"palīgsistēmā vai to pilnībā apkalpo bibliotēka (skatiet L<guestfs-internals"
"(1)/ARHITEKTŪRA>).  L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_sync> ir pirmā veida piemērs, jo "
"sinhronizācija notiek palīgsistēmā.  L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_trace> ir otrā "
"veida piemērs, jo izsekošanas karogs tiek uzturēts rokturī un visa "
"izsekošana notiek bibliotēkas pusē."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:395
msgid ""
"Most new actions are of the first type, and get added to the "
"C<daemon_functions> list.  Each function has a unique procedure number used "
"in the RPC protocol which is assigned to that action when we publish "
"libguestfs and cannot be reused.  Take the latest procedure number and "
"increment it."
msgstr ""
"Lielākā daļa jauno darbību ir pirmā veida un tiek pievienotas sarakstam "
"C<daemon_functions>.  Katrai funkcijai ir unikāls RPC protokolā izmantots "
"procedūras numurs, kas tiek piešķirts darbībai, kad publicējam libguestfs, "
"un to nevar izmantot atkārtoti.  Ņemiet jaunāko procedūras numuru un "
"palieliniet to."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:401
msgid ""
"For library-only actions of the second type, add to the "
"C<non_daemon_functions> list.  Since these functions are serviced by the "
"library and do not travel over the RPC mechanism to the daemon, these "
"functions do not need a procedure number, and so the procedure number is set "
"to C<-1>."
msgstr ""
"Otrā veida tikai bibliotēkas darbībām pievienojiet tās sarakstam "
"C<non_daemon_functions>.  Tā kā šīs funkcijas apkalpo bibliotēka un tās caur "
"RPC mehānismu nenonāk līdz dēmonam, tām nav vajadzīgs procedūras numurs, "
"tāpēc procedūras numurs ir iestatīts uz C<-1>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:409
msgid "Implement the action (in C):"
msgstr "Realizējiet darbību (C valodā):"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:411
msgid ""
"For daemon actions, implement the function C<do_E<lt>nameE<gt>> in the "
"C<daemon/> directory."
msgstr ""
"Dēmona darbībām realizējiet funkciju C<do_E<lt>nameE<gt>> direktorijā "
"C<daemon/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:414
msgid ""
"For library actions, implement the function C<guestfs_impl_E<lt>nameE<gt>> "
"in the C<lib/> directory."
msgstr ""
"Bibliotēkas darbībām realizējiet funkciju C<guestfs_impl_E<lt>nameE<gt>> "
"direktorijā C<lib/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:417
msgid "In either case, use another function as an example of what to do."
msgstr "Jebkurā gadījumā kā paraugu izmantojiet citu funkciju."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:421
msgid ""
"As an alternative to step 2: Since libguestfs 1.38, daemon actions can be "
"implemented in OCaml.  You have to set the C<impl = OCaml ...> flag in the "
"generator.  Take a look at F<daemon/file.ml> for an example."
msgstr ""
"Alternatīva 2. solim: kopš libguestfs 1.38 dēmona darbības var realizēt "
"OCaml.  Ģeneratorā jāiestata karogs C<impl = OCaml ...>.  Piemēru apskatiet "
"failā F<daemon/file.ml>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:428
msgid "After making these changes, use C<make> to compile."
msgstr "Pēc šo izmaiņu veikšanas kompilējiet ar C<make>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:430
msgid ""
"Note that you don’t need to implement the RPC, language bindings, manual "
"pages or anything else.  It’s all automatically generated from the OCaml "
"description."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka RPC, valodu saistījumi, rokasgrāmatas lapas vai jebkas cits "
"nav jārealizē.  Tas viss tiek automātiski ģenerēts no OCaml apraksta."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:434
msgid "Adding tests for an API"
msgstr "Testu pievienošana API"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:436
msgid ""
"You can supply zero or as many tests as you want per API call.  The tests "
"can either be added as part of the API description "
"(F<generator/actions_*.ml>), or in some rarer cases you may want to drop a "
"script into C<tests/*/>.  Note that adding a script to C<tests/*/> is "
"slower, so if possible use the first method."
msgstr ""
"Katram API izsaukumam varat nodrošināt nulli vai tik daudz testu, cik "
"vēlaties.  Testus var pievienot vai nu kā API apraksta daļu (F<generator/"
"actions_*.ml>), vai dažos retākos gadījumos var ievietot skriptu C<tests/*/>"
".  Ņemiet vērā, ka skripta pievienošana C<tests/*/> ir lēnāka, tāpēc, ja "
"iespējams, izmantojiet pirmo metodi."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:442
msgid ""
"The following describes the test environment used when you add an API test "
"in F<actions_*.ml>."
msgstr ""
"Tālāk aprakstīta testa vide, ko izmanto, pievienojot API testu failā "
"F<actions_*.ml>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:445
msgid "The test environment has 4 block devices:"
msgstr "Testa videi ir 4 bloku ierīces:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:449
msgid "F</dev/sda> 2 GB"
msgstr "F</dev/sda> 2 GB"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:451
msgid "General block device for testing."
msgstr "Vispārīga bloku ierīce testēšanai."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:453
msgid "F</dev/sdb> 2 GB"
msgstr "F</dev/sdb> 2 GB"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:455
msgid ""
"F</dev/sdb1> is an ext2 filesystem used for testing filesystem write "
"operations."
msgstr ""
"F</dev/sdb1> ir ext2 failu sistēma, ko izmanto failu sistēmas rakstīšanas "
"darbību testēšanai."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:458
msgid "F</dev/sdc> 10 MB"
msgstr "F</dev/sdc> 10 MB"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:460
msgid "Used in a few tests where two block devices are needed."
msgstr "Izmanto dažos testos, kur vajadzīgas divas bloku ierīces."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:462
msgid "F</dev/sdd>"
msgstr "F</dev/sdd>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:464
msgid "ISO with fixed content (see F<images/test.iso>)."
msgstr "ISO ar fiksētu saturu (skatiet F<images/test.iso>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:468
msgid ""
"To be able to run the tests in a reasonable amount of time, the libguestfs "
"appliance and block devices are reused between tests.  So don't try testing "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_kill_subprocess> :-x"
msgstr ""
"Lai testus varētu izpildīt saprātīgā laikā, libguestfs palīgsistēma un bloku "
"ierīces tiek izmantotas atkārtoti starp testiem.  Tāpēc nemēģiniet testēt "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_kill_subprocess> :-x"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:472
msgid ""
"Each test starts with an initial scenario, selected using one of the "
"C<Init*> expressions, described in F<generator/types.ml>.  These initialize "
"the disks mentioned above in a particular way as documented in F<types.ml>.  "
"You should not assume anything about the previous contents of other disks "
"that are not initialized."
msgstr ""
"Katrs tests sākas ar sākotnējo scenāriju, kas izvēlēts ar kādu no izteiksmēm "
"C<Init*>, kas aprakstītas F<generator/types.ml>.  Tās inicializē iepriekš "
"minētos diskus noteiktā veidā, kā dokumentēts F<types.ml>.  Nevajadzētu neko "
"pieņemt par citu, neinicializētu disku iepriekšējo saturu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:478
msgid ""
"You can add a prerequisite clause to any individual test.  This is a "
"run-time check, which, if it fails, causes the test to be skipped.  Useful "
"if testing a command which might not work on all variations of libguestfs "
"builds.  A test that has prerequisite of C<Always> means to run "
"unconditionally."
msgstr ""
"Jebkuram atsevišķam testam var pievienot priekšnoteikuma klauzulu.  Tā ir "
"izpildlaika pārbaude, kuras neizdošanās gadījumā tests tiek izlaists.  "
"Noderīgi, testējot komandu, kas var nedarboties visās libguestfs būvju "
"variācijās.  Tests ar priekšnoteikumu C<Always> nozīmē beznosacījumu izpildi."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:484
msgid ""
"In addition, packagers can skip individual tests by setting environment "
"variables before running C<make check>."
msgstr ""
"Turklāt pakotāji var izlaist atsevišķus testus, pirms C<make check> izpildes "
"iestatot vides mainīgos."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:487
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" SKIP_TEST_<CMD>_<NUM>=1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" SKIP_TEST_<CMD>_<NUM>=1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:489
msgid "eg: C<SKIP_TEST_COMMAND_3=1> skips test #3 of L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_command>."
msgstr ""
"piem.: C<SKIP_TEST_COMMAND_3=1> izlaiž L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_command> 3. "
"testu."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:493
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" SKIP_TEST_<CMD>=1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" SKIP_TEST_<CMD>=1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:495
msgid "eg: C<SKIP_TEST_ZEROFREE=1> skips all L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_zerofree> tests."
msgstr ""
"piem.: C<SKIP_TEST_ZEROFREE=1> izlaiž visus L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_zerofree> "
"testus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:497
msgid "Packagers can run only certain tests by setting for example:"
msgstr "Pakotāji var izpildīt tikai noteiktus testus, iestatot, piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:499
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" TEST_ONLY=\"vfs_type zerofree\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" TEST_ONLY=\"vfs_type zerofree\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:501
msgid ""
"See F<tests/c-api/tests.c> for more details of how these environment "
"variables work."
msgstr ""
"Sīkāku informāciju par šo vides mainīgo darbību skatiet F<tests/c-api/"
"tests.c>."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:504
msgid "Debugging new APIs"
msgstr "Jaunu API atkļūdošana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:506
msgid "Test new actions work before submitting them."
msgstr "Pirms iesniegšanas pārbaudiet, vai jaunās darbības darbojas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:508
msgid "You can use guestfish to try out new commands."
msgstr "Jaunu komandu izmēģināšanai varat izmantot guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:510
msgid ""
"Debugging the daemon is a problem because it runs inside a minimal "
"environment.  However you can fprintf messages in the daemon to stderr, and "
"they will show up if you use C<guestfish -v>."
msgstr ""
"Dēmona atkļūdošana ir problemātiska, jo tas darbojas minimālā vidē.  Tomēr "
"dēmonā var izdrukāt ziņojumus ar fprintf uz stderr, un tie parādīsies, ja "
"izmantojat C<guestfish -v>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:514
msgid "ADDING A NEW LANGUAGE BINDING"
msgstr "JAUNAS VALODAS SAISTĪJUMA PIEVIENOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:516
msgid ""
"All language bindings must be generated by the generator (see the "
"F<generator> subdirectory)."
msgstr ""
"Visi valodu saistījumi jāģenerē ģeneratoram (skatiet apakšdirektoriju "
"F<generator>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:519
msgid ""
"There is no documentation for this yet.  We suggest you look at an existing "
"binding, eg. F<generator/ocaml.ml> or F<generator/perl.ml>."
msgstr ""
"Tam vēl nav dokumentācijas.  Iesakām apskatīt esošu saistījumu, piem., "
"F<generator/ocaml.ml> vai F<generator/perl.ml>."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:523
msgid "Adding tests for language bindings"
msgstr "Testu pievienošana valodu saistījumiem"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:525
msgid ""
"Language bindings should come with tests.  Previously testing of language "
"bindings was rather ad-hoc, but we have been trying to formalize the set of "
"tests that every language binding should use."
msgstr ""
"Valodu saistījumiem jābūt ar testiem.  Iepriekš valodu saistījumu testēšana "
"bija diezgan ad-hoc, taču esam centušies formalizēt testu kopu, ko jāizmanto "
"katram valodas saistījumam."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:529
msgid ""
"Currently only the OCaml and Perl bindings actually implement the full set "
"of tests, and the OCaml bindings are canonical, so you should emulate what "
"the OCaml tests do."
msgstr ""
"Pašlaik pilnu testu kopu faktiski realizē tikai OCaml un Perl saistījumi, un "
"OCaml saistījumi ir kanoniski, tāpēc atdariniet to, ko dara OCaml testi."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:533
msgid "This is the numbering scheme used by the tests:"
msgstr "Šī ir testu izmantotā numurēšanas shēma:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:535
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - 000+ basic tests:\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" - 000+ basic tests:\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:537
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   010  load the library\n"
"   020  create\n"
"   030  create-flags\n"
"   040  create multiple handles\n"
"   050  test setting and getting config properties\n"
"   060  explicit close\n"
"   065  implicit close (in GC'd languages)\n"
"   070  optargs\n"
"   080  version\n"
"   090  retvalues\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   010  load the library\n"
"   020  create\n"
"   030  create-flags\n"
"   040  create multiple handles\n"
"   050  test setting and getting config properties\n"
"   060  explicit close\n"
"   065  implicit close (in GC'd languages)\n"
"   070  optargs\n"
"   080  version\n"
"   090  retvalues\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:548
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - 100  launch, create partitions and LVs and filesystems\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" - 100  launch, create partitions and LVs and filesystems\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:550
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - 400+ events:\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" - 400+ events:\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:552
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   410  close event\n"
"   420  log messages\n"
"   430  progress messages\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   410  close event\n"
"   420  log messages\n"
"   430  progress messages\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:556
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - 800+ regression tests (specific to the language)\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" - 800+ regression tests (specific to the language)\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:558
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - 900+ any other custom tests for the language\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" - 900+ any other custom tests for the language\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:560
msgid ""
"To save time when running the tests, only 100, 430, 800+, 900+ should launch "
"the handle."
msgstr ""
"Lai ietaupītu laiku, izpildot testus, rokturi jāpalaiž tikai 100, 430, 800+, "
"900+."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:563
msgid "FORMATTING CODE"
msgstr "KODA FORMATĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:565
msgid ""
"Our C source code generally adheres to some basic code-formatting "
"conventions.  The existing code base is not totally consistent on this "
"front, but we do prefer that contributed code be formatted similarly.  In "
"short, use spaces-not-TABs for indentation, use 2 spaces for each "
"indentation level, and other than that, follow the K&R style."
msgstr ""
"Mūsu C pirmkods parasti ievēro dažas pamata koda formatēšanas konvencijas.  "
"Esošā koda bāze šajā ziņā nav pilnīgi konsekventa, taču dodam priekšroku "
"tam, lai iesniegtais kods būtu formatēts līdzīgi.  Īsumā: atkāpēm "
"izmantojiet atstarpes, nevis tabulācijas, katram atkāpes līmenim 2 "
"atstarpes, un citādi ievērojiet K&R stilu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:571
msgid ""
"If you use Emacs, add the following to one of your start-up files (e.g., "
"~/.emacs), to help ensure that you get indentation right:"
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat Emacs, pievienojiet šo kādam no saviem palaišanas failiem "
"(piem., ~/.emacs), lai palīdzētu nodrošināt pareizas atkāpes:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:574
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ;;; In libguestfs, indent with spaces everywhere (not TABs).\n"
" ;;; Exceptions: Makefile and ChangeLog modes.\n"
" (add-hook 'find-file-hook\n"
"     '(lambda () (if (and buffer-file-name\n"
"                          (string-match \"/libguestfs\\\\>\"\n"
"                              (buffer-file-name))\n"
"                          (not (string-equal mode-name \"Change Log\"))\n"
"                          (not (string-equal mode-name \"Makefile\")))\n"
"                     (setq indent-tabs-mode nil))))\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" ;;; In libguestfs, indent with spaces everywhere (not TABs).\n"
" ;;; Exceptions: Makefile and ChangeLog modes.\n"
" (add-hook 'find-file-hook\n"
"     '(lambda () (if (and buffer-file-name\n"
"                          (string-match \"/libguestfs\\\\>\"\n"
"                              (buffer-file-name))\n"
"                          (not (string-equal mode-name \"Change Log\"))\n"
"                          (not (string-equal mode-name \"Makefile\")))\n"
"                     (setq indent-tabs-mode nil))))\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:584
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ;;; When editing C sources in libguestfs, use this style.\n"
" (defun libguestfs-c-mode ()\n"
"   \"C mode with adjusted defaults for use with libguestfs.\"\n"
"   (interactive)\n"
"   (c-set-style \"K&R\")\n"
"   (setq c-indent-level 2)\n"
"   (setq c-basic-offset 2))\n"
" (add-hook 'c-mode-hook\n"
"           '(lambda () (if (string-match \"/libguestfs\\\\>\"\n"
"                               (buffer-file-name))\n"
"                           (libguestfs-c-mode))))\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ;;; When editing C sources in libguestfs, use this style.\n"
" (defun libguestfs-c-mode ()\n"
"   \"C mode with adjusted defaults for use with libguestfs.\"\n"
"   (interactive)\n"
"   (c-set-style \"K&R\")\n"
"   (setq c-indent-level 2)\n"
"   (setq c-basic-offset 2))\n"
" (add-hook 'c-mode-hook\n"
"           '(lambda () (if (string-match \"/libguestfs\\\\>\"\n"
"                               (buffer-file-name))\n"
"                           (libguestfs-c-mode))))\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:596
msgid "TESTING YOUR CHANGES"
msgstr "IZMAIŅU TESTĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:598
msgid "Turn warnings into errors when developing to make warnings hard to ignore:"
msgstr ""
"Izstrādes laikā pārvērtiet brīdinājumus kļūdās, lai brīdinājumus būtu grūti "
"ignorēt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:601
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./configure --enable-werror\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./configure --enable-werror\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:603
msgid "Useful targets are:"
msgstr "Noderīgi mērķi ir:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:607
msgid "C<make check>"
msgstr "C<make check>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:609
msgid "Runs the regular test suite."
msgstr "Izpilda parasto testu komplektu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:611
msgid ""
"This is implemented using the regular automake C<TESTS> target.  See the "
"automake documentation for details."
msgstr ""
"Tas realizēts, izmantojot parasto automake mērķi C<TESTS>.  Sīkāk skatiet "
"automake dokumentāciju."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:614
msgid "C<make check-valgrind>"
msgstr "C<make check-valgrind>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:616
msgid "Runs a subset of the test suite under valgrind."
msgstr "Izpilda testu komplekta apakškopu ar valgrind."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:618
msgid "See L</VALGRIND> below."
msgstr "Skatiet L</VALGRIND> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:620
msgid "C<make check-valgrind-local-guests>"
msgstr "C<make check-valgrind-local-guests>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:622
msgid ""
"Runs a subset of the test suite under valgrind using locally installed "
"libvirt guests (read-only)."
msgstr ""
"Izpilda testu komplekta apakškopu ar valgrind, izmantojot lokāli instalētus "
"libvirt viesus (tikai lasīšanai)."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:625
msgid "C<make check-direct>"
msgstr "C<make check-direct>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:627
msgid ""
"Runs all tests using default appliance back-end.  This only has any effect "
"if a non-default backend was selected using C<./configure "
"--with-default-backend=...>"
msgstr ""
"Izpilda visus testus, izmantojot noklusējuma palīgsistēmas aizmugursistēmu.  "
"Tam ir ietekme tikai tad, ja ar C<./configure --with-default-backend=...> "
"izvēlēta aizmugursistēma, kas nav noklusējuma."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:631
msgid "C<make check-valgrind-direct>"
msgstr "C<make check-valgrind-direct>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:633
msgid ""
"Run a subset of the test suite under valgrind using the default appliance "
"back-end."
msgstr ""
"Izpildīt testu komplekta apakškopu ar valgrind, izmantojot noklusējuma "
"palīgsistēmas aizmugursistēmu."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:636
msgid "C<make check-with-upstream-qemu>"
msgstr "C<make check-with-upstream-qemu>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:638
msgid ""
"Runs all tests using a local qemu binary.  It looks for the qemu binary in "
"QEMUDIR (defaults to F<$HOME/d/qemu>), but you can set this to another "
"directory on the command line, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Izpilda visus testus, izmantojot lokālu qemu bināro failu.  Tas meklē qemu "
"bināro failu QEMUDIR (noklusējums F<$HOME/d/qemu>), taču komandrindā to var "
"iestatīt uz citu direktoriju, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:642
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" make check-with-upstream-qemu QEMUDIR=/usr/src/qemu\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" make check-with-upstream-qemu QEMUDIR=/usr/src/qemu\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:644
msgid "C<make check-with-upstream-libvirt>"
msgstr "C<make check-with-upstream-libvirt>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:646
msgid ""
"Runs all tests using a local libvirt.  This only has any effect if the "
"libvirt backend was selected using C<./configure "
"--with-default-backend=libvirt>"
msgstr ""
"Izpilda visus testus, izmantojot lokālu libvirt.  Tam ir ietekme tikai tad, "
"ja ar C<./configure --with-default-backend=libvirt> izvēlēta libvirt "
"aizmugursistēma"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:650
msgid ""
"It looks for libvirt in LIBVIRTDIR (defaults to F<$HOME/d/libvirt>), but you "
"can set this to another directory on the command line, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Tas meklē libvirt LIBVIRTDIR (noklusējums F<$HOME/d/libvirt>), taču "
"komandrindā to var iestatīt uz citu direktoriju, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:653
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" make check-with-upstream-libvirt LIBVIRTDIR=/usr/src/libvirt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" make check-with-upstream-libvirt LIBVIRTDIR=/usr/src/libvirt\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:655
msgid "C<make check-slow>"
msgstr "C<make check-slow>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:657
msgid "Runs some slow/long-running tests which are not run by default."
msgstr ""
"Izpilda dažus lēnus/ilgstošus testus, kas pēc noklusējuma netiek izpildīti."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:659
msgid "To mark a test as slow/long-running:"
msgstr "Lai atzīmētu testu kā lēnu/ilgstošu:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:665 docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:701
msgid ""
"Add it to the list of C<TESTS> in the F<Makefile.am>, just like a normal "
"test."
msgstr ""
"Pievienojiet to F<Makefile.am> sarakstam C<TESTS> tāpat kā parastu testu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:670
msgid ""
"Modify the test so it checks if the C<SLOW=1> environment variable is set, "
"and if I<not> set it skips (ie. returns with exit code 77).  If using "
"F<tests/functions.sh>, you can call the function C<slow_test> for this."
msgstr ""
"Mainiet testu, lai tas pārbaudītu, vai ir iestatīts vides mainīgais C<SLOW=1>"
", un, ja I<nav> iestatīts, izlaistu (t. i., atgrieztos ar izejas kodu 77).  "
"Ja izmantojat F<tests/functions.sh>, šim nolūkam var izsaukt funkciju "
"C<slow_test>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:677
msgid "Add a variable C<SLOW_TESTS> to the F<Makefile.am> listing the slow tests."
msgstr ""
"Pievienojiet F<Makefile.am> mainīgo C<SLOW_TESTS>, kas uzskaita lēnos testus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:682 docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:717
msgid "Add a rule to the F<Makefile.am>:"
msgstr "Pievienojiet F<Makefile.am> kārtulu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:684
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" check-slow:\n"
"   $(MAKE) check TESTS=\"$(SLOW_TESTS)\" SLOW=1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" check-slow:\n"
"   $(MAKE) check TESTS=\"$(SLOW_TESTS)\" SLOW=1\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:689
msgid "C<sudo make check-root>"
msgstr "C<sudo make check-root>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:691
msgid ""
"Runs some tests which require root privileges.  These are supposed to be "
"safe, but take care.  You have to run this as root (eg. using L<sudo(8)> "
"explicitly)."
msgstr ""
"Izpilda dažus testus, kuriem vajadzīgas root privilēģijas.  Tiem vajadzētu "
"būt drošiem, taču esiet uzmanīgi.  Tas jāizpilda kā root (piem., eksplicīti "
"izmantojot L<sudo(8)>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:695
msgid "To mark a test as requiring root:"
msgstr "Lai atzīmētu testu kā tādu, kam vajadzīgs root:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:706
msgid ""
"Modify the test so it checks if euid == 0, and if I<not> set it skips "
"(ie. returns with exit code 77).  If using F<tests/functions.sh>, you can "
"call the function C<root_test> for this."
msgstr ""
"Mainiet testu, lai tas pārbaudītu, vai euid == 0, un, ja I<nav>, izlaistu "
"(t. i., atgrieztos ar izejas kodu 77).  Ja izmantojat F<tests/functions.sh>, "
"šim nolūkam var izsaukt funkciju C<root_test>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:712
msgid "Add a variable C<ROOT_TESTS> to the F<Makefile.am> listing the root tests."
msgstr ""
"Pievienojiet F<Makefile.am> mainīgo C<ROOT_TESTS>, kas uzskaita root testus."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:719
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" check-root:\n"
"   $(MAKE) check TESTS=\"$(ROOT_TESTS)\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" check-root:\n"
"   $(MAKE) check TESTS=\"$(ROOT_TESTS)\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:724
msgid "C<make check-all>"
msgstr "C<make check-all>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:726
msgid "Equivalent to running all C<make check*> rules except C<check-root>."
msgstr ""
"Līdzvērtīgi visu C<make check*> kārtulu izpildei, izņemot C<check-root>."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:728
msgid "C<make check-release>"
msgstr "C<make check-release>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:730
msgid ""
"Runs a subset of C<make check*> rules that are required to pass before a "
"tarball can be released.  Currently this is:"
msgstr ""
"Izpilda C<make check*> kārtulu apakškopu, kurām jāizdodas, pirms var izdot "
"tar arhīvu.  Pašlaik tas ir:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:737
msgid "check"
msgstr "check"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:741
msgid "check-valgrind"
msgstr "check-valgrind"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:745
msgid "check-direct"
msgstr "check-direct"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:749
msgid "check-valgrind-direct"
msgstr "check-valgrind-direct"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:753
msgid "check-slow"
msgstr "check-slow"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:757
msgid "C<make installcheck>"
msgstr "C<make installcheck>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:759
msgid "Run C<make check> on the installed copy of libguestfs."
msgstr "Izpildīt C<make check> instalētajai libguestfs kopijai."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:761
msgid ""
"The version of installed libguestfs being tested, and the version of the "
"libguestfs source tree must be the same."
msgstr ""
"Testējamās instalētās libguestfs versijai un libguestfs pirmkoda koka "
"versijai jābūt vienādām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:764
msgid "Do:"
msgstr "Izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:766
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./configure\n"
" make clean ||:\n"
" make\n"
" make installcheck\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./configure\n"
" make clean ||:\n"
" make\n"
" make installcheck\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:773
msgid "VALGRIND"
msgstr "VALGRIND"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:775
msgid ""
"When you do C<make check-valgrind>, it searches for any F<Makefile.am> in "
"the tree that has a C<check-valgrind:> target and runs it."
msgstr ""
"Kad izpildāt C<make check-valgrind>, tas meklē kokā jebkuru F<Makefile.am> "
"ar mērķi C<check-valgrind:> un izpilda to."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:778
msgid ""
"Writing the F<Makefile.am> and tests correctly to use valgrind and working "
"with automake parallel tests is subtle."
msgstr ""
"Pareizi uzrakstīt F<Makefile.am> un testus valgrind izmantošanai un darbam "
"ar automake paralēlajiem testiem ir smalks darbs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:781
msgid "If your tests are run via a shell script wrapper, then in the wrapper use:"
msgstr ""
"Ja testi tiek izpildīti caur čaulas skripta ietinēju, ietinējā izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:784
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $VG virt-foo\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $VG virt-foo\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:786
msgid "and in the F<Makefile.am> use:"
msgstr "un F<Makefile.am> izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:788 docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:796
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" check-valgrind:\n"
"     make VG=\"@VG@\" check\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" check-valgrind:\n"
"     make VG=\"@VG@\" check\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:791
msgid ""
"However, if your binaries run directly from the C<TESTS> rule, you have to "
"modify the F<Makefile.am> like this:"
msgstr ""
"Tomēr, ja binārie faili tiek izpildīti tieši no kārtulas C<TESTS>, "
"F<Makefile.am> jāmaina šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:794
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" LOG_COMPILER = $(VG)\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" LOG_COMPILER = $(VG)\n"
" \n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:799
msgid ""
"In either case, check that the right program is being tested by examining "
"the F<tmp/valgrind*> log files carefully."
msgstr ""
"Jebkurā gadījumā pārbaudiet, vai tiek testēta pareizā programma, rūpīgi "
"aplūkojot žurnālu failus F<tmp/valgrind*>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:802
msgid "SUBMITTING PATCHES"
msgstr "IELĀPU IESNIEGŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:804
msgid ""
"Submit patches to the mailing list: L<https://lists.libguestfs.org> and CC "
"to L<rjones@redhat.com>."
msgstr ""
"Iesniedziet ielāpus pasta sarakstam: L<https://lists.libguestfs.org> un "
"kopiju uz L<rjones@redhat.com>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:808
msgid ""
"You do not need to subscribe to the mailing list if you don’t want to.  "
"There may be a short delay while your message is moderated."
msgstr ""
"Pasta saraksts nav jāabonē, ja nevēlaties.  Kamēr jūsu ziņojums tiek "
"moderēts, var būt neliela aizkave."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:811
msgid "INTERNATIONALIZATION (I18N) SUPPORT"
msgstr "INTERNACIONALIZĀCIJAS (I18N) ATBALSTS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:813
msgid "We support i18n (gettext anyhow) in the library."
msgstr "Bibliotēkā atbalstām i18n (vismaz gettext)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:815
msgid ""
"However many messages come from the daemon, and we don’t translate those at "
"the moment.  One reason is that the appliance generally has all locale files "
"removed from it, because they take up a lot of space.  So we'd have to "
"re-add some of those, as well as copying our PO files into the appliance."
msgstr ""
"Tomēr daudzi ziņojumi nāk no dēmona, un tos pašlaik netulkojam.  Viens "
"iemesls ir tas, ka no palīgsistēmas parasti ir noņemti visi lokāļu faili, jo "
"tie aizņem daudz vietas.  Tāpēc daļa no tiem būtu jāpievieno atpakaļ, kā arī "
"jākopē mūsu PO faili palīgsistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:821
msgid ""
"Debugging messages are never translated, since they are intended for the "
"programmers."
msgstr ""
"Atkļūdošanas ziņojumi nekad netiek tulkoti, jo tie paredzēti programmētājiem."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:824
msgid "MISCELLANEOUS TOPICS"
msgstr "DAŽĀDAS TĒMAS"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:826
msgid "HOW OCAML PROGRAMS ARE COMPILED AND LINKED"
msgstr "KĀ OCAML PROGRAMMAS TIEK KOMPILĒTAS UN SAISTĪTAS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:828
msgid ""
"Mostly this section is \"how we make automake & ocamlopt work together\" "
"since OCaml programs themselves are easy to compile."
msgstr ""
"Galvenokārt šī sadaļa ir par to, „kā panākt, lai automake un ocamlopt "
"strādātu kopā”, jo pašas OCaml programmas ir viegli kompilēt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:831
msgid ""
"Automake has no native support for OCaml programs, ocamlc nor ocamlopt.  "
"What we do instead is to treat OCaml programs as C programs which happen to "
"contain these \"other objects\" (C<\"DEPENDENCIES\"> in automake-speak) that "
"happen to be the OCaml objects.  This works because OCaml programs usually "
"have C files for native bindings etc."
msgstr ""
"Automake nav vietējā atbalsta OCaml programmām, ocamlc vai ocamlopt.  Tā "
"vietā mēs apstrādājam OCaml programmas kā C programmas, kas gadās saturēt "
"šos „citus objektus” (automake valodā C<\"DEPENDENCIES\">), kas gadās būt "
"OCaml objekti.  Tas darbojas, jo OCaml programmām parasti ir C faili "
"vietējiem saistījumiem u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:837
msgid "So a typical program is described as just its C sources:"
msgstr "Tātad tipiska programma tiek aprakstīta tikai ar tās C pirmkodu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:839
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt_customize_SOURCES = ... crypt-c.c perl_edit-c.c\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt_customize_SOURCES = ... crypt-c.c perl_edit-c.c\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:841
msgid ""
"For programs that have no explicit C sources, we create an empty F<dummy.c> "
"file, and list that instead:"
msgstr ""
"Programmām bez eksplicīta C pirmkoda izveidojam tukšu failu F<dummy.c> un "
"uzskaitām to:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:844
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt_resize_SOURCES = dummy.c\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt_resize_SOURCES = dummy.c\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:846
msgid ""
"The OCaml objects which contain most of the code are listed as automake "
"dependencies (other dependencies may also be listed):"
msgstr ""
"OCaml objekti, kas satur lielāko daļu koda, tiek uzskaitīti kā automake "
"atkarības (var būt uzskaitītas arī citas atkarības):"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:849
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt_customize_DEPENDENCIES = ... customize_main.cmx\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt_customize_DEPENDENCIES = ... customize_main.cmx\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:851
msgid ""
"The only other special thing we need to do is to provide a custom link "
"command.  This is needed because automake won't assemble the ocamlopt "
"command, the list of objects and the C<-cclib> libraries in the correct "
"order otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Vienīgā cita īpašā lieta, kas jādara, ir nodrošināt pielāgotu saistīšanas "
"komandu.  Tas vajadzīgs, jo citādi automake nesaliks ocamlopt komandu, "
"objektu sarakstu un C<-cclib> bibliotēkas pareizā secībā."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:856
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt_customize_LINK = \\\n"
"     $(top_builddir)/ocaml-link.sh -cclib '-lutils' -- ...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt_customize_LINK = \\\n"
"     $(top_builddir)/ocaml-link.sh -cclib '-lutils' -- ...\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:859
msgid ""
"The actual rules, which you can examine in F<customize/Makefile.am>, are a "
"little bit more complicated than this because they have to handle:"
msgstr ""
"Faktiskās kārtulas, ko varat apskatīt F<customize/Makefile.am>, ir nedaudz "
"sarežģītākas, jo tām jāapstrādā:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:866
msgid "Compiling for byte code or native code."
msgstr "Kompilēšana baitkodā vai vietējā kodā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:870
msgid "The pattern rules needed to compile the OCaml sources to objects."
msgstr "Šablonu kārtulas, kas vajadzīgas OCaml pirmkoda kompilēšanai objektos."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:872
msgid ""
"These are now kept in F<subdir-rules.mk> at the top level, which is included "
"in every subdirectory F<Makefile.am>."
msgstr ""
"Tās tagad tiek glabātas augšējā līmeņa F<subdir-rules.mk>, kas tiek iekļauts "
"katras apakšdirektorijas F<Makefile.am>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:877
msgid "Adding OCaml sources files to C<EXTRA_DIST>."
msgstr "OCaml pirmkoda failu pievienošana C<EXTRA_DIST>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:879
msgid ""
"Automake isn't aware of the complete list of sources for a binary, so it "
"will not add them all automatically."
msgstr ""
"Automake nezina pilnu binārā faila pirmkoda sarakstu, tāpēc tas tos visus "
"automātiski nepievienos."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:884
msgid "MAINTAINER TASKS"
msgstr "UZTURĒTĀJA UZDEVUMI"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:886
msgid "MAINTAINER MAKEFILE TARGETS"
msgstr "UZTURĒTĀJA MAKEFILE MĒRĶI"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:888
msgid ""
"These C<make> targets probably won’t work and aren't useful unless you are a "
"libguestfs maintainer."
msgstr ""
"Šie C<make> mērķi droši vien nedarbosies un nav noderīgi, ja vien neesat "
"libguestfs uzturētājs."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:891
msgid "make maintainer-commit"
msgstr "make maintainer-commit"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:893
msgid ""
"This commits everything in the working directory with the commit message "
"C<Version $(VERSION).>.  You must update F<configure.ac>, clean and rebuild "
"first."
msgstr ""
"Tas iesūta visu darba direktorijā ar iesūtījuma ziņojumu C<Version $(VERSION)"
".>.  Vispirms jāatjaunina F<configure.ac>, jāiztīra un jāpārbūvē."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:897
msgid "make maintainer-tag"
msgstr "make maintainer-tag"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:899
msgid ""
"This tags the current HEAD commit with the tag C<v$(VERSION)> and one of the "
"messages:"
msgstr ""
"Tas atzīmē pašreizējo HEAD iesūtījumu ar tagu C<v$(VERSION)> un vienu no "
"ziņojumiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-hacking.pod:902
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Version $(VERSION) stable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Version $(VERSION) stable\n"
