#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-internals - architecture and internals of libguestfs"
msgstr "guestfs-internals - libguestfs arhitektūra un iekšējā darbība"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:7
msgid ""
"This manual page is for hackers who want to understand how libguestfs works "
"internally.  This is just a description of how libguestfs works now, and it "
"may change at any time in the future."
msgstr ""
"Šī rokasgrāmatas lapa paredzēta izstrādātājiem, kas vēlas saprast, kā "
"libguestfs darbojas iekšēji.  Tas ir tikai apraksts par to, kā libguestfs "
"darbojas tagad, un nākotnē tas jebkurā laikā var mainīties."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:11
msgid "ARCHITECTURE"
msgstr "ARHITEKTŪRA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:13
msgid ""
"Internally, libguestfs is implemented by running an appliance (a special "
"type of small virtual machine) using L<qemu(1)>.  Qemu runs as a child "
"process of the main program."
msgstr ""
"Iekšēji libguestfs ir realizēta, izpildot palīgsistēmu (īpaša veida nelielu "
"virtuālo mašīnu), izmantojot L<qemu(1)>.  Qemu darbojas kā galvenās "
"programmas bērnprocess."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ┌───────────────────┐\n"
" │ main program      │\n"
" │                   │\n"
" │                   │           child process / appliance\n"
" │                   │          ┌──────────────────────────┐\n"
" │                   │          │ qemu                     │\n"
" ├───────────────────┤   RPC    │      ┌─────────────────┐ │\n"
" │ libguestfs  ◀╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍▶ guestfsd        │ │\n"
" │                   │          │      ├─────────────────┤ │\n"
" └───────────────────┘          │      │ Linux kernel    │ │\n"
"                                │      └────────┬────────┘ │\n"
"                                └───────────────│──────────┘\n"
"                                                │\n"
"                                                │ virtio-scsi\n"
"                                         ┌──────┴──────┐\n"
"                                         │  Device or  │\n"
"                                         │  disk image │\n"
"                                         └─────────────┘\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ┌───────────────────┐\n"
" │ main program      │\n"
" │                   │\n"
" │                   │           child process / appliance\n"
" │                   │          ┌──────────────────────────┐\n"
" │                   │          │ qemu                     │\n"
" ├───────────────────┤   RPC    │      ┌─────────────────┐ │\n"
" │ libguestfs  ◀╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍▶ guestfsd        │ │\n"
" │                   │          │      ├─────────────────┤ │\n"
" └───────────────────┘          │      │ Linux kernel    │ │\n"
"                                │      └────────┬────────┘ │\n"
"                                └───────────────│──────────┘\n"
"                                                │\n"
"                                                │ virtio-scsi\n"
"                                         ┌──────┴──────┐\n"
"                                         │  Device or  │\n"
"                                         │  disk image │\n"
"                                         └─────────────┘\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:36
msgid ""
"The library, linked to the main program, creates the child process and hence "
"the appliance in the L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_launch> function."
msgstr ""
"Bibliotēka, kas saistīta ar galveno programmu, funkcijā L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_launch> izveido bērnprocesu un līdz ar to palīgsistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:39
msgid ""
"Inside the appliance is a Linux kernel and a complete stack of userspace "
"tools (such as LVM and ext2 programs) and a small controlling daemon called "
"L</guestfsd>.  The library talks to L</guestfsd> using remote procedure "
"calls (RPC).  There is a mostly one-to-one correspondence between libguestfs "
"API calls and RPC calls to the daemon.  Lastly the disk image(s) are "
"attached to the qemu process which translates device access by the "
"appliance’s Linux kernel into accesses to the image."
msgstr ""
"Palīgsistēmā ir Linux kodols un pilns lietotāja telpas rīku komplekts "
"(piemēram, LVM un ext2 programmas) un neliels vadošais dēmons L</guestfsd>.  "
"Bibliotēka sazinās ar L</guestfsd>, izmantojot attālās procedūras izsaukumus "
"(RPC).  Starp libguestfs API izsaukumiem un RPC izsaukumiem dēmonam pārsvarā "
"ir atbilstība viens pret vienu.  Visbeidzot, diska attēls(-i) ir pievienots "
"qemu procesam, kas palīgsistēmas Linux kodola ierīču piekļuves pārvērš "
"piekļuvēs attēlam."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:48
msgid ""
"A common misunderstanding is that the appliance \"is\" the virtual machine.  "
"Although the disk image you are attached to might also be used by some "
"virtual machine, libguestfs doesn't know or care about this.  (But you will "
"care if both libguestfs’s qemu process and your virtual machine are trying "
"to update the disk image at the same time, since these usually results in "
"massive disk corruption)."
msgstr ""
"Bieži sastopams pārpratums ir tas, ka palīgsistēma „ir” virtuālā mašīna.  "
"Lai gan diska attēlu, kam pievienojaties, var izmantot arī kāda virtuālā "
"mašīna, libguestfs par to nezina un tas viņu neinteresē.  (Bet jums tas būs "
"svarīgi, ja gan libguestfs qemu process, gan jūsu virtuālā mašīna vienlaikus "
"mēģina atjaunināt diska attēlu, jo tas parasti izraisa milzīgus diska "
"bojājumus.)"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:55
msgid "STATE MACHINE"
msgstr "STĀVOKĻU MAŠĪNA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:57
msgid "libguestfs uses a state machine to model the child process:"
msgstr "libguestfs bērnprocesa modelēšanai izmanto stāvokļu mašīnu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:59
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                         |\n"
"          guestfs_create / guestfs_create_flags\n"
"                         |\n"
"                         |\n"
"                     ____V_____\n"
"                    /          \\\n"
"                    |  CONFIG  |\n"
"                    \\__________/\n"
"                       ^   ^  \\\n"
"                       |    \\  \\ guestfs_launch\n"
"                       |    _\\__V______\n"
"                       |   /           \\\n"
"                       |   | LAUNCHING |\n"
"                       |   \\___________/\n"
"                       |       /\n"
"                       |  guestfs_launch\n"
"                       |     /\n"
"                     __|____V\n"
"                    /        \\\n"
"                    | READY  |\n"
"                    \\________/\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"                         |\n"
"          guestfs_create / guestfs_create_flags\n"
"                         |\n"
"                         |\n"
"                     ____V_____\n"
"                    /          \\\n"
"                    |  CONFIG  |\n"
"                    \\__________/\n"
"                       ^   ^  \\\n"
"                       |    \\  \\ guestfs_launch\n"
"                       |    _\\__V______\n"
"                       |   /           \\\n"
"                       |   | LAUNCHING |\n"
"                       |   \\___________/\n"
"                       |       /\n"
"                       |  guestfs_launch\n"
"                       |     /\n"
"                     __|____V\n"
"                    /        \\\n"
"                    | READY  |\n"
"                    \\________/\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:81
msgid ""
"The normal transitions are (1) CONFIG (when the handle is created, but there "
"is no child process), (2) LAUNCHING (when the child process is booting up), "
"(3) READY meaning the appliance is up, actions can be issued to, and carried "
"out by, the child process."
msgstr ""
"Parastās pārejas ir (1) CONFIG (kad rokturis ir izveidots, bet bērnprocesa "
"nav), (2) LAUNCHING (kad bērnprocess sāknējas), (3) READY, kas nozīmē, ka "
"palīgsistēma darbojas un bērnprocesam var nodot darbības, ko tas izpilda."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:86
msgid ""
"The guest may be killed by L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_kill_subprocess>, or may die "
"asynchronously at any time (eg. due to some internal error), and that causes "
"the state to transition back to CONFIG."
msgstr ""
"Viesi var nobeigt ar L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_kill_subprocess>, vai tas jebkurā "
"laikā var asinhroni beigt darbību (piem., kādas iekšējas kļūdas dēļ), un tas "
"izraisa stāvokļa pāreju atpakaļ uz CONFIG."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:90
msgid ""
"Configuration commands for qemu such as L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_path> can "
"only be issued when in the CONFIG state."
msgstr ""
"Qemu konfigurācijas komandas, piemēram, L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_path>, var "
"izdot tikai stāvoklī CONFIG."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:93
msgid ""
"The API offers one call that goes from CONFIG through LAUNCHING to READY.  "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_launch> blocks until the child process is READY to "
"accept commands (or until some failure or timeout).  "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_launch> internally moves the state from CONFIG to "
"LAUNCHING while it is running."
msgstr ""
"API piedāvā vienu izsaukumu, kas iet no CONFIG caur LAUNCHING uz READY.  "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_launch> bloķē, līdz bērnprocess ir READY pieņemt "
"komandas (vai līdz kādai kļūmei vai noildzei).  L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_launch> "
"darbības laikā iekšēji pārvieto stāvokli no CONFIG uz LAUNCHING."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:99
msgid ""
"API actions such as L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_mount> can only be issued when in "
"the READY state.  These API calls block waiting for the command to be "
"carried out.  There are no non-blocking versions, and no way to issue more "
"than one command per handle at the same time."
msgstr ""
"API darbības, piemēram, L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_mount>, var izdot tikai "
"stāvoklī READY.  Šie API izsaukumi bloķē, gaidot komandas izpildi.  Nav "
"nebloķējošu versiju un nav veida, kā vienam rokturim vienlaikus izdot vairāk "
"nekā vienu komandu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:104
msgid ""
"Finally, the child process sends asynchronous messages back to the main "
"program, such as kernel log messages.  You can register a callback to "
"receive these messages."
msgstr ""
"Visbeidzot, bērnprocess sūta galvenajai programmai asinhronus ziņojumus, "
"piemēram, kodola žurnāla ziņojumus.  Šo ziņojumu saņemšanai varat reģistrēt "
"atzvanu."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:108
msgid "INTERNALS"
msgstr "IEKŠĒJĀ DARBĪBA"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:110
msgid "APPLIANCE BOOT PROCESS"
msgstr "PALĪGSISTĒMAS SĀKNĒŠANAS PROCESS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:112
msgid ""
"This process has evolved and continues to evolve.  The description here "
"corresponds only to the current version of libguestfs and is provided for "
"information only."
msgstr ""
"Šis process ir attīstījies un turpina attīstīties.  Šeit sniegtais apraksts "
"atbilst tikai pašreizējai libguestfs versijai un ir tikai informatīvs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:116
msgid ""
"In order to follow the stages involved below, enable libguestfs debugging "
"(set the environment variable C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1>)."
msgstr ""
"Lai sekotu tālāk aprakstītajiem posmiem, iespējojiet libguestfs atkļūdošanu "
"(iestatiet vides mainīgo C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1>)."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:121
msgid "Create the appliance"
msgstr "Palīgsistēmas izveide"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:123
msgid ""
"C<supermin --build> is invoked to create the kernel, a small initrd and the "
"appliance."
msgstr ""
"Kodola, neliela initrd un palīgsistēmas izveidei tiek izsaukts C<supermin --"
"build>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:126
msgid ""
"The appliance is cached in F</var/tmp/.guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>> (or in another "
"directory if C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> or C<TMPDIR> are set)."
msgstr ""
"Palīgsistēma tiek kešota F</var/tmp/.guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>> (vai citā "
"direktorijā, ja iestatīts C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> vai C<TMPDIR>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:129
msgid ""
"For a complete description of how the appliance is created and cached, read "
"the L<supermin(1)> man page."
msgstr ""
"Pilnu aprakstu par to, kā palīgsistēma tiek veidota un kešota, lasiet "
"L<supermin(1)> rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:132
msgid "Start qemu and boot the kernel"
msgstr "Qemu palaišana un kodola sāknēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:134
msgid "qemu is invoked to boot the kernel."
msgstr "Kodola sāknēšanai tiek izsaukts qemu."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:136
msgid "Run the initrd"
msgstr "Initrd izpilde"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:138
msgid ""
"C<supermin --build> builds a small initrd.  The initrd is not the "
"appliance.  The purpose of the initrd is to load enough kernel modules in "
"order that the appliance itself can be mounted and started."
msgstr ""
"C<supermin --build> uzbūvē nelielu initrd.  Initrd nav palīgsistēma.  Initrd "
"mērķis ir ielādēt pietiekami daudz kodola moduļu, lai pašu palīgsistēmu "
"varētu montēt un palaist."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:142
msgid ""
"The initrd is a cpio archive called "
"F</var/tmp/.guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>/appliance.d/initrd>."
msgstr ""
"Initrd ir cpio arhīvs ar nosaukumu F</var/tmp/.guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>/"
"appliance.d/initrd>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:145
msgid ""
"When the initrd has started you will see messages showing that kernel "
"modules are being loaded, similar to this:"
msgstr ""
"Kad initrd ir palaists, redzēsiet ziņojumus par kodola moduļu ielādi, "
"līdzīgus šiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" supermin: ext2 mini initrd starting up\n"
" supermin: mounting /sys\n"
" supermin: internal insmod libcrc32c.ko\n"
" supermin: internal insmod crc32c-intel.ko\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" supermin: ext2 mini initrd starting up\n"
" supermin: mounting /sys\n"
" supermin: internal insmod libcrc32c.ko\n"
" supermin: internal insmod crc32c-intel.ko\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:153
msgid "Find and mount the appliance device"
msgstr "Palīgsistēmas ierīces atrašana un montēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:155
msgid ""
"The appliance is a sparse file containing an ext2 filesystem which contains "
"a familiar (although reduced in size) Linux operating system.  It would "
"normally be called F</var/tmp/.guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>/appliance.d/root>."
msgstr ""
"Palīgsistēma ir retināts fails ar ext2 failu sistēmu, kurā ir pazīstama (lai "
"gan samazināta izmēra) Linux operētājsistēma.  Parasti tās nosaukums būtu F</"
"var/tmp/.guestfs-E<lt>UIDE<gt>/appliance.d/root>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:160
msgid ""
"The regular disks being inspected by libguestfs are the first devices "
"exposed by qemu (eg. as F</dev/vda>)."
msgstr ""
"Parastie diski, ko inspicē libguestfs, ir pirmās qemu atklātās ierīces "
"(piem., kā F</dev/vda>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:163
msgid ""
"The last disk added to qemu is the appliance itself (eg. F</dev/vdb> if "
"there was only one regular disk)."
msgstr ""
"Pēdējais qemu pievienotais disks ir pati palīgsistēma (piem., F</dev/vdb>, "
"ja bija tikai viens parastais disks)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:166
msgid ""
"Thus the final job of the initrd is to locate the appliance disk, mount it, "
"and switch root into the appliance, and run F</init> from the appliance."
msgstr ""
"Tātad initrd pēdējais uzdevums ir atrast palīgsistēmas disku, montēt to, "
"pārslēgt sakni uz palīgsistēmu un izpildīt palīgsistēmas F</init>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:170
msgid "If this works successfully you will see messages such as:"
msgstr "Ja tas izdodas, redzēsiet tādus ziņojumus kā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:172
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" supermin: picked /sys/block/vdb/dev as root device\n"
" supermin: creating /dev/root as block special 252:16\n"
" supermin: mounting new root on /root\n"
" supermin: chroot\n"
" Starting /init script ...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" supermin: picked /sys/block/vdb/dev as root device\n"
" supermin: creating /dev/root as block special 252:16\n"
" supermin: mounting new root on /root\n"
" supermin: chroot\n"
" Starting /init script ...\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:178
msgid ""
"Note that C<Starting /init script ...> indicates that the appliance's init "
"script is now running."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka C<Starting /init script ...> norāda, ka palīgsistēmas init "
"skripts tagad darbojas."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:181
msgid "Initialize the appliance"
msgstr "Palīgsistēmas inicializēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:183
msgid ""
"The appliance itself now initializes itself.  This involves starting certain "
"processes like C<udev>, possibly printing some debug information, and "
"finally running the daemon (C<guestfsd>)."
msgstr ""
"Tagad palīgsistēma inicializē pati sevi.  Tas ietver dažu procesu, piemēram, "
"C<udev>, palaišanu, iespējams, kādas atkļūdošanas informācijas izdrukāšanu "
"un visbeidzot dēmona (C<guestfsd>) izpildi."

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:187
msgid "The daemon"
msgstr "Dēmons"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:189
msgid ""
"Finally the daemon (C<guestfsd>) runs inside the appliance.  If it runs you "
"should see:"
msgstr ""
"Visbeidzot dēmons (C<guestfsd>) darbojas palīgsistēmā.  Ja tas darbojas, "
"vajadzētu redzēt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:192
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" verbose daemon enabled\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" verbose daemon enabled\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:194
msgid ""
"The daemon expects to see a named virtio-serial port exposed by qemu and "
"connected on the other end to the library."
msgstr ""
"Dēmons sagaida, ka qemu atklās nosauktu virtio-serial portu, kas otrā galā "
"savienots ar bibliotēku."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:197
msgid ""
"The daemon connects to this port (and hence to the library) and sends a four "
"byte message C<GUESTFS_LAUNCH_FLAG>, which initiates the communication "
"protocol (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Dēmons savienojas ar šo portu (un līdz ar to ar bibliotēku) un nosūta četru "
"baitu ziņojumu C<GUESTFS_LAUNCH_FLAG>, kas uzsāk saziņas protokolu (skatiet "
"tālāk)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:203
msgid "COMMUNICATION PROTOCOL"
msgstr "SAZIŅAS PROTOKOLS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:205
msgid ""
"Don’t rely on using this protocol directly.  This section documents how it "
"currently works, but it may change at any time."
msgstr ""
"Nepaļaujieties uz šī protokola tiešu izmantošanu.  Šajā sadaļā dokumentēts, "
"kā tas darbojas pašlaik, taču tas jebkurā laikā var mainīties."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:208
msgid ""
"The protocol used to talk between the library and the daemon running inside "
"the qemu virtual machine is a simple RPC mechanism built on top of XDR (RFC "
"1014, RFC 1832, RFC 4506)."
msgstr ""
"Protokols saziņai starp bibliotēku un qemu virtuālajā mašīnā darbojošos "
"dēmonu ir vienkāršs RPC mehānisms, kas veidots virs XDR (RFC 1014, RFC 1832, "
"RFC 4506)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:212
msgid ""
"The detailed format of structures is in "
"F<common/protocol/guestfs_protocol.x> (note: this file is automatically "
"generated)."
msgstr ""
"Detalizēts struktūru formāts ir failā F<common/protocol/guestfs_protocol.x> "
"(piezīme: šis fails tiek ģenerēts automātiski)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:215
msgid ""
"There are two broad cases, ordinary functions that don’t have any C<FileIn> "
"and C<FileOut> parameters, which are handled with very simple request/reply "
"messages.  Then there are functions that have any C<FileIn> or C<FileOut> "
"parameters, which use the same request and reply messages, but they may also "
"be followed by files sent using a chunked encoding."
msgstr ""
"Ir divi vispārīgi gadījumi: parastas funkcijas bez parametriem C<FileIn> un "
"C<FileOut>, kas tiek apstrādātas ar ļoti vienkāršiem pieprasījuma/atbildes "
"ziņojumiem.  Un funkcijas ar parametriem C<FileIn> vai C<FileOut>, kas "
"izmanto tos pašus pieprasījuma un atbildes ziņojumus, taču tiem var sekot "
"arī faili, kas nosūtīti, izmantojot gabalu kodējumu."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:222
msgid "ORDINARY FUNCTIONS (NO FILEIN/FILEOUT PARAMS)"
msgstr "PARASTAS FUNKCIJAS (BEZ FILEIN/FILEOUT PARAMETRIEM)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:224
msgid "For ordinary functions, the request message is:"
msgstr "Parastām funkcijām pieprasījuma ziņojums ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:226
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" total length (header + arguments,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_args (encoded as XDR)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" total length (header + arguments,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_args (encoded as XDR)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:231
msgid ""
"The total length field allows the daemon to allocate a fixed size buffer "
"into which it slurps the rest of the message.  As a result, the total length "
"is limited to C<GUESTFS_MESSAGE_MAX> bytes (currently 4MB), which means the "
"effective size of any request is limited to somewhere under this size."
msgstr ""
"Kopējā garuma lauks ļauj dēmonam piešķirt fiksēta izmēra buferi, kurā tas "
"iesūc pārējo ziņojumu.  Rezultātā kopējais garums ir ierobežots līdz "
"C<GUESTFS_MESSAGE_MAX> baitiem (pašlaik 4MB), kas nozīmē, ka jebkura "
"pieprasījuma efektīvais izmērs ir ierobežots līdz kaut kam mazākam par šo "
"izmēru."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:237
msgid ""
"Note also that many functions don’t take any arguments, in which case the "
"C<guestfs_I<foo>_args> is completely omitted."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā arī, ka daudzas funkcijas nepieņem nekādus argumentus, un tādā "
"gadījumā C<guestfs_I<foo>_args> tiek pilnībā izlaists."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:240
msgid ""
"The header contains the procedure number (C<guestfs_proc>) which is how the "
"receiver knows what type of args structure to expect, or none at all."
msgstr ""
"Galvene satur procedūras numuru (C<guestfs_proc>), pēc kura saņēmējs zina, "
"kāda tipa argumentu struktūru gaidīt vai negaidīt nekādu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:244
msgid ""
"For functions that take optional arguments, the optional arguments are "
"encoded in the C<guestfs_I<foo>_args> structure in the same way as ordinary "
"arguments.  A bitmask in the header indicates which optional arguments are "
"meaningful.  The bitmask is also checked to see if it contains bits set "
"which the daemon does not know about (eg. if more optional arguments were "
"added in a later version of the library), and this causes the call to be "
"rejected."
msgstr ""
"Funkcijām, kas pieņem neobligātus argumentus, neobligātie argumenti tiek "
"kodēti struktūrā C<guestfs_I<foo>_args> tāpat kā parastie argumenti.  Bitu "
"maska galvenē norāda, kuri neobligātie argumenti ir nozīmīgi.  Bitu maska "
"tiek pārbaudīta arī, vai tajā nav iestatīti biti, par kuriem dēmons nezina "
"(piem., ja vēlākā bibliotēkas versijā pievienoti papildu neobligāti "
"argumenti), un tas izraisa izsaukuma noraidīšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:252
msgid "The reply message for ordinary functions is:"
msgstr "Parastu funkciju atbildes ziņojums ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:254
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" total length (header + ret,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_ret (encoded as XDR)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" total length (header + ret,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_ret (encoded as XDR)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:259
msgid ""
"As above the C<guestfs_I<foo>_ret> structure may be completely omitted for "
"functions that return no formal return values."
msgstr ""
"Kā iepriekš, struktūru C<guestfs_I<foo>_ret> var pilnībā izlaist funkcijām, "
"kas neatgriež formālas atgriešanas vērtības."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:262
msgid "As above the total length of the reply is limited to C<GUESTFS_MESSAGE_MAX>."
msgstr ""
"Kā iepriekš, atbildes kopējais garums ir ierobežots līdz "
"C<GUESTFS_MESSAGE_MAX>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:265
msgid ""
"In the case of an error, a flag is set in the header, and the reply message "
"is slightly changed:"
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas gadījumā galvenē tiek iestatīts karogs, un atbildes ziņojums ir "
"nedaudz mainīts:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:268
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" total length (header + error,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_error (encoded as XDR)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" total length (header + error,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_error (encoded as XDR)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:273
msgid ""
"The C<guestfs_message_error> structure contains the error message as a "
"string."
msgstr "Struktūra C<guestfs_message_error> satur kļūdas ziņojumu kā virkni."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:276
msgid "FUNCTIONS THAT HAVE FILEIN PARAMETERS"
msgstr "FUNKCIJAS AR FILEIN PARAMETRIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:278
msgid ""
"A C<FileIn> parameter indicates that we transfer a file I<into> the guest.  "
"The normal request message is sent (see above).  However this is followed by "
"a sequence of file chunks."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<FileIn> norāda, ka pārsūtām failu I<uz> viesi.  Tiek nosūtīts "
"parastais pieprasījuma ziņojums (skatiet iepriekš).  Tomēr tam seko failu "
"gabalu secība."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:282
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" total length (header + arguments,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself,\n"
"      and not including the chunks)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_args (encoded as XDR)\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileIn param #0\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileIn param #1 etc.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" total length (header + arguments,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself,\n"
"      and not including the chunks)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_args (encoded as XDR)\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileIn param #0\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileIn param #1 etc.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:290
msgid "The \"sequence of chunks\" is:"
msgstr "„Gabalu secība” ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:292
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" length of chunk (not including length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_chunk (encoded as XDR)\n"
" length of chunk\n"
" struct guestfs_chunk (encoded as XDR)\n"
"   ...\n"
" length of chunk\n"
" struct guestfs_chunk (with data.data_len == 0)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" length of chunk (not including length word itself)\n"
" struct guestfs_chunk (encoded as XDR)\n"
" length of chunk\n"
" struct guestfs_chunk (encoded as XDR)\n"
"   ...\n"
" length of chunk\n"
" struct guestfs_chunk (with data.data_len == 0)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:300
msgid ""
"The final chunk has the C<data_len> field set to zero.  Additionally a flag "
"is set in the final chunk to indicate either successful completion or early "
"cancellation."
msgstr ""
"Pēdējam gabalam lauks C<data_len> ir iestatīts uz nulli.  Turklāt pēdējā "
"gabalā tiek iestatīts karogs, kas norāda veiksmīgu pabeigšanu vai agrīnu "
"atcelšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:304
msgid ""
"At time of writing there are no functions that have more than one FileIn "
"parameter.  However this is (theoretically) supported, by sending the "
"sequence of chunks for each FileIn parameter one after another (from left to "
"right)."
msgstr ""
"Rakstīšanas brīdī nav funkciju ar vairāk nekā vienu FileIn parametru.  Tomēr "
"tas (teorētiski) tiek atbalstīts, katram FileIn parametram nosūtot gabalu "
"secību vienu pēc otras (no kreisās uz labo)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:309
msgid ""
"Both the library (sender) I<and> the daemon (receiver) may cancel the "
"transfer.  The library does this by sending a chunk with a special flag set "
"to indicate cancellation.  When the daemon sees this, it cancels the whole "
"RPC, does I<not> send any reply, and goes back to reading the next request."
msgstr ""
"Gan bibliotēka (sūtītājs), I<gan> dēmons (saņēmējs) var atcelt pārsūtīšanu.  "
"Bibliotēka to dara, nosūtot gabalu ar īpašu karogu, kas norāda atcelšanu.  "
"Kad dēmons to redz, tas atceļ visu RPC, I<nesūta> nekādu atbildi un "
"atgriežas pie nākamā pieprasījuma lasīšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:315
msgid ""
"The daemon may also cancel.  It does this by writing a special word "
"C<GUESTFS_CANCEL_FLAG> to the socket.  The library listens for this during "
"the transfer, and if it gets it, it will cancel the transfer (it sends a "
"cancel chunk).  The special word is chosen so that even if cancellation "
"happens right at the end of the transfer (after the library has finished "
"writing and has started listening for the reply), the \"spurious\" cancel "
"flag will not be confused with the reply message."
msgstr ""
"Arī dēmons var atcelt.  Tas to dara, ierakstot ligzdā īpašu vārdu "
"C<GUESTFS_CANCEL_FLAG>.  Bibliotēka pārsūtīšanas laikā to gaida un, ja "
"saņem, atceļ pārsūtīšanu (tā nosūta atcelšanas gabalu).  Īpašais vārds ir "
"izvēlēts tā, lai pat tad, ja atcelšana notiek tieši pārsūtīšanas beigās (kad "
"bibliotēka ir beigusi rakstīt un sākusi gaidīt atbildi), „liekais” "
"atcelšanas karogs netiktu sajaukts ar atbildes ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:324
msgid ""
"This protocol allows the transfer of arbitrary sized files (no 32 bit "
"limit), and also files where the size is not known in advance (eg. from "
"pipes or sockets).  However the chunks are rather small "
"(C<GUESTFS_MAX_CHUNK_SIZE>), so that neither the library nor the daemon need "
"to keep much in memory."
msgstr ""
"Šis protokols ļauj pārsūtīt patvaļīga izmēra failus (bez 32 bitu "
"ierobežojuma), kā arī failus, kuru izmērs iepriekš nav zināms (piem., no "
"kanāliem vai ligzdām).  Tomēr gabali ir diezgan mazi "
"(C<GUESTFS_MAX_CHUNK_SIZE>), lai ne bibliotēkai, ne dēmonam nebūtu daudz "
"jātur atmiņā."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:330
msgid "FUNCTIONS THAT HAVE FILEOUT PARAMETERS"
msgstr "FUNKCIJAS AR FILEOUT PARAMETRIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:332
msgid ""
"The protocol for FileOut parameters is exactly the same as for FileIn "
"parameters, but with the roles of daemon and library reversed."
msgstr ""
"FileOut parametru protokols ir tieši tāds pats kā FileIn parametriem, tikai "
"ar apmainītām dēmona un bibliotēkas lomām."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:335
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" total length (header + ret,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself,\n"
"      and not including the chunks)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_ret (encoded as XDR)\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileOut param #0\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileOut param #1 etc.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" total length (header + ret,\n"
"      but not including the length word itself,\n"
"      and not including the chunks)\n"
" struct guestfs_message_header (encoded as XDR)\n"
" struct guestfs_<foo>_ret (encoded as XDR)\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileOut param #0\n"
" sequence of chunks for FileOut param #1 etc.\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:343
msgid "INITIAL MESSAGE"
msgstr "SĀKOTNĒJAIS ZIŅOJUMS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:345
msgid ""
"When the daemon launches it sends an initial word (C<GUESTFS_LAUNCH_FLAG>) "
"which indicates that the guest and daemon is alive.  This is what "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_launch> waits for."
msgstr ""
"Kad dēmons tiek palaists, tas nosūta sākotnēju vārdu (C<GUESTFS_LAUNCH_FLAG>)"
", kas norāda, ka viesis un dēmons ir dzīvi.  Tieši to gaida L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_launch>."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:349
msgid "PROGRESS NOTIFICATION MESSAGES"
msgstr "PROGRESA PAZIŅOJUMU ZIŅOJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:351
msgid ""
"The daemon may send progress notification messages at any time.  These are "
"distinguished by the normal length word being replaced by "
"C<GUESTFS_PROGRESS_FLAG>, followed by a fixed size progress message."
msgstr ""
"Dēmons jebkurā laikā var sūtīt progresa paziņojumu ziņojumus.  Tos atšķir ar "
"to, ka parastā garuma vārda vietā ir C<GUESTFS_PROGRESS_FLAG>, kam seko "
"fiksēta izmēra progresa ziņojums."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:355
msgid ""
"The library turns them into progress callbacks (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/GUESTFS_EVENT_PROGRESS>) if there is a callback registered, or "
"discards them if not."
msgstr ""
"Bibliotēka tos pārvērš progresa atzvanos (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/"
"GUESTFS_EVENT_PROGRESS>), ja ir reģistrēts atzvans, vai citādi tos atmet."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:359
msgid ""
"The daemon self-limits the frequency of progress messages it sends (see "
"C<daemon/proto.c:notify_progress>).  Not all calls generate progress "
"messages."
msgstr ""
"Dēmons pats ierobežo nosūtīto progresa ziņojumu biežumu (skatiet C<daemon/"
"proto.c:notify_progress>).  Ne visi izsaukumi ģenerē progresa ziņojumus."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:363
msgid "FIXED APPLIANCE"
msgstr "FIKSĒTA PALĪGSISTĒMA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:365
msgid ""
"When libguestfs (or libguestfs tools) are run, they search a path looking "
"for an appliance.  The path is built into libguestfs, or can be set using "
"the C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH> environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Kad tiek izpildīts libguestfs (vai libguestfs rīki), tie meklē palīgsistēmu "
"ceļā.  Ceļš ir iebūvēts libguestfs, vai to var iestatīt ar vides mainīgo "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:369
msgid ""
"Normally a supermin appliance is located on this path (see "
"L<supermin(1)/SUPERMIN APPLIANCE>).  libguestfs reconstructs this into a "
"full appliance by running C<supermin --build>."
msgstr ""
"Parasti šajā ceļā atrodas supermin palīgsistēma (skatiet L<supermin(1)/"
"SUPERMIN APPLIANCE>).  libguestfs to pārveido par pilnu palīgsistēmu, "
"izpildot C<supermin --build>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:373
msgid ""
"However, a simpler \"fixed appliance\" can also be used.  libguestfs detects "
"this by looking for a directory on the path containing all the following "
"files:"
msgstr ""
"Tomēr var izmantot arī vienkāršāku „fiksētu palīgsistēmu”.  libguestfs to "
"nosaka, meklējot ceļā direktoriju ar visiem šiem failiem:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:379
msgid "* F<kernel>"
msgstr "* F<kernel>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:381
msgid "* F<initrd>"
msgstr "* F<initrd>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:383
msgid "* F<root>"
msgstr "* F<root>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:385
msgid "* F<README.fixed> (note that it B<must> be present as well)"
msgstr "* F<README.fixed> (ņemiet vērā, ka arī tam B<jābūt>)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:389
msgid ""
"If the fixed appliance is found, libguestfs skips supermin entirely and just "
"runs the virtual machine (using qemu or the current backend, see "
"L<guestfs(3)/BACKEND>) with the kernel, initrd and root disk from the fixed "
"appliance."
msgstr ""
"Ja tiek atrasta fiksētā palīgsistēma, libguestfs pilnībā izlaiž supermin un "
"vienkārši palaiž virtuālo mašīnu (izmantojot qemu vai pašreizējo "
"aizmugursistēmu, skatiet L<guestfs(3)/AIZMUGURSISTĒMA>) ar fiksētās "
"palīgsistēmas kodolu, initrd un saknes disku."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:394
msgid ""
"Thus the fixed appliance can be used when a platform or a Linux distribution "
"does not support supermin.  You build the fixed appliance on a platform that "
"does support supermin using L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>, copy it "
"over, and use that to run libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Tādējādi fiksēto palīgsistēmu var izmantot, ja platforma vai Linux "
"distribūcija neatbalsta supermin.  Fiksēto palīgsistēmu uzbūvējat platformā, "
"kas atbalsta supermin, izmantojot L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>, "
"nokopējat to un izmantojat libguestfs izpildei."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-internals.pod:402
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-hacking(1)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, "
"L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)>, L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-hacking(1)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<libguestfs-"
"test-tool(1)>, L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-performance - engineering libguestfs for greatest performance"
msgstr "guestfs-performance - libguestfs pielāgošana vislielākajai veiktspējai"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:7
msgid ""
"This page documents how to get the greatest performance out of libguestfs, "
"especially when you expect to use libguestfs to manipulate thousands of "
"virtual machines or disk images."
msgstr ""
"Šajā lapā dokumentēts, kā iegūt vislielāko veiktspēju no libguestfs, it "
"īpaši, ja plānojat izmantot libguestfs tūkstošiem virtuālo mašīnu vai disku "
"attēlu apstrādei."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:11
msgid ""
"Three main areas are covered. Libguestfs runs an appliance (a small Linux "
"distribution) inside qemu/KVM.  The first two areas are: minimizing the time "
"taken to start this appliance, and the number of times the appliance has to "
"be started.  The third area is shortening the time taken for inspection of "
"VMs."
msgstr ""
"Aplūkotas trīs galvenās jomas. Libguestfs izpilda palīgsistēmu (nelielu "
"Linux distribūciju) qemu/KVM.  Pirmās divas jomas ir: šīs palīgsistēmas "
"palaišanas laika samazināšana un palaišanas reižu skaita samazināšana.  "
"Trešā joma ir VM inspicēšanai vajadzīgā laika saīsināšana."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:17
msgid "BASELINE MEASUREMENTS"
msgstr "BĀZES MĒRĪJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:19
msgid "Before making changes to how you use libguestfs, take baseline measurements."
msgstr "Pirms maināt libguestfs izmantošanas veidu, veiciet bāzes mērījumus."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:22
msgid "Baseline: Starting the appliance"
msgstr "Bāze: palīgsistēmas palaišana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:24
msgid "On an unloaded machine, time how long it takes to start up the appliance:"
msgstr ""
"Neslogotā datorā izmēriet, cik ilgs laiks vajadzīgs palīgsistēmas palaišanai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:27 docs/guestfs-performance.pod:175
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" time guestfish -a /dev/null run\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" time guestfish -a /dev/null run\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:29
msgid ""
"Run this command several times in a row and discard the first few runs, so "
"that you are measuring a typical \"hot cache\" case."
msgstr ""
"Izpildiet šo komandu vairākas reizes pēc kārtas un atmetiet pirmās izpildes, "
"lai mērītu tipisku „karstās kešatmiņas” gadījumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:32
msgid ""
"I<Side note for developers:> There is a program called F<boot-benchmark> in "
"L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs-analysis-tools> which does the "
"same thing, but performs multiple runs and prints the mean and standard "
"deviation."
msgstr ""
"I<Piezīme izstrādātājiem:> L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs-"
"analysis-tools> ir programma F<boot-benchmark>, kas dara to pašu, bet veic "
"vairākas izpildes un izdrukā vidējo vērtību un standartnovirzi."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:38 docs/guestfs-performance.pod:71
msgid "Explanation"
msgstr "Paskaidrojums"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:40
msgid ""
"The guestfish command above starts up the libguestfs appliance on a null "
"disk, and then immediately shuts it down.  The first time you run the "
"command, it will create an appliance and cache it (usually under "
"F</var/tmp/.guestfs-*>).  Subsequent runs should reuse the cached appliance."
msgstr ""
"Iepriekšējā guestfish komanda palaiž libguestfs palīgsistēmu ar null disku "
"un uzreiz to izslēdz.  Pirmajā komandas izpildes reizē tā izveidos "
"palīgsistēmu un kešos to (parasti zem F</var/tmp/.guestfs-*>).  Nākamajās "
"izpildēs vajadzētu atkārtoti izmantot kešoto palīgsistēmu."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:46 docs/guestfs-performance.pod:82
msgid "Expected results"
msgstr "Gaidāmie rezultāti"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:48
msgid ""
"You should expect to be getting times under 6 seconds.  If the times you see "
"on an unloaded machine are above this, then see the section "
"L</TROUBLESHOOTING POOR PERFORMANCE> below."
msgstr ""
"Jāsagaida laiki zem 6 sekundēm.  Ja neslogotā datorā redzamie laiki ir "
"lielāki, skatiet sadaļu L</SLIKTAS VEIKTSPĒJAS PROBLĒMU NOVĒRŠANA> tālāk."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:52
msgid "Baseline: Performing inspection of a guest"
msgstr "Bāze: viesa inspicēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:54
msgid ""
"For this test you will need an unloaded machine and at least one real guest "
"or disk image.  If you are planning to use libguestfs against only X guests "
"(eg. X = Windows), then using an X guest here would be most appropriate.  If "
"you are planning to run libguestfs against a mix of guests, then use a mix "
"of guests for testing here."
msgstr ""
"Šim testam būs vajadzīgs neslogots dators un vismaz viens reāls viesis vai "
"diska attēls.  Ja plānojat izmantot libguestfs tikai ar X viesiem (piem., X "
"= Windows), šeit vispiemērotāk būtu izmantot X viesi.  Ja plānojat izmantot "
"libguestfs ar dažādu viesu kopumu, testēšanai izmantojiet dažādu viesu "
"kopumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:60
msgid ""
"Time how long it takes to perform inspection and mount the disks of the "
"guest.  Use the first command if you will be using disk images, and the "
"second command if you will be using libvirt."
msgstr ""
"Izmēriet, cik ilgs laiks vajadzīgs inspicēšanai un viesa disku montēšanai.  "
"Izmantojiet pirmo komandu, ja izmantosiet disku attēlus, un otro, ja "
"izmantosiet libvirt."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" time guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i exit\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" time guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i exit\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:66
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" time guestfish --ro -d GuestName -i exit\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" time guestfish --ro -d GuestName -i exit\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:68
msgid ""
"Run the command several times in a row and discard the first few runs, so "
"that you are measuring a typical \"hot cache\" case."
msgstr ""
"Izpildiet komandu vairākas reizes pēc kārtas un atmetiet pirmās izpildes, "
"lai mērītu tipisku „karstās kešatmiņas” gadījumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:73
msgid ""
"This command starts up the libguestfs appliance on the named disk image or "
"libvirt guest, performs libguestfs inspection on it (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION>), mounts the guest’s disks, then discards all these "
"results and shuts down."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda palaiž libguestfs palīgsistēmu ar nosaukto diska attēlu vai "
"libvirt viesi, veic tajā libguestfs inspicēšanu (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/"
"INSPICĒŠANA>), montē viesa diskus, pēc tam atmet visus šos rezultātus un "
"izslēdzas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:78
msgid ""
"The first time you run the command, it will create an appliance and cache it "
"(usually under F</var/tmp/.guestfs-*>).  Subsequent runs should reuse the "
"cached appliance."
msgstr ""
"Pirmajā komandas izpildes reizē tā izveidos palīgsistēmu un kešos to "
"(parasti zem F</var/tmp/.guestfs-*>).  Nākamajās izpildēs vajadzētu "
"atkārtoti izmantot kešoto palīgsistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:84
msgid ""
"You should expect times which are E<le> 5 seconds greater than measured in "
"the first baseline test above.  (For example, if the first baseline test ran "
"in 5 seconds, then this test should run in E<le> 10 seconds)."
msgstr ""
"Jāsagaida laiki, kas ir par E<le> 5 sekundēm lielāki nekā iepriekšējā "
"pirmajā bāzes testā.  (Piemēram, ja pirmais bāzes tests izpildījās 5 "
"sekundēs, šim testam jāizpildās E<le> 10 sekundēs.)"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:89
msgid "UNDERSTANDING THE APPLIANCE AND WHEN IT IS BUILT/CACHED"
msgstr "PALĪGSISTĒMAS IZPRATNE UN KAD TĀ TIEK BŪVĒTA/KEŠOTA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:91
msgid ""
"The first time you use libguestfs, it will build and cache an appliance.  "
"This is usually in F</var/tmp/.guestfs-*>, unless you have set C<$TMPDIR> or "
"C<$LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> in which case it will be under that temporary "
"directory."
msgstr ""
"Pirmajā libguestfs izmantošanas reizē tā uzbūvēs un kešos palīgsistēmu.  "
"Parasti tā atrodas F</var/tmp/.guestfs-*>, ja vien nav iestatīts C<$TMPDIR> "
"vai C<$LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> — tad tā būs zem šīs pagaidu direktorijas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:96
msgid ""
"For more information about how the appliance is constructed, see "
"L<supermin(1)/SUPERMIN APPLIANCES>."
msgstr ""
"Plašāku informāciju par to, kā palīgsistēma tiek veidota, skatiet L<supermin"
"(1)/SUPERMIN APPLIANCES>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:99
msgid ""
"Every time libguestfs runs it will check that no host files used by the "
"appliance have changed.  If any have, then the appliance is rebuilt.  This "
"usually happens when a package is installed or updated on the host "
"(eg. using programs like C<yum> or C<apt-get>).  The reason for "
"reconstructing the appliance is security: the new program that has been "
"installed might contain a security fix, and so we want to include the fixed "
"program in the appliance automatically."
msgstr ""
"Katru reizi, kad libguestfs tiek izpildīta, tā pārbauda, vai nav mainījušies "
"palīgsistēmas izmantotie resursdatora faili.  Ja kāds ir mainījies, "
"palīgsistēma tiek pārbūvēta.  Parasti tas notiek, kad resursdatorā tiek "
"instalēta vai atjaunināta pakotne (piem., ar tādām programmām kā C<yum> vai "
"C<apt-get>).  Palīgsistēmas pārbūves iemesls ir drošība: jaunajā instalētajā "
"programmā var būt drošības labojums, tāpēc vēlamies izlaboto programmu "
"automātiski iekļaut palīgsistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:107
msgid "These are the performance implications:"
msgstr "Ietekme uz veiktspēju ir šāda:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:113
msgid ""
"The process of building (or rebuilding) the cached appliance is slow, and "
"you can avoid this happening by using a fixed appliance (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Kešotās palīgsistēmas būvēšanas (vai pārbūvēšanas) process ir lēns, un no tā "
"var izvairīties, izmantojot fiksētu palīgsistēmu (skatiet tālāk)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:119
msgid ""
"If not using a fixed appliance, be aware that updating software on the host "
"will cause a one time rebuild of the appliance."
msgstr ""
"Ja neizmantojat fiksētu palīgsistēmu, ņemiet vērā, ka programmatūras "
"atjaunināšana resursdatorā izraisīs vienreizēju palīgsistēmas pārbūvi."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:124
msgid ""
"F</var/tmp> (or C<$TMPDIR>, C<$LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>) should be on a fast "
"disk, and have plenty of space for the appliance."
msgstr ""
"F</var/tmp> (vai C<$TMPDIR>, C<$LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>) jāatrodas ātrā diskā, "
"un tajā jābūt daudz vietas palīgsistēmai."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:129
msgid "USING A FIXED APPLIANCE"
msgstr "FIKSĒTAS PALĪGSISTĒMAS IZMANTOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:131
msgid ""
"To fully control when the appliance is built, you can build a fixed "
"appliance.  This appliance should be stored on a fast local disk."
msgstr ""
"Lai pilnībā kontrolētu, kad palīgsistēma tiek būvēta, varat uzbūvēt fiksētu "
"palīgsistēmu.  Šī palīgsistēma jāglabā ātrā lokālā diskā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:134
msgid "To build the appliance, run the command:"
msgstr "Lai uzbūvētu palīgsistēmu, izpildiet komandu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance <directory>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance <directory>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:138
msgid ""
"replacing C<E<lt>directoryE<gt>> with the name of a directory where the "
"appliance will be stored (normally you would name a subdirectory, for "
"example: F</usr/local/lib/guestfs/appliance> or F</dev/shm/appliance>)."
msgstr ""
"aizstājot C<E<lt>directoryE<gt>> ar direktorijas nosaukumu, kur palīgsistēma "
"tiks glabāta (parasti norādītu apakšdirektoriju, piemēram: F</usr/local/lib/"
"guestfs/appliance> vai F</dev/shm/appliance>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:143
msgid ""
"Then set C<$LIBGUESTFS_PATH> (and ensure this environment variable is set in "
"your libguestfs program), or modify your program so it calls "
"C<guestfs_set_path>.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam iestatiet C<$LIBGUESTFS_PATH> (un nodrošiniet, ka šis vides "
"mainīgais ir iestatīts jūsu libguestfs programmā) vai mainiet programmu, lai "
"tā izsauktu C<guestfs_set_path>.  Piemēram:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:149
msgid ""
"Now you can run libguestfs programs, virt tools, guestfish etc. as normal.  "
"The programs will use your fixed appliance, and will not ever build, "
"rebuild, or cache their own appliance."
msgstr ""
"Tagad libguestfs programmas, virt rīkus, guestfish u. c. var izpildīt kā "
"parasti.  Programmas izmantos jūsu fiksēto palīgsistēmu un nekad nebūvēs, "
"nepārbūvēs vai nekešos savu palīgsistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:153
msgid ""
"(For detailed information on this subject, see: "
"L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>)."
msgstr ""
"(Detalizētu informāciju par šo tēmu skatiet: L<libguestfs-make-fixed-"
"appliance(1)>.)"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:156
msgid "Performance of the fixed appliance"
msgstr "Fiksētās palīgsistēmas veiktspēja"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:158
msgid ""
"In our testing we did not find that using a fixed appliance gave any "
"measurable performance benefit, even when the appliance was located in "
"memory (ie. on F</dev/shm>).  However there are two points to consider:"
msgstr ""
"Mūsu testos fiksētās palīgsistēmas izmantošana nedeva izmērāmu veiktspējas "
"ieguvumu, pat ja palīgsistēma atradās atmiņā (t. i., F</dev/shm>).  Tomēr "
"jāņem vērā divi punkti:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:167
msgid ""
"Using a fixed appliance stops libguestfs from ever rebuilding the appliance, "
"meaning that libguestfs will have more predictable start-up times."
msgstr ""
"Fiksētas palīgsistēmas izmantošana neļauj libguestfs nekad pārbūvēt "
"palīgsistēmu, kas nozīmē, ka libguestfs palaišanas laiki būs paredzamāki."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:173
msgid "The appliance is loaded on demand.  A simple test such as:"
msgstr ""
"Palīgsistēma tiek ielādēta pēc pieprasījuma.  Vienkāršs tests, piemēram:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:177
msgid ""
"does not load very much of the appliance.  A real libguestfs program using "
"complicated API calls would demand-load a lot more of the appliance.  Being "
"able to store the appliance in a specified location makes the performance "
"more predictable."
msgstr ""
"neielādē daudz palīgsistēmas.  Reāla libguestfs programma ar sarežģītiem API "
"izsaukumiem pēc pieprasījuma ielādētu daudz vairāk palīgsistēmas.  Iespēja "
"glabāt palīgsistēmu norādītā vietā padara veiktspēju paredzamāku."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:184
msgid "REDUCING THE NUMBER OF TIMES THE APPLIANCE IS LAUNCHED"
msgstr "PALĪGSISTĒMAS PALAIŠANAS REIŽU SKAITA SAMAZINĀŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:186
msgid ""
"By far the most effective, though not always the simplest way to get good "
"performance is to ensure that the appliance is launched the minimum number "
"of times.  This will probably involve changing your libguestfs application."
msgstr ""
"Neapšaubāmi efektīvākais, lai gan ne vienmēr vienkāršākais veids, kā iegūt "
"labu veiktspēju, ir nodrošināt, ka palīgsistēma tiek palaista minimālo reižu "
"skaitu.  Tas, visticamāk, nozīmēs jūsu libguestfs lietotnes maiņu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:191
msgid ""
"Try to call C<guestfs_launch> at most once per target virtual machine or "
"disk image."
msgstr ""
"Mēģiniet izsaukt C<guestfs_launch> ne vairāk kā vienreiz katrai mērķa "
"virtuālajai mašīnai vai diska attēlam."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:194
msgid ""
"Instead of using a separate instance of L<guestfish(1)> to make a series of "
"changes to the same guest, use a single instance of guestfish and/or use the "
"guestfish I<--listen> option."
msgstr ""
"Tā vietā, lai izmantotu atsevišķu L<guestfish(1)> instanci virknei izmaiņu "
"vienā viesī, izmantojiet vienu guestfish instanci un/vai guestfish opciju "
"I<--listen>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:198
msgid ""
"Consider writing your program as a daemon which holds a guest open while "
"making a series of changes.  Or marshal all the operations you want to "
"perform before opening the guest."
msgstr ""
"Apsveriet iespēju rakstīt programmu kā dēmonu, kas tur viesi atvērtu, veicot "
"virkni izmaiņu.  Vai arī sagatavojiet visas veicamās darbības pirms viesa "
"atvēršanas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:202
msgid ""
"You can also try adding disks from multiple guests to a single appliance.  "
"Before trying this, note the following points:"
msgstr ""
"Varat arī mēģināt vienai palīgsistēmai pievienot vairāku viesu diskus.  "
"Pirms to mēģināt, ņemiet vērā šos punktus:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:209
msgid ""
"Adding multiple guests to one appliance is a security problem because it may "
"allow one guest to interfere with the disks of another guest.  Only do it if "
"you trust all the guests, or if you can group guests by trust."
msgstr ""
"Vairāku viesu pievienošana vienai palīgsistēmai ir drošības problēma, jo tā "
"var ļaut vienam viesim traucēt cita viesa diskus.  Dariet to tikai tad, ja "
"uzticaties visiem viesiem vai varat grupēt viesus pēc uzticamības."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:216
msgid ""
"There is a hard limit to the number of disks you can add to a single "
"appliance.  Call L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_max_disks> to get this limit.  For "
"further information see L<guestfs(3)/LIMITS>."
msgstr ""
"Ir stingrs ierobežojums diskiem, ko var pievienot vienai palīgsistēmai.  Lai "
"iegūtu šo ierobežojumu, izsauciet L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_max_disks>.  Plašāku "
"informāciju skatiet L<guestfs(3)/LIMITI>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:222
msgid ""
"Using libguestfs this way is complicated.  Disks can have unexpected "
"interactions: for example, if two guests use the same UUID for a filesystem "
"(because they were cloned), or have volume groups with the same name (but "
"see C<guestfs_lvm_set_filter>)."
msgstr ""
"Šāda libguestfs izmantošana ir sarežģīta.  Diskiem var būt negaidītas "
"mijiedarbības: piemēram, ja divi viesi izmanto vienu un to pašu failu "
"sistēmas UUID (jo tie tika klonēti) vai ja tiem ir sējumu grupas ar vienādu "
"nosaukumu (bet skatiet C<guestfs_lvm_set_filter>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:229
msgid ""
"L<virt-df(1)> adds multiple disks by default, so the source code for this "
"program would be a good place to start."
msgstr ""
"L<virt-df(1)> pēc noklusējuma pievieno vairākus diskus, tāpēc šīs programmas "
"pirmkods būtu laba vieta, kur sākt."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:232
msgid "SHORTENING THE TIME TAKEN FOR INSPECTION OF VMs"
msgstr "VM INSPICĒŠANAS LAIKA SAĪSINĀŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:234
msgid ""
"The main advice is obvious: Do not perform inspection (which is expensive) "
"unless you need the results."
msgstr ""
"Galvenais padoms ir acīmredzams: neveiciet inspicēšanu (kas ir dārga), ja "
"vien jums nav vajadzīgi rezultāti."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:237
msgid ""
"If you previously performed inspection on the guest, then it may be safe to "
"cache and reuse the results from last time."
msgstr ""
"Ja iepriekš veicāt viesa inspicēšanu, var būt droši kešot un atkārtoti "
"izmantot iepriekšējās reizes rezultātus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:240
msgid ""
"Some disks don’t need to be inspected at all: for example, if you are "
"creating a disk image, or if the disk image is not a VM, or if the disk "
"image has a known layout."
msgstr ""
"Dažus diskus nemaz nav jāinspicē: piemēram, ja veidojat diska attēlu, ja "
"diska attēls nav VM vai ja diska attēlam ir zināms izkārtojums."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:244
msgid ""
"Even when basic inspection (C<guestfs_inspect_os>) is required, auxiliary "
"inspection operations may be avoided:"
msgstr ""
"Pat ja nepieciešama pamata inspicēšana (C<guestfs_inspect_os>), no papildu "
"inspicēšanas darbībām var izvairīties:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:251
msgid "Mounting disks is only necessary to get further filesystem information."
msgstr ""
"Disku montēšana ir nepieciešama tikai papildu failu sistēmas informācijas "
"iegūšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:256
msgid ""
"Listing applications (C<guestfs_inspect_list_applications>) is an expensive "
"operation on Linux, but almost free on Windows."
msgstr ""
"Lietotņu uzskaitīšana (C<guestfs_inspect_list_applications>) Linux ir dārga "
"darbība, bet Windows gandrīz bezmaksas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:261
msgid ""
"Generating a guest icon (C<guestfs_inspect_get_icon>) is cheap on Linux but "
"expensive on Windows."
msgstr ""
"Viesa ikonas ģenerēšana (C<guestfs_inspect_get_icon>) Linux ir lēta, bet "
"Windows dārga."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:266
msgid "PARALLEL APPLIANCES"
msgstr "PARALĒLAS PALĪGSISTĒMAS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:268
msgid ""
"Libguestfs appliances are mostly I/O bound and you can launch multiple "
"appliances in parallel.  Provided there is enough free memory, there should "
"be little difference in launching 1 appliance vs N appliances in parallel."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs palīgsistēmas pārsvarā ierobežo I/O, un vairākas palīgsistēmas "
"var palaist paralēli.  Ja ir pietiekami daudz brīvas atmiņas, starp 1 "
"palīgsistēmas un N palīgsistēmu paralēlu palaišanu vajadzētu būt nelielai "
"atšķirībai."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:273
msgid ""
"On a 2-core (4-thread) laptop with 16 GB of RAM, using the (not especially "
"realistic) test Perl script below, the following plot shows excellent "
"scalability when running between 1 and 20 appliances in parallel:"
msgstr ""
"Divkodolu (4 pavedienu) klēpjdatorā ar 16 GB RAM, izmantojot (ne īpaši "
"reālistisko) tālāk doto testa Perl skriptu, šis grafiks rāda izcilu "
