#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:317
msgid ""
"It is possible to run many more than 20 appliances in parallel, but if you "
"are using the libvirt backend then you should be aware that out of the box "
"libvirt limits the number of client connections to 20."
msgstr ""
"Paralēli var darbināt daudz vairāk nekā 20 palīgsistēmas, taču, ja "
"izmantojat libvirt aizmugursistēmu, ņemiet vērā, ka libvirt pēc noklusējuma "
"ierobežo klientu savienojumu skaitu līdz 20."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:321
msgid ""
"The simple Perl script below was used to collect the data for the plot "
"above, but there is much more information on this subject, including more "
"advanced test scripts and graphs, available in the following blog postings:"
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotais vienkāršais Perl skripts tika izmantots iepriekšējā grafika "
"datu vākšanai, taču par šo tēmu ir daudz vairāk informācijas, ieskaitot "
"sarežģītākus testa skriptus un grafikus, šajos emuāra ierakstos:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:326
msgid ""
"L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/multiple-libguestfs-appliances-in-parallel-part-1/> "
"L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/multiple-libguestfs-appliances-in-parallel-part-2/> "
"L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/multiple-libguestfs-appliances-in-parallel-part-3/> "
"L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/multiple-libguestfs-appliances-in-parallel-part-4/>"
msgstr ""
"L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/multiple-libguestfs-appliances-in-"
"parallel-part-1/> L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/multiple-libguestfs-"
"appliances-in-parallel-part-2/> L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/"
"multiple-libguestfs-appliances-in-parallel-part-3/> L<http://"
"rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/02/25/multiple-libguestfs-appliances-in-parallel-"
"part-4/>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:331
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #!/usr/bin/env perl\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" #!/usr/bin/env perl\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:333
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" use strict;\n"
" use threads;\n"
" use warnings;\n"
" use Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" use Time::HiRes qw(time);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" use strict;\n"
" use threads;\n"
" use warnings;\n"
" use Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" use Time::HiRes qw(time);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:339
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sub test {\n"
"     my $g = Sys::Guestfs->new;\n"
"     $g->add_drive_ro (\"/dev/null\");\n"
"     $g->launch ();\n"
"     \n"
msgstr ""
" sub test {\n"
"     my $g = Sys::Guestfs->new;\n"
"     $g->add_drive_ro (\"/dev/null\");\n"
"     $g->launch ();\n"
"     \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:344
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     # You could add some work for libguestfs to do here.\n"
"     \n"
msgstr ""
"     # You could add some work for libguestfs to do here.\n"
"     \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:346
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     $g->close ();\n"
" }\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"     $g->close ();\n"
" }\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:349
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Get everything into cache.\n"
" test (); test (); test ();\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" # Get everything into cache.\n"
" test (); test (); test ();\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:352
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" for my $nr_threads (1..20) {\n"
"     my $start_t = time ();\n"
"     my @threads;\n"
"     foreach (1..$nr_threads) {\n"
"         push @threads, threads->create (\\&test)\n"
"     }\n"
"     foreach (@threads) {\n"
"         $_->join ();\n"
"         if (my $err = $_->error ()) {\n"
"             die \"launch failed with $nr_threads threads: $err\"\n"
"         }\n"
"     }\n"
"     my $end_t = time ();\n"
"     printf (\"%d %.2f\\n\", $nr_threads, $end_t - $start_t);\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" for my $nr_threads (1..20) {\n"
"     my $start_t = time ();\n"
"     my @threads;\n"
"     foreach (1..$nr_threads) {\n"
"         push @threads, threads->create (\\&test)\n"
"     }\n"
"     foreach (@threads) {\n"
"         $_->join ();\n"
"         if (my $err = $_->error ()) {\n"
"             die \"launch failed with $nr_threads threads: $err\"\n"
"         }\n"
"     }\n"
"     my $end_t = time ();\n"
"     printf (\"%d %.2f\\n\", $nr_threads, $end_t - $start_t);\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:368
msgid "TROUBLESHOOTING POOR PERFORMANCE"
msgstr "SLIKTAS VEIKTSPĒJAS PROBLĒMU NOVĒRŠANA"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:370
msgid "Ensure hardware virtualization is available"
msgstr "Pārliecinieties, ka aparatūras virtualizācija ir pieejama"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:372
msgid ""
"Use F</proc/cpuinfo> to ensure that hardware virtualization is available.  "
"Note that you may need to enable it in your BIOS."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet F</proc/cpuinfo>, lai pārliecinātos, ka aparatūras "
"virtualizācija ir pieejama.  Ņemiet vērā, ka, iespējams, tā jāiespējo BIOS."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:375
msgid ""
"Hardware virt is not usually available inside VMs, and libguestfs will run "
"slowly inside another virtual machine whatever you do.  Nested "
"virtualization does not work well in our experience, and is certainly no "
"substitute for running libguestfs on baremetal."
msgstr ""
"Aparatūras virtualizācija VM iekšienē parasti nav pieejama, un libguestfs "
"citā virtuālajā mašīnā darbosies lēni, lai ko jūs darītu.  Mūsu pieredzē "
"ligzdotā virtualizācija nedarbojas labi un noteikti neaizstāj libguestfs "
"izpildi uz fiziskas aparatūras."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:380
msgid "Ensure KVM is available"
msgstr "Pārliecinieties, ka KVM ir pieejams"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:382
msgid ""
"Ensure that KVM is enabled and available to the user that will run "
"libguestfs.  It should be safe to set 0666 permissions on F</dev/kvm> and "
"most distributions now do this."
msgstr ""
"Pārliecinieties, ka KVM ir iespējots un pieejams lietotājam, kas izpildīs "
"libguestfs.  F</dev/kvm> vajadzētu būt droši iestatīt atļaujas 0666, un "
"lielākā daļa distribūciju tagad to dara."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:386
msgid "Processors to avoid"
msgstr "No kādiem procesoriem izvairīties"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:388
msgid ""
"Avoid processors that don’t have hardware virtualization, and some "
"processors which are simply very slow (AMD Geode being a great example)."
msgstr ""
"Izvairieties no procesoriem bez aparatūras virtualizācijas un dažiem "
"procesoriem, kas vienkārši ir ļoti lēni (AMD Geode ir lielisks piemērs)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:392
msgid "Xen dom0"
msgstr "Xen dom0"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:394
msgid ""
"In Xen, dom0 is a virtual machine, and so hardware virtualization is not "
"available."
msgstr ""
"Xen dom0 ir virtuālā mašīna, tāpēc aparatūras virtualizācija nav pieejama."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:397
msgid "Use libguestfs E<ge> 1.34 and qemu E<ge> 2.7"
msgstr "Izmantojiet libguestfs E<ge> 1.34 un qemu E<ge> 2.7"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:399
msgid ""
"During the libguestfs 1.33 development cycle, we spent a large amount of "
"time concentrating on boot performance, and added some patches to "
"libguestfs, qemu and Linux which in some cases can reduce boot times to well "
"under 1 second.  You may therefore get much better performance by moving to "
"the versions of libguestfs or qemu mentioned in the heading."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs 1.33 izstrādes ciklā daudz laika veltījām sāknēšanas veiktspējai "
"un pievienojām dažus ielāpus libguestfs, qemu un Linux, kas dažos gadījumos "
"var samazināt sāknēšanas laiku krietni zem 1 sekundes.  Tāpēc, pārejot uz "
"virsrakstā minētajām libguestfs vai qemu versijām, varat iegūt daudz labāku "
"veiktspēju."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:406
msgid "DETAILED ANALYSIS"
msgstr "DETALIZĒTA ANALĪZE"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:408
msgid "Boot analysis"
msgstr "Sāknēšanas analīze"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:410
msgid ""
"In L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs-analysis-tools> is a program "
"called C<boot-analysis>.  This program is able to produce a very detailed "
"breakdown of the boot steps (eg. qemu, BIOS, kernel, libguestfs init "
"script), and can measure how long it takes to perform each step."
msgstr ""
"L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs-analysis-tools> ir programma "
"C<boot-analysis>.  Šī programma spēj sniegt ļoti detalizētu sāknēšanas soļu "
"sadalījumu (piem., qemu, BIOS, kodols, libguestfs init skripts) un var "
"izmērīt, cik ilgs laiks vajadzīgs katram solim."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:416
msgid "Detailed timings using ts"
msgstr "Detalizēti laiki, izmantojot ts"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:418
msgid "Use the L<ts(1)> command (from moreutils) to show detailed timings:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet komandu L<ts(1)> (no moreutils), lai parādītu detalizētus laikus:"

