" 0.000031 libguestfs: launch: euid=1000\n"
" 0.000030 libguestfs: libvirt version = 1002012 (1.2.12)\n"
" [etc]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:435
msgid "The timestamps are seconds (incrementally since the previous line)."
msgstr "Laikspiedoli ir sekundes (pieaugoši kopš iepriekšējās rindas)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:437
msgid "Detailed debugging using gdb"
msgstr "Detalizēta atkļūdošana, izmantojot gdb"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:439
msgid ""
"You can attach to the appliance BIOS/kernel using gdb.  If you know what "
"you're doing, this can be a useful way to diagnose boot regressions."
msgstr ""
"Ar gdb var pievienoties palīgsistēmas BIOS/kodolam.  Ja zināt, ko darāt, tas "
"var būt noderīgs veids sāknēšanas regresiju diagnosticēšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:443
msgid ""
"Firstly, you have to change qemu so it runs with the C<-S> and C<-s> "
"options.  These options cause qemu to pause at boot and allow you to attach "
"a debugger.  Read L<qemu(1)> for further information.  Libguestfs invokes "
"qemu several times (to scan the help output and so on) and you only want the "
"final invocation of qemu to use these options, so use a qemu wrapper script "
"like this:"
msgstr ""
"Vispirms jāmaina qemu, lai tas darbotos ar opcijām C<-S> un C<-s>.  Šīs "
"opcijas liek qemu sāknēšanas laikā apturēties un ļauj pievienot "
"atkļūdotāju.  Plašāku informāciju lasiet L<qemu(1)>.  Libguestfs izsauc qemu "
"vairākas reizes (lai skenētu palīdzības izvadi u. tml.), un jums vajag, lai "
"šīs opcijas izmantotu tikai pēdējais qemu izsaukums, tāpēc izmantojiet qemu "
"ietinēja skriptu, piemēram, šo:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:450 fish/guestfish.pod:1017
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #!/bin/bash -\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" #!/bin/bash -\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:452
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Set this to point to the real qemu binary.\n"
" qemu=/usr/bin/qemu-kvm\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" # Set this to point to the real qemu binary.\n"
" qemu=/usr/bin/qemu-kvm\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:455
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" if [ \"$1\" != \"-global\" ]; then\n"
"     # Scanning help output etc.\n"
"     exec $qemu \"$@\"\n"
" else \n"
"     # Really running qemu.\n"
"     exec $qemu -S -s \"$@\"\n"
" fi\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" if [ \"$1\" != \"-global\" ]; then\n"
"     # Scanning help output etc.\n"
"     exec $qemu \"$@\"\n"
" else \n"
"     # Really running qemu.\n"
"     exec $qemu -S -s \"$@\"\n"
" fi\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:463
msgid ""
"Now run guestfish or another libguestfs tool with the qemu wrapper (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/QEMU WRAPPERS> to understand what this is doing):"
msgstr ""
"Tagad izpildiet guestfish vai citu libguestfs rīku ar qemu ietinēju (lai "
"saprastu, ko tas dara, skatiet L<guestfs(3)/QEMU IETINĒJI>):"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:466
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" LIBGUESTFS_HV=/path/to/qemu-wrapper guestfish -a /dev/null -v run\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" LIBGUESTFS_HV=/path/to/qemu-wrapper guestfish -a /dev/null -v run\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:468
msgid ""
"This should pause just after qemu launches.  In another window, attach to "
"qemu using gdb:"
msgstr ""
"Tam vajadzētu apstāties uzreiz pēc qemu palaišanas.  Citā logā "
"pievienojieties qemu ar gdb:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:471
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ gdb\n"
" (gdb) set architecture i8086\n"
" The target architecture is assumed to be i8086\n"
" (gdb) target remote :1234\n"
" Remote debugging using :1234\n"
" 0x0000fff0 in ?? ()\n"
" (gdb) cont\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ gdb\n"
" (gdb) set architecture i8086\n"
" The target architecture is assumed to be i8086\n"
" (gdb) target remote :1234\n"
" Remote debugging using :1234\n"
" 0x0000fff0 in ?? ()\n"
" (gdb) cont\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:479
msgid ""
"At this point you can use standard gdb techniques, eg. hitting C<^C> to "
"interrupt the boot and C<bt> get a stack trace, setting breakpoints, etc.  "
"Note that when you are past the BIOS and into the Linux kernel, you'll want "
"to change the architecture back to 32 or 64 bit."
msgstr ""
"Šajā brīdī var izmantot standarta gdb paņēmienus, piem., nospiest C<^C>, lai "
"pārtrauktu sāknēšanu, un C<bt>, lai iegūtu steka trasējumu, iestatīt "
"pārtraukumpunktus u. c.  Ņemiet vērā, ka, pārejot no BIOS uz Linux kodolu, "
"arhitektūru vajadzēs mainīt atpakaļ uz 32 vai 64 bitiem."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:485
msgid "PERFORMANCE REGRESSIONS IN OTHER PROGRAMS"
msgstr "VEIKTSPĒJAS REGRESIJAS CITĀS PROGRAMMĀS"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:487
msgid ""
"Sometimes performance regressions happen in other programs (eg. qemu, the "
"kernel) that cause problems for libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Dažreiz veiktspējas regresijas rodas citās programmās (piem., qemu, kodolā), "
"kas rada problēmas libguestfs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:490
msgid ""
"In L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs-analysis-tools> "
"F<boot-benchmark/boot-benchmark-range.pl> is a script which can be used to "
"benchmark libguestfs across a range of git commits in another project to "
"find out if any commit is causing a slowdown (or speedup)."
msgstr ""
"L<https://github.com/libguestfs/libguestfs-analysis-tools> F<boot-benchmark/"
"boot-benchmark-range.pl> ir skripts, ar kuru var veikt libguestfs "
"veiktspējas salīdzinošo testēšanu cita projekta git iesūtījumu diapazonā, "
"lai noskaidrotu, vai kāds iesūtījums izraisa palēnināšanos (vai "
"paātrināšanos)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:496
msgid "To find out how to use this script, consult the manual:"
msgstr "Lai uzzinātu, kā izmantot šo skriptu, skatiet rokasgrāmatu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:498
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./boot-benchmark/boot-benchmark-range.pl --man\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./boot-benchmark/boot-benchmark-range.pl --man\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-performance.pod:502
msgid ""
"L<supermin(1)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-internals(1)>, L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>, L<stap(1)>, "
"L<qemu(1)>, L<gdb(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<supermin(1)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-internals(1)>, L<libguestfs-make-fixed-appliance(1)>, L<stap(1)>, "
"L<qemu(1)>, L<gdb(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:3
msgid ""
"We break with tradition here and don’t use ALL CAPS for the section "
"headings, as this makes them much easier to read."
msgstr ""
"Šeit atkāpjamies no tradīcijas un sadaļu virsrakstos neizmantojam TIKAI "
"LIELOS BURTUS, jo tā tos ir daudz vieglāk lasīt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:10
msgid "guestfs-recipes - libguestfs, guestfish and virt tools recipes"
msgstr "guestfs-recipes - libguestfs, guestfish un virt rīku receptes"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:14
msgid ""
"This page contains recipes for and links to things you can do using "
"libguestfs, L<guestfish(1)> and the virt tools."
msgstr ""
"Šajā lapā ir receptes un saites uz lietām, ko var darīt ar libguestfs, "
"L<guestfish(1)> un virt rīkiem."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:17
msgid "Access a remote disk image using guestfish"
msgstr "Piekļuve attālam diska attēlam, izmantojot guestfish"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:19
msgid ""
"If the disk image is on a remote server which is accessible using SSH, HTTP, "
"FTP, NBD, iSCSI, or similar, then you can open it directly.  See "
"L<guestfish(1)/ADDING REMOTE STORAGE> for several examples.  This requires "
"libguestfs E<ge> 1.22 and qemu E<ge> 1.5."
msgstr ""
"Ja diska attēls atrodas attālā serverī, kas pieejams caur SSH, HTTP, FTP, "
"NBD, iSCSI u. tml., to var atvērt tieši.  Vairākus piemērus skatiet "
"L<guestfish(1)/ATTĀLĀS KRĀTUVES PIEVIENOŠANA>.  Tam nepieciešama libguestfs "
"E<ge> 1.22 un qemu E<ge> 1.5."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:24
msgid "Audit a virtual machine for setuid files"
msgstr "Virtuālās mašīnas audits setuid failu meklēšanai"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:26
msgid "See: L<virt-ls(1)/EXAMPLES>."
msgstr "Skatiet: L<virt-ls(1)/PIEMĒRI>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:28
msgid "Audit a virtual machine for vulnerabilities and security problems"
msgstr "Virtuālās mašīnas audits ievainojamību un drošības problēmu meklēšanai"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:30
msgid ""
"See: "
"L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/05/16/scanning-offline-guests-using-openscap-and-guestmount/#content>"
msgstr ""
"Skatiet: L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/05/16/scanning-offline-guests-"
"using-openscap-and-guestmount/#content>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:33
msgid "Change the background image in a Windows XP VM"
msgstr "Fona attēla maiņa Windows XP VM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:35
msgid ""
"The links below explain how to use L<guestfish(1)> to change the background "
"image for a user of a Windows XP VM.  Unfortunately the technique appears to "
"be substantially different for each version of Windows."
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotās saites skaidro, kā izmantot L<guestfish(1)>, lai mainītu fona "
"attēlu Windows XP VM lietotājam.  Diemžēl katrai Windows versijai paņēmiens "
"šķiet būtiski atšķirīgs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:40
msgid ""
"L<https://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/virt/2011-May/002655.html> "
"L<https://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/virt/2011-May/002658.html>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/virt/2011-May/002655.html> "
"L<https://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/virt/2011-May/002658.html>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:43
msgid "Checksum a file or device within a disk image"
msgstr "Faila vai ierīces kontrolsummas aprēķināšana diska attēlā"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:45
msgid "To checksum a whole device, or a partition, LV etc within a disk image:"
msgstr ""
"Lai aprēķinātu kontrolsummu visai ierīcei vai nodalījumam, LV u. c. diska "
"attēlā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img run : checksum-device md5 /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img run : checksum-device md5 /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:49
msgid ""
"Replace C<md5> with the type of checksum you want.  See "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_checksum_device> for a list of supported types."
msgstr ""
"Aizstājiet C<md5> ar vajadzīgo kontrolsummas tipu.  Atbalstīto tipu sarakstu "
"skatiet L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_checksum_device>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:52
msgid ""
"F</dev/sda1> means \"the first partition\".  You could use F</dev/sda> to "
"checksum the whole disk image, or the name of a logical volume or RAID "
"device."
msgstr ""
"F</dev/sda1> nozīmē „pirmais nodalījums”.  Lai aprēķinātu kontrolsummu visam "
"diska attēlam, varat izmantot F</dev/sda> vai loģiskā sējuma vai RAID "
"ierīces nosaukumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:56
msgid "To checksum a single file:"
msgstr "Lai aprēķinātu kontrolsummu vienam failam:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i checksum sha256 /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i checksum sha256 /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:60
msgid "or for a Windows guest:"
msgstr "vai Windows viesim:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i \\\n"
"   checksum sha256 'win:\\windows\\system32\\config\\SOFTWARE'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i \\\n"
"   checksum sha256 'win:\\windows\\system32\\config\\SOFTWARE'\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:65
msgid "Cloning a virtual machine"
msgstr "Virtuālās mašīnas klonēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:67
msgid ""
"Use a combination of tools like L<cp(1)>, L<dd(1)>, and virt tools like "
"L<virt-sysprep(1)>, L<virt-sparsify(1)> and L<virt-resize(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet tādu rīku kombināciju kā L<cp(1)>, L<dd(1)> un virt rīkus, "
"piemēram, L<virt-sysprep(1)>, L<virt-sparsify(1)> un L<virt-resize(1)>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:71
msgid "Convert a CD-ROM / DVD / ISO to a tarball"
msgstr "CD-ROM / DVD / ISO pārveidošana tar arhīvā"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:73
msgid "This converts input F<cd.iso> to output F<cd.tar.gz>:"
msgstr "Šis pārveido ievades F<cd.iso> par izvades F<cd.tar.gz>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:75
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a cd.iso -m /dev/sda tgz-out / cd.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a cd.iso -m /dev/sda tgz-out / cd.tar.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:77
msgid "To export just a subdirectory, eg. F</files>, do:"
msgstr "Lai eksportētu tikai apakšdirektoriju, piem., F</files>, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a cd.iso -m /dev/sda tgz-out /files cd.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a cd.iso -m /dev/sda tgz-out /files cd.tar.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:81
msgid "Convert from one format/filesystem to another"
msgstr "Pārveidošana no viena formāta/failu sistēmas citā"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:83
msgid ""
"If you have a data disk in one format / filesystem / partition / volume "
"manager, you can convert it another using this technique."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir datu disks vienā formātā / failu sistēmā / nodalījumā / sējumu "
"pārvaldniekā, to var pārveidot citā, izmantojot šo paņēmienu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:86
msgid ""
"In this example, we start with a data disk that has a single partition "
"containing a filesystem, and we want to create another disk that contains "
"the same files but on an ext3 filesystem embedded in a logical volume on a "
"sparse raw-format disk."
msgstr ""
"Šajā piemērā sākam ar datu disku, kurā ir viens nodalījums ar failu sistēmu, "
"un vēlamies izveidot citu disku ar tiem pašiem failiem, bet ext3 failu "
"sistēmā, kas iegulta loģiskajā sējumā retinātā raw formāta diskā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:91
msgid "First create the formatted-but-empty target disk:"
msgstr "Vispirms izveidojiet formatētu, bet tukšu mērķa disku:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" truncate -s 10G target.img\n"
" virt-format -a target.img --partition=mbr --lvm --filesystem=ext3\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" truncate -s 10G target.img\n"
" virt-format -a target.img --partition=mbr --lvm --filesystem=ext3\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:96
msgid ""
"Now, pipe two guestfish instances together to transfer the old data to the "
"new disk:"
msgstr ""
"Tagad savienojiet divas guestfish instances ar kanālu, lai pārsūtītu vecos "
"datus uz jauno disku:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:99
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a source.img -m /dev/sda1  -- tar-out / - | \\\n"
" guestfish --rw -a target.img -m /dev/VG/LV -- tar-in - /\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a source.img -m /dev/sda1  -- tar-out / - | \\\n"
" guestfish --rw -a target.img -m /dev/VG/LV -- tar-in - /\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:102
msgid "To browse the final disk image, do:"
msgstr "Lai pārlūkotu galīgo diska attēlu, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:104
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a target.img -m /dev/VG/LV\n"
" ><fs> ll /\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a target.img -m /dev/VG/LV\n"
" ><fs> ll /\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:107
msgid ""
"This technique is quite powerful, allowing you for example to split up "
"source directories over the target filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Šis paņēmiens ir diezgan jaudīgs — tas, piemēram, ļauj sadalīt avota "
"direktorijas pa mērķa failu sistēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:110
msgid ""
"Note this won’t work (at least, not directly) for bootable virtual machine "
"disks because it doesn't copy over the boot loader."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka sāknējamu virtuālo mašīnu diskiem tas nedarbosies (vismaz ne "
"tieši), jo tas nepārkopē sāknēšanas ielādētāju."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:113
msgid "Convert Windows DVD to bootable USB key"
msgstr "Windows DVD pārveidošana par sāknējamu USB atmiņu"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:115
msgid "L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/05/09/tip-convert-a-windows-dvd-iso-to-a-bootable-usb-key-using-guestfish/#content>"
msgstr ""
"L<http://rwmj.wordpress.com/2013/05/09/tip-convert-a-windows-dvd-iso-to-a-"
"bootable-usb-key-using-guestfish/#content>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:117
msgid "Convert Xen-style partitionless image to partitioned disk image"
msgstr ""
"Xen stila bez nodalījumu attēla pārveidošana par diska attēlu ar nodalījumiem"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:119
msgid ""
"Xen disk images are often partitionless, meaning that the filesystem starts "
"directly at the beginning of the disk with no partition table.  You can in "
"fact use these directly in KVM (provided the guest isn't Windows), but some "
"people like to convert them to regular partitioned disk images, and this is "
"required for Windows guests.  Here is how to use guestfish to do this:"
msgstr ""
"Xen disku attēli bieži ir bez nodalījumiem, t. i., failu sistēma sākas tieši "
"diska sākumā bez nodalījumu tabulas.  Patiesībā tos var izmantot tieši KVM "
"(ja vien viesis nav Windows), taču daži cilvēki tos labprāt pārveido par "
"parastiem diska attēliem ar nodalījumiem, un Windows viesiem tas ir "
"obligāti.  Lūk, kā to izdarīt ar guestfish:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:126
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish\n"
" ><fs> add-ro input.img\n"
" ><fs> sparse output.img 10G     # adjust the output size\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" # Create a partition table on the output disk:\n"
" ><fs> part-init /dev/sdb mbr\n"
" ><fs> part-add /dev/sdb p 2048 -2048\n"
" # Copy the data to the target partition:\n"
" ><fs> copy-device-to-device /dev/sda /dev/sdb1 sparse:true\n"
" # Optionally resize the target filesystem.  Use ntfsresize\n"
" # for Windows guests:\n"
" ><fs> resize2fs /dev/sdb1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish\n"
" ><fs> add-ro input.img\n"
" ><fs> sparse output.img 10G     # adjust the output size\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" # Create a partition table on the output disk:\n"
" ><fs> part-init /dev/sdb mbr\n"
" ><fs> part-add /dev/sdb p 2048 -2048\n"
" # Copy the data to the target partition:\n"
" ><fs> copy-device-to-device /dev/sda /dev/sdb1 sparse:true\n"
" # Optionally resize the target filesystem.  Use ntfsresize\n"
" # for Windows guests:\n"
" ><fs> resize2fs /dev/sdb1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:139
msgid ""
"Such a disk image won’t be directly bootable.  You may need to boot it with "
"an external kernel and initramfs (see below).  Or you can use the guestfish "
"commands C<syslinux> or C<extlinux> to install a SYSLINUX bootloader."
msgstr ""
"Šāds diska attēls nebūs tieši sāknējams.  Iespējams, tas būs jāsāknē ar "
"ārēju kodolu un initramfs (skatiet tālāk).  Vai arī varat izmantot guestfish "
"komandas C<syslinux> vai C<extlinux>, lai instalētu SYSLINUX sāknēšanas "
"ielādētāju."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:144
msgid "Create empty disk images"
msgstr "Tukšu disku attēlu izveide"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:146
msgid "The L<virt-format(1)> tool can do this directly."
msgstr "Rīks L<virt-format(1)> to var izdarīt tieši."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:148
msgid ""
"Use L<virt-make-fs(1)> to create a disk image with content.  This can also "
"create some standard disk images such as virtual floppy devices (VFDs)."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L<virt-make-fs(1)>, lai izveidotu diska attēlu ar saturu.  Tas "
"var izveidot arī dažus standarta disku attēlus, piemēram, virtuālās disketes "
"(VFD)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:152
msgid ""
"You can also use the L<guestfish(1)> I<-N> option to create empty disk "
"images.  The useful guide below explains the options available."
msgstr ""
"Tukšu disku attēlu izveidei varat izmantot arī L<guestfish(1)> opciju I<-N>"
".  Tālāk dotajā noderīgajā ceļvedī izskaidrotas pieejamās opcijas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:155
msgid "L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2010/09/08/new-guestfish-n-options-in-1-5-9/#content>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2010/09/08/new-guestfish-n-options-in-1-5-9/"
"#content>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:157
msgid "L<virt-builder(1)> can create minimal guests."
msgstr "L<virt-builder(1)> var izveidot minimālus viesus."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:159
msgid "Delete a file (or other simple file operations)"
msgstr "Faila dzēšana (vai citas vienkāršas failu darbības)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:161
msgid "Use guestfish.  To delete a file:"
msgstr "Izmantojiet guestfish.  Lai dzēstu failu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:163
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i rm /file/to/delete\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i rm /file/to/delete\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:165
msgid "To touch a file (bring it up to date or create it):"
msgstr "Lai „touch” failu (atjauninātu laiku vai izveidotu to):"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:167
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i touch /file/to/touch\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i touch /file/to/touch\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:169
msgid ""
"To stat a file.  Since this is a read-only operation, we can make it safer "
"by adding the I<--ro> flag."
msgstr ""
"Lai izpildītu stat failam.  Tā kā šī ir tikai lasīšanas darbība, to var "
"padarīt drošāku, pievienojot karogu I<--ro>."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:172
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i stat /file/to/stat\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i stat /file/to/stat\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:174
msgid ""
"There are dozens of these commands.  See L<guestfish(1)> or the output of "
"C<guestfish -h>"
msgstr ""
"Šādu komandu ir desmitiem.  Skatiet L<guestfish(1)> vai C<guestfish -h> "
"izvadi"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:177
msgid "Diff two guests; compare a snapshot to the current version"
msgstr ""
"Divu viesu salīdzināšana; momentuzņēmuma salīdzināšana ar pašreizējo versiju"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:179
msgid ""
"Since libguestfs E<ge> 1.26, use L<virt-diff(1)> to look for differences "
"between two guests (for example if they were originally cloned from the same "
"source), or between two snapshots from the same guest.  In earlier versions "
"of libguestfs, use L<virt-ls(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Kopš libguestfs E<ge> 1.26 izmantojiet L<virt-diff(1)>, lai meklētu "
"atšķirības starp diviem viesiem (piemēram, ja tie sākotnēji klonēti no viena "
"avota) vai starp diviem viena viesa momentuzņēmumiem.  Vecākās libguestfs "
"versijās izmantojiet L<virt-ls(1)>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:184
msgid "Disable a systemd service"
msgstr "Systemd pakalpojuma atspējošana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:186
msgid ""
"The following is the equivalent of C<systemctl mask ...>. To disable the "
"C<cloud-init> service so it doesn't start at next boot:"
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotais ir līdzvērtīgs C<systemctl mask ...>. Lai atspējotu pakalpojumu "
"C<cloud-init>, lai tas nākamajā sāknēšanā netiktu palaists:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:189
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i \\\n"
"     ln-sf /dev/null /etc/systemd/system/cloud-init.service\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i \\\n"
"     ln-sf /dev/null /etc/systemd/system/cloud-init.service\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:192
msgid "To disable tmp-on-tmpfs:"
msgstr "Lai atspējotu tmp-on-tmpfs:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i \\\n"
"     ln-sf /dev/null /etc/systemd/system/tmp.mount\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a disk.img -i \\\n"
"     ln-sf /dev/null /etc/systemd/system/tmp.mount\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:197
msgid ""
"One problem with the commands above is there is no feedback if you get the "
"name of the service you are trying to mask wrong.  But you can use "
"L<virt-ls(1)> to list the available systemd services like this:"
msgstr ""
"Viena problēma ar iepriekšējām komandām ir tā, ka nav atgriezeniskās saites, "
"ja maskējamā pakalpojuma nosaukums ir nepareizs.  Taču pieejamos systemd "
"pakalpojumus var uzskaitīt ar L<virt-ls(1)>, piemēram, šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:201
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -a /tmp/fedora-19.img -R /lib/systemd/system\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -a /tmp/fedora-19.img -R /lib/systemd/system\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:203
msgid "Drive letters over FUSE"
msgstr "Disku burti caur FUSE"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:205
msgid ""
"You have a Windows guest, and you want to expose the drive letters as FUSE "
"mountpoints (F</C/...>, F</D/...> etc).  Instead of L<guestmount(1)>, use "
"this Perl script:"
msgstr ""
"Jums ir Windows viesis, un vēlaties atklāt disku burtus kā FUSE montēšanas "
"punktus (F</C/...>, F</D/...> u. c.).  L<guestmount(1)> vietā izmantojiet šo "
"Perl skriptu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:209
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #!/usr/bin/perl -w\n"
" use strict;\n"
" use Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" $| = 1;\n"
" die \"usage: $0 mountpoint disk.img\" if @ARGV < 2;\n"
" my $mp = shift @ARGV;\n"
" my $g = new Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" $g->add_drive_opts ($_) foreach @ARGV;\n"
" $g->launch;\n"
" my @roots = $g->inspect_os;\n"
" die \"$0: no operating system found\" if @roots != 1;\n"
" my $root = $roots[0];\n"
" die \"$0: not Windows\" if $g->inspect_get_type ($root) ne \"windows\";\n"
" my %map = $g->inspect_get_drive_mappings ($root);\n"
" foreach (keys %map) {\n"
"     $g->mkmountpoint (\"/$_\");\n"
"     eval { $g->mount ($map{$_}, \"/$_\") };\n"
"     warn \"$@ (ignored)\\n\" if $@;\n"
" }\n"
" $g->mount_local ($mp);\n"
" print \"filesystem ready on $mp\\n\";\n"
" $g->mount_local_run;\n"
" $g->shutdown;\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #!/usr/bin/perl -w\n"
" use strict;\n"
" use Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" $| = 1;\n"
" die \"usage: $0 mountpoint disk.img\" if @ARGV < 2;\n"
" my $mp = shift @ARGV;\n"
" my $g = new Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" $g->add_drive_opts ($_) foreach @ARGV;\n"
" $g->launch;\n"
" my @roots = $g->inspect_os;\n"
" die \"$0: no operating system found\" if @roots != 1;\n"
" my $root = $roots[0];\n"
" die \"$0: not Windows\" if $g->inspect_get_type ($root) ne \"windows\";\n"
" my %map = $g->inspect_get_drive_mappings ($root);\n"
" foreach (keys %map) {\n"
"     $g->mkmountpoint (\"/$_\");\n"
"     eval { $g->mount ($map{$_}, \"/$_\") };\n"
"     warn \"$@ (ignored)\\n\" if $@;\n"
" }\n"
" $g->mount_local ($mp);\n"
" print \"filesystem ready on $mp\\n\";\n"
" $g->mount_local_run;\n"
" $g->shutdown;\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:233
msgid "You can use the script like this:"
msgstr "Skriptu var izmantot šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:235
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ mkdir /tmp/mnt\n"
" $ ./drive-letters.pl /tmp/mnt windows7.img\n"
" filesystem ready on /tmp/mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ mkdir /tmp/mnt\n"
" $ ./drive-letters.pl /tmp/mnt windows7.img\n"
" filesystem ready on /tmp/mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:239
msgid "In another window:"
msgstr "Citā logā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:241
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ cd /tmp/mnt\n"
" $ ls\n"
" C  D\n"
" $ cd C\n"
" $ ls\n"
" Documents and Settings\n"
" PerfLogs\n"
" ProgramData\n"
" Program Files\n"
" [etc]\n"
" $ cd ../..\n"
" $ guestunmount /tmp/mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ cd /tmp/mnt\n"
" $ ls\n"
" C  D\n"
" $ cd C\n"
" $ ls\n"
" Documents and Settings\n"
" PerfLogs\n"
" ProgramData\n"
" Program Files\n"
" [etc]\n"
" $ cd ../..\n"
" $ guestunmount /tmp/mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:254
msgid "Dump raw filesystem content from inside a disk image or VM"
msgstr "Neapstrādāta failu sistēmas satura izmešana no diska attēla vai VM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:256
msgid ""
"You can use the L<guestfish(1)> C<download> command to extract the raw "
"filesystem content from any filesystem in a disk image or a VM (even one "
"which is encrypted or buried inside an LV or RAID device):"
msgstr ""
"Ar L<guestfish(1)> komandu C<download> var izgūt neapstrādātu failu sistēmas "
"saturu no jebkuras failu sistēmas diska attēlā vai VM (pat tādas, kas ir "
"šifrēta vai paslēpta LV vai RAID ierīcē):"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:260
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img run : download /dev/sda1 sda1.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img run : download /dev/sda1 sda1.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:262
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -d Guest run : download /dev/vg_guest/lv_root lv.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -d Guest run : download /dev/vg_guest/lv_root lv.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:264
msgid "To download to stdout, replace the filename with a C<-> character:"
msgstr ""
"Lai lejupielādētu uz stdout, aizstājiet faila nosaukumu ar rakstzīmi C<->:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:266
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img run : download /dev/sda1 - | gzip > sda1.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img run : download /dev/sda1 - | gzip > sda1.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:268
msgid "To list the filesystems in a disk image, use L<virt-filesystems(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Lai uzskaitītu diska attēla failu sistēmas, izmantojiet L<virt-filesystems"
"(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:270
msgid "See also L</Uploading raw filesystem content>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</Neapstrādāta failu sistēmas satura augšupielāde>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:272
msgid "Edit grub configuration in a VM"
msgstr "Grub konfigurācijas rediģēšana VM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:274
msgid "You can use this to:"
msgstr "To var izmantot, lai:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:280
msgid "Fix a virtual machine that does not boot."
msgstr "Salabotu virtuālo mašīnu, kas nesāknējas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:284
msgid "Change which kernel is used to boot the VM."
msgstr "Mainītu, kurš kodols tiek izmantots VM sāknēšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:288
msgid "Change kernel command line options."
msgstr "Mainītu kodola komandrindas opcijas."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:292
msgid "Use L<virt-edit(1)> to edit the grub configuration:"
msgstr "Grub konfigurācijas rediģēšanai izmantojiet L<virt-edit(1)>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:294
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d BrokenGuest /boot/grub2/grub.cfg\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d BrokenGuest /boot/grub2/grub.cfg\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:296
msgid ""
"or for general tinkering inside an unbootable VM use L<virt-rescue(1)> like "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"vai vispārīgai rosīšanai nesāknējamā VM izmantojiet L<virt-rescue(1)> šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:299
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue -d BrokenGuest\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue -d BrokenGuest\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:301
msgid "Export any directory from a VM"
msgstr "Jebkuras direktorijas eksportēšana no VM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:303
msgid "To export F</home> from a VM into a local directory use L<virt-copy-out(1)>:"
msgstr ""
"Lai eksportētu F</home> no VM uz lokālu direktoriju, izmantojiet L<virt-copy-"
"out(1)>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:306 docs/guestfs-testing.pod:177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-out -d Guest /home .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-out -d Guest /home .\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:308 docs/internal-documentation.pod:1358
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3072 docs/internal-documentation.pod:3455
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:3075 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:3716
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4503 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:5119
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6145 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7236
#: lib/guestfs.pod:785 lib/guestfs.pod:2223
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr "Piezīmes:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:314
msgid ""
"The final dot of the command is not a printing error.  It means we want to "
"copy out to the current directory."
msgstr ""
"Komandas beigu punkts nav drukas kļūda.  Tas nozīmē, ka vēlamies kopēt uz "
"pašreizējo direktoriju."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:319
msgid "This creates a directory called C<home> under the current directory."
msgstr "Tas pašreizējā direktorijā izveido direktoriju C<home>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:323
msgid ""
"If the guest is a Windows guest then you can use drive letters and "
"backslashes, but you must prefix the path with C<win:> and quote it to "
"protect it from the shell, like this:"
msgstr ""
"Ja viesis ir Windows viesis, varat izmantot disku burtus un atpakaļvērstās "
"slīpsvītras, taču ceļam jāpievieno priedēklis C<win:> un tas jāliek pēdiņās, "
"lai aizsargātu no čaulas, piemēram, šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:327
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-out -d WinGuest 'win:c:\\windows\\system32\\config' .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-out -d WinGuest 'win:c:\\windows\\system32\\config' .\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:329
msgid "To get the output as a compressed tarball, do:"
msgstr "Lai iegūtu izvadi kā saspiestu tar arhīvu, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:331
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-out -d Guest /home - | gzip --best > home.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-out -d Guest /home - | gzip --best > home.tar.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:333
msgid ""
"Although it sounds tempting, this is usually not a reliable way to get a "
"backup from a running guest.  See the entry in the FAQ: "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/FAQ.html#backup>"
msgstr ""
"Lai gan tas izklausās vilinoši, parasti tas nav uzticams veids, kā iegūt "
"darbojoša viesa dublējumu.  Skatiet ierakstu BUJ: L<http://libguestfs.org/"
"FAQ.html#backup>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:337
msgid "Export external kernel and initramfs (initrd)"
msgstr "Ārēja kodola un initramfs (initrd) eksportēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:339
msgid ""
"If a Linux guest doesn't have a boot loader or it is broken, then you can "
"usually boot it using an external kernel and initramfs.  In this "
"configuration, the hypervisor acts like a bootloader, loading the kernel "
"from the host disk into guest memory and jumping straight into the kernel."
msgstr ""
"Ja Linux viesim nav sāknēšanas ielādētāja vai tas ir bojāts, parasti to var "
"sāknēt, izmantojot ārēju kodolu un initramfs.  Šajā konfigurācijā "
"hipervizors darbojas kā sāknēšanas ielādētājs, ielādējot kodolu no "
"resursdatora diska viesa atmiņā un pārlecot tieši uz kodolu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:345
msgid ""
"However you may wonder how to get the right kernel corresponding to the disk "
"image you have.  Since libguestfs E<ge> 1.24 L<virt-builder(1)> can get the "
"latest kernel and corresponding initramfs for you:"
msgstr ""
"Tomēr var rasties jautājums, kā iegūt pareizo kodolu, kas atbilst jūsu diska "
"attēlam.  Kopš libguestfs E<ge> 1.24 L<virt-builder(1)> var iegūt jaunāko "
"kodolu un atbilstošo initramfs jūsu vietā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:350
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkdir outputdir\n"
" virt-builder --get-kernel disk.img -o outputdir\n"
" ls -lh outputdir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkdir outputdir\n"
" virt-builder --get-kernel disk.img -o outputdir\n"
" ls -lh outputdir\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:354
msgid "Find out which user is using the most space"
msgstr "Noskaidrot, kurš lietotājs izmanto visvairāk vietas"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:356
msgid ""
"This simple script examines a Linux guest to find out which user is using "
"the most space in their home directory:"
msgstr ""
"Šis vienkāršais skripts pārbauda Linux viesi, lai noskaidrotu, kurš "
"lietotājs savā mājas direktorijā izmanto visvairāk vietas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:359
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #!/bin/sh -\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" #!/bin/sh -\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:361 fish/guestfish.pod:1019
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set -e\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" set -e\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:363
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vm=\"$1\"\n"
" dir=/home\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" vm=\"$1\"\n"
" dir=/home\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:366
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" eval $(guestfish --ro -d \"$vm\" -i --listen)\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" eval $(guestfish --ro -d \"$vm\" -i --listen)\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:368
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" for d in $(guestfish --remote ls \"$dir\"); do\n"
"     echo -n \"$dir/$d\"\n"
"     echo -ne '\\t'\n"
"     guestfish --remote du \"$dir/$d\";\n"
" done | sort -nr -k 2\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" for d in $(guestfish --remote ls \"$dir\"); do\n"
"     echo -n \"$dir/$d\"\n"
"     echo -ne '\\t'\n"
"     guestfish --remote du \"$dir/$d\";\n"
" done | sort -nr -k 2\n"
