msgstr "Diska attēla retināšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:627
msgid "Use L<virt-sparsify(1)>."
msgstr "Izmantojiet L<virt-sparsify(1)>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:629
msgid "Monitor disk usage over time"
msgstr "Diska lietojuma uzraudzība laika gaitā"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:631
msgid ""
"You can use L<virt-df(1)> to monitor disk usage of your guests over time.  "
"The link below contains a guide."
msgstr ""
"Ar L<virt-df(1)> var uzraudzīt viesu diska lietojumu laika gaitā.  Tālāk "
"dotajā saitē ir ceļvedis."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:634
msgid "L<http://web.archive.org/web/20130214073726/http://virt-tools.org/learning/advanced-virt-df/>"
msgstr ""
"L<http://web.archive.org/web/20130214073726/http://virt-tools.org/learning/"
"advanced-virt-df/>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:636
msgid "Reading the Windows Event Log from Windows Vista (or later)"
msgstr "Windows notikumu žurnāla lasīšana no Windows Vista (vai jaunākas)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:638
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)> plus the tools described in the link below can be used to "
"read out the Windows Event Log from any virtual machine running Windows "
"Vista or a later version."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)> kopā ar tālāk dotajā saitē aprakstītajiem rīkiem var "
"izmantot, lai nolasītu Windows notikumu žurnālu no jebkuras virtuālās "
"mašīnas ar Windows Vista vai jaunāku versiju."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:644
msgid "Remove root password (Linux)"
msgstr "Root paroles noņemšana (Linux)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:646
msgid ""
"Using the L<virt-edit(1)> I<-e> option you can do simple replacements on "
"files.  One use is to remove the root password from a Linux guest:"
msgstr ""
"Ar L<virt-edit(1)> opciju I<-e> failos var veikt vienkāršas aizstāšanas.  "
"Viens lietojums ir root paroles noņemšana no Linux viesa:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:649
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d domname /etc/passwd -e 's/^root:.*?:/root::/'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d domname /etc/passwd -e 's/^root:.*?:/root::/'\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:651
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -a disk.img /etc/passwd -e 's/^root:.*?:/root::/'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -a disk.img /etc/passwd -e 's/^root:.*?:/root::/'\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:653
msgid "Remove Administrator password (Windows)"
msgstr "Administrator paroles noņemšana (Windows)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:655
msgid ""
"The link below contains one technique for removing the Administrator "
"password from a Windows VM, or to be more precise, it gives you a command "
"prompt the next time you log in which you can use to bypass any security:"
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotajā saitē ir viens paņēmiens Administrator paroles noņemšanai no "
"Windows VM vai, precīzāk, tas nākamajā pieteikšanās reizē dod komandu "
"uzvedni, ar kuru var apiet jebkādu drošību:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:660
msgid "L<https://mdbooth.wordpress.com/2010/10/18/resetting-a-windows-guests-administrator-password-with-guestfish/>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://mdbooth.wordpress.com/2010/10/18/resetting-a-windows-guests-"
"administrator-password-with-guestfish/>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:662
msgid "Sysprepping a virtual machine (Windows)"
msgstr "Virtuālās mašīnas sysprep (Windows)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:664
msgid ""
"It is possible to do a \"sysprep\" using libguestfs alone, although not "
"straightforward.  Currently there is code in the Aeolus Oz project which "
"does this (using libguestfs).  It is likely we will add this to "
"L<virt-sysprep(1)> in future."
msgstr ""
"„Sysprep” iespējams veikt tikai ar libguestfs, lai gan ne vienkārši.  "
"Pašlaik projektā Aeolus Oz ir kods, kas to dara (izmantojot libguestfs).  "
"Visticamāk, nākotnē to pievienosim L<virt-sysprep(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:669
msgid ""
"L<https://github.com/clalancette/oz> "
"L<https://www.redhat.com/archives/virt-tools-list/2011-May/msg00019.html>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://github.com/clalancette/oz> L<https://www.redhat.com/archives/virt-"
"tools-list/2011-May/msg00019.html>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:672
msgid "Unpack a live CD"
msgstr "Live CD izpakošana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:674
msgid ""
"Linux live CDs often contain multiple layers of disk images wrapped like a "
"Russian doll.  You can use L<guestfish(1)> to look inside these multiple "
"layers, as outlined in the guide below."
msgstr ""
"Linux live CD bieži satur vairākus disku attēlu slāņus, kas ietīti cits citā "
"kā matrjoška.  Ar L<guestfish(1)> var ieskatīties šajos vairākajos slāņos, "
"kā aprakstīts tālāk dotajā ceļvedī."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:678
msgid "L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2009/07/15/unpack-the-russian-doll-of-a-f11-live-cd/#content>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2009/07/15/unpack-the-russian-doll-of-a-f11-"
"live-cd/#content>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:680
msgid "Uploading and downloading files"
msgstr "Failu augšupielāde un lejupielāde"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:682
msgid ""
"The link below contains general tips on uploading (copying in)  and "
"downloading (copying out) files from VMs."
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotajā saitē ir vispārīgi padomi par failu augšupielādi (iekopēšanu) "
"un lejupielādi (izkopēšanu) no VM."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:685
msgid "L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2010/12/02/tip-uploading-and-downloading/#content>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2010/12/02/tip-uploading-and-downloading/"
"#content>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:687
msgid "Uploading raw filesystem content"
msgstr "Neapstrādāta failu sistēmas satura augšupielāde"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:689
msgid ""
"You can use L<guestfish(1)> to upload whole filesystems into a VM, even into "
"a filesystem which is encrypted or buried inside an LV or RAID device:"
msgstr ""
"Ar L<guestfish(1)> var augšupielādēt veselas failu sistēmas VM, pat failu "
"sistēmā, kas ir šifrēta vai paslēpta LV vai RAID ierīcē:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:693
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -a disk.img run : upload sda1.img /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -a disk.img run : upload sda1.img /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:695
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -d Guest run : upload lv.img /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -d Guest run : upload lv.img /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:697
msgid ""
"One common problem is that the filesystem isn't the right size for the "
"target.  If it is too large, there’s not much you can do with libguestfs - "
"you have to prepare the filesystem differently.  But if the filesystem needs "
"to expand into the target, you can use guestfish to resize it to the right "
"size:"
msgstr ""
"Viena bieža problēma ir tā, ka failu sistēma nav mērķim pareizā izmērā.  Ja "
"tā ir pārāk liela, ar libguestfs daudz neko nevar izdarīt — failu sistēma "
"jāsagatavo citādi.  Bet, ja failu sistēmai jāizplešas mērķī, ar guestfish "
"var mainīt tās izmēru uz pareizo:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:703
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -d Guest run : \\\n"
"   upload lv.img /dev/vg_guest/lv_root : \\\n"
"   resize2fs /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -d Guest run : \\\n"
"   upload lv.img /dev/vg_guest/lv_root : \\\n"
"   resize2fs /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:707
msgid "(or use C<ntfsresize> if the filesystem is NTFS)."
msgstr "(vai izmantojiet C<ntfsresize>, ja failu sistēma ir NTFS)."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:709
msgid "Use libguestfs tools on VMware ESX guests"
msgstr "Libguestfs rīku izmantošana ar VMware ESX viesiem"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:711
msgid ""
"The link below explains how to use libguestfs, L<guestfish(1)> and the virt "
"tools on any VMware ESX guests, by first sharing the VMware VMFS over sshfs."
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotā saite skaidro, kā izmantot libguestfs, L<guestfish(1)> un virt "
"rīkus ar jebkuriem VMware ESX viesiem, vispirms koplietojot VMware VMFS caur "
"sshfs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:715
msgid "L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2011/05/10/tip-use-libguestfs-on-vmware-esx-guests/#content>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://rwmj.wordpress.com/2011/05/10/tip-use-libguestfs-on-vmware-esx-"
"guests/#content>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-recipes.pod:719
