#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-security - security of libguestfs"
msgstr "guestfs-security - libguestfs drošība"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:7
msgid ""
"This manual page discusses security implications of using libguestfs, "
"particularly with untrusted or malicious guests or disk images."
msgstr ""
"Šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā aplūkota libguestfs izmantošanas ietekme uz drošību, "
"it īpaši ar neuzticamiem vai ļaunprātīgiem viesiem vai disku attēliem."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:10
msgid "REPORTING SECURITY PROBLEMS"
msgstr "ZIŅOŠANA PAR DROŠĪBAS PROBLĒMĀM"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:12
msgid ""
"If you wish to privately report a security issue, please follow the Red Hat "
"security procedure at L<https://access.redhat.com/security/team/contact>"
msgstr ""
"Ja vēlaties privāti ziņot par drošības problēmu, lūdzu, ievērojiet Red Hat "
"drošības procedūru L<https://access.redhat.com/security/team/contact>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:16
msgid ""
"If the security problem is not so serious, you can simply file a bug (see "
"L</BUGS> below), or send an email to our mailing list "
"(L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>).  You do not need to subscribe to the "
"mailing list to send email, but there will be a delay while the message is "
"moderated."
msgstr ""
"Ja drošības problēma nav tik nopietna, varat vienkārši iesniegt kļūdas "
"ziņojumu (skatiet L</BUGS> tālāk) vai nosūtīt e-pastu mūsu pasta sarakstam "
"(L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>).  Lai sūtītu e-pastu, pasta saraksts nav "
"jāabonē, taču, kamēr ziņojums tiek moderēts, būs aizkave."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:22
msgid "GENERAL ISSUES"
msgstr "VISPĀRĪGAS PROBLĒMAS"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:24
msgid "Security of mounting filesystems"
msgstr "Failu sistēmu montēšanas drošība"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:26
msgid ""
"You should never mount an untrusted guest filesystem directly on your host "
"kernel (eg. using loopback or kpartx)."
msgstr ""
"Nekad nevajadzētu montēt neuzticamu viesa failu sistēmu tieši resursdatora "
"kodolā (piem., izmantojot cilpas ierīci vai kpartx)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:29
msgid ""
"When you mount a filesystem, mistakes in the kernel filesystem (VFS)  can be "
"escalated into exploits by attackers creating a malicious filesystem.  These "
"exploits are very severe for two reasons.  Firstly there are very many "
"filesystem drivers in the kernel, and many of them are infrequently used and "
"not much developer attention has been paid to the code.  Linux userspace "
"helps potential crackers by detecting the filesystem type and automatically "
"choosing the right VFS driver, even if that filesystem type is unexpected.  "
"Secondly, a kernel-level exploit is like a local root exploit (worse in some "
"ways), giving immediate and total access to the system right down to the "
"hardware level."
msgstr ""
"Montējot failu sistēmu, kļūdas kodola failu sistēmā (VFS) uzbrucēji var "
"pārvērst ievainojamību izmantošanā, izveidojot ļaunprātīgu failu sistēmu.  "
"Šīs izmantošanas ir ļoti nopietnas divu iemeslu dēļ.  Pirmkārt, kodolā ir "
"ļoti daudz failu sistēmu draiveru, un daudzi no tiem tiek izmantoti reti, un "
"to kodam izstrādātāji nav pievērsuši daudz uzmanības.  Linux lietotāja telpa "
"palīdz potenciāliem uzlauzējiem, nosakot failu sistēmas tipu un automātiski "
"izvēloties pareizo VFS draiveri, pat ja šis failu sistēmas tips ir "
"negaidīts.  Otrkārt, kodola līmeņa izmantošana ir kā lokāla root izmantošana "
"(dažos aspektos sliktāka), dodot tūlītēju un pilnīgu piekļuvi sistēmai līdz "
"pat aparatūras līmenim."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:41
msgid ""
"These exploits can be present in the kernel for a very long time "
"(L<https://lwn.net/Articles/538898/>)."
msgstr ""
"Šīs ievainojamības kodolā var pastāvēt ļoti ilgi (L<https://lwn.net/Articles/"
"538898/>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:44
msgid "Libguestfs provides a layered approach to protecting you from exploits:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs nodrošina slāņotu pieeju, lai jūs aizsargātu no ievainojamību "
"izmantošanas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   untrusted filesystem\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   appliance kernel\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   qemu process running as non-root\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   sVirt [if using libvirt + SELinux]\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   host kernel\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"   untrusted filesystem\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   appliance kernel\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   qemu process running as non-root\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   sVirt [if using libvirt + SELinux]\n"
" --------------------------------------\n"
"   host kernel\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:57
msgid ""
"We run a Linux kernel inside a qemu virtual machine, usually running as a "
"non-root user.  The attacker would need to write a filesystem which first "
"exploited the kernel, and then exploited either qemu virtualization (eg. a "
"faulty qemu driver) or the libguestfs protocol, and finally to be as serious "
"as the host kernel exploit it would need to escalate its privileges to "
"root.  Additionally if you use the libvirt back end and SELinux, sVirt is "
"used to confine the qemu process.  This multi-step escalation, performed by "
"a static piece of data, is thought to be extremely hard to do, although we "
"never say ‘never’ about security issues."
msgstr ""
"Mēs izpildām Linux kodolu qemu virtuālajā mašīnā, parasti kā ne-root "
"lietotājs.  Uzbrucējam būtu jāuzraksta failu sistēma, kas vispirms izmantotu "
"kodola ievainojamību un pēc tam vai nu qemu virtualizācijas (piem., kļūdaina "
"qemu draivera), vai libguestfs protokola ievainojamību, un visbeidzot, lai "
"tā būtu tikpat nopietna kā resursdatora kodola ievainojamības izmantošana, "
"tai būtu jāpaaugstina savas privilēģijas līdz root.  Turklāt, ja izmantojat "
"libvirt aizmugursistēmu un SELinux, qemu procesa ierobežošanai tiek "
"izmantots sVirt.  Tiek uzskatīts, ka šādu daudzpakāpju eskalāciju, ko veic "
"statisks datu gabals, ir ārkārtīgi grūti paveikt, lai gan drošības "
"jautājumos nekad nesakām „nekad”."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:68
msgid ""
"Callers can also reduce the attack surface by forcing the filesystem type "
"when mounting (use L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_mount_vfs>)."
msgstr ""
"Izsaucēji var arī samazināt uzbrukuma virsmu, montējot piespiedu kārtā "
"norādot failu sistēmas tipu (izmantojiet L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_mount_vfs>)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:71
msgid "General security considerations"
msgstr "Vispārīgi drošības apsvērumi"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:73
msgid ""
"Be careful with any files or data that you download from a guest (by "
"\"download\" we mean not just the L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_download> command but "
"any command that reads files, filenames, directories or anything else from a "
"disk image).  An attacker could manipulate the data to fool your program "
"into doing the wrong thing.  Consider cases such as:"
msgstr ""
"Esiet uzmanīgi ar jebkuriem failiem vai datiem, ko lejupielādējat no viesa "
"(ar „lejupielādi” domājam ne tikai komandu L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_download>, "
"bet jebkuru komandu, kas nolasa failus, failu nosaukumus, direktorijas vai "
"jebko citu no diska attēla).  Uzbrucējs var manipulēt ar datiem, lai "
"piemānītu jūsu programmu izdarīt nepareizo.  Apsveriet tādus gadījumus kā:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:83
msgid "the data (file etc) not being present"
msgstr "dati (fails u. c.) nav klāt"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:87
msgid "being present but empty"
msgstr "ir klāt, bet tukši"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:91
msgid "being much larger than normal"
msgstr "ir daudz lielāki nekā parasti"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:95
msgid "containing arbitrary 8 bit data"
msgstr "satur patvaļīgus 8 bitu datus"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:99
msgid "being in an unexpected character encoding"
msgstr "ir negaidītā rakstzīmju kodējumā"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:103
msgid "containing homoglyphs."
msgstr "satur homoglifus."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:107
msgid "Protocol security"
msgstr "Protokola drošība"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:109
msgid ""
"The protocol is designed to be secure, being based on RFC 4506 (XDR)  with a "
"defined upper message size.  However a program that uses libguestfs must "
"also take care - for example you can write a program that downloads a binary "
"from a disk image and executes it locally, and no amount of protocol "
"security will save you from the consequences."
msgstr ""
"Protokols ir izstrādāts drošs, balstīts uz RFC 4506 (XDR) ar definētu "
"ziņojuma maksimālo izmēru.  Tomēr programmai, kas izmanto libguestfs, arī "
"jābūt uzmanīgai — piemēram, varat uzrakstīt programmu, kas lejupielādē "
"bināro failu no diska attēla un izpilda to lokāli, un nekāda protokola "
"drošība jūs neglābs no sekām."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:115
msgid "Inspection security"
msgstr "Inspicēšanas drošība"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:117
msgid ""
"Parts of the inspection API (see L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION>) return untrusted "
"strings directly from the guest, and these could contain any 8 bit data.  "
"Callers should be careful to escape these before printing them to a "
"structured file (for example, use HTML escaping if creating a web page)."
msgstr ""
"Daļa inspicēšanas API (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>) atgriež "
"neuzticamas virknes tieši no viesa, un tās var saturēt jebkādus 8 bitu "
"datus.  Izsaucējiem vajadzētu uzmanīgi tās atsoļot, pirms izdrukāt "
"strukturētā failā (piemēram, izmantojiet HTML atsoļošanu, ja veidojat "
"tīmekļa lapu)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:123
msgid ""
"Guest configuration may be altered in unusual ways by the administrator of "
"the virtual machine, and may not reflect reality (particularly for untrusted "
"or actively malicious guests).  For example we parse the hostname from "
"configuration files like F</etc/sysconfig/network> that we find in the "
"guest, but the guest administrator can easily manipulate these files to "
"provide the wrong hostname."
msgstr ""
"Virtuālās mašīnas administrators var neparastos veidos mainīt viesa "
"konfigurāciju, un tā var neatspoguļot realitāti (it īpaši neuzticamiem vai "
"aktīvi ļaunprātīgiem viesiem).  Piemēram, resursdatora nosaukumu parsējam no "
"konfigurācijas failiem, piemēram, F</etc/sysconfig/network>, ko atrodam "
"viesī, taču viesa administrators var viegli manipulēt ar šiem failiem, lai "
"sniegtu nepareizu resursdatora nosaukumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:131
msgid ""
"The inspection API parses guest configuration using two external libraries: "
"Augeas (Linux configuration) and hivex (Windows Registry).  Both are "
"designed to be robust in the face of malicious data, although denial of "
"service attacks are still possible, for example with oversized configuration "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Inspicēšanas API parsē viesa konfigurāciju, izmantojot divas ārējas "
"bibliotēkas: Augeas (Linux konfigurācija) un hivex (Windows reģistrs).  Abas "
"ir izstrādātas robustas pret ļaunprātīgiem datiem, lai gan pakalpojuma "
"atteices uzbrukumi joprojām ir iespējami, piemēram, ar pārmērīga izmēra "
"konfigurācijas failiem."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:137
msgid "Running untrusted guest commands"
msgstr "Neuzticamu viesa komandu izpilde"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:139
msgid ""
"Be very cautious about running commands from the guest.  By running a "
"command in the guest, you are giving CPU time to a binary that you do not "
"control, under the same user account as the library, albeit wrapped in qemu "
"virtualization.  More information and alternatives can be found in "
"L<guestfs(3)/RUNNING COMMANDS>."
msgstr ""
"Esiet ļoti piesardzīgi, izpildot komandas no viesa.  Izpildot komandu viesī, "
"jūs dodat CPU laiku binārajam failam, ko nekontrolējat, ar to pašu lietotāja "
"kontu kā bibliotēkai, kaut arī ietītu qemu virtualizācijā.  Plašāka "
"informācija un alternatīvas atrodamas L<guestfs(3)/KOMANDU IZPILDE>."

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:145
msgid "HISTORICAL SECURITY ISSUES IN LIBGUESTFS"
msgstr "VĒSTURISKAS LIBGUESTFS DROŠĪBAS PROBLĒMAS"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:147
msgid "CVE-2010-3851"
msgstr "CVE-2010-3851"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:149
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/642934>"
msgstr "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/642934>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:151
msgid ""
"This security bug concerns the automatic disk format detection that qemu "
"does on disk images."
msgstr ""
"Šī drošības kļūda attiecas uz automātisku diska formāta noteikšanu, ko qemu "
"veic disku attēliem."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:154
msgid ""
"A raw disk image is just the raw bytes, there is no header.  Other disk "
"images like qcow2 contain a special header.  Qemu deals with this by looking "
"for one of the known headers, and if none is found then assuming the disk "
"image must be raw."
msgstr ""
"Raw diska attēls ir tikai neapstrādāti baiti, bez galvenes.  Citiem disku "
"attēliem, piemēram, qcow2, ir īpaša galvene.  Qemu to risina, meklējot kādu "
"no zināmajām galvenēm, un, ja neviena netiek atrasta, pieņem, ka diska "
"attēlam jābūt raw."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:159
msgid ""
"This allows a guest which has been given a raw disk image to write some "
"other header.  At next boot (or when the disk image is accessed by "
"libguestfs) qemu would do autodetection and think the disk image format was, "
"say, qcow2 based on the header written by the guest."
msgstr ""
"Tas ļauj viesim, kuram dots raw diska attēls, ierakstīt kādu citu galveni.  "
"Nākamajā sāknēšanā (vai kad libguestfs piekļūst diska attēlam) qemu veiktu "
"automātisku noteikšanu un, balstoties uz viesa ierakstīto galveni, "
"uzskatītu, ka diska attēla formāts ir, teiksim, qcow2."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:164
msgid ""
"This in itself would not be a problem, but qcow2 offers many features, one "
"of which is to allow a disk image to refer to another image (called the "
"\"backing disk\").  It does this by placing the path to the backing disk "
"into the qcow2 header.  This path is not validated and could point to any "
"host file (eg. \"/etc/passwd\").  The backing disk is then exposed through "
"\"holes\" in the qcow2 disk image, which of course is completely under the "
"control of the attacker."
msgstr ""
"Tas pats par sevi nebūtu problēma, taču qcow2 piedāvā daudzus līdzekļus, no "
"kuriem viens ļauj diska attēlam atsaukties uz citu attēlu (ko sauc par „"
"pamatdisku”).  Tas to dara, ievietojot ceļu uz pamatdisku qcow2 galvenē.  "
"Šis ceļš netiek validēts un var norādīt uz jebkuru resursdatora failu "
"(piem., „/etc/passwd”).  Pamatdisks tad tiek atklāts caur „caurumiem” qcow2 "
"diska attēlā, kas, protams, ir pilnībā uzbrucēja kontrolē."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:172
msgid "In libguestfs this is rather hard to exploit except under two circumstances:"
msgstr "Libguestfs to ir diezgan grūti izmantot, izņemot divus apstākļus:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:179
msgid "You have enabled the network or have opened the disk in write mode."
msgstr "Ir iespējots tīkls vai disks atvērts rakstīšanas režīmā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:183
msgid ""
"You are also running untrusted code from the guest (see L<guestfs(3)/RUNNING "
"COMMANDS>)."
msgstr ""
"Jūs arī izpildāt neuzticamu kodu no viesa (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/KOMANDU "
"IZPILDE>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:188
msgid ""
"The way to avoid this is to specify the expected disk format when adding "
"disks (the optional C<format> option to "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts>).  You should always do this if the "
"disk is raw format, and it’s a good idea for other cases too.  (See also "
"L<guestfs(3)/DISK IMAGE FORMATS>)."
msgstr ""
"No tā var izvairīties, pievienojot diskus, norādot gaidāmo diska formātu "
"(L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts> neobligātā opcija C<format>).  Tas "
"vienmēr jādara, ja disks ir raw formātā, un tā ir laba doma arī citos "
"gadījumos.  (Skatīt arī L<guestfs(3)/DISKU ATTĒLU FORMĀTI>)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:194
msgid ""
"For disks added from libvirt using calls like "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_domain>, the format is fetched from libvirt and "
"passed through."
msgstr ""
"Diskiem, kas pievienoti no libvirt ar tādiem izsaukumiem kā L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_add_domain>, formāts tiek iegūts no libvirt un nodots tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:198
msgid ""
"For libguestfs tools, use the I<--format> command line parameter as "
"appropriate."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs rīkiem atbilstoši izmantojiet komandrindas parametru I<--format>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:201
msgid "CVE-2011-4127"
msgstr "CVE-2011-4127"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:203
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/752375>"
msgstr "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/752375>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:205
msgid ""
"This is a bug in the kernel which allowed guests to overwrite parts of the "
"host’s drives which they should not normally have access to."
msgstr ""
"Šī ir kodola kļūda, kas ļāva viesiem pārrakstīt tās resursdatora disku "
"daļas, kurām tiem parasti nevajadzētu piekļūt."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:209
msgid ""
"It is sufficient to update libguestfs to any version E<ge> 1.16 which "
"contains a change that mitigates the problem."
msgstr ""
"Pietiek atjaunināt libguestfs uz jebkuru versiju E<ge> 1.16, kas satur "
"izmaiņas, kas mazina problēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:214
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/831117>"
msgstr "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/831117>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:216
msgid ""
"Old versions of both virt-edit and the guestfish C<edit> command created a "
"new file containing the changes but did not set the permissions, etc of the "
"new file to match the old one.  The result of this was that if you edited a "
"security sensitive file such as F</etc/shadow> then it would be left "
"world-readable after the edit."
msgstr ""
"Vecās gan virt-edit, gan guestfish komandas C<edit> versijas izveidoja jaunu "
"failu ar izmaiņām, taču neiestatīja jaunā faila atļaujas u. c. atbilstoši "
"vecajam.  Rezultātā, ja rediģējāt drošībai jutīgu failu, piemēram, F</etc/"
"shadow>, pēc rediģēšanas tas palika lasāms visiem."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:222
msgid "It is sufficient to update libguestfs to any version E<ge> 1.16."
msgstr "Pietiek atjaunināt libguestfs uz jebkuru versiju E<ge> 1.16."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:226
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/968306>"
msgstr "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/968306>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:228
msgid ""
"This security bug was a flaw in inspection where an untrusted guest using a "
"specially crafted file in the guest OS could cause a double-free in the C "
"library (denial of service)."
msgstr ""
"Šī drošības kļūda bija inspicēšanas defekts, kur neuzticams viesis, "
"izmantojot īpaši izveidotu failu viesa OS, varēja izraisīt dubultu "
"atbrīvošanu C bibliotēkā (pakalpojuma atteici)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:232
msgid ""
"It is sufficient to update libguestfs to a version that is not vulnerable: "
"libguestfs E<ge> 1.20.8, E<ge> 1.22.2 or E<ge> 1.23.2."
msgstr ""
"Pietiek atjaunināt libguestfs uz versiju, kas nav ievainojama: libguestfs "
"E<ge> 1.20.8, E<ge> 1.22.2 vai E<ge> 1.23.2."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:237
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/1016960>"
msgstr "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/1016960>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:239
msgid ""
"When using the L<guestfish(1)> I<--remote> or guestfish I<--listen> options, "
"guestfish would create a socket in a known location "
"(F</tmp/.guestfish-$UID/socket-$PID>)."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot L<guestfish(1)> opcijas I<--remote> vai guestfish I<--listen>, "
"guestfish izveidoja ligzdu zināmā vietā (F</tmp/.guestfish-$UID/socket-$PID>)"
"."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:243
msgid ""
"The location has to be a known one in order for both ends to communicate.  "
"However no checking was done that the containing directory "
"(F</tmp/.guestfish-$UID>) is owned by the user.  Thus another user could "
"create this directory and potentially hijack sockets owned by another user’s "
"guestfish client or server."
msgstr ""
"Lai abi gali varētu sazināties, vietai jābūt zināmai.  Tomēr netika "
"pārbaudīts, vai saturošā direktorija (F</tmp/.guestfish-$UID>) pieder "
"lietotājam.  Tādējādi cits lietotājs varēja izveidot šo direktoriju un, "
"iespējams, nolaupīt ligzdas, kas pieder cita lietotāja guestfish klientam "
"vai serverim."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:249
msgid ""
"It is sufficient to update libguestfs to a version that is not vulnerable: "
"libguestfs E<ge> 1.20.12, E<ge> 1.22.7 or E<ge> 1.24."
msgstr ""
"Pietiek atjaunināt libguestfs uz versiju, kas nav ievainojama: libguestfs "
"E<ge> 1.20.12, E<ge> 1.22.7 vai E<ge> 1.24."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:266
msgid "CVE-2014-0191"
msgstr "CVE-2014-0191"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:277
msgid ""
"This was fixed in libguestfs E<ge> 1.27.9 and the fix was backported to "
"stable versions E<ge> 1.26.2, E<ge> 1.24.9, E<ge> 1.22.10 and E<ge> 1.20.13."
msgstr ""
"Tas tika izlabots libguestfs E<ge> 1.27.9, un labojums tika pārnests uz "
"stabilajām versijām E<ge> 1.26.2, E<ge> 1.24.9, E<ge> 1.22.10 un E<ge> "
"1.20.13."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:291
msgid ""
"These two bugs in binutils affect the GNU L<strings(1)> program, and thus "
"the L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_strings> and L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_strings_e> APIs "
"in libguestfs.  Running strings on an untrusted file could cause arbitrary "
"code execution (confined to the libguestfs appliance)."
msgstr ""
"Šīs divas binutils kļūdas ietekmē GNU programmu L<strings(1)> un līdz ar to "
"libguestfs API L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_strings> un L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_strings_e>.  Strings izpilde neuzticamam failam varēja izraisīt "
"patvaļīga koda izpildi (ierobežotu libguestfs palīgsistēmā)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:297
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.29.5 and E<ge> 1.28.3, libguestfs uses the C<strings> "
"I<-a> option to avoid BFD parsing on the file."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.29.5 un E<ge> 1.28.3 libguestfs izmanto C<strings> opciju "
"I<-a>, lai izvairītos no faila BFD parsēšanas."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:300
msgid "CVE-2015-5745"
msgstr "CVE-2015-5745"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:302
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1251157>"
msgstr "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1251157>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:313
msgid ""
"your libguestfs program runs untrusted programs out of the guest (using "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_sh> etc), or"
msgstr ""
"jūsu libguestfs programma izpilda neuzticamas programmas no viesa "
"(izmantojot L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_sh> u. c.) vai"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:325
msgid "Permissions of F<.ssh> and F<.ssh/authorized_keys>"
msgstr "F<.ssh> un F<.ssh/authorized_keys> atļaujas"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:329
msgid ""
"The tools L<virt-customize(1)>, L<virt-sysprep(1)> and L<virt-builder(1)> "
"have an I<--ssh-inject> option for injecting an SSH key into virtual machine "
"disk images.  They may create a F<~user/.ssh> directory and "
"F<~user/.ssh/authorized_keys> file in the guest to do this."
msgstr ""
"Rīkiem L<virt-customize(1)>, L<virt-sysprep(1)> un L<virt-builder(1)> ir "
"opcija I<--ssh-inject> SSH atslēgas ievietošanai virtuālo mašīnu disku "
"attēlos.  Lai to izdarītu, tie viesī var izveidot direktoriju F<~user/.ssh> "
"un failu F<~user/.ssh/authorized_keys>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:335
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<lt> 1.31.5 and libguestfs E<lt> 1.30.2, the new directory "
"and file would get mode C<0755> and mode C<0644> respectively.  However "
"these permissions (especially for F<~user/.ssh>) are wider than the "
"permissions that OpenSSH uses.  In current libguestfs, the directory and "
"file are created with mode C<0700> and mode C<0600>."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<lt> 1.31.5 un libguestfs E<lt> 1.30.2 jaunā direktorija un "
"fails saņēma attiecīgi režīmu C<0755> un C<0644>.  Tomēr šīs atļaujas (it "
"īpaši F<~user/.ssh>) ir plašākas par atļaujām, ko izmanto OpenSSH.  "
"Pašreizējā libguestfs direktorija un fails tiek izveidoti ar režīmu C<0700> "
"un C<0600>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:354
msgid ""
"CVE-2017-5208, CVE-2017-5331, CVE-2017-5332, CVE-2017-5333, CVE-2017-6009, "
"CVE-2017-6010, CVE-2017-6011"
msgstr ""
"CVE-2017-5208, CVE-2017-5331, CVE-2017-5332, CVE-2017-5333, CVE-2017-6009, "
"CVE-2017-6010, CVE-2017-6011"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:357
msgid ""
"Multiple vulnerabilities in the L<wrestool(1)> program in the C<icoutils> "
"package can be exploited for local code execution on the host."
msgstr ""
"Vairākas ievainojamības programmā L<wrestool(1)> pakotnē C<icoutils> var "
"izmantot lokāla koda izpildei resursdatorā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:361
msgid ""
"When libguestfs inspection (see L</Inspection security> above) detects a "
"Windows XP or Windows 7 guest and is asked to find an associated icon for "
"the guest, it will download an untrusted file from the guest and run "
"C<wrestool -x> on that file.  This can lead to local code execution on the "
"host.  Any disk image or guest can be crafted to look like a Windows guest "
"to libguestfs inspection, so just because you do not have Windows guests "
"does not help."
msgstr ""
"Kad libguestfs inspicēšana (skatiet L</Inspicēšanas drošība> iepriekš) "
"nosaka Windows XP vai Windows 7 viesi un tai jāatrod viesim piesaistīta "
"ikona, tā lejupielādē neuzticamu failu no viesa un izpilda šim failam "
"C<wrestool -x>.  Tas var novest pie lokāla koda izpildes resursdatorā.  "
"Jebkuru diska attēlu vai viesi var izveidot tā, lai libguestfs inspicēšanai "
"tas izskatītos pēc Windows viesa, tāpēc tas, ka jums nav Windows viesu, "
"nepalīdz."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:369
msgid ""
"Any program calling the libguestfs API C<guestfs_inspect_get_icon> could be "
"vulnerable.  This includes L<virt-inspector(1)> and L<virt-manager(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Jebkura programma, kas izsauc libguestfs API C<guestfs_inspect_get_icon>, "
"var būt ievainojama.  Tas ietver L<virt-inspector(1)> un L<virt-manager(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:373
msgid ""
"The solution is to update to the non-vulnerable version of icoutils (at "
"least 0.31.1)."
msgstr ""
"Risinājums ir atjaunināt uz icoutils versiju, kas nav ievainojama (vismaz "
"0.31.1)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:376
msgid "CVE-2017-7244, CVE-2017-7245, CVE-2017-7246"
msgstr "CVE-2017-7244, CVE-2017-7245, CVE-2017-7246"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:378
msgid ""
"Multiple vulnerabilities in PCRE could be exploited to crash libguestfs "
"(ie. cause a denial of service) when performing inspection on an untrusted "
"virtual machine."
msgstr ""
"Vairākas PCRE ievainojamības varēja izmantot, lai avarētu libguestfs (t. i., "
"izraisītu pakalpojuma atteici), veicot neuzticamas virtuālās mašīnas "
"inspicēšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:382
msgid ""
"The solution is to update to a version of PCRE with these bugs fixed "
"(upstream version E<ge> 8.41)."
msgstr ""
"Risinājums ir atjaunināt uz PCRE versiju, kurā šīs kļūdas izlabotas "
"(augšteces versija E<ge> 8.41)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:387
msgid ""
"Vulnerabilities affecting qemu user networking (SLIRP) allow a malicious "
"filesystem image to take control of qemu and from there attack the host."
msgstr ""
"Ievainojamības, kas ietekmē qemu lietotāja tīklošanu (SLIRP), ļauj "
"ļaunprātīgam failu sistēmas attēlam pārņemt qemu kontroli un no turienes "
"uzbrukt resursdatoram."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:391
msgid ""
"This affects libguestfs when the backend is set to C<direct> I<and> "
"networking is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Tas ietekmē libguestfs, ja aizmugursistēma ir iestatīta uz C<direct> I<un> "
"tīklošana ir iespējota."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:394
msgid ""
"The direct backend is the default upstream, but not in some downstream Linux "
"distributions including Fedora, Red Hat Enterprise Linux and CentOS.  It "
"might also have been selected if you set the C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=direct> "
"environment variable or called S<C<guestfs_set_backend (g, \"direct\")>>."
msgstr ""
"Tiešā aizmugursistēma ir noklusējums augštecē, bet ne dažās lejteces Linux "
"distribūcijās, tostarp Fedora, Red Hat Enterprise Linux un CentOS.  Tā "
"varēja būt izvēlēta arī tad, ja iestatījāt vides mainīgo "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=direct> vai izsaucāt S<C<guestfs_set_backend (g, "
"\"direct\")>>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:400
msgid ""
"Networking is enabled automatically by some tools (eg. L<virt-builder(1)>), "
"or is enabled if your code called S<C<guestfs_set_network (g, 1)>> (which is "
"not the default)."
msgstr ""
"Tīklošanu automātiski iespējo daži rīki (piem., L<virt-builder(1)>), vai tā "
"tiek iespējota, ja jūsu kods izsauca S<C<guestfs_set_network (g, 1)>> (kas "
"nav noklusējums)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:404
msgid "The libvirt backend is not affected."
msgstr "Libvirt aizmugursistēma netiek ietekmēta."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:406
msgid ""
"The solution is to update qemu to a version containing the fix (see "
"L<https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/qemu-devel/2018-06/msg01012.html>)."
msgstr ""
"Risinājums ir atjaunināt qemu uz versiju, kas satur labojumu (skatiet "
"L<https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/qemu-devel/2018-06/msg01012.html>)."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:409
msgid "CVE-2022-2211"
msgstr "CVE-2022-2211"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:411
msgid "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/CVE-2022-2211>"
msgstr "L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/CVE-2022-2211>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:413
msgid ""
"The C<get_keys> function in F<libguestfs-common/options/keys.c> collects "
"those I<--key> options from the command line into a new array that match a "
"particular block device that's being decrypted for inspection. The function "
"intends to size the result array such that potentially all I<--key> options, "
"plus a terminating C<NULL> element, fit into it. The code mistakenly uses "
"the C<MIN> macro instead of C<MAX>, and therefore only one element is "
"allocated before the C<NULL> terminator."
msgstr ""
"Funkcija C<get_keys> failā F<libguestfs-common/options/keys.c> savāc no "
"komandrindas jaunā masīvā tās I<--key> opcijas, kas atbilst konkrētai bloku "
"ierīcei, kura tiek atšifrēta inspicēšanai. Funkcija paredz noteikt rezultāta "
"masīva izmēru tā, lai tajā ietilptu potenciāli visas I<--key> opcijas un "
"noslēdzošais C<NULL> elements. Kods kļūdaini izmanto makro C<MIN>, nevis "
"C<MAX>, un tāpēc pirms C<NULL> noslēdzēja tiek piešķirts tikai viens "
"elements."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:421
msgid ""
"Passing precisely two I<--key ID:...> options on the command line for the "
"encrypted block device C<ID> causes C<get_keys> to overwrite the terminating "
"C<NULL>, leading to an out-of-bounds read in C<decrypt_mountables>, file "
"F<libguestfs-common/options/decrypt.c>."
msgstr ""
"Precīzi divu I<--key ID:...> opciju nodošana komandrindā šifrētajai bloku "
"ierīcei C<ID> liek C<get_keys> pārrakstīt noslēdzošo C<NULL>, izraisot "
"lasīšanu ārpus robežām funkcijā C<decrypt_mountables>, failā F<libguestfs-"
"common/options/decrypt.c>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:426
msgid ""
"Passing more than two I<--key ID:...> options on the command line for the "
"encrypted block device C<ID> causes C<get_keys> itself to perform "
"out-of-bounds writes. The most common symptom is a crash with C<SIGSEGV> "
"later on."
msgstr ""
"Vairāk nekā divu I<--key ID:...> opciju nodošana komandrindā šifrētajai "
"bloku ierīcei C<ID> liek pašai C<get_keys> veikt rakstīšanu ārpus robežām. "
"Biežākais simptoms ir vēlāka avārija ar C<SIGSEGV>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:431
msgid ""
"This issue affects -- broadly speaking -- all libguestfs-based utilities "
"that accept I<--key>, namely: C<guestfish>, C<guestmount>, C<virt-cat>, "
"C<virt-customize>, C<virt-diff>, C<virt-edit>, C<virt-get-kernel>, "
"C<virt-inspector>, C<virt-log>, C<virt-ls>, C<virt-sparsify>, "
"C<virt-sysprep>, C<virt-tail>, C<virt-v2v>."
msgstr ""
"Šī problēma ietekmē — vispārīgi runājot — visas uz libguestfs balstītās "
"utilītas, kas pieņem I<--key>, proti: C<guestfish>, C<guestmount>, C<virt-"
"cat>, C<virt-customize>, C<virt-diff>, C<virt-edit>, C<virt-get-kernel>, "
"C<virt-inspector>, C<virt-log>, C<virt-ls>, C<virt-sparsify>, C<virt-sysprep>"
", C<virt-tail>, C<virt-v2v>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-security.pod:439
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-internals(1)>, L<guestfs-release-notes(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-testing(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-internals(1)>, L<guestfs-release-notes(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-testing(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-testing - manual testing of libguestfs, you can help!"
msgstr "guestfs-testing - libguestfs manuāla testēšana, jūs varat palīdzēt!"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:7
msgid ""
"This page has manual tests you can try on libguestfs.  Everyone has a "
"slightly different combination of platform, hardware and guests, so this "
"testing is very valuable.  Thanks for helping out!"
msgstr ""
"Šajā lapā ir manuāli testi, ko varat izmēģināt ar libguestfs.  Katram ir "
"nedaudz atšķirīga platformas, aparatūras un viesu kombinācija, tāpēc šī "
"testēšana ir ļoti vērtīga.  Paldies par palīdzību!"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:11
msgid ""
"Tests marked with a B<*> (asterisk) can B<destroy data> if you're not "
"careful.  The others are safe and won't modify anything."
msgstr ""
"Testi, kas atzīmēti ar B<*> (zvaigznīti), var B<iznīcināt datus>, ja neesat "
"uzmanīgi.  Pārējie ir droši un neko nemainīs."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:14
msgid "These tests B<require libguestfs E<ge> 1.22>."
msgstr "Šiem testiem B<nepieciešama libguestfs E<ge> 1.22>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:16
msgid "You can report bugs you find through this link:"
msgstr "Atrastās kļūdas varat ziņot, izmantojot šo saiti:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:20
msgid ""
"or post on the mailing list (registration is B<not> required, but if you're "
"not registered then you'll have to wait for a moderator to manually approve "
"your message):"
msgstr ""
"vai rakstiet pasta sarakstā (reģistrācija B<nav> nepieciešama, taču, bez "
"reģistrācijas, būs jāgaida, kamēr moderators manuāli apstiprinās jūsu "
"ziņojumu):"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:24
msgid "L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>"
msgstr "L<https://lists.libguestfs.org>"

#. type: =head1
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:26
msgid "TESTS"
msgstr "TESTI"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:28
msgid "Run libguestfs-test-tool"
msgstr "Izpildiet libguestfs-test-tool"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:30 docs/guestfs-testing.pod:215
msgid "Run:"
msgstr "Izpildiet:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:34
msgid ""
"This command does a very simple, non-destructive test that basic libguestfs "
"is functioning.  You don't need to run it as root."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda veic ļoti vienkāršu, nedestruktīvu testu, vai pamata libguestfs "
"darbojas.  Tā nav jāizpilda kā root."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:37
msgid ""
"If it I<doesn't> print C<===== TEST FINISHED OK =====>, report it as a bug.  "
"It is very important that you include the B<complete, unedited> output of "
"C<libguestfs-test-tool> in your bug report.  See the L</BUGS> section at the "
"end of this page."
msgstr ""
"Ja tā I<neizdrukā> C<===== TEST FINISHED OK =====>, ziņojiet par to kā "
"kļūdu.  Ir ļoti svarīgi kļūdas ziņojumā iekļaut B<pilnu, nerediģētu> "
"C<libguestfs-test-tool> izvadi.  Skatiet sadaļu L</BUGS> šīs lapas beigās."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:42
msgid "Check KVM acceleration is being used."
msgstr "Pārbaudiet, vai tiek izmantots KVM paātrinājums."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:44
msgid ""
"If your host has hardware virt acceleration, then with a hot cache "
"libguestfs should be able to start up in a few seconds.  Run the following "
"command a few times:"
msgstr ""
"Ja jūsu resursdatoram ir aparatūras virtualizācijas paātrinājums, tad ar "
"karstu kešatmiņu libguestfs vajadzētu startēt dažās sekundēs.  Izpildiet šo "
"komandu dažas reizes:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:50
msgid ""
"After a few runs, the time should settle down to a few seconds (under 3 "
"seconds on fast 64 bit hardware)."
msgstr ""
"Pēc dažām izpildēm laikam vajadzētu nostabilizēties dažās sekundēs (zem 3 "
"sekundēm ātrā 64 bitu aparatūrā)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:53
msgid "If the command above does not work at all, use L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Ja iepriekšējā komanda nemaz nedarbojas, izmantojiet L<libguestfs-test-tool"
"(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:56
msgid "Check which version of libguestfs, qemu, libvirt, etc is being used."
msgstr ""
"Pārbaudiet, kura libguestfs, qemu, libvirt u. c. versija tiek izmantota."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:58
msgid "Look at the output of C<libguestfs-test-tool> and check:"
msgstr "Apskatiet C<libguestfs-test-tool> izvadi un pārbaudiet:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:64
msgid ""
"Which version of libguestfs is being used? Near the beginning of the output "
"you'll see a line like:"
msgstr ""
"Kura libguestfs versija tiek izmantota? Netālu no izvades sākuma redzēsiet "
"tādu rindu kā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" library version: 1.22.0fedora=19,release=1.fc19,libvirt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" library version: 1.22.0fedora=19,release=1.fc19,libvirt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:71
msgid ""
"Is libvirt being used? You can tell the difference by looking for the "
"backend:"
msgstr ""
"Vai tiek izmantots libvirt? Atšķirību var noteikt, meklējot aizmugursistēmu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:74
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_get_backend: direct\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_get_backend: direct\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_get_backend: libvirt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_get_backend: libvirt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:82
msgid "Which version of qemu is being used? It may be printed out:"
msgstr "Kura qemu versija tiek izmantota? Tā var tikt izdrukāta:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" libguestfs: qemu version 1.5\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" libguestfs: qemu version 1.5\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:88
msgid ""
"Which kernel is being used? L<supermin(1)> will try to pick the latest "
"kernel installed on your machine.  You can see the version in the appliance "
"output, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Kurš kodols tiek izmantots? L<supermin(1)> mēģinās izvēlēties jaunāko jūsu "
"datorā instalēto kodolu.  Versiju var redzēt palīgsistēmas izvadē, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" [    0.000000] Linux version 3.9.2-200.fc18.x86_64 [...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" [    0.000000] Linux version 3.9.2-200.fc18.x86_64 [...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:96
msgid "Try to open a local guest image with guestfish."
msgstr "Mēģiniet atvērt lokālu viesa attēlu ar guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:98
msgid ""
"You can use any guest disk image for this test.  Make sure you use the "
"C<--ro> flag so that L<guestfish(1)> will open the disk image read-only."
msgstr ""
"Šim testam varat izmantot jebkuru viesa diska attēlu.  Pārliecinieties, ka "
"izmantojat karogu C<--ro>, lai L<guestfish(1)> atvērtu diska attēlu tikai "
"lasīšanai."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a /path/to/disk.img -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a /path/to/disk.img -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:104
msgid ""
"If the command is successful, it should print out the guest operating system "
"name and put you at the guestfish C<E<gt>E<lt>fsE<gt>> prompt.  You can use "
"guestfish commands like S<C<ll />> to look inside the disk image.  To exit, "
"type C<exit>."
msgstr ""
"Ja komanda izdodas, tai vajadzētu izdrukāt viesa operētājsistēmas nosaukumu "
"un novietot jūs guestfish uzvednē C<E<gt>E<lt>fsE<gt>>.  Lai ieskatītos "
"diska attēlā, varat izmantot tādas guestfish komandas kā S<C<ll />>.  Lai "
"izietu, ierakstiet C<exit>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:109 docs/guestfs-testing.pod:129
msgid ""
"If you get an error, try enabling debugging (add C<-v> to the command "
"line).  Also make sure that L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)> succeeds."
msgstr ""
"Ja saņemat kļūdu, mēģiniet iespējot atkļūdošanu (pievienojiet komandrindai "
"C<-v>).  Pārliecinieties arī, ka L<libguestfs-test-tool(1)> izdodas."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:112
msgid "Try to open a remote guest image with guestfish."
msgstr "Mēģiniet atvērt attālu viesa attēlu ar guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:114
msgid "You may also have to disable libvirt by setting this:"
msgstr "Iespējams, būs arī jāatspējo libvirt, iestatot šo:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:118
msgid "If you have a disk image available over HTTP/FTP, try to open it."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir diska attēls, kas pieejams caur HTTP/FTP, mēģiniet to atvērt."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -i --format=raw -a http://www.example.com/disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -i --format=raw -a http://www.example.com/disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:122
msgid ""
"For SSH you will need to make sure that ssh-agent is set up so you don't "
"need a password to log in to the remote machine.  Then a command similar to "
"this should work:"
msgstr ""
"SSH gadījumā jāpārliecinās, ka ssh-agent ir iestatīts tā, lai pieteikšanās "
"attālajā datorā nebūtu vajadzīga parole.  Tad vajadzētu darboties šādai "
"komandai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:126
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -i --format=raw \\\n"
"   -a ssh://remote.example.com/path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -i --format=raw \\\n"
"   -a ssh://remote.example.com/path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:132
msgid "Run virt-alignment-scan on all your guests."
msgstr "Izpildiet virt-alignment-scan visiem saviem viesiem."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:134
msgid "Run L<virt-alignment-scan(1)> on guests or disk images:"
msgstr "Izpildiet L<virt-alignment-scan(1)> viesiem vai disku attēliem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-alignment-scan -a /path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-alignment-scan -a /path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:140
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-alignment-scan -d Guest\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-alignment-scan -d Guest\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:142
msgid "Does the alignment report match how the guest partitions are aligned?"
msgstr "Vai līdzinājuma atskaite atbilst tam, kā ir līdzināti viesa nodalījumi?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:144
msgid "Run virt-cat on some files in guests."
msgstr "Izpildiet virt-cat dažiem failiem viesos."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:146
msgid "L<virt-cat(1)> can display files from guests.  For a Linux guest, try:"
msgstr "L<virt-cat(1)> var parādīt failus no viesiem.  Linux viesim izmēģiniet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-cat LinuxGuest /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-cat LinuxGuest /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:150
msgid "A recent feature is support for Windows paths, for example:"
msgstr "Nesens līdzeklis ir Windows ceļu atbalsts, piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:152
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-cat WindowsGuest 'c:\\windows\\win.ini'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-cat WindowsGuest 'c:\\windows\\win.ini'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:154
msgid ""
"An even better test is if you have a Windows guest with multiple drives.  Do "
"C<D:>, C<E:> etc paths work correctly?"
msgstr ""
"Vēl labāks tests ir, ja jums ir Windows viesis ar vairākiem diskiem.  Vai "
"ceļi C<D:>, C<E:> u. c. darbojas pareizi?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:157
msgid "B<*> Copy some files into a B<shut off> guest."
msgstr "B<*> Iekopējiet dažus failus B<izslēgtā> viesī."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:159
msgid ""
"L<virt-copy-in(1)> can recursively copy files and directories into a guest "
"or disk image."
msgstr ""
"L<virt-copy-in(1)> var rekursīvi iekopēt failus un direktorijas viesī vai "
"diska attēlā."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-in -d Guest /etc /tmp\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-in -d Guest /etc /tmp\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:164
msgid ""
"This should copy local directory F</etc> to F</tmp/etc> in the guest "
"(recursively).  If you boot the guest, can you see all of the copied files "
"and directories?"
msgstr ""
"Tam vajadzētu nokopēt lokālo direktoriju F</etc> uz F</tmp/etc> viesī "
"(rekursīvi).  Ja sāknējat viesi, vai redzat visus nokopētos failus un "
"direktorijas?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:168
msgid "Shut the guest down and try copying multiple files and directories:"
msgstr "Izslēdziet viesi un mēģiniet kopēt vairākus failus un direktorijas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:170
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-in -d Guest /home /etc/issue /tmp\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-in -d Guest /home /etc/issue /tmp\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:172
msgid "Copy some files out of a guest."
msgstr "Izkopējiet dažus failus no viesa."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:174
msgid ""
"L<virt-copy-out(1)> can recursively copy files and directories out of a "
"guest or disk image."
msgstr ""
"L<virt-copy-out(1)> var rekursīvi izkopēt failus un direktorijas no viesa "
"vai diska attēla."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:179
msgid "Note the final space and period in the command is not a typo."
msgstr "Ņemiet vērā, ka atstarpe un punkts komandas beigās nav drukas kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:181
msgid "This should copy F</home> from the guest into the current directory."
msgstr "Tam vajadzētu nokopēt F</home> no viesa uz pašreizējo direktoriju."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:183
msgid "Run virt-df."
msgstr "Izpildiet virt-df."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:185
msgid "L<virt-df(1)> lists disk space.  Run:"
msgstr "L<virt-df(1)> uzskaita diska vietu.  Izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-df\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-df\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:189
msgid ""
"You can try comparing this to the results from L<df(1)> inside the guest, "
"but there are some provisos:"
msgstr ""
"Varat mēģināt to salīdzināt ar L<df(1)> rezultātiem viesī, taču ir dažas "
"atrunas:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:196
msgid "The guest must be idle."
msgstr "Viesim jābūt dīkstāvē."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:200
msgid "The guest disks must be synched using L<sync(1)>."
msgstr "Viesa diskiem jābūt sinhronizētiem ar L<sync(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:204
msgid ""
"Any action such as booting the guest will write log files causing the "
"numbers to change."
msgstr ""
"Jebkura darbība, piemēram, viesa sāknēšana, rakstīs žurnālu failus, izraisot "
"skaitļu maiņu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:209
msgid ""
"We don’t guarantee that the numbers will be identical even under these "
"circumstances.  They should be similar.  It would indicate a bug if you saw "
"greatly differing numbers."
msgstr ""
"Negarantējam, ka skaitļi būs identiski pat šādos apstākļos.  Tiem vajadzētu "
"būt līdzīgiem.  Ja redzētu ļoti atšķirīgus skaitļus, tas norādītu uz kļūdu."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:213
msgid "Try importing virt-df CSV output into a spreadsheet or database."
msgstr "Mēģiniet importēt virt-df CSV izvadi izklājlapā vai datubāzē."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:217
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-df --csv > /tmp/report.csv\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-df --csv > /tmp/report.csv\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:219
msgid ""
"Now try to load this into your favorite spreadsheet or database.  Are the "
"results reproduced faithfully in the spreadsheet/database?"
msgstr ""
"Tagad mēģiniet to ielādēt savā iecienītajā izklājlapā vai datubāzē.  Vai "
"rezultāti izklājlapā/datubāzē ir atveidoti precīzi?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:222
msgid ""
"L<http://www.postgresql.org/docs/8.1/static/sql-copy.html> "
"L<http://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/5.1/en/load-data.html>"
msgstr ""
"L<http://www.postgresql.org/docs/8.1/static/sql-copy.html> L<http://"
"dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/5.1/en/load-data.html>"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:225
msgid "B<*> Edit a file in a B<shut off> guest."
msgstr "B<*> Rediģējiet failu B<izslēgtā> viesī."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:227
msgid ""
"L<virt-edit(1)> can edit files in guests.  Try this command on a RHEL or "
"Fedora guest:"
msgstr ""
"L<virt-edit(1)> var rediģēt failus viesos.  Izmēģiniet šo komandu RHEL vai "
"Fedora viesī:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:230
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit LinuxGuest /etc/sysconfig/network\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit LinuxGuest /etc/sysconfig/network\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:232
msgid "On other Linux guests try editing other files such as:"
msgstr "Citos Linux viesos mēģiniet rediģēt citus failus, piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:234
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit LinuxGuest /etc/motd\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit LinuxGuest /etc/motd\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:236
msgid "Are the changes seen inside the guest when it is booted?"
msgstr "Vai izmaiņas ir redzamas viesī, kad tas ir sāknēts?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:238
msgid "Display the filesystems / partitions / LVs in a guest."
msgstr "Parādiet viesa failu sistēmas / nodalījumus / LV."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:240
msgid ""
"L<virt-filesystems(1)> can be used to display filesystems in a guest.  Try "
"this command on any disk image or guest:"
msgstr ""
"L<virt-filesystems(1)> var izmantot viesa failu sistēmu parādīšanai.  "
"Izmēģiniet šo komandu jebkuram diska attēlam vai viesim:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:243
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems -a /path/to/disk.img --all --long -h\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems -a /path/to/disk.img --all --long -h\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:247
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems -d Guest --all --long -h\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems -d Guest --all --long -h\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:249
msgid "Do the results match what is seen in the guest?"
msgstr "Vai rezultāti atbilst tam, kas redzams viesī?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:251
msgid "Run virt-inspector on all your guests."
msgstr "Izpildiet virt-inspector visiem saviem viesiem."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:253
msgid ""
"Use L<virt-inspector(1)> to get a report on all of your guests or disk "
"images:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L<virt-inspector(1)>, lai iegūtu atskaiti par visiem saviem "
"viesiem vai disku attēliem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:256
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector -a /path/to/disk.img | less\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector -a /path/to/disk.img | less\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:260
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector -d Guest | less\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector -d Guest | less\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:262
msgid "Do the results match what is actually in the guest?"
msgstr "Vai rezultāti atbilst tam, kas faktiski ir viesī?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:264
msgid ""
"If you have an unusual guest (a rare Linux distro, a very new version of "
"Windows), does virt-inspector recognize it? If not, then it's probably a "
"bug."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir neparasts viesis (reta Linux distribūcija, ļoti jauna Windows "
"versija), vai virt-inspector to atpazīst? Ja nē, tā, visticamāk, ir kļūda."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:268
msgid "Try the auditing features of virt-ls on all your guests."
msgstr "Izmēģiniet virt-ls audita līdzekļus visiem saviem viesiem."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:270
msgid "List all setuid or setgid programs in a Linux virtual machine:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas setuid vai setgid programmas Linux virtuālajā mašīnā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:272
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep '^- [42]'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep '^- [42]'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:274
msgid "List all public-writable directories in a Linux virtual machine:"
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visas publiski rakstāmās direktorijas Linux virtuālajā mašīnā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep '^d ...7'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep '^d ...7'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:278
msgid "List all Unix domain sockets in a Linux virtual machine:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas Unix domēna ligzdas Linux virtuālajā mašīnā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:280
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep '^s'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep '^s'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:282
msgid "List all regular files with filenames ending in ‘.png’:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visus parastos failus, kuru nosaukumi beidzas ar ‘.png’:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:284
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep -i '^-.*\\.png$'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest / | grep -i '^-.*\\.png$'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:286
msgid "Display files larger than 10MB in home directories:"
msgstr "Parādīt failus, kas lielāki par 10MB, mājas direktorijās:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:288
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest /home | awk '$3 > 10*1024*1024'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest /home | awk '$3 > 10*1024*1024'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:290
msgid "Find everything modified in the last 7 days:"
msgstr "Atrast visu, kas mainīts pēdējo 7 dienu laikā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:292
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest --time-days / | awk '$6 <= 7'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest --time-days / | awk '$6 <= 7'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:294
msgid "Find regular files modified in the last 24 hours:"
msgstr "Atrast parastos failus, kas mainīti pēdējo 24 stundu laikā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:296
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest --time-days / | grep '^-' | awk '$6 < 1'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d Guest --time-days / | grep '^-' | awk '$6 < 1'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:298
msgid "Do the results match what is in the guest?"
msgstr "Vai rezultāti atbilst tam, kas ir viesī?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:300
msgid "Create a disk image from a tarball."
msgstr "Izveidojiet diska attēlu no tar arhīva."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:302
msgid ""
"Use L<virt-make-fs(1)> to create a disk image from any tarball that you "
"happen to have:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L<virt-make-fs(1)>, lai izveidotu diska attēlu no jebkura tar "
"arhīva, kas jums gadās būt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:305
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs --partition=mbr --type=vfat /any/tarball.tar.gz output.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs --partition=mbr --type=vfat /any/tarball.tar.gz output.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:307
msgid ""
"Add ‘output.img’ as a raw disk to an existing guest.  Check the guest can "
"see the files.  This test is particularly useful if you try it with a "
"Windows guest."
msgstr ""
"Pievienojiet ‘output.img’ kā raw disku esošam viesim.  Pārbaudiet, vai "
"viesis redz failus.  Šis tests ir īpaši noderīgs, ja to izmēģināt ar Windows "
"viesi."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:311
msgid "Try other partitioning schemes, eg. I<--partition=gpt>."
msgstr "Izmēģiniet citas nodalījumu shēmas, piem., I<--partition=gpt>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:313
msgid "Try other filesystem formats, eg. I<--type=ntfs>, I<--type=ext2>."
msgstr ""
"Izmēģiniet citus failu sistēmu formātus, piem., I<--type=ntfs>, I<--"
"type=ext2>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:315
msgid "B<*> Run virt-rescue on a B<shut off> disk image or guest."
msgstr "B<*> Izpildiet virt-rescue B<izslēgtam> diska attēlam vai viesim."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:317
msgid ""
"Use L<virt-rescue(1)> to examine, rescue or repair a B<shut off> guest or "
"disk image:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L<virt-rescue(1)>, lai pārbaudītu, glābtu vai labotu B<izslēgtu> "
"viesi vai diska attēlu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:320
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue -a /path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue -a /path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:324
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue -d Guest\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue -d Guest\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:326
msgid "Can you use ordinary shell commands to examine the guest?"
msgstr "Vai viesa pārbaudei varat izmantot parastas čaulas komandas?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:328
msgid "B<*> Resize your guests."
msgstr "B<*> Mainiet savu viesu izmēru."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:330
msgid ""
"Use L<virt-resize(1)> to give a guest some more disk space.  For example, if "
"you have a disk image that is smaller than 30G, increase it to 30G by doing:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L<virt-resize(1)>, lai dotu viesim vairāk diska vietas.  "
"Piemēram, ja jums ir diska attēls, kas mazāks par 30G, palieliniet to līdz "
"30G šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:334
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" truncate -s 30G newdisk.img\n"
" virt-filesystems -a /path/to/olddisk.img --all --long -h\n"
" virt-resize /path/to/olddisk.img newdisk.img --expand /dev/sda1\n"
" qemu-kvm -m 1024 -hda newdisk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" truncate -s 30G newdisk.img\n"
" virt-filesystems -a /path/to/olddisk.img --all --long -h\n"
" virt-resize /path/to/olddisk.img newdisk.img --expand /dev/sda1\n"
" qemu-kvm -m 1024 -hda newdisk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:339
msgid "Does the guest still boot? Try expanding other partitions."
msgstr "Vai viesis joprojām sāknējas? Mēģiniet paplašināt citus nodalījumus."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:341
msgid "B<*> Sparsify a guest disk."
msgstr "B<*> Retiniet viesa disku."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:343
msgid "Using L<virt-sparsify(1)>, make a disk image more sparse:"
msgstr "Izmantojot L<virt-sparsify(1)>, padariet diska attēlu retinātāku:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:345
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify /path/to/olddisk.img newdisk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify /path/to/olddisk.img newdisk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:347
msgid ""
"Is F<newdisk.img> still bootable after sparsifying? Is the resulting disk "
"image smaller (use C<du> to check)?"
msgstr ""
"Vai F<newdisk.img> pēc retināšanas joprojām ir sāknējams? Vai iegūtais diska "
"attēls ir mazāks (pārbaudiet ar C<du>)?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:350
msgid "Build and boot a guest"
msgstr "Viesa būvēšana un sāknēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:352
msgid "Using L<virt-builder(1)>, choose a guest from the list:"
msgstr "Izmantojot L<virt-builder(1)>, izvēlieties viesi no saraksta:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:354
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-builder -l\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-builder -l\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:356
msgid "build it:"
msgstr "uzbūvējiet to:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:358
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-builder -o disk.img [os-version from list above]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-builder -o disk.img [os-version from list above]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:360
msgid "and boot it:"
msgstr "un sāknējiet to:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" qemu-kvm -cpu host -m 2048 -drive file=disk.img,format=raw\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" qemu-kvm -cpu host -m 2048 -drive file=disk.img,format=raw\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:364
msgid "Does it boot?"
msgstr "Vai tas sāknējas?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:366
msgid "B<*> \"Sysprep\" a B<shut off> Linux guest."
msgstr "B<*> Veiciet „sysprep” B<izslēgtam> Linux viesim."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:368
msgid ""
"B<Note> that this really will mess up an existing guest, so it's better to "
"clone the guest before trying this."
msgstr ""
"B<Ņemiet vērā>, ka tas tiešām sabojās esošu viesi, tāpēc pirms izmēģināšanas "
"labāk viesi klonēt."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:371
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sysprep --hostname newhost.example.com -a /path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sysprep --hostname newhost.example.com -a /path/to/disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:373
msgid ""
"Was the sysprep successful? After booting, what changes were made and were "
"they successful?"
msgstr ""
"Vai sysprep izdevās? Kādas izmaiņas tika veiktas pēc sāknēšanas un vai tās "
"izdevās?"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:376
msgid "Dump the Windows Registry from your Windows guests."
msgstr "Izmetiet Windows reģistru no saviem Windows viesiem."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:378
msgid ""
"Use L<virt-win-reg(1)> to dump out the Windows Registry from any Windows "
"guests that you have."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L<virt-win-reg(1)>, lai izmestu Windows reģistru no jebkuriem "
"jums esošajiem Windows viesiem."

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:381
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-win-reg --unsafe-printable-strings WindowsGuest 'HKLM\\Software' |\n"
"   less\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-win-reg --unsafe-printable-strings WindowsGuest 'HKLM\\Software' |\n"
"   less\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:384
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-win-reg --unsafe-printable-strings WindowsGuest 'HKLM\\System' |\n"
"   less\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-win-reg --unsafe-printable-strings WindowsGuest 'HKLM\\System' |\n"
"   less\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:387
msgid "Does the output match running C<regedit> inside the guest?"
msgstr "Vai izvade atbilst C<regedit> izpildei viesī?"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:389
msgid ""
"A recent feature is the ability to dump user registries, so try this, "
"replacing I<username> with the name of a local user in the guest:"
msgstr ""
"Nesens līdzeklis ir iespēja izmest lietotāju reģistrus, tāpēc izmēģiniet to, "
"aizstājot I<username> ar viesa lokālā lietotāja vārdu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:392
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-win-reg --unsafe-printable-strings WindowsGuest 'HKEY_USERS\\username' "
"|\n"
"   less\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-win-reg --unsafe-printable-strings WindowsGuest 'HKEY_USERS\\username' "
"|\n"
"   less\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:397
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-testing.pod:408 erlang/examples/guestfs-erlang.pod:116
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:102 fish/virt-copy-in.pod:58
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:53 fish/virt-tar-in.pod:56 fish/virt-tar-out.pod:55
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:180 perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:59
msgid "Copyright (C) 2011-2025 Red Hat Inc."
msgstr "Copyright (C) 2011-2025 Red Hat Inc."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1
msgid "Subdirectory F<lib>"
msgstr "Apakšdirektorija F<lib>"

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3
msgid "File F<lib/actions-support.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<lib/actions-support.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:5
msgid "Helper functions for the actions code in F<lib/actions-*.c>."
msgstr "Palīgfunkcijas darbību kodam failos F<lib/actions-*.c>."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:7
msgid "File F<lib/appliance-cpu.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<lib/appliance-cpu.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:9
msgid "The appliance choice of CPU model."
msgstr "Palīgsistēmas CPU modeļa izvēle."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:11
msgid "Function C<lib/appliance-cpu.c:guestfs_int_get_cpu_model>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/appliance-cpu.c:guestfs_int_get_cpu_model>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" const char *\n"
" guestfs_int_get_cpu_model (int kvm)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" const char *\n"
" guestfs_int_get_cpu_model (int kvm)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:16
msgid ""
"Return the right CPU model to use as the qemu C<-cpu> parameter or its "
"equivalent in libvirt.  This returns:"
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt pareizo CPU modeli, ko izmantot kā qemu parametru C<-cpu> vai tā "
"ekvivalentu libvirt.  Tas atgriež:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:21
msgid "C<\"host\">"
msgstr "C<\"host\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:23
msgid "The literal string C<\"host\"> means use C<-cpu host>."
msgstr "Burtiskā virkne C<\"host\"> nozīmē izmantot C<-cpu host>."

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:25
msgid "C<\"max\">"
msgstr "C<\"max\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:27
msgid ""
"The literal string C<\"max\"> means use C<-cpu max> (the best possible).  "
"This requires awkward translation for libvirt."
msgstr ""
"Burtiskā virkne C<\"max\"> nozīmē izmantot C<-cpu max> (labāko iespējamo).  "
"Tam libvirt nepieciešama neveikla tulkošana."

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:30
msgid "some string"
msgstr "kāda virkne"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:32
msgid "Some string such as C<\"cortex-a57\"> means use C<-cpu cortex-a57>."
msgstr ""
"Kāda virkne, piemēram, C<\"cortex-a57\">, nozīmē izmantot C<-cpu cortex-a57>."

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:34
msgid "C<NULL>"
msgstr "C<NULL>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:36
msgid ""
"C<NULL> means no C<-cpu> option at all.  Note returning C<NULL> does not "
"indicate an error."
msgstr ""
"C<NULL> nozīmē, ka opcijas C<-cpu> vispār nav.  Ņemiet vērā, ka C<NULL> "
"atgriešana nenorāda kļūdu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:41
msgid ""
"This is made unnecessarily hard and fragile because of two stupid choices in "
"QEMU:"
msgstr ""
"Tas ir padarīts nevajadzīgi grūts un trausls divu muļķīgu QEMU izvēļu dēļ:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:48
msgid ""
"The default for C<qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt> is to emulate a C<cortex-a15> "
"(WTF?)."
msgstr ""
"C<qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt> noklusējums ir emulēt C<cortex-a15> (WTF?)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:53
msgid ""
"We don't know for sure if KVM will work, but C<-cpu host> is broken with "
"TCG, so we almost always pass a broken C<-cpu> flag if KVM is semi-broken in "
"any way."
msgstr ""
"Mēs nezinām droši, vai KVM darbosies, bet C<-cpu host> ar TCG ir bojāts, "
"tāpēc gandrīz vienmēr nododam bojātu C<-cpu> karogu, ja KVM jebkādā veidā ir "
"daļēji bojāts."

