msgid ""
"Errors in libguestfs API calls are handled by setting an error message and "
"optional errno in the handle.  The caller has the choice of testing API "
"calls to find out if they failed and then querying the last error from the "
"handle, and/or getting a callback."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas libguestfs API izsaukumos tiek apstrādātas, rokturī iestatot kļūdas "
"ziņojumu un pēc izvēles errno.  Izsaucējs var izvēlēties pārbaudīt API "
"izsaukumus, lai noskaidrotu, vai tie neizdevās, un pēc tam vaicāt rokturim "
"pēdējo kļūdu, un/vai saņemt atzvanu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:755
msgid ""
"From the point of view of the library source, generally you should use the "
"C<error> or C<perrorf> macros along error paths, eg:"
msgstr ""
"No bibliotēkas pirmkoda viedokļa kļūdu ceļos parasti jāizmanto makro "
"C<error> vai C<perrorf>, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:758
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" if (something_bad) {\n"
"   error (g, \"something bad happened\");\n"
"   return -1;\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" if (something_bad) {\n"
"   error (g, \"something bad happened\");\n"
"   return -1;\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:763
msgid ""
"Make sure to call the C<error> or C<perrorf> macro exactly once along each "
"error path, since the handle can only store a single error and the previous "
"error will be overwritten."
msgstr ""
"Pārliecinieties, ka katrā kļūdas ceļā makro C<error> vai C<perrorf> tiek "
"izsaukts tieši vienreiz, jo rokturis var glabāt tikai vienu kļūdu, un "
"iepriekšējā kļūda tiks pārrakstīta."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:767
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_warning>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_warning>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:769
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_warning (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_warning (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:772
msgid "Print a warning."
msgstr "Izdrukāt brīdinājumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:774
msgid ""
"Code should I<not> call this function directly.  Use the S<C<warning (g, fs, "
"...)>> macro."
msgstr ""
"Kodam šo funkciju I<nevajadzētu> izsaukt tieši.  Izmantojiet makro "
"S<C<warning (g, fs, ...)>>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:777
msgid ""
"Warnings are printed unconditionally.  We try to make these rare: Generally "
"speaking, a warning should either be an error, or if it's not important for "
"end users then it should be a debug message."
msgstr ""
"Brīdinājumi tiek izdrukāti bez nosacījumiem.  Cenšamies, lai tie būtu reti: "
"vispārīgi runājot, brīdinājumam vajadzētu būt vai nu kļūdai, vai, ja tas "
"galalietotājiem nav svarīgs, atkļūdošanas ziņojumam."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:781
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_debug>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_debug>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:783
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_debug (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_debug (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:786
msgid "Print a debug message."
msgstr "Izdrukāt atkļūdošanas ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:788
msgid ""
"Code should I<not> call this function directly.  To add debug messages in "
"the library, use the S<C<debug (g, fs, ...)>> macro.  The macro checks if "
"C<g-E<gt>verbose> is false and avoids the function call, meaning the macro "
"is more efficient."
msgstr ""
"Kodam šo funkciju I<nevajadzētu> izsaukt tieši.  Lai pievienotu atkļūdošanas "
"ziņojumus bibliotēkā, izmantojiet makro S<C<debug (g, fs, ...)>>.  Makro "
"pārbauda, vai C<g-E<gt>verbose> ir false, un izvairās no funkcijas "
"izsaukuma, tāpēc makro ir efektīvāks."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:793
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_trace>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_trace>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:795
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_trace (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_trace (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:798
msgid "Print a trace message."
msgstr "Izdrukāt izsekošanas ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:800
msgid "Do not call this function.  All calls are generated automatically."
msgstr "Neizsauciet šo funkciju.  Visi izsaukumi tiek ģenerēti automātiski."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:802
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_error_errno>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_error_errno>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:804
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_error_errno (guestfs_h *g, int errnum, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_error_errno (guestfs_h *g, int errnum, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:807
msgid ""
"Set the last error and errno in the handle, and optionally raise the error "
"callback if one is defined."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt rokturī pēdējo kļūdu un errno un pēc izvēles izraisīt kļūdas "
"atzvanu, ja tāds ir definēts."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:810
msgid ""
"If you don't need to set errno, use the S<C<error (g, fs, ...)>> macro "
"instead of calling this directly.  If you need to set errno then there is no "
"macro wrapper, so calling this function directly is fine."
msgstr ""
"Ja errno nav jāiestata, šīs funkcijas tiešas izsaukšanas vietā izmantojiet "
"makro S<C<error (g, fs, ...)>>.  Ja errno jāiestata, makro ietinēja nav, "
"tāpēc šīs funkcijas tieša izsaukšana ir pareiza."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:815
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_perrorf>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_perrorf>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:817
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_perrorf (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_perrorf (guestfs_h *g, const char *fs, ...)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:820
msgid ""
"Similar to L<perror(3)>, but it sets the last error in the handle, raises "
"the error callback if one is defined, and supports format strings."
msgstr ""
"Līdzīgi L<perror(3)>, taču tas iestata rokturī pēdējo kļūdu, izraisa kļūdas "
"atzvanu, ja tāds ir definēts, un atbalsta formāta virknes."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:824
msgid ""
"You should probably use the S<C<perrorf (g, fs, ...)>> macro instead of "
"calling this directly."
msgstr ""
"Visticamāk, šīs funkcijas tiešas izsaukšanas vietā jāizmanto makro "
"S<C<perrorf (g, fs, ...)>>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:827
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_launch_failed_error>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_launch_failed_error>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:829
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_launch_failed_error (guestfs_h *g)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_launch_failed_error (guestfs_h *g)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:832
msgid "Raise a launch failed error in a standard format."
msgstr "Izraisīt palaišanas neizdošanās kļūdu standarta formātā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:834
msgid ""
"Since this is the most common error seen by people who have installation "
"problems, buggy qemu, etc, and since no one reads the FAQ, describe in this "
"error message what resources are available to debug launch problems."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā šī ir visbiežākā kļūda, ko redz cilvēki ar instalēšanas problēmām, "
"kļūdainu qemu u. c., un tā kā neviens nelasa BUJ, šajā kļūdas ziņojumā "
"aprakstīt, kādi resursi ir pieejami palaišanas problēmu atkļūdošanai."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:839
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_unexpected_close_error>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_unexpected_close_error>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:841
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_unexpected_close_error (guestfs_h *g)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" guestfs_int_unexpected_close_error (guestfs_h *g)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:844
msgid "Raise an error if the appliance unexpectedly crashes after launch."
msgstr "Izraisīt kļūdu, ja palīgsistēma pēc palaišanas negaidīti avarē."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:846
msgid "Function C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_launch_timeout>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/errors.c:guestfs_int_launch_timeout>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:848
#, no-wrap
