#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1447
msgid ""
"Return C<true> if we can call S<C<passt --help>>, and it exits with status "
"C<0> or C<1>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt C<true>, ja varam izsaukt S<C<passt --help>> un tas iziet ar "
"statusu C<0> vai C<1>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1450
msgid ""
"(At least C<passt-0^20230222.g4ddbcb9-2.el9_2.x86_64> terminates with status "
"C<1> in response to \"--help\", which is arguably wrong, and potentially "
"subject to change, but it doesn't really matter.)"
msgstr ""
"(Vismaz C<passt-0^20230222.g4ddbcb9-2.el9_2.x86_64> atbildē uz „--help” "
"beidzas ar statusu C<1>, kas, iespējams, ir nepareizi un var mainīties, taču "
"tam nav īstas nozīmes.)"

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1454
msgid "File F<lib/private-data.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<lib/private-data.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1456
msgid ""
"Implement a private data area where libguestfs C API users can attach "
"arbitrary pieces of data to a C<guestfs_h> handle."
msgstr ""
"Realizēt privātu datu apgabalu, kur libguestfs C API lietotāji var "
"piesaistīt rokturim C<guestfs_h> patvaļīgus datu gabalus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1459
msgid "For more information see L<guestfs(3)/PRIVATE DATA AREA>."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<guestfs(3)/PRIVĀTO DATU APGABALS>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1461
msgid ""
"Language bindings do not generally expose this, largely because in non-C "
"languages it is easy to associate data with handles in other ways (using "
"hash tables or maps)."
msgstr ""
"Valodu saistījumi to parasti neatklāj, galvenokārt tāpēc, ka ne-C valodās "
"datus ar rokturiem ir viegli saistīt citos veidos (izmantojot jaucējtabulas "
"vai kartes)."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1465
msgid "Structure C<lib/private-data.c:pda_entry>"
msgstr "Struktūra C<lib/private-data.c:pda_entry>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1467
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" struct pda_entry {\n"
"   char *key;                    /* key */\n"
"   void *data;                   /* opaque user data pointer */\n"
" };\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" struct pda_entry {\n"
"   char *key;                    /* key */\n"
"   void *data;                   /* opaque user data pointer */\n"
" };\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1472
msgid ""
"The private data area is internally stored as a gnulib hash table containing "
"C<pda_entry> structures."
msgstr ""
"Privātais datu apgabals iekšēji tiek glabāts kā gnulib jaucējtabula ar "
"C<pda_entry> struktūrām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1475
msgid ""
"Note the private data area is allocated lazily, since the vast majority of "
"callers will never use it.  This means C<g-E<gt>pda> is likely to be "
"C<NULL>."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka privātais datu apgabals tiek piešķirts slinki, jo lielākā "
"daļa izsaucēju to nekad neizmantos.  Tas nozīmē, ka C<g-E<gt>pda>, "
"visticamāk, būs C<NULL>."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1479
msgid "File F<lib/proto.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<lib/proto.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1481
msgid ""
"This is the code used to send and receive RPC messages and (for certain "
"types of message) to perform file transfers.  This code is driven from the "
"generated actions (F<lib/actions-*.c>).  There are five different cases to "
"consider:"
msgstr ""
"Šis ir kods, ko izmanto RPC ziņojumu sūtīšanai un saņemšanai un (noteiktiem "
"ziņojumu tipiem) failu pārsūtīšanai.  Šo kodu vada ģenerētās darbības (F<lib/"
"actions-*.c>).  Jāapsver pieci dažādi gadījumi:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1490
msgid ""
"A non-daemon function (eg. L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_verbose>).  There is no "
"RPC involved at all, it's all handled inside the library."
msgstr ""
"Ne-dēmona funkcija (piem., L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_verbose>).  RPC vispār "
"nav iesaistīts, viss tiek apstrādāts bibliotēkā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1496
msgid ""
"A simple RPC (eg. L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_mount>).  We write the request, then "
"read the reply.  The sequence of calls is:"
msgstr ""
"Vienkāršs RPC (piem., L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_mount>).  Rakstām pieprasījumu, "
"tad nolasām atbildi.  Izsaukumu secība ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1499
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  guestfs_int_send\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  guestfs_int_send\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1504
msgid ""
"An RPC with C<FileIn> parameters (eg. L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_upload>).  We "
"write the request, then write the file(s), then read the reply.  The "
"sequence of calls is:"
msgstr ""
"RPC ar C<FileIn> parametriem (piem., L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_upload>).  Rakstām "
"pieprasījumu, tad rakstām failu(s), tad nolasām atbildi.  Izsaukumu secība "
"ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1508
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  guestfs_int_send\n"
"  guestfs_int_send_file  (possibly multiple times)\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  guestfs_int_send\n"
"  guestfs_int_send_file  (possibly multiple times)\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1514
msgid ""
"An RPC with C<FileOut> parameters (eg. L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_download>).  We "
"write the request, then read the reply, then read the file(s).  The sequence "
"of calls is:"
msgstr ""
"RPC ar C<FileOut> parametriem (piem., L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_download>).  "
"Rakstām pieprasījumu, tad nolasām atbildi, tad nolasām failu(s).  Izsaukumu "
"secība ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1518
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  guestfs_int_send\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv_file  (possibly multiple times)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  guestfs_int_send\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv\n"
"  guestfs_int_recv_file  (possibly multiple times)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1524
msgid ""
"Both C<FileIn> and C<FileOut> parameters.  There are no calls like this in "
"the current API, but they would be implemented as a combination of cases 3 "
"and 4."
msgstr ""
"Gan C<FileIn>, gan C<FileOut> parametri.  Pašreizējā API šādu izsaukumu nav, "
"taču tie tiktu realizēti kā 3. un 4. gadījuma kombinācija."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:1530
msgid ""
"All read/write/etc operations are performed using the current connection "
"module (C<g-E<gt>conn>).  During operations the connection module "
"transparently handles log messages that appear on the console."
msgstr ""
"Visas lasīšanas/rakstīšanas u. c. darbības tiek veiktas, izmantojot "
"pašreizējo savienojuma moduli (C<g-E<gt>conn>).  Darbību laikā savienojuma "
"modulis caurspīdīgi apstrādā žurnāla ziņojumus, kas parādās konsolē."

