msgstr "Funkcija C<lib/wait.c:guestfs_int_waitpid>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" guestfs_int_waitpid (guestfs_h *g, pid_t pid, int *status, const char "
"*errmsg)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" guestfs_int_waitpid (guestfs_h *g, pid_t pid, int *status, const char "
"*errmsg)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2112
msgid "A safe version of L<waitpid(3)> which retries if C<EINTR> is returned."
msgstr ""
"Droša L<waitpid(3)> versija, kas mēģina atkārtoti, ja tiek atgriezts C<EINTR>"
"."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2115
msgid ""
"I<Note:> this only needs to be used in the library, or in programs that "
"install a non-restartable C<SIGCHLD> handler (which is not the case for any "
"current libguestfs virt tools)."
msgstr ""
"I<Piezīme:> tas jāizmanto tikai bibliotēkā vai programmās, kas instalē "
"nepārstartējamu C<SIGCHLD> apstrādātāju (kas neattiecas ne uz vienu "
"pašreizējo libguestfs virt rīku)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2119
msgid ""
"If the main program installs a SIGCHLD handler and sets it to be "
"non-restartable, then what can happen is the library is waiting in a wait "
"syscall, the child exits, C<SIGCHLD> is sent to the process, and the wait "
"syscall returns C<EINTR>.  Since the library cannot control the signal "
"handler, we have to instead restart the wait syscall, which is the purpose "
"of this wrapper."
msgstr ""
"Ja galvenā programma instalē SIGCHLD apstrādātāju un iestata to kā "
"nepārstartējamu, var gadīties, ka bibliotēka gaida wait sistēmas izsaukumā, "
"bērnprocess iziet, procesam tiek nosūtīts C<SIGCHLD>, un wait sistēmas "
"izsaukums atgriež C<EINTR>.  Tā kā bibliotēka nevar kontrolēt signālu "
"apstrādātāju, mums tā vietā jāpārstartē wait sistēmas izsaukums, kas ir šī "
"ietinēja mērķis."

