#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2508
msgid "File F<common/qemuopts/qemuopts.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<common/qemuopts/qemuopts.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2512
msgid ""
"There are some shortcomings with the model used for qemu options which "
"aren't clear until you try to convert options into a configuration file.  "
"However if we attempted to model the options in more detail then this "
"library would be both very difficult to use and incompatible with older "
"versions of qemu.  Hopefully the current model is a decent compromise."
msgstr ""
"qemu opcijām izmantotajam modelim ir daži trūkumi, kas nav skaidri, līdz "
"mēģināt pārveidot opcijas konfigurācijas failā.  Tomēr, ja mēģinātu modelēt "
"opcijas sīkāk, šī bibliotēka būtu gan ļoti grūti lietojama, gan nesaderīga "
"ar vecākām qemu versijām.  Cerams, pašreizējais modelis ir pieņemams "
"kompromiss."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2519
msgid "For reference here are the problems:"
msgstr "Atsaucei šeit ir problēmas:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2525
msgid ""
"There's inconsistency in qemu between options and config file, eg.  C<-smp "
"4> becomes:"
msgstr ""
"Qemu ir nekonsekvence starp opcijām un konfigurācijas failu, piem., C<-smp "
"4> kļūst par:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2528
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" [smp-opts]\n"
"   cpus = \"4\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" [smp-opts]\n"
"   cpus = \"4\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2533
msgid ""
"Similar to the previous point, you can write either C<-smp 4> or C<-smp "
"cpus=4> (although this won't work in very old qemu).  When generating a "
"config file you need to know the implicit key name."
msgstr ""
"Līdzīgi iepriekšējam punktam var rakstīt vai nu C<-smp 4>, vai C<-smp "
"cpus=4> (lai gan ļoti vecā qemu tas nedarbosies).  Ģenerējot konfigurācijas "
"failu, jāzina netiešais atslēgas nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2539
msgid ""
"In C<-opt key=value,...> the C<key> is really a tree/array specifier.  The "
"way this works is complicated but hinted at here: "
"L<http://git.qemu.org/?p=qemu.git;a=blob;f=util/keyval.c;h=93d5db6b590427e412dfb172f1c406d6dd8958c1;hb=HEAD>"
msgstr ""
"Konstrukcijā C<-opt key=value,...> C<key> patiesībā ir koka/masīva "
"specifikators.  Tas, kā tas darbojas, ir sarežģīti, bet mājiens dots šeit: "
"L<http://git.qemu.org/?p=qemu.git;a=blob;f=util/"
"keyval.c;h=93d5db6b590427e412dfb172f1c406d6dd8958c1;hb=HEAD>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2546
msgid ""
"Some options are syntactic sugar.  eg. C<-kernel foo> is sugar for "
"C<-machine kernel=foo>."
msgstr ""
"Dažas opcijas ir sintaktiskais cukurs.  Piem., C<-kernel foo> ir "
"sintaktiskais cukurs izteiksmei C<-machine kernel=foo>."

