" char **\n"
" qemuopts_to_argv (struct qemuopts *qopts)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2738
msgid ""
"Return a NULL-terminated argument list, of the kind that can be passed "
"directly to L<execv(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt ar NULL noslēgtu argumentu sarakstu tādā veidā, ko var nodot tieši "
"L<execv(3)>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2741
msgid ""
"C<qemuopts_set_binary*> must be called first.  It will be returned as "
"C<argv[0]> in the returned list."
msgstr ""
"Vispirms jāizsauc C<qemuopts_set_binary*>.  Tas tiks atgriezts kā C<argv[0]> "
"atgrieztajā sarakstā."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2744
msgid "The list of strings and the strings themselves must be freed by the caller."
msgstr "Virkņu sarakstu un pašas virknes jāatbrīvo izsaucējam."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2749
msgid "Function C<common/qemuopts/qemuopts.c:qemuopts_to_config_file>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<common/qemuopts/qemuopts.c:qemuopts_to_config_file>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2751
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" qemuopts_to_config_file (struct qemuopts *qopts, const char *filename)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" qemuopts_to_config_file (struct qemuopts *qopts, const char *filename)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2754
msgid ""
"Write the qemu options to a qemu config file, suitable for reading in using "
"C<qemu -readconfig filename>."
msgstr ""
"Ierakstīt qemu opcijas qemu konfigurācijas failā, kas piemērots nolasīšanai "
"ar C<qemu -readconfig filename>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2757
msgid ""
"Note that qemu config files have limitations on content and quoting, so not "
"all qemuopts structs can be written (this function returns an error in these "
"cases).  For more information see "
"L<https://habkost.net/posts/2016/12/qemu-apis-qemuopts.html> "
"L<https://bugs.launchpad.net/qemu/+bug/1686364>"
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka qemu konfigurācijas failiem ir satura un pēdiņu "
"ierobežojumi, tāpēc ne visas qemuopts struktūras var ierakstīt (šādos "
"gadījumos šī funkcija atgriež kļūdu).  Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<https://"
"habkost.net/posts/2016/12/qemu-apis-qemuopts.html> L<https://"
"bugs.launchpad.net/qemu/+bug/1686364>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2763
msgid ""
"Also, command line argument names and config file sections sometimes have "
"different names.  For example the equivalent of C<-m 1024> is:"
msgstr ""
"Turklāt komandrindas argumentu nosaukumiem un konfigurācijas faila sadaļām "
"dažreiz ir atšķirīgi nosaukumi.  Piemēram, C<-m 1024> ekvivalents ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2767
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" [memory]\n"
"   size = \"1024\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" [memory]\n"
"   size = \"1024\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2770
msgid ""
"This code does I<not> attempt to convert between the two forms.  You just "
"need to know how to do that yourself."
msgstr ""
"Šis kods I<nemēģina> pārveidot starp abām formām.  Jums vienkārši pašiem "
"jāzina, kā to izdarīt."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2775
msgid "Function C<common/qemuopts/qemuopts.c:qemuopts_to_config_channel>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<common/qemuopts/qemuopts.c:qemuopts_to_config_channel>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2777
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" qemuopts_to_config_channel (struct qemuopts *qopts, FILE *fp)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" qemuopts_to_config_channel (struct qemuopts *qopts, FILE *fp)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2780
msgid "Same as C<qemuopts_to_config_file>, but this writes to a C<FILE *fp>."
msgstr "Tas pats, kas C<qemuopts_to_config_file>, bet raksta C<FILE *fp>."

#. type: =head2
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2782
msgid "Subdirectory F<common/utils>"
msgstr "Apakšdirektorija F<common/utils>"

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2784
msgid "File F<common/utils/cleanups.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<common/utils/cleanups.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2786 docs/internal-documentation.pod:2826
msgid ""
"Libguestfs uses C<CLEANUP_*> macros to simplify temporary allocations.  They "
"are implemented using the C<__attribute__((cleanup))> feature of gcc and "
"clang.  Typical usage is:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs izmanto makro C<CLEANUP_*>, lai vienkāršotu pagaidu piešķiršanu.  "
"Tie realizēti, izmantojot gcc un clang līdzekli C<__attribute__((cleanup))>"
".  Tipisks lietojums ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2791 docs/internal-documentation.pod:2831
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" fn ()\n"
" {\n"
"   CLEANUP_FREE char *str = NULL;\n"
"   str = safe_asprintf (g, \"foo\");\n"
"   // str is freed automatically when the function returns\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" fn ()\n"
" {\n"
"   CLEANUP_FREE char *str = NULL;\n"
"   str = safe_asprintf (g, \"foo\");\n"
"   // str is freed automatically when the function returns\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2798 docs/internal-documentation.pod:2838
msgid "There are a few catches to be aware of with the cleanup mechanism:"
msgstr "Ar tīrīšanas mehānismu jāņem vērā daži āķi:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2804 docs/internal-documentation.pod:2844
msgid ""
"If a cleanup variable is not initialized, then you can end up calling "
"L<free(3)> with an undefined value, resulting in the program crashing.  For "
"this reason, you should usually initialize every cleanup variable with "
"something, eg. C<NULL>"
msgstr ""
"Ja tīrīšanas mainīgais nav inicializēts, var nākties izsaukt L<free(3)> ar "
"nedefinētu vērtību, izraisot programmas avāriju.  Šī iemesla dēļ parasti "
"katrs tīrīšanas mainīgais jāinicializē ar kaut ko, piem., C<NULL>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2811 docs/internal-documentation.pod:2851
msgid "Don't mark variables holding return values as cleanup variables."
msgstr ""
"Neatzīmējiet mainīgos, kas glabā atgriešanas vērtības, kā tīrīšanas mainīgos."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2815 docs/internal-documentation.pod:2855
msgid ""
"The C<main()> function shouldn't use cleanup variables since it is normally "
"exited by calling L<exit(3)>, and that doesn't call the cleanup handlers."
msgstr ""
"Funkcijai C<main()> nevajadzētu izmantot tīrīšanas mainīgos, jo no tās "
"parasti iziet, izsaucot L<exit(3)>, un tas neizsauc tīrīšanas apstrādātājus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2821 docs/internal-documentation.pod:2861
msgid ""
"The functions in this file are used internally by the C<CLEANUP_*> macros.  "
"Don't call them directly."
msgstr ""
"Šajā failā esošās funkcijas iekšēji izmanto makro C<CLEANUP_*>.  Neizsauciet "
"tās tieši."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2824
msgid "File F<common/utils/gnulib-cleanups.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<common/utils/gnulib-cleanups.c>"

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2864
msgid "File F<common/utils/guestfs-utils.h>"
msgstr "Fails F<common/utils/guestfs-utils.h>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2866
msgid ""
"This header file is included in all \"frontend\" parts of libguestfs, namely "
"the library, non-C language bindings, virt tools and tests."
msgstr ""
"Šis galvenes fails tiek iekļauts visās libguestfs „priekšgala” daļās, proti, "
"bibliotēkā, ne-C valodu saistījumos, virt rīkos un testos."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2869
msgid ""
"The daemon does B<not> use this header.  If you need a place to put "
"something shared with absolutely everything including the daemon, put it in "
"F<lib/guestfs-internal-all.h>"
msgstr ""
"Dēmons šo galveni B<neizmanto>.  Ja jums vajadzīga vieta kaut kam, kas tiek "
"koplietots ar pilnīgi visu, ieskaitot dēmonu, ievietojiet to failā F<lib/"
"guestfs-internal-all.h>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2873
msgid ""
"If a definition is only needed by a single component of libguestfs (eg. just "
"the library, or just a single virt tool) then it should B<not> be here!"
msgstr ""
"Ja definīcija nepieciešama tikai vienam libguestfs komponentam (piem., tikai "
"bibliotēkai vai tikai vienam virt rīkam), tai B<nevajadzētu> būt šeit!"

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2877
msgid "File F<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h>"
msgstr "Fails F<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2879
msgid ""
"These macros make it easier to write XML.  To use them correctly you must be "
"aware of these assumptions:"
msgstr ""
"Šie makro atvieglo XML rakstīšanu.  Lai tos izmantotu pareizi, jāzina šie "
"pieņēmumi:"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2886
msgid ""
"The C<xmlTextWriterPtr> is called C<xo>.  It is used implicitly by all the "
"macros."
msgstr "C<xmlTextWriterPtr> sauc C<xo>.  To netieši izmanto visi makro."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2891
msgid ""
"On failure, a function called C<xml_error> is called which you must define "
"(usually as a macro).  You must use C<CLEANUP_*> macros in your functions if "
"you want correct cleanup of local variables along the error path."
msgstr ""
"Neizdošanās gadījumā tiek izsaukta funkcija C<xml_error>, kas jums jādefinē "
"(parasti kā makro).  Ja vēlaties pareizu lokālo mainīgo tīrīšanu kļūdas "
"ceļā, savās funkcijās jāizmanto makro C<CLEANUP_*>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2898
msgid "All the \"bad\" casting is hidden inside the macros."
msgstr "Visa „sliktā” tipu pārveidošana ir paslēpta makro iekšienē."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2902
msgid "Definition C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:start_element>"
msgstr "Definīcija C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:start_element>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2904
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #define start_element\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #define start_element\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2906
msgid "To define an XML element use:"
msgstr "Lai definētu XML elementu, izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2908
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" start_element (\"name\") {\n"
"   ...\n"
" } end_element ();\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" start_element (\"name\") {\n"
"   ...\n"
" } end_element ();\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2912
msgid "which produces C<<< <name>...</name> >>>"
msgstr "kas rada C<<< <name>...</name> >>>"

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2914
msgid "Definition C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:empty_element>"
msgstr "Definīcija C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:empty_element>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2916
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #define empty_element\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #define empty_element\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2918
msgid "To define an empty element:"
msgstr "Lai definētu tukšu elementu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2920
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" empty_element (\"name\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" empty_element (\"name\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2922
msgid "which produces C<<< <name/> >>>"
msgstr "kas rada C<<< <name/> >>>"

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2924
msgid "Definition C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:single_element>"
msgstr "Definīcija C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:single_element>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2926
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #define single_element\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #define single_element\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2928
msgid "To define a single element with no attributes containing some text:"
msgstr "Lai definētu vienu elementu bez atribūtiem, kas satur kādu tekstu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2930
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" single_element (\"name\", text);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" single_element (\"name\", text);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2932
msgid "which produces C<<< <name>text</name> >>>"
msgstr "kas rada C<<< <name>text</name> >>>"

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2934
msgid "Definition C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:single_element_format>"
msgstr ""
"Definīcija C<common/utils/libxml2-writer-macros.h:single_element_format>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2936
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #define single_element_format\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #define single_element_format\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2938
msgid ""
"To define a single element with no attributes containing some text using a "
"format string:"
msgstr ""
"Lai definētu vienu elementu bez atribūtiem, kas satur kādu tekstu, "
"izmantojot formāta virkni:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:2941
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" single_element_format (\"cores\", \"%d\", nr_cores);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" single_element_format (\"cores\", \"%d\", nr_cores);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
