msgstr ""
"Atrisina C<path> kā iespējamu Windows ceļu atbilstoši C<root>, dodot jaunu "
"ceļu, ko var izmantot libguestfs API izsaukumos."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3461
msgid "C<root> must be a Windows installation"
msgstr "C<root> jābūt Windows instalācijai"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3465
msgid "relies on an already being done introspection"
msgstr "paļaujas uz jau veiktu introspekciju"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3469
msgid ""
"will unmount all the existing mount points and mount the Windows root "
"(according to C<readonly>)"
msgstr ""
"atmontēs visus esošos montēšanas punktus un montēs Windows sakni (atbilstoši "
"C<readonly>)"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3474
msgid "calls L<exit(3)> on memory allocation failures"
msgstr "atmiņas piešķiršanas neizdošanās gadījumā izsauc L<exit(3)>"

#. type: =head2
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3478
msgid "Subdirectory F<daemon>"
msgstr "Apakšdirektorija F<daemon>"

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3480
msgid "File F<daemon/command.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<daemon/command.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3482
msgid ""
"This file contains a number of useful functions for running external "
"commands and capturing their output."
msgstr ""
"Šis fails satur vairākas noderīgas funkcijas ārēju komandu izpildei un to "
"izvades tveršanai."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3485
msgid "Function C<daemon/command.c:commandf>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/command.c:commandf>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3487
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" commandf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"           const char *name, ...)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" commandf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"           const char *name, ...)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3491
msgid "Run a command.  Optionally capture stdout and stderr as strings."
msgstr "Izpildīt komandu.  Pēc izvēles tvert stdout un stderr kā virknes."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3493
msgid ""
"Returns C<0> if the command ran successfully, or C<-1> if there was any "
"error."
msgstr ""
"Atgriež C<0>, ja komanda izpildījās veiksmīgi, vai C<-1>, ja bija kāda kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3496
msgid "For a description of the C<flags> see C<commandrvf>."
msgstr "C<flags> aprakstu skatiet C<commandrvf>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3498
msgid ""
"There is also a macro C<command(out,err,name,...)> which calls C<commandf> "
"with C<flags=0>."
msgstr ""
"Ir arī makro C<command(out,err,name,...)>, kas izsauc C<commandf> ar "
"C<flags=0>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3501
msgid "Function C<daemon/command.c:commandrf>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/command.c:commandrf>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3503
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" commandrf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"            const char *name, ...)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" commandrf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"            const char *name, ...)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3507
msgid ""
"Same as C<command>, but we allow the status code from the subcommand to be "
"non-zero, and return that status code."
msgstr ""
"Tas pats, kas C<command>, bet ļaujam apakškomandas statusa kodam nebūt "
"nullei un atgriežam šo statusa kodu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3510
msgid "We still return C<-1> if there was some other error."
msgstr "Joprojām atgriežam C<-1>, ja bija kāda cita kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3512
msgid ""
"There is also a macro C<commandr(out,err,name,...)> which calls C<commandrf> "
"with C<flags=0>."
msgstr ""
"Ir arī makro C<commandr(out,err,name,...)>, kas izsauc C<commandrf> ar "
"C<flags=0>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3515
msgid "Function C<daemon/command.c:commandvf>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/command.c:commandvf>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3517
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" commandvf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"            char const *const *argv)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" commandvf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"            char const *const *argv)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3521
msgid "Same as C<command>, but passing in an argv array."
msgstr "Tas pats, kas C<command>, bet nododot argv masīvu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3523
msgid ""
"There is also a macro C<commandv(out,err,argv)> which calls C<commandvf> "
"with C<flags=0>."
msgstr ""
"Ir arī makro C<commandv(out,err,argv)>, kas izsauc C<commandvf> ar C<flags=0>"
"."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3526
msgid "Function C<daemon/command.c:commandrvf>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/command.c:commandrvf>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3528
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" commandrvf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"             char const* const *argv)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" commandrvf (char **stdoutput, char **stderror, unsigned flags,\n"
"             char const* const *argv)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3532
msgid ""
"This is a more sane version of L<system(3)> for running external commands.  "
"It uses fork/execvp, so we don't need to worry about quoting of parameters, "
"and it allows us to capture any error messages in a buffer."
msgstr ""
"Šī ir saprātīgāka L<system(3)> versija ārēju komandu izpildei.  Tā izmanto "
"fork/execvp, tāpēc mums nav jāuztraucas par parametru pēdiņām, un tā ļauj "
"tvert jebkurus kļūdu ziņojumus buferī."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3537
msgid ""
"If C<stdoutput> is not C<NULL>, then C<*stdoutput> will return the stdout of "
"the command as a string."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<stdoutput> nav C<NULL>, C<*stdoutput> atgriezīs komandas stdout kā "
"virkni."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3540
msgid ""
"If C<stderror> is not C<NULL>, then C<*stderror> will return the stderr of "
"the command.  If there is a final \\n character, it is removed so you can "
"use the error string directly in a call to C<reply_with_error>."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<stderror> nav C<NULL>, C<*stderror> atgriezīs komandas stderr.  Ja "
"beigās ir rakstzīme \\n, tā tiek noņemta, lai kļūdas virkni varētu tieši "
"izmantot izsaukumā C<reply_with_error>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3545
msgid "Flags are:"
msgstr "Karogi ir:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3549
msgid "C<COMMAND_FLAG_FOLD_STDOUT_ON_STDERR>"
msgstr "C<COMMAND_FLAG_FOLD_STDOUT_ON_STDERR>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3551
msgid ""
"For broken external commands that send error messages to stdout (hello, "
"parted) but that don't have any useful stdout information, use this flag to "
"capture the error messages in the C<*stderror> buffer.  If using this flag, "
"you should pass C<stdoutput=NULL> because nothing could ever be captured in "
"that buffer."
msgstr ""
"Bojātām ārējām komandām, kas sūta kļūdu ziņojumus uz stdout (sveiks, parted)"
", bet kurām nav noderīgas stdout informācijas, izmantojiet šo karogu, lai "
"tvertu kļūdu ziņojumus buferī C<*stderror>.  Ja izmantojat šo karogu, "
"jānodod C<stdoutput=NULL>, jo šajā buferī nekad nekas netiktu tverts."

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3557
msgid "C<COMMAND_FLAG_CHROOT_COPY_FILE_TO_STDIN>"
msgstr "C<COMMAND_FLAG_CHROOT_COPY_FILE_TO_STDIN>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3559
msgid ""
"For running external commands on chrooted files correctly (see "
"L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/579608>) specifying this flag causes another "
"process to be forked which chroots into sysroot and just copies the input "
"file to stdin of the specified command.  The file descriptor is ORed with "
"the flags, and that file descriptor is always closed by this function.  See "
"F<daemon/hexdump.c> for an example of usage."
msgstr ""
"Pareizai ārēju komandu izpildei ar chroot failiem (skatiet L<https://"
"bugzilla.redhat.com/579608>) šī karoga norādīšana liek sazarot vēl vienu "
"procesu, kas veic chroot uz sysroot un vienkārši kopē ievades failu "
"norādītās komandas stdin.  Failu deskriptors tiek apvienots ar karogiem ar "
"OR, un šī funkcija šo failu deskriptoru vienmēr aizver.  Lietojuma piemēru "
"skatiet F<daemon/hexdump.c>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3569
msgid ""
"There is also a macro C<commandrv(out,err,argv)> which calls C<commandrvf> "
"with C<flags=0>."
msgstr ""
"Ir arī makro C<commandrv(out,err,argv)>, kas izsauc C<commandrvf> ar "
"C<flags=0>."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3572
msgid "File F<daemon/device-name-translation.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<daemon/device-name-translation.c>"

