#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3579
msgid "Cache daemon disk mapping."
msgstr "Kešot dēmona disku kartēšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3581
msgid ""
"When the daemon starts up, populate a cache with the contents of "
"/dev/disk/by-path.  It's easiest to use C<ls -lv> here since the names are "
"sorted awkwardly."
msgstr ""
"Kad dēmons startē, aizpildīt kešatmiņu ar /dev/disk/by-path saturu.  Šeit "
"vieglāk ir izmantot C<ls -lv>, jo nosaukumi ir sakārtoti neērti."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3585
msgid "Function C<daemon/device-name-translation.c:device_name_translation>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/device-name-translation.c:device_name_translation>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3587
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char *\n"
" device_name_translation (const char *device)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char *\n"
" device_name_translation (const char *device)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3590
msgid "Perform device name translation."
msgstr "Veikt ierīču nosaukumu tulkošanu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3592
msgid ""
"Libguestfs defines a few standard formats for device names.  (see also "
"L<guestfs(3)/BLOCK DEVICE NAMING> and "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_canonical_device_name>).  They are:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs definē dažus standarta ierīču nosaukumu formātus.  (Skatīt arī "
"L<guestfs(3)/BLOKU IERĪČU NOSAUKUMI> un L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_canonical_device_name>.)  Tie ir:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3598
msgid "F</dev/sdX[N]>"
msgstr "F</dev/sdX[N]>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3600
msgid "F</dev/hdX[N]>"
msgstr "F</dev/hdX[N]>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3602
msgid "F</dev/vdX[N]>"
msgstr "F</dev/vdX[N]>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3604
msgid ""
"These mean the Nth partition on the Xth device.  Because Linux no longer "
"enumerates devices in the order they are passed to qemu, we must translate "
"these by looking up the actual device using /dev/disk/by-path/"
msgstr ""
"Tie nozīmē N-to nodalījumu X-ajā ierīcē.  Tā kā Linux vairs neuzskaita "
"ierīces secībā, kādā tās tiek nodotas qemu, tās jātulko, meklējot faktisko "
"ierīci caur /dev/disk/by-path/"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3609
msgid "F</dev/mdX>"
msgstr "F</dev/mdX>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3611
msgid "F</dev/VG/LV>"
msgstr "F</dev/VG/LV>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3613
msgid "F</dev/mapper/...>"
msgstr "F</dev/mapper/...>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3615 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:1473
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:2489
msgid "F</dev/dm-N>"
msgstr "F</dev/dm-N>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3617
msgid "These are not translated here."
msgstr "Tie šeit netiek tulkoti."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3621
msgid "It returns a newly allocated string which the caller must free."
msgstr "Tā atgriež jaunpiešķirtu virkni, kas izsaucējam jāatbrīvo."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3623
msgid "It returns C<NULL> on error.  B<Note> it does I<not> call C<reply_with_*>."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas gadījumā tā atgriež C<NULL>.  B<Ņemiet vērā>, ka tā I<neizsauc> "
"C<reply_with_*>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3626
msgid ""
"We have to open the device and test for C<ENXIO>, because the device nodes "
"may exist in the appliance."
msgstr ""
"Ierīce jāatver un jāpārbauda C<ENXIO>, jo ierīču mezgli var eksistēt "
"palīgsistēmā."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3629
msgid "File F<daemon/guestfsd.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<daemon/guestfsd.c>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3631
msgid ""
"This is the guestfs daemon which runs inside the guestfs appliance.  This "
"file handles start up and connecting back to the library."
msgstr ""
"Šis ir guestfs dēmons, kas darbojas guestfs palīgsistēmā.  Šis fails "
"apstrādā startēšanu un savienošanos atpakaļ ar bibliotēku."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3634
msgid "Function C<daemon/guestfsd.c:shell_quote>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/guestfsd.c:shell_quote>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3636
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" shell_quote (const char *str, FILE *fp)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" shell_quote (const char *str, FILE *fp)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3639
msgid "Write C<str> to the file C<fp>, ensuring it is shell quoted."
msgstr "Ierakstīt C<str> failā C<fp>, nodrošinot, ka tas ir čaulas pēdiņās."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3641
msgid "Function C<daemon/guestfsd.c:sysroot_shell_quote>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/guestfsd.c:sysroot_shell_quote>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3643
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" sysroot_shell_quote (const char *path, FILE *fp)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" sysroot_shell_quote (const char *path, FILE *fp)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3646
msgid ""
"Write C<sysroot> + C<path> to the file C<fp>, ensuring it is shell quoted.  "
"The path must be an absolute path."
msgstr ""
"Ierakstīt C<sysroot> + C<path> failā C<fp>, nodrošinot, ka tas ir čaulas "
"pēdiņās.  Ceļam jābūt absolūtam ceļam."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3649
msgid "File F<daemon/initrd.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<daemon/initrd.c>"

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3651
msgid "Function C<daemon/initrd.c:skip_early_cpio_archive>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/initrd.c:skip_early_cpio_archive>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3653
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" static off_t\n"
" skip_early_cpio_archive (int fd, off_t offset, off_t file_size)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" static off_t\n"
" skip_early_cpio_archive (int fd, off_t offset, off_t file_size)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3656
msgid ""
"Modern initramfs images are often composed of several concatenated cpio "
"archives: one or more uncompressed \"early cpio\" archives (used by the "
"kernel/dracut to carry CPU microcode etc, see "
"F<Documentation/x86/microcode.rst> in the kernel sources) followed by the "
"main, compressed cpio archive containing the real initramfs contents."
msgstr ""
"Mūsdienu initramfs attēli bieži sastāv no vairākiem savienotiem cpio "
"arhīviem: viena vai vairākiem nesaspiestiem „agrīnajiem cpio” arhīviem (ko "
"kodols/dracut izmanto CPU mikrokoda u. c. pārnēsāšanai, skatiet "
"F<Documentation/x86/microcode.rst> kodola pirmkodā), kam seko galvenais, "
"saspiestais cpio arhīvs ar īsto initramfs saturu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3663
msgid ""
"This parses a single newc/crc format cpio archive starting at C<offset> in "
"C<fd>, up to and including its C<TRAILER!!!> entry, and returns the offset "
"of the byte following it, rounded up to the next 512-byte boundary (early "
"cpio archives are padded to a block boundary before the next archive is "
"appended).  Returns C<-1> if the archive is truncated or malformed."
msgstr ""
"Šis parsē vienu newc/crc formāta cpio arhīvu, sākot no C<offset> failā C<fd>"
", līdz pat tā ierakstam C<TRAILER!!!> ieskaitot, un atgriež aiz tā sekojošā "
"baita nobīdi, noapaļotu uz augšu līdz nākamajai 512 baitu robežai (agrīnie "
"cpio arhīvi pirms nākamā arhīva pievienošanas tiek papildināti līdz bloka "
"robežai).  Atgriež C<-1>, ja arhīvs ir saīsināts vai nepareizi veidots."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3670
msgid "Function C<daemon/initrd.c:detect_initrd>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/initrd.c:detect_initrd>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3672
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" static int\n"
" detect_initrd (const char *path, off_t *offset_r,\n"
"                enum initrd_compression *compression_r)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" static int\n"
" detect_initrd (const char *path, off_t *offset_r,\n"
"                enum initrd_compression *compression_r)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3676
msgid ""
"Work out where the \"real\" (possibly compressed) cpio archive starts within "
"C<path>, skipping over any leading uncompressed early cpio archives, and "
"detect its compression format (if any)  by looking at its magic bytes."
msgstr ""
"Noskaidrot, kur C<path> sākas „īstais” (iespējams, saspiestais) cpio arhīvs, "
"izlaižot jebkurus sākuma nesaspiestos agrīnos cpio arhīvus, un noteikt tā "
"saspiešanas formātu (ja tāds ir), aplūkojot tā maģiskos baitus."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3681
msgid ""
"Returns 0 on success, or -1 on error (having already called "
"C<reply_with_*>)."
msgstr ""
"Atgriež 0 veiksmes gadījumā vai -1 kļūdas gadījumā (jau izsaucot "
"C<reply_with_*>)."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3684
