msgstr ""
"Atgriezt true tad un tikai tad, ja ierīce ir saknes ierīce (un tāpēc no "
"lietotāja izsaukumu viedokļa ir jāignorē)."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3707
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:is_device_parameter>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:is_device_parameter>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3709
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" is_device_parameter (const char *device)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" is_device_parameter (const char *device)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3712
msgid ""
"Parameters marked as C<Device>, C<Dev_or_Path>, etc can be passed a block "
"device name.  This function tests if the parameter is a block device name."
msgstr ""
"Parametriem, kas atzīmēti kā C<Device>, C<Dev_or_Path> u. c., var nodot "
"bloku ierīces nosaukumu.  Šī funkcija pārbauda, vai parametrs ir bloku "
"ierīces nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3716
msgid ""
"It can also be used in daemon code to test if the string passed as a "
"C<Dev_or_Path> parameter is a device or path."
msgstr ""
"To var izmantot arī dēmona kodā, lai pārbaudītu, vai virkne, kas nodota kā "
"C<Dev_or_Path> parametrs, ir ierīce vai ceļš."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3719
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:sysroot_path>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:sysroot_path>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3721
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char *\n"
" sysroot_path (const char *path)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char *\n"
" sysroot_path (const char *path)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3724
msgid "Turn C<\"/path\"> into C<\"/sysroot/path\">."
msgstr "Pārvērst C<\"/path\"> par C<\"/sysroot/path\">."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3726 docs/internal-documentation.pod:3740
msgid ""
"Returns C<NULL> on failure.  The caller I<must> check for this and call "
"S<C<reply_with_perror (\"malloc\")>>.  The caller must also free the "
"returned string."
msgstr ""
"Neizdošanās gadījumā atgriež C<NULL>.  Izsaucējam tas I<jāpārbauda> un "
"jāizsauc S<C<reply_with_perror (\"malloc\")>>.  Izsaucējam arī jāatbrīvo "
"atgrieztā virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3730 docs/internal-documentation.pod:3744
msgid "See also the custom C<%R> printf formatter which does shell quoting too."
msgstr ""
"Skatīt arī pielāgoto printf formatētāju C<%R>, kas arī liek čaulas pēdiņas."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3732
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:sysroot_realpath>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:sysroot_realpath>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3734
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char *\n"
" sysroot_realpath (const char *path)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char *\n"
" sysroot_realpath (const char *path)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3737
msgid "Resolve path within sysroot, calling C<sysroot_path> on the resolved path."
msgstr ""
"Atrisināt ceļu sysroot ietvaros, izsaucot C<sysroot_path> atrisinātajam "
"ceļam."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3746
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:is_power_of_2>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:is_power_of_2>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3748
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" is_power_of_2 (unsigned long v)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" is_power_of_2 (unsigned long v)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3751
msgid "Returns true if C<v> is a power of 2."
msgstr "Atgriež true, ja C<v> ir 2 pakāpe."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3753
msgid ""
"Uses the algorithm described at "
"L<http://graphics.stanford.edu/~seander/bithacks.html#DetermineIfPowerOf2>"
msgstr ""
"Izmanto algoritmu, kas aprakstīts L<http://graphics.stanford.edu/~seander/"
"bithacks.html#DetermineIfPowerOf2>"

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3756
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:split_lines_sb>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:split_lines_sb>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3758
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" struct stringsbuf\n"
" split_lines_sb (char *str)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" struct stringsbuf\n"
" split_lines_sb (char *str)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3761
msgid ""
"Split an output string into a NULL-terminated list of lines, wrapped into a "
"stringsbuf."
msgstr ""
"Sadalīt izvades virkni ar NULL noslēgtā rindu sarakstā, ietītā stringsbuf."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3764
msgid ""
"Typically this is used where we have run an external command which has "
"printed out a list of things, and we want to return an actual list."
msgstr ""
"Parasti to izmanto, ja esam izpildījuši ārēju komandu, kas izdrukājusi lietu "
"sarakstu, un vēlamies atgriezt īstu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3768
msgid "The corner cases here are quite tricky.  Note in particular:"
msgstr "Robežgadījumi šeit ir diezgan viltīgi.  It īpaši ņemiet vērā:"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3772
msgid "C<\"\">"
msgstr "C<\"\">"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3776
msgid "C<\"\\n\">"
msgstr "C<\"\\n\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3778
msgid "returns C<[\"\"]>"
msgstr "atgriež C<[\"\"]>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3780
msgid "C<\"a\\nb\">"
msgstr ""
"C<\"a\\n"
"b\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3782 docs/internal-documentation.pod:3786
msgid "returns C<[\"a\"; \"b\"]>"
msgstr "atgriež C<[\"a\"; \"b\"]>"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3784
msgid "C<\"a\\nb\\n\">"
msgstr ""
"C<\"a\\n"
"b\\n\">"

#. type: =item
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3788
msgid "C<\"a\\nb\\n\\n\">"
msgstr ""
"C<\"a\\n"
"b\\n\\n\">"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3790
msgid "returns C<[\"a\"; \"b\"; \"\"]>"
msgstr "atgriež C<[\"a\"; \"b\"; \"\"]>"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3794
msgid ""
"The original string is written over and destroyed by this function (which is "
"usually OK because it's the 'out' string from C<command*()>).  You can free "
"the original string, because C<add_string()> strdups the strings."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija pārraksta un iznīcina oriģinālo virkni (kas parasti ir labi, jo "
"tā ir C<command*()> 'out' virkne).  Oriģinālo virkni var atbrīvot, jo "
"C<add_string()> izveido virkņu kopijas ar strdup."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3799
msgid "C<argv> in the C<struct stringsbuf> will be C<NULL> in case of errors."
msgstr "Kļūdu gadījumā C<argv> struktūrā C<struct stringsbuf> būs C<NULL>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3801
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:filter_list>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:filter_list>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3803
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char **\n"
" filter_list (bool (*p) (const char *str), char **strs)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char **\n"
" filter_list (bool (*p) (const char *str), char **strs)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3806
msgid ""
"Filter a list of strings.  Returns a newly allocated list of only the "
"strings where C<p (str) == true>."
msgstr ""
"Filtrēt virkņu sarakstu.  Atgriež jaunpiešķirtu sarakstu tikai ar tām "
"virknēm, kurām C<p (str) == true>."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3809
msgid "B<Note> it does not copy the strings, be careful not to double-free them."
msgstr ""
"B<Ņemiet vērā>, ka tas nekopē virknes, uzmanieties tās neatbrīvot divreiz."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3812
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:trim>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:trim>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3814
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" trim (char *str)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" trim (char *str)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3817
msgid "Skip leading and trailing whitespace, updating the original string in-place."
msgstr ""
"Izlaist sākuma un beigu atstarpes, atjauninot oriģinālo virkni uz vietas."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3820
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:parse_btrfsvol>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:parse_btrfsvol>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3822
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" parse_btrfsvol (const char *desc_orig, mountable_t *mountable)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" parse_btrfsvol (const char *desc_orig, mountable_t *mountable)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3825
msgid ""
"Parse the mountable descriptor for a btrfs subvolume.  Don't call this "
"directly; it is only used from the stubs."
msgstr ""
"Parsēt btrfs apakšsējuma montējamā objekta deskriptoru.  Neizsauciet to "
"tieši; to izmanto tikai no aizstājējiem."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3828
msgid "A btrfs subvolume is given as:"
msgstr "Btrfs apakšsējums tiek norādīts kā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3830
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" btrfsvol:/dev/sda3/root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" btrfsvol:/dev/sda3/root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3832
msgid ""
"where F</dev/sda3> is a block device containing a btrfs filesystem, and root "
"is the name of a subvolume on it. This function is passed the string "
"following C<\"btrfsvol:\">."
msgstr ""
"kur F</dev/sda3> ir bloku ierīce ar btrfs failu sistēmu, un root ir "
"apakšsējuma nosaukums tajā. Šai funkcijai tiek nodota virkne aiz "
"C<\"btrfsvol:\">."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3836
msgid ""
"On success, C<mountable-E<gt>device> and C<mountable-E<gt>volume> must be "
"freed by the caller."
msgstr ""
"Veiksmes gadījumā izsaucējam jāatbrīvo C<mountable-E<gt>device> un "
"C<mountable-E<gt>volume>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3839
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:mountable_to_string>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:mountable_to_string>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3841
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char *\n"
" mountable_to_string (const mountable_t *mountable)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char *\n"
" mountable_to_string (const mountable_t *mountable)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3844
msgid "Convert a C<mountable_t> back to its string representation"
msgstr "Pārvērst C<mountable_t> atpakaļ tā virknes attēlojumā"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3846
msgid ""
"This function can be used in an error path, so must not call "
"C<reply_with_error>."
msgstr ""
"Šo funkciju var izmantot kļūdas ceļā, tāpēc tā nedrīkst izsaukt "
"C<reply_with_error>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3849
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:prog_exists>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:prog_exists>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3851
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" prog_exists (const char *prog)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" prog_exists (const char *prog)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3854
msgid "Check program exists and is executable on C<$PATH>."
msgstr "Pārbaudīt, vai programma eksistē un ir izpildāma C<$PATH>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3856
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:random_name>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:random_name>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3858
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" random_name (char *template)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" random_name (char *template)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3861
msgid ""
"Pass a template such as C<\"/sysroot/XXXXXXXX.XXX\">.  This updates the "
"template to contain a randomly named file.  Any C<'X'> characters after the "
"final C<'/'> in the template are replaced with random characters."
msgstr ""
"Nododiet veidni, piemēram, C<\"/sysroot/XXXXXXXX.XXX\">.  Tas atjaunina "
"veidni, lai tā saturētu nejauši nosauktu failu.  Visas rakstzīmes C<'X'> aiz "
"pēdējās C<'/'> veidnē tiek aizstātas ar nejaušām rakstzīmēm."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3866
msgid ""
"Notes: You should probably use an 8.3 path, so it's compatible with all "
"filesystems including basic FAT.  Also this only substitutes lowercase ASCII "
"letters and numbers, again for compatibility with lowest common denominator "
"filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Piezīmes: visticamāk, jāizmanto 8.3 ceļš, lai tas būtu saderīgs ar visām "
"failu sistēmām, ieskaitot pamata FAT.  Turklāt tas aizstāj tikai ar mazajiem "
"ASCII burtiem un cipariem, atkal saderībai ar vismazākā kopsaucēja failu "
"sistēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3871
msgid ""
"This doesn't create a file or check whether or not the file exists (it would "
"be extremely unlikely to exist as long as the RNG is working)."
msgstr ""
"Tas neizveido failu un nepārbauda, vai fails eksistē (ir ārkārtīgi maz "
"ticams, ka tas eksistētu, kamēr RNG darbojas)."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3875
msgid "If there is an error, C<-1> is returned."
msgstr "Kļūdas gadījumā tiek atgriezts C<-1>."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3877
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:udev_settle_file>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:udev_settle_file>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3879
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void\n"
" udev_settle_file (const char *file)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void\n"
" udev_settle_file (const char *file)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3882
msgid ""
"LVM and other commands aren't synchronous, especially when udev is "
"involved.  eg. You can create or remove some device, but the C</dev> device "
"node won't appear until some time later.  This means that you get an error "
"if you run one command followed by another."
msgstr ""
"LVM un citas komandas nav sinhronas, it īpaši, ja iesaistīts udev.  Piem., "
"var izveidot vai noņemt kādu ierīci, bet C</dev> ierīces mezgls parādīsies "
"tikai vēlāk.  Tas nozīmē, ka saņemat kļūdu, ja izpildāt vienu komandu, kam "
"seko cita."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3887
msgid ""
"Use C<udevadm settle> after certain commands, but don't be too fussed if it "
"fails."
msgstr ""
"Pēc dažām komandām izmantojiet C<udevadm settle>, bet neuztraucieties pārāk "
"daudz, ja tas neizdodas."

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3890
msgid "Function C<daemon/utils.c:make_exclude_from_file>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/utils.c:make_exclude_from_file>"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3892
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char *\n"
" make_exclude_from_file (const char *function, char *const *excludes)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char *\n"
" make_exclude_from_file (const char *function, char *const *excludes)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3895
msgid ""
"Turn list C<excludes> into a temporary file, and return a string containing "
"the temporary file name.  Caller must unlink the file and free the string."
msgstr ""
"Pārvērst sarakstu C<excludes> pagaidu failā un atgriezt virkni ar pagaidu "
"faila nosaukumu.  Izsaucējam jāatsaista fails un jāatbrīvo virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3899
msgid ""
"C<function> is the function that invoked this helper, and it is used mainly "
"for errors/debugging."
msgstr ""
"C<function> ir funkcija, kas izsauca šo palīgu, un to izmanto galvenokārt "
"kļūdām/atkļūdošanai."

#. type: =head3
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3902
msgid "File F<daemon/xattr.c>"
msgstr "Fails F<daemon/xattr.c>"

#. type: =head4
#: docs/internal-documentation.pod:3904
msgid "Function C<daemon/xattr.c:split_attr_names>"
msgstr "Funkcija C<daemon/xattr.c:split_attr_names>"

#. type: verbatim
