#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4381
msgid "inspect-get-drive-mappings"
msgstr "inspect-get-drive-mappings"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4383
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-drive-mappings root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-drive-mappings root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4385 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7076
msgid ""
"This call is useful for Windows which uses a primitive system of assigning "
"drive letters (like F<C:\\>) to partitions.  This inspection API examines "
"the Windows Registry to find out how disks/partitions are mapped to drive "
"letters, and returns a hash table as in the example below:"
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums noder Windows, kas nodalījumiem izmanto primitīvu disku burtu "
"(piemēram, F<C:\\>) piešķiršanas sistēmu.  Šī inspicēšanas API pārbauda "
"Windows reģistru, lai noskaidrotu, kā diski/nodalījumi tiek kartēti uz disku "
"burtiem, un atgriež jaucējtabulu kā tālāk dotajā piemērā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4391 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7082
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" C      =>     /dev/vda2\n"
" E      =>     /dev/vdb1\n"
" F      =>     /dev/vdc1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" C      =>     /dev/vda2\n"
" E      =>     /dev/vdb1\n"
" F      =>     /dev/vdc1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4395 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7086
msgid ""
"Note that keys are drive letters.  For Windows, the key is case insensitive "
"and just contains the drive letter, without the customary colon separator "
"character."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka atslēgas ir disku burti.  Windows gadījumā atslēga ir "
"reģistrnejutīga un satur tikai diska burtu, bez ierastās kola atdalītāja "
"rakstzīmes."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4399 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7090
msgid ""
"In future we may support other operating systems that also used drive "
"letters, but the keys for those might not be case insensitive and might be "
"longer than 1 character.  For example in OS-9, hard drives were named C<h0>, "
"C<h1> etc."
msgstr ""
"Nākotnē varam atbalstīt citas operētājsistēmas, kas arī izmantoja disku "
"burtus, taču to atslēgas var nebūt reģistrnejutīgas un var būt garākas par 1 "
"rakstzīmi.  Piemēram, OS-9 cietie diski tika nosaukti C<h0>, C<h1> u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4404 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7095
msgid ""
"For Windows guests, currently only hard drive mappings are returned.  "
"Removable disks (eg. DVD-ROMs) are ignored."
msgstr ""
"Windows viesiem pašlaik tiek atgriezti tikai cieto disku kartējumi.  "
"Noņemamie diski (piem., DVD-ROM) tiek ignorēti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4407 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7098
msgid ""
"For guests that do not use drive mappings, or if the drive mappings could "
"not be determined, this returns an empty hash table."
msgstr ""
"Viesiem, kas neizmanto disku kartējumus, vai ja disku kartējumus nevarēja "
"noteikt, tas atgriež tukšu jaucējtabulu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4410
msgid ""
"Please read L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION> for more details.  See also "
"L</inspect-get-mountpoints>, L</inspect-get-filesystems>."
msgstr ""
"Sīkāk lasiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>.  Skatīt arī L</inspect-get-"
"mountpoints>, L</inspect-get-filesystems>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4414
msgid "inspect-get-filesystems"
msgstr "inspect-get-filesystems"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4416
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-filesystems root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-filesystems root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4418 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7119
msgid ""
"This returns a list of all the filesystems that we think are associated with "
"this operating system.  This includes the root filesystem, other ordinary "
"filesystems, and non-mounted devices like swap partitions."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež visu failu sistēmu sarakstu, kas, mūsuprāt, ir saistītas ar šo "
"operētājsistēmu.  Tas ietver saknes failu sistēmu, citas parastas failu "
"sistēmas un nemontētas ierīces, piemēram, maiņatmiņas nodalījumus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4423 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7124
msgid ""
"In the case of a multi-boot virtual machine, it is possible for a filesystem "
"to be shared between operating systems."
msgstr ""
"Vairāksāknēšanas virtuālās mašīnas gadījumā failu sistēma var tikt "
"koplietota starp operētājsistēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4426
msgid ""
"Please read L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION> for more details.  See also "
"L</inspect-get-mountpoints>."
msgstr ""
"Sīkāku informāciju skatiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>.  Skatīt arī L</inspect-"
"get-mountpoints>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4429
msgid "inspect-get-format"
msgstr "inspect-get-format"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4431
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-format root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-format root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4433 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7150
msgid ""
"Before libguestfs 1.38, there was some unreliable support for detecting "
"installer CDs.  This API would return:"
msgstr ""
"Pirms libguestfs 1.38 bija daļēji neuzticams atbalsts instalētāju CD "
"noteikšanai.  Šī API atgrieza:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4438 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7155
msgid "C<installed>"
msgstr "C<installed>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4440 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7157
msgid "This is an installed operating system."
msgstr "Šī ir instalēta operētājsistēma."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4442 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7159
msgid "C<installer>"
msgstr "C<installer>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4444 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7161
msgid ""
"The disk image being inspected is not an installed operating system, but a "
"I<bootable> install disk, live CD, or similar."
msgstr ""
"Inspicētais diska attēls nav instalēta operētājsistēma, bet I<sāknējams> "
"instalēšanas disks, live CD vai līdzīgs."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4447 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7164
msgid "C<unknown>"
msgstr "C<unknown>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4449 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7166
msgid "The format of this disk image is not known."
msgstr "Šī diska attēla formāts nav zināms."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4453 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7170
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.38, this only returns C<installed>.  Use libosinfo "
"directly to detect installer CDs."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.38 tas atgriež tikai C<installed>.  Instalētāju CD "
"noteikšanai tieši izmantojiet libosinfo."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4466
msgid "inspect-get-hostname"
msgstr "inspect-get-hostname"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4468
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-hostname root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-hostname root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4470 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7186
msgid ""
"This function returns the hostname of the operating system as found by "
"inspection of the guest’s configuration files."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija atgriež operētājsistēmas resursdatora nosaukumu, kas atrasts, "
"inspicējot viesa konfigurācijas failus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4473 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7189
msgid ""
"If the hostname could not be determined, then the string C<unknown> is "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"Ja resursdatora nosaukumu nevarēja noteikt, tiek atgriezta virkne C<unknown>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4478
msgid "inspect-get-icon"
msgstr "inspect-get-icon"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4480
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-icon root [favicon:true|false] [highquality:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-icon root [favicon:true|false] [highquality:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4482 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7215
msgid ""
"This function returns an icon corresponding to the inspected operating "
"system.  The icon is returned as a buffer containing a PNG image (re-encoded "
"to PNG if necessary)."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija atgriež inspicētajai operētājsistēmai atbilstošu ikonu.  Ikona "
"tiek atgriezta kā buferis, kas satur PNG attēlu (ja nepieciešams, pārkodētu "
"uz PNG)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4486 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7219
msgid ""
"If it was not possible to get an icon this function returns a zero-length "
"(non-NULL) buffer.  I<Callers must check for this case>."
msgstr ""
"Ja ikonu iegūt nebija iespējams, šī funkcija atgriež nulles garuma (ne-NULL) "
"buferi.  I<Izsaucējiem jāpārbauda šis gadījums>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4489 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7222
msgid ""
"Libguestfs will start by looking for a file called F</etc/favicon.png> or "
"F<C:\\etc\\favicon.png> and if it has the correct format, the contents of "
"this file will be returned.  You can disable favicons by passing the "
"optional C<favicon> boolean as false (default is true)."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs sāks, meklējot failu F</etc/favicon.png> vai F<C:\\etc\\f"
"avicon.png>, un, ja tam ir pareizs formāts, tiks atgriezts šī faila saturs.  "
"Favicon var atspējot, nododot neobligāto Būla parametru C<favicon> kā false "
"(noklusējums ir true)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4495 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7228
msgid ""
"If finding the favicon fails, then we look in other places in the guest for "
"a suitable icon."
msgstr ""
"Ja favicon atrast neizdodas, meklējam piemērotu ikonu citās viesa vietās."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4498 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7231
msgid ""
"If the optional C<highquality> boolean is true then only high quality icons "
"are returned, which means only icons of high resolution with an alpha "
"channel.  The default (false) is to return any icon we can, even if it is of "
"substandard quality."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais Būla parametrs C<highquality> ir true, tiek atgrieztas tikai "
"augstas kvalitātes ikonas, kas nozīmē tikai augstas izšķirtspējas ikonas ar "
"alfa kanālu.  Noklusējums (false) ir atgriezt jebkuru ikonu, kādu varam, pat "
"ja tā ir zemas kvalitātes."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4509 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7242
msgid ""
"Unlike most other inspection API calls, the guest’s disks must be mounted up "
"before you call this, since it needs to read information from the guest "
"filesystem during the call."
msgstr ""
"Atšķirībā no lielākās daļas citu inspicēšanas API izsaukumu, pirms šī "
"izsaukšanas viesa diskiem jābūt montētiem, jo izsaukuma laikā tam jānolasa "
"informācija no viesa failu sistēmas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4515 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7248
msgid ""
"B<Security:> The icon data comes from the untrusted guest, and should be "
"treated with caution.  PNG files have been known to contain exploits.  "
"Ensure that libpng (or other relevant libraries) are fully up to date before "
"trying to process or display the icon."
msgstr ""
"B<Drošība:> ikonas dati nāk no neuzticama viesa, un ar tiem jāapietas "
"piesardzīgi.  Ir zināms, ka PNG faili satur ievainojamību izmantošanas "
"kodu.  Pirms mēģināt apstrādāt vai parādīt ikonu, pārliecinieties, ka libpng "
"(vai citas attiecīgās bibliotēkas) ir pilnībā atjauninātas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4523 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7256
msgid ""
"The PNG image returned can be any size.  It might not be square.  Libguestfs "
"tries to return the largest, highest quality icon available.  The "
"application must scale the icon to the required size."
msgstr ""
"Atgrieztais PNG attēls var būt jebkura izmēra.  Tas var nebūt kvadrātveida.  "
"Libguestfs mēģina atgriezt lielāko, augstākās kvalitātes pieejamo ikonu.  "
"Lietotnei ikona jāpielāgo vajadzīgajam izmēram."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4530 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7263
msgid ""
"Extracting icons from Windows guests requires the external L<wrestool(1)> "
"program from the C<icoutils> package, and several programs (L<bmptopnm(1)>, "
"L<pnmtopng(1)>, L<pamcut(1)>)  from the C<netpbm> package.  These must be "
"installed separately."
msgstr ""
"Ikonu izgūšanai no Windows viesiem nepieciešama ārējā programma L<wrestool"
"(1)> no pakotnes C<icoutils> un vairākas programmas (L<bmptopnm(1)>, "
"L<pnmtopng(1)>, L<pamcut(1)>) no pakotnes C<netpbm>.  Tās jāinstalē "
"atsevišķi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4537 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7270
msgid ""
"Operating system icons are usually trademarks.  Seek legal advice before "
"using trademarks in applications."
msgstr ""
"Operētājsistēmu ikonas parasti ir preču zīmes.  Pirms preču zīmju "
"izmantošanas lietotnēs konsultējieties ar juristu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4544
msgid "inspect-get-major-version"
msgstr "inspect-get-major-version"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4546
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-major-version root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-major-version root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4548 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7311
msgid "This returns the major version number of the inspected operating system."
msgstr "Tas atgriež inspicētās operētājsistēmas galveno versijas numuru."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4551 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7314
msgid ""
"Windows uses a consistent versioning scheme which is I<not> reflected in the "
"popular public names used by the operating system.  Notably the operating "
"system known as \"Windows 7\" is really version 6.1 (ie. major = 6, minor = "
"1).  You can find out the real versions corresponding to releases of Windows "
"by consulting Wikipedia or MSDN."
msgstr ""
"Windows izmanto konsekventu versiju shēmu, kas I<neatspoguļojas> "
"operētājsistēmas populārajos publiskajos nosaukumos.  Proti, "
"operētājsistēma, kas pazīstama kā „Windows 7”, patiesībā ir versija 6.1 (t. "
"i., major = 6, minor = 1).  Īstās Windows laidieniem atbilstošās versijas "
"varat uzzināt, skatot Wikipedia vai MSDN."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4558 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4569
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7321 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7338
msgid "If the version could not be determined, then C<0> is returned."
msgstr "Ja versiju nevarēja noteikt, tiek atgriezts C<0>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4562
msgid "inspect-get-minor-version"
msgstr "inspect-get-minor-version"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4564
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-minor-version root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-minor-version root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4566 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7335
msgid "This returns the minor version number of the inspected operating system."
msgstr "Tas atgriež inspicētās operētājsistēmas mazāko versijas numuru."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4571
msgid ""
"Please read L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION> for more details.  See also "
"L</inspect-get-major-version>."
msgstr ""
"Sīkāku informāciju skatiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>.  Skatīt arī L</inspect-"
"get-major-version>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4574
msgid "inspect-get-mountpoints"
msgstr "inspect-get-mountpoints"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4576
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-mountpoints root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-mountpoints root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4578 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7353
msgid ""
"This returns a hash of where we think the filesystems associated with this "
"operating system should be mounted.  Callers should note that this is at "
"best an educated guess made by reading configuration files such as "
"F</etc/fstab>.  I<In particular note> that this may return filesystems which "
"are non-existent or not mountable and callers should be prepared to handle "
"or ignore failures if they try to mount them."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež jaucējtabulu ar to, kur, mūsuprāt, jāmontē ar šo operētājsistēmu "
"saistītās failu sistēmas.  Izsaucējiem jāņem vērā, ka tas labākajā gadījumā "
"ir izglītots minējums, kas veikts, lasot konfigurācijas failus, piemēram, F</"
"etc/fstab>.  I<It īpaši ņemiet vērā>, ka tas var atgriezt failu sistēmas, "
"kas neeksistē vai nav montējamas, un izsaucējiem jābūt gataviem apstrādāt "
"vai ignorēt neveiksmes, ja tie mēģina tās montēt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4587 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7362
msgid ""
"Each element in the returned hashtable has a key which is the path of the "
"mountpoint (eg. F</boot>) and a value which is the filesystem that would be "
"mounted there (eg. F</dev/sda1>)."
msgstr ""
"Katram elementam atgrieztajā jaucējtabulā ir atslēga, kas ir montēšanas "
"punkta ceļš (piem., F</boot>), un vērtība, kas ir failu sistēma, kura tur "
"tiktu montēta (piem., F</dev/sda1>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4592 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7367
msgid "Non-mounted devices such as swap devices are I<not> returned in this list."
msgstr ""
"Nemontētas ierīces, piemēram, maiņatmiņas ierīces, šajā sarakstā I<netiek> "
"atgrieztas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4595
msgid ""
"For operating systems like Windows which still use drive letters, this call "
"will only return an entry for the first drive \"mounted on\" F</>.  For "
"information about the mapping of drive letters to partitions, see "
"L</inspect-get-drive-mappings>."
msgstr ""
"Tādām operētājsistēmām kā Windows, kas joprojām izmanto disku burtus, šis "
"izsaukums atgriezīs ierakstu tikai pirmajam diskam, kas „montēts” F</>.  "
"Informāciju par disku burtu kartēšanu uz nodalījumiem skatiet L</inspect-get-"
"drive-mappings>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4601
msgid ""
"Please read L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION> for more details.  See also "
"L</inspect-get-filesystems>."
msgstr ""
"Sīkāku informāciju skatiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>.  Skatīt arī L</inspect-"
"get-filesystems>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4604
msgid "inspect-get-osinfo"
msgstr "inspect-get-osinfo"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4606
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-osinfo root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-osinfo root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4608 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7393
msgid ""
"This function returns a possible short ID for libosinfo corresponding to the "
"guest."
msgstr "Šī funkcija atgriež iespējamo libosinfo īso ID, kas atbilst viesim."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4611 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7396
msgid ""
"I<Note:> The returned ID is only a guess by libguestfs, and nothing ensures "
"that it actually exists in osinfo-db."
msgstr ""
"I<Piezīme:> atgrieztais ID ir tikai libguestfs minējums, un nekas "
"nenodrošina, ka tas tiešām eksistē osinfo-db."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4614 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7399
msgid "If no ID could not be determined, then the string C<unknown> is returned."
msgstr "Ja ID nevarēja noteikt, tiek atgriezta virkne C<unknown>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4617
msgid "inspect-get-package-format"
msgstr "inspect-get-package-format"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4619
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-package-format root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-package-format root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4621
msgid ""
"This function and L</inspect-get-package-management> return the package "
"format and package management tool used by the inspected operating system.  "
"For example for Fedora these functions would return C<rpm> (package format), "
"and C<yum> or C<dnf> (package management)."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija un L</inspect-get-package-management> atgriež inspicētās "
"operētājsistēmas izmantoto pakotņu formātu un pakotņu pārvaldības rīku.  "
"Piemēram, Fedorā šīs funkcijas atgrieztu C<rpm> (pakotņu formāts) un C<yum> "
"vai C<dnf> (pakotņu pārvaldība)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4627 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7419
msgid ""
"This returns the string C<unknown> if we could not determine the package "
"format I<or> if the operating system does not have a real packaging system "
"(eg. Windows)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež virkni C<unknown>, ja nevarējām noteikt pakotņu formātu, I<vai> "
"ja operētājsistēmai nav īstas pakotņu sistēmas (piem., Windows)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4631 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7423
msgid ""
"Possible strings include: C<rpm>, C<deb>, C<ebuild>, C<pisi>, C<pacman>, "
"C<pkgsrc>, C<apk>, C<xbps>.  Future versions of libguestfs may return other "
"strings."
msgstr ""
"Iespējamās virknes ietver: C<rpm>, C<deb>, C<ebuild>, C<pisi>, C<pacman>, "
"C<pkgsrc>, C<apk>, C<xbps>.  Nākamās libguestfs versijas var atgriezt citas "
"virknes."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4638
msgid "inspect-get-package-management"
msgstr "inspect-get-package-management"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4640
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-package-management root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-package-management root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4642
msgid ""
"L</inspect-get-package-format> and this function return the package format "
"and package management tool used by the inspected operating system.  For "
"example for Fedora these functions would return C<rpm> (package format), and "
"C<yum> or C<dnf> (package management)."
msgstr ""
"L</inspect-get-package-format> un šī funkcija atgriež inspicētās "
"operētājsistēmas izmantoto pakotņu formātu un pakotņu pārvaldības rīku.  "
"Piemēram, Fedorā šīs funkcijas atgrieztu C<rpm> (pakotņu formāts) un C<yum> "
"vai C<dnf> (pakotņu pārvaldība)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4648 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7447
msgid ""
"This returns the string C<unknown> if we could not determine the package "
"management tool I<or> if the operating system does not have a real packaging "
"system (eg. Windows)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež virkni C<unknown>, ja nevarējām noteikt pakotņu pārvaldības "
"rīku, I<vai> ja operētājsistēmai nav īstas pakotņu sistēmas (piem., Windows)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4652 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7451
msgid ""
"Possible strings include: C<yum>, C<dnf>, C<up2date>, C<apt> (for all Debian "
"derivatives), C<portage>, C<pisi>, C<pacman>, C<urpmi>, C<zypper>, C<apk>, "
"C<xbps>.  Future versions of libguestfs may return other strings."
msgstr ""
"Iespējamās virknes ietver: C<yum>, C<dnf>, C<up2date>, C<apt> (visiem Debian "
"atvasinājumiem), C<portage>, C<pisi>, C<pacman>, C<urpmi>, C<zypper>, C<apk>"
", C<xbps>.  Nākamās libguestfs versijas var atgriezt citas virknes."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4659
msgid "inspect-get-product-name"
msgstr "inspect-get-product-name"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4661
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-product-name root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-product-name root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4663 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7469
msgid ""
"This returns the product name of the inspected operating system.  The "
"product name is generally some freeform string which can be displayed to the "
"user, but should not be parsed by programs."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež inspicētās operētājsistēmas produkta nosaukumu.  Produkta "
"nosaukums parasti ir kāda brīvas formas virkne, ko var parādīt lietotājam, "
"bet ko programmām nevajadzētu parsēt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4668 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7474
msgid ""
"If the product name could not be determined, then the string C<unknown> is "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"Ja produkta nosaukumu nevarēja noteikt, tiek atgriezta virkne C<unknown>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4673
msgid "inspect-get-product-variant"
msgstr "inspect-get-product-variant"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4675
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-product-variant root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-product-variant root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4677 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7490
msgid "This returns the product variant of the inspected operating system."
msgstr "Tas atgriež inspicētās operētājsistēmas produkta variantu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4680 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7493
msgid ""
"For Windows guests, this returns the contents of the Registry key "
"C<HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion> C<InstallationType> "
"which is usually a string such as C<Client> or C<Server> (other values are "
"possible).  This can be used to distinguish consumer and enterprise versions "
"of Windows that have the same version number (for example, Windows 7 and "
"Windows 2008 Server are both version 6.1, but the former is C<Client> and "
"the latter is C<Server>)."
msgstr ""
"Windows viesiem tas atgriež reģistra atslēgas C<HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\W"
"indows NT\\CurrentVersion> C<InstallationType> saturu, kas parasti ir tāda "
"virkne kā C<Client> vai C<Server> (iespējamas arī citas vērtības).  To var "
"izmantot, lai atšķirtu patērētāju un uzņēmumu Windows versijas ar vienādu "
"versijas numuru (piemēram, Windows 7 un Windows 2008 Server abas ir versija "
"6.1, bet pirmā ir C<Client>, otrā — C<Server>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4689 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7502
msgid ""
"For enterprise Linux guests, in future we intend this to return the product "
"variant such as C<Desktop>, C<Server> and so on.  But this is not "
"implemented at present."
msgstr ""
"Uzņēmumu Linux viesiem nākotnē plānojam, lai tas atgrieztu produkta "
"variantu, piemēram, C<Desktop>, C<Server> u. tml.  Taču pašlaik tas nav "
"realizēts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4693 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7506
msgid ""
"If the product variant could not be determined, then the string C<unknown> "
"is returned."
msgstr ""
"Ja produkta variantu nevarēja noteikt, tiek atgriezta virkne C<unknown>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4696
msgid ""
"Please read L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION> for more details.  See also "
"L</inspect-get-product-name>, L</inspect-get-major-version>."
msgstr ""
"Sīkāk lasiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>.  Skatīt arī L</inspect-get-product-"
"name>, L</inspect-get-major-version>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4700
msgid "inspect-get-roots"
msgstr "inspect-get-roots"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4702
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-roots\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-roots\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4704
msgid ""
"This function is a convenient way to get the list of root devices, as "
"returned from a previous call to L</inspect-os>, but without redoing the "
"whole inspection process."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija ir ērts veids, kā iegūt saknes ierīču sarakstu, kā to atgrieza "
"iepriekšējs L</inspect-os> izsaukums, bet neveicot visu inspicēšanas procesu "
"no jauna."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4708
msgid ""
"This returns an empty list if either no root devices were found or the "
"caller has not called L</inspect-os>."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež tukšu sarakstu, ja vai nu netika atrastas saknes ierīces, vai "
"izsaucējs nav izsaucis L</inspect-os>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4713
msgid "inspect-get-type"
msgstr "inspect-get-type"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4715
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-type root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-type root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4717 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7544
msgid ""
"This returns the type of the inspected operating system.  Currently defined "
"types are:"
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež inspicētās operētājsistēmas tipu.  Pašlaik definētie tipi ir:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4722 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7549
msgid "\"linux\""
msgstr "\"linux\""

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4724 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7551
msgid "Any Linux-based operating system."
msgstr "Jebkura uz Linux balstīta operētājsistēma."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4728 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7555
msgid "Any Microsoft Windows operating system."
msgstr "Jebkura Microsoft Windows operētājsistēma."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4742 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7569
msgid "\"hurd\""
msgstr "\"hurd\""

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4744 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7571
msgid "GNU/Hurd."
msgstr "GNU/Hurd."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4746 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7573
msgid "\"dos\""
msgstr "\"dos\""

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4748 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7575
msgid "MS-DOS, FreeDOS and others."
msgstr "MS-DOS, FreeDOS un citas."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4750 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7577
msgid "\"minix\""
msgstr "\"minix\""

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4752 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7579
msgid "MINIX."
msgstr "MINIX."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4756 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7583
msgid "The operating system type could not be determined."
msgstr "Operētājsistēmas tipu nevarēja noteikt."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4765
msgid "inspect-get-windows-current-control-set"
msgstr "inspect-get-windows-current-control-set"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4767
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-windows-current-control-set root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-windows-current-control-set root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4769 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7603
msgid ""
"This returns the Windows CurrentControlSet of the inspected guest.  The "
"CurrentControlSet is a registry key name such as C<ControlSet001>."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež inspicētā viesa Windows CurrentControlSet.  CurrentControlSet ir "
"reģistra atslēgas nosaukums, piemēram, C<ControlSet001>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4772 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4793
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7606 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7634
msgid ""
"This call assumes that the guest is Windows and that the Registry could be "
"examined by inspection.  If this is not the case then an error is returned."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums pieņem, ka viesis ir Windows un ka reģistru varēja pārbaudīt "
"inspicēšanas laikā.  Ja tā nav, tiek atgriezta kļūda."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4778
msgid "inspect-get-windows-group-policy"
msgstr "inspect-get-windows-group-policy"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4780
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-windows-group-policy root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-windows-group-policy root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4782 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7623
msgid ""
"This returns true if the Windows guest has group policy.  Group policy can "
"interfere with device driver installation, preventing libguestfs features "
"like driver injection from working."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež true, ja Windows viesim ir grupas politika.  Grupas politika var "
"traucēt ierīču draiveru instalēšanu, neļaujot darboties tādiem libguestfs "
"līdzekļiem kā draiveru ievietošana."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4787 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7628
msgid ""
"Note that the presence of group policy is only an indication that there may "
"be a problem with driver installation.  As group policy is extremely complex "
"and covers many different aspects of Windows configuration, and we make no "
"attempt to parse it, presence of group policy should only raise a warning."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka grupas politikas klātbūtne ir tikai norāde, ka ar draiveru "
"instalēšanu var būt problēma.  Tā kā grupas politika ir ārkārtīgi sarežģīta "
"un aptver daudzus dažādus Windows konfigurācijas aspektus, un mēs nemēģinām "
"to parsēt, grupas politikas klātbūtnei jārada tikai brīdinājums."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4799
msgid "inspect-get-windows-software-hive"
msgstr "inspect-get-windows-software-hive"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4801
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-windows-software-hive root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-windows-software-hive root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4803 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7650
msgid ""
"This returns the path to the hive (binary Windows Registry file)  "
"corresponding to HKLM\\SOFTWARE."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež ceļu uz stropu (bināru Windows reģistra failu), kas atbilst "
"HKLM\\SOFTWARE."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4806 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7653
msgid ""
"This call assumes that the guest is Windows and that the guest has a "
"software hive file with the right name.  If this is not the case then an "
"error is returned.  This call does not check that the hive is a valid "
"Windows Registry hive."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums pieņem, ka viesis ir Windows un ka viesim ir software stropa "
"fails ar pareizo nosaukumu.  Ja tā nav, tiek atgriezta kļūda.  Šis izsaukums "
"nepārbauda, vai strops ir derīgs Windows reģistra strops."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4811 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4827
msgid "You can use L</hivex-open> to read or write to the hive."
msgstr "Stropa lasīšanai vai rakstīšanai varat izmantot L</hivex-open>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4815
msgid "inspect-get-windows-system-hive"
msgstr "inspect-get-windows-system-hive"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4817
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-windows-system-hive root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-windows-system-hive root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4819 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7673
msgid ""
"This returns the path to the hive (binary Windows Registry file)  "
"corresponding to HKLM\\SYSTEM."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež ceļu uz stropu (bināru Windows reģistra failu), kas atbilst "
"HKLM\\SYSTEM."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4822 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7676
msgid ""
"This call assumes that the guest is Windows and that the guest has a system "
"hive file with the right name.  If this is not the case then an error is "
"returned.  This call does not check that the hive is a valid Windows "
"Registry hive."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums pieņem, ka viesis ir Windows un ka viesim ir system stropa "
"fails ar pareizo nosaukumu.  Ja tā nav, tiek atgriezta kļūda.  Šis izsaukums "
"nepārbauda, vai strops ir derīgs Windows reģistra strops."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4831
msgid "inspect-get-windows-systemroot"
msgstr "inspect-get-windows-systemroot"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4833
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-get-windows-systemroot root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-get-windows-systemroot root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4835 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7696
msgid ""
"This returns the Windows systemroot of the inspected guest.  The systemroot "
"is a directory path such as F</WINDOWS>."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež inspicētā viesa Windows systemroot.  Systemroot ir direktorijas "
"ceļš, piemēram, F</WINDOWS>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4838 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7699
msgid ""
"This call assumes that the guest is Windows and that the systemroot could be "
"determined by inspection.  If this is not the case then an error is "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums pieņem, ka viesis ir Windows un ka systemroot varēja noteikt "
"inspicēšanas laikā.  Ja tā nav, tiek atgriezta kļūda."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4844
msgid "inspect-is-live"
msgstr "inspect-is-live"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4846
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-is-live root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-is-live root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4848 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4864
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4880 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7724
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7746 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7768
msgid "This is deprecated and always returns C<false>."
msgstr "Tas ir novecojis un vienmēr atgriež C<false>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4860
msgid "inspect-is-multipart"
msgstr "inspect-is-multipart"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4862
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-is-multipart root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-is-multipart root\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4876
msgid "inspect-is-netinst"
msgstr "inspect-is-netinst"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4878
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-is-netinst root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-is-netinst root\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4892
msgid "inspect-list-applications"
msgstr "inspect-list-applications"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4894
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-list-applications root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-list-applications root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4896 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4999
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7789 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7893
msgid "Return the list of applications installed in the operating system."
msgstr "Atgriezt operētājsistēmā instalēto lietotņu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4898 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5001
msgid ""
"I<Note:> This call works differently from other parts of the inspection "
"API.  You have to call L</inspect-os>, then L</inspect-get-mountpoints>, "
"then mount up the disks, before calling this.  Listing applications is a "
"significantly more difficult operation which requires access to the full "
"filesystem.  Also note that unlike the other L</inspect-get-*> calls which "
"are just returning data cached in the libguestfs handle, this call actually "
"reads parts of the mounted filesystems during the call."
msgstr ""
"I<Piezīme:> šis izsaukums darbojas citādi nekā citas inspicēšanas API "
"daļas.  Pirms šī izsaukšanas jāizsauc L</inspect-os>, pēc tam L</inspect-get-"
"mountpoints> un jāmontē diski.  Lietotņu uzskaitīšana ir ievērojami "
"sarežģītāka darbība, kurai nepieciešama piekļuve visai failu sistēmai.  "
"Ņemiet vērā arī, ka atšķirībā no citiem L</inspect-get-*> izsaukumiem, kas "
"tikai atgriež libguestfs rokturī kešotus datus, šis izsaukums izsaukuma "
"laikā faktiski nolasa montēto failu sistēmu daļas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4908 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5011
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7801 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7905
msgid ""
"This returns an empty list if the inspection code was not able to determine "
"the list of applications."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež tukšu sarakstu, ja inspicēšanas kods nespēja noteikt lietotņu "
"sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4911 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5014
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7804 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7908
msgid "The application structure contains the following fields:"
msgstr "Lietotnes struktūra satur šādus laukus:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4915 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7808
msgid "C<app_name>"
msgstr "C<app_name>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4917 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5020
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7810 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7914
msgid "The name of the application.  For Linux guests, this is the package name."
msgstr "Lietotnes nosaukums.  Linux viesiem tas ir pakotnes nosaukums."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4920 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7813
msgid "C<app_display_name>"
msgstr "C<app_display_name>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4922 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5025
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7815 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7919
msgid ""
"The display name of the application, sometimes localized to the install "
"language of the guest operating system."
msgstr ""
"Lietotnes attēlojamais nosaukums, dažreiz lokalizēts viesa operētājsistēmas "
"instalēšanas valodā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4925 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7818
msgid ""
"If unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">.  Callers needing "
"to display something can use C<app_name> instead."
msgstr ""
"Ja nav pieejams, tas tiek atgriezts kā tukša virkne C<\"\">.  Izsaucēji, "
"kuriem kaut kas jāparāda, tā vietā var izmantot C<app_name>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4928 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7821
msgid "C<app_epoch>"
msgstr "C<app_epoch>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4930 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5033
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7823 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7927
msgid ""
"For package managers which use epochs, this contains the epoch of the "
"package (an integer).  If unavailable, this is returned as C<0>."
msgstr ""
"Pakotņu pārvaldniekiem, kas izmanto epohas, tas satur pakotnes epohu (veselu "
"skaitli).  Ja nav pieejams, tas tiek atgriezts kā C<0>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4933 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7826
msgid "C<app_version>"
msgstr "C<app_version>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4935 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5038
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7828 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7932
msgid ""
"The version string of the application or package.  If unavailable this is "
"returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Lietotnes vai pakotnes versijas virkne.  Ja nav pieejams, tiek atgriezta "
"tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4938 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7831
msgid "C<app_release>"
msgstr "C<app_release>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4940 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5043
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7833 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7937
msgid ""
"The release string of the application or package, for package managers that "
"use this.  If unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Lietotnes vai pakotnes laidiena virkne pakotņu pārvaldniekiem, kas to "
"izmanto.  Ja nav pieejams, tiek atgriezta tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4944 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7837
msgid "C<app_install_path>"
msgstr "C<app_install_path>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4946 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5055
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7839 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7949
msgid ""
"The installation path of the application (on operating systems such as "
"Windows which use installation paths).  This path is in the format used by "
"the guest operating system, it is not a libguestfs path."
msgstr ""
"Lietotnes instalēšanas ceļš (operētājsistēmās, kas izmanto instalēšanas "
"ceļus, piemēram, Windows).  Šis ceļš ir viesa operētājsistēmas izmantotajā "
"formātā, tas nav libguestfs ceļš."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4951 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5060
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7844 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7954
msgid "If unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr "Ja nav pieejams, tas tiek atgriezts kā tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4953 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7846
msgid "C<app_trans_path>"
msgstr "C<app_trans_path>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4955 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5064
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7848 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7958
msgid ""
"The install path translated into a libguestfs path.  If unavailable this is "
"returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Instalēšanas ceļš, pārveidots libguestfs ceļā.  Ja nav pieejams, tiek "
"atgriezta tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4958 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7851
msgid "C<app_publisher>"
msgstr "C<app_publisher>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4960 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5069
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7853 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7963
msgid ""
"The name of the publisher of the application, for package managers that use "
"this.  If unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Lietotnes izdevēja nosaukums pakotņu pārvaldniekiem, kas to izmanto.  Ja nav "
"pieejams, tiek atgriezta tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4964 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7857
msgid "C<app_url>"
msgstr "C<app_url>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4966 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5075
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7859 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7969
msgid ""
"The URL (eg. upstream URL) of the application.  If unavailable this is "
"returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Lietotnes URL (piem., augšteces URL).  Ja nav pieejams, tiek atgriezta tukša "
"virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4969 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7862
msgid "C<app_source_package>"
msgstr "C<app_source_package>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4971 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5080
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7864 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7974
msgid ""
"For packaging systems which support this, the name of the source package.  "
"If unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Pakotņu sistēmām, kas to atbalsta, — pirmkoda pakotnes nosaukums.  Ja nav "
"pieejams, tiek atgriezta tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4974 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7867
msgid "C<app_summary>"
msgstr "C<app_summary>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4976 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5085
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7869 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7979
msgid ""
"A short (usually one line) description of the application or package.  If "
"unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Īss (parasti vienas rindas) lietotnes vai pakotnes apraksts.  Ja nav "
"pieejams, tiek atgriezta tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4979 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7872
msgid "C<app_description>"
msgstr "C<app_description>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4981 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5090
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7874 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7984
msgid ""
"A longer description of the application or package.  If unavailable this is "
"returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Garāks lietotnes vai pakotnes apraksts.  Ja nav pieejams, tiek atgriezta "
"tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4988
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the "
"L</inspect-list-applications2> call instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"inspect-list-applications2>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4995
msgid "inspect-list-applications2"
msgstr "inspect-list-applications2"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:4997
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-list-applications2 root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-list-applications2 root\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5018 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7912
msgid "C<app2_name>"
msgstr "C<app2_name>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5023 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7917
msgid "C<app2_display_name>"
msgstr "C<app2_display_name>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5028 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7922
msgid ""
"If unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">.  Callers needing "
"to display something can use C<app2_name> instead."
msgstr ""
"Ja nav pieejams, tas tiek atgriezts kā tukša virkne C<\"\">.  Izsaucēji, "
"kuriem kaut kas jāparāda, tā vietā var izmantot C<app2_name>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5031 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7925
msgid "C<app2_epoch>"
msgstr "C<app2_epoch>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5036 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7930
msgid "C<app2_version>"
msgstr "C<app2_version>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5041 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7935
msgid "C<app2_release>"
msgstr "C<app2_release>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5047 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7941
msgid "C<app2_arch>"
msgstr "C<app2_arch>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5049 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7943
msgid ""
"The architecture string of the application or package, for package managers "
"that use this.  If unavailable this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Lietotnes vai pakotnes arhitektūras virkne pakotņu pārvaldniekiem, kas to "
"izmanto.  Ja nav pieejams, tiek atgriezta tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5053 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7947
msgid "C<app2_install_path>"
msgstr "C<app2_install_path>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5062 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7956
msgid "C<app2_trans_path>"
msgstr "C<app2_trans_path>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5067 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7961
msgid "C<app2_publisher>"
msgstr "C<app2_publisher>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5073 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7967
msgid "C<app2_url>"
msgstr "C<app2_url>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5078 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7972
msgid "C<app2_source_package>"
msgstr "C<app2_source_package>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5083 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7977
msgid "C<app2_summary>"
msgstr "C<app2_summary>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5088 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7982
msgid "C<app2_description>"
msgstr "C<app2_description>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5093 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7987
msgid "C<app2_class>"
msgstr "C<app2_class>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5095 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:7989
msgid ""
"Classification or primary use of this application.  Currently the only "
"defined classification is C<\"antivirus\"> for Windows antivirus software.  "
"If unknown this is returned as an empty string C<\"\">."
msgstr ""
"Šīs lietotnes klasifikācija vai galvenais lietojums.  Pašlaik vienīgā "
"definētā klasifikācija ir C<\"antivirus\"> Windows pretvīrusu "
"programmatūrai.  Ja nezināms, tas tiek atgriezts kā tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5104
msgid "inspect-os"
msgstr "inspect-os"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" inspect-os\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" inspect-os\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5108 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8009
msgid ""
"This function uses other libguestfs functions and certain heuristics to "
"inspect the disk(s) (usually disks belonging to a virtual machine), looking "
"for operating systems."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija izmanto citas libguestfs funkcijas un noteiktu heiristiku, lai "
"inspicētu disku(-s) (parasti diskus, kas pieder virtuālajai mašīnai), "
"meklējot operētājsistēmas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5112 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8013
msgid "The list returned is empty if no operating systems were found."
msgstr "Atgrieztais saraksts ir tukšs, ja netika atrastas operētājsistēmas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5114 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8015
msgid ""
"If one operating system was found, then this returns a list with a single "
"element, which is the name of the root filesystem of this operating system.  "
"It is also possible for this function to return a list containing more than "
"one element, indicating a dual-boot or multi-boot virtual machine, with each "
"element being the root filesystem of one of the operating systems."
msgstr ""
"Ja tika atrasta viena operētājsistēma, tas atgriež sarakstu ar vienu "
"elementu, kas ir šīs operētājsistēmas saknes failu sistēmas nosaukums.  Šī "
"funkcija var atgriezt arī sarakstu ar vairāk nekā vienu elementu, norādot "
"divsāknēšanas vai vairāksāknēšanas virtuālo mašīnu, kur katrs elements ir "
"vienas operētājsistēmas saknes failu sistēma."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5121
msgid ""
"You can pass the root string(s) returned to other L</inspect-get-*> "
"functions in order to query further information about each operating system, "
"such as the name and version."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezto(-ās) saknes virkni(-es) varat nodot citām L</inspect-get-*> "
"funkcijām, lai vaicātu papildu informāciju par katru operētājsistēmu, "
"piemēram, nosaukumu un versiju."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5126
msgid ""
"This function uses other libguestfs features such as L</mount-ro> and "
"L</umount-all> in order to mount and unmount filesystems and look at the "
"contents.  This should be called with no disks currently mounted.  The "
"function may also use Augeas, so any existing Augeas handle will be closed."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija izmanto citus libguestfs līdzekļus, piemēram, L</mount-ro> un L</"
"umount-all>, lai montētu un atmontētu failu sistēmas un apskatītu saturu.  "
"To jāizsauc, kad neviens disks nav montēts.  Funkcija var izmantot arī "
"Augeas, tāpēc jebkurš esošs Augeas rokturis tiks aizvērts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5132 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8033
msgid ""
"This function cannot decrypt encrypted disks.  The caller must do that first "
"(supplying the necessary keys) if the disk is encrypted."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija nevar atšifrēt šifrētus diskus.  Ja disks ir šifrēts, izsaucējam "
"tas vispirms jādara (nodrošinot nepieciešamās atslēgas)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5138 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5673
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5779
msgid "See also L</list-filesystems>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</list-filesystems>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5140
msgid "is-blockdev"
msgstr "is-blockdev"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5142
msgid "is-blockdev-opts"
msgstr "is-blockdev-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5144
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-blockdev path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-blockdev path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5146 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8074
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if there is a block device with the given "
"C<path> name."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja ir bloku ierīce ar doto nosaukumu "
"C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5149 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8077
msgid ""
"If the optional flag C<followsymlinks> is true, then a symlink (or chain of "
"symlinks) that ends with a block device also causes the function to return "
"true."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<followsymlinks> ir true, arī simboliskā saite (vai "
"simbolisko saišu ķēde), kas beidzas ar bloku ierīci, liek funkcijai atgriezt "
"true."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5153 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8081
msgid ""
"This call only looks at files within the guest filesystem.  Libguestfs "
"partitions and block devices (eg. F</dev/sda>) cannot be used as the C<path> "
"parameter of this call."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums aplūko tikai failus viesa failu sistēmā.  Libguestfs "
"nodalījumus un bloku ierīces (piem., F</dev/sda>) nevar izmantot kā šī "
"izsaukuma parametru C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5157 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5174
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5201 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5218
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5236 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5260
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5271
msgid "See also L</stat>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</stat>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5161
msgid "is-chardev"
msgstr "is-chardev"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5163
msgid "is-chardev-opts"
msgstr "is-chardev-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5165
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-chardev path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-chardev path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5167 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8154
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if there is a character device with the "
"given C<path> name."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja ir rakstzīmju ierīce ar doto "
"nosaukumu C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5170 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8157
msgid ""
"If the optional flag C<followsymlinks> is true, then a symlink (or chain of "
"symlinks) that ends with a chardev also causes the function to return true."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<followsymlinks> ir true, arī simboliskā saite (vai "
"simbolisko saišu ķēde), kas beidzas ar rakstzīmju ierīci, liek funkcijai "
"atgriezt true."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5178
msgid "is-config"
msgstr "is-config"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5180
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-config\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-config\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5182 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8194
msgid ""
"This returns true iff this handle is being configured (in the C<CONFIG> "
"state)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež true tad un tikai tad, ja šis rokturis tiek konfigurēts "
"(stāvoklī C<CONFIG>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5185 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:5809
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8121 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8197
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8399 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8426
msgid "For more information on states, see L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju par stāvokļiem skatiet L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5187
msgid "is-dir"
msgstr "is-dir"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5189
msgid "is-dir-opts"
msgstr "is-dir-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5191
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-dir path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-dir path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5193 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8230
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if there is a directory with the given "
"C<path> name.  Note that it returns false for other objects like files."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja ir direktorija ar doto nosaukumu "
"C<path>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka citiem objektiem, piemēram, failiem, tas atgriež "
"false."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5197 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8234
msgid ""
"If the optional flag C<followsymlinks> is true, then a symlink (or chain of "
"symlinks) that ends with a directory also causes the function to return "
"true."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<followsymlinks> ir true, arī simboliskā saite (vai "
"simbolisko saišu ķēde), kas beidzas ar direktoriju, liek funkcijai atgriezt "
"true."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5205
msgid "is-fifo"
msgstr "is-fifo"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5207
msgid "is-fifo-opts"
msgstr "is-fifo-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5209
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-fifo path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-fifo path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5211 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8293
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if there is a FIFO (named pipe)  with the "
"given C<path> name."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja ir FIFO (nosaukts kanāls) ar doto "
"nosaukumu C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5214 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8296
msgid ""
"If the optional flag C<followsymlinks> is true, then a symlink (or chain of "
"symlinks) that ends with a FIFO also causes the function to return true."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<followsymlinks> ir true, arī simboliskā saite (vai "
"simbolisko saišu ķēde), kas beidzas ar FIFO, liek funkcijai atgriezt true."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5222
msgid "is-file"
msgstr "is-file"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5224
msgid "is-file-opts"
msgstr "is-file-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5226
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-file path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-file path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5228 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8355
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if there is a regular file with the given "
"C<path> name.  Note that it returns false for other objects like "
"directories."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja ir parasts fails ar doto nosaukumu "
"C<path>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka citiem objektiem, piemēram, direktorijām, tas "
"atgriež false."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5232 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8359
msgid ""
"If the optional flag C<followsymlinks> is true, then a symlink (or chain of "
"symlinks) that ends with a file also causes the function to return true."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<followsymlinks> ir true, arī simboliskā saite (vai "
"simbolisko saišu ķēde), kas beidzas ar failu, liek funkcijai atgriezt true."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5240
msgid "is-lv"
msgstr "is-lv"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5242
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-lv mountable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-lv mountable\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5244 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8411
msgid ""
"This command tests whether C<mountable> is a logical volume, and returns "
"true iff this is the case."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda pārbauda, vai C<mountable> ir loģiskais sējums, un atgriež true "
"tad un tikai tad, ja tā ir."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5247
msgid "is-socket"
msgstr "is-socket"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5249
msgid "is-socket-opts"
msgstr "is-socket-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5251
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-socket path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-socket path [followsymlinks:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5253 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8459
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if there is a Unix domain socket with the "
"given C<path> name."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja ir Unix domēna ligzda ar doto "
"nosaukumu C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5256 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8462
msgid ""
"If the optional flag C<followsymlinks> is true, then a symlink (or chain of "
"symlinks) that ends with a socket also causes the function to return true."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<followsymlinks> ir true, arī simboliskā saite (vai "
"simbolisko saišu ķēde), kas beidzas ar ligzdu, liek funkcijai atgriezt true."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5264
msgid "is-symlink"
msgstr "is-symlink"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5266
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-symlink path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-symlink path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5268 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8500
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if there is a symbolic link with the given "
"C<path> name."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja ir simboliskā saite ar doto "
"nosaukumu C<path>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5273
msgid "is-whole-device"
msgstr "is-whole-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5275
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-whole-device device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-whole-device device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5277 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8515
msgid ""
"This returns C<true> if and only if C<device> refers to a whole block "
"device. That is, not a partition or a logical device."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež C<true> tad un tikai tad, ja C<device> norāda uz visu bloku "
"ierīci. T. i., nevis nodalījumu vai loģisku ierīci."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5280
msgid "is-zero"
msgstr "is-zero"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5282
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-zero path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-zero path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5284 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8528
msgid ""
"This returns true iff the file exists and the file is empty or it contains "
"all zero bytes."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež true tad un tikai tad, ja fails eksistē un ir tukšs vai satur "
"tikai nulles baitus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5287
msgid "is-zero-device"
msgstr "is-zero-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5289
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" is-zero-device device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" is-zero-device device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5291 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8541
msgid "This returns true iff the device exists and contains all zero bytes."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež true tad un tikai tad, ja ierīce eksistē un satur tikai nulles "
"baitus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5293 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8543
msgid "Note that for large devices this can take a long time to run."
msgstr "Ņemiet vērā, ka lielām ierīcēm tas var aizņemt ilgu laiku."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5295
msgid "isoinfo"
msgstr "isoinfo"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5297
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" isoinfo isofile\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" isoinfo isofile\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5299
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</isoinfo-device> except that it works for an ISO file "
"located inside some other mounted filesystem.  Note that in the common case "
"where you have added an ISO file as a libguestfs device, you would I<not> "
"call this.  Instead you would call L</isoinfo-device>."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</isoinfo-device>, izņemot to, ka tas darbojas ar ISO "
"failu, kas atrodas kādā citā montētā failu sistēmā.  Ņemiet vērā, ka "
"parastajā gadījumā, kad ISO fails pievienots kā libguestfs ierīce, šo "
"I<neizsauktu>.  Tā vietā izsauktu L</isoinfo-device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5305
msgid "isoinfo-device"
msgstr "isoinfo-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5307
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" isoinfo-device device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" isoinfo-device device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5309 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8573
msgid ""
"C<device> is an ISO device.  This returns a struct of information read from "
"the primary volume descriptor (the ISO equivalent of the superblock) of the "
"device."
msgstr ""
"C<device> ir ISO ierīce.  Tas atgriež informācijas struktūru, kas nolasīta "
"no ierīces primārā sējuma deskriptora (ISO superbloka ekvivalenta)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5313 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8577
msgid ""
"Usually it is more efficient to use the L<isoinfo(1)> command with the I<-d> "
"option on the host to analyze ISO files, instead of going through "
"libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Parasti ISO failu analīzei efektīvāk ir izmantot komandu L<isoinfo(1)> ar "
"opciju I<-d> resursdatorā, nevis izmantot libguestfs."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5317 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8581
msgid ""
"For information on the primary volume descriptor fields, see "
"L<https://wiki.osdev.org/ISO_9660#The_Primary_Volume_Descriptor>"
msgstr ""
"Informāciju par primārā sējuma deskriptora laukiem skatiet L<https://"
"wiki.osdev.org/ISO_9660#The_Primary_Volume_Descriptor>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5320
msgid "journal-close"
msgstr "journal-close"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5322
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-close\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-close\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5324 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8595
msgid "Close the journal handle."
msgstr "Aizvērt žurnāla rokturi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5326 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5349
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5363 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5372
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5388 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5404
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5418 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5433
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<journal>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<journal>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5329
msgid "journal-get"
msgstr "journal-get"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5331
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-get\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-get\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5333 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8609
msgid ""
"Read the current journal entry.  This returns all the fields in the journal "
"as a set of C<(attrname, attrval)> pairs.  The C<attrname> is the field name "
"(a string)."
msgstr ""
"Nolasīt pašreizējo žurnāla ierakstu.  Tas atgriež visus žurnāla laukus kā "
"pāru C<(attrname, attrval)> kopu.  C<attrname> ir lauka nosaukums (virkne)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5337 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8613
msgid ""
"The C<attrval> is the field value (a binary blob, often but not always a "
"string).  Please note that C<attrval> is a byte array, I<not> a "
"\\0-terminated C string."
msgstr ""
"C<attrval> ir lauka vērtība (binārs bloks, bieži, bet ne vienmēr virkne).  "
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka C<attrval> ir baitu masīvs, I<nevis> ar \\0 noslēgta "
"C virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5341
msgid ""
"The length of data may be truncated to the data threshold (see: "
"L</journal-set-data-threshold>, L</journal-get-data-threshold>)."
msgstr ""
"Datu garums var tikt saīsināts līdz datu slieksnim (skatiet: L</journal-set-"
"data-threshold>, L</journal-get-data-threshold>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5345 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8621
msgid ""
"If you set the data threshold to unlimited (C<0>) then this call can read a "
"journal entry of any size, ie. it is not limited by the libguestfs protocol."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatāt datu slieksni uz neierobežotu (C<0>), šis izsaukums var nolasīt "
"jebkura izmēra žurnāla ierakstu, t. i., to neierobežo libguestfs protokols."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5352
msgid "journal-get-data-threshold"
msgstr "journal-get-data-threshold"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5354
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-get-data-threshold\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-get-data-threshold\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5356 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8639
msgid ""
"Get the current data threshold for reading journal entries.  This is a hint "
"to the journal that it may truncate data fields to this size when reading "
"them (note also that it may not truncate them).  If this returns C<0>, then "
"the threshold is unlimited."
msgstr ""
"Iegūt pašreizējo datu slieksni žurnāla ierakstu lasīšanai.  Tas ir mājiens "
"žurnālam, ka, lasot datu laukus, tas var tos saīsināt līdz šim izmēram "
"(ņemiet vērā arī, ka tas var tos nesaīsināt).  Ja tas atgriež C<0>, "
"slieksnis ir neierobežots."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5361
msgid "See also L</journal-set-data-threshold>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</journal-set-data-threshold>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5366
msgid "journal-get-realtime-usec"
msgstr "journal-get-realtime-usec"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5368
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-get-realtime-usec\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-get-realtime-usec\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5370 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8658
msgid "Get the realtime (wallclock) timestamp of the current journal entry."
msgstr ""
"Iegūt pašreizējā žurnāla ieraksta reāllaika (sienas pulksteņa) laikspiedolu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5375
msgid "journal-next"
msgstr "journal-next"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5377
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-next\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-next\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5379 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8672
msgid ""
"Move to the next journal entry.  You have to call this at least once after "
"opening the handle before you are able to read data."
msgstr ""
"Pāriet uz nākamo žurnāla ierakstu.  Pēc roktura atvēršanas tas jāizsauc "
"vismaz vienreiz, pirms varat lasīt datus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5383
msgid ""
"The returned boolean tells you if there are any more journal records to "
"read.  C<true> means you can read the next record (eg. using "
"L</journal-get>), and C<false> means you have reached the end of the "
"journal."
msgstr ""
"Atgrieztā Būla vērtība norāda, vai ir vēl žurnāla ieraksti lasīšanai.  "
"C<true> nozīmē, ka varat nolasīt nākamo ierakstu (piem., ar L</journal-get>)"
", un C<false> nozīmē, ka sasniegtas žurnāla beigas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5391
msgid "journal-open"
msgstr "journal-open"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5393
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-open directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-open directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5395 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8694
msgid ""
"Open the systemd journal located in F<directory>.  Any previously opened "
"journal handle is closed."
msgstr ""
"Atvērt systemd žurnālu, kas atrodas F<directory>.  Jebkurš iepriekš atvērts "
"žurnāla rokturis tiek aizvērts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5398
msgid ""
"The contents of the journal can be read using L</journal-next> and "
"L</journal-get>."
msgstr ""
"Žurnāla saturu var nolasīt, izmantojot L</journal-next> un L</journal-get>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5401
msgid ""
"After you have finished using the journal, you should close the handle by "
"calling L</journal-close>."
msgstr ""
"Pēc žurnāla izmantošanas, rokturis jāaizver, izsaucot L</journal-close>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5407
msgid "journal-set-data-threshold"
msgstr "journal-set-data-threshold"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5409
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-set-data-threshold threshold\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-set-data-threshold threshold\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5411 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8716
msgid ""
"Set the data threshold for reading journal entries.  This is a hint to the "
"journal that it may truncate data fields to this size when reading them "
"(note also that it may not truncate them).  If you set this to C<0>, then "
"the threshold is unlimited."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt datu slieksni žurnāla ierakstu lasīšanai.  Tas ir mājiens žurnālam, "
"ka, lasot datu laukus, tas var tos saīsināt līdz šim izmēram (ņemiet vērā "
"arī, ka tas var tos nesaīsināt).  Ja iestatāt to uz C<0>, slieksnis ir "
"neierobežots."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5416
msgid "See also L</journal-get-data-threshold>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</journal-get-data-threshold>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5421
msgid "journal-skip"
msgstr "journal-skip"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5423
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" journal-skip skip\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" journal-skip skip\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5425 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8736
msgid ""
"Skip forwards (C<skip E<ge> 0>) or backwards (C<skip E<lt> 0>) in the "
"journal."
msgstr ""
"Pārlēkt uz priekšu (C<skip E<ge> 0>) vai atpakaļ (C<skip E<lt> 0>) žurnālā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5428 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8739
msgid ""
"The number of entries actually skipped is returned (note S<C<rskip E<ge> "
"0>>).  If this is not the same as the absolute value of the skip parameter "
"(C<|skip|>) you passed in then it means you have reached the end or the "
"start of the journal."
msgstr ""
"Tiek atgriezts faktiski izlaisto ierakstu skaits (piezīme: S<C<rskip E<ge> "
"0>>).  Ja tas nav tāds pats kā nodotā izlaišanas parametra absolūtā vērtība "
"(C<|skip|>), tas nozīmē, ka sasniegtas žurnāla beigas vai sākums."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5436
msgid "kill-procs"
msgstr "kill-procs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5438
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" kill-procs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" kill-procs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5440 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8756
msgid ""
"This call kills any processes inside the libguestfs appliance that are using "
"the guest filesystem (ie. have the sysroot as their root)."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums nobeidz visus procesus libguestfs palīgsistēmā, kas izmanto "
"viesa failu sistēmu (t. i., kuriem sakne ir sysroot)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5444 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8760
msgid ""
"This is a best-effort call: it will silently succeed even if no processes "
"are found or if the kill attempt fails."
msgstr ""
"Šis ir izsaukums pēc labākās iespējas: tas klusi izdosies pat tad, ja "
"procesi netiek atrasti vai ja nobeigšanas mēģinājums neizdodas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5447
msgid ""
"This is called after customization operations like L</install> to clean up "
"any daemons that may have been started by package installation scripts."
msgstr ""
"To izsauc pēc tādām pielāgošanas darbībām kā L</install>, lai sakoptu visus "
"dēmonus, ko, iespējams, palaiduši pakotņu instalēšanas skripti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5451
msgid "kill-subprocess"
msgstr "kill-subprocess"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5453
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" kill-subprocess\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" kill-subprocess\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5455 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8783
msgid "This kills the hypervisor."
msgstr "Tas nobeidz hipervizoru."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5457
msgid "Do not call this.  See: L</shutdown> instead."
msgstr "Neizsauciet šo.  Tā vietā skatiet: L</shutdown>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5459
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</shutdown> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"shutdown>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5466
msgid "launch"
msgstr "launch"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5468
msgid "run"
msgstr "run"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5470
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" launch\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" launch\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5472 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8796
msgid ""
"You should call this after configuring the handle (eg. adding drives) but "
"before performing any actions."
msgstr ""
"To jāizsauc pēc roktura konfigurēšanas (piem., disku pievienošanas), bet "
"pirms jebkuru darbību veikšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5475
msgid ""
"Do not call L</launch> twice on the same handle.  Although it will not give "
"an error (for historical reasons), the precise behaviour when you do this is "
"not well defined.  Handles are very cheap to create, so create a new one for "
"each launch."
msgstr ""
"Neizsauciet L</launch> divreiz vienam rokturim.  Lai gan tas (vēsturisku "
"iemeslu dēļ) nedos kļūdu, precīzā uzvedība šādā gadījumā nav labi definēta.  "
"Rokturus ir ļoti lēti izveidot, tāpēc katrai palaišanai izveidojiet jaunu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5480
msgid "lchown"
msgstr "lchown"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5482
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lchown owner group path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lchown owner group path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5484
msgid ""
"Change the file owner to C<owner> and group to C<group>.  This is like "
"L</chown> but if C<path> is a symlink then the link itself is changed, not "
"the target."
msgstr ""
"Mainīt faila īpašnieku uz C<owner> un grupu uz C<group>.  Tas ir līdzīgi L</"
"chown>, bet, ja C<path> ir simboliskā saite, tiek mainīta pati saite, nevis "
"mērķis."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5492
msgid "ldmtool-create-all"
msgstr "ldmtool-create-all"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-create-all\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-create-all\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5496 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8838
msgid ""
"This function scans all block devices looking for Windows dynamic disk "
"volumes and partitions, and creates devices for any that were found."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija skenē visas bloku ierīces, meklējot Windows dinamisko disku "
"sējumus un nodalījumus, un izveido ierīces visiem atrastajiem."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5500
msgid "Call L</list-ldm-volumes> and L</list-ldm-partitions> to return all devices."
msgstr ""
"Lai atgrieztu visas ierīces, izsauciet L</list-ldm-volumes> un L</list-ldm-"
"partitions>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5503
msgid ""
"Note that you B<don't> normally need to call this explicitly, since it is "
"done automatically at L</launch> time."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka parasti šis B<nav> jāizsauc eksplicīti, jo tas tiek darīts "
"automātiski L</launch> laikā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5506 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5517
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5528 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5539
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5550 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5564
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5578 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5590
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5600 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5614
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5748 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5759
msgid "This command depends on the feature C<ldm>.  See also L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<ldm>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5509
msgid "ldmtool-diskgroup-disks"
msgstr "ldmtool-diskgroup-disks"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5511
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-diskgroup-disks diskgroup\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-diskgroup-disks diskgroup\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5513
msgid ""
"Return the disks in a Windows dynamic disk group.  The C<diskgroup> "
"parameter should be the GUID of a disk group, one element from the list "
"returned by L</ldmtool-scan>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt diskus Windows dinamisko disku grupā.  Parametram C<diskgroup> "
"jābūt disku grupas GUID, vienam elementam no saraksta, ko atgriež L</ldmtool-"
"scan>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5520
msgid "ldmtool-diskgroup-name"
msgstr "ldmtool-diskgroup-name"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5522
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-diskgroup-name diskgroup\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-diskgroup-name diskgroup\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5524
msgid ""
"Return the name of a Windows dynamic disk group.  The C<diskgroup> parameter "
"should be the GUID of a disk group, one element from the list returned by "
"L</ldmtool-scan>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt Windows dinamisko disku grupas nosaukumu.  Parametram C<diskgroup> "
"jābūt disku grupas GUID, vienam elementam no saraksta, ko atgriež L</ldmtool-"
"scan>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5531
msgid "ldmtool-diskgroup-volumes"
msgstr "ldmtool-diskgroup-volumes"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5533
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-diskgroup-volumes diskgroup\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-diskgroup-volumes diskgroup\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5535
msgid ""
"Return the volumes in a Windows dynamic disk group.  The C<diskgroup> "
"parameter should be the GUID of a disk group, one element from the list "
"returned by L</ldmtool-scan>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt sējumus Windows dinamisko disku grupā.  Parametram C<diskgroup> "
"jābūt disku grupas GUID, vienam elementam no saraksta, ko atgriež L</ldmtool-"
"scan>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5542
msgid "ldmtool-remove-all"
msgstr "ldmtool-remove-all"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5544
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-remove-all\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-remove-all\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5546
msgid ""
"This is essentially the opposite of L</ldmtool-create-all>.  It removes the "
"device mapper mappings for all Windows dynamic disk volumes"
msgstr ""
"Tas būtībā ir pretējs L</ldmtool-create-all>.  Tas noņem device mapper "
"kartējumus visiem Windows dinamisko disku sējumiem"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5553
msgid "ldmtool-scan"
msgstr "ldmtool-scan"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5555
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-scan\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-scan\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5557 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5571
msgid ""
"This function scans for Windows dynamic disks.  It returns a list of "
"identifiers (GUIDs) for all disk groups that were found.  These identifiers "
"can be passed to other L</ldmtool-*> functions."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija meklē Windows dinamiskos diskus.  Tā atgriež visu atrasto disku "
"grupu identifikatoru (GUID) sarakstu.  Šos identifikatorus var nodot citām "
"L</ldmtool-*> funkcijām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5561
msgid ""
"This function scans all block devices.  To scan a subset of block devices, "
"call L</ldmtool-scan-devices> instead."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija skenē visas bloku ierīces.  Lai skenētu bloku ierīču apakškopu, "
"tā vietā izsauciet L</ldmtool-scan-devices>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5567
msgid "ldmtool-scan-devices"
msgstr "ldmtool-scan-devices"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5569
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-scan-devices 'devices ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-scan-devices 'devices ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5575 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8958
msgid ""
"The parameter C<devices> is a list of block devices which are scanned.  If "
"this list is empty, all block devices are scanned."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<devices> ir skenējamo bloku ierīču saraksts.  Ja šis saraksts ir "
"tukšs, tiek skenētas visas bloku ierīces."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5581
msgid "ldmtool-volume-hint"
msgstr "ldmtool-volume-hint"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5583
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-volume-hint diskgroup volume\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-volume-hint diskgroup volume\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5585 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8977
msgid ""
"Return the hint field of the volume named C<volume> in the disk group with "
"GUID C<diskgroup>.  This may not be defined, in which case the empty string "
"is returned.  The hint field is often, though not always, the name of a "
"Windows drive, eg. C<E:>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt sējuma C<volume> mājiena lauku disku grupā ar GUID C<diskgroup>.  "
"Tas var nebūt definēts, tādā gadījumā tiek atgriezta tukša virkne.  Mājiena "
"lauks bieži, lai gan ne vienmēr, ir Windows diska nosaukums, piem., C<E:>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5593
msgid "ldmtool-volume-partitions"
msgstr "ldmtool-volume-partitions"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5595
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-volume-partitions diskgroup volume\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-volume-partitions diskgroup volume\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5597 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:8997
msgid ""
"Return the list of partitions in the volume named C<volume> in the disk "
"group with GUID C<diskgroup>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt sējuma C<volume> nodalījumu sarakstu disku grupā ar GUID "
"C<diskgroup>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5603
msgid "ldmtool-volume-type"
msgstr "ldmtool-volume-type"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5605
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ldmtool-volume-type diskgroup volume\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ldmtool-volume-type diskgroup volume\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5607 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9016
msgid ""
"Return the type of the volume named C<volume> in the disk group with GUID "
"C<diskgroup>."
msgstr "Atgriezt sējuma C<volume> tipu disku grupā ar GUID C<diskgroup>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5610 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9019
msgid ""
"Possible volume types that can be returned here include: C<simple>, "
"C<spanned>, C<striped>, C<mirrored>, C<raid5>.  Other types may also be "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"Iespējamie sējumu tipi, ko var atgriezt, ietver: C<simple>, C<spanned>, "
"C<striped>, C<mirrored>, C<raid5>.  Var tikt atgriezti arī citi tipi."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5617
msgid "lgetxattr"
msgstr "lgetxattr"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5619
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lgetxattr path name\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lgetxattr path name\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5621 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9039
msgid ""
"Get a single extended attribute from file C<path> named C<name>.  If C<path> "
"is a symlink, then this call returns an extended attribute from the symlink."
msgstr ""
"Iegūt vienu paplašināto atribūtu C<name> no faila C<path>.  Ja C<path> ir "
"simboliskā saite, šis izsaukums atgriež simboliskās saites paplašināto "
"atribūtu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5635
msgid "See also: L</lgetxattrs>, L</getxattr>, L<attr(5)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</lgetxattrs>, L</getxattr>, L<attr(5)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5640
msgid "lgetxattrs"
msgstr "lgetxattrs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5642
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lgetxattrs path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lgetxattrs path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5644
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</getxattrs>, but if C<path> is a symbolic link, then "
"it returns the extended attributes of the link itself."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</getxattrs>, bet, ja C<path> ir simboliskā saite, tas "
"atgriež pašas saites paplašinātos atribūtus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5651
msgid "list-9p"
msgstr "list-9p"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5653
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-9p\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-9p\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5655 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7001
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8023 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9096
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11310 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13057
msgid "This call does nothing and returns an error."
msgstr "Šis izsaukums neko nedara un atgriež kļūdu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5665
msgid "list-devices"
msgstr "list-devices"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5667
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-devices\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-devices\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5669 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9109
msgid "List all the block devices."
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas bloku ierīces."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5671 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9111
msgid "The full block device names are returned, eg. F</dev/sda>."
msgstr "Tiek atgriezti pilni bloku ierīču nosaukumi, piem., F</dev/sda>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5675
msgid "list-disk-labels"
msgstr "list-disk-labels"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5677
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-disk-labels\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-disk-labels\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5679
msgid ""
"If you add drives using the optional C<label> parameter of "
"L</add-drive-opts>, you can use this call to map between disk labels, and "
"raw block device and partition names (like F</dev/sda> and F</dev/sda1>)."
msgstr ""
"Ja pievienojat diskus, izmantojot L</add-drive-opts> neobligāto parametru "
"C<label>, ar šo izsaukumu var kartēt starp disku etiķetēm un neapstrādātiem "
"bloku ierīču un nodalījumu nosaukumiem (piemēram, F</dev/sda> un F</dev/"
"sda1>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5684 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9131
msgid ""
"This returns a hashtable, where keys are the disk labels (I<without> the "
"F</dev/disk/guestfs> prefix), and the values are the full raw block device "
"and partition names (eg. F</dev/sda> and F</dev/sda1>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež jaucējtabulu, kur atslēgas ir disku etiķetes (I<bez> priedēkļa "
"F</dev/disk/guestfs>), un vērtības ir pilni neapstrādātie bloku ierīču un "
"nodalījumu nosaukumi (piem., F</dev/sda> un F</dev/sda1>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5689
msgid "list-dm-devices"
msgstr "list-dm-devices"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5691
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-dm-devices\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-dm-devices\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5693 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9149
msgid "List all device mapper devices."
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas device mapper ierīces."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5695
msgid ""
"The returned list contains F</dev/mapper/*> devices, eg. ones created by a "
"previous call to L</luks-open>."
msgstr ""
"Atgrieztais saraksts satur F</dev/mapper/*> ierīces, piem., tās, kas "
"izveidotas ar iepriekšēju L</luks-open> izsaukumu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5698
msgid ""
"Device mapper devices which correspond to logical volumes are I<not> "
"returned in this list.  Call L</lvs> if you want to list logical volumes."
msgstr ""
"Device mapper ierīces, kas atbilst loģiskajiem sējumiem, šajā sarakstā "
"I<netiek> atgrieztas.  Ja vēlaties uzskaitīt loģiskos sējumus, izsauciet L</"
"lvs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5702
msgid "list-filesystems"
msgstr "list-filesystems"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5704
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-filesystems\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-filesystems\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5706 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9169
msgid ""
"This inspection command looks for filesystems on partitions, block devices "
"and logical volumes, returning a list of C<mountables> containing "
"filesystems and their type."
msgstr ""
"Šī inspicēšanas komanda meklē failu sistēmas nodalījumos, bloku ierīcēs un "
"loģiskajos sējumos, atgriežot C<mountables> sarakstu, kas satur failu "
"sistēmas un to tipu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5710 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9173
msgid ""
"The return value is a hash, where the keys are the devices containing "
"filesystems, and the values are the filesystem types.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Atgriešanas vērtība ir jaucējtabula, kur atslēgas ir ierīces, kas satur "
"failu sistēmas, un vērtības ir failu sistēmu tipi.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5714 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" \"/dev/sda1\" => \"ntfs\"\n"
" \"/dev/sda2\" => \"ext2\"\n"
" \"/dev/vg_guest/lv_root\" => \"ext4\"\n"
" \"/dev/vg_guest/lv_swap\" => \"swap\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" \"/dev/sda1\" => \"ntfs\"\n"
" \"/dev/sda2\" => \"ext2\"\n"
" \"/dev/vg_guest/lv_root\" => \"ext4\"\n"
" \"/dev/vg_guest/lv_swap\" => \"swap\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5719
msgid ""
"The key is not necessarily a block device. It may also be an opaque "
"‘mountable’ string which can be passed to L</mount>."
msgstr ""
"Atslēga ne vienmēr ir bloku ierīce. Tā var būt arī necaurredzama ‘montējamā "
"objekta’ virkne, ko var nodot L</mount>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5722 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9185
msgid ""
"The value can have the special value \"unknown\", meaning the content of the "
"device is undetermined or empty.  \"swap\" means a Linux swap partition."
msgstr ""
"Vērtībai var būt īpašā vērtība „unknown”, kas nozīmē, ka ierīces saturs nav "
"noteikts vai ir tukšs.  „swap” nozīmē Linux maiņatmiņas nodalījumu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5726
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<le> 1.36 this command ran other libguestfs commands, which "
"might have included L</mount> and L</umount>, and therefore you had to use "
"this soon after launch and only when nothing else was mounted.  This "
"restriction is removed in libguestfs E<ge> 1.38."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<le> 1.36 šī komanda izpildīja citas libguestfs komandas, kas, "
"iespējams, ietvēra L</mount> un L</umount>, un tāpēc to bija jāizmanto drīz "
"pēc palaišanas un tikai tad, kad nekas cits nebija montēts.  Libguestfs "
"E<ge> 1.38 šis ierobežojums ir noņemts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5732
msgid ""
"Not all of the filesystems returned will be mountable.  In particular, swap "
"partitions are returned in the list.  Also this command does not check that "
"each filesystem found is valid and mountable, and some filesystems might be "
"mountable but require special options.  Filesystems may not all belong to a "
"single logical operating system (use L</inspect-os> to look for OSes)."
msgstr ""
"Ne visas atgrieztās failu sistēmas būs montējamas.  It īpaši sarakstā tiek "
"atgriezti maiņatmiņas nodalījumi.  Turklāt šī komanda nepārbauda, vai katra "
"atrastā failu sistēma ir derīga un montējama, un dažas failu sistēmas var "
"būt montējamas, bet prasīt īpašas opcijas.  Failu sistēmas var nepiederēt "
"vienai loģiskai operētājsistēmai (OS meklēšanai izmantojiet L</inspect-os>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5740
msgid "list-ldm-partitions"
msgstr "list-ldm-partitions"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5742
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-ldm-partitions\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-ldm-partitions\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5744 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9216
msgid ""
"This function returns all Windows dynamic disk partitions that were found at "
"launch time.  It returns a list of device names."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija atgriež visus Windows dinamisko disku nodalījumus, kas tika "
"atrasti palaišanas laikā.  Tā atgriež ierīču nosaukumu sarakstu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5751
msgid "list-ldm-volumes"
msgstr "list-ldm-volumes"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5753
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-ldm-volumes\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-ldm-volumes\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5755 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9234
msgid ""
"This function returns all Windows dynamic disk volumes that were found at "
"launch time.  It returns a list of device names."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija atgriež visus Windows dinamisko disku sējumus, kas tika atrasti "
"palaišanas laikā.  Tā atgriež ierīču nosaukumu sarakstu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5762
msgid "list-md-devices"
msgstr "list-md-devices"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5764
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-md-devices\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-md-devices\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5766 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9252
msgid "List all Linux md devices."
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas Linux md ierīces."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5768
msgid "list-partitions"
msgstr "list-partitions"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5770
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-partitions\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-partitions\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5772 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9265
msgid "List all the partitions detected on all block devices."
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visus nodalījumus, kas noteikti visās bloku ierīcēs."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5774 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9267
msgid "The full partition device names are returned, eg. F</dev/sda1>"
msgstr "Tiek atgriezti pilni nodalījumu ierīču nosaukumi, piem., F</dev/sda1>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5776
msgid ""
"This does not return logical volumes.  For that you will need to call "
"L</lvs>."
msgstr "Tas neatgriež loģiskos sējumus.  Tam jāizsauc L</lvs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5781
msgid "ll"
msgstr "ll"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5783
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ll directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ll directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5785 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9286
msgid ""
"List the files in F<directory> (relative to the root directory, there is no "
"cwd) in the format of C<ls -la>."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt failus F<directory> (attiecībā pret saknes direktoriju, cwd nav) "
"formātā C<ls -la>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5788 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5797
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9289 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9312
msgid ""
"This command is mostly useful for interactive sessions.  It is I<not> "
"intended that you try to parse the output string."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda galvenokārt noder interaktīvās sesijās.  I<Nav> paredzēts, ka "
"mēģināsiet parsēt izvades virkni."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5791
msgid "llz"
msgstr "llz"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5793
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" llz directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" llz directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5795 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9310
msgid "List the files in F<directory> in the format of C<ls -laZ>."
msgstr "Uzskaitīt failus F<directory> formātā C<ls -laZ>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5800
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</lgetxattrs> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"lgetxattrs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5807
msgid "ln"
msgstr "ln"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5809
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ln target linkname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ln target linkname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5811 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9327
msgid "This command creates a hard link."
msgstr "Šī komanda izveido cieto saiti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5813
msgid "ln-f"
msgstr "ln-f"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5815
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ln-f target linkname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ln-f target linkname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5817 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9340
msgid ""
"This command creates a hard link, removing the link C<linkname> if it exists "
"already."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izveido cieto saiti, noņemot saiti C<linkname>, ja tā jau eksistē."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5820
msgid "ln-s"
msgstr "ln-s"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5822
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ln-s target linkname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ln-s target linkname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5824 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9354
msgid "This command creates a symbolic link using the C<ln -s> command."
msgstr "Šī komanda izveido simbolisko saiti, izmantojot komandu C<ln -s>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5826
msgid "ln-sf"
msgstr "ln-sf"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5828
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ln-sf target linkname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ln-sf target linkname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5830 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9367
msgid ""
"This command creates a symbolic link using the C<ln -sf> command, The I<-f> "
"option removes the link (C<linkname>) if it exists already."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izveido simbolisko saiti, izmantojot komandu C<ln -sf>. Opcija I<-"
"f> noņem saiti (C<linkname>), ja tā jau eksistē."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5833
msgid "lremovexattr"
msgstr "lremovexattr"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5835
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lremovexattr xattr path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lremovexattr xattr path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5837
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</removexattr>, but if C<path> is a symbolic link, then "
"it removes an extended attribute of the link itself."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</removexattr>, bet, ja C<path> ir simboliskā saite, "
"tas noņem pašas saites paplašināto atribūtu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5844
msgid "ls"
msgstr "ls"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5846
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ls directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ls directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5848 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9398
msgid ""
"List the files in F<directory> (relative to the root directory, there is no "
"cwd).  The C<.> and C<..> entries are not returned, but hidden files are "
"shown."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt failus F<directory> (attiecībā pret saknes direktoriju, cwd nav).  "
"Ieraksti C<.> un C<..> netiek atgriezti, bet slēptie faili tiek rādīti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5852
msgid "ls0"
msgstr "ls0"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5854
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ls0 dir (filenames|-)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ls0 dir (filenames|-)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5856 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9415
msgid ""
"This specialized command is used to get a listing of the filenames in the "
"directory C<dir>.  The list of filenames is written to the local file "
"F<filenames> (on the host)."
msgstr ""
"Šo specializēto komandu izmanto failu nosaukumu saraksta iegūšanai "
"direktorijā C<dir>.  Failu nosaukumu saraksts tiek ierakstīts lokālajā failā "
"F<filenames> (resursdatorā)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5860 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9419
msgid "In the output file, the filenames are separated by C<\\0> characters."
msgstr "Izvades failā failu nosaukumi ir atdalīti ar rakstzīmēm C<\\0>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5862 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9421
msgid "C<.> and C<..> are not returned.  The filenames are not sorted."
msgstr "C<.> un C<..> netiek atgriezti.  Failu nosaukumi nav sakārtoti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5866
msgid "lsetxattr"
msgstr "lsetxattr"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5868
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lsetxattr xattr val vallen path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lsetxattr xattr val vallen path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5870
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</setxattr>, but if C<path> is a symbolic link, then it "
"sets an extended attribute of the link itself."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</setxattr>, bet, ja C<path> ir simboliskā saite, tas "
"iestata pašas saites paplašināto atribūtu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5877
msgid "lstat"
msgstr "lstat"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5879
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lstat path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lstat path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5881 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5925
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9115 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9130
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9460 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9514
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14704 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14720
msgid "Returns file information for the given C<path>."
msgstr "Atgriež faila informāciju dotajam C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5883
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</stat> except that if C<path> is a symbolic link, then "
"the link is stat-ed, not the file it refers to."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</stat>, izņemot to, ka, ja C<path> ir simboliskā "
"saite, stat tiek veikts saitei, nevis failam, uz kuru tā norāda."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5887 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5931
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9466 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9520
msgid "This is the same as the L<lstat(2)> system call."
msgstr "Tas ir tas pats, kas sistēmas izsaukums L<lstat(2)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5889
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</lstatns> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"lstatns>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5896
msgid "lstatlist"
msgstr "lstatlist"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5898
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lstatlist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lstatlist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5900
msgid ""
"This call allows you to perform the L</lstat> operation on multiple files, "
"where all files are in the directory C<path>.  C<names> is the list of files "
"from this directory."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ļauj veikt L</lstat> darbību vairākiem failiem, kur visi faili "
"atrodas direktorijā C<path>.  C<names> ir šīs direktorijas failu saraksts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5904 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5941
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9492 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9539
msgid ""
"On return you get a list of stat structs, with a one-to-one correspondence "
"to the C<names> list.  If any name did not exist or could not be lstat'd, "
"then the C<st_ino> field of that structure is set to C<-1>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriežot saņemat stat struktūru sarakstu ar atbilstību viens pret vienu "
"sarakstam C<names>.  Ja kāds nosaukums neeksistēja vai tam nevarēja izpildīt "
"lstat, šīs struktūras lauks C<st_ino> tiek iestatīts uz C<-1>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5909 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5946
msgid ""
"This call is intended for programs that want to efficiently list a directory "
"contents without making many round-trips.  See also L</lxattrlist> for a "
"similarly efficient call for getting extended attributes."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums paredzēts programmām, kas vēlas efektīvi uzskaitīt "
"direktorijas saturu bez daudzām turp-atpakaļ apmaiņām.  Skatīt arī L</"
"lxattrlist> līdzīgi efektīvam izsaukumam paplašināto atribūtu iegūšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5914
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</lstatnslist> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"lstatnslist>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5921
msgid "lstatns"
msgstr "lstatns"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5923
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lstatns path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lstatns path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5927
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</statns> except that if C<path> is a symbolic link, "
"then the link is stat-ed, not the file it refers to."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</statns>, izņemot to, ka, ja C<path> ir simboliskā "
"saite, stat tiek veikts saitei, nevis failam, uz kuru tā norāda."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5933
msgid "lstatnslist"
msgstr "lstatnslist"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5935
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lstatnslist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lstatnslist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5937
msgid ""
"This call allows you to perform the L</lstatns> operation on multiple files, "
"where all files are in the directory C<path>.  C<names> is the list of files "
"from this directory."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ļauj veikt L</lstatns> darbību vairākiem failiem, kur visi "
"faili atrodas direktorijā C<path>.  C<names> ir šīs direktorijas failu "
"saraksts."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5951
msgid "luks-add-key"
msgstr "luks-add-key"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5953
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-add-key device keyslot\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-add-key device keyslot\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5955 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9564
msgid ""
"This command adds a new key on LUKS device C<device>.  C<key> is any "
"existing key, and is used to access the device.  C<newkey> is the new key to "
"add.  C<keyslot> is the key slot that will be replaced."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda pievieno jaunu atslēgu LUKS ierīcē C<device>.  C<key> ir jebkura "
"esoša atslēga, ko izmanto piekļuvei ierīcei.  C<newkey> ir jaunā "
"pievienojamā atslēga.  C<keyslot> ir atslēgas slots, kas tiks aizstāts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5960
msgid ""
"Note that if C<keyslot> already contains a key, then this command will "
"fail.  You have to use L</luks-kill-slot> first to remove that key."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, ja C<keyslot> jau satur atslēgu, šī komanda neizdosies.  "
"Vispirms jāizmanto L</luks-kill-slot>, lai noņemtu šo atslēgu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5970
msgid "luks-close"
msgstr "luks-close"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5972
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-close device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-close device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5974
msgid ""
"This closes a LUKS device that was created earlier by L</luks-open> or "
"L</luks-open-ro>.  The C<device> parameter must be the name of the LUKS "
"mapping device (ie. F</dev/mapper/mapname>) and I<not> the name of the "
"underlying block device."
msgstr ""
"Tas aizver LUKS ierīci, kas iepriekš izveidota ar L</luks-open> vai L</luks-"
"open-ro>.  Parametram C<device> jābūt LUKS kartēšanas ierīces nosaukumam (t. "
"i., F</dev/mapper/mapname>), I<nevis> pamatā esošās bloku ierīces nosaukumam."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5980
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</cryptsetup-close> "
"call instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"cryptsetup-close>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5990
msgid "luks-format"
msgstr "luks-format"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5992
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-format device keyslot\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-format device keyslot\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:5994 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9618
msgid ""
"This command erases existing data on C<device> and formats the device as a "
"LUKS encrypted device.  C<key> is the initial key, which is added to key "
"slot C<keyslot>.  (LUKS supports 8 key slots, numbered 0-7)."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izdzēš esošos datus ierīcē C<device> un formatē ierīci kā LUKS "
"šifrētu ierīci.  C<key> ir sākotnējā atslēga, kas tiek pievienota atslēgas "
"slotam C<keyslot>.  (LUKS atbalsta 8 atslēgu slotus, numurētus 0-7.)"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6005
msgid "luks-format-cipher"
msgstr "luks-format-cipher"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6007
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-format-cipher device keyslot cipher\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-format-cipher device keyslot cipher\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6009
msgid ""
"This command is the same as L</luks-format> but it also allows you to set "
"the C<cipher> used."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tāda pati kā L</luks-format>, bet tā ļauj arī iestatīt "
"izmantoto C<cipher>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6018
msgid "luks-kill-slot"
msgstr "luks-kill-slot"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6020
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-kill-slot device keyslot\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-kill-slot device keyslot\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6022 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9665
msgid ""
"This command deletes the key in key slot C<keyslot> from the encrypted LUKS "
"device C<device>.  C<key> must be one of the I<other> keys."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda dzēš atslēgu atslēgas slotā C<keyslot> no šifrētās LUKS ierīces "
"C<device>.  C<key> jābūt vienai no I<citām> atslēgām."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6032
msgid "luks-open"
msgstr "luks-open"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6034
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-open device mapname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-open device mapname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6036 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9695
msgid ""
"This command opens a block device which has been encrypted according to the "
"Linux Unified Key Setup (LUKS) standard."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atver bloku ierīci, kas šifrēta saskaņā ar Linux Unified Key "
"Setup (LUKS) standartu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6041 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9700
msgid ""
"The caller must supply one of the keys associated with the LUKS block "
"device, in the C<key> parameter."
msgstr ""
"Izsaucējam parametrā C<key> jānorāda viena no ar LUKS bloku ierīci "
"saistītajām atslēgām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6058 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6078
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</cryptsetup-open> "
"call instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"cryptsetup-open>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6068
msgid "luks-open-ro"
msgstr "luks-open-ro"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6070
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-open-ro device mapname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-open-ro device mapname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6072
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</luks-open> except that a read-only mapping is "
"created."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</luks-open>, izņemot to, ka tiek izveidota tikai "
"lasāma kartēšana."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6088
msgid "luks-uuid"
msgstr "luks-uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6090
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" luks-uuid device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" luks-uuid device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6092 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9760
msgid "This returns the UUID of the LUKS device C<device>."
msgstr "Tas atgriež LUKS ierīces C<device> UUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6097
msgid "lvcreate"
msgstr "lvcreate"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6099
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvcreate logvol volgroup mbytes\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvcreate logvol volgroup mbytes\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6101 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9778
msgid ""
"This creates an LVM logical volume called C<logvol> on the volume group "
"C<volgroup>, with C<size> megabytes."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido LVM loģisko sējumu C<logvol> sējumu grupā C<volgroup> ar izmēru "
"C<size> megabaiti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6104 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6116
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6150 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6197
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6210 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6227
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6240 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6255
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6265 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7766
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7775 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7786
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7800 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7810
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7820 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7835
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7845 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9881
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9893 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9902
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9911 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9921
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9946 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9970
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9991 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10001
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<lvm2>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<lvm2>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-available>"
"."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6107
msgid "lvcreate-free"
msgstr "lvcreate-free"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvcreate-free logvol volgroup percent\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvcreate-free logvol volgroup percent\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6111 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9796
msgid ""
"Create an LVM logical volume called F</dev/volgroup/logvol>, using "
"approximately C<percent> % of the free space remaining in the volume group.  "
"Most usefully, when C<percent> is C<100> this will create the largest "
"possible LV."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot LVM loģisko sējumu F</dev/volgroup/logvol>, izmantojot aptuveni "
"C<percent> % no sējumu grupā atlikušās brīvās vietas.  Visnoderīgāk — ja "
"C<percent> ir C<100>, tiks izveidots lielākais iespējamais LV."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6119
msgid "lvm-canonical-lv-name"
msgstr "lvm-canonical-lv-name"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvm-canonical-lv-name lvname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvm-canonical-lv-name lvname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6123 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9814
msgid ""
"This converts alternative naming schemes for LVs that you might find to the "
"canonical name.  For example, F</dev/mapper/VG-LV> is converted to "
"F</dev/VG/LV>."
msgstr ""
"Tas pārveido alternatīvas LV nosaukšanas shēmas, ko varat sastapt, "
"kanoniskajā nosaukumā.  Piemēram, F</dev/mapper/VG-LV> tiek pārveidots par "
"F</dev/VG/LV>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6127 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9818
msgid ""
"This command returns an error if the C<lvname> parameter does not refer to a "
"logical volume.  In this case errno will be set to C<EINVAL>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atgriež kļūdu, ja parametrs C<lvname> nenorāda uz loģisko "
"sējumu.  Šajā gadījumā errno tiks iestatīts uz C<EINVAL>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6131
msgid "See also L</is-lv>, L</canonical-device-name>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</is-lv>, L</canonical-device-name>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6133
msgid "lvm-clear-filter"
msgstr "lvm-clear-filter"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6135
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvm-clear-filter\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvm-clear-filter\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6137
msgid ""
"This undoes the effect of L</lvm-set-filter>.  LVM will be able to see every "
"block device."
msgstr ""
"Tas atceļ L</lvm-set-filter> ietekmi.  LVM varēs redzēt katru bloku ierīci."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6140 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6188
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9837 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9902
msgid "This command also clears the LVM cache and performs a volume group scan."
msgstr "Šī komanda arī notīra LVM kešatmiņu un veic sējumu grupu skenēšanu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6143
msgid "lvm-remove-all"
msgstr "lvm-remove-all"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvm-remove-all\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvm-remove-all\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6147 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9849
msgid ""
"This command removes all LVM logical volumes, volume groups and physical "
"volumes."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda noņem visus LVM loģiskos sējumus, sējumu grupas un fiziskos "
"sējumus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6153
msgid "lvm-scan"
msgstr "lvm-scan"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6155
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvm-scan true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvm-scan true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6157 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9865
msgid ""
"This scans all block devices and rebuilds the list of LVM physical volumes, "
"volume groups and logical volumes."
msgstr ""
"Tas skenē visas bloku ierīces un pārbūvē LVM fizisko sējumu, sējumu grupu un "
"loģisko sējumu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6160 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9868
msgid ""
"If the C<activate> parameter is C<true> then newly found volume groups and "
"logical volumes are activated, meaning the LV F</dev/VG/LV> devices become "
"visible."
msgstr ""
"Ja parametrs C<activate> ir C<true>, jaunatrastās sējumu grupas un loģiskie "
"sējumi tiek aktivizēti, t. i., LV ierīces F</dev/VG/LV> kļūst redzamas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6164
msgid ""
"When a libguestfs handle is launched it scans for existing devices, so you "
"do not normally need to use this API.  However it is useful when you have "
"added a new device or deleted an existing device (such as when the "
"L</luks-open> API is used)."
msgstr ""
"Kad libguestfs rokturis tiek palaists, tas skenē esošās ierīces, tāpēc "
"parasti šī API nav jāizmanto.  Tomēr tā noder, ja pievienota jauna ierīce "
"vai dzēsta esoša (piemēram, kad tiek izmantota API L</luks-open>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6170
msgid "lvm-set-filter"
msgstr "lvm-set-filter"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6172
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvm-set-filter 'devices ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvm-set-filter 'devices ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6174 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9888
msgid ""
"This sets the LVM device filter so that LVM will only be able to \"see\" the "
"block devices in the list C<devices>, and will ignore all other attached "
"block devices."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata LVM ierīču filtru, lai LVM varētu „redzēt” tikai bloku ierīces "
"sarakstā C<devices> un ignorētu visas pārējās pievienotās bloku ierīces."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6178 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9892
msgid ""
"Where disk image(s) contain duplicate PVs or VGs, this command is useful to "
"get LVM to ignore the duplicates, otherwise LVM can get confused.  Note also "
"there are two types of duplication possible: either cloned PVs/VGs which "
"have identical UUIDs; or VGs that are not cloned but just happen to have the "
"same name.  In normal operation you cannot create this situation, but you "
"can do it outside LVM, eg.  by cloning disk images or by bit twiddling "
"inside the LVM metadata."
msgstr ""
"Ja disku attēlos ir dublēti PV vai VG, šī komanda noder, lai LVM ignorētu "
"dublikātus, citādi LVM var apjukt.  Ņemiet vērā arī, ka iespējami divu veidu "
"dublējumi: vai nu klonēti PV/VG ar identiskiem UUID, vai VG, kas nav "
"klonēti, bet kuriem gadās vienāds nosaukums.  Parastā darbībā šādu situāciju "
"nevar izveidot, bet to var izdarīt ārpus LVM, piem., klonējot disku attēlus "
"vai mainot bitus LVM metadatos."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6191 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9905
msgid "You can filter whole block devices or individual partitions."
msgstr "Var filtrēt veselas bloku ierīces vai atsevišķus nodalījumus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6193 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9907
msgid ""
"You cannot use this if any VG is currently in use (eg.  contains a mounted "
"filesystem), even if you are not filtering out that VG."
msgstr ""
"To nevar izmantot, ja kāds VG pašlaik tiek izmantots (piem., satur montētu "
"failu sistēmu), pat ja šo VG neizfiltrējat."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6200
msgid "lvremove"
msgstr "lvremove"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6202
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvremove device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvremove device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6204 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9924
msgid ""
"Remove an LVM logical volume C<device>, where C<device> is the path to the "
"LV, such as F</dev/VG/LV>."
msgstr ""
"Noņemt LVM loģisko sējumu C<device>, kur C<device> ir ceļš uz LV, piemēram, "
"F</dev/VG/LV>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6207 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9927
msgid ""
"You can also remove all LVs in a volume group by specifying the VG name, "
"F</dev/VG>."
msgstr ""
"Varat arī noņemt visus LV sējumu grupā, norādot VG nosaukumu, F</dev/VG>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6213
msgid "lvrename"
msgstr "lvrename"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6215
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvrename logvol newlogvol\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvrename logvol newlogvol\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6217 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9944
msgid "Rename a logical volume C<logvol> with the new name C<newlogvol>."
msgstr "Pārdēvēt loģisko sējumu C<logvol> ar jauno nosaukumu C<newlogvol>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6219
msgid "lvresize"
msgstr "lvresize"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6221
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvresize device mbytes\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvresize device mbytes\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6223 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9957
msgid ""
"This resizes (expands or shrinks) an existing LVM logical volume to "
"C<mbytes>.  When reducing, data in the reduced part is lost."
msgstr ""
"Tas maina esoša LVM loģiskā sējuma izmēru (paplašina vai samazina) uz "
"C<mbytes>.  Samazinot dati samazinātajā daļā tiek zaudēti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6230
msgid "lvresize-free"
msgstr "lvresize-free"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6232
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvresize-free lv percent\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvresize-free lv percent\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6234 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9975
msgid ""
"This expands an existing logical volume C<lv> so that it fills C<pc> % of "
"the remaining free space in the volume group.  Commonly you would call this "
"with pc = 100 which expands the logical volume as much as possible, using "
"all remaining free space in the volume group."
msgstr ""
"Tas paplašina esošu loģisko sējumu C<lv>, lai tas aizpildītu C<pc> % no "
"sējumu grupā atlikušās brīvās vietas.  Parasti to izsauktu ar pc = 100, kas "
"paplašina loģisko sējumu, cik iespējams, izmantojot visu sējumu grupā "
"atlikušo brīvo vietu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6243
msgid "lvs"
msgstr "lvs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6245
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6247 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9993
msgid ""
"List all the logical volumes detected.  This is the equivalent of the "
"L<lvs(8)> command."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visus noteiktos loģiskos sējumus.  Tas ir ekvivalents komandai "
"L<lvs(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6250 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:9996
msgid ""
"This returns a list of the logical volume device names "
"(eg. F</dev/VolGroup00/LogVol00>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež loģisko sējumu ierīču nosaukumu sarakstu (piem., F</dev/"
"VolGroup00/LogVol00>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6253
msgid "See also L</lvs-full>, L</list-filesystems>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</lvs-full>, L</list-filesystems>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6258
msgid "lvs-full"
msgstr "lvs-full"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6260
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvs-full\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvs-full\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6262 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10015
msgid ""
"List all the logical volumes detected.  This is the equivalent of the "
"L<lvs(8)> command.  The \"full\" version includes all fields."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visus noteiktos loģiskos sējumus.  Tas ir ekvivalents komandai "
"L<lvs(8)>.  „Pilnā” versija ietver visus laukus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6268
msgid "lvuuid"
msgstr "lvuuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6270
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvuuid device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvuuid device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6272 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10033
msgid "This command returns the UUID of the LVM LV C<device>."
msgstr "Šī komanda atgriež LVM LV C<device> UUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6274
msgid "lxattrlist"
msgstr "lxattrlist"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lxattrlist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lxattrlist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6278 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10047
msgid ""
"This call allows you to get the extended attributes of multiple files, where "
"all files are in the directory C<path>.  C<names> is the list of files from "
"this directory."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ļauj iegūt vairāku failu paplašinātos atribūtus, kur visi "
"faili atrodas direktorijā C<path>.  C<names> ir šīs direktorijas failu "
"saraksts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6282
msgid ""
"On return you get a flat list of xattr structs which must be interpreted "
"sequentially.  The first xattr struct always has a zero-length C<attrname>.  "
"C<attrval> in this struct is zero-length to indicate there was an error "
"doing L</lgetxattr> for this file, I<or> is a C string which is a decimal "
"number (the number of following attributes for this file, which could be "
"C<\"0\">).  Then after the first xattr struct are the zero or more "
"attributes for the first named file.  This repeats for the second and "
"subsequent files."
msgstr ""
"Atgriežot saņemat plakanu xattr struktūru sarakstu, kas jāinterpretē "
"secīgi.  Pirmajai xattr struktūrai vienmēr ir nulles garuma C<attrname>.  "
"C<attrval> šajā struktūrā ir nulles garuma, lai norādītu, ka šim failam, "
"veicot L</lgetxattr>, radās kļūda, I<vai> ir C virkne, kas ir decimāls "
"skaitlis (sekojošo atribūtu skaits šim failam, kas var būt C<\"0\">).  Pēc "
"pirmās xattr struktūras seko nulle vai vairāk pirmā nosauktā faila "
"atribūtu.  Tas atkārtojas otrajam un nākamajiem failiem."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6292
msgid ""
"This call is intended for programs that want to efficiently list a directory "
"contents without making many round-trips.  See also L</lstatlist> for a "
"similarly efficient call for getting standard stats."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums paredzēts programmām, kas vēlas efektīvi uzskaitīt "
"direktorijas saturu bez daudzām turp-atpakaļ apmaiņām.  Skatīt arī L</"
"lstatlist> līdzīgi efektīvam izsaukumam standarta stat iegūšanai."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6300
msgid "max-disks"
msgstr "max-disks"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6302
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" max-disks\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" max-disks\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6304
msgid ""
"Return the maximum number of disks that may be added to a handle (eg. by "
"L</add-drive-opts> and similar calls)."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt maksimālo disku skaitu, ko var pievienot rokturim (piem., ar L</add-"
"drive-opts> un līdzīgiem izsaukumiem)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6307 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10083
msgid ""
"This function was added in libguestfs 1.19.7.  In previous versions of "
"libguestfs the limit was 25."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija tika pievienota libguestfs 1.19.7.  Iepriekšējās libguestfs "
"versijās ierobežojums bija 25."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6310 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10086
msgid ""
"See L<guestfs(3)/MAXIMUM NUMBER OF DISKS> for additional information on this "
"topic."
msgstr ""
"Papildu informāciju par šo tēmu skatiet L<guestfs(3)/MAKSIMĀLAIS DISKU "
"SKAITS>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6313
msgid "md-create"
msgstr "md-create"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6315
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" md-create name 'devices ...' [missingbitmap:N] [nrdevices:N] [spare:N] "
"[chunk:N] [level:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" md-create name 'devices ...' [missingbitmap:N] [nrdevices:N] [spare:N] "
"[chunk:N] [level:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6317 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10112
msgid ""
"Create a Linux md (RAID) device named C<name> on the devices in the list "
"C<devices>."
msgstr "Izveidot Linux md (RAID) ierīci C<name> ierīcēs no saraksta C<devices>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6324 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10119
msgid "C<missingbitmap>"
msgstr "C<missingbitmap>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6326 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10121
msgid ""
"A bitmap of missing devices.  If a bit is set it means that a missing device "
"is added to the array.  The least significant bit corresponds to the first "
"device in the array."
msgstr ""
"Trūkstošo ierīču bitkarte.  Ja bits ir iestatīts, tas nozīmē, ka masīvam "
"tiek pievienota trūkstoša ierīce.  Mazākais nozīmīgais bits atbilst pirmajai "
"masīva ierīcei."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6330 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10125
msgid "As examples:"
msgstr "Piemēram:"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6332 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10127
msgid ""
"If C<devices = [\"/dev/sda\"]> and C<missingbitmap = 0x1> then the resulting "
"array would be C<[E<lt>missingE<gt>, \"/dev/sda\"]>."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<devices = [\"/dev/sda\"]> un C<missingbitmap = 0x1>, iegūtais masīvs "
"būtu C<[E<lt>missingE<gt>, \"/dev/sda\"]>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6335 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10130
msgid ""
"If C<devices = [\"/dev/sda\"]> and C<missingbitmap = 0x2> then the resulting "
"array would be C<[\"/dev/sda\", E<lt>missingE<gt>]>."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<devices = [\"/dev/sda\"]> un C<missingbitmap = 0x2>, iegūtais masīvs "
"būtu C<[\"/dev/sda\", E<lt>missingE<gt>]>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6338 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10133
msgid "This defaults to C<0> (no missing devices)."
msgstr "Noklusējums ir C<0> (nav trūkstošu ierīču)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6340 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10135
msgid ""
"The length of C<devices> + the number of bits set in C<missingbitmap> must "
"equal C<nrdevices> + C<spare>."
msgstr ""
"C<devices> garumam + C<missingbitmap> iestatīto bitu skaitam jābūt vienādam "
"ar C<nrdevices> + C<spare>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6343 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10138
msgid "C<nrdevices>"
msgstr "C<nrdevices>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6345 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10140
msgid "The number of active RAID devices."
msgstr "Aktīvo RAID ierīču skaits."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6347 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10142
msgid ""
"If not set, this defaults to the length of C<devices> plus the number of "
"bits set in C<missingbitmap>."
msgstr ""
"Ja nav iestatīts, noklusējums ir C<devices> garums plus C<missingbitmap> "
"iestatīto bitu skaits."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6350 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10145
msgid "C<spare>"
msgstr "C<spare>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6352 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10147
msgid "The number of spare devices."
msgstr "Rezerves ierīču skaits."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6354 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10149
msgid "If not set, this defaults to C<0>."
msgstr "Ja nav iestatīts, noklusējums ir C<0>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6356 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10151
msgid "C<chunk>"
msgstr "C<chunk>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6358 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10153
msgid "The chunk size in bytes."
msgstr "Gabala izmērs baitos."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6360 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10155
msgid ""
"The C<chunk> parameter does not make sense, and should not be specified, "
"when C<level> is C<raid1> (which is the default; see below)."
msgstr ""
"Parametram C<chunk> nav jēgas, un to nevajadzētu norādīt, ja C<level> ir "
"C<raid1> (kas ir noklusējums; skatiet tālāk)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6363 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6389
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10158 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10212
msgid "C<level>"
msgstr "C<level>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6365 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10160
msgid ""
"The RAID level, which can be one of: C<linear>, C<raid0>, C<0>, C<stripe>, "
"C<raid1>, C<1>, C<mirror>, C<raid4>, C<4>, C<raid5>, C<5>, C<raid6>, C<6>, "
"C<raid10>, C<10>.  Some of these are synonymous, and more levels may be "
"added in future."
msgstr ""
"RAID līmenis, kas var būt viens no: C<linear>, C<raid0>, C<0>, C<stripe>, "
"C<raid1>, C<1>, C<mirror>, C<raid4>, C<4>, C<raid5>, C<5>, C<raid6>, C<6>, "
"C<raid10>, C<10>.  Daži no tiem ir sinonīmi, un nākotnē var tikt pievienoti "
"citi līmeņi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6370 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10165
msgid "If not set, this defaults to C<raid1>."
msgstr "Ja nav iestatīts, noklusējums ir C<raid1>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6376 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6411
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6463 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6473
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<mdadm>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<mdadm>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6379
msgid "md-detail"
msgstr "md-detail"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6381
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" md-detail md\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" md-detail md\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6383 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10206
msgid ""
"This command exposes the output of C<mdadm -DY E<lt>mdE<gt>>.  The following "
"fields are usually present in the returned hash.  Other fields may also be "
"present."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atklāj C<mdadm -DY E<lt>mdE<gt>> izvadi.  Atgrieztajā "
"jaucējtabulā parasti ir šādi lauki.  Var būt arī citi lauki."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6391 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10214
msgid "The raid level of the MD device."
msgstr "MD ierīces raid līmenis."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6393 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10216
msgid "C<devices>"
msgstr "C<devices>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6395 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10218
msgid "The number of underlying devices in the MD device."
msgstr "Pamatā esošo ierīču skaits MD ierīcē."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6397 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10220
msgid "C<metadata>"
msgstr "C<metadata>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6399 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10222
msgid "The metadata version used."
msgstr "Izmantotā metadatu versija."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6401 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10224
msgid "C<uuid>"
msgstr "C<uuid>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6403 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10226
msgid "The UUID of the MD device."
msgstr "MD ierīces UUID."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6407 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10230
msgid "The name of the MD device."
msgstr "MD ierīces nosaukums."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6414
msgid "md-stat"
msgstr "md-stat"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6416
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" md-stat md\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" md-stat md\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6418 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10251
msgid ""
"This call returns a list of the underlying devices which make up the single "
"software RAID array device C<md>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums atgriež pamatā esošo ierīču sarakstu, kas veido vienu "
"programmatūras RAID masīva ierīci C<md>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6421
msgid "To get a list of software RAID devices, call L</list-md-devices>."
msgstr ""
"Lai iegūtu programmatūras RAID ierīču sarakstu, izsauciet L</list-md-devices>"
"."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6423 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10256
msgid ""
"Each structure returned corresponds to one device along with additional "
"status information:"
msgstr ""
"Katra atgrieztā struktūra atbilst vienai ierīcei kopā ar papildu statusa "
"informāciju:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6428 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10261
msgid "C<mdstat_device>"
msgstr "C<mdstat_device>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6430 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10263
msgid "The name of the underlying device."
msgstr "Pamatā esošās ierīces nosaukums."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6432 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10265
msgid "C<mdstat_index>"
msgstr "C<mdstat_index>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6434 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10267
msgid "The index of this device within the array."
msgstr "Šīs ierīces indekss masīvā."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6436 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10269
msgid "C<mdstat_flags>"
msgstr "C<mdstat_flags>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6438 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10271
msgid ""
"Flags associated with this device.  This is a string containing (in no "
"specific order) zero or more of the following flags:"
msgstr ""
"Ar šo ierīci saistītie karogi.  Tā ir virkne, kas satur (nekādā konkrētā "
"secībā) nulli vai vairāk no šiem karogiem:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6443 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10276
msgid "C<W>"
msgstr "C<W>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6445 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10278
msgid "write-mostly"
msgstr "write-mostly"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6447 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10280
msgid "C<F>"
msgstr "C<F>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6449 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10282
msgid "device is faulty"
msgstr "ierīce ir bojāta"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6451 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10284
msgid "C<S>"
msgstr "C<S>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6453 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10286
msgid "device is a RAID spare"
msgstr "ierīce ir RAID rezerve"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6455 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10288
msgid "C<R>"
msgstr "C<R>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6457 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10290
msgid "replacement"
msgstr "replacement"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6466
msgid "md-stop"
msgstr "md-stop"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6468
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" md-stop md\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" md-stop md\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6470 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10311
msgid ""
"This command deactivates the MD array named C<md>.  The device is stopped, "
"but it is not destroyed or zeroed."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda deaktivizē MD masīvu C<md>.  Ierīce tiek apturēta, bet netiek "
"iznīcināta vai aizpildīta ar nullēm."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6476
msgid "mkdir"
msgstr "mkdir"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6478
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkdir path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkdir path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6480 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10327
msgid "Create a directory named C<path>."
msgstr "Izveidot direktoriju C<path>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6482
msgid "mkdir-mode"
msgstr "mkdir-mode"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6484
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkdir-mode path mode\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkdir-mode path mode\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6486 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10340
msgid ""
"This command creates a directory, setting the initial permissions of the "
"directory to C<mode>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izveido direktoriju, iestatot direktorijas sākotnējās atļaujas uz "
"C<mode>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6489 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10343
msgid ""
"For common Linux filesystems, the actual mode which is set will be C<mode & "
"~umask & 01777>.  Non-native-Linux filesystems may interpret the mode in "
"other ways."
msgstr ""
"Parastām Linux failu sistēmām faktiski iestatītais režīms būs C<mode & "
"~umask & 01777>.  Ne-Linux failu sistēmas var interpretēt režīmu citādi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6493
msgid "See also L</mkdir>, L</umask>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</mkdir>, L</umask>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6495
msgid "mkdir-p"
msgstr "mkdir-p"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6497
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkdir-p path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkdir-p path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6499 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10359
msgid ""
"Create a directory named C<path>, creating any parent directories as "
"necessary.  This is like the C<mkdir -p> shell command."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot direktoriju C<path>, pēc vajadzības izveidojot vecākdirektorijas.  "
"Tas ir līdzīgi čaulas komandai C<mkdir -p>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6502
msgid "mkdtemp"
msgstr "mkdtemp"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6504
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkdtemp tmpl\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkdtemp tmpl\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6506 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10372
msgid ""
"This command creates a temporary directory.  The C<tmpl> parameter should be "
"a full pathname for the temporary directory name with the final six "
"characters being \"XXXXXX\"."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izveido pagaidu direktoriju.  Parametram C<tmpl> jābūt pilnam "
"ceļa nosaukumam pagaidu direktorijas nosaukumam, kura pēdējās sešas "
"rakstzīmes ir „XXXXXX”."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6511 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6943
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10377 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11195
msgid ""
"For example: \"/tmp/myprogXXXXXX\" or \"/Temp/myprogXXXXXX\", the second one "
"being suitable for Windows filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Piemēram: „/tmp/myprogXXXXXX” vai „/Temp/myprogXXXXXX”, otrais ir piemērots "
"Windows failu sistēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6514 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10380
msgid "The name of the temporary directory that was created is returned."
msgstr "Tiek atgriezts izveidotās pagaidu direktorijas nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6517 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10383
msgid "The temporary directory is created with mode 0700 and is owned by root."
msgstr ""
"Pagaidu direktorija tiek izveidota ar režīmu 0700, un tās īpašnieks ir root."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6520 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10386
msgid ""
"The caller is responsible for deleting the temporary directory and its "
"contents after use."
msgstr ""
"Izsaucējs ir atbildīgs par pagaidu direktorijas un tās satura dzēšanu pēc "
"lietošanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6523 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10389
msgid "See also: L<mkdtemp(3)>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L<mkdtemp(3)>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6525
msgid "mke2fs"
msgstr "mke2fs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6527
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2fs device [blockscount:N] [blocksize:N] [fragsize:N] [blockspergroup:N] "
"[numberofgroups:N] [bytesperinode:N] [inodesize:N] [journalsize:N] "
"[numberofinodes:N] [stridesize:N] [stripewidth:N] [maxonlineresize:N] "
"[reservedblockspercentage:N] [mmpupdateinterval:N] [journaldevice:..] "
"[label:..] [lastmounteddir:..] [creatoros:..] [fstype:..] [usagetype:..] "
"[uuid:..] [forcecreate:true|false] [writesbandgrouponly:true|false] "
"[lazyitableinit:true|false] [lazyjournalinit:true|false] [testfs:true|false] "
"[discard:true|false] [quotatype:true|false] [extent:true|false] "
"[filetype:true|false] [flexbg:true|false] [hasjournal:true|false] "
"[journaldev:true|false] [largefile:true|false] [quota:true|false] "
"[resizeinode:true|false] [sparsesuper:true|false] [uninitbg:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2fs device [blockscount:N] [blocksize:N] [fragsize:N] [blockspergroup:N] "
"[numberofgroups:N] [bytesperinode:N] [inodesize:N] [journalsize:N] "
"[numberofinodes:N] [stridesize:N] [stripewidth:N] [maxonlineresize:N] "
"[reservedblockspercentage:N] [mmpupdateinterval:N] [journaldevice:..] "
"[label:..] [lastmounteddir:..] [creatoros:..] [fstype:..] [usagetype:..] "
"[uuid:..] [forcecreate:true|false] [writesbandgrouponly:true|false] "
"[lazyitableinit:true|false] [lazyjournalinit:true|false] [testfs:true|false] "
"[discard:true|false] [quotatype:true|false] [extent:true|false] "
"[filetype:true|false] [flexbg:true|false] [hasjournal:true|false] "
"[journaldev:true|false] [largefile:true|false] [quota:true|false] "
"[resizeinode:true|false] [sparsesuper:true|false] [uninitbg:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6529 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10447
msgid "C<mke2fs> is used to create an ext2, ext3, or ext4 filesystem on C<device>."
msgstr ""
"C<mke2fs> tiek izmantots, lai ierīcē C<device> izveidotu ext2, ext3 vai ext4 "
"failu sistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6532 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10450
msgid ""
"The optional C<blockscount> is the size of the filesystem in blocks.  If "
"omitted it defaults to the size of C<device>.  Note if the filesystem is too "
"small to contain a journal, C<mke2fs> will silently create an ext2 "
"filesystem instead."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātais C<blockscount> ir failu sistēmas izmērs blokos.  Ja izlaists, "
"noklusējums ir C<device> izmērs.  Ņemiet vērā: ja failu sistēma ir pārāk "
"maza, lai saturētu žurnālu, C<mke2fs> tā vietā klusi izveidos ext2 failu "
"sistēmu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6539
msgid "mke2fs-J"
msgstr "mke2fs-J"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6541
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2fs-J fstype blocksize device journal\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2fs-J fstype blocksize device journal\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6543 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10497
msgid ""
"This creates an ext2/3/4 filesystem on C<device> with an external journal on "
"C<journal>.  It is equivalent to the command:"
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido ext2/3/4 failu sistēmu ierīcē C<device> ar ārēju žurnālu "
"C<journal>.  Tas ir līdzvērtīgi komandai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6547 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10501
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2fs -t fstype -b blocksize -J device=<journal> <device>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2fs -t fstype -b blocksize -J device=<journal> <device>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6549
msgid "See also L</mke2journal>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</mke2journal>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6551 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6567
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6583 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6602
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6615 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6628
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</mke2fs> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"mke2fs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6558
msgid "mke2fs-JL"
msgstr "mke2fs-JL"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6560
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2fs-JL fstype blocksize device label\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2fs-JL fstype blocksize device label\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6562 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10525
msgid ""
"This creates an ext2/3/4 filesystem on C<device> with an external journal on "
"the journal labeled C<label>."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido ext2/3/4 failu sistēmu ierīcē C<device> ar ārēju žurnālu žurnālā "
"ar etiķeti C<label>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6565
msgid "See also L</mke2journal-L>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</mke2journal-L>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6574
msgid "mke2fs-JU"
msgstr "mke2fs-JU"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6576
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2fs-JU fstype blocksize device uuid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2fs-JU fstype blocksize device uuid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6578 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10550
msgid ""
"This creates an ext2/3/4 filesystem on C<device> with an external journal on "
"the journal with UUID C<uuid>."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido ext2/3/4 failu sistēmu ierīcē C<device> ar ārēju žurnālu žurnālā "
"ar UUID C<uuid>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6581
msgid "See also L</mke2journal-U>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</mke2journal-U>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6590 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6635
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6922 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9236
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9276
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<linuxfsuuid>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<linuxfsuuid>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6593
msgid "mke2journal"
msgstr "mke2journal"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6595
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2journal blocksize device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2journal blocksize device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6597 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10576
msgid ""
"This creates an ext2 external journal on C<device>.  It is equivalent to the "
"command:"
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido ext2 ārēju žurnālu ierīcē C<device>.  Tas ir līdzvērtīgi "
"komandai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6600 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10579
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2fs -O journal_dev -b blocksize device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2fs -O journal_dev -b blocksize device\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6609
msgid "mke2journal-L"
msgstr "mke2journal-L"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6611
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2journal-L blocksize label device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2journal-L blocksize label device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6613 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10600
msgid "This creates an ext2 external journal on C<device> with label C<label>."
msgstr "Tas izveido ext2 ārēju žurnālu ierīcē C<device> ar etiķeti C<label>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6622
msgid "mke2journal-U"
msgstr "mke2journal-U"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6624
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mke2journal-U blocksize uuid device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mke2journal-U blocksize uuid device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6626 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10621
msgid "This creates an ext2 external journal on C<device> with UUID C<uuid>."
msgstr "Tas izveido ext2 ārēju žurnālu ierīcē C<device> ar UUID C<uuid>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6638
msgid "mkfifo"
msgstr "mkfifo"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6640
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkfifo mode path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkfifo mode path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6642
msgid ""
"This call creates a FIFO (named pipe) called C<path> with mode C<mode>.  It "
"is just a convenient wrapper around L</mknod>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums izveido FIFO (nosauktu kanālu) C<path> ar režīmu C<mode>.  Tas "
"ir tikai ērts ietinējs ap L</mknod>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6646 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6823
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6839
msgid "Unlike with L</mknod>, C<mode> B<must> contain only permissions bits."
msgstr "Atšķirībā no L</mknod>, C<mode> B<jāsatur> tikai atļauju biti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6651 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6812
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6828 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6844
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<mknod>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<mknod>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6654
msgid "mkfs"
msgstr "mkfs"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6656
msgid "mkfs-opts"
msgstr "mkfs-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6658
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkfs fstype device [blocksize:N] [features:..] [inode:N] [sectorsize:N] "
"[label:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkfs fstype device [blocksize:N] [features:..] [inode:N] [sectorsize:N] "
"[label:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6660 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10686
msgid ""
"This function creates a filesystem on C<device>.  The filesystem type is "
"C<fstype>, for example C<ext3>."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija izveido failu sistēmu ierīcē C<device>.  Failu sistēmas tips ir "
"C<fstype>, piemēram, C<ext3>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6669 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10695
msgid ""
"The filesystem block size.  Supported block sizes depend on the filesystem "
"type, but typically they are C<1024>, C<2048> or C<4096> for Linux ext2/3 "
"filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēmas bloka izmērs.  Atbalstītie bloku izmēri ir atkarīgi no failu "
"sistēmas tipa, bet Linux ext2/3 failu sistēmām parasti tie ir C<1024>, "
"C<2048> vai C<4096>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6673 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6712
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10699 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10775
msgid ""
"For VFAT and NTFS the C<blocksize> parameter is treated as the requested "
"cluster size."
msgstr ""
"VFAT un NTFS gadījumā parametrs C<blocksize> tiek uzskatīts par pieprasīto "
"klastera izmēru."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6676 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10702
msgid "For UFS block sizes, please see L<mkfs.ufs(8)>."
msgstr "UFS bloku izmērus, lūdzu, skatiet L<mkfs.ufs(8)>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6678 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10704
msgid "C<features>"
msgstr "C<features>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6680 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10706
msgid "This passes the I<-O> parameter to the external mkfs program."
msgstr "Tas nodod ārējai mkfs programmai parametru I<-O>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6682 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10708
msgid ""
"For certain filesystem types, this allows extra filesystem features to be "
"selected.  See L<mke2fs(8)> and L<mkfs.ufs(8)> for more details."
msgstr ""
"Dažiem failu sistēmu tipiem tas ļauj izvēlēties papildu failu sistēmas "
"līdzekļus.  Sīkāk skatiet L<mke2fs(8)> un L<mkfs.ufs(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6686 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10712
msgid ""
"You cannot use this optional parameter with the C<gfs> or C<gfs2> filesystem "
"type."
msgstr ""
"Šo neobligāto parametru nevar izmantot ar failu sistēmas tipu C<gfs> vai "
"C<gfs2>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6689 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10715
msgid "C<inode>"
msgstr "C<inode>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6691 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10717
msgid ""
"This passes the I<-I> parameter to the external L<mke2fs(8)> program which "
"sets the inode size (only for ext2/3/4 filesystems at present)."
msgstr ""
"Tas nodod ārējai programmai L<mke2fs(8)> parametru I<-I>, kas iestata inode "
"izmēru (pašlaik tikai ext2/3/4 failu sistēmām)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6694 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10720
msgid "C<sectorsize>"
msgstr "C<sectorsize>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6696 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10722
msgid ""
"This passes the I<-S> parameter to external L<mkfs.ufs(8)> program, which "
"sets sector size for ufs filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Tas nodod ārējai programmai L<mkfs.ufs(8)> parametru I<-S>, kas iestata "
"sektora izmēru ufs failu sistēmai."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6703
msgid "mkfs-b"
msgstr "mkfs-b"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6705
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkfs-b fstype blocksize device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkfs-b fstype blocksize device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6707
msgid ""
"This call is similar to L</mkfs>, but it allows you to control the block "
"size of the resulting filesystem.  Supported block sizes depend on the "
"filesystem type, but typically they are C<1024>, C<2048> or C<4096> only."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ir līdzīgs L</mkfs>, bet ļauj kontrolēt iegūtās failu sistēmas "
"bloka izmēru.  Atbalstītie bloku izmēri ir atkarīgi no failu sistēmas tipa, "
"bet parasti tie ir tikai C<1024>, C<2048> vai C<4096>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6715
msgid "I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</mkfs> call instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"mkfs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6722
msgid "mkfs-btrfs"
msgstr "mkfs-btrfs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6724
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkfs-btrfs 'devices ...' [allocstart:N] [bytecount:N] [datatype:..] "
"[leafsize:N] [label:..] [metadata:..] [nodesize:N] [sectorsize:N]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkfs-btrfs 'devices ...' [allocstart:N] [bytecount:N] [datatype:..] "
"[leafsize:N] [label:..] [metadata:..] [nodesize:N] [sectorsize:N]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6726 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10803
msgid ""
"Create a btrfs filesystem, allowing all configurables to be set.  For more "
"information on the optional arguments, see L<mkfs.btrfs(8)>."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot btrfs failu sistēmu, ļaujot iestatīt visus konfigurējamos "
"parametrus.  Plašāku informāciju par neobligātajiem argumentiem skatiet "
"L<mkfs.btrfs(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6729 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10806
msgid ""
"Since btrfs filesystems can span multiple devices, this takes a non-empty "
"list of devices."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā btrfs failu sistēmas var izvērsties pa vairākām ierīcēm, tas pieņem "
"netukšu ierīču sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6732
msgid "To create general filesystems, use L</mkfs>."
msgstr "Vispārīgu failu sistēmu izveidei izmantojiet L</mkfs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6739
msgid "mklost-and-found"
msgstr "mklost-and-found"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6741
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mklost-and-found mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mklost-and-found mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6743 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10846
msgid ""
"Make the C<lost+found> directory, normally in the root directory of an "
"ext2/3/4 filesystem.  C<mountpoint> is the directory under which we try to "
"create the C<lost+found> directory."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot direktoriju C<lost+found>, parasti ext2/3/4 failu sistēmas saknes "
"direktorijā.  C<mountpoint> ir direktorija, zem kuras mēģinām izveidot "
"direktoriju C<lost+found>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6747
msgid "mkmountpoint"
msgstr "mkmountpoint"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6749
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkmountpoint exemptpath\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkmountpoint exemptpath\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6751
msgid ""
"L</mkmountpoint> and L</rmmountpoint> are specialized calls that can be used "
"to create extra mountpoints before mounting the first filesystem."
msgstr ""
"L</mkmountpoint> un L</rmmountpoint> ir specializēti izsaukumi, ko var "
"izmantot papildu montēšanas punktu izveidei pirms pirmās failu sistēmas "
"montēšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6755 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10864
msgid ""
"These calls are I<only> necessary in some very limited circumstances, mainly "
"the case where you want to mount a mix of unrelated and/or read-only "
"filesystems together."
msgstr ""
"Šie izsaukumi ir nepieciešami I<tikai> dažos ļoti ierobežotos apstākļos, "
"galvenokārt gadījumā, kad vēlaties kopā montēt nesaistītu un/vai tikai "
"lasāmu failu sistēmu kombināciju."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6759 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10868
msgid ""
"For example, live CDs often contain a \"Russian doll\" nest of filesystems, "
"an ISO outer layer, with a squashfs image inside, with an ext2/3 image "
"inside that.  You can unpack this as follows in guestfish:"
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, live CD bieži satur failu sistēmu „matrjošku” — ISO ārējo slāni, "
"kurā ir squashfs attēls, kurā savukārt ir ext2/3 attēls.  Guestfish to var "
"izpakot šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6764 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10873
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" add-ro Fedora-11-i686-Live.iso\n"
" run\n"
" mkmountpoint /cd\n"
" mkmountpoint /sqsh\n"
" mkmountpoint /ext3fs\n"
" mount /dev/sda /cd\n"
" mount-loop /cd/LiveOS/squashfs.img /sqsh\n"
" mount-loop /sqsh/LiveOS/ext3fs.img /ext3fs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" add-ro Fedora-11-i686-Live.iso\n"
" run\n"
" mkmountpoint /cd\n"
" mkmountpoint /sqsh\n"
" mkmountpoint /ext3fs\n"
" mount /dev/sda /cd\n"
" mount-loop /cd/LiveOS/squashfs.img /sqsh\n"
" mount-loop /sqsh/LiveOS/ext3fs.img /ext3fs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6773 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10882
msgid "The inner filesystem is now unpacked under the /ext3fs mountpoint."
msgstr "Iekšējā failu sistēma tagad ir izpakota zem montēšanas punkta /ext3fs."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6775
msgid ""
"L</mkmountpoint> is not compatible with L</umount-all>.  You may get "
"unexpected errors if you try to mix these calls.  It is safest to manually "
"unmount filesystems and remove mountpoints after use."
msgstr ""
"L</mkmountpoint> nav saderīgs ar L</umount-all>.  Ja mēģināsiet jaukt šos "
"izsaukumus, varat saņemt negaidītas kļūdas.  Visdrošāk ir pēc lietošanas "
"manuāli atmontēt failu sistēmas un noņemt montēšanas punktus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6779
msgid ""
"L</umount-all> unmounts filesystems by sorting the paths longest first, so "
"for this to work for manual mountpoints, you must ensure that the innermost "
"mountpoints have the longest pathnames, as in the example code above."
msgstr ""
"L</umount-all> atmontē failu sistēmas, kārtojot ceļus no garākā, tāpēc, lai "
"tas darbotos ar manuāliem montēšanas punktiem, jānodrošina, ka "
"visdziļākajiem montēšanas punktiem ir garākie ceļu nosaukumi, kā iepriekšējā "
"koda piemērā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6784 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10893
msgid "For more details see L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=599503>"
msgstr "Sīkāk skatiet L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=599503>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6786
msgid ""
"Autosync [see L</set-autosync>, this is set by default on handles] can cause "
"L</umount-all> to be called when the handle is closed which can also trigger "
"these issues."
msgstr ""
"Automātiskā sinhronizācija [skatiet L</set-autosync>, rokturiem tā ir "
"iestatīta pēc noklusējuma] var izraisīt L</umount-all> izsaukšanu, kad "
"rokturis tiek aizvērts, kas arī var izraisīt šīs problēmas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6790
msgid "mknod"
msgstr "mknod"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6792
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mknod mode devmajor devminor path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mknod mode devmajor devminor path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6794 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10912
msgid ""
"This call creates block or character special devices, or named pipes "
"(FIFOs)."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums izveido bloku vai rakstzīmju speciālās ierīces vai nosauktus "
"kanālus (FIFO)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6797 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10915
msgid ""
"The C<mode> parameter should be the mode, using the standard constants.  "
"C<devmajor> and C<devminor> are the device major and minor numbers, only "
"used when creating block and character special devices."
msgstr ""
"Parametram C<mode> jābūt režīmam, izmantojot standarta konstantes.  "
"C<devmajor> un C<devminor> ir ierīces galvenais un mazākais numurs, ko "
"izmanto tikai, veidojot bloku un rakstzīmju speciālās ierīces."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6802
msgid ""
"Note that, just like L<mknod(2)>, the mode must be bitwise OR'd with "
"S_IFBLK, S_IFCHR, S_IFIFO or S_IFSOCK (otherwise this call just creates a "
"regular file).  These constants are available in the standard Linux header "
"files, or you can use L</mknod-b>, L</mknod-c> or L</mkfifo> which are "
"wrappers around this command which bitwise OR in the appropriate constant "
"for you."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, tāpat kā L<mknod(2)>, režīms bitu līmenī jāapvieno ar OR ar "
"S_IFBLK, S_IFCHR, S_IFIFO vai S_IFSOCK (citādi šis izsaukums vienkārši "
"izveido parastu failu).  Šīs konstantes ir pieejamas standarta Linux "
"galvenes failos, vai varat izmantot L</mknod-b>, L</mknod-c> vai L</mkfifo>, "
"kas ir ietinēji ap šo komandu un jūsu vietā bitu līmenī pievieno ar OR "
"atbilstošo konstanti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6815
msgid "mknod-b"
msgstr "mknod-b"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6817
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mknod-b mode devmajor devminor path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mknod-b mode devmajor devminor path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6819
msgid ""
"This call creates a block device node called C<path> with mode C<mode> and "
"device major/minor C<devmajor> and C<devminor>.  It is just a convenient "
"wrapper around L</mknod>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums izveido bloku ierīces mezglu C<path> ar režīmu C<mode> un "
"ierīces galveno/mazāko numuru C<devmajor> un C<devminor>.  Tas ir tikai ērts "
"ietinējs ap L</mknod>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6831
msgid "mknod-c"
msgstr "mknod-c"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6833
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mknod-c mode devmajor devminor path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mknod-c mode devmajor devminor path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6835
msgid ""
"This call creates a char device node called C<path> with mode C<mode> and "
"device major/minor C<devmajor> and C<devminor>.  It is just a convenient "
"wrapper around L</mknod>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums izveido rakstzīmju ierīces mezglu C<path> ar režīmu C<mode> un "
"ierīces galveno/mazāko numuru C<devmajor> un C<devminor>.  Tas ir tikai ērts "
"ietinējs ap L</mknod>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6847
msgid "mksquashfs"
msgstr "mksquashfs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6849
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mksquashfs path (filename|-) [compress:..] [excludes:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mksquashfs path (filename|-) [compress:..] [excludes:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6851 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11003
msgid "Create a squashfs filesystem for the specified C<path>."
msgstr "Izveidot squashfs failu sistēmu norādītajam C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6853 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11005
msgid ""
"The optional C<compress> flag controls compression.  If not given, then the "
"output compressed using C<gzip>.  Otherwise one of the following strings may "
"be given to select the compression type of the squashfs: C<gzip>, C<lzma>, "
"C<lzo>, C<lz4>, C<xz>."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātais karogs C<compress> kontrolē saspiešanu.  Ja nav norādīts, "
"izvade tiek saspiesta ar C<gzip>.  Citādi var norādīt vienu no šīm virknēm, "
"lai izvēlētos squashfs saspiešanas tipu: C<gzip>, C<lzma>, C<lzo>, C<lz4>, "
"C<xz>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6858 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9368
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9412 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11010
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15120 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15216
msgid "The other optional arguments are:"
msgstr "Pārējie neobligātie argumenti ir:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6862 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9416
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11014 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15220
msgid "C<excludes>"
msgstr "C<excludes>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6864 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9418
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11016 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15222
msgid "A list of wildcards.  Files are excluded if they match any of the wildcards."
msgstr ""
"Aizstājējzīmju saraksts.  Faili tiek izslēgti, ja tie atbilst kādai no "
"aizstājējzīmēm."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6869 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11021
msgid ""
"Please note that this API may fail when used to compress directories with "
"large files, such as the resulting squashfs will be over 3GB big."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka šī API var neizdoties, ja to izmanto direktoriju ar "
"lieliem failiem saspiešanai, piemēram, ja iegūtā squashfs būs lielāka par "
"3GB."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6876
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<squashfs>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<squashfs>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6879
msgid "mkswap"
msgstr "mkswap"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6881
msgid "mkswap-opts"
msgstr "mkswap-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6883
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkswap device [label:..] [uuid:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkswap device [label:..] [uuid:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6885 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11083
msgid "Create a Linux swap partition on C<device>."
msgstr "Izveidot Linux maiņatmiņas nodalījumu ierīcē C<device>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6887 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11085
msgid ""
"The option arguments C<label> and C<uuid> allow you to set the label and/or "
"UUID of the new swap partition."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātie argumenti C<label> un C<uuid> ļauj iestatīt jaunā maiņatmiņas "
"nodalījuma etiķeti un/vai UUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6892
msgid "mkswap-L"
msgstr "mkswap-L"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6894
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkswap-L label device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkswap-L label device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6896 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11128
msgid "Create a swap partition on C<device> with label C<label>."
msgstr "Izveidot maiņatmiņas nodalījumu ierīcē C<device> ar etiķeti C<label>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6898 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11130
msgid ""
"Note that you cannot attach a swap label to a block device "
"(eg. F</dev/sda>), just to a partition.  This appears to be a limitation of "
"the kernel or swap tools."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka maiņatmiņas etiķeti nevar piesaistīt bloku ierīcei (piem., "
"F</dev/sda>), tikai nodalījumam.  Šķiet, tas ir kodola vai maiņatmiņas rīku "
"ierobežojums."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6902 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6915
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</mkswap> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"mkswap>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6909
msgid "mkswap-U"
msgstr "mkswap-U"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6911
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkswap-U uuid device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkswap-U uuid device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6913 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11152
msgid "Create a swap partition on C<device> with UUID C<uuid>."
msgstr "Izveidot maiņatmiņas nodalījumu ierīcē C<device> ar UUID C<uuid>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6925
msgid "mkswap-file"
msgstr "mkswap-file"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6927
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkswap-file path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkswap-file path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6929 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11167
msgid "Create a swap file."
msgstr "Izveidot maiņatmiņas failu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6931
msgid ""
"This command just writes a swap file signature to an existing file.  To "
"create the file itself, use something like L</fallocate>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda tikai ieraksta maiņatmiņas faila parakstu esošā failā.  Paša "
"faila izveidei izmantojiet kaut ko līdzīgu L</fallocate>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6934
msgid "mktemp"
msgstr "mktemp"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6936
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mktemp tmpl [suffix:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mktemp tmpl [suffix:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6938 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11190
msgid ""
"This command creates a temporary file.  The C<tmpl> parameter should be a "
"full pathname for the temporary directory name with the final six characters "
"being \"XXXXXX\"."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izveido pagaidu failu.  Parametram C<tmpl> jābūt pilnam ceļa "
"nosaukumam pagaidu direktorijas nosaukumam, kura pēdējās sešas rakstzīmes ir "
"„XXXXXX”."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6946 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11198
msgid "The name of the temporary file that was created is returned."
msgstr "Tiek atgriezts izveidotā pagaidu faila nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6949 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11201
msgid "The temporary file is created with mode 0600 and is owned by root."
msgstr "Pagaidu fails tiek izveidots ar režīmu 0600, un tā īpašnieks ir root."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6952 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11204
msgid "The caller is responsible for deleting the temporary file after use."
msgstr "Izsaucējs ir atbildīgs par pagaidu faila dzēšanu pēc lietošanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6955 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11207
msgid ""
"If the optional C<suffix> parameter is given, then the suffix (eg. C<.txt>) "
"is appended to the temporary name."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādīts neobligātais parametrs C<suffix>, sufikss (piem., C<.txt>) tiek "
"pievienots pagaidu nosaukumam."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6958
msgid "See also: L</mkdtemp>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</mkdtemp>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6962
msgid "modprobe"
msgstr "modprobe"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6964
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" modprobe modulename\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" modprobe modulename\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6966 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11245
msgid "This loads a kernel module in the appliance."
msgstr "Tas ielādē kodola moduli palīgsistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6968
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<linuxmodules>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<linuxmodules>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6971
msgid "mount"
msgstr "mount"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6973
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6975
msgid ""
"Mount a guest disk at a position in the filesystem.  Block devices are named "
"F</dev/sda>, F</dev/sdb> and so on, as they were added to the guest.  If "
"those block devices contain partitions, they will have the usual names "
"(eg. F</dev/sda1>).  Also LVM F</dev/VG/LV>-style names can be used, or "
"‘mountable’ strings returned by L</list-filesystems> or "
"L</inspect-get-mountpoints>."
msgstr ""
"Montēt viesa disku pozīcijā failu sistēmā.  Bloku ierīces tiek nosauktas F</"
"dev/sda>, F</dev/sdb> un tā tālāk, secībā, kādā tās tika pievienotas "
"viesim.  Ja šajās bloku ierīcēs ir nodalījumi, tiem būs parastie nosaukumi "
"(piem., F</dev/sda1>).  Var izmantot arī LVM F</dev/VG/LV> stila nosaukumus "
"vai ‘montējamo objektu’ virknes, ko atgriež L</list-filesystems> vai L</"
"inspect-get-mountpoints>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6982 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11268
msgid ""
"The rules are the same as for L<mount(2)>: A filesystem must first be "
"mounted on F</> before others can be mounted.  Other filesystems can only be "
"mounted on directories which already exist."
msgstr ""
"Kārtulas ir tādas pašas kā L<mount(2)>: failu sistēma vispirms jāmontē F</>, "
"pirms var montēt citas.  Citas failu sistēmas var montēt tikai jau "
"eksistējošās direktorijās."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6987 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11273
msgid ""
"The mounted filesystem is writable, if we have sufficient permissions on the "
"underlying device."
msgstr ""
"Montētā failu sistēma ir rakstāma, ja mums ir pietiekamas atļaujas pamatā "
"esošajai ierīcei."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6990
msgid ""
"Before libguestfs 1.13.16, this call implicitly added the options C<sync> "
"and C<noatime>.  The C<sync> option greatly slowed writes and caused many "
"problems for users.  If your program might need to work with older versions "
"of libguestfs, use L</mount-options> instead (using an empty string for the "
"first parameter if you don't want any options)."
msgstr ""
"Pirms libguestfs 1.13.16 šis izsaukums netieši pievienoja opcijas C<sync> un "
"C<noatime>.  Opcija C<sync> ievērojami palēnināja rakstīšanu un radīja daudz "
"problēmu lietotājiem.  Ja jūsu programmai var nākties strādāt ar vecākām "
"libguestfs versijām, tā vietā izmantojiet L</mount-options> (pirmajam "
"parametram izmantojot tukšu virkni, ja nevēlaties nekādas opcijas)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6997
msgid "mount-9p"
msgstr "mount-9p"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:6999
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount-9p mounttag mountpoint [options:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount-9p mounttag mountpoint [options:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7013
msgid "mount-local"
msgstr "mount-local"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7015
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount-local localmountpoint [readonly:true|false] [options:..] "
"[cachetimeout:N] [debugcalls:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount-local localmountpoint [readonly:true|false] [options:..] "
"[cachetimeout:N] [debugcalls:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7017 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11357
msgid ""
"This call exports the libguestfs-accessible filesystem to a local mountpoint "
"(directory) called C<localmountpoint>.  Ordinary reads and writes to files "
"and directories under C<localmountpoint> are redirected through libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums eksportē libguestfs pieejamo failu sistēmu uz lokālu "
"montēšanas punktu (direktoriju) C<localmountpoint>.  Parastā lasīšana un "
"rakstīšana failos un direktorijās zem C<localmountpoint> tiek novirzīta caur "
"libguestfs."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7022 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11362
msgid ""
"If the optional C<readonly> flag is set to true, then writes to the "
"filesystem return error C<EROFS>."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<readonly> iestatīts uz true, rakstīšana failu "
"sistēmā atgriež kļūdu C<EROFS>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7025 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11365
msgid ""
"C<options> is a comma-separated list of mount options.  See L<guestmount(1)> "
"for some useful options."
msgstr ""
"C<options> ir ar komatiem atdalīts montēšanas opciju saraksts.  Dažas "
"noderīgas opcijas skatiet L<guestmount(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7028 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11368
msgid ""
"C<cachetimeout> sets the timeout (in seconds) for cached directory entries.  "
"The default is 60 seconds.  See L<guestmount(1)> for further information."
msgstr ""
"C<cachetimeout> iestata kešoto direktoriju ierakstu noildzi (sekundēs).  "
"Noklusējums ir 60 sekundes.  Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<guestmount(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7032 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11372
msgid ""
"If C<debugcalls> is set to true, then additional debugging information is "
"generated for every FUSE call."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<debugcalls> iestatīts uz true, katram FUSE izsaukumam tiek ģenerēta "
"papildu atkļūdošanas informācija."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7035
msgid ""
"When L</mount-local> returns, the filesystem is ready, but is not processing "
"requests (access to it will block).  You have to call L</mount-local-run> to "
"run the main loop."
msgstr ""
"Kad L</mount-local> atgriežas, failu sistēma ir gatava, bet neapstrādā "
"pieprasījumus (piekļuve tai bloķēs).  Lai izpildītu galveno ciklu, jāizsauc "
"L</mount-local-run>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7039 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7062
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9688 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11379
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11427 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15670
msgid "See L<guestfs(3)/MOUNT LOCAL> for full documentation."
msgstr "Pilnu dokumentāciju skatiet L<guestfs(3)/LOKĀLĀ MONTĒŠANA>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7043
msgid "mount-local-run"
msgstr "mount-local-run"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7045
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount-local-run\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount-local-run\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7047 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11412
msgid "Run the main loop which translates kernel calls to libguestfs calls."
msgstr ""
"Izpildīt galveno ciklu, kas pārvērš kodola izsaukumus libguestfs izsaukumos."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7050
msgid ""
"This should only be called after L</mount-local> returns successfully.  The "
"call will not return until the filesystem is unmounted."
msgstr ""
"To jāizsauc tikai pēc tam, kad L</mount-local> ir veiksmīgi atgriezies.  "
"Izsaukums neatgriezīsies, kamēr failu sistēma nav atmontēta."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7054 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11419
msgid ""
"B<Note> you must I<not> make concurrent libguestfs calls on the same handle "
"from another thread."
msgstr ""
"B<Ņemiet vērā>, ka no cita pavediena tam pašam rokturim I<nedrīkst> veikt "
"vienlaicīgus libguestfs izsaukumus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7057
msgid ""
"You may call this from a different thread than the one which called "
"L</mount-local>, subject to the usual rules for threads and libguestfs (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/MULTIPLE HANDLES AND MULTIPLE THREADS>)."
msgstr ""
"To var izsaukt no cita pavediena, nevis tā, kas izsauca L</mount-local>, "
"ievērojot parastās pavedienu un libguestfs kārtulas (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/"
"VAIRĀKI ROKTURI UN VAIRĀKI PAVEDIENI>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7064
msgid "mount-loop"
msgstr "mount-loop"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7066
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount-loop file mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount-loop file mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7068 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11440
msgid ""
"This command lets you mount F<file> (a filesystem image in a file) on a "
"mount point.  It is entirely equivalent to the command C<mount -o loop file "
"mountpoint>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ļauj montēt F<file> (failu sistēmas attēlu failā) montēšanas "
"punktā.  Tā ir pilnībā līdzvērtīga komandai C<mount -o loop file mountpoint>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7072
msgid "mount-options"
msgstr "mount-options"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7074
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount-options options mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount-options options mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7076
msgid ""
"This is the same as the L</mount> command, but it allows you to set the "
"mount options as for the L<mount(8)> I<-o> flag."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas komanda L</mount>, bet ļauj iestatīt montēšanas opcijas "
"kā L<mount(8)> karogam I<-o>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7080 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11460
msgid ""
"If the C<options> parameter is an empty string, then no options are passed "
"(all options default to whatever the filesystem uses)."
msgstr ""
"Ja parametrs C<options> ir tukša virkne, opcijas netiek nodotas (visas "
"opcijas ir failu sistēmas noklusējuma)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7084
msgid "mount-ro"
msgstr "mount-ro"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7086
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount-ro mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount-ro mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7088
msgid ""
"This is the same as the L</mount> command, but it mounts the filesystem with "
"the read-only (I<-o ro>) flag."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas komanda L</mount>, bet montē failu sistēmu ar tikai "
"lasīšanas (I<-o ro>) karogu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7091
msgid "mount-vfs"
msgstr "mount-vfs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7093
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount-vfs options vfstype mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount-vfs options vfstype mountable mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7095
msgid ""
"This is the same as the L</mount> command, but it allows you to set both the "
"mount options and the vfstype as for the L<mount(8)> I<-o> and I<-t> flags."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas komanda L</mount>, bet ļauj iestatīt gan montēšanas "
"opcijas, gan vfstype kā L<mount(8)> karogiem I<-o> un I<-t>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7099
msgid "mountable-device"
msgstr "mountable-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mountable-device mountable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mountable-device mountable\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7103 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11505
msgid ""
"Returns the device name of a mountable. In quite a lot of cases, the "
"mountable is the device name."
msgstr ""
"Atgriež montējamā objekta ierīces nosaukumu. Diezgan daudzos gadījumos "
"montējamais objekts ir ierīces nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7106
msgid ""
"However this doesn't apply for btrfs subvolumes, where the mountable is a "
"combination of both the device name and the subvolume path (see also "
"L</mountable-subvolume> to extract the subvolume path of the mountable if "
"any)."
msgstr ""
"Tomēr tas neattiecas uz btrfs apakšsējumiem, kur montējamais objekts ir gan "
"ierīces nosaukuma, gan apakšsējuma ceļa kombinācija (skatīt arī L</mountable-"
"subvolume>, lai izgūtu montējamā objekta apakšsējuma ceļu, ja tāds ir)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7111
msgid "mountable-subvolume"
msgstr "mountable-subvolume"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7113
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mountable-subvolume mountable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mountable-subvolume mountable\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7115
msgid ""
"Returns the subvolume path of a mountable. Btrfs subvolumes mountables are a "
"combination of both the device name and the subvolume path (see also "
"L</mountable-device> to extract the device of the mountable)."
msgstr ""
"Atgriež montējamā objekta apakšsējuma ceļu. Btrfs apakšsējumu montējamie "
"objekti ir gan ierīces nosaukuma, gan apakšsējuma ceļa kombinācija (skatīt "
"arī L</mountable-device>, lai izgūtu montējamā objekta ierīci)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7120 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11529
msgid ""
"If the mountable does not represent a btrfs subvolume, then this function "
"fails and the C<errno> is set to C<EINVAL>."
msgstr ""
"Ja montējamais objekts neattēlo btrfs apakšsējumu, šī funkcija neizdodas, un "
"C<errno> tiek iestatīts uz C<EINVAL>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7123
msgid "mountpoints"
msgstr "mountpoints"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mountpoints\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mountpoints\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7127
msgid ""
"This call is similar to L</mounts>.  That call returns a list of devices.  "
"This one returns a hash table (map) of device name to directory where the "
"device is mounted."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ir līdzīgs L</mounts>.  Tas izsaukums atgriež ierīču "
"sarakstu.  Šis atgriež jaucējtabulu (karti) no ierīces nosaukuma uz "
"direktoriju, kur ierīce ir montēta."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7131
msgid "mounts"
msgstr "mounts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7133
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mounts\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mounts\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7135 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11559
msgid ""
"This returns the list of currently mounted filesystems.  It returns the list "
"of devices (eg. F</dev/sda1>, F</dev/VG/LV>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež pašlaik montēto failu sistēmu sarakstu.  Tas atgriež ierīču "
"sarakstu (piem., F</dev/sda1>, F</dev/VG/LV>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7138 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11562
msgid "Some internal mounts are not shown."
msgstr "Daži iekšējie montējumi netiek rādīti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7140
msgid "See also: L</mountpoints>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</mountpoints>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7142
msgid "mv"
msgstr "mv"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7144
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mv src dest\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mv src dest\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7146 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11579
msgid ""
"This moves a file from C<src> to C<dest> where C<dest> is either a "
"destination filename or destination directory."
msgstr ""
"Tas pārvieto failu no C<src> uz C<dest>, kur C<dest> ir vai nu mērķa faila "
"nosaukums, vai mērķa direktorija."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7149
msgid "See also: L</rename>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</rename>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7151
msgid "nr-devices"
msgstr "nr-devices"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7153
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" nr-devices\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" nr-devices\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7155
msgid ""
"This returns the number of whole block devices that were added.  This is the "
"same as the number of devices that would be returned if you called "
"L</list-devices>."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež pievienoto veselo bloku ierīču skaitu.  Tas ir tāds pats kā "
"ierīču skaits, kas tiktu atgriezts, ja izsauktu L</list-devices>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7159
msgid ""
"To find out the maximum number of devices that could be added, call "
"L</max-disks>."
msgstr ""
"Lai noskaidrotu maksimālo ierīču skaitu, ko varētu pievienot, izsauciet L</"
"max-disks>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7162
msgid "ntfs-3g-probe"
msgstr "ntfs-3g-probe"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7164
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfs-3g-probe true|false device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfs-3g-probe true|false device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7166 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11611
msgid ""
"This command runs the L<ntfs-3g.probe(8)> command which probes an NTFS "
"C<device> for mountability.  (Not all NTFS volumes can be mounted "
"read-write, and some cannot be mounted at all)."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izpilda komandu L<ntfs-3g.probe(8)>, kas zondē NTFS ierīci "
"C<device> attiecībā uz montējamību.  (Ne visus NTFS sējumus var montēt "
"lasīšanai un rakstīšanai, un dažus nevar montēt vispār.)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7170 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11615
msgid ""
"C<rw> is a boolean flag.  Set it to true if you want to test if the volume "
"can be mounted read-write.  Set it to false if you want to test if the "
"volume can be mounted read-only."
msgstr ""
"C<rw> ir Būla karogs.  Iestatiet to uz true, ja vēlaties pārbaudīt, vai "
"sējumu var montēt lasīšanai un rakstīšanai.  Iestatiet to uz false, ja "
"vēlaties pārbaudīt, vai sējumu var montēt tikai lasīšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7174 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11619
msgid ""
"The return value is an integer which C<0> if the operation would succeed, or "
"some non-zero value documented in the L<ntfs-3g.probe(8)> manual page."
msgstr ""
"Atgriešanas vērtība ir vesels skaitlis, kas ir C<0>, ja darbība izdotos, vai "
"kāda vērtība, kas nav nulle, kā dokumentēts L<ntfs-3g.probe(8)> "
"rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7178 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7202
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7230 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7256
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7275
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<ntfs3g>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<ntfs3g>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7181
msgid "ntfs-chmod"
msgstr "ntfs-chmod"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7183
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfs-chmod device mode path [recursive:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfs-chmod device mode path [recursive:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7185 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11646
msgid ""
"Change file permissions on an NTFS filesystem with a chmod-style permission "
"mask, using L<ntfssecaudit(8)>. Only numeric modes are supported."
msgstr ""
"Mainīt failu atļaujas NTFS failu sistēmā ar chmod stila atļauju masku, "
"izmantojot L<ntfssecaudit(8)>. Tiek atbalstīti tikai skaitliski režīmi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7193 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11654
msgid ""
"The C<device> parameter is the NTFS partition device (eg. C</dev/sda5>).  "
"This must be unmounted.  The C<mode> parameter is the permission mode "
"(eg. C<0744>).  The C<path> parameter is the file or directory path within "
"the filesystem.  If the optional C<recursive> flag is set, directory "
"permissions are set recursively."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<device> ir NTFS nodalījuma ierīce (piem., C</dev/sda5>).  Tai "
"jābūt atmontētai.  Parametrs C<mode> ir atļauju režīms (piem., C<0744>).  "
"Parametrs C<path> ir faila vai direktorijas ceļš failu sistēmā.  Ja "
"iestatīts neobligātais karogs C<recursive>, direktoriju atļaujas tiek "
"iestatītas rekursīvi."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7205
msgid "ntfscat-i"
msgstr "ntfscat-i"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7207
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfscat-i device inode (filename|-)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfscat-i device inode (filename|-)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7209 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11702
msgid ""
"Download a file given its inode from a NTFS filesystem and save it as "
"F<filename> on the local machine."
msgstr ""
"Lejupielādēt failu pēc tā inode no NTFS failu sistēmas un saglabāt to kā "
"F<filename> lokālajā datorā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7212 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11705
msgid ""
"This allows to download some otherwise inaccessible files such as the ones "
"within the C<$Extend> folder."
msgstr ""
"Tas ļauj lejupielādēt dažus citādi nepieejamus failus, piemēram, tos, kas "
"atrodas mapē C<$Extend>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7215 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11708
msgid ""
"The filesystem from which to extract the file must be unmounted, otherwise "
"the call will fail."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēmai, no kuras izgūt failu, jābūt atmontētai, citādi izsaukums "
"neizdosies."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7220
msgid "ntfsclone-in"
msgstr "ntfsclone-in"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7222
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfsclone-in (backupfile|-) device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfsclone-in (backupfile|-) device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7224
msgid ""
"Restore the C<backupfile> (from a previous call to L</ntfsclone-out>) to "
"C<device>, overwriting any existing contents of this device."
msgstr ""
"Atjaunot C<backupfile> (no iepriekšēja L</ntfsclone-out> izsaukuma) uz "
"C<device>, pārrakstot jebkuru esošo šīs ierīces saturu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7233
msgid "ntfsclone-out"
msgstr "ntfsclone-out"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7235
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfsclone-out device (backupfile|-) [metadataonly:true|false] "
"[rescue:true|false] [ignorefscheck:true|false] "
"[preservetimestamps:true|false] [force:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfsclone-out device (backupfile|-) [metadataonly:true|false] "
"[rescue:true|false] [ignorefscheck:true|false] "
"[preservetimestamps:true|false] [force:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7237 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11757
msgid ""
"Stream the NTFS filesystem C<device> to the local file C<backupfile>.  The "
"format used for the backup file is a special format used by the "
"L<ntfsclone(8)> tool."
msgstr ""
"Straumēt NTFS failu sistēmu C<device> uz lokālo failu C<backupfile>.  "
"Dublējuma faila formāts ir īpašs formāts, ko izmanto rīks L<ntfsclone(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7241 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11761
msgid ""
"If the optional C<metadataonly> flag is true, then I<only> the metadata is "
"saved, losing all the user data (this is useful for diagnosing some "
"filesystem problems)."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātais karogs C<metadataonly> ir true, tiek saglabāti I<tikai> "
"metadati, zaudējot visus lietotāja datus (tas noder dažu failu sistēmas "
"problēmu diagnosticēšanai)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7245 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11765
msgid ""
"The optional C<rescue>, C<ignorefscheck>, C<preservetimestamps> and C<force> "
"flags have precise meanings detailed in the L<ntfsclone(8)> man page."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātajiem karogiem C<rescue>, C<ignorefscheck>, C<preservetimestamps> "
"un C<force> ir precīzas nozīmes, kas sīki aprakstītas L<ntfsclone(8)> "
"rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7249
msgid "Use L</ntfsclone-in> to restore the file back to a libguestfs device."
msgstr ""
"Lai atjaunotu failu atpakaļ libguestfs ierīcē, izmantojiet L</ntfsclone-in>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7259
msgid "ntfsfix"
msgstr "ntfsfix"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7261
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfsfix device [clearbadsectors:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfsfix device [clearbadsectors:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7263 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11817
msgid ""
"This command repairs some fundamental NTFS inconsistencies, resets the NTFS "
"journal file, and schedules an NTFS consistency check for the first boot "
"into Windows."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda labo dažas fundamentālas NTFS nekonsekvences, atiestata NTFS "
"žurnāla failu un ieplāno NTFS konsekvences pārbaudi pirmajā sāknēšanā "
"Windows."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7267 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11821
msgid ""
"This is I<not> an equivalent of Windows C<chkdsk>.  It does I<not> scan the "
"filesystem for inconsistencies."
msgstr ""
"Tas I<nav> Windows C<chkdsk> ekvivalents.  Tas I<neskenē> failu sistēmu, "
"meklējot nekonsekvences."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7270 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11824
msgid ""
"The optional C<clearbadsectors> flag clears the list of bad sectors.  This "
"is useful after cloning a disk with bad sectors to a new disk."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātais karogs C<clearbadsectors> notīra bojāto sektoru sarakstu.  Tas "
"noder pēc diska ar bojātiem sektoriem klonēšanas uz jaunu disku."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7278
msgid "ntfsresize"
msgstr "ntfsresize"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7280
msgid "ntfsresize-opts"
msgstr "ntfsresize-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7282
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfsresize device [size:N] [force:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfsresize device [size:N] [force:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7284 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11884
msgid ""
"This command resizes an NTFS filesystem, expanding or shrinking it to the "
"size of the underlying device."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda maina NTFS failu sistēmas izmēru, paplašinot vai samazinot to "
"līdz pamatā esošās ierīces izmēram."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7293 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11893
msgid ""
"The new size (in bytes) of the filesystem.  If omitted, the filesystem is "
"resized to fit the container (eg. partition)."
msgstr ""
"Jaunais failu sistēmas izmērs (baitos).  Ja izlaists, failu sistēmas izmērs "
"tiek mainīts, lai tā ietilptu konteinerā (piem., nodalījumā)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7296 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9518
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11896 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15394
msgid "C<force>"
msgstr "C<force>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7298 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11898
msgid ""
"If this option is true, then force the resize of the filesystem even if the "
"filesystem is marked as requiring a consistency check."
msgstr ""
"Ja šī opcija ir true, piespiest failu sistēmas izmēra maiņu pat tad, ja "
"failu sistēma ir atzīmēta kā tāda, kurai nepieciešama konsekvences pārbaude."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7301
msgid ""
"After the resize operation, the filesystem is always marked as requiring a "
"consistency check (for safety).  You have to boot into Windows to perform "
"this check and clear this condition.  If you I<don't> set the C<force> "
"option then it is not possible to call L</ntfsresize> multiple times on a "
"single filesystem without booting into Windows between each resize."
msgstr ""
"Pēc izmēra maiņas darbības failu sistēma vienmēr tiek atzīmēta kā tāda, "
"kurai nepieciešama konsekvences pārbaude (drošības labad).  Lai veiktu šo "
"pārbaudi un notīrītu šo stāvokli, jāsāknē Windows.  Ja I<neiestatāt> opciju "
"C<force>, L</ntfsresize> nav iespējams izsaukt vairākas reizes vienai failu "
"sistēmai, starp katru izmēra maiņu nesāknējot Windows."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7310 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11910
msgid "See also L<ntfsresize(8)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<ntfsresize(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7314 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7331
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<ntfsprogs>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<ntfsprogs>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7317
msgid "ntfsresize-size"
msgstr "ntfsresize-size"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7319
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ntfsresize-size device size\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ntfsresize-size device size\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7321
msgid ""
"This command is the same as L</ntfsresize> except that it allows you to "
"specify the new size (in bytes) explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tāda pati kā L</ntfsresize>, izņemot to, ka tā ļauj eksplicīti "
"norādīt jauno izmēru (baitos)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7324
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</ntfsresize> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"ntfsresize>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7334
msgid "parse-environment"
msgstr "parse-environment"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7336
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" parse-environment\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" parse-environment\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7338 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11970
msgid ""
"Parse the program’s environment and set flags in the handle accordingly.  "
"For example if C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1> then the ‘verbose’ flag is set in the "
"handle."
msgstr ""
"Parsēt programmas vidi un atbilstoši iestatīt karogus rokturī.  Piemēram, ja "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1>, rokturī tiek iestatīts karogs ‘verbose’."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7342
msgid ""
"I<Most programs do not need to call this>.  It is done implicitly when you "
"call L</create>."
msgstr ""
"I<Lielākajai daļai programmu tas nav jāizsauc>.  Tas tiek darīts netieši, "
"kad izsaucat L</create>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7345
msgid ""
"See L<guestfs(3)/ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES> for a list of environment variables "
"that can affect libguestfs handles.  See also "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_create_flags>, and L</parse-environment-list>."
msgstr ""
"Vides mainīgo sarakstu, kas var ietekmēt libguestfs rokturus, skatiet "
"L<guestfs(3)/VIDES MAINĪGIE>.  Skatīt arī L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_create_flags> "
"un L</parse-environment-list>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7350
msgid "parse-environment-list"
msgstr "parse-environment-list"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7352
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" parse-environment-list 'environment ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" parse-environment-list 'environment ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7354 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11992
msgid ""
"Parse the list of strings in the argument C<environment> and set flags in "
"the handle accordingly.  For example if C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1> is a string in "
"the list, then the ‘verbose’ flag is set in the handle."
msgstr ""
"Parsēt virkņu sarakstu argumentā C<environment> un atbilstoši iestatīt "
"karogus rokturī.  Piemēram, ja sarakstā ir virkne C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1>, "
"rokturī tiek iestatīts karogs ‘verbose’."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7359
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</parse-environment> except that it parses an explicit "
"list of strings instead of the program's environment."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</parse-environment>, izņemot to, ka tas parsē "
"eksplicītu virkņu sarakstu, nevis programmas vidi."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7363
msgid "part-add"
msgstr "part-add"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7365
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-add device prlogex startsect endsect\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-add device prlogex startsect endsect\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7367
msgid ""
"This command adds a partition to C<device>.  If there is no partition table "
"on the device, call L</part-init> first."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda pievieno nodalījumu ierīcei C<device>.  Ja ierīcē nav nodalījumu "
"tabulas, vispirms izsauciet L</part-init>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7370 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12017
msgid ""
"The C<prlogex> parameter is the type of partition.  Normally you should pass "
"C<p> or C<primary> here, but MBR partition tables also support C<l> (or "
"C<logical>) and C<e> (or C<extended>) partition types."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<prlogex> ir nodalījuma tips.  Parasti šeit jānodod C<p> vai "
"C<primary>, bet MBR nodalījumu tabulas atbalsta arī nodalījumu tipus C<l> "
"(vai C<logical>) un C<e> (vai C<extended>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7375 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12022
msgid ""
"C<startsect> and C<endsect> are the start and end of the partition in "
"I<sectors>.  C<endsect> may be negative, which means it counts backwards "
"from the end of the disk (C<-1> is the last sector)."
msgstr ""
"C<startsect> un C<endsect> ir nodalījuma sākums un beigas I<sektoros>.  "
"C<endsect> var būt negatīvs, kas nozīmē, ka tas tiek skaitīts atpakaļ no "
"diska beigām (C<-1> ir pēdējais sektors)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7379
msgid ""
"Creating a partition which covers the whole disk is not so easy.  Use "
"L</part-disk> to do that."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījuma izveide, kas aptver visu disku, nav tik vienkārša.  Tam "
"izmantojiet L</part-disk>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7382
msgid "part-del"
msgstr "part-del"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7384
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-del device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-del device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7386 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12040
msgid "This command deletes the partition numbered C<partnum> on C<device>."
msgstr "Šī komanda dzēš nodalījumu ar numuru C<partnum> ierīcē C<device>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7388 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12042
msgid ""
"Note that in the case of MBR partitioning, deleting an extended partition "
"also deletes any logical partitions it contains."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka MBR nodalīšanas gadījumā paplašinātā nodalījuma dzēšana dzēš "
"arī visus tajā esošos loģiskos nodalījumus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7392
msgid "part-disk"
msgstr "part-disk"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7394
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-disk device parttype\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-disk device parttype\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7396
msgid ""
"This command is simply a combination of L</part-init> followed by "
"L</part-add> to create a single primary partition covering the whole disk."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir vienkārši L</part-init> un tam sekojoša L</part-add> "
"kombinācija, lai izveidotu vienu primāro nodalījumu, kas aptver visu disku."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7400
msgid ""
"C<parttype> is the partition table type, usually C<mbr> or C<gpt>, but other "
"possible values are described in L</part-init>."
msgstr ""
"C<parttype> ir nodalījumu tabulas tips, parasti C<mbr> vai C<gpt>, bet citas "
"iespējamās vērtības aprakstītas pie L</part-init>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7403
msgid "part-expand-gpt"
msgstr "part-expand-gpt"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7405
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-expand-gpt device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-expand-gpt device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7407 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12074
msgid ""
"Move backup GPT data structures to the end of the disk.  This is useful in "
"case of in-place image expand since disk space after backup GPT header is "
"not usable.  This is equivalent to C<sgdisk -e>."
msgstr ""
"Pārvietot GPT rezerves datu struktūras uz diska beigām.  Tas noder attēla "
"paplašināšanas uz vietas gadījumā, jo diska vieta aiz GPT rezerves galvenes "
"nav izmantojama.  Tas ir līdzvērtīgi C<sgdisk -e>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7412 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12079
msgid "See also L<sgdisk(8)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<sgdisk(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7414
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<gdisk>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<gdisk>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7417
msgid "part-get-bootable"
msgstr "part-get-bootable"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7419
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-bootable device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-bootable device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7421 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12095
msgid ""
"This command returns true if the partition C<partnum> on C<device> has the "
"bootable flag set."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atgriež true, ja nodalījumam C<partnum> ierīcē C<device> ir "
"iestatīts sāknējamības karogs."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7424
msgid "See also L</part-set-bootable>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</part-set-bootable>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7426
msgid "part-get-disk-guid"
msgstr "part-get-disk-guid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7428
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-disk-guid device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-disk-guid device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7430 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12110
msgid ""
"Return the disk identifier (GUID) of a GPT-partitioned C<device>.  Behaviour "
"is undefined for other partition types."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt GPT nodalītas ierīces C<device> diska identifikatoru (GUID).  "
"Citiem nodalījumu tipiem uzvedība nav definēta."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7433
msgid "part-get-gpt-attributes"
msgstr "part-get-gpt-attributes"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7435
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-gpt-attributes device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-gpt-attributes device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7437 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12125
msgid ""
"Return the attribute flags of numbered GPT partition C<partnum>.  An error "
"is returned for MBR partitions."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt numurētā GPT nodalījuma C<partnum> atribūtu karogus.  MBR "
"nodalījumiem tiek atgriezta kļūda."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7440
msgid "part-get-gpt-guid"
msgstr "part-get-gpt-guid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7442
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-gpt-guid device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-gpt-guid device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7444 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12139
msgid "Return the GUID of numbered GPT partition C<partnum>."
msgstr "Atgriezt numurētā GPT nodalījuma C<partnum> GUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7446
msgid "part-get-gpt-type"
msgstr "part-get-gpt-type"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7448
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-gpt-type device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-gpt-type device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7450 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12153
msgid "Return the type GUID of numbered GPT partition C<partnum>."
msgstr "Atgriezt numurētā GPT nodalījuma C<partnum> tipa GUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7452
msgid "part-get-mbr-id"
msgstr "part-get-mbr-id"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7454
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-mbr-id device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-mbr-id device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7456 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12167
msgid ""
"Returns the MBR type byte (also known as the ID byte) from the numbered "
"partition C<partnum>."
msgstr ""
"Atgriež MBR tipa baitu (saukts arī par ID baitu) no numurētā nodalījuma "
"C<partnum>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7459 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7682
msgid ""
"Note that only MBR (old DOS-style) partitions have type bytes.  You will get "
"undefined results for other partition table types (see "
"L</part-get-parttype>)."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka tipa baiti ir tikai MBR (vecā DOS stila) nodalījumiem.  "
"Citiem nodalījumu tabulu tipiem saņemsiet nedefinētus rezultātus (skatiet L</"
"part-get-parttype>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7463
msgid "part-get-mbr-part-type"
msgstr "part-get-mbr-part-type"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7465
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-mbr-part-type device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-mbr-part-type device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7467 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12185
msgid ""
"This returns the partition type of an MBR partition numbered C<partnum> on "
"device C<device>."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež MBR nodalījuma ar numuru C<partnum> ierīcē C<device> nodalījuma "
"tipu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7470 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12188
msgid "It returns C<primary>, C<logical>, or C<extended>."
msgstr "Tas atgriež C<primary>, C<logical> vai C<extended>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7472
msgid "part-get-name"
msgstr "part-get-name"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7474
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-name device partnum\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-name device partnum\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7476 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12202
msgid ""
"This gets the partition name on partition numbered C<partnum> on device "
"C<device>.  Note that partitions are numbered from 1."
msgstr ""
"Tas iegūst nodalījuma nosaukumu nodalījumam ar numuru C<partnum> ierīcē "
"C<device>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka nodalījumi tiek numurēti no 1."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7479 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12205
msgid ""
"The partition name can only be read on certain types of partition table.  "
"This works on C<gpt> but not on C<mbr> partitions."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījuma nosaukumu var nolasīt tikai noteiktu tipu nodalījumu tabulās.  "
"Tas darbojas ar C<gpt>, bet ne ar C<mbr> nodalījumiem."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7482
msgid "part-get-parttype"
msgstr "part-get-parttype"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7484
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-get-parttype device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-get-parttype device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7486 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12219
msgid ""
"This command examines the partition table on C<device> and returns the "
"partition table type (format) being used."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda pārbauda nodalījumu tabulu ierīcē C<device> un atgriež izmantoto "
"nodalījumu tabulas tipu (formātu)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7489
msgid ""
"Common return values include: C<msdos> (a DOS/Windows style MBR partition "
"table), C<gpt> (a GPT/EFI-style partition table).  Other values are "
"possible, although unusual.  See L</part-init> for a full list."
msgstr ""
"Bieži sastopamās atgriešanas vērtības ietver: C<msdos> (DOS/Windows stila "
"MBR nodalījumu tabula), C<gpt> (GPT/EFI stila nodalījumu tabula).  "
"Iespējamas arī citas vērtības, lai gan neparastas.  Pilnu sarakstu skatiet "
"L</part-init>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7494
msgid "part-init"
msgstr "part-init"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7496
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-init device parttype\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-init device parttype\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7498 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12239
msgid ""
"This creates an empty partition table on C<device> of one of the partition "
"types listed below.  Usually C<parttype> should be either C<msdos> or C<gpt> "
"(for large disks)."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido tukšu nodalījumu tabulu ierīcē C<device> ar vienu no tālāk "
"uzskaitītajiem nodalījumu tipiem.  Parasti C<parttype> jābūt vai nu C<msdos>"
", vai C<gpt> (lieliem diskiem)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7502
msgid ""
"Initially there are no partitions.  Following this, you should call "
"L</part-add> for each partition required."
msgstr ""
"Sākotnēji nodalījumu nav.  Pēc tam katram vajadzīgajam nodalījumam jāizsauc "
"L</part-add>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7505 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12246
msgid "Possible values for C<parttype> are:"
msgstr "Iespējamās C<parttype> vērtības ir:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7509 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12250
msgid "C<efi>"
msgstr "C<efi>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7511 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12252
msgid "C<gpt>"
msgstr "C<gpt>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7513 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12254
msgid "Intel EFI / GPT partition table."
msgstr "Intel EFI / GPT nodalījumu tabula."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7515 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12256
msgid ""
"This is recommended for >= 2 TB partitions that will be accessed from Linux "
"and Intel-based Mac OS X.  It also has limited backwards compatibility with "
"the C<mbr> format."
msgstr ""
"To ieteicams izmantot nodalījumiem >= 2 TB, kuriem piekļūs no Linux un uz "
"Intel balstīta Mac OS X.  Tai ir arī ierobežota atpakaļsaderība ar formātu "
"C<mbr>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7519 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12260
msgid "C<mbr>"
msgstr "C<mbr>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7521 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12262
msgid "C<msdos>"
msgstr "C<msdos>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7523 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12264
msgid ""
"The standard PC \"Master Boot Record\" (MBR) format used by MS-DOS and "
"Windows.  This partition type will B<only> work for device sizes up to 2 "
"TB.  For large disks we recommend using C<gpt>."
msgstr ""
"Standarta PC „Master Boot Record” (MBR) formāts, ko izmanto MS-DOS un "
"Windows.  Šis nodalījuma tips darbosies B<tikai> ierīcēm līdz 2 TB.  Lieliem "
"diskiem iesakām izmantot C<gpt>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7530 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12271
msgid "Other partition table types that may work but are not supported include:"
msgstr ""
"Citi nodalījumu tabulu tipi, kas var darboties, bet netiek atbalstīti, "
"ietver:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7535 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12276
msgid "C<aix>"
msgstr "C<aix>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7537 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12278
msgid "AIX disk labels."
msgstr "AIX disku etiķetes."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7539 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12280
msgid "C<amiga>"
msgstr "C<amiga>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7541 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12282
msgid "C<rdb>"
msgstr "C<rdb>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7543 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12284
msgid "Amiga \"Rigid Disk Block\" format."
msgstr "Amiga „Rigid Disk Block” formāts."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7545 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12286
msgid "C<bsd>"
msgstr "C<bsd>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7547 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12288
msgid "BSD disk labels."
msgstr "BSD disku etiķetes."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7549 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12290
msgid "C<dasd>"
msgstr "C<dasd>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7551 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12292
msgid "DASD, used on IBM mainframes."
msgstr "DASD, ko izmanto IBM lieldatoros."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7553 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12294
msgid "C<dvh>"
msgstr "C<dvh>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7555 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12296
msgid "MIPS/SGI volumes."
msgstr "MIPS/SGI sējumi."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7557 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12298
msgid "C<mac>"
msgstr "C<mac>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7559 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12300
msgid "Old Mac partition format.  Modern Macs use C<gpt>."
msgstr "Vecais Mac nodalījumu formāts.  Modernie Mac izmanto C<gpt>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7561 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12302
msgid "C<pc98>"
msgstr "C<pc98>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7563 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12304
msgid "NEC PC-98 format, common in Japan apparently."
msgstr "NEC PC-98 formāts, acīmredzot izplatīts Japānā."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7565 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12306
msgid "C<sun>"
msgstr "C<sun>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7567 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12308
msgid "Sun disk labels."
msgstr "Sun disku etiķetes."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7571
msgid "part-list"
msgstr "part-list"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7573
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-list device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-list device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7575 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12322
msgid ""
"This command parses the partition table on C<device> and returns the list of "
"partitions found."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda parsē nodalījumu tabulu ierīcē C<device> un atgriež atrasto "
"nodalījumu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7578 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12325
msgid "The fields in the returned structure are:"
msgstr "Atgrieztās struktūras lauki ir:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7582 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12329
msgid "C<part_num>"
msgstr "C<part_num>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7584 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12331
msgid "Partition number, counting from 1."
msgstr "Nodalījuma numurs, skaitot no 1."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7586 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12333
msgid "C<part_start>"
msgstr "C<part_start>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7588
msgid ""
"Start of the partition I<in bytes>.  To get sectors you have to divide by "
"the device’s sector size, see L</blockdev-getss>."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījuma sākums I<baitos>.  Lai iegūtu sektorus, jādala ar ierīces sektora "
"izmēru, skatiet L</blockdev-getss>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7591 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12338
msgid "C<part_end>"
msgstr "C<part_end>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7593 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12340
msgid "End of the partition in bytes."
msgstr "Nodalījuma beigas baitos."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7595 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12342
msgid "C<part_size>"
msgstr "C<part_size>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7597 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12344
msgid "Size of the partition in bytes."
msgstr "Nodalījuma izmērs baitos."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7601
msgid "part-resize"
msgstr "part-resize"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7603
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-resize device partnum endsect\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-resize device partnum endsect\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7605 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12362
msgid ""
"This command resizes the partition numbered C<partnum> on C<device> by "
"moving the end position."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda maina nodalījuma ar numuru C<partnum> izmēru ierīcē C<device>, "
"pārvietojot beigu pozīciju."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7608
msgid ""
"Note that this does not modify any filesystem present in the partition.  If "
"you wish to do this, you will need to use filesystem resizing commands like "
"L</resize2fs>."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka tas nemaina nodalījumā esošo failu sistēmu.  Ja vēlaties to "
"darīt, jāizmanto failu sistēmas izmēra maiņas komandas, piemēram, L</"
"resize2fs>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7612 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12369
msgid ""
"When growing a partition you will want to grow the filesystem afterwards, "
"but when shrinking, you need to shrink the filesystem before the partition."
msgstr ""
"Palielinot nodalījumu, pēc tam būs jāpalielina failu sistēma, bet, "
"samazinot, failu sistēma jāsamazina pirms nodalījuma."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7616
msgid "part-set-bootable"
msgstr "part-set-bootable"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7618
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-bootable device partnum true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-bootable device partnum true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7620 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12385
msgid ""
"This sets the bootable flag on partition numbered C<partnum> on device "
"C<device>.  Note that partitions are numbered from 1."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata sāknējamības karogu nodalījumam ar numuru C<partnum> ierīcē "
"C<device>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka nodalījumi tiek numurēti no 1."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7623 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12388
msgid ""
"The bootable flag is used by some operating systems (notably Windows) to "
"determine which partition to boot from.  It is by no means universally "
"recognized."
msgstr ""
"Sāknējamības karogu dažas operētājsistēmas (it īpaši Windows) izmanto, lai "
"noteiktu, no kura nodalījuma sāknēt.  Tas nekādā ziņā netiek atpazīts "
"universāli."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7627
msgid "part-set-disk-guid"
msgstr "part-set-disk-guid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7629
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-disk-guid device guid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-disk-guid device guid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7631 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12403
msgid ""
"Set the disk identifier (GUID) of a GPT-partitioned C<device> to C<guid>.  "
"Return an error if the partition table of C<device> isn't GPT, or if C<guid> "
"is not a valid GUID."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt GPT nodalītas ierīces C<device> diska identifikatoru (GUID) uz "
"C<guid>.  Atgriezt kļūdu, ja ierīces C<device> nodalījumu tabula nav GPT vai "
"ja C<guid> nav derīgs GUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7635
msgid "part-set-disk-guid-random"
msgstr "part-set-disk-guid-random"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7637
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-disk-guid-random device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-disk-guid-random device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7639 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12417
msgid ""
"Set the disk identifier (GUID) of a GPT-partitioned C<device> to a randomly "
"generated value.  Return an error if the partition table of C<device> isn't "
"GPT."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt GPT nodalītas ierīces C<device> diska identifikatoru (GUID) uz "
"nejauši ģenerētu vērtību.  Atgriezt kļūdu, ja ierīces C<device> nodalījumu "
"tabula nav GPT."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7643
msgid "part-set-gpt-attributes"
msgstr "part-set-gpt-attributes"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7645
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-gpt-attributes device partnum attributes\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-gpt-attributes device partnum attributes\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7647 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12433
msgid ""
"Set the attribute flags of numbered GPT partition C<partnum> to "
"C<attributes>. Return an error if the partition table of C<device> isn't "
"GPT."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt numurētā GPT nodalījuma C<partnum> atribūtu karogus uz C<attributes>"
".  Atgriezt kļūdu, ja ierīces C<device> nodalījumu tabula nav GPT."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7650 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12436
msgid ""
"See L<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GUID_Partition_Table#Partition_entries> "
"for a useful list of partition attributes."
msgstr ""
"Noderīgu nodalījumu atribūtu sarakstu skatiet L<https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/GUID_Partition_Table#Partition_entries>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7653
msgid "part-set-gpt-guid"
msgstr "part-set-gpt-guid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7655
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-gpt-guid device partnum guid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-gpt-guid device partnum guid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7657 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12451
msgid ""
"Set the GUID of numbered GPT partition C<partnum> to C<guid>.  Return an "
"error if the partition table of C<device> isn't GPT, or if C<guid> is not a "
"valid GUID."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt numurētā GPT nodalījuma C<partnum> GUID uz C<guid>.  Atgriezt "
"kļūdu, ja ierīces C<device> nodalījumu tabula nav GPT vai ja C<guid> nav "
"derīgs GUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7661
msgid "part-set-gpt-type"
msgstr "part-set-gpt-type"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7663
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-gpt-type device partnum guid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-gpt-type device partnum guid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7665 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12467
msgid ""
"Set the type GUID of numbered GPT partition C<partnum> to C<guid>. Return an "
"error if the partition table of C<device> isn't GPT, or if C<guid> is not a "
"valid GUID."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt numurētā GPT nodalījuma C<partnum> tipa GUID uz C<guid>.  Atgriezt "
"kļūdu, ja ierīces C<device> nodalījumu tabula nav GPT vai ja C<guid> nav "
"derīgs GUID."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7669 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12471
msgid ""
"See "
"L<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GUID_Partition_Table#Partition_type_GUIDs> "
"for a useful list of type GUIDs."
msgstr ""
"Noderīgu tipu GUID sarakstu skatiet L<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"GUID_Partition_Table#Partition_type_GUIDs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7672
msgid "part-set-mbr-id"
msgstr "part-set-mbr-id"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7674
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-mbr-id device partnum idbyte\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-mbr-id device partnum idbyte\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7676 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12486
msgid ""
"Sets the MBR type byte (also known as the ID byte) of the numbered partition "
"C<partnum> to C<idbyte>.  Note that the type bytes quoted in most "
"documentation are in fact hexadecimal numbers, but usually documented "
"without any leading \"0x\" which might be confusing."
msgstr ""
"Iestata numurētā nodalījuma C<partnum> MBR tipa baitu (saukts arī par ID "
"baitu) uz C<idbyte>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka lielākajā daļā dokumentācijas minētie "
"tipa baiti patiesībā ir heksadecimāli skaitļi, bet parasti dokumentēti bez "
"sākuma „0x”, kas var mulsināt."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7686
msgid "part-set-name"
msgstr "part-set-name"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7688
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-set-name device partnum name\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-set-name device partnum name\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7690 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12508
msgid ""
"This sets the partition name on partition numbered C<partnum> on device "
"C<device>.  Note that partitions are numbered from 1."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata nodalījuma nosaukumu nodalījumam ar numuru C<partnum> ierīcē "
"C<device>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka nodalījumi tiek numurēti no 1."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7693 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12511
msgid ""
"The partition name can only be set on certain types of partition table.  "
"This works on C<gpt> but not on C<mbr> partitions."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījuma nosaukumu var iestatīt tikai noteiktu tipu nodalījumu tabulās.  "
"Tas darbojas ar C<gpt>, bet ne ar C<mbr> nodalījumiem."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7696
msgid "part-to-dev"
msgstr "part-to-dev"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7698
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-to-dev partition\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-to-dev partition\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7700 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12524
msgid ""
"This function takes a partition name (eg. \"/dev/sdb1\") and removes the "
"partition number, returning the device name (eg. \"/dev/sdb\")."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija pieņem nodalījuma nosaukumu (piem., „/dev/sdb1”) un noņem "
"nodalījuma numuru, atgriežot ierīces nosaukumu (piem., „/dev/sdb”)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7704 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7716
msgid ""
"The named partition must exist, for example as a string returned from "
"L</list-partitions>."
msgstr ""
"Nosauktajam nodalījumam jāeksistē, piemēram, kā virknei, ko atgriezis L</"
"list-partitions>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7707
msgid "See also L</part-to-partnum>, L</device-index>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</part-to-partnum>, L</device-index>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7709
msgid "part-to-partnum"
msgstr "part-to-partnum"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7711
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" part-to-partnum partition\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" part-to-partnum partition\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7713 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12544
msgid ""
"This function takes a partition name (eg. \"/dev/sdb1\") and returns the "
"partition number (eg. C<1>)."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija pieņem nodalījuma nosaukumu (piem., „/dev/sdb1”) un atgriež "
"nodalījuma numuru (piem., C<1>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7719
msgid "See also L</part-to-dev>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</part-to-dev>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7721
msgid "ping-daemon"
msgstr "ping-daemon"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7723
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ping-daemon\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ping-daemon\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7725 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12561
msgid ""
"This is a test probe into the guestfs daemon running inside the libguestfs "
"appliance.  Calling this function checks that the daemon responds to the "
"ping message, without affecting the daemon or attached block device(s) in "
"any other way."
msgstr ""
"Šī ir testa zonde uz guestfs dēmonu, kas darbojas libguestfs palīgsistēmā.  "
"Šīs funkcijas izsaukšana pārbauda, vai dēmons atbild uz ping ziņojumu, "
"nekādā citā veidā neietekmējot dēmonu vai pievienoto(-ās) bloku ierīci(-es)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7730
msgid "pread"
msgstr "pread"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7732
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pread path count offset\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pread path count offset\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7734 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12579
msgid ""
"This command lets you read part of a file.  It reads C<count> bytes of the "
"file, starting at C<offset>, from file C<path>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ļauj nolasīt faila daļu.  Tā nolasa C<count> baitus no faila "
"C<path>, sākot no C<offset>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7737 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7752
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12582 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12608
msgid ""
"This may read fewer bytes than requested.  For further details see the "
"L<pread(2)> system call."
msgstr ""
"Tas var nolasīt mazāk baitu, nekā pieprasīts.  Sīkāk skatiet sistēmas "
"izsaukumu L<pread(2)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7740
msgid "See also L</pwrite>, L</pread-device>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</pwrite>, L</pread-device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7745
msgid "pread-device"
msgstr "pread-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7747
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pread-device device count offset\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pread-device device count offset\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7749 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12605
msgid ""
"This command lets you read part of a block device.  It reads C<count> bytes "
"of C<device>, starting at C<offset>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ļauj nolasīt bloku ierīces daļu.  Tā nolasa C<count> baitus no "
"C<device>, sākot no C<offset>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7755
msgid "See also L</pread>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</pread>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7760
msgid "pvchange-uuid"
msgstr "pvchange-uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7762
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvchange-uuid device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvchange-uuid device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7764 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12628
msgid "Generate a new random UUID for the physical volume C<device>."
msgstr "Ģenerēt jaunu nejaušu UUID fiziskajam sējumam C<device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7769
msgid "pvchange-uuid-all"
msgstr "pvchange-uuid-all"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7771
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvchange-uuid-all\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvchange-uuid-all\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7773 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12642
msgid "Generate new random UUIDs for all physical volumes."
msgstr "Ģenerēt jaunus nejaušus UUID visiem fiziskajiem sējumiem."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7778
msgid "pvcreate"
msgstr "pvcreate"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7780
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvcreate device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvcreate device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7782 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12657
msgid ""
"This creates an LVM physical volume on the named C<device>, where C<device> "
"should usually be a partition name such as F</dev/sda1>."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido LVM fizisko sējumu nosauktajā ierīcē C<device>, kur C<device> "
"parasti jābūt nodalījuma nosaukumam, piemēram, F</dev/sda1>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7789
msgid "pvremove"
msgstr "pvremove"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7791
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvremove device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvremove device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7793 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12674
msgid ""
"This wipes a physical volume C<device> so that LVM will no longer recognise "
"it."
msgstr "Tas notīra fizisko sējumu C<device>, lai LVM to vairs neatpazītu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7796 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12677
msgid ""
"The implementation uses the L<pvremove(8)> command which refuses to wipe "
"physical volumes that contain any volume groups, so you have to remove those "
"first."
msgstr ""
"Realizācija izmanto komandu L<pvremove(8)>, kas atsakās notīrīt fiziskos "
"sējumus, kas satur jebkādas sējumu grupas, tāpēc tās vispirms jānoņem."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7803
msgid "pvresize"
msgstr "pvresize"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7805
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvresize device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvresize device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7807 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12694
msgid ""
"This resizes (expands or shrinks) an existing LVM physical volume to match "
"the new size of the underlying device."
msgstr ""
"Tas maina esoša LVM fiziskā sējuma izmēru (paplašina vai samazina), lai tas "
"atbilstu pamatā esošās ierīces jaunajam izmēram."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7813
msgid "pvresize-size"
msgstr "pvresize-size"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7815
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvresize-size device size\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvresize-size device size\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7817
msgid ""
"This command is the same as L</pvresize> except that it allows you to "
"specify the new size (in bytes) explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tāda pati kā L</pvresize>, izņemot to, ka tā ļauj eksplicīti "
"norādīt jauno izmēru (baitos)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7823
msgid "pvs"
msgstr "pvs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7825
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7827 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12726
msgid ""
"List all the physical volumes detected.  This is the equivalent of the "
"L<pvs(8)> command."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visus noteiktos fiziskos sējumus.  Tas ir ekvivalents komandai "
"L<pvs(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7830 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12729
msgid ""
"This returns a list of just the device names that contain PVs "
"(eg. F</dev/sda2>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež tikai to ierīču nosaukumu sarakstu, kas satur PV (piem., F</dev/"
"sda2>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7833
msgid "See also L</pvs-full>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</pvs-full>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7838
msgid "pvs-full"
msgstr "pvs-full"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7840
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvs-full\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvs-full\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7842 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12748
msgid ""
"List all the physical volumes detected.  This is the equivalent of the "
"L<pvs(8)> command.  The \"full\" version includes all fields."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visus noteiktos fiziskos sējumus.  Tas ir ekvivalents komandai "
"L<pvs(8)>.  „Pilnā” versija ietver visus laukus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7848
msgid "pvuuid"
msgstr "pvuuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7850
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pvuuid device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pvuuid device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7852 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12766
msgid "This command returns the UUID of the LVM PV C<device>."
msgstr "Šī komanda atgriež LVM PV C<device> UUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7854
msgid "pwrite"
msgstr "pwrite"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7856
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pwrite path content offset\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pwrite path content offset\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7858 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12782
msgid ""
"This command writes to part of a file.  It writes the data buffer C<content> "
"to the file C<path> starting at offset C<offset>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda raksta faila daļā.  Tā ieraksta datu buferi C<content> failā "
"C<path>, sākot no nobīdes C<offset>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7861 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12785
msgid ""
"This command implements the L<pwrite(2)> system call, and like that system "
"call it may not write the full data requested.  The return value is the "
"number of bytes that were actually written to the file.  This could even be "
"0, although short writes are unlikely for regular files in ordinary "
"circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda realizē sistēmas izsaukumu L<pwrite(2)>, un tāpat kā šis sistēmas "
"izsaukums tā var neierakstīt visus pieprasītos datus.  Atgriešanas vērtība "
"ir failā faktiski ierakstīto baitu skaits.  Tas var būt pat 0, lai gan īsas "
"rakstīšanas parastiem failiem parastos apstākļos ir maz ticamas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7867
msgid "See also L</pread>, L</pwrite-device>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</pread>, L</pwrite-device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7872
msgid "pwrite-device"
msgstr "pwrite-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7874
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pwrite-device device content offset\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pwrite-device device content offset\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7876 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12809
msgid ""
"This command writes to part of a device.  It writes the data buffer "
"C<content> to C<device> starting at offset C<offset>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda raksta ierīces daļā.  Tā ieraksta datu buferi C<content> ierīcē "
"C<device>, sākot no nobīdes C<offset>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7879 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12812
msgid ""
"This command implements the L<pwrite(2)> system call, and like that system "
"call it may not write the full data requested (although short writes to disk "
"devices and partitions are probably impossible with standard Linux kernels)."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda realizē sistēmas izsaukumu L<pwrite(2)>, un tāpat kā šis sistēmas "
"izsaukums tā var neierakstīt visus pieprasītos datus (lai gan īsas "
"rakstīšanas disku ierīcēs un nodalījumos ar standarta Linux kodoliem, "
"visticamāk, nav iespējamas)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7884
msgid "See also L</pwrite>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</pwrite>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7889
msgid "read-file"
msgstr "read-file"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7891
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" read-file path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" read-file path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7893 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12833
msgid "This call returns the contents of the file C<path> as a buffer."
msgstr "Šis izsaukums atgriež faila C<path> saturu kā buferi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7896
msgid ""
"Unlike L</cat>, this function can correctly handle files that contain "
"embedded ASCII NUL characters."
msgstr ""
"Atšķirībā no L</cat>, šī funkcija var pareizi apstrādāt failus, kas satur "
"iegultas ASCII NUL rakstzīmes."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7899
msgid "read-lines"
msgstr "read-lines"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7901
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" read-lines path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" read-lines path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7905 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12853
msgid ""
"The file contents are returned as a list of lines.  Trailing C<LF> and "
"C<CRLF> character sequences are I<not> returned."
msgstr ""
"Faila saturs tiek atgriezts kā rindu saraksts.  Beigu rakstzīmju secības "
"C<LF> un C<CRLF> I<netiek> atgrieztas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7908
msgid ""
"Note that this function cannot correctly handle binary files (specifically, "
"files containing C<\\0> character which is treated as end of string).  For "
"those you need to use the L</read-file> function and split the buffer into "
"lines yourself."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šī funkcija nevar pareizi apstrādāt binārus failus "
"(konkrēti, failus ar rakstzīmi C<\\0>, kas tiek uzskatīta par virknes beigām)"
".  Tiem jāizmanto funkcija L</read-file> un buferis pašiem jāsadala rindās."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7913
msgid "readdir"
msgstr "readdir"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7915
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" readdir dir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" readdir dir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7917 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12873
msgid "This returns the list of directory entries in directory C<dir>."
msgstr "Tas atgriež direktorijas C<dir> ierakstu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7919 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12875
msgid ""
"All entries in the directory are returned, including C<.> and C<..>.  The "
"entries are I<not> sorted, but returned in the same order as the underlying "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Tiek atgriezti visi direktorijas ieraksti, ieskaitot C<.> un C<..>.  "
"Ieraksti I<nav> sakārtoti, bet atgriezti tādā pašā secībā kā pamatā esošajā "
"failu sistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7923 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12879
msgid ""
"Also this call returns basic file type information about each file.  The "
"C<ftyp> field will contain one of the following characters:"
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums arī atgriež pamata informāciju par katra faila tipu.  Lauks "
"C<ftyp> saturēs vienu no šīm rakstzīmēm:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7960 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12916
msgid "'?'"
msgstr "'?'"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7962 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12918
msgid "The L<readdir(3)> call returned a C<d_type> field with an unexpected value"
msgstr "Izsaukums L<readdir(3)> atgrieza lauku C<d_type> ar negaidītu vērtību"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7967
msgid ""
"This function is primarily intended for use by programs.  To get a simple "
"list of names, use L</ls>.  To get a printable directory for human "
"consumption, use L</ll>."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija galvenokārt paredzēta programmām.  Lai iegūtu vienkāršu "
"nosaukumu sarakstu, izmantojiet L</ls>.  Lai iegūtu cilvēkam izdrukājamu "
"direktoriju, izmantojiet L</ll>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7971
msgid "readlink"
msgstr "readlink"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7973
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" readlink path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" readlink path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7975 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12944
msgid "This command reads the target of a symbolic link."
msgstr "Šī komanda nolasa simboliskās saites mērķi."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7977
msgid "readlinklist"
msgstr "readlinklist"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7979
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" readlinklist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" readlinklist path 'names ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7981 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12958
msgid ""
"This call allows you to do a C<readlink> operation on multiple files, where "
"all files are in the directory C<path>.  C<names> is the list of files from "
"this directory."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ļauj veikt C<readlink> darbību vairākiem failiem, kur visi "
"faili atrodas direktorijā C<path>.  C<names> ir šīs direktorijas failu "
"saraksts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7985 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12962
msgid ""
"On return you get a list of strings, with a one-to-one correspondence to the "
"C<names> list.  Each string is the value of the symbolic link."
msgstr ""
"Atgriežot saņemat virkņu sarakstu ar atbilstību viens pret vienu sarakstam "
"C<names>.  Katra virkne ir simboliskās saites vērtība."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7989 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12966
msgid ""
"If the L<readlink(2)> operation fails on any name, then the corresponding "
"result string is the empty string C<\"\">.  However the whole operation is "
"completed even if there were L<readlink(2)> errors, and so you can call this "
"function with names where you don't know if they are symbolic links already "
"(albeit slightly less efficient)."
msgstr ""
"Ja L<readlink(2)> darbība kādam nosaukumam neizdodas, atbilstošā rezultāta "
"virkne ir tukša virkne C<\"\">.  Tomēr visa darbība tiek pabeigta pat tad, "
"ja bija L<readlink(2)> kļūdas, tāpēc šo funkciju var izsaukt ar nosaukumiem, "
"par kuriem nezināt, vai tie jau ir simboliskās saites (lai gan nedaudz mazāk "
"efektīvi)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:7996 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12973
msgid ""
"This call is intended for programs that want to efficiently list a directory "
"contents without making many round-trips."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums paredzēts programmām, kas vēlas efektīvi uzskaitīt "
"direktorijas saturu bez daudzām turp-atpakaļ apmaiņām."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8001
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" realpath path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" realpath path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8003 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:12988
msgid ""
"Return the canonicalized absolute pathname of C<path>.  The returned path "
"has no C<.>, C<..> or symbolic link path elements."
msgstr ""
"Atgriezt C<path> kanonizēto absolūto ceļa nosaukumu.  Atgrieztajā ceļā nav "
"C<.>, C<..> vai simbolisko saišu ceļa elementu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8006
msgid "remount"
msgstr "remount"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8008
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" remount mountpoint [rw:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" remount mountpoint [rw:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8010 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13010
msgid ""
"This call allows you to change the C<rw> (readonly/read-write)  flag on an "
"already mounted filesystem at C<mountpoint>, converting a readonly "
"filesystem to be read-write, or vice-versa."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ļauj mainīt C<rw> (tikai lasāms/lasāms-rakstāms) karogu jau "
"montētai failu sistēmai C<mountpoint>, pārvēršot tikai lasāmu failu sistēmu "
"par lasāmu-rakstāmu vai otrādi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8014 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13014
msgid ""
"Note that at the moment you must supply the \"optional\" C<rw> parameter.  "
"In future we may allow other flags to be adjusted."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka pašlaik jānorāda „neobligātais” parametrs C<rw>.  Nākotnē, "
"iespējams, ļausim pielāgot citus karogus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8019
msgid "remove-drive"
msgstr "remove-drive"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8021
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" remove-drive label\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" remove-drive label\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8033
msgid "removexattr"
msgstr "removexattr"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8035
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" removexattr xattr path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" removexattr xattr path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8037 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13070
msgid "This call removes the extended attribute named C<xattr> of the file C<path>."
msgstr "Šis izsaukums noņem faila C<path> paplašināto atribūtu C<xattr>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8040
msgid "See also: L</lremovexattr>, L<attr(5)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</lremovexattr>, L<attr(5)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8045
msgid "rename"
msgstr "rename"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8047
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rename oldpath newpath\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rename oldpath newpath\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8049
msgid ""
"Rename a file to a new place on the same filesystem.  This is the same as "
"the Linux L<rename(2)> system call.  In most cases you are better to use "
"L</mv> instead."
msgstr ""
"Pārdēvēt failu uz jaunu vietu tajā pašā failu sistēmā.  Tas ir tas pats, kas "
"Linux sistēmas izsaukums L<rename(2)>.  Vairumā gadījumu labāk izmantot L</"
"mv>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8053
msgid "resize2fs"
msgstr "resize2fs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8055
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" resize2fs device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" resize2fs device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8057 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13103
msgid ""
"This resizes an ext2, ext3 or ext4 filesystem to match the size of the "
"underlying device."
msgstr ""
"Tas maina ext2, ext3 vai ext4 failu sistēmas izmēru, lai tā atbilstu pamatā "
"esošās ierīces izmēram."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8060 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8075
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8084 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13106
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13127 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13143
msgid "See also L<guestfs(3)/RESIZE2FS ERRORS>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<guestfs(3)/RESIZE2FS KĻŪDAS>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8062
msgid "resize2fs-M"
msgstr "resize2fs-M"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8064
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" resize2fs-M device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" resize2fs-M device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8066
msgid ""
"This command is the same as L</resize2fs>, but the filesystem is resized to "
"its minimum size.  This works like the I<-M> option to the L<resize2fs(8)> "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tāda pati kā L</resize2fs>, bet failu sistēmas izmērs tiek "
"mainīts uz tās minimālo izmēru.  Tas darbojas kā komandas L<resize2fs(8)> "
"opcija I<-M>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8070
msgid ""
"To get the resulting size of the filesystem you should call L</tune2fs-l> "
"and read the C<Block size> and C<Block count> values.  These two numbers, "
"multiplied together, give the resulting size of the minimal filesystem in "
"bytes."
msgstr ""
"Lai iegūtu failu sistēmas iegūto izmēru, jāizsauc L</tune2fs-l> un jānolasa "
"vērtības C<Block size> un C<Block count>.  Šie divi skaitļi, sareizināti "
"kopā, dod minimālās failu sistēmas iegūto izmēru baitos."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8077
msgid "resize2fs-size"
msgstr "resize2fs-size"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8079
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" resize2fs-size device size\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" resize2fs-size device size\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8081
msgid ""
"This command is the same as L</resize2fs> except that it allows you to "
"specify the new size (in bytes) explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tāda pati kā L</resize2fs>, izņemot to, ka tā ļauj eksplicīti "
"norādīt jauno izmēru (baitos)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8086
msgid "rm"
msgstr "rm"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8088
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rm path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rm path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8090 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13155
msgid "Remove the single file C<path>."
msgstr "Noņemt vienu failu C<path>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8092
msgid "rm-f"
msgstr "rm-f"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8094
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rm-f path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rm-f path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8096 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13167
msgid "Remove the file C<path>."
msgstr "Noņemt failu C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8098 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13169
msgid ""
"If the file doesn't exist, that error is ignored.  (Other errors, eg. I/O "
"errors or bad paths, are not ignored)"
msgstr ""
"Ja fails neeksistē, šī kļūda tiek ignorēta.  (Citas kļūdas, piem., I/O "
"kļūdas vai nederīgi ceļi, netiek ignorētas.)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8101
msgid ""
"This call cannot remove directories.  Use L</rmdir> to remove an empty "
"directory, or L</rm-rf> to remove directories recursively."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums nevar noņemt direktorijas.  Tukšas direktorijas noņemšanai "
"izmantojiet L</rmdir> vai direktoriju rekursīvai noņemšanai L</rm-rf>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8105
msgid "rm-rf"
msgstr "rm-rf"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rm-rf path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rm-rf path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8109 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13186
msgid ""
"Remove the file or directory C<path>, recursively removing the contents if "
"its a directory.  This is like the C<rm -rf> shell command."
msgstr ""
"Noņemt failu vai direktoriju C<path>, rekursīvi noņemot saturu, ja tā ir "
"direktorija.  Tas ir līdzīgi čaulas komandai C<rm -rf>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8113
msgid "rmdir"
msgstr "rmdir"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rmdir path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rmdir path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8117 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13200
msgid "Remove the single directory C<path>."
msgstr "Noņemt vienu direktoriju C<path>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8119
msgid "rmmountpoint"
msgstr "rmmountpoint"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rmmountpoint exemptpath\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rmmountpoint exemptpath\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8123
msgid ""
"This call removes a mountpoint that was previously created with "
"L</mkmountpoint>.  See L</mkmountpoint> for full details."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums noņem montēšanas punktu, kas iepriekš izveidots ar L</"
"mkmountpoint>.  Pilnu informāciju skatiet L</mkmountpoint>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8127
msgid "rsync"
msgstr "rsync"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rsync src dest [archive:true|false] [deletedest:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rsync src dest [archive:true|false] [deletedest:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8131 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13236
msgid ""
"This call may be used to copy or synchronize two directories under the same "
"libguestfs handle.  This uses the L<rsync(1)> program which uses a fast "
"algorithm that avoids copying files unnecessarily."
msgstr ""
"Šo izsaukumu var izmantot divu direktoriju kopēšanai vai sinhronizēšanai zem "
"viena libguestfs roktura.  Tas izmanto programmu L<rsync(1)>, kas izmanto "
"ātru algoritmu, kas izvairās no nevajadzīgas failu kopēšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8136 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13241
msgid ""
"C<src> and C<dest> are the source and destination directories.  Files are "
"copied from C<src> to C<dest>."
msgstr ""
"C<src> un C<dest> ir avota un mērķa direktorijas.  Faili tiek kopēti no "
"C<src> uz C<dest>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8143 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13248
msgid "C<archive>"
msgstr "C<archive>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8145 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13250
msgid ""
"Turns on archive mode.  This is the same as passing the I<--archive> flag to "
"C<rsync>."
msgstr ""
"Ieslēdz arhīva režīmu.  Tas ir tas pats, kas karoga I<--archive> nodošana "
"C<rsync>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8148 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13253
msgid "C<deletedest>"
msgstr "C<deletedest>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8150 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13255
msgid "Delete files at the destination that do not exist at the source."
msgstr "Dzēst mērķī failus, kas neeksistē avotā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8156 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8183
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8217
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<rsync>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<rsync>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8159
msgid "rsync-in"
msgstr "rsync-in"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rsync-in remote dest [archive:true|false] [deletedest:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rsync-in remote dest [archive:true|false] [deletedest:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8163 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13306
msgid ""
"This call may be used to copy or synchronize the filesystem on the host or "
"on a remote computer with the filesystem within libguestfs.  This uses the "
"L<rsync(1)> program which uses a fast algorithm that avoids copying files "
"unnecessarily."
msgstr ""
"Šo izsaukumu var izmantot failu sistēmas resursdatorā vai attālā datorā "
"kopēšanai vai sinhronizēšanai ar failu sistēmu libguestfs.  Tas izmanto "
"programmu L<rsync(1)>, kas izmanto ātru algoritmu, kas izvairās no "
"nevajadzīgas failu kopēšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8168 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8195
msgid ""
"This call only works if the network is enabled.  See L</set-network> or the "
"I<--network> option to various tools like L<guestfish(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums darbojas tikai tad, ja tīkls ir iespējots.  Skatiet L</set-"
"network> vai dažādu rīku, piemēram, L<guestfish(1)>, opciju I<--network>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8172 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13315
msgid ""
"Files are copied from the remote server and directory specified by C<remote> "
"to the destination directory C<dest>."
msgstr ""
"Faili tiek kopēti no attālā servera un direktorijas, kas norādīti ar "
"C<remote>, uz mērķa direktoriju C<dest>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8175 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8202
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13318 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13383
msgid ""
"The format of the remote server string is defined by L<rsync(1)>.  Note that "
"there is no way to supply a password or passphrase so the target must be set "
"up not to require one."
msgstr ""
"Attālā servera virknes formātu definē L<rsync(1)>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka nav "
"veida, kā nodot paroli vai paroles frāzi, tāpēc mērķis jāiestata tā, lai tā "
"nebūtu vajadzīga."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8179 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8206
msgid "The optional arguments are the same as those of L</rsync>."
msgstr "Neobligātie argumenti ir tie paši, kas L</rsync>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8186
msgid "rsync-out"
msgstr "rsync-out"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8188
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rsync-out src remote [archive:true|false] [deletedest:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rsync-out src remote [archive:true|false] [deletedest:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8190 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13371
msgid ""
"This call may be used to copy or synchronize the filesystem within "
"libguestfs with a filesystem on the host or on a remote computer.  This uses "
"the L<rsync(1)> program which uses a fast algorithm that avoids copying "
"files unnecessarily."
msgstr ""
"Šo izsaukumu var izmantot failu sistēmas libguestfs kopēšanai vai "
"sinhronizēšanai ar failu sistēmu resursdatorā vai attālā datorā.  Tas "
"izmanto programmu L<rsync(1)>, kas izmanto ātru algoritmu, kas izvairās no "
"nevajadzīgas failu kopēšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8199 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13380
msgid ""
"Files are copied from the source directory C<src> to the remote server and "
"directory specified by C<remote>."
msgstr ""
"Faili tiek kopēti no avota direktorijas C<src> uz attālo serveri un "
"direktoriju, kas norādīti ar C<remote>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8208
msgid ""
"Globbing does not happen on the C<src> parameter.  In programs which use the "
"API directly you have to expand wildcards yourself (see L</glob-expand>).  "
"In guestfish you can use the C<glob> command (see L<guestfish(1)/glob>), for "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Parametram C<src> glob izvēršana nenotiek.  Programmās, kas tieši izmanto "
"API, aizstājējzīmes jāizvērš pašiem (skatiet L</glob-expand>).  Guestfish "
"varat izmantot komandu C<glob> (skatiet L<guestfish(1)/glob>), piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8213 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13394
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> glob rsync-out /* rsync://remote/\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> glob rsync-out /* rsync://remote/\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8220
msgid "scrub-device"
msgstr "scrub-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8222
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" scrub-device device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" scrub-device device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8224 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13433
msgid ""
"This command writes patterns over C<device> to make data retrieval more "
"difficult."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda raksta šablonus pāri ierīcei C<device>, lai apgrūtinātu datu "
"atgūšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8227 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8242
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8258 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13436
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13457 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13479
msgid ""
"It is an interface to the L<scrub(1)> program.  See that manual page for "
"more details."
msgstr ""
"Tā ir saskarne programmai L<scrub(1)>.  Sīkāk skatiet šo rokasgrāmatas lapu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8230 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8245
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8261
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<scrub>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<scrub>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8233
msgid "scrub-file"
msgstr "scrub-file"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8235
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" scrub-file file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" scrub-file file\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8237 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13452
msgid ""
"This command writes patterns over a file to make data retrieval more "
"difficult."
msgstr "Šī komanda raksta šablonus pāri failam, lai apgrūtinātu datu atgūšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8240 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13455
msgid "The file is I<removed> after scrubbing."
msgstr "Pēc attīrīšanas fails tiek I<noņemts>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8248
msgid "scrub-freespace"
msgstr "scrub-freespace"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8250
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" scrub-freespace dir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" scrub-freespace dir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8252
msgid ""
"This command creates the directory C<dir> and then fills it with files until "
"the filesystem is full, and scrubs the files as for L</scrub-file>, and "
"deletes them.  The intention is to scrub any free space on the partition "
"containing C<dir>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izveido direktoriju C<dir> un tad aizpilda to ar failiem, līdz "
"failu sistēma ir pilna, attīra failus kā L</scrub-file> un dzēš tos.  Mērķis "
"ir attīrīt jebkuru brīvo vietu nodalījumā, kas satur C<dir>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8264
msgid "selinux-relabel"
msgstr "selinux-relabel"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8266
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" selinux-relabel specfile path [force:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" selinux-relabel specfile path [force:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8268 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13511
msgid "SELinux relabel parts of the filesystem."
msgstr "Atkārtoti piešķirt SELinux etiķetes failu sistēmas daļām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8270 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8900
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13513 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14365
msgid ""
"The C<specfile> parameter controls the policy spec file used.  You have to "
"parse C</etc/selinux/config> to find the correct SELinux policy and then "
"pass the spec file, usually: C</etc/selinux/> + I<selinuxtype> + "
"C</contexts/files/file_contexts>."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<specfile> kontrolē izmantoto politikas specifikācijas failu.  "
"Jāparsē C</etc/selinux/config>, lai atrastu pareizo SELinux politiku, un pēc "
"tam jānodod specifikācijas fails, parasti: C</etc/selinux/> + I<selinuxtype> "
"+ C</contexts/files/file_contexts>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8275 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13518
msgid ""
"The required C<path> parameter is the top level directory where relabelling "
"starts.  Normally you should pass C<path> as C</> to relabel the whole guest "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Obligātais parametrs C<path> ir augšējā līmeņa direktorija, kur sākas "
"etiķešu atkārtota piešķiršana.  Parasti C<path> jānodod kā C</>, lai "
"atkārtoti piešķirtu etiķetes visai viesa failu sistēmai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8279 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8911
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13522 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14376
msgid ""
"The optional C<force> boolean controls whether the context is reset for "
"customizable files, and also whether the user, role and range parts of the "
"file context is changed."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātais Būla parametrs C<force> kontrolē, vai konteksts tiek "
"atiestatīts pielāgojamiem failiem, kā arī, vai tiek mainītas faila konteksta "
"lietotāja, lomas un diapazona daļas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8292 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8920
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<selinuxrelabel>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<selinuxrelabel>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8295
msgid "set-append"
msgstr "set-append"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8297
msgid "append"
msgstr "append"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8299
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-append append\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-append append\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8301 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13563
msgid ""
"This function is used to add additional options to the libguestfs appliance "
"kernel command line."
msgstr ""
"Šo funkciju izmanto, lai libguestfs palīgsistēmas kodola komandrindai "
"pievienotu papildu opcijas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8304 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13566
msgid ""
"The default is C<NULL> unless overridden by setting C<LIBGUESTFS_APPEND> "
"environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums ir C<NULL>, ja vien tas nav ignorēts, iestatot vides mainīgo "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_APPEND>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8307 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13569
msgid ""
"Setting C<append> to C<NULL> means I<no> additional options are passed "
"(libguestfs always adds a few of its own)."
msgstr ""
"C<append> iestatīšana uz C<NULL> nozīmē, ka I<netiek> nodotas papildu "
"opcijas (libguestfs vienmēr pievieno dažas savas)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8310
msgid "set-attach-method"
msgstr "set-attach-method"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8312
msgid "attach-method"
msgstr "attach-method"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8314
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-attach-method backend\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-attach-method backend\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8316 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8348
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13589 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13622
msgid ""
"Set the method that libguestfs uses to connect to the backend guestfsd "
"daemon."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt metodi, ko libguestfs izmanto savienošanai ar aizmugursistēmas "
"guestfsd dēmonu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8319 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8353
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13592 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13627
msgid "See L<guestfs(3)/BACKEND>."
msgstr "Skatiet L<guestfs(3)/AIZMUGURSISTĒMA>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8321
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</set-backend> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"set-backend>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8328
msgid "set-autosync"
msgstr "set-autosync"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8330
msgid "autosync"
msgstr "autosync"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8332
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-autosync true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-autosync true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8334 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13604
msgid ""
"If C<autosync> is true, this enables autosync.  Libguestfs will make a best "
"effort attempt to make filesystems consistent and synchronized when the "
"handle is closed (also if the program exits without closing handles)."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<autosync> ir true, tas iespējo automātisko sinhronizāciju.  Libguestfs "
"pēc labākās iespējas mēģinās padarīt failu sistēmas konsekventas un "
"sinhronizētas, kad rokturis tiek aizvērts (arī tad, ja programma iziet, "
"neaizverot rokturus)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8339 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13609
msgid ""
"This is enabled by default (since libguestfs 1.5.24, previously it was "
"disabled by default)."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir iespējots pēc noklusējuma (kopš libguestfs 1.5.24, iepriekš tas pēc "
"noklusējuma bija atspējots)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8342
msgid "set-backend"
msgstr "set-backend"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8344
msgid "backend"
msgstr "backend"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8346
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-backend backend\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-backend backend\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8355
msgid "set-backend-setting"
msgstr "set-backend-setting"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8357
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-backend-setting name val\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-backend-setting name val\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8359 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13640
msgid ""
"Append C<\"name=value\"> to the backend settings string list.  However if a "
"string already exists matching C<\"name\"> or beginning with C<\"name=\">, "
"then that setting is replaced."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot C<\"name=value\"> aizmugursistēmas iestatījumu virkņu sarakstam.  "
"Tomēr, ja jau eksistē virkne, kas atbilst C<\"name\"> vai sākas ar "
"C<\"name=\">, šis iestatījums tiek aizstāts."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8365
msgid "set-backend-settings"
msgstr "set-backend-settings"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8367
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-backend-settings 'settings ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-backend-settings 'settings ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8369 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13656
msgid ""
"Set a list of zero or more settings which are passed through to the current "
"backend.  Each setting is a string which is interpreted in a "
"backend-specific way, or ignored if not understood by the backend."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt nulles vai vairāku iestatījumu sarakstu, kas tiek nodoti "
"pašreizējai aizmugursistēmai.  Katrs iestatījums ir virkne, ko interpretē "
"aizmugursistēmai specifiskā veidā vai ignorē, ja aizmugursistēma to nesaprot."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8374 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13661
msgid ""
"The default value is an empty list, unless the environment variable "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS> was set when the handle was created.  This "
"environment variable contains a colon-separated list of settings."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma vērtība ir tukšs saraksts, ja vien, veidojot rokturi, nebija "
"iestatīts vides mainīgais C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS>.  Šis vides "
"mainīgais satur ar koliem atdalītu iestatījumu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8379
msgid ""
"This call replaces all backend settings.  If you want to replace a single "
"backend setting, see L</set-backend-setting>.  If you want to clear a single "
"backend setting, see L</clear-backend-setting>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums aizstāj visus aizmugursistēmas iestatījumus.  Ja vēlaties "
"aizstāt vienu aizmugursistēmas iestatījumu, skatiet L</set-backend-setting>"
".  Ja vēlaties notīrīt vienu aizmugursistēmas iestatījumu, skatiet L</clear-"
"backend-setting>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8386
msgid "set-cachedir"
msgstr "set-cachedir"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8388
msgid "cachedir"
msgstr "cachedir"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8390
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-cachedir cachedir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-cachedir cachedir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8392 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13683
msgid ""
"Set the directory used by the handle to store the appliance cache, when "
"using a supermin appliance.  The appliance is cached and shared between all "
"handles which have the same effective user ID."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt direktoriju, ko rokturis izmanto palīgsistēmas kešatmiņas "
"glabāšanai, izmantojot supermin palīgsistēmu.  Palīgsistēma tiek kešota un "
"koplietota starp visiem rokturiem ar vienādu efektīvo lietotāja ID."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8397 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13688
msgid ""
"The environment variables C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> and C<TMPDIR> control the "
"default value: If C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> is set, then that is the default.  "
"Else if C<TMPDIR> is set, then that is the default.  Else F</var/tmp> is the "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma vērtību kontrolē vides mainīgie C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> un "
"C<TMPDIR>: ja C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> ir iestatīts, tas ir noklusējums.  "
"Citādi, ja C<TMPDIR> ir iestatīts, tas ir noklusējums.  Citādi noklusējums "
"ir F</var/tmp>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8402
msgid "set-direct"
msgstr "set-direct"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8404
msgid "direct"
msgstr "direct"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8406
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-direct true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-direct true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8408 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13710
msgid ""
"If the direct appliance mode flag is enabled, then stdin and stdout are "
"passed directly through to the appliance once it is launched."
msgstr ""
"Ja tiešās palīgsistēmas režīma karogs ir iespējots, stdin un stdout tiek "
"nodoti tieši palīgsistēmai, tiklīdz tā ir palaista."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8412
msgid ""
"One consequence of this is that log messages aren't caught by the library "
"and handled by L</set-log-message-callback>, but go straight to stdout."
msgstr ""
"Viena no sekām ir tā, ka žurnāla ziņojumus netver bibliotēka un neapstrādā "
"L</set-log-message-callback>, bet tie nonāk tieši stdout."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8416 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13718
msgid "You probably don't want to use this unless you know what you are doing."
msgstr "Visticamāk, nevēlaties to izmantot, ja vien nezināt, ko darāt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8419 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13721
msgid "The default is disabled."
msgstr "Noklusējumā tas ir atspējots."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8428
msgid "set-e2attrs"
msgstr "set-e2attrs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8430
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-e2attrs file attrs [clear:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-e2attrs file attrs [clear:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8432 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13742
msgid ""
"This sets or clears the file attributes C<attrs> associated with the inode "
"F<file>."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata vai notīra ar inode F<file> saistītos faila atribūtus C<attrs>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8435
msgid ""
"C<attrs> is a string of characters representing file attributes.  See "
"L</get-e2attrs> for a list of possible attributes.  Not all attributes can "
"be changed."
msgstr ""
"C<attrs> ir rakstzīmju virkne, kas attēlo faila atribūtus.  Iespējamo "
"atribūtu sarakstu skatiet L</get-e2attrs>.  Ne visus atribūtus var mainīt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8439 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13749
msgid ""
"If optional boolean C<clear> is not present or false, then the C<attrs> "
"listed are set in the inode."
msgstr ""
"Ja neobligātā Būla parametra C<clear> nav vai tas ir false, uzskaitītie "
"C<attrs> tiek iestatīti inode."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8442 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13752
msgid "If C<clear> is true, then the C<attrs> listed are cleared in the inode."
msgstr "Ja C<clear> ir true, uzskaitītie C<attrs> tiek notīrīti inode."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8445 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13755
msgid ""
"In both cases, other attributes not present in the C<attrs> string are left "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Abos gadījumos citi atribūti, kas nav virknē C<attrs>, paliek nemainīti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8454
msgid "set-e2generation"
msgstr "set-e2generation"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8456
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-e2generation file generation\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-e2generation file generation\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8458 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13797
msgid "This sets the ext2 file generation of a file."
msgstr "Tas iestata faila ext2 paaudzi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8460
msgid "See L</get-e2generation>."
msgstr "Skatiet L</get-e2generation>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8462
msgid "set-e2label"
msgstr "set-e2label"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8464
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-e2label device label\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-e2label device label\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8466 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13819
msgid ""
"This sets the ext2/3/4 filesystem label of the filesystem on C<device> to "
"C<label>.  Filesystem labels are limited to 16 characters."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata ierīces C<device> failu sistēmas ext2/3/4 etiķeti uz C<label>.  "
"Failu sistēmu etiķetes ir ierobežotas līdz 16 rakstzīmēm."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8470
msgid ""
"You can use either L</tune2fs-l> or L</get-e2label> to return the existing "
"label on a filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Lai atgrieztu failu sistēmas esošo etiķeti, varat izmantot L</tune2fs-l> vai "
"L</get-e2label>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8473
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</set-label> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"set-label>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8480
msgid "set-e2uuid"
msgstr "set-e2uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8482
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-e2uuid device uuid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-e2uuid device uuid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8484 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13844
msgid ""
"This sets the ext2/3/4 filesystem UUID of the filesystem on C<device> to "
"C<uuid>.  The format of the UUID and alternatives such as C<clear>, "
"C<random> and C<time> are described in the L<tune2fs(8)> manpage."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata ierīces C<device> failu sistēmas ext2/3/4 UUID uz C<uuid>.  UUID "
"formāts un alternatīvas, piemēram, C<clear>, C<random> un C<time>, "
"aprakstītas L<tune2fs(8)> rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8489
msgid "You can use L</vfs-uuid> to return the existing UUID of a filesystem."
msgstr "Lai atgrieztu failu sistēmas esošo UUID, varat izmantot L</vfs-uuid>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8492
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</set-uuid> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"set-uuid>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8499
msgid "set-hv"
msgstr "set-hv"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8501
msgid "hv"
msgstr "hv"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8503
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-hv hv\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-hv hv\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8505 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13862
msgid ""
"Set the hypervisor binary that we will use.  The hypervisor depends on the "
"backend, but is usually the location of the qemu/KVM hypervisor."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt izmantojamo hipervizora bināro failu.  Hipervizors ir atkarīgs no "
"aizmugursistēmas, bet parasti tā ir qemu/KVM hipervizora atrašanās vieta."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8509 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8726
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13866 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14139
msgid ""
"You can also override this by setting the C<LIBGUESTFS_HV> environment "
"variable."
msgstr "To var ignorēt arī, iestatot vides mainīgo C<LIBGUESTFS_HV>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8512 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8731
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13869 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14144
msgid ""
"Note that you should call this function as early as possible after creating "
"the handle.  This is because some pre-launch operations depend on testing "
"qemu features (by running C<qemu -help>).  If the qemu binary changes, we "
"don't retest features, and so you might see inconsistent results.  Using the "
"environment variable C<LIBGUESTFS_HV> is safest of all since that picks the "
"qemu binary at the same time as the handle is created."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šī funkcija jāizsauc pēc iespējas agrāk pēc roktura "
"izveides.  Tas ir tāpēc, ka dažas darbības pirms palaišanas ir atkarīgas no "
"qemu līdzekļu testēšanas (izpildot C<qemu -help>).  Ja qemu binārais fails "
"mainās, līdzekļus atkārtoti netestējam, tāpēc varat redzēt nekonsekventus "
"rezultātus.  Vides mainīgā C<LIBGUESTFS_HV> izmantošana ir visdrošākā, jo "
"tas izvēlas qemu bināro failu vienlaikus ar roktura izveidi."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8520
msgid "set-identifier"
msgstr "set-identifier"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8522
msgid "identifier"
msgstr "identifier"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8524
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-identifier identifier\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-identifier identifier\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8526 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13887
msgid ""
"This is an informative string which the caller may optionally set in the "
"handle.  It is printed in various places, allowing the current handle to be "
"identified in debugging output."
msgstr ""
"Šī ir informatīva virkne, ko izsaucējs pēc izvēles var iestatīt rokturī.  Tā "
"tiek izdrukāta dažādās vietās, ļaujot identificēt pašreizējo rokturi "
"atkļūdošanas izvadē."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8530 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13891
msgid ""
"One important place is when tracing is enabled.  If the identifier string is "
"not an empty string, then trace messages change from this:"
msgstr ""
"Viena svarīga vieta ir, kad iespējota izsekošana.  Ja identifikatora virkne "
"nav tukša virkne, izsekošanas ziņojumi mainās no šī:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8534 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13895
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" libguestfs: trace: get_tmpdir\n"
" libguestfs: trace: get_tmpdir = \"/tmp\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" libguestfs: trace: get_tmpdir\n"
" libguestfs: trace: get_tmpdir = \"/tmp\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8537 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13898
msgid "to this:"
msgstr "uz šo:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8539 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13900
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" libguestfs: trace: ID: get_tmpdir\n"
" libguestfs: trace: ID: get_tmpdir = \"/tmp\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" libguestfs: trace: ID: get_tmpdir\n"
" libguestfs: trace: ID: get_tmpdir = \"/tmp\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8542 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13903
msgid "where C<ID> is the identifier string set by this call."
msgstr "kur C<ID> ir ar šo izsaukumu iestatītā identifikatora virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8544 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13905
msgid ""
"The identifier must only contain alphanumeric ASCII characters, underscore "
"and minus sign.  The default is the empty string."
msgstr ""
"Identifikators drīkst saturēt tikai burtciparu ASCII rakstzīmes, pasvītru un "
"mīnusa zīmi.  Noklusējums ir tukša virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8547
msgid "See also L</set-program>, L</set-trace>, L</get-identifier>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</set-program>, L</set-trace>, L</get-identifier>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8550
msgid "set-label"
msgstr "set-label"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8552
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-label mountable label\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-label mountable label\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8554 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13922
msgid "Set the filesystem label on C<mountable> to C<label>."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt failu sistēmas etiķeti montējamajam objektam C<mountable> uz "
"C<label>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8556 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13924
msgid ""
"Only some filesystem types support labels, and libguestfs supports setting "
"labels on only a subset of these."
msgstr ""
"Tikai daži failu sistēmu tipi atbalsta etiķetes, un libguestfs atbalsta "
"etiķešu iestatīšanu tikai daļai no tiem."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8561 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13929
msgid "ext2, ext3, ext4"
msgstr "ext2, ext3, ext4"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8563 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13931
msgid "Labels are limited to 16 bytes."
msgstr "Etiķetes ir ierobežotas līdz 16 baitiem."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8565 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13933
msgid "NTFS"
msgstr "NTFS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8567 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13935
msgid "Labels are limited to 128 unicode characters."
msgstr "Etiķetes ir ierobežotas līdz 128 unikoda rakstzīmēm."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8569 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13937
msgid "XFS"
msgstr "XFS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8571 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13939
msgid ""
"The label is limited to 12 bytes.  The filesystem must not be mounted when "
"trying to set the label."
msgstr ""
"Etiķete ir ierobežota līdz 12 baitiem.  Mēģinot iestatīt etiķeti, failu "
"sistēma nedrīkst būt montēta."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8574 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13942
msgid "btrfs"
msgstr "btrfs"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8576 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13944
msgid ""
"The label is limited to 255 bytes and some characters are not allowed.  "
"Setting the label on a btrfs subvolume will set the label on its parent "
"filesystem.  The filesystem must not be mounted when trying to set the "
"label."
msgstr ""
"Etiķete ir ierobežota līdz 255 baitiem, un dažas rakstzīmes nav atļautas.  "
"Etiķetes iestatīšana btrfs apakšsējumam iestatīs etiķeti tā vecākfailu "
"sistēmai.  Mēģinot iestatīt etiķeti, failu sistēma nedrīkst būt montēta."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8581 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13949
msgid "fat"
msgstr "fat"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8583 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13951
msgid "The label is limited to 11 bytes."
msgstr "Etiķete ir ierobežota līdz 11 baitiem."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8585 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13953
msgid "swap"
msgstr "swap"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8587 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13955
msgid "The label is limited to 16 bytes."
msgstr "Etiķete ir ierobežota līdz 16 baitiem."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8591 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13959
msgid ""
"If there is no support for changing the label for the type of the specified "
"filesystem, set_label will fail and set errno as ENOTSUP."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādītās failu sistēmas tipam nav atbalsta etiķetes maiņai, set_label "
"neizdosies un iestatīs errno uz ENOTSUP."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8595
msgid "To read the label on a filesystem, call L</vfs-label>."
msgstr "Lai nolasītu failu sistēmas etiķeti, izsauciet L</vfs-label>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8597
msgid "set-libvirt-requested-credential"
msgstr "set-libvirt-requested-credential"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8599
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-libvirt-requested-credential index cred\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-libvirt-requested-credential index cred\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8601 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13977
msgid ""
"After requesting the C<index>'th credential from the user, call this "
"function to pass the answer back to libvirt."
msgstr ""
"Pēc C<index>-o akreditācijas datu pieprasīšanas no lietotāja izsauciet šo "
"funkciju, lai nodotu atbildi atpakaļ libvirt."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8606
msgid "set-libvirt-supported-credentials"
msgstr "set-libvirt-supported-credentials"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8608
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-libvirt-supported-credentials 'creds ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-libvirt-supported-credentials 'creds ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8610 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13992
msgid ""
"Call this function before setting an event handler for "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH>, to supply the list of credential types that "
"the program knows how to process."
msgstr ""
"Izsauciet šo funkciju pirms notikumu apstrādātāja iestatīšanas "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH>, lai nodrošinātu akreditācijas datu tipu "
"sarakstu, ko programma prot apstrādāt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8614 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13996
msgid ""
"The C<creds> list must be a non-empty list of strings.  Possible strings "
"are:"
msgstr ""
"Sarakstam C<creds> jābūt netukšam virkņu sarakstam.  Iespējamās virknes ir:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8621 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14003
msgid "C<authname>"
msgstr "C<authname>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8623 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14005
msgid "C<language>"
msgstr "C<language>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8625 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14007
msgid "C<cnonce>"
msgstr "C<cnonce>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8627 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14009
msgid "C<passphrase>"
msgstr "C<passphrase>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8629 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14011
msgid "C<echoprompt>"
msgstr "C<echoprompt>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8631 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14013
msgid "C<noechoprompt>"
msgstr "C<noechoprompt>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8633 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14015
msgid "C<realm>"
msgstr "C<realm>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8635 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14017
msgid "C<external>"
msgstr "C<external>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8639 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14021
msgid "See libvirt documentation for the meaning of these credential types."
msgstr "Šo akreditācijas datu tipu nozīmi skatiet libvirt dokumentācijā."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8643
msgid "set-memsize"
msgstr "set-memsize"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8645
msgid "memsize"
msgstr "memsize"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8647
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-memsize memsize\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-memsize memsize\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8649
msgid ""
"This sets the memory size in megabytes allocated to the hypervisor.  This "
"only has any effect if called before L</launch>."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata hipervizoram piešķirtās atmiņas izmēru megabaitos.  Tam ir "
"ietekme tikai tad, ja izsaukts pirms L</launch>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8653 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14039
msgid ""
"You can also change this by setting the environment variable "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_MEMSIZE> before the handle is created."
msgstr ""
"To var mainīt arī, pirms roktura izveides iestatot vides mainīgo "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_MEMSIZE>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8660
msgid "set-network"
msgstr "set-network"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8662
msgid "network"
msgstr "network"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8664
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-network true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-network true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8666 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14056
msgid ""
"If C<network> is true, then the network is enabled in the libguestfs "
"appliance.  The default is false."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<network> ir true, libguestfs palīgsistēmā tiek iespējots tīkls.  "
"Noklusējums ir false."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8669 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14059
msgid ""
"This affects whether commands are able to access the network (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/RUNNING COMMANDS>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas ietekmē, vai komandas var piekļūt tīklam (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/KOMANDU "
"IZPILDE>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8672
msgid "You must call this before calling L</launch>, otherwise it has no effect."
msgstr "Tas jāizsauc pirms L</launch> izsaukšanas, citādi tam nav ietekmes."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8675
msgid "set-path"
msgstr "set-path"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8677
msgid "path"
msgstr "path"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8679
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-path searchpath\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-path searchpath\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8681 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14075
msgid "Set the path that libguestfs searches for kernel and initrd.img."
msgstr "Iestatīt ceļu, kurā libguestfs meklē kodolu un initrd.img."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8683 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14077
msgid ""
"The default is C<$libdir/guestfs> unless overridden by setting "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH> environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums ir C<$libdir/guestfs>, ja vien tas nav ignorēts, iestatot vides "
"mainīgo C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8686 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14080
msgid "Setting C<path> to C<NULL> restores the default path."
msgstr "C<path> iestatīšana uz C<NULL> atjauno noklusējuma ceļu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8688
msgid "set-pgroup"
msgstr "set-pgroup"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8690
msgid "pgroup"
msgstr "pgroup"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8692
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-pgroup true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-pgroup true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8694 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14092
msgid ""
"If C<pgroup> is true, child processes are placed into their own process "
"group."
msgstr "Ja C<pgroup> ir true, bērnprocesi tiek ievietoti savā procesu grupā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8697 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14095
msgid ""
"The practical upshot of this is that signals like C<SIGINT> (from users "
"pressing C<^C>) won't be received by the child process."
msgstr ""
"Praktiskās sekas ir tādas, ka bērnprocess nesaņems tādus signālus kā "
"C<SIGINT> (kad lietotāji nospiež C<^C>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8700
msgid ""
"The default for this flag is false, because usually you want C<^C> to kill "
"the subprocess.  Guestfish sets this flag to true when used interactively, "
"so that C<^C> can cancel long-running commands gracefully (see "
"L</user-cancel>)."
msgstr ""
"Šī karoga noklusējums ir false, jo parasti vēlaties, lai C<^C> nobeigtu "
"apakšprocesu.  Guestfish, izmantots interaktīvi, iestata šo karogu uz true, "
"lai C<^C> varētu pieklājīgi atcelt ilgstošas komandas (skatiet L</user-"
"cancel>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8705
msgid "set-program"
msgstr "set-program"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8707
msgid "program"
msgstr "program"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8709
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-program program\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-program program\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8711 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14113
msgid ""
"Set the program name.  This is an informative string which the main program "
"may optionally set in the handle."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt programmas nosaukumu.  Tā ir informatīva virkne, ko galvenā "
"programma pēc izvēles var iestatīt rokturī."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8714 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14116
msgid ""
"When the handle is created, the program name in the handle is set to the "
"basename from C<argv[0]>.  The program name can never be C<NULL>."
msgstr ""
"Kad rokturis tiek izveidots, programmas nosaukums rokturī tiek iestatīts uz "
"C<argv[0]> bāzes nosaukumu.  Programmas nosaukums nekad nevar būt C<NULL>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8718
msgid "set-qemu"
msgstr "set-qemu"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8720
msgid "qemu"
msgstr "qemu"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8722
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-qemu hv\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-qemu hv\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8724 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14137
msgid "Set the hypervisor binary (usually qemu) that we will use."
msgstr "Iestatīt izmantojamo hipervizora bināro failu (parasti qemu)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8729 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14142
msgid "Setting C<hv> to C<NULL> restores the default qemu binary."
msgstr "C<hv> iestatīšana uz C<NULL> atjauno noklusējuma qemu bināro failu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8739
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</set-hv> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"set-hv>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8746
msgid "set-recovery-proc"
msgstr "set-recovery-proc"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8748
msgid "recovery-proc"
msgstr "recovery-proc"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8750
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-recovery-proc true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-recovery-proc true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8752
msgid ""
"If this is called with the parameter C<false> then L</launch> does not "
"create a recovery process.  The purpose of the recovery process is to stop "
"runaway hypervisor processes in the case where the main program aborts "
"abruptly."
msgstr ""
"Ja to izsauc ar parametru C<false>, L</launch> neizveido atkopšanas "
"procesu.  Atkopšanas procesa mērķis ir apturēt aizbēgušus hipervizora "
"procesus gadījumā, ja galvenā programma pēkšņi pārtrauc darbību."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8757
msgid ""
"This only has any effect if called before L</launch>, and the default is "
"true."
msgstr ""
"Tam ir ietekme tikai tad, ja izsaukts pirms L</launch>, un noklusējums ir "
"true."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8760 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14170
msgid ""
"About the only time when you would want to disable this is if the main "
"process will fork itself into the background (\"daemonize\" itself).  In "
"this case the recovery process thinks that the main program has disappeared "
"and so kills the hypervisor, which is not very helpful."
msgstr ""
"Gandrīz vienīgais gadījums, kad to vajadzētu atspējot, ir, ja galvenais "
"process sazarosies fonā (kļūs par „dēmonu”).  Šajā gadījumā atkopšanas "
"process uzskata, ka galvenā programma ir pazudusi, un tāpēc nobeidz "
"hipervizoru, kas nav īpaši noderīgi."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8766
msgid "set-selinux"
msgstr "set-selinux"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8768
msgid "selinux"
msgstr "selinux"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8770
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-selinux true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-selinux true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8772 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14193
msgid ""
"This sets the selinux flag that is passed to the appliance at boot time.  "
"The default is C<selinux=0> (disabled)."
msgstr ""
"Tas iestata selinux karogu, kas tiek nodots palīgsistēmai sāknēšanas laikā.  "
"Noklusējums ir C<selinux=0> (atspējots)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8775 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14196
msgid ""
"Note that if SELinux is enabled, it is always in Permissive mode "
"(C<enforcing=0>)."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, ja SELinux ir iespējots, tas vienmēr ir atļaujošajā režīmā "
"(C<enforcing=0>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8788
msgid "set-smp"
msgstr "set-smp"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8790
msgid "smp"
msgstr "smp"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8792
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-smp smp\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-smp smp\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8794 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14212
msgid ""
"Change the number of virtual CPUs assigned to the appliance.  The default is "
"C<1>.  Increasing this may improve performance, though often it has no "
"effect."
msgstr ""
"Mainīt palīgsistēmai piešķirto virtuālo CPU skaitu.  Noklusējums ir C<1>.  "
"To palielinot, var uzlaboties veiktspēja, lai gan bieži tam nav ietekmes."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8798
msgid "This function must be called before L</launch>."
msgstr "Šī funkcija jāizsauc pirms L</launch>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8800
msgid "set-tmpdir"
msgstr "set-tmpdir"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8802
msgid "tmpdir"
msgstr "tmpdir"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8804
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-tmpdir tmpdir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-tmpdir tmpdir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8806 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14228
msgid "Set the directory used by the handle to store temporary files."
msgstr "Iestatīt direktoriju, ko rokturis izmanto pagaidu failu glabāšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8808 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14230
msgid ""
"The environment variables C<LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR> and C<TMPDIR> control the "
"default value: If C<LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR> is set, then that is the default.  "
"Else if C<TMPDIR> is set, then that is the default.  Else F</tmp> is the "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma vērtību kontrolē vides mainīgie C<LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR> un C<TMPDIR>"
": ja C<LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR> ir iestatīts, tas ir noklusējums.  Citādi, ja "
"C<TMPDIR> ir iestatīts, tas ir noklusējums.  Citādi noklusējums ir F</tmp>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8813
msgid "set-trace"
msgstr "set-trace"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8815
msgid "trace"
msgstr "trace"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8817
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-trace true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-trace true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8819 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14245
msgid ""
"If the command trace flag is set to 1, then libguestfs calls, parameters and "
"return values are traced."
msgstr ""
"Ja komandu izsekošanas karogs ir iestatīts uz 1, libguestfs izsaukumi, "
"parametri un atgriešanas vērtības tiek izsekoti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8822 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14248
msgid ""
"If you want to trace C API calls into libguestfs (and other libraries) then "
"possibly a better way is to use the external L<ltrace(1)> command."
msgstr ""
"Ja vēlaties izsekot C API izsaukumus libguestfs (un citās bibliotēkās), "
"iespējams, labāks veids ir izmantot ārējo komandu L<ltrace(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8826 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14252
msgid ""
"Command traces are disabled unless the environment variable "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE> is defined and set to C<1>."
msgstr ""
"Komandu izsekošana ir atspējota, ja vien vides mainīgais C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE> "
"nav definēts un iestatīts uz C<1>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8829
msgid ""
"Trace messages are normally sent to C<stderr>, unless you register a "
"callback to send them somewhere else (see L</set-event-callback>)."
msgstr ""
"Izsekošanas ziņojumi parasti tiek sūtīti uz C<stderr>, ja vien nereģistrējat "
"atzvanu, lai tos sūtītu citur (skatiet L</set-event-callback>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8833
msgid "set-uuid"
msgstr "set-uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8835
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-uuid device uuid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-uuid device uuid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8837 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14270
msgid ""
"Set the filesystem UUID on C<device> to C<uuid>.  If this fails and the "
"errno is ENOTSUP, means that there is no support for changing the UUID for "
"the type of the specified filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt failu sistēmas UUID ierīcē C<device> uz C<uuid>.  Ja tas neizdodas "
"un errno ir ENOTSUP, tas nozīmē, ka norādītās failu sistēmas tipam nav "
"atbalsta UUID maiņai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8842 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8855
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14275 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14294
msgid "Only some filesystem types support setting UUIDs."
msgstr "Tikai daži failu sistēmu tipi atbalsta UUID iestatīšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8844 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8857
msgid "To read the UUID on a filesystem, call L</vfs-uuid>."
msgstr "Lai nolasītu failu sistēmas UUID, izsauciet L</vfs-uuid>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8846
msgid "set-uuid-random"
msgstr "set-uuid-random"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8848
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-uuid-random device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-uuid-random device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8850 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14289
msgid ""
"Set the filesystem UUID on C<device> to a random UUID.  If this fails and "
"the errno is ENOTSUP, means that there is no support for changing the UUID "
"for the type of the specified filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt failu sistēmas UUID ierīcē C<device> uz nejaušu UUID.  Ja tas "
"neizdodas un errno ir ENOTSUP, tas nozīmē, ka norādītās failu sistēmas tipam "
"nav atbalsta UUID maiņai."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8859
msgid "set-verbose"
msgstr "set-verbose"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8861
msgid "verbose"
msgstr "verbose"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8863
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set-verbose true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set-verbose true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8865 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14308
msgid "If C<verbose> is true, this turns on verbose messages."
msgstr "Ja C<verbose> ir true, tas ieslēdz izvērstos ziņojumus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8867 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14310
msgid ""
"Verbose messages are disabled unless the environment variable "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG> is defined and set to C<1>."
msgstr ""
"Izvērstie ziņojumi ir atspējoti, ja vien vides mainīgais C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG> "
"nav definēts un iestatīts uz C<1>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8870
msgid ""
"Verbose messages are normally sent to C<stderr>, unless you register a "
"callback to send them somewhere else (see L</set-event-callback>)."
msgstr ""
"Izvērstie ziņojumi parasti tiek sūtīti uz C<stderr>, ja vien nereģistrējat "
"atzvanu, lai tos sūtītu citur (skatiet L</set-event-callback>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8874
msgid "setcon"
msgstr "setcon"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8876
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" setcon context\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" setcon context\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8878 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14334
msgid ""
"This sets the SELinux security context of the daemon to the string "
"C<context>."
msgstr "Tas iestata dēmona SELinux drošības kontekstu uz virkni C<context>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8881 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14337
msgid "See the documentation about SELINUX in L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr "Skatiet dokumentāciju par SELINUX L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8893
msgid "setfiles"
msgstr "setfiles"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8895
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" setfiles specfile 'paths ...' [force:true|false] [excludes:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" setfiles specfile 'paths ...' [force:true|false] [excludes:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8897 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14362
msgid ""
"This invokes the SELinux C<setfiles> command which is a low level tool used "
"to relabel parts of the filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Tas izsauc SELinux komandu C<setfiles>, kas ir zema līmeņa rīks failu "
"sistēmas daļu etiķešu atkārtotai piešķiršanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8905 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14370
msgid ""
"The required C<paths> parameter is the list of top level directories where "
"relabelling starts.  C<setfiles> will only relabel up to filesystem "
"boundaries so, for example, passing just C<\"/\"> will relabel the whole "
"root filesystem, but no other mounted filesystems.  If the list is empty, "
"setfiles is not called."
msgstr ""
"Obligātais parametrs C<paths> ir augšējā līmeņa direktoriju saraksts, kur "
"sākas etiķešu atkārtota piešķiršana.  C<setfiles> atkārtoti piešķirs "
"etiķetes tikai līdz failu sistēmu robežām, tāpēc, piemēram, nododot tikai "
"C<\"/\">, tiks atkārtoti piešķirtas etiķetes visai saknes failu sistēmai, "
"bet ne citām montētām failu sistēmām.  Ja saraksts ir tukšs, setfiles netiek "
"izsaukts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8915 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14380
msgid ""
"The optional C<excludes> list allows you to exclude parts of the directory "
"tree by appending the C<setfiles> I<-e> option."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātais saraksts C<excludes> ļauj izslēgt direktoriju koka daļas, "
"pievienojot C<setfiles> opciju I<-e>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8923
msgid "setxattr"
msgstr "setxattr"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8925
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" setxattr xattr val vallen path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" setxattr xattr val vallen path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8927 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14423
msgid ""
"This call sets the extended attribute named C<xattr> of the file C<path> to "
"the value C<val> (of length C<vallen>).  The value is arbitrary 8 bit data."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums iestata faila C<path> paplašināto atribūtu C<xattr> uz vērtību "
"C<val> (garumā C<vallen>).  Vērtība ir patvaļīgi 8 bitu dati."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8931
msgid "See also: L</lsetxattr>, L<attr(5)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</lsetxattr>, L<attr(5)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8936
msgid "sfdisk"
msgstr "sfdisk"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8938
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sfdisk device cyls heads sectors 'lines ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sfdisk device cyls heads sectors 'lines ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8940 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14453
msgid ""
"This is a direct interface to the L<sfdisk(8)> program for creating "
"partitions on block devices."
msgstr ""
"Šī ir tieša saskarne programmai L<sfdisk(8)> nodalījumu izveidei bloku "
"ierīcēs."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8943 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14456
msgid "C<device> should be a block device, for example F</dev/sda>."
msgstr "C<device> jābūt bloku ierīcei, piemēram, F</dev/sda>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8945 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14458
msgid ""
"C<cyls>, C<heads> and C<sectors> are the number of cylinders, heads and "
"sectors on the device, which are passed directly to L<sfdisk(8)> as the "
"I<-C>, I<-H> and I<-S> parameters.  If you pass C<0> for any of these, then "
"the corresponding parameter is omitted.  Usually for ‘large’ disks, you can "
"just pass C<0> for these, but for small (floppy-sized) disks, L<sfdisk(8)> "
"(or rather, the kernel) cannot work out the right geometry and you will need "
"to tell it."
msgstr ""
"C<cyls>, C<heads> un C<sectors> ir cilindru, galviņu un sektoru skaits "
"ierīcē, kas tiek nodoti tieši L<sfdisk(8)> kā parametri I<-C>, I<-H> un I<-S>"
".  Ja kādam no tiem nododat C<0>, atbilstošais parametrs tiek izlaists.  "
"Parasti ‘lieliem’ diskiem tiem var vienkārši nodot C<0>, bet maziem "
"(disketes izmēra) diskiem L<sfdisk(8)> (precīzāk, kodols) nevar noteikt "
"pareizo ģeometriju, un tā būs jānorāda."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8953 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14466
msgid ""
"C<lines> is a list of lines that we feed to L<sfdisk(8)>.  For more "
"information refer to the L<sfdisk(8)> manpage."
msgstr ""
"C<lines> ir rindu saraksts, ko padodam L<sfdisk(8)>.  Plašāku informāciju "
"skatiet L<sfdisk(8)> rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8956 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14469
msgid ""
"To create a single partition occupying the whole disk, you would pass "
"C<lines> as a single element list, when the single element being the string "
"C<,> (comma)."
msgstr ""
"Lai izveidotu vienu nodalījumu, kas aizņem visu disku, C<lines> jānodod kā "
"viena elementa saraksts, kur vienīgais elements ir virkne C<,> (komats)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8960
msgid "See also: L</sfdisk-l>, L</sfdisk-N>, L</part-init>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</sfdisk-l>, L</sfdisk-N>, L</part-init>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8963 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8983
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9002
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</part-add> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"part-add>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8970
msgid "sfdiskM"
msgstr "sfdiskM"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8972
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sfdiskM device 'lines ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sfdiskM device 'lines ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8974
msgid ""
"This is a simplified interface to the L</sfdisk> command, where partition "
"sizes are specified in megabytes only (rounded to the nearest cylinder) and "
"you don't need to specify the cyls, heads and sectors parameters which were "
"rarely if ever used anyway."
msgstr ""
"Šī ir vienkāršota saskarne komandai L</sfdisk>, kur nodalījumu izmēri "
"norādīti tikai megabaitos (noapaļoti līdz tuvākajam cilindram), un nav "
"jānorāda parametri cyls, heads un sectors, kas tik un tā tika izmantoti "
"reti, ja vispār."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8980
msgid "See also: L</sfdisk>, the L<sfdisk(8)> manpage and L</part-disk>"
msgstr ""
"Skatīt arī: L</sfdisk>, L<sfdisk(8)> rokasgrāmatas lapu un L</part-disk>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8990
msgid "sfdisk-N"
msgstr "sfdisk-N"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8992
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sfdisk-N device partnum cyls heads sectors line\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sfdisk-N device partnum cyls heads sectors line\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8994 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14525
msgid ""
"This runs L<sfdisk(8)> option to modify just the single partition C<n> "
"(note: C<n> counts from 1)."
msgstr ""
"Tas izpilda L<sfdisk(8)> opciju, lai mainītu tikai vienu nodalījumu C<n> "
"(piezīme: C<n> tiek skaitīts no 1)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:8997
msgid ""
"For other parameters, see L</sfdisk>.  You should usually pass C<0> for the "
"cyls/heads/sectors parameters."
msgstr ""
"Citus parametrus skatiet L</sfdisk>.  Parametriem cyls/heads/sectors parasti "
"jānodod C<0>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9000
msgid "See also: L</part-add>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</part-add>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9009
msgid "sfdisk-disk-geometry"
msgstr "sfdisk-disk-geometry"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9011
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sfdisk-disk-geometry device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sfdisk-disk-geometry device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9013
msgid ""
"This displays the disk geometry of C<device> read from the partition table.  "
"Especially in the case where the underlying block device has been resized, "
"this can be different from the kernel’s idea of the geometry (see "
"L</sfdisk-kernel-geometry>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas parāda ierīces C<device> diska ģeometriju, kas nolasīta no nodalījumu "
"tabulas.  It īpaši gadījumā, ja pamatā esošās bloku ierīces izmērs ir "
"mainīts, tā var atšķirties no kodola priekšstata par ģeometriju (skatiet L</"
"sfdisk-kernel-geometry>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9018 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9027
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14548 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14564
msgid "The result is in human-readable format, and not designed to be parsed."
msgstr "Rezultāts ir cilvēkam lasāmā formātā un nav paredzēts parsēšanai."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9021
msgid "sfdisk-kernel-geometry"
msgstr "sfdisk-kernel-geometry"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9023
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sfdisk-kernel-geometry device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sfdisk-kernel-geometry device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9025 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14562
msgid "This displays the kernel’s idea of the geometry of C<device>."
msgstr "Tas parāda kodola priekšstatu par ierīces C<device> ģeometriju."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9030
msgid "sfdisk-l"
msgstr "sfdisk-l"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9032
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sfdisk-l device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sfdisk-l device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9034 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14585
msgid ""
"This displays the partition table on C<device>, in the human-readable output "
"of the L<sfdisk(8)> command.  It is not intended to be parsed."
msgstr ""
"Tas parāda nodalījumu tabulu ierīcē C<device> komandas L<sfdisk(8)> cilvēkam "
"lasāmajā izvadē.  Tā nav paredzēta parsēšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9038
msgid "See also: L</part-list>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</part-list>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9040
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</part-list> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"part-list>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9047
msgid "sh"
msgstr "sh"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9049
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sh command\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sh command\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9051 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14602
msgid ""
"This call runs a command from the guest filesystem via the guest’s "
"F</bin/sh>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums izpilda komandu no viesa failu sistēmas caur viesa F</bin/sh>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9054
msgid "This is like L</command>, but passes the command to:"
msgstr "Tas ir līdzīgi L</command>, bet nodod komandu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9056 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14607
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /bin/sh -c \"command\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /bin/sh -c \"command\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9058 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14609
msgid ""
"Depending on the guest’s shell, this usually results in wildcards being "
"expanded, shell expressions being interpolated and so on."
msgstr ""
"Atkarībā no viesa čaulas tas parasti nozīmē, ka aizstājējzīmes tiek "
"izvērstas, čaulas izteiksmes tiek interpolētas u. tml."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9062
msgid "All the provisos about L</command> apply to this call."
msgstr "Uz šo izsaukumu attiecas visas L</command> atrunas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9064
msgid "sh-lines"
msgstr "sh-lines"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9066
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sh-lines command\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sh-lines command\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9068
msgid "This is the same as L</sh>, but splits the result into a list of lines."
msgstr "Tas ir tas pats, kas L</sh>, bet sadala rezultātu rindu sarakstā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9071
msgid "See also: L</command-lines>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</command-lines>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9073
msgid "sh-out"
msgstr "sh-out"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9075
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sh-out command (output|-)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sh-out command (output|-)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9077
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</sh>, but streams the output back, handling the case "
"where the output from the command is larger than the protocol limit."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</sh>, bet straumē izvadi atpakaļ, apstrādājot "
"gadījumu, kad komandas izvade ir lielāka par protokola ierobežojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9081
msgid "See also: L</command-out>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</command-out>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9085
msgid "shutdown"
msgstr "shutdown"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9087
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" shutdown\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" shutdown\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9089
msgid ""
"This is the opposite of L</launch>.  It performs an orderly shutdown of the "
"backend process(es).  If the autosync flag is set (which is the default) "
"then the disk image is synchronized."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir pretējs L</launch>.  Tas veic sakārtotu aizmugursistēmas procesa(-u) "
"izslēgšanu.  Ja ir iestatīts automātiskās sinhronizācijas karogs (kas ir "
"noklusējums), diska attēls tiek sinhronizēts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9093 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14663
msgid ""
"If the subprocess exits with an error then this function will return an "
"error, which should I<not> be ignored (it may indicate that the disk image "
"could not be written out properly)."
msgstr ""
"Ja apakšprocess iziet ar kļūdu, šī funkcija atgriezīs kļūdu, ko "
"I<nevajadzētu> ignorēt (tā var norādīt, ka diska attēlu nevarēja pareizi "
"izrakstīt)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9097 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14667
msgid "It is safe to call this multiple times.  Extra calls are ignored."
msgstr "To droši var izsaukt vairākas reizes.  Papildu izsaukumi tiek ignorēti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9099
msgid ""
"This call does I<not> close or free up the handle.  You still need to call "
"L</close> afterwards."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums I<neaizver> un neatbrīvo rokturi.  Pēc tam joprojām jāizsauc "
"L</close>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9102
msgid ""
"L</close> will call this if you don't do it explicitly, but note that any "
"errors are ignored in that case."
msgstr ""
"L</close> to izsauks, ja to neizdarāt eksplicīti, taču ņemiet vērā, ka tādā "
"gadījumā visas kļūdas tiek ignorētas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9105
msgid "sleep"
msgstr "sleep"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sleep secs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sleep secs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9109 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14685
msgid "Sleep for C<secs> seconds."
msgstr "Gulēt C<secs> sekundes."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9111
msgid "stat"
msgstr "stat"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9113
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" stat path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" stat path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9117 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9132
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14706 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14722
msgid "This is the same as the L<stat(2)> system call."
msgstr "Tas ir tas pats, kas sistēmas izsaukums L<stat(2)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9119
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</statns> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"statns>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9126
msgid "statns"
msgstr "statns"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" statns path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" statns path\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9134
msgid "statvfs"
msgstr "statvfs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" statvfs path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" statvfs path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9138 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14736
msgid ""
"Returns file system statistics for any mounted file system.  C<path> should "
"be a file or directory in the mounted file system (typically it is the mount "
"point itself, but it doesn't need to be)."
msgstr ""
"Atgriež failu sistēmas statistiku jebkurai montētai failu sistēmai.  C<path> "
"jābūt failam vai direktorijai montētajā failu sistēmā (parasti tas ir pats "
"montēšanas punkts, bet tam nav jābūt)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9142 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14740
msgid "This is the same as the L<statvfs(2)> system call."
msgstr "Tas ir tas pats, kas sistēmas izsaukums L<statvfs(2)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9144
msgid "strings"
msgstr "strings"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9146
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" strings path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" strings path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9148 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14754
msgid ""
"This runs the L<strings(1)> command on a file and returns the list of "
"printable strings found."
msgstr ""
"Tas izpilda komandu L<strings(1)> failam un atgriež atrasto izdrukājamo "
"virkņu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9151 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9201
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14757 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14816
msgid ""
"The C<strings> command has, in the past, had problems with parsing untrusted "
"files.  These are mitigated in the current version of libguestfs, but see "
"L<guestfs(3)/CVE-2014-8484>."
msgstr ""
"Komandai C<strings> agrāk bija problēmas ar neuzticamu failu parsēšanu.  "
"Pašreizējā libguestfs versijā tās ir mazinātas, bet skatiet L<guestfs(3)/CVE-"
"2014-8484>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9158
msgid "strings-e"
msgstr "strings-e"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9160
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" strings-e encoding path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" strings-e encoding path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9162
msgid ""
"This is like the L</strings> command, but allows you to specify the encoding "
"of strings that are looked for in the source file C<path>."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir līdzīgi komandai L</strings>, bet ļauj norādīt virkņu kodējumu, kas "
"tiek meklētas avota failā C<path>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9166 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14781
msgid "Allowed encodings are:"
msgstr "Atļautie kodējumi ir:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9170 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14785
msgid "s"
msgstr "s"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9172
msgid ""
"Single 7-bit-byte characters like ASCII and the ASCII-compatible parts of "
"ISO-8859-X (this is what L</strings> uses)."
msgstr ""
"Vienbaita 7 bitu rakstzīmes, piemēram, ASCII un ISO-8859-X ar ASCII "
"saderīgās daļas (to izmanto L</strings>)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9175 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14790
msgid "S"
msgstr "S"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9177 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14792
msgid "Single 8-bit-byte characters."
msgstr "Vienbaita 8 bitu rakstzīmes."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9179 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14794
msgid "b"
msgstr "b"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9181 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14796
msgid "16-bit big endian strings such as those encoded in UTF-16BE or UCS-2BE."
msgstr "16 bitu big endian virknes, piemēram, kodētas UTF-16BE vai UCS-2BE."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9184 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14799
msgid "l (lower case letter L)"
msgstr "l (mazais burts L)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9186 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14801
msgid ""
"16-bit little endian such as UTF-16LE and UCS-2LE.  This is useful for "
"examining binaries in Windows guests."
msgstr ""
"16 bitu little endian, piemēram, UTF-16LE un UCS-2LE.  Tas noder bināro "
"failu pārbaudei Windows viesos."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9189 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14804
msgid "B"
msgstr "B"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9191 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14806
msgid "32-bit big endian such as UCS-4BE."
msgstr "32 bitu big endian, piemēram, UCS-4BE."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9193 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14808
msgid "L"
msgstr "L"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9195 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14810
msgid "32-bit little endian such as UCS-4LE."
msgstr "32 bitu little endian, piemēram, UCS-4LE."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9199 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14814
msgid "The returned strings are transcoded to UTF-8."
msgstr "Atgrieztās virknes tiek pārkodētas uz UTF-8."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9208
msgid "swapoff-device"
msgstr "swapoff-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9210
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapoff-device device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapoff-device device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9212
msgid ""
"This command disables the libguestfs appliance swap device or partition "
"named C<device>.  See L</swapon-device>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atspējo libguestfs palīgsistēmas maiņatmiņas ierīci vai "
"nodalījumu C<device>.  Skatiet L</swapon-device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9216
msgid "swapoff-file"
msgstr "swapoff-file"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9218
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapoff-file file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapoff-file file\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9220 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14849
msgid "This command disables the libguestfs appliance swap on file."
msgstr "Šī komanda atspējo libguestfs palīgsistēmas maiņatmiņu failā."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9222
msgid "swapoff-label"
msgstr "swapoff-label"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9224
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapoff-label label\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapoff-label label\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9226 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14861
msgid ""
"This command disables the libguestfs appliance swap on labeled swap "
"partition."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atspējo libguestfs palīgsistēmas maiņatmiņu maiņatmiņas "
"nodalījumā ar etiķeti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9229
msgid "swapoff-uuid"
msgstr "swapoff-uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapoff-uuid uuid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapoff-uuid uuid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9233 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14874
msgid ""
"This command disables the libguestfs appliance swap partition with the given "
"UUID."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atspējo libguestfs palīgsistēmas maiņatmiņas nodalījumu ar doto "
"UUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9239
msgid "swapon-device"
msgstr "swapon-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9241
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapon-device device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapon-device device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9243
msgid ""
"This command enables the libguestfs appliance to use the swap device or "
"partition named C<device>.  The increased memory is made available for all "
"commands, for example those run using L</command> or L</sh>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ļauj libguestfs palīgsistēmai izmantot maiņatmiņas ierīci vai "
"nodalījumu C<device>.  Palielinātā atmiņa ir pieejama visām komandām, "
"piemēram, tām, kas izpildītas ar L</command> vai L</sh>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9248 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14895
msgid ""
"Note that you should not swap to existing guest swap partitions unless you "
"know what you are doing.  They may contain hibernation information, or other "
"information that the guest doesn't want you to trash.  You also risk leaking "
"information about the host to the guest this way.  Instead, attach a new "
"host device to the guest and swap on that."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka nevajadzētu izmantot esošos viesa maiņatmiņas nodalījumus, "
"ja vien nezināt, ko darāt.  Tie var saturēt hibernācijas informāciju vai "
"citu informāciju, ko viesis nevēlas, lai jūs sabojātu.  Šādi arī riskējat "
"nopludināt viesim informāciju par resursdatoru.  Tā vietā pievienojiet "
"viesim jaunu resursdatora ierīci un izmantojiet maiņatmiņu tajā."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9255
msgid "swapon-file"
msgstr "swapon-file"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9257
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapon-file file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapon-file file\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9259
msgid "This command enables swap to a file.  See L</swapon-device> for other notes."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda iespējo maiņatmiņu failā.  Citas piezīmes skatiet L</swapon-"
"device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9262
msgid "swapon-label"
msgstr "swapon-label"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9264
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapon-label label\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapon-label label\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9266
msgid ""
"This command enables swap to a labeled swap partition.  See "
"L</swapon-device> for other notes."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda iespējo maiņatmiņu maiņatmiņas nodalījumā ar etiķeti.  Citas "
"piezīmes skatiet L</swapon-device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9269
msgid "swapon-uuid"
msgstr "swapon-uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9271
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" swapon-uuid uuid\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" swapon-uuid uuid\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9273
msgid ""
"This command enables swap to a swap partition with the given UUID.  See "
"L</swapon-device> for other notes."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda iespējo maiņatmiņu maiņatmiņas nodalījumā ar doto UUID.  Citas "
"piezīmes skatiet L</swapon-device>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9279
msgid "sync"
msgstr "sync"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9281
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sync\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sync\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9283 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14953
msgid ""
"This syncs the disk, so that any writes are flushed through to the "
"underlying disk image."
msgstr ""
"Tas sinhronizē disku, lai visa rakstīšana tiktu izskalota uz pamatā esošo "
"diska attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9286 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14956
msgid ""
"You should always call this if you have modified a disk image, before "
"closing the handle."
msgstr ""
"Ja diska attēls mainīts, pirms roktura aizvēršanas to vienmēr vajadzētu "
"izsaukt."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9289
msgid "syslinux"
msgstr "syslinux"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9291
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" syslinux device [directory:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" syslinux device [directory:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9293 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14977
msgid "Install the SYSLINUX bootloader on C<device>."
msgstr "Instalēt SYSLINUX sāknēšanas ielādētāju ierīcē C<device>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9295
msgid ""
"The device parameter must be either a whole disk formatted as a FAT "
"filesystem, or a partition formatted as a FAT filesystem.  In the latter "
"case, the partition should be marked as \"active\" (L</part-set-bootable>) "
"and a Master Boot Record must be installed (eg. using L</pwrite-device>) on "
"the first sector of the whole disk.  The SYSLINUX package comes with some "
"suitable Master Boot Records.  See the L<syslinux(1)> man page for further "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Parametram device jābūt vai nu visam diskam, kas formatēts kā FAT failu "
"sistēma, vai nodalījumam, kas formatēts kā FAT failu sistēma.  Pēdējā "
"gadījumā nodalījums jāatzīmē kā „aktīvs” (L</part-set-bootable>), un visa "
"diska pirmajā sektorā jāinstalē galvenais sāknēšanas ieraksts (piem., ar L</"
"pwrite-device>).  SYSLINUX pakotnei ir daži piemēroti galvenie sāknēšanas "
"ieraksti.  Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<syslinux(1)> rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9308 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14992
msgid "F<directory>"
msgstr "F<directory>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9310 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14994
msgid ""
"Install SYSLINUX in the named subdirectory, instead of in the root directory "
"of the FAT filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Instalēt SYSLINUX nosauktajā apakšdirektorijā, nevis FAT failu sistēmas "
"saknes direktorijā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9315 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:14999
msgid ""
"Additional configuration can be supplied to SYSLINUX by placing a file "
"called F<syslinux.cfg> on the FAT filesystem, either in the root directory, "
"or under F<directory> if that optional argument is being used.  For further "
"information about the contents of this file, see L<syslinux(1)>."
msgstr ""
"SYSLINUX papildu konfigurāciju var nodrošināt, novietojot failu "
"F<syslinux.cfg> FAT failu sistēmā vai nu saknes direktorijā, vai zem "
"F<directory>, ja tiek izmantots šis neobligātais arguments.  Plašāku "
"informāciju par šī faila saturu skatiet L<syslinux(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9321
msgid "See also L</extlinux>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</extlinux>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9325
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<syslinux>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<syslinux>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9328
msgid "tail"
msgstr "tail"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9330
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tail path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tail path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9332 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15042
msgid "This command returns up to the last 10 lines of a file as a list of strings."
msgstr "Šī komanda atgriež līdz 10 pēdējām faila rindām kā virkņu sarakstu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9338
msgid "tail-n"
msgstr "tail-n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9340
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tail-n nrlines path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tail-n nrlines path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9342 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15061
msgid ""
"If the parameter C<nrlines> is a positive number, this returns the last "
"C<nrlines> lines of the file C<path>."
msgstr ""
"Ja parametrs C<nrlines> ir pozitīvs skaitlis, tas atgriež faila C<path> "
"pēdējās C<nrlines> rindas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9345 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15064
msgid ""
"If the parameter C<nrlines> is a negative number, this returns lines from "
"the file C<path>, starting with the C<-nrlines>'th line."
msgstr ""
"Ja parametrs C<nrlines> ir negatīvs skaitlis, tas atgriež faila C<path> "
"rindas, sākot ar C<-nrlines>-o rindu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9353
msgid "tar-in"
msgstr "tar-in"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9355
msgid "tar-in-opts"
msgstr "tar-in-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9357
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tar-in (tarfile|-) directory [compress:..] [xattrs:true|false] "
"[selinux:true|false] [acls:true|false] [keepdirlink:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tar-in (tarfile|-) directory [compress:..] [xattrs:true|false] "
"[selinux:true|false] [acls:true|false] [keepdirlink:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9359 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15111
msgid "This command uploads and unpacks local file C<tarfile> into F<directory>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda augšupielādē un izpako lokālo failu C<tarfile> direktorijā "
"F<directory>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9361 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15113
msgid ""
"The optional C<compress> flag controls compression.  If not given, then the "
"input should be an uncompressed tar file.  Otherwise one of the following "
"strings may be given to select the compression type of the input file: "
"C<compress>, C<gzip>, C<bzip2>, C<xz>, C<lzop>, C<lzma>, C<zstd>.  (Note "
"that not all builds of libguestfs will support all of these compression "
"types)."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātais karogs C<compress> kontrolē saspiešanu.  Ja nav norādīts, "
"ievadei jābūt nesaspiestam tar failam.  Citādi var norādīt vienu no šīm "
"virknēm, lai izvēlētos ievades faila saspiešanas tipu: C<compress>, C<gzip>, "
"C<bzip2>, C<xz>, C<lzop>, C<lzma>, C<zstd>.  (Ņemiet vērā, ka ne visas "
"libguestfs būves atbalstīs visus šos saspiešanas tipus.)"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9372 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9426
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15124 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15230
msgid "C<xattrs>"
msgstr "C<xattrs>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9374 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15126
msgid "If set to true, extended attributes are restored from the tar file."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīts uz true, paplašinātie atribūti tiek atjaunoti no tar faila."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9376 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9430
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15128 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15234
msgid "C<selinux>"
msgstr "C<selinux>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9378 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15130
msgid "If set to true, SELinux contexts are restored from the tar file."
msgstr "Ja iestatīts uz true, SELinux konteksti tiek atjaunoti no tar faila."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9380 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9434
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15132 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15238
msgid "C<acls>"
msgstr "C<acls>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9382 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15134
msgid "If set to true, POSIX ACLs are restored from the tar file."
msgstr "Ja iestatīts uz true, POSIX ACL tiek atjaunoti no tar faila."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9384 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15136
msgid "C<keepdirlink>"
msgstr "C<keepdirlink>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9386 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15138
msgid ""
"If set to true, existing symlinks to directories are followed when "
"extracting from the tar file.  This is important for usrmerge systems where "
"F</lib> is a symlink to F</usr/lib>."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīts uz true, izpakojot no tar faila, tiek sekots esošajām "
"simboliskajām saitēm uz direktorijām.  Tas ir svarīgi usrmerge sistēmām, kur "
"F</lib> ir simboliskā saite uz F</usr/lib>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9396
msgid "tar-out"
msgstr "tar-out"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9398
msgid "tar-out-opts"
msgstr "tar-out-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9400
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tar-out directory (tarfile|-) [compress:..] [numericowner:true|false] "
"[excludes:..] [xattrs:true|false] [selinux:true|false] [acls:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tar-out directory (tarfile|-) [compress:..] [numericowner:true|false] "
"[excludes:..] [xattrs:true|false] [selinux:true|false] [acls:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9402 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15206
msgid ""
"This command packs the contents of F<directory> and downloads it to local "
"file C<tarfile>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda iepako F<directory> saturu un lejupielādē to lokālajā failā "
"C<tarfile>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9405 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15209
msgid ""
"The optional C<compress> flag controls compression.  If not given, then the "
"output will be an uncompressed tar file.  Otherwise one of the following "
"strings may be given to select the compression type of the output file: "
"C<compress>, C<gzip>, C<bzip2>, C<xz>, C<lzop>, C<lzma>, C<zstd>.  (Note "
"that not all builds of libguestfs will support all of these compression "
"types)."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātais karogs C<compress> kontrolē saspiešanu.  Ja nav norādīts, "
"izvade būs nesaspiests tar fails.  Citādi var norādīt vienu no šīm virknēm, "
"lai izvēlētos izvades faila saspiešanas tipu: C<compress>, C<gzip>, C<bzip2>"
", C<xz>, C<lzop>, C<lzma>, C<zstd>.  (Ņemiet vērā, ka ne visas libguestfs "
"būves atbalstīs visus šos saspiešanas tipus.)"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9421 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15225
msgid "C<numericowner>"
msgstr "C<numericowner>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9423 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15227
msgid ""
"If set to true, the output tar file will contain UID/GID numbers instead of "
"user/group names."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīts uz true, izvades tar fails saturēs UID/GID numurus, nevis "
"lietotāju/grupu nosaukumus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9428 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15232
msgid "If set to true, extended attributes are saved in the output tar."
msgstr "Ja iestatīts uz true, paplašinātie atribūti tiek saglabāti izvades tar."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9432 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15236
msgid "If set to true, SELinux contexts are saved in the output tar."
msgstr "Ja iestatīts uz true, SELinux konteksti tiek saglabāti izvades tar."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9436 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15240
msgid "If set to true, POSIX ACLs are saved in the output tar."
msgstr "Ja iestatīts uz true, POSIX ACL tiek saglabāti izvades tar."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9444
msgid "tgz-in"
msgstr "tgz-in"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9446
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tgz-in (tarball|-) directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tgz-in (tarball|-) directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9448 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15286
msgid ""
"This command uploads and unpacks local file C<tarball> (a I<gzip compressed> "
"tar file) into F<directory>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda augšupielādē un izpako lokālo failu C<tarball> (ar I<gzip "
"saspiestu> tar failu) direktorijā F<directory>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9453 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9607
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</tar-in> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"tar-in>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9460
msgid "tgz-out"
msgstr "tgz-out"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9462
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tgz-out directory (tarball|-)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tgz-out directory (tarball|-)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9464 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15307
msgid ""
"This command packs the contents of F<directory> and downloads it to local "
"file C<tarball>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda iepako F<directory> saturu un lejupielādē to lokālajā failā "
"C<tarball>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9469 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9626
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</tar-out> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"tar-out>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9476
msgid "touch"
msgstr "touch"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9478
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" touch path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" touch path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9480 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15320
msgid ""
"Touch acts like the L<touch(1)> command.  It can be used to update the "
"timestamps on a file, or, if the file does not exist, to create a new "
"zero-length file."
msgstr ""
"Touch darbojas kā komanda L<touch(1)>.  To var izmantot faila laikspiedolu "
"atjaunināšanai vai, ja fails neeksistē, jauna nulles garuma faila izveidei."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9484 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15324
msgid ""
"This command only works on regular files, and will fail on other file types "
"such as directories, symbolic links, block special etc."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda darbojas tikai ar parastiem failiem un neizdosies ar citiem failu "
"tipiem, piemēram, direktorijām, simboliskajām saitēm, bloku speciālajiem "
"failiem u. c."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9487
msgid "truncate"
msgstr "truncate"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9489
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" truncate path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" truncate path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9491 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15337
msgid ""
"This command truncates C<path> to a zero-length file.  The file must exist "
"already."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda saīsina C<path> līdz nulles garuma failam.  Failam jau jāeksistē."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9494
msgid "truncate-size"
msgstr "truncate-size"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9496
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" truncate-size path size\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" truncate-size path size\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9498 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15351
msgid ""
"This command truncates C<path> to size C<size> bytes.  The file must exist "
"already."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda saīsina C<path> līdz izmēram C<size> baiti.  Failam jau jāeksistē."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9501
msgid ""
"If the current file size is less than C<size> then the file is extended to "
"the required size with zero bytes.  This creates a sparse file (ie. disk "
"blocks are not allocated for the file until you write to it).  To create a "
"non-sparse file of zeroes, use L</fallocate64> instead."
msgstr ""
"Ja pašreizējais faila izmērs ir mazāks par C<size>, fails tiek paplašināts "
"līdz vajadzīgajam izmēram ar nulles baitiem.  Tas izveido retinātu failu (t. "
"i., diska bloki failam netiek piešķirti, līdz tajā rakstāt).  Lai izveidotu "
"neretinātu nulles failu, tā vietā izmantojiet L</fallocate64>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9507
msgid "tune2fs"
msgstr "tune2fs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9509
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tune2fs device [force:true|false] [maxmountcount:N] [mountcount:N] "
"[errorbehavior:..] [group:N] [intervalbetweenchecks:N] "
"[reservedblockspercentage:N] [lastmounteddirectory:..] "
"[reservedblockscount:N] [user:N]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tune2fs device [force:true|false] [maxmountcount:N] [mountcount:N] "
"[errorbehavior:..] [group:N] [intervalbetweenchecks:N] "
"[reservedblockspercentage:N] [lastmounteddirectory:..] "
"[reservedblockscount:N] [user:N]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9511 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15387
msgid ""
"This call allows you to adjust various filesystem parameters of an "
"ext2/ext3/ext4 filesystem called C<device>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums ļauj pielāgot dažādus ext2/ext3/ext4 failu sistēmas C<device> "
"parametrus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9520 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15396
msgid ""
"Force tune2fs to complete the operation even in the face of errors.  This is "
"the same as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-f> option."
msgstr ""
"Piespiest tune2fs pabeigt darbību pat kļūdu gadījumā.  Tas ir tas pats, kas "
"L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-f>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9523 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15399
msgid "C<maxmountcount>"
msgstr "C<maxmountcount>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9525 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15401
msgid ""
"Set the number of mounts after which the filesystem is checked by "
"L<e2fsck(8)>.  If this is C<0> then the number of mounts is disregarded.  "
"This is the same as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-c> option."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt montēšanu skaitu, pēc kura failu sistēmu pārbauda L<e2fsck(8)>.  Ja "
"tas ir C<0>, montēšanu skaits netiek ņemts vērā.  Tas ir tas pats, kas "
"L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-c>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9529 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15405
msgid "C<mountcount>"
msgstr "C<mountcount>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9531 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15407
msgid ""
"Set the number of times the filesystem has been mounted.  This is the same "
"as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-C> option."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt, cik reižu failu sistēma ir montēta.  Tas ir tas pats, kas L<tune2fs"
"(8)> opcija C<-C>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9534 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15410
msgid "C<errorbehavior>"
msgstr "C<errorbehavior>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9536 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15412
msgid ""
"Change the behavior of the kernel code when errors are detected.  Possible "
"values currently are: C<continue>, C<remount-ro>, C<panic>.  In practice "
"these options don't really make any difference, particularly for write "
"errors."
msgstr ""
"Mainīt kodola koda uzvedību, kad tiek konstatētas kļūdas.  Pašlaik "
"iespējamās vērtības ir: C<continue>, C<remount-ro>, C<panic>.  Praksē šīs "
"opcijas īsti neko nemaina, it īpaši rakstīšanas kļūdām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9541 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15417
msgid "This is the same as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-e> option."
msgstr "Tas ir tas pats, kas L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-e>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9543 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15419
msgid "C<group>"
msgstr "C<group>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9545 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15421
msgid ""
"Set the group which can use reserved filesystem blocks.  This is the same as "
"the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-g> option except that it can only be specified as a "
"number."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt grupu, kas var izmantot rezervētos failu sistēmas blokus.  Tas ir "
"tas pats, kas L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-g>, izņemot to, ka to var norādīt "
"tikai kā skaitli."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9549 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15425
msgid "C<intervalbetweenchecks>"
msgstr "C<intervalbetweenchecks>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9551 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15427
msgid ""
"Adjust the maximal time between two filesystem checks (in seconds).  If the "
"option is passed as C<0> then time-dependent checking is disabled."
msgstr ""
"Pielāgot maksimālo laiku starp divām failu sistēmas pārbaudēm (sekundēs).  "
"Ja opcija nodota kā C<0>, no laika atkarīgā pārbaude ir atspējota."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9555 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15431
msgid "This is the same as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-i> option."
msgstr "Tas ir tas pats, kas L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-i>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9557 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15433
msgid "C<reservedblockspercentage>"
msgstr "C<reservedblockspercentage>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9559 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15435
msgid ""
"Set the percentage of the filesystem which may only be allocated by "
"privileged processes.  This is the same as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-m> option."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt failu sistēmas procentuālo daļu, ko var piešķirt tikai priviliģēti "
"procesi.  Tas ir tas pats, kas L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-m>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9563 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15439
msgid "C<lastmounteddirectory>"
msgstr "C<lastmounteddirectory>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9565 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15441
msgid ""
"Set the last mounted directory.  This is the same as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-M> "
"option."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt pēdējo montēšanas direktoriju.  Tas ir tas pats, kas L<tune2fs(8)> "
"opcija C<-M>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9568 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15444
msgid ""
"C<reservedblockscount> Set the number of reserved filesystem blocks.  This "
"is the same as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-r> option."
msgstr ""
"C<reservedblockscount> Iestatīt rezervēto failu sistēmas bloku skaitu.  Tas "
"ir tas pats, kas L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-r>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9572 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15448
msgid "C<user>"
msgstr "C<user>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9574 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15450
msgid ""
"Set the user who can use the reserved filesystem blocks.  This is the same "
"as the L<tune2fs(8)> C<-u> option except that it can only be specified as a "
"number."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt lietotāju, kas var izmantot rezervētos failu sistēmas blokus.  Tas "
"ir tas pats, kas L<tune2fs(8)> opcija C<-u>, izņemot to, ka to var norādīt "
"tikai kā skaitli."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9580
msgid ""
"To get the current values of filesystem parameters, see L</tune2fs-l>.  For "
"precise details of how tune2fs works, see the L<tune2fs(8)> man page."
msgstr ""
"Lai iegūtu pašreizējās failu sistēmas parametru vērtības, skatiet L</tune2fs-"
"l>.  Precīzu informāciju par tune2fs darbību skatiet L<tune2fs(8)> "
"rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9586
msgid "tune2fs-l"
msgstr "tune2fs-l"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9588
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tune2fs-l device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tune2fs-l device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9590 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15492
msgid ""
"This returns the contents of the ext2, ext3 or ext4 filesystem superblock on "
"C<device>."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež ext2, ext3 vai ext4 failu sistēmas superbloka saturu ierīcē "
"C<device>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9593 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15495
msgid ""
"It is the same as running C<tune2fs -l device>.  See L<tune2fs(8)> manpage "
"for more details.  The list of fields returned isn't clearly defined, and "
"depends on both the version of C<tune2fs> that libguestfs was built against, "
"and the filesystem itself."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas C<tune2fs -l device> izpilde.  Sīkāk skatiet L<tune2fs"
"(8)> rokasgrāmatas lapu.  Atgriezto lauku saraksts nav skaidri definēts un "
"ir atkarīgs gan no C<tune2fs> versijas, pret kuru libguestfs tika būvēta, "
"gan no pašas failu sistēmas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9598
msgid "txz-in"
msgstr "txz-in"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9600
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" txz-in (tarball|-) directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" txz-in (tarball|-) directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9602 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15522
msgid ""
"This command uploads and unpacks local file C<tarball> (an I<xz compressed> "
"tar file) into F<directory>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda augšupielādē un izpako lokālo failu C<tarball> (ar I<xz "
"saspiestu> tar failu) direktorijā F<directory>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9614 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9633
msgid "This command depends on the feature C<xz>.  See also L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<xz>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9617
msgid "txz-out"
msgstr "txz-out"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9619
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" txz-out directory (tarball|-)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" txz-out directory (tarball|-)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9621 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15546
msgid ""
"This command packs the contents of F<directory> and downloads it to local "
"file C<tarball> (as an xz compressed tar archive)."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda iepako F<directory> saturu un lejupielādē to lokālajā failā "
"C<tarball> (kā ar xz saspiestu tar arhīvu)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9636
msgid "umask"
msgstr "umask"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9638
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" umask mask\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" umask mask\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9640 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15562
msgid ""
"This function sets the mask used for creating new files and device nodes to "
"C<mask & 0777>."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija iestata masku, ko izmanto jaunu failu un ierīču mezglu izveidei, "
"uz C<mask & 0777>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9643 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15565
msgid ""
"Typical umask values would be C<022> which creates new files with "
"permissions like \"-rw-r--r--\" or \"-rwxr-xr-x\", and C<002> which creates "
"new files with permissions like \"-rw-rw-r--\" or \"-rwxrwxr-x\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipiskas umask vērtības būtu C<022>, kas izveido jaunus failus ar atļaujām, "
"piemēram, „-rw-r--r--” vai „-rwxr-xr-x”, un C<002>, kas izveido jaunus "
"failus ar atļaujām, piemēram, „-rw-rw-r--” vai „-rwxrwxr-x”."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9648 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15570
msgid ""
"The default umask is C<022>.  This is important because it means that "
"directories and device nodes will be created with C<0644> or C<0755> mode "
"even if you specify C<0777>."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma umask ir C<022>.  Tas ir svarīgi, jo tas nozīmē, ka direktorijas "
"un ierīču mezgli tiks izveidoti ar režīmu C<0644> vai C<0755>, pat ja "
"norādāt C<0777>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9652
msgid "See also L</get-umask>, L<umask(2)>, L</mknod>, L</mkdir>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</get-umask>, L<umask(2)>, L</mknod>, L</mkdir>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9655 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15577
msgid "This call returns the previous umask."
msgstr "Šis izsaukums atgriež iepriekšējo umask."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9657
msgid "umount"
msgstr "umount"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9659
msgid "unmount"
msgstr "unmount"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9661
msgid "umount-opts"
msgstr "umount-opts"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9663
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" umount pathordevice [force:true|false] [lazyunmount:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" umount pathordevice [force:true|false] [lazyunmount:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9665 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15611
msgid ""
"This unmounts the given filesystem.  The filesystem may be specified either "
"by its mountpoint (path) or the device which contains the filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Tas atmontē doto failu sistēmu.  Failu sistēmu var norādīt vai nu ar tās "
"montēšanas punktu (ceļu), vai ar ierīci, kas satur failu sistēmu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9671
msgid "umount-all"
msgstr "umount-all"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9673
msgid "unmount-all"
msgstr "unmount-all"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9675
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" umount-all\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" umount-all\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9677 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15646
msgid "This unmounts all mounted filesystems."
msgstr "Tas atmontē visas montētās failu sistēmas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9679 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15648
msgid "Some internal mounts are not unmounted by this call."
msgstr "Daži iekšējie montējumi ar šo izsaukumu netiek atmontēti."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9681
msgid "umount-local"
msgstr "umount-local"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9683
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" umount-local [retry:true|false]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" umount-local [retry:true|false]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9685 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15667
msgid ""
"If libguestfs is exporting the filesystem on a local mountpoint, then this "
"unmounts it."
msgstr ""
"Ja libguestfs eksportē failu sistēmu lokālā montēšanas punktā, tas to "
"atmontē."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9692
msgid "upload"
msgstr "upload"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9694
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" upload (filename|-) remotefilename\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" upload (filename|-) remotefilename\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9696 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9709
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15703 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15727
msgid "Upload local file F<filename> to F<remotefilename> on the filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Augšupielādēt lokālo failu F<filename> uz F<remotefilename> failu sistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9701
msgid "See also L</download>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</download>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9705
msgid "upload-offset"
msgstr "upload-offset"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9707
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" upload-offset (filename|-) remotefilename offset\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" upload-offset (filename|-) remotefilename offset\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9712 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15730
msgid ""
"F<remotefilename> is overwritten starting at the byte C<offset> specified.  "
"The intention is to overwrite parts of existing files or devices, although "
"if a non-existent file is specified then it is created with a \"hole\" "
"before C<offset>.  The size of the data written is implicit in the size of "
"the source F<filename>."
msgstr ""
"F<remotefilename> tiek pārrakstīts, sākot no norādītā baita C<offset>.  "
"Mērķis ir pārrakstīt esošu failu vai ierīču daļas, lai gan, ja norādīts "
"neeksistējošs fails, tas tiek izveidots ar „caurumu” pirms C<offset>.  "
"Ierakstīto datu izmērs izriet no avota F<filename> izmēra."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9719
msgid ""
"Note that there is no limit on the amount of data that can be uploaded with "
"this call, unlike with L</pwrite>, and this call always writes the full "
"amount unless an error occurs."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka atšķirībā no L</pwrite> datu apjomam, ko var augšupielādēt "
"ar šo izsaukumu, nav ierobežojuma, un šis izsaukums vienmēr ieraksta pilnu "
"apjomu, ja vien nenotiek kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9724
msgid "See also L</upload>, L</pwrite>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</upload>, L</pwrite>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9728
msgid "user-cancel"
msgstr "user-cancel"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9730
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" user-cancel\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" user-cancel\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9732 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15758
msgid "This function cancels the current upload or download operation."
msgstr "Šī funkcija atceļ pašreizējo augšupielādes vai lejupielādes darbību."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9734 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15760
msgid ""
"Unlike most other libguestfs calls, this function is signal safe and thread "
"safe.  You can call it from a signal handler or from another thread, without "
"needing to do any locking."
msgstr ""
"Atšķirībā no lielākās daļas citu libguestfs izsaukumu šī funkcija ir signālu "
"droša un pavedienu droša.  To var izsaukt no signālu apstrādātāja vai no "
"cita pavediena bez jebkādas bloķēšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9738 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15764
msgid ""
"The transfer that was in progress (if there is one) will stop shortly "
"afterwards, and will return an error.  The errno (see "
"L</guestfs_last_errno>) is set to C<EINTR>, so you can test for this to find "
"out if the operation was cancelled or failed because of another error."
msgstr ""
"Notiekošā pārsūtīšana (ja tāda ir) drīz pēc tam apstāsies un atgriezīs "
"kļūdu.  Errno (skatiet L</guestfs_last_errno>) tiek iestatīts uz C<EINTR>, "
"tāpēc varat to pārbaudīt, lai noskaidrotu, vai darbība tika atcelta vai "
"neizdevās citas kļūdas dēļ."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9744 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15770
msgid ""
"No cleanup is performed: for example, if a file was being uploaded then "
"after cancellation there may be a partially uploaded file.  It is the "
"caller’s responsibility to clean up if necessary."
msgstr ""
"Tīrīšana netiek veikta: piemēram, ja tika augšupielādēts fails, pēc "
"atcelšanas var palikt daļēji augšupielādēts fails.  Izsaucēja atbildība ir, "
"ja nepieciešams, sakopt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9748
msgid "There are two common places that you might call L</user-cancel>:"
msgstr "Ir divas bieži sastopamas vietas, kur varētu izsaukt L</user-cancel>:"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9750
msgid ""
"In an interactive text-based program, you might call it from a C<SIGINT> "
"signal handler so that pressing C<^C> cancels the current operation.  (You "
"also need to call L</set-pgroup> so that child processes don't receive the "
"C<^C> signal)."
msgstr ""
"Interaktīvā teksta programmā to varētu izsaukt no C<SIGINT> signāla "
"apstrādātāja, lai C<^C> nospiešana atceltu pašreizējo darbību.  (Jāizsauc "
"arī L</set-pgroup>, lai bērnprocesi nesaņemtu signālu C<^C>.)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9755 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15781
msgid ""
"In a graphical program, when the main thread is displaying a progress bar "
"with a cancel button, wire up the cancel button to call this function."
msgstr ""
"Grafiskā programmā, kad galvenais pavediens rāda progresa joslu ar "
"atcelšanas pogu, savienojiet atcelšanas pogu ar šīs funkcijas izsaukumu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9759
msgid "utimens"
msgstr "utimens"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9761
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" utimens path atsecs atnsecs mtsecs mtnsecs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" utimens path atsecs atnsecs mtsecs mtnsecs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9763 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15799
msgid "This command sets the timestamps of a file with nanosecond precision."
msgstr "Šī komanda iestata faila laikspiedolus ar nanosekunžu precizitāti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9766 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15802
msgid ""
"C<atsecs>, C<atnsecs> are the last access time (atime) in secs and "
"nanoseconds from the epoch."
msgstr ""
"C<atsecs>, C<atnsecs> ir pēdējās piekļuves laiks (atime) sekundēs un "
"nanosekundēs kopš epohas sākuma."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9769 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15805
msgid ""
"C<mtsecs>, C<mtnsecs> are the last modification time (mtime) in secs and "
"nanoseconds from the epoch."
msgstr ""
"C<mtsecs>, C<mtnsecs> ir pēdējās modificēšanas laiks (mtime) sekundēs un "
"nanosekundēs kopš epohas sākuma."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9772 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15808
msgid ""
"If the C<*nsecs> field contains the special value C<-1> then the "
"corresponding timestamp is set to the current time.  (The C<*secs> field is "
"ignored in this case)."
msgstr ""
"Ja lauks C<*nsecs> satur īpašo vērtību C<-1>, atbilstošais laikspiedols tiek "
"iestatīts uz pašreizējo laiku.  (Lauks C<*secs> šajā gadījumā tiek ignorēts.)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9776 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15812
msgid ""
"If the C<*nsecs> field contains the special value C<-2> then the "
"corresponding timestamp is left unchanged.  (The C<*secs> field is ignored "
"in this case)."
msgstr ""
"Ja lauks C<*nsecs> satur īpašo vērtību C<-2>, atbilstošais laikspiedols "
"paliek nemainīts.  (Lauks C<*secs> šajā gadījumā tiek ignorēts.)"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9780
msgid "utsname"
msgstr "utsname"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9782
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" utsname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" utsname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9784 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15825
msgid ""
"This returns the kernel version of the appliance, where this is available.  "
"This information is only useful for debugging.  Nothing in the returned "
"structure is defined by the API."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež palīgsistēmas kodola versiju, ja tā ir pieejama.  Šī informācija "
"noder tikai atkļūdošanai.  API nedefinē neko atgrieztajā struktūrā."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9788
msgid "version"
msgstr "version"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9790
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" version\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" version\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9792 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15840
msgid "Return the libguestfs version number that the program is linked against."
msgstr "Atgriezt libguestfs versijas numuru, ar kuru programma ir saistīta."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9795 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15843
msgid ""
"Note that because of dynamic linking this is not necessarily the version of "
"libguestfs that you compiled against.  You can compile the program, and then "
"at runtime dynamically link against a completely different F<libguestfs.so> "
"library."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka dinamiskās saistīšanas dēļ tā ne vienmēr ir libguestfs "
"versija, pret kuru kompilējāt.  Programmu var kompilēt un tad izpildes laikā "
"dinamiski saistīt ar pilnīgi citu F<libguestfs.so> bibliotēku."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9800 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15848
msgid ""
"This call was added in version C<1.0.58>.  In previous versions of "
"libguestfs there was no way to get the version number.  From C code you can "
"use dynamic linker functions to find out if this symbol exists (if it "
"doesn't, then it’s an earlier version)."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums tika pievienots versijā C<1.0.58>.  Iepriekšējās libguestfs "
"versijās nebija veida, kā iegūt versijas numuru.  No C koda varat izmantot "
"dinamiskā saistītāja funkcijas, lai noskaidrotu, vai šis simbols eksistē (ja "
"ne, tā ir vecāka versija)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9806 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15854
msgid ""
"The call returns a structure with four elements.  The first three (C<major>, "
"C<minor> and C<release>) are numbers and correspond to the usual version "
"triplet.  The fourth element (C<extra>) is a string and is normally empty, "
"but may be used for distro-specific information."
msgstr ""
"Izsaukums atgriež struktūru ar četriem elementiem.  Pirmie trīs (C<major>, "
"C<minor> un C<release>) ir skaitļi un atbilst parastajam versijas "
"trijniekam.  Ceturtais elements (C<extra>) ir virkne un parasti ir tukšs, "
"bet var tikt izmantots distribūcijai specifiskai informācijai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9812 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15860
msgid "To construct the original version string: C<$major.$minor.$release$extra>"
msgstr ""
"Lai izveidotu oriģinālo versijas virkni: C<$major.$minor.$release$extra>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9815 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15863
msgid "See also: L<guestfs(3)/LIBGUESTFS VERSION NUMBERS>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L<guestfs(3)/LIBGUESTFS VERSIJU NUMURI>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9817
msgid ""
"I<Note:> Don't use this call to test for availability of features.  In "
"enterprise distributions we backport features from later versions into "
"earlier versions, making this an unreliable way to test for features.  Use "
"L</available> or L</feature-available> instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Piezīme:> neizmantojiet šo izsaukumu līdzekļu pieejamības pārbaudei.  "
"Uzņēmumu distribūcijās mēs pārnesam līdzekļus no vēlākām versijām uz "
"agrākām, padarot šo par neuzticamu veidu līdzekļu pārbaudei.  Tā vietā "
"izmantojiet L</available> vai L</feature-available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9823
msgid "vfs-label"
msgstr "vfs-label"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9825
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vfs-label mountable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vfs-label mountable\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9827 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15883
msgid "This returns the label of the filesystem on C<mountable>."
msgstr "Tas atgriež failu sistēmas etiķeti montējamajā objektā C<mountable>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9829 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15885
msgid "If the filesystem is unlabeled, this returns the empty string."
msgstr "Ja failu sistēmai nav etiķetes, tas atgriež tukšu virkni."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9831
msgid "To find a filesystem from the label, use L</findfs-label>."
msgstr "Lai atrastu failu sistēmu pēc etiķetes, izmantojiet L</findfs-label>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9833
msgid "vfs-minimum-size"
msgstr "vfs-minimum-size"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9835
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vfs-minimum-size mountable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vfs-minimum-size mountable\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9837 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15900
msgid ""
"Get the minimum size of filesystem in bytes.  This is the minimum possible "
"size for filesystem shrinking."
msgstr ""
"Iegūt failu sistēmas minimālo izmēru baitos.  Tas ir minimālais iespējamais "
"izmērs failu sistēmas samazināšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9840 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15903
msgid ""
"If getting minimum size of specified filesystem is not supported, this will "
"fail and set errno as ENOTSUP."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādītās failu sistēmas minimālā izmēra iegūšana netiek atbalstīta, tas "
"neizdosies un iestatīs errno uz ENOTSUP."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9843 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15906
msgid "See also L<ntfsresize(8)>, L<resize2fs(8)>, L<btrfs(8)>, L<xfs_info(8)>."
msgstr ""
"Skatīt arī L<ntfsresize(8)>, L<resize2fs(8)>, L<btrfs(8)>, L<xfs_info(8)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9845
msgid "vfs-type"
msgstr "vfs-type"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9847
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vfs-type mountable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vfs-type mountable\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9849 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15918
msgid ""
"This command gets the filesystem type corresponding to the filesystem on "
"C<mountable>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda iegūst failu sistēmas tipu, kas atbilst failu sistēmai "
"montējamajā objektā C<mountable>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9852 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15921
msgid ""
"For most filesystems, the result is the name of the Linux VFS module which "
"would be used to mount this filesystem if you mounted it without specifying "
"the filesystem type.  For example a string such as C<ext3> or C<ntfs>."
msgstr ""
"Lielākajai daļai failu sistēmu rezultāts ir Linux VFS moduļa nosaukums, kas "
"tiktu izmantots šīs failu sistēmas montēšanai, ja to montētu, nenorādot "
"failu sistēmas tipu.  Piemēram, tāda virkne kā C<ext3> vai C<ntfs>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9857
msgid "vfs-uuid"
msgstr "vfs-uuid"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9859
msgid "get-uuid"
msgstr "get-uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9861
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vfs-uuid mountable\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vfs-uuid mountable\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9863 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15937
msgid "This returns the filesystem UUID of the filesystem on C<mountable>."
msgstr "Tas atgriež failu sistēmas UUID montējamajā objektā C<mountable>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9865 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15939
msgid "If the filesystem does not have a UUID, this returns the empty string."
msgstr "Ja failu sistēmai nav UUID, tas atgriež tukšu virkni."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9867
msgid "To find a filesystem from the UUID, use L</findfs-uuid>."
msgstr "Lai atrastu failu sistēmu pēc UUID, izmantojiet L</findfs-uuid>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9869
msgid "vg-activate"
msgstr "vg-activate"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9871
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vg-activate true|false 'volgroups ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vg-activate true|false 'volgroups ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9873 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15955
msgid ""
"This command activates or (if C<activate> is false) deactivates all logical "
"volumes in the listed volume groups C<volgroups>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda aktivizē vai (ja C<activate> ir false) deaktivizē visus loģiskos "
"sējumus uzskaitītajās sējumu grupās C<volgroups>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9876 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15958
msgid "This command is the same as running C<vgchange -a y|n volgroups...>"
msgstr "Šī komanda ir tāda pati kā C<vgchange -a y|n volgroups...> izpilde"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9878 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15960
msgid ""
"Note that if C<volgroups> is an empty list then B<all> volume groups are "
"activated or deactivated."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, ja C<volgroups> ir tukšs saraksts, tiek aktivizētas vai "
"deaktivizētas B<visas> sējumu grupas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9884
msgid "vg-activate-all"
msgstr "vg-activate-all"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9886
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vg-activate-all true|false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vg-activate-all true|false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9888 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15976
msgid ""
"This command activates or (if C<activate> is false) deactivates all logical "
"volumes in all volume groups."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda aktivizē vai (ja C<activate> ir false) deaktivizē visus loģiskos "
"sējumus visās sējumu grupās."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9891 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15979
msgid "This command is the same as running C<vgchange -a y|n>"
msgstr "Šī komanda ir tāda pati kā C<vgchange -a y|n> izpilde"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9896
msgid "vgchange-uuid"
msgstr "vgchange-uuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9898
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgchange-uuid vg\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgchange-uuid vg\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9900 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:15994
msgid "Generate a new random UUID for the volume group C<vg>."
msgstr "Ģenerēt jaunu nejaušu UUID sējumu grupai C<vg>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9905
msgid "vgchange-uuid-all"
msgstr "vgchange-uuid-all"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9907
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgchange-uuid-all\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgchange-uuid-all\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9909 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16008
msgid "Generate new random UUIDs for all volume groups."
msgstr "Ģenerēt jaunus nejaušus UUID visām sējumu grupām."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9914
msgid "vgcreate"
msgstr "vgcreate"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9916
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgcreate volgroup 'physvols ...'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgcreate volgroup 'physvols ...'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9918 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16024
msgid ""
"This creates an LVM volume group called C<volgroup> from the non-empty list "
"of physical volumes C<physvols>."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido LVM sējumu grupu C<volgroup> no netukša fizisko sējumu saraksta "
"C<physvols>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9924
msgid "vglvuuids"
msgstr "vglvuuids"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9926
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vglvuuids vgname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vglvuuids vgname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9928 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16040
msgid ""
"Given a VG called C<vgname>, this returns the UUIDs of all the logical "
"volumes created in this volume group."
msgstr ""
"Dotai VG C<vgname> tas atgriež visu šajā sējumu grupā izveidoto loģisko "
"sējumu UUID."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9931
msgid ""
"You can use this along with L</lvs> and L</lvuuid> calls to associate "
"logical volumes and volume groups."
msgstr ""
"To var izmantot kopā ar izsaukumiem L</lvs> un L</lvuuid>, lai sasaistītu "
"loģiskos sējumus un sējumu grupas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9934
msgid "See also L</vgpvuuids>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</vgpvuuids>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9936
msgid "vgmeta"
msgstr "vgmeta"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9938
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgmeta vgname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgmeta vgname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9940 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16061
msgid ""
"C<vgname> is an LVM volume group.  This command examines the volume group "
"and returns its metadata."
msgstr ""
"C<vgname> ir LVM sējumu grupa.  Šī komanda pārbauda sējumu grupu un atgriež "
"tās metadatus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9943 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16064
msgid ""
"Note that the metadata is an internal structure used by LVM, subject to "
"change at any time, and is provided for information only."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka metadati ir LVM izmantota iekšēja struktūra, kas jebkurā "
"laikā var mainīties, un tie ir sniegti tikai informācijai."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9949
msgid "vgpvuuids"
msgstr "vgpvuuids"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9951
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgpvuuids vgname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgpvuuids vgname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9953 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16082
msgid ""
"Given a VG called C<vgname>, this returns the UUIDs of all the physical "
"volumes that this volume group resides on."
msgstr ""
"Dotai VG C<vgname> tas atgriež visu fizisko sējumu UUID, uz kuriem atrodas "
"šī sējumu grupa."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9956
msgid ""
"You can use this along with L</pvs> and L</pvuuid> calls to associate "
"physical volumes and volume groups."
msgstr ""
"To var izmantot kopā ar izsaukumiem L</pvs> un L</pvuuid>, lai sasaistītu "
"fiziskos sējumus un sējumu grupas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9959
msgid "See also L</vglvuuids>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</vglvuuids>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9961
msgid "vgremove"
msgstr "vgremove"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9963
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgremove vgname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgremove vgname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9965 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16102
msgid "Remove an LVM volume group C<vgname>, (for example C<VG>)."
msgstr "Noņemt LVM sējumu grupu C<vgname> (piemēram, C<VG>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9967 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16104
msgid "This also forcibly removes all logical volumes in the volume group (if any)."
msgstr ""
"Tas arī piespiedu kārtā noņem visus loģiskos sējumus sējumu grupā (ja tādi "
"ir)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9973
msgid "vgrename"
msgstr "vgrename"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9975
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgrename volgroup newvolgroup\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgrename volgroup newvolgroup\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9977 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16121
msgid "Rename a volume group C<volgroup> with the new name C<newvolgroup>."
msgstr "Pārdēvēt sējumu grupu C<volgroup> ar jauno nosaukumu C<newvolgroup>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9979
msgid "vgs"
msgstr "vgs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9981
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9983 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16132
msgid ""
"List all the volumes groups detected.  This is the equivalent of the "
"L<vgs(8)> command."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visas noteiktās sējumu grupas.  Tas ir ekvivalents komandai L<vgs"
"(8)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9986 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16135
msgid ""
"This returns a list of just the volume group names that were detected "
"(eg. C<VolGroup00>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež tikai noteikto sējumu grupu nosaukumu sarakstu (piem., "
"C<VolGroup00>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9989
msgid "See also L</vgs-full>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</vgs-full>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9994
msgid "vgs-full"
msgstr "vgs-full"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9996
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgs-full\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgs-full\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:9998 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16154
msgid ""
"List all the volumes groups detected.  This is the equivalent of the "
"L<vgs(8)> command.  The \"full\" version includes all fields."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visas noteiktās sējumu grupas.  Tas ir ekvivalents komandai L<vgs"
"(8)>.  „Pilnā” versija ietver visus laukus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10004
msgid "vgscan"
msgstr "vgscan"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10006
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgscan\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgscan\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10008 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16178
msgid ""
"This rescans all block devices and rebuilds the list of LVM physical "
"volumes, volume groups and logical volumes."
msgstr ""
"Tas atkārtoti skenē visas bloku ierīces un pārbūvē LVM fizisko sējumu, "
"sējumu grupu un loģisko sējumu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10011
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</lvm-scan> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"lvm-scan>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10018
msgid "vguuid"
msgstr "vguuid"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10020
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vguuid vgname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vguuid vgname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10022 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16191
msgid "This command returns the UUID of the LVM VG named C<vgname>."
msgstr "Šī komanda atgriež LVM VG C<vgname> UUID."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10024
msgid "wc-c"
msgstr "wc-c"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10026
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" wc-c path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" wc-c path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10028 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16232
msgid ""
"This command counts the characters in a file, using the C<wc -c> external "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda saskaita rakstzīmes failā, izmantojot ārējo komandu C<wc -c>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10031
msgid "wc-l"
msgstr "wc-l"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10033
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" wc-l path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" wc-l path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10035 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16245
msgid ""
"This command counts the lines in a file, using the C<wc -l> external "
"command."
msgstr "Šī komanda saskaita rindas failā, izmantojot ārējo komandu C<wc -l>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10038
msgid "wc-w"
msgstr "wc-w"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10040
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" wc-w path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" wc-w path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10042 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16258
msgid ""
"This command counts the words in a file, using the C<wc -w> external "
"command."
msgstr "Šī komanda saskaita vārdus failā, izmantojot ārējo komandu C<wc -w>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10045
msgid "wipefs"
msgstr "wipefs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10047
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" wipefs device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" wipefs device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10049 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16271
msgid ""
"This command erases filesystem or RAID signatures from the specified "
"C<device> to make the filesystem invisible to libblkid."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda izdzēš failu sistēmas vai RAID parakstus no norādītās ierīces "
"C<device>, lai failu sistēma kļūtu neredzama libblkid."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10052 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16274
msgid ""
"This does not erase the filesystem itself nor any other data from the "
"C<device>."
msgstr "Tas neizdzēš pašu failu sistēmu vai jebkādus citus datus no C<device>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10055
msgid "Compare with L</zero> which zeroes the first few blocks of a device."
msgstr ""
"Salīdziniet ar L</zero>, kas aizpilda ar nullēm ierīces dažus pirmos blokus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10058
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<wipefs>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<wipefs>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10061
msgid "write"
msgstr "write"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10063
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" write path content\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" write path content\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10065 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16295
msgid ""
"This call creates a file called C<path>.  The content of the file is the "
"string C<content> (which can contain any 8 bit data)."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums izveido failu C<path>.  Faila saturs ir virkne C<content> (kas "
"var saturēt jebkādus 8 bitu datus)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10068
msgid "See also L</write-append>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</write-append>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10070
msgid "write-append"
msgstr "write-append"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10072
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" write-append path content\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" write-append path content\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10074 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16312
msgid ""
"This call appends C<content> to the end of file C<path>.  If C<path> does "
"not exist, then a new file is created."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums pievieno C<content> faila C<path> beigās.  Ja C<path> "
"neeksistē, tiek izveidots jauns fails."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10077
msgid "See also L</write>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</write>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10079
msgid "write-file"
msgstr "write-file"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10081
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" write-file path content size\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" write-file path content size\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10083 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16336
msgid ""
"This call creates a file called C<path>.  The contents of the file is the "
"string C<content> (which can contain any 8 bit data), with length C<size>."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums izveido failu C<path>.  Faila saturs ir virkne C<content> (kas "
"var saturēt jebkādus 8 bitu datus) garumā C<size>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10087 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16340
msgid ""
"As a special case, if C<size> is C<0> then the length is calculated using "
"C<strlen> (so in this case the content cannot contain embedded ASCII NULs)."
msgstr ""
"Kā īpašs gadījums, ja C<size> ir C<0>, garums tiek aprēķināts ar C<strlen> "
"(tāpēc šajā gadījumā saturs nevar saturēt iegultas ASCII NUL)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10091 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16344
msgid ""
"I<NB.> Owing to a bug, writing content containing ASCII NUL characters does "
"I<not> work, even if the length is specified."
msgstr ""
"I<Piezīme.> Kļūdas dēļ satura ar ASCII NUL rakstzīmēm rakstīšana "
"I<nedarbojas> pat tad, ja garums ir norādīts."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10097
msgid "I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</write> call instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"write>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10104
msgid "xfs-admin"
msgstr "xfs-admin"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" xfs-admin device [extunwritten:true|false] [imgfile:true|false] "
"[v2log:true|false] [projid32bit:true|false] [lazycounter:true|false] "
"[label:..] [uuid:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" xfs-admin device [extunwritten:true|false] [imgfile:true|false] "
"[v2log:true|false] [projid32bit:true|false] [lazycounter:true|false] "
"[label:..] [uuid:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10108 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16374
msgid "Change the parameters of the XFS filesystem on C<device>."
msgstr "Mainīt XFS failu sistēmas parametrus ierīcē C<device>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10110 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16376
msgid ""
"Devices that are mounted cannot be modified.  Administrators must unmount "
"filesystems before this call can modify parameters."
msgstr ""
"Montētas ierīces nevar mainīt.  Administratoriem failu sistēmas jānomontē, "
"pirms šis izsaukums var mainīt parametrus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10114
msgid ""
"Some of the parameters of a mounted filesystem can be examined and modified "
"using the L</xfs-info> and L</xfs-growfs> calls."
msgstr ""
"Dažus montētas failu sistēmas parametrus var pārbaudīt un mainīt, izmantojot "
"izsaukumus L</xfs-info> un L</xfs-growfs>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10118 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16384
msgid ""
"Beginning with XFS version 5, it is no longer possible to modify the "
"lazy-counters setting (ie. C<lazycounter> parameter has no effect)."
msgstr ""
"Sākot ar XFS 5. versiju, slinko skaitītāju iestatījumu vairs nav iespējams "
"mainīt (t. i., parametram C<lazycounter> nav ietekmes)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10123 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10134
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10156 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10185
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10208
msgid "This command depends on the feature C<xfs>.  See also L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<xfs>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10126
msgid "xfs-growfs"
msgstr "xfs-growfs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" xfs-growfs path [datasec:true|false] [logsec:true|false] [rtsec:true|false] "
"[datasize:N] [logsize:N] [rtsize:N] [rtextsize:N] [maxpct:N]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" xfs-growfs path [datasec:true|false] [logsec:true|false] [rtsec:true|false] "
"[datasize:N] [logsize:N] [rtsize:N] [rtextsize:N] [maxpct:N]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10130 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16437
msgid "Grow the XFS filesystem mounted at C<path>."
msgstr "Palielināt XFS failu sistēmu, kas montēta C<path>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10137
msgid "xfs-info"
msgstr "xfs-info"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" xfs-info pathordevice\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" xfs-info pathordevice\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10141 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10163
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16481 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16504
msgid ""
"C<pathordevice> is a mounted XFS filesystem or a device containing an XFS "
"filesystem.  This command returns miscellaneous metadata about the XFS "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""
"C<pathordevice> ir montēta XFS failu sistēma vai ierīce, kas satur XFS failu "
"sistēmu.  Šī komanda atgriež dažādus metadatus par XFS failu sistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10145 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16485
msgid ""
"The returned struct contains miscellaneous metadata.  Missing fields are "
"returned as C<-1> (for numeric fields) or empty string."
msgstr ""
"Atgrieztā struktūra satur dažādus metadatus.  Trūkstošie lauki tiek "
"atgriezti kā C<-1> (skaitliskiem laukiem) vai tukša virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10149
msgid ""
"I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</xfs-info2> call "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"xfs-info2>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10159
msgid "xfs-info2"
msgstr "xfs-info2"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" xfs-info2 pathordevice\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" xfs-info2 pathordevice\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10167 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16508
msgid ""
"The output is a hash derived from the output of L<xfs_info(8)>, and "
"generally looks like:"
msgstr ""
"Izvade ir jaucējtabula, kas atvasināta no L<xfs_info(8)> izvades, un parasti "
"izskatās šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10170 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16511
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" meta-data: /dev/sda1\n"
" meta-data.isize: 512\n"
" meta-data.agcount: 4\n"
" meta-data.agsize: 65528 blks\n"
" meta-data.sectsz: 512\n"
" meta-data.attr: 2\n"
" meta-data.projid32bit: 1\n"
" meta-data.crc: 1\n"
" [...]\n"
" data.bsize: 4096\n"
" data.blocks: 262112\n"
" [...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" meta-data: /dev/sda1\n"
" meta-data.isize: 512\n"
" meta-data.agcount: 4\n"
" meta-data.agsize: 65528 blks\n"
" meta-data.sectsz: 512\n"
" meta-data.attr: 2\n"
" meta-data.projid32bit: 1\n"
" meta-data.crc: 1\n"
" [...]\n"
" data.bsize: 4096\n"
" data.blocks: 262112\n"
" [...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10183 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16524
msgid "More information can be found by reading L<xfs_info(8)>."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju var atrast, lasot L<xfs_info(8)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10188
msgid "xfs-repair"
msgstr "xfs-repair"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10190
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" xfs-repair device [forcelogzero:true|false] [nomodify:true|false] "
"[noprefetch:true|false] [forcegeometry:true|false] [maxmem:N] [ihashsize:N] "
"[bhashsize:N] [agstride:N] [logdev:..] [rtdev:..]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" xfs-repair device [forcelogzero:true|false] [nomodify:true|false] "
"[noprefetch:true|false] [forcegeometry:true|false] [maxmem:N] [ihashsize:N] "
"[bhashsize:N] [agstride:N] [logdev:..] [rtdev:..]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10192 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16560
msgid "Repair corrupt or damaged XFS filesystem on C<device>."
msgstr "Labot bojātu XFS failu sistēmu ierīcē C<device>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10194 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16562
msgid ""
"The filesystem is specified using the C<device> argument which should be the "
"device name of the disk partition or volume containing the filesystem.  If "
"given the name of a block device, C<xfs_repair> will attempt to find the raw "
"device associated with the specified block device and will use the raw "
"device instead."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēma tiek norādīta ar argumentu C<device>, kam jābūt diska "
"nodalījuma vai sējuma, kas satur failu sistēmu, ierīces nosaukumam.  Ja dots "
"bloku ierīces nosaukums, C<xfs_repair> mēģinās atrast ar norādīto bloku "
"ierīci saistīto neapstrādāto ierīci un tā vietā izmantos to."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10200 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16568
msgid ""
"Regardless, the filesystem to be repaired must be unmounted, otherwise, the "
"resulting filesystem may be inconsistent or corrupt."
msgstr ""
"Jebkurā gadījumā labojamajai failu sistēmai jābūt atmontētai, citādi iegūtā "
"failu sistēma var būt nekonsekventa vai bojāta."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10203 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16571
msgid ""
"The returned status indicates whether filesystem corruption was detected "
"(returns C<1>) or was not detected (returns C<0>)."
msgstr ""
"Atgrieztais statuss norāda, vai failu sistēmas bojājums tika konstatēts "
"(atgriež C<1>) vai netika konstatēts (atgriež C<0>)."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10211
msgid "yara-destroy"
msgstr "yara-destroy"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10213
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" yara-destroy\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" yara-destroy\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10215 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16608
msgid "Destroy previously loaded Yara rules in order to free libguestfs resources."
msgstr ""
"Iznīcināt iepriekš ielādētās Yara kārtulas, lai atbrīvotu libguestfs "
"resursus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10217 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10241
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10266
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<libyara>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<libyara>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10220
msgid "yara-load"
msgstr "yara-load"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10222
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" yara-load (filename|-)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" yara-load (filename|-)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10224 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16623
msgid "Upload a set of Yara rules from local file F<filename>."
msgstr "Augšupielādēt Yara kārtulu kopu no lokālā faila F<filename>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10226
msgid ""
"Yara rules allow to categorize files based on textual or binary patterns "
"within their content.  See L</yara-scan> to see how to scan files with the "
"loaded rules."
msgstr ""
"Yara kārtulas ļauj kategorizēt failus, balstoties uz teksta vai bināriem "
"šabloniem to saturā.  Kā skenēt failus ar ielādētajām kārtulām, skatiet L</"
"yara-scan>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10230 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16629
msgid ""
"Rules can be in binary format, as when compiled with yarac command, or in "
"source code format. In the latter case, the rules will be first compiled and "
"then loaded."
msgstr ""
"Kārtulas var būt binārā formātā, kā kompilējot ar komandu yarac, vai "
"pirmkoda formātā. Pēdējā gadījumā kārtulas vispirms tiks kompilētas un pēc "
"tam ielādētas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10234 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16633
msgid ""
"Rules in source code format cannot include external files. In such cases, it "
"is recommended to compile them first."
msgstr ""
"Pirmkoda formāta kārtulas nevar iekļaut ārējus failus. Šādos gadījumos "
"ieteicams tās vispirms kompilēt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10237 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16636
msgid "Previously loaded rules will be destroyed."
msgstr "Iepriekš ielādētās kārtulas tiks iznīcinātas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10244
msgid "yara-scan"
msgstr "yara-scan"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10246
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" yara-scan path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" yara-scan path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10248 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16656
msgid "Scan a file with the previously loaded Yara rules."
msgstr "Skenēt failu ar iepriekš ielādētajām Yara kārtulām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10250 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16658
msgid "For each matching rule, a C<yara_detection> structure is returned."
msgstr ""
"Katrai atbilstošajai kārtulai tiek atgriezta struktūra C<yara_detection>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10252 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16660
msgid "The C<yara_detection> structure contains the following fields."
msgstr "Struktūra C<yara_detection> satur šādus laukus."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10256 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16664
msgid "C<yara_name>"
msgstr "C<yara_name>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10258 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16666
msgid "Path of the file matching a Yara rule."
msgstr "Faila, kas atbilst Yara kārtulai, ceļš."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10260 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16668
msgid "C<yara_rule>"
msgstr "C<yara_rule>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10262 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16670
msgid "Identifier of the Yara rule which matched against the given file."
msgstr "Yara kārtulas identifikators, kas atbilda dotajam failam."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10269
msgid "zegrep"
msgstr "zegrep"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10271
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zegrep regex path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zegrep regex path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10273 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16702
msgid "This calls the external C<zegrep> program and returns the matching lines."
msgstr "Izsauc ārējo programmu C<zegrep> un atgriež atbilstošās rindas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10286
msgid "zegrepi"
msgstr "zegrepi"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10288
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zegrepi regex path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zegrepi regex path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10290 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16728
msgid "This calls the external C<zegrep -i> program and returns the matching lines."
msgstr "Izsauc ārējo programmu C<zegrep -i> un atgriež atbilstošās rindas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10303
msgid "zero"
msgstr "zero"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10305
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zero device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zero device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10307 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16746
msgid "This command writes zeroes over the first few blocks of C<device>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda raksta nulles pāri ierīces C<device> dažiem pirmajiem blokiem."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10309 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16748
msgid ""
"How many blocks are zeroed isn't specified (but it’s I<not> enough to "
"securely wipe the device).  It should be sufficient to remove any partition "
"tables, filesystem superblocks and so on."
msgstr ""
"Cik bloku tiek aizpildīti ar nullēm, nav norādīts (bet tas I<nav> "
"pietiekami, lai droši notīrītu ierīci).  Tam vajadzētu pietikt, lai noņemtu "
"jebkuras nodalījumu tabulas, failu sistēmu superblokus u. tml."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10313 fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10328
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16752 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16778
msgid ""
"If blocks are already zero, then this command avoids writing zeroes.  This "
"prevents the underlying device from becoming non-sparse or growing "
"unnecessarily."
msgstr ""
"Ja bloki jau ir nulles, šī komanda izvairās no nulļu rakstīšanas.  Tas "
"neļauj pamatā esošajai ierīcei kļūt neretinātai vai nevajadzīgi augt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10317
msgid "See also: L</zero-device>, L</scrub-device>, L</is-zero-device>"
msgstr "Skatīt arī: L</zero-device>, L</scrub-device>, L</is-zero-device>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10320
msgid "zero-device"
msgstr "zero-device"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10322
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zero-device device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zero-device device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10324
msgid ""
"This command writes zeroes over the entire C<device>.  Compare with L</zero> "
"which just zeroes the first few blocks of a device."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda raksta nulles pāri visai ierīcei C<device>.  Salīdziniet ar L</"
"zero>, kas aizpilda ar nullēm tikai ierīces dažus pirmos blokus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10332
msgid "zero-free-space"
msgstr "zero-free-space"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10334
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zero-free-space directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zero-free-space directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10336 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16797
msgid ""
"Zero the free space in the filesystem mounted on F<directory>.  The "
"filesystem must be mounted read-write."
msgstr ""
"Aizpildīt ar nullēm brīvo vietu failu sistēmā, kas montēta F<directory>.  "
"Failu sistēmai jābūt montētai lasīšanai un rakstīšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10339 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16800
msgid ""
"The filesystem contents are not affected, but any free space in the "
"filesystem is freed."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēmas saturs netiek ietekmēts, bet jebkura brīvā vieta failu "
"sistēmā tiek atbrīvota."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10342
msgid ""
"Free space is not \"trimmed\".  You may want to call L</fstrim> either as an "
"alternative to this, or after calling this, depending on your requirements."
msgstr ""
"Brīvā vieta netiek „apgriezta”.  Atkarībā no jūsu prasībām, iespējams, "
"vēlēsieties izsaukt L</fstrim> vai nu kā alternatīvu šim, vai pēc šī "
"izsaukšanas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10346
msgid "zerofree"
msgstr "zerofree"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10348
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zerofree device\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zerofree device\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10350 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16822
msgid ""
"This runs the I<zerofree> program on C<device>.  This program claims to zero "
"unused inodes and disk blocks on an ext2/3 filesystem, thus making it "
"possible to compress the filesystem more effectively."
msgstr ""
"Tas izpilda programmu I<zerofree> ierīcei C<device>.  Šī programma apgalvo, "
"ka aizpilda ar nullēm neizmantotos inode un diska blokus ext2/3 failu "
"sistēmā, tādējādi ļaujot failu sistēmu saspiest efektīvāk."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10355 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16827
msgid "You should B<not> run this program if the filesystem is mounted."
msgstr "Šo programmu B<nevajadzētu> izpildīt, ja failu sistēma ir montēta."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10358 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16830
msgid ""
"It is possible that using this program can damage the filesystem or data on "
"the filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Iespējams, ka šīs programmas izmantošana var sabojāt failu sistēmu vai datus "
"failu sistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10361
msgid ""
"This command depends on the feature C<zerofree>.  See also "
"L</feature-available>."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir atkarīga no līdzekļa C<zerofree>.  Skatīt arī L</feature-"
"available>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10364
msgid "zfgrep"
msgstr "zfgrep"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10366
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zfgrep pattern path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zfgrep pattern path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10368 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16854
msgid "This calls the external C<zfgrep> program and returns the matching lines."
msgstr "Izsauc ārējo programmu C<zfgrep> un atgriež atbilstošās rindas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10381
msgid "zfgrepi"
msgstr "zfgrepi"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10383
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zfgrepi pattern path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zfgrepi pattern path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10385 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16880
msgid "This calls the external C<zfgrep -i> program and returns the matching lines."
msgstr "Izsauc ārējo programmu C<zfgrep -i> un atgriež atbilstošās rindas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10398
msgid "zfile"
msgstr "zfile"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10400
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zfile meth path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zfile meth path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10402 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16906
msgid ""
"This command runs L<file(1)> after first decompressing C<path> using "
"C<meth>."
msgstr "Šī komanda izpilda L<file(1)>, vispirms atspiežot C<path> ar C<meth>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10405 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16909
msgid "C<meth> must be one of C<gzip>, C<compress> or C<bzip2>."
msgstr "C<meth> jābūt vienam no C<gzip>, C<compress> vai C<bzip2>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10407
msgid "Since 1.0.63, use L</file> instead which can now process compressed files."
msgstr ""
"Kopš 1.0.63 tā vietā izmantojiet L</file>, kas tagad var apstrādāt "
"saspiestus failus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10410
msgid "I<This function is deprecated.> In new code, use the L</file> call instead."
msgstr ""
"I<Šī funkcija ir novecojusi.> Jaunā kodā tā vietā izmantojiet izsaukumu L</"
"file>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10417
msgid "zgrep"
msgstr "zgrep"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10419
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zgrep regex path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zgrep regex path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10421 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16933
msgid "This calls the external L<zgrep(1)> program and returns the matching lines."
msgstr "Izsauc ārējo programmu L<zgrep(1)> un atgriež atbilstošās rindas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10434
msgid "zgrepi"
msgstr "zgrepi"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10436
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zgrepi regex path\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zgrepi regex path\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-actions.pod:10438 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:16959
msgid "This calls the external C<zgrep -i> program and returns the matching lines."
msgstr "Izsauc ārējo programmu C<zgrep -i> un atgriež atbilstošās rindas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:27
msgid "alloc"
msgstr "alloc"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:29
msgid "allocate"
msgstr "allocate"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" alloc filename size\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" alloc filename size\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:33
msgid ""
"This creates an empty (zeroed) file of the given size, and then adds so it "
"can be further examined."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido tukšu (ar nullēm aizpildītu) dotā izmēra failu un pēc tam to "
"pievieno, lai to varētu tālāk pārbaudīt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:36 fish/guestfish-commands.pod:281
msgid "For more advanced image creation, see L</disk-create>."
msgstr "Sarežģītākai attēlu izveidei skatiet L</disk-create>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:38 fish/guestfish-commands.pod:283
msgid "Size can be specified using standard suffixes, eg. C<1M>."
msgstr "Izmēru var norādīt, izmantojot standarta sufiksus, piem., C<1M>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:40
msgid ""
"To create a sparse file, use L</sparse> instead.  To create a prepared disk "
"image, see L</PREPARED DISK IMAGES>."
msgstr ""
"Lai izveidotu retinātu failu, tā vietā izmantojiet L</sparse>.  Lai "
"izveidotu sagatavotu diska attēlu, skatiet L</SAGATAVOTI DISKU ATTĒLI>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:43
msgid "copy-in"
msgstr "copy-in"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" copy-in local [local ...] /remotedir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" copy-in local [local ...] /remotedir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:47
msgid ""
"C<copy-in> copies local files or directories recursively into the disk "
"image, placing them in the directory called F</remotedir> (which must "
"exist).  This guestfish meta-command turns into a sequence of L</tar-in> and "
"other commands as necessary."
msgstr ""
"C<copy-in> rekursīvi iekopē lokālos failus vai direktorijas diska attēlā, "
"ievietojot tos direktorijā F</remotedir> (kam jāeksistē).  Šī guestfish "
"metakomanda pēc vajadzības pārvēršas L</tar-in> un citu komandu secībā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:52
msgid ""
"Multiple local files and directories can be specified, but the last "
"parameter must always be a remote directory.  Wildcards cannot be used."
msgstr ""
"Var norādīt vairākus lokālos failus un direktorijas, bet pēdējam parametram "
"vienmēr jābūt attālai direktorijai.  Aizstājējzīmes nevar izmantot."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:56
msgid "copy-out"
msgstr "copy-out"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" copy-out remote [remote ...] localdir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" copy-out remote [remote ...] localdir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:60
msgid ""
"C<copy-out> copies remote files or directories recursively out of the disk "
"image, placing them on the host disk in a local directory called C<localdir> "
"(which must exist).  This guestfish meta-command turns into a sequence of "
"L</download>, L</tar-out> and other commands as necessary."
msgstr ""
"C<copy-out> rekursīvi izkopē attālos failus vai direktorijas no diska "
"attēla, ievietojot tos resursdatora diskā lokālā direktorijā C<localdir> "
"(kam jāeksistē).  Šī guestfish metakomanda pēc vajadzības pārvēršas L</"
"download>, L</tar-out> un citu komandu secībā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:66
msgid ""
"Multiple remote files and directories can be specified, but the last "
"parameter must always be a local directory.  To download to the current "
"directory, use C<.> as in:"
msgstr ""
"Var norādīt vairākus attālos failus un direktorijas, bet pēdējam parametram "
"vienmēr jābūt lokālai direktorijai.  Lai lejupielādētu pašreizējā "
"direktorijā, izmantojiet C<.>, kā šeit:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" copy-out /home .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" copy-out /home .\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:72
msgid ""
"Wildcards cannot be used in the ordinary command, but you can use them with "
"the help of L</glob> like this:"
msgstr ""
"Parastajā komandā aizstājējzīmes nevar izmantot, taču tās var izmantot ar L</"
"glob> palīdzību šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:75
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" glob copy-out /home/* .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" glob copy-out /home/* .\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:77
msgid "delete-event"
msgstr "delete-event"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" delete-event name\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" delete-event name\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:81
msgid ""
"Delete the event handler which was previously registered as C<name>.  If "
"multiple event handlers were registered with the same name, they are all "
"deleted."
msgstr ""
"Dzēst notikumu apstrādātāju, kas iepriekš reģistrēts kā C<name>.  Ja ar "
"vienādu nosaukumu reģistrēti vairāki notikumu apstrādātāji, tie visi tiek "
"dzēsti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:85
msgid "See also the guestfish commands C<event> and C<list-events>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī guestfish komandas C<event> un C<list-events>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:87
msgid "display"
msgstr "display"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" display filename\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" display filename\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:91
msgid ""
"Use C<display> (a graphical display program) to display an image file.  It "
"downloads the file, and runs C<display> on it."
msgstr ""
"Izmantot C<display> (grafisku attēlošanas programmu), lai parādītu attēla "
"failu.  Tas lejupielādē failu un izpilda tam C<display>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:94
msgid ""
"To use an alternative program, set the C<GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE> "
"environment variable.  For example to use the GNOME display program:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izmantotu alternatīvu programmu, iestatiet vides mainīgo "
"C<GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE>.  Piemēram, lai izmantotu GNOME attēlošanas "
"programmu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE=eog\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE=eog\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:99
msgid "See also L<display(1)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<display(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:101
msgid "echo"
msgstr "echo"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" echo [params ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" echo [params ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:105
msgid "This echos the parameters to the terminal."
msgstr "Tas izvada parametrus terminālī."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:107
msgid "edit"
msgstr "edit"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:109
msgid "vi"
msgstr "vi"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:111
msgid "emacs"
msgstr "emacs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:113
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" edit filename\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" edit filename\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:115
msgid ""
"This is used to edit a file.  It downloads the file, edits it locally using "
"your editor, then uploads the result."
msgstr ""
"To izmanto faila rediģēšanai.  Tas lejupielādē failu, rediģē to lokāli ar "
"jūsu redaktoru un tad augšupielādē rezultātu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:118
msgid ""
"The editor is C<$EDITOR>.  However if you use the alternate commands C<vi> "
"or C<emacs> you will get those corresponding editors."
msgstr ""
"Redaktors ir C<$EDITOR>.  Tomēr, ja izmantojat alternatīvās komandas C<vi> "
"vai C<emacs>, saņemsiet atbilstošos redaktorus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:122
msgid "event"
msgstr "event"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" event name eventset \"shell script ...\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" event name eventset \"shell script ...\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:126
msgid ""
"Register a shell script fragment which is executed when an event is raised.  "
"See L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_event_callback> for a discussion of the event "
"API in libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Reģistrēt čaulas skripta fragmentu, kas tiek izpildīts, kad tiek izraisīts "
"notikums.  Libguestfs notikumu API aplūkojumu skatiet L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_set_event_callback>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:130
msgid ""
"The C<name> parameter is a name that you give to this event handler.  It can "
"be any string (even the empty string) and is simply there so you can delete "
"the handler using the guestfish C<delete-event> command."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<name> ir nosaukums, ko piešķirat šim notikumu apstrādātājam.  Tā "
"var būt jebkura virkne (pat tukša virkne), un tā ir paredzēta tikai tam, lai "
"apstrādātāju varētu dzēst ar guestfish komandu C<delete-event>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:135
msgid ""
"The C<eventset> parameter is a comma-separated list of one or more events, "
"for example C<close> or C<close,trace>.  The special value C<*> means all "
"events."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<eventset> ir ar komatiem atdalīts viena vai vairāku notikumu "
"saraksts, piemēram, C<close> vai C<close,trace>.  Īpašā vērtība C<*> nozīmē "
"visus notikumus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:139
msgid ""
"The third and final parameter is the shell script fragment (or any external "
"command) that is executed when any of the events in the eventset occurs.  It "
"is executed using C<$SHELL -c>, or if C<$SHELL> is not set then F</bin/sh "
"-c>."
msgstr ""
"Trešais un pēdējais parametrs ir čaulas skripta fragments (vai jebkura ārēja "
"komanda), kas tiek izpildīts, kad notiek jebkurš no notikumiem kopā.  Tas "
"tiek izpildīts ar C<$SHELL -c> vai, ja C<$SHELL> nav iestatīts, ar F</bin/"
"sh -c>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:144
msgid ""
"The shell script fragment receives callback parameters as arguments C<$1>, "
"C<$2> etc.  The actual event that was called is available in the environment "
"variable C<$EVENT>."
msgstr ""
"Čaulas skripta fragments saņem atzvana parametrus kā argumentus C<$1>, C<$2> "
"u. c.  Faktiskais izsauktais notikums ir pieejams vides mainīgajā C<$EVENT>."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" event \"\" close \"echo closed\"\n"
" event messages appliance,library,trace \"echo $@\"\n"
" event \"\" progress \"echo progress: $3/$4\"\n"
" event \"\" * \"echo $EVENT $@\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" event \"\" close \"echo closed\"\n"
" event messages appliance,library,trace \"echo $@\"\n"
" event \"\" progress \"echo progress: $3/$4\"\n"
" event \"\" * \"echo $EVENT $@\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:153
msgid "See also the guestfish commands C<delete-event> and C<list-events>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī guestfish komandas C<delete-event> un C<list-events>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:155
msgid "glob"
msgstr "glob"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:157
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" glob command args...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" glob command args...\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:159
msgid ""
"Expand wildcards in any paths in the args list, and run C<command> "
"repeatedly on each matching path."
msgstr ""
"Izvērst aizstājējzīmes jebkuros ceļos argumentu sarakstā un atkārtoti "
"izpildīt C<command> katram atbilstošajam ceļam."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:162
msgid "See L</WILDCARDS AND GLOBBING>."
msgstr "Skatiet L</AIZSTĀJĒJZĪMES UN GLOBĒŠANA>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:164
msgid "hexedit"
msgstr "hexedit"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:166
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" hexedit <filename|device>\n"
" hexedit <filename|device> <max>\n"
" hexedit <filename|device> <start> <max>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" hexedit <filename|device>\n"
" hexedit <filename|device> <max>\n"
" hexedit <filename|device> <start> <max>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:170
msgid ""
"Use hexedit (a hex editor) to edit all or part of a binary file or block "
"device."
msgstr ""
"Izmantot hexedit (heksadecimālo redaktoru), lai rediģētu visu bināro failu "
"vai bloku ierīci vai tās daļu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:173
msgid ""
"This command works by downloading potentially the whole file or device, "
"editing it locally, then uploading it.  If the file or device is large, you "
"have to specify which part you wish to edit by using C<max> and/or C<start> "
"C<max> parameters.  C<start> and C<max> are specified in bytes, with the "
"usual modifiers allowed such as C<1M> (1 megabyte)."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda darbojas, lejupielādējot, iespējams, visu failu vai ierīci, "
"rediģējot to lokāli un pēc tam augšupielādējot.  Ja fails vai ierīce ir "
"liela, jānorāda, kuru daļu vēlaties rediģēt, izmantojot parametrus C<max> un/"
"vai C<start> C<max>.  C<start> un C<max> tiek norādīti baitos ar atļautajiem "
"parastajiem modifikatoriem, piemēram, C<1M> (1 megabaits)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:180
msgid "For example to edit the first few sectors of a disk you might do:"
msgstr "Piemēram, lai rediģētu diska dažus pirmos sektorus, varētu izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:183
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" hexedit /dev/sda 1M\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" hexedit /dev/sda 1M\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:185
msgid ""
"which would allow you to edit anywhere within the first megabyte of the "
"disk."
msgstr "kas ļautu rediģēt jebkur diska pirmajā megabaitā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:188
msgid "To edit the superblock of an ext2 filesystem on F</dev/sda1>, do:"
msgstr ""
"Lai rediģētu ext2 failu sistēmas superbloku ierīcē F</dev/sda1>, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:190
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" hexedit /dev/sda1 0x400 0x400\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" hexedit /dev/sda1 0x400 0x400\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:192
msgid "(assuming the superblock is in the standard location)."
msgstr "(pieņemot, ka superbloks atrodas standarta vietā)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:194
msgid ""
"This command requires the external L<hexedit(1)> program.  You can specify "
"another program to use by setting the C<HEXEDITOR> environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Šai komandai nepieciešama ārējā programma L<hexedit(1)>.  Citu izmantojamo "
"programmu var norādīt, iestatot vides mainīgo C<HEXEDITOR>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:198
msgid "See also L</hexdump>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</hexdump>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:200
msgid "lcd"
msgstr "lcd"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:202
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lcd directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lcd directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:204
msgid "Change the local directory, ie. the current directory of guestfish itself."
msgstr ""
"Mainīt lokālo direktoriju, t. i., paša guestfish pašreizējo direktoriju."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:207
msgid "Note that C<!cd> won't do what you might expect."
msgstr "Ņemiet vērā, ka C<!cd> nedarīs to, ko varētu gaidīt."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:209
msgid "list-events"
msgstr "list-events"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:211
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" list-events\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" list-events\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:213
msgid "List the event handlers registered using the guestfish C<event> command."
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt notikumu apstrādātājus, kas reģistrēti ar guestfish komandu "
"C<event>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:216
msgid "man"
msgstr "man"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:218
msgid "manual"
msgstr "manual"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:220
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  man\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  man\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:222
msgid "Opens the manual page for guestfish."
msgstr "Atver guestfish rokasgrāmatas lapu."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:224
msgid "more"
msgstr "more"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:226
msgid "less"
msgstr "less"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:228
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" more filename\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" more filename\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:230
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" less filename\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" less filename\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:232
msgid "This is used to view a file."
msgstr "To izmanto faila skatīšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:234
msgid ""
"The default viewer is C<$PAGER>.  However if you use the alternate command "
"C<less> you will get the C<less> command specifically."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma skatītājs ir C<$PAGER>.  Tomēr, ja izmantojat alternatīvo "
"komandu C<less>, saņemsiet tieši komandu C<less>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:237
msgid "not"
msgstr "not"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:239
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" not command [args...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" not command [args...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:241
msgid ""
"This runs an existing guestfish command and negates the exit code, so if the "
"command fails, then C<not command> succeeds."
msgstr ""
"Tas izpilda esošu guestfish komandu un noliedz izejas kodu, tāpēc, ja "
"komanda neizdodas, C<not command> izdodas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:244
msgid ""
"Note this doesn't reverse the sense of commands which return booleans.  "
"(eg. C<not exists /foo> doesn't do what you think)."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka tas neapgriež komandu, kas atgriež Būla vērtības, nozīmi.  "
"(Piem., C<not exists /foo> nedara to, ko domājat.)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:247
msgid "For example C<not cat /foo> will check that the file does not exist."
msgstr "Piemēram, C<not cat /foo> pārbaudīs, ka fails neeksistē."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:249
msgid "reopen"
msgstr "reopen"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:251
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  reopen\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  reopen\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:253
msgid ""
"Close and reopen the libguestfs handle.  It is not necessary to use this "
"normally, because the handle is closed properly when guestfish exits.  "
"However this is occasionally useful for testing."
msgstr ""
"Aizvērt un atkārtoti atvērt libguestfs rokturi.  Parasti tas nav jāizmanto, "
"jo rokturis tiek pareizi aizvērts, kad guestfish iziet.  Tomēr tas dažreiz "
"noder testēšanai."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:257
msgid "setenv"
msgstr "setenv"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:259
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  setenv VAR value\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  setenv VAR value\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:261
msgid "Set the environment variable C<VAR> to the string C<value>."
msgstr "Iestatīt vides mainīgo C<VAR> uz virkni C<value>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:263
msgid "To print the value of an environment variable use a shell command such as:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izdrukātu vides mainīgā vērtību, izmantojiet čaulas komandu, piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:266
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" !echo $VAR\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" !echo $VAR\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:268
msgid "sparse"
msgstr "sparse"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:270
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sparse filename size\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sparse filename size\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:272
msgid ""
"This creates an empty sparse file of the given size, and then adds so it can "
"be further examined."
msgstr ""
"Tas izveido tukšu dotā izmēra retinātu failu un pēc tam to pievieno, lai to "
"varētu tālāk pārbaudīt."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:275
msgid ""
"In all respects it works the same as the L</alloc> command, except that the "
"image file is allocated sparsely, which means that disk blocks are not "
"assigned to the file until they are needed.  Sparse disk files only use "
"space when written to, but they are slower and there is a danger you could "
"run out of real disk space during a write operation."
msgstr ""
"Visos aspektos tas darbojas tāpat kā komanda L</alloc>, izņemot to, ka "
"attēla fails tiek piešķirts retināti, t. i., diska bloki failam netiek "
"piešķirti, līdz tie ir vajadzīgi.  Retināti diska faili izmanto vietu tikai, "
"kad tajos raksta, bet tie ir lēnāki, un ir risks, ka rakstīšanas laikā var "
"pietrūkt reālas diska vietas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:285
msgid "See also the guestfish L</scratch> command."
msgstr "Skatīt arī guestfish komandu L</scratch>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:287
msgid "supported"
msgstr "supported"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:289
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" supported\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" supported\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:291
msgid ""
"This command returns a list of the optional groups known to the daemon, and "
"indicates which ones are supported by this build of the libguestfs "
"appliance."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda atgriež dēmonam zināmo neobligāto grupu sarakstu un norāda, kuras "
"atbalsta šī libguestfs palīgsistēmas būve."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:295
msgid "See also L<guestfs(3)/AVAILABILITY>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<guestfs(3)/PIEEJAMĪBA>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:297
msgid "time"
msgstr "time"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:299
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" time command args...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" time command args...\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:301
msgid ""
"Run the command as usual, but print the elapsed time afterwards.  This can "
"be useful for benchmarking operations."
msgstr ""
"Izpildīt komandu kā parasti, bet pēc tam izdrukāt pagājušo laiku.  Tas var "
"noderēt darbību veiktspējas mērīšanai."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:304
msgid "unsetenv"
msgstr "unsetenv"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:306
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  unsetenv VAR\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  unsetenv VAR\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-commands.pod:308
msgid "Remove C<VAR> from the environment."
msgstr "Noņemt C<VAR> no vides."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:27
msgid "B<-N disk> - create a blank disk"
msgstr "B<-N disk> - create a blank disk"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:29
msgid "C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]disk[:I<size>]>"
msgstr "C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]disk[:I<size>]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:31
msgid "Create a blank disk, size 1G (by default)."
msgstr "Izveidot tukšu disku, izmērs 1G (pēc noklusējuma)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:33
msgid "The default size can be changed by supplying an optional parameter."
msgstr "Noklusējuma izmēru var mainīt, norādot neobligātu parametru."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:40
msgid "B<-N part> - create a partitioned disk"
msgstr "B<-N part> - create a partitioned disk"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:42
msgid "C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]part[:I<size>[:I<partition>]]>"
msgstr "C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]part[:I<size>[:I<partition>]]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:44
msgid ""
"Create a disk with a single partition.  By default the size of the disk is "
"1G (the available space in the partition will be a tiny bit smaller)  and "
"the partition table will be MBR (old DOS-style)."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot disku ar vienu nodalījumu.  Pēc noklusējuma diska izmērs ir 1G "
"(pieejamā vieta nodalījumā būs nedaudz mazāka), un nodalījumu tabula būs MBR "
"(vecā DOS stila)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:48 fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:65
msgid "These defaults can be changed by supplying optional parameters."
msgstr "Šos noklusējumus var mainīt, norādot neobligātus parametrus."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:56
msgid "B<-N fs> - create a filesystem"
msgstr "B<-N fs> - create a filesystem"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:58
msgid "C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]fs[:I<filesystem>[:I<size>[:I<partition>]]]>"
msgstr ""
"C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]fs[:I<filesystem>[:I<size>[:I<partition>]]]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:60
msgid ""
"Create a disk with a single partition, with the partition containing an "
"empty filesystem.  This defaults to creating a 1G disk (the available space "
"in the filesystem will be a tiny bit smaller) with an MBR (old DOS-style) "
"partition table and an ext2 filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot disku ar vienu nodalījumu, kurā ir tukša failu sistēma.  Pēc "
"noklusējuma tiek izveidots 1G disks (pieejamā vieta failu sistēmā būs "
"nedaudz mazāka) ar MBR (vecā DOS stila) nodalījumu tabulu un ext2 failu "
"sistēmu."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:69
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" filesystem    ext2          the type of filesystem to use\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" filesystem    ext2          the type of filesystem to use\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:74
msgid "B<-N lv> - create a disk with logical volume"
msgstr "B<-N lv> - create a disk with logical volume"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:76
msgid "C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]lv[:I<name>[:I<size>[:I<partition>]]]>"
msgstr "C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]lv[:I<name>[:I<size>[:I<partition>]]]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:78
msgid ""
"Create a disk with a single partition, set up the partition as an LVM2 "
"physical volume, and place a volume group and logical volume on there.  This "
"defaults to creating a 1G disk with the VG and LV called C</dev/VG/LV>.  You "
"can change the name of the VG and LV by supplying an alternate name as the "
"first optional parameter."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot disku ar vienu nodalījumu, iestatīt nodalījumu kā LVM2 fizisko "
"sējumu un izvietot tajā sējumu grupu un loģisko sējumu.  Pēc noklusējuma "
"tiek izveidots 1G disks ar VG un LV C</dev/VG/LV>.  VG un LV nosaukumu var "
"mainīt, kā pirmo neobligāto parametru norādot alternatīvu nosaukumu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:84
msgid "Note this does not create a filesystem.  Use 'lvfs' to do that."
msgstr "Ņemiet vērā, ka tas neizveido failu sistēmu.  Tam izmantojiet 'lvfs'."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:88
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" name          /dev/VG/LV    the name of the VG and LV to use\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" name          /dev/VG/LV    the name of the VG and LV to use\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:93
msgid "B<-N lvfs> - create a disk with logical volume and filesystem"
msgstr "B<-N lvfs> - create a disk with logical volume and filesystem"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:95
msgid ""
"C<guestfish -N "
"[I<filename>=]lvfs[:I<name>[:I<filesystem>[:I<size>[:I<partition>]]]]>"
msgstr ""
"C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]lvfs[:I<name>[:I<filesystem>[:I<size>"
"[:I<partition>]]]]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:97
msgid ""
"Create a disk with a single partition, set up the partition as an LVM2 "
"physical volume, and place a volume group and logical volume on there.  Then "
"format the LV with a filesystem.  This defaults to creating a 1G disk with "
"the VG and LV called C</dev/VG/LV>, with an ext2 filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot disku ar vienu nodalījumu, iestatīt nodalījumu kā LVM2 fizisko "
"sējumu un izvietot tajā sējumu grupu un loģisko sējumu.  Pēc tam formatēt LV "
"ar failu sistēmu.  Pēc noklusējuma tiek izveidots 1G disks ar VG un LV C</"
"dev/VG/LV> ar ext2 failu sistēmu."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" name          /dev/VG/LV    the name of the VG and LV to use\n"
" filesystem    ext2          the type of filesystem to use\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" name          /dev/VG/LV    the name of the VG and LV to use\n"
" filesystem    ext2          the type of filesystem to use\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:111
msgid "B<-N bootroot> - create a boot and root filesystem"
msgstr "B<-N bootroot> - create a boot and root filesystem"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:113
msgid ""
"C<guestfish -N "
"[I<filename>=]bootroot[:I<bootfs>[:I<rootfs>[:I<size>[:I<bootsize>[:I<partition>]]]]]>"
msgstr ""
"C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]bootroot[:I<bootfs>[:I<rootfs>[:I<size>"
"[:I<bootsize>[:I<partition>]]]]]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:115
msgid ""
"Create a disk with two partitions, for boot and root filesystem.  Format the "
"two filesystems independently.  There are several optional parameters which "
"control the exact layout and filesystem types."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot disku ar diviem nodalījumiem — sāknēšanas un saknes failu "
"sistēmai.  Formatēt abas failu sistēmas neatkarīgi.  Ir vairāki neobligāti "
"parametri, kas kontrolē precīzu izkārtojumu un failu sistēmu tipus."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" bootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for boot\n"
" rootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for root\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" bootsize      128M          the size of the boot filesystem\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" bootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for boot\n"
" rootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for root\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" bootsize      128M          the size of the boot filesystem\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:128
msgid "B<-N bootrootlv> - create a boot and root filesystem using LVM"
msgstr "B<-N bootrootlv> - create a boot and root filesystem using LVM"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:130
msgid ""
"C<guestfish -N "
"[I<filename>=]bootrootlv[:I<name>[:I<bootfs>[:I<rootfs>[:I<size>[:I<bootsize>[:I<partition>]]]]]]>"
msgstr ""
"C<guestfish -N [I<filename>=]bootrootlv[:I<name>[:I<bootfs>[:I<rootfs>"
"[:I<size>[:I<bootsize>[:I<partition>]]]]]]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:132
msgid ""
"This is the same as C<bootroot> but the root filesystem (only) is placed on "
"a logical volume, named by default C</dev/VG/LV>.  There are several "
"optional parameters which control the exact layout."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas C<bootroot>, bet (tikai) saknes failu sistēma tiek "
"izvietota loģiskajā sējumā, pēc noklusējuma ar nosaukumu C</dev/VG/LV>.  Ir "
"vairāki neobligāti parametri, kas kontrolē precīzu izkārtojumu."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish-prepopts.pod:138
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" name          /dev/VG/LV    the name of the VG and LV for root\n"
" bootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for boot\n"
" rootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for root\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" bootsize      128M          the size of the boot filesystem\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Name          Default value\n"
" name          /dev/VG/LV    the name of the VG and LV for root\n"
" bootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for boot\n"
" rootfs        ext2          the type of filesystem to use for root\n"
" size          1G            the size of the disk image\n"
" bootsize      128M          the size of the boot filesystem\n"
" partition     mbr           partition table type\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:3
msgid "guestfish - the guest filesystem shell"
msgstr "guestfish - viesa failu sistēmas čaula"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish [--options] [commands]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish [--options] [commands]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish [--ro|--rw] -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish [--ro|--rw] -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish [--ro|--rw] -a disk.img -m dev[:mountpoint]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish [--ro|--rw] -a disk.img -m dev[:mountpoint]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -d libvirt-domain\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -d libvirt-domain\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish [--ro|--rw] -a disk.img -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish [--ro|--rw] -a disk.img -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -d libvirt-domain -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -d libvirt-domain -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:23
msgid ""
"Guestfish is a shell and command-line tool for examining and modifying "
"virtual machine filesystems.  It uses libguestfs and exposes all of the "
"functionality of the guestfs API, see L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Guestfish ir čaula un komandrindas rīks virtuālo mašīnu failu sistēmu "
"pārbaudei un mainīšanai.  Tas izmanto libguestfs un atklāj visu guestfs API "
"funkcionalitāti, skatiet L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:27
msgid ""
"Guestfish gives you structured access to the libguestfs API, from shell "
"scripts or the command line or interactively.  If you want to rescue a "
"broken virtual machine image, you should look at the L<virt-rescue(1)> "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Guestfish dod strukturētu piekļuvi libguestfs API no čaulas skriptiem, "
"komandrindas vai interaktīvi.  Ja vēlaties glābt bojātu virtuālās mašīnas "
"attēlu, apskatiet komandu L<virt-rescue(1)>."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:32 fish/guestfish.pod:1101 fish/virt-copy-in.pod:21
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:19 fish/virt-tar-in.pod:22 fish/virt-tar-out.pod:22
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:32
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr "PIEMĒRI"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:34
msgid "As an interactive shell"
msgstr "Kā interaktīva čaula"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ guestfish\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" $ guestfish\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Welcome to guestfish, the guest filesystem shell for\n"
" editing virtual machine filesystems.\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" Welcome to guestfish, the guest filesystem shell for\n"
" editing virtual machine filesystems.\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Type: 'help' for a list of commands\n"
"       'man' to read the manual\n"
"       'quit' to quit the shell\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" Type: 'help' for a list of commands\n"
"       'man' to read the manual\n"
"       'quit' to quit the shell\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> add-ro disk.img\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" ><fs> list-filesystems\n"
" /dev/sda1: ext4\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root: ext4\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_swap: swap\n"
" ><fs> mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root /\n"
" ><fs> cat /etc/fstab\n"
" # /etc/fstab\n"
" # Created by anaconda\n"
" [...]\n"
" ><fs> exit\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> add-ro disk.img\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" ><fs> list-filesystems\n"
" /dev/sda1: ext4\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root: ext4\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_swap: swap\n"
" ><fs> mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root /\n"
" ><fs> cat /etc/fstab\n"
" # /etc/fstab\n"
" # Created by anaconda\n"
" [...]\n"
" ><fs> exit\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:58
msgid "From shell scripts"
msgstr "No čaulas skriptiem"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:60
msgid "Create a new F</etc/motd> file in a guest or disk image:"
msgstr "Izveidot jaunu failu F</etc/motd> viesī vai diska attēlā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish <<_EOF_\n"
" add disk.img\n"
" run\n"
" mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root /\n"
" write /etc/motd \"Welcome, new users\"\n"
" _EOF_\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish <<_EOF_\n"
" add disk.img\n"
" run\n"
" mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root /\n"
" write /etc/motd \"Welcome, new users\"\n"
" _EOF_\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:69
msgid "List the LVM logical volumes in a disk image:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt LVM loģiskos sējumus diska attēlā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:71
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a disk.img --ro <<_EOF_\n"
" run\n"
" lvs\n"
" _EOF_\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a disk.img --ro <<_EOF_\n"
" run\n"
" lvs\n"
" _EOF_\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:76
msgid "List all the filesystems in a disk image:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas failu sistēmas diska attēlā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a disk.img --ro <<_EOF_\n"
" run\n"
" list-filesystems\n"
" _EOF_\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a disk.img --ro <<_EOF_\n"
" run\n"
" list-filesystems\n"
" _EOF_\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:83
msgid "On one command line"
msgstr "Vienā komandrindā"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:85 fish/virt-copy-in.pod:23
msgid "Update F</etc/resolv.conf> in a guest:"
msgstr "Atjaunināt F</etc/resolv.conf> viesī:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:87
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish \\\n"
"   add disk.img : run : mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root / : \\\n"
"   write /etc/resolv.conf \"nameserver 1.2.3.4\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish \\\n"
"   add disk.img : run : mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root / : \\\n"
"   write /etc/resolv.conf \"nameserver 1.2.3.4\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:91
msgid "Edit F</boot/grub/grub.conf> interactively:"
msgstr "Interaktīvi rediģēt F</boot/grub/grub.conf>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw --add disk.img \\\n"
"   --mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root \\\n"
"   --mount /dev/sda1:/boot \\\n"
"   edit /boot/grub/grub.conf\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw --add disk.img \\\n"
"   --mount /dev/vg_guest/lv_root \\\n"
"   --mount /dev/sda1:/boot \\\n"
"   edit /boot/grub/grub.conf\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:98
msgid "Mount disks automatically"
msgstr "Automātiska disku montēšana"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:100
msgid ""
"Use the I<-i> option to automatically mount the disks from a virtual "
"machine:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet opciju I<-i>, lai automātiski montētu virtuālās mašīnas diskus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i cat /etc/group\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a disk.img -i cat /etc/group\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -d libvirt-domain -i cat /etc/group\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -d libvirt-domain -i cat /etc/group\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:107
msgid "Another way to edit F</boot/grub/grub.conf> interactively is:"
msgstr "Vēl viens veids, kā interaktīvi rediģēt F</boot/grub/grub.conf>, ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -a disk.img -i edit /boot/grub/grub.conf\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -a disk.img -i edit /boot/grub/grub.conf\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:111
msgid "As a script interpreter"
msgstr "Kā skriptu interpretators"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:113
msgid "Create a 100MB disk containing an ext2-formatted partition:"
msgstr "Izveidot 100MB disku ar ext2 formatētu nodalījumu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #!/usr/bin/guestfish -f\n"
" sparse test1.img 100M\n"
" run\n"
" part-disk /dev/sda mbr\n"
" mkfs ext2 /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #!/usr/bin/guestfish -f\n"
" sparse test1.img 100M\n"
" run\n"
" part-disk /dev/sda mbr\n"
" mkfs ext2 /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:121
msgid "Start with a prepared disk"
msgstr "Sākšana ar sagatavotu disku"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:123
msgid ""
"Create a 1G disk called F<test1.img> containing a single ext2-formatted "
"partition:"
msgstr "Izveidot 1G disku F<test1.img> ar vienu ext2 formatētu nodalījumu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:126
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -N fs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -N fs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:128
msgid "To list what is available do:"
msgstr "Lai uzskaitītu, kas ir pieejams, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:130
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -N help | less\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -N help | less\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:132
msgid "Remote drives"
msgstr "Attāli diski"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:134
msgid "Access a remote disk using ssh:"
msgstr "Piekļūt attālam diskam, izmantojot ssh:"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:138
msgid "Remote control"
msgstr "Tālvadība"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:140
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
" guestfish --remote add-ro disk.img\n"
" guestfish --remote run\n"
" guestfish --remote lvs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
" guestfish --remote add-ro disk.img\n"
" guestfish --remote run\n"
" guestfish --remote lvs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:151
msgid "Displays general help on options."
msgstr "Parāda vispārīgu palīdzību par opcijām."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:153
msgid "B<-h>"
msgstr "B<-h>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:155
msgid "B<--cmd-help>"
msgstr "B<--cmd-help>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:157
msgid "Lists all available guestfish commands."
msgstr "Uzskaita visas pieejamās guestfish komandas."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:159
msgid "B<-h> CMD"
msgstr "B<-h> CMD"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:161
msgid "B<--cmd-help> CMD"
msgstr "B<--cmd-help> CMD"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:163
msgid "Displays detailed help on a single command C<cmd>."
msgstr "Parāda detalizētu palīdzību par vienu komandu C<cmd>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:165 fuse/guestmount.pod:160
msgid "B<-a> IMAGE"
msgstr "B<-a> IMAGE"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:167 fuse/guestmount.pod:162
msgid "B<--add> IMAGE"
msgstr "B<--add> IMAGE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:169
msgid "Add a block device or virtual machine image to the shell."
msgstr "Pievienot čaulai bloku ierīci vai virtuālās mašīnas attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:171 fuse/guestmount.pod:166 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:102
msgid ""
"The format of the disk image is auto-detected.  To override this and force a "
"particular format use the I<--format=..> option."
msgstr ""
"Diska attēla formāts tiek noteikts automātiski.  Lai to pārdefinētu un "
"piespiestu konkrētu formātu, izmantojiet opciju I<--format=..>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:174
msgid ""
"Using this flag is mostly equivalent to using the C<add> command, with "
"C<readonly:true> if the I<--ro> flag was given, and with C<format:...> if "
"the I<--format=...> flag was given."
msgstr ""
"Šī karoga izmantošana lielākoties ir līdzvērtīga komandas C<add> "
"izmantošanai ar C<readonly:true>, ja tika norādīts karogs I<--ro>, un ar "
"C<format:...>, ja tika norādīts karogs I<--format=...>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:178 fuse/guestmount.pod:169 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:105
msgid "B<-a> URI"
msgstr "B<-a> URI"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:180 fuse/guestmount.pod:171 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:107
msgid "B<--add> URI"
msgstr "B<--add> URI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:182
msgid "Add a remote disk.  See L</ADDING REMOTE STORAGE>."
msgstr "Pievienot attālu disku.  Skatiet L</ATTĀLĀS KRĀTUVES PIEVIENOŠANA>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:184 fuse/guestmount.pod:175 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:115
msgid "__INCLUDE:blocksize-option.pod__"
msgstr "__INCLUDE:blocksize-option.pod__"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:186 fuse/guestmount.pod:177 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:117
msgid "B<-c> URI"
msgstr "B<-c> URI"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:188 fuse/guestmount.pod:179 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:119
msgid "B<--connect> URI"
msgstr "B<--connect> URI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:190 fuse/guestmount.pod:181
msgid ""
"When used in conjunction with the I<-d> option, this specifies the libvirt "
"URI to use.  The default is to use the default libvirt connection."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmanto kopā ar opciju I<-d>, tas norāda izmantojamo libvirt URI.  "
"Noklusējums ir izmantot noklusējuma libvirt savienojumu."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:194
msgid "B<--csh>"
msgstr "B<--csh>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:196
msgid ""
"If using the I<--listen> option and a csh-like shell, use this option.  See "
"section L</REMOTE CONTROL AND CSH> below."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat opciju I<--listen> un csh līdzīgu čaulu, izmantojiet šo "
"opciju.  Skatiet sadaļu L</TĀLVADĪBA UN CSH> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:199 fuse/guestmount.pod:185
msgid "B<-d> LIBVIRT-DOMAIN"
msgstr "B<-d> LIBVIRT-DOMAIN"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:201 fuse/guestmount.pod:187
msgid "B<--domain> LIBVIRT-DOMAIN"
msgstr "B<--domain> LIBVIRT-DOMAIN"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:203 fuse/guestmount.pod:189
msgid ""
"Add disks from the named libvirt domain.  If the I<--ro> option is also "
"used, then any libvirt domain can be used.  However in write mode, only "
"libvirt domains which are shut down can be named here."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot diskus no nosauktā libvirt domēna.  Ja izmantota arī opcija I<--ro>"
", var izmantot jebkuru libvirt domēnu.  Tomēr rakstīšanas režīmā šeit var "
"nosaukt tikai izslēgtus libvirt domēnus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:207 fuse/guestmount.pod:193
msgid "Domain UUIDs can be used instead of names."
msgstr "Nosaukumu vietā var izmantot domēnu UUID."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:209
msgid ""
"Using this flag is mostly equivalent to using the C<add-domain> command, "
"with C<readonly:true> if the I<--ro> flag was given, and with C<format:...> "
"if the I<--format=...> flag was given."
msgstr ""
"Šī karoga izmantošana lielākoties ir līdzvērtīga komandas C<add-domain> "
"izmantošanai ar C<readonly:true>, ja tika norādīts karogs I<--ro>, un ar "
"C<format:...>, ja tika norādīts karogs I<--format=...>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:213 fuse/guestmount.pod:207
msgid "B<--echo-keys>"
msgstr "B<--echo-keys>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:215 fuse/guestmount.pod:209
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, guestfish normally turns echoing "
"off so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried about "
"Tempest attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify this "
"flag to see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, guestfish parasti izslēdz atbalsi, lai "
"nevarētu redzēt rakstīto.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest uzbrukumiem un "
"telpā nav neviena cita, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu rakstīto."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:220
msgid "B<-f> FILE"
msgstr "B<-f> FILE"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:222
msgid "B<--file> FILE"
msgstr "B<--file> FILE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:224
msgid "Read commands from C<FILE>.  To write pure guestfish scripts, use:"
msgstr ""
"Nolasīt komandas no C<FILE>.  Lai rakstītu tīrus guestfish skriptus, "
"izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:227
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #!/usr/bin/guestfish -f\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #!/usr/bin/guestfish -f\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:229 fuse/guestmount.pod:221 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:157
msgid "B<--format=raw|qcow2|..>"
msgstr "B<--format=raw|qcow2|..>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:231 fuse/guestmount.pod:223 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:159
msgid "B<--format>"
msgstr "B<--format>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:233 fuse/guestmount.pod:225 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:161
msgid ""
"The default for the I<-a> option is to auto-detect the format of the disk "
"image.  Using this forces the disk format for I<-a> options which follow on "
"the command line.  Using I<--format> with no argument switches back to "
"auto-detection for subsequent I<-a> options."
msgstr ""
"Opcijai I<-a> pēc noklusējuma diska attēla formāts tiek noteikts "
"automātiski.  Šī opcija piespiež diska formātu komandrindā sekojošām opcijām "
"I<-a>.  I<--format> bez argumenta pārslēdz atpakaļ uz automātisku noteikšanu "
"nākamajām opcijām I<-a>."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:240
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:242 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:170
msgid "forces raw format (no auto-detection) for F<disk.img>."
msgstr "piespiež raw formātu (bez automātiskas noteikšanas) failam F<disk.img>."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:244
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:246 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:174
msgid ""
"forces raw format (no auto-detection) for F<disk.img> and reverts to "
"auto-detection for F<another.img>."
msgstr ""
"piespiež raw formātu (bez automātiskas noteikšanas) failam F<disk.img> un "
"atgriežas pie automātiskas noteikšanas failam F<another.img>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:249
msgid ""
"If you have untrusted raw-format guest disk images, you should use this "
"option to specify the disk format.  This avoids a possible security problem "
"with malicious guests (CVE-2010-3851).  See also L</add>."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir neuzticami raw formāta viesa disku attēli, šī opcija jāizmanto "
"diska formāta norādīšanai.  Tas novērš iespējamu drošības problēmu ar "
"ļaunprātīgiem viesiem (CVE-2010-3851).  Skatīt arī L</add>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:254 fuse/guestmount.pod:243 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:181
msgid "B<-i>"
msgstr "B<-i>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:256 fuse/guestmount.pod:245 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:183
msgid "B<--inspector>"
msgstr "B<--inspector>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:258 fuse/guestmount.pod:247 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:185
msgid ""
"Using L<virt-inspector(1)> code, inspect the disks looking for an operating "
"system and mount filesystems as they would be mounted on the real virtual "
"machine."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot L<virt-inspector(1)> kodu, inspicēt diskus, meklējot "
"operētājsistēmu, un montēt failu sistēmas tā, kā tās tiktu montētas reālajā "
"virtuālajā mašīnā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:262
msgid "Typical usage is either:"
msgstr "Tipisks lietojums ir vai nu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:264
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -d myguest -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -d myguest -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:266
msgid "(for an inactive libvirt domain called I<myguest>), or:"
msgstr "(neaktīvam libvirt domēnam I<myguest>), vai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:268
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -d myguest -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -d myguest -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:270
msgid "(for active domains, readonly), or specify the block device directly:"
msgstr "(aktīviem domēniem, tikai lasīšanai), vai norādiet bloku ierīci tieši:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:272
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -a /dev/Guests/MyGuest -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -a /dev/Guests/MyGuest -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:274
msgid ""
"Note that the command line syntax changed slightly over older versions of "
"guestfish.  You can still use the old syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka komandrindas sintakse salīdzinājumā ar vecākām guestfish "
"versijām ir nedaudz mainījusies.  Joprojām varat izmantot veco sintaksi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:277
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish [--ro] -i disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish [--ro] -i disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:279
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish [--ro] -i libvirt-domain\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish [--ro] -i libvirt-domain\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:281
msgid ""
"Using this flag is mostly equivalent to using the C<inspect-os> command and "
"then using other commands to mount the filesystems that were found."
msgstr ""
"Šī karoga izmantošana lielākoties ir līdzvērtīga komandas C<inspect-os> "
"izmantošanai un pēc tam citu komandu izmantošanai atrasto failu sistēmu "
"montēšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:285 fuse/guestmount.pod:251
msgid "__INCLUDE:key-option.pod__"
msgstr "__INCLUDE:key-option.pod__"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:287 fuse/guestmount.pod:253
msgid "__INCLUDE:keys-from-stdin-option.pod__"
msgstr "__INCLUDE:keys-from-stdin-option.pod__"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:291
msgid ""
"Fork into the background and listen for remote commands.  See section "
"L</REMOTE CONTROL GUESTFISH OVER A SOCKET> below."
msgstr ""
"Sazaroties fonā un klausīties attālās komandas.  Skatiet sadaļu L</GUESTFISH "
"TĀLVADĪBA CAUR LIGZDU> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:294 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:198
msgid "B<-m> dev[:mountpoint[:options[:fstype]]]"
msgstr "B<-m> dev[:mountpoint[:options[:fstype]]]"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:296 fuse/guestmount.pod:257 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:200
msgid "B<--mount> dev[:mountpoint[:options[:fstype]]]"
msgstr "B<--mount> dev[:mountpoint[:options[:fstype]]]"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:298
msgid "Mount the named partition or logical volume on the given mountpoint."
msgstr ""
"Montēt nosaukto nodalījumu vai loģisko sējumu norādītajā montēšanas punktā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:300
msgid "If the mountpoint is omitted, it defaults to F</>."
msgstr "Ja montēšanas punkts ir izlaists, noklusējums ir F</>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:302
msgid "You have to mount something on F</> before most commands will work."
msgstr "Lai lielākā daļa komandu darbotos, kaut kas jāmontē F</>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:304
msgid ""
"If any I<-m> or I<--mount> options are given, the guest is automatically "
"launched."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādītas jebkuras opcijas I<-m> vai I<--mount>, viesis tiek palaists "
"automātiski."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:307
msgid ""
"If you don’t know what filesystems a disk image contains, you can either run "
"guestfish without this option, then list the partitions, filesystems and LVs "
"available (see L</list-partitions>, L</list-filesystems> and L</lvs> "
"commands), or you can use the L<virt-filesystems(1)> program."
msgstr ""
"Ja nezināt, kādas failu sistēmas ir diska attēlā, varat palaist guestfish "
"bez šīs opcijas un tad uzskaitīt pieejamos nodalījumus, failu sistēmas un LV "
"(skatiet komandas L</list-partitions>, L</list-filesystems> un L</lvs>), vai "
"izmantot programmu L<virt-filesystems(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:313 fuse/guestmount.pod:265 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:210
msgid ""
"The third (and rarely used) part of the mount parameter is the list of mount "
"options used to mount the underlying filesystem.  If this is not given, then "
"the mount options are either the empty string or C<ro> (the latter if the "
"I<--ro> flag is used).  By specifying the mount options, you override this "
"default choice.  Probably the only time you would use this is to enable ACLs "
"and/or extended attributes if the filesystem can support them:"
msgstr ""
"Montēšanas parametra trešā (un reti izmantotā) daļa ir montēšanas opciju "
"saraksts, ar ko montēt pamatā esošo failu sistēmu.  Ja tā nav norādīta, "
"montēšanas opcijas ir vai nu tukša virkne, vai C<ro> (pēdējā, ja izmantots "
"karogs I<--ro>).  Norādot montēšanas opcijas, jūs pārdefinējat šo "
"noklusējuma izvēli.  Droši vien vienīgais gadījums, kad to izmantotu, ir ACL "
"un/vai paplašināto atribūtu iespējošana, ja failu sistēma tos atbalsta:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:321 fuse/guestmount.pod:273 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:218
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" -m /dev/sda1:/:acl,user_xattr\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" -m /dev/sda1:/:acl,user_xattr\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:323
msgid "Using this flag is equivalent to using the C<mount-options> command."
msgstr ""
"Šī karoga izmantošana ir līdzvērtīga komandas C<mount-options> izmantošanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:325 fuse/guestmount.pod:275 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:220
msgid ""
"The fourth part of the parameter is the filesystem driver to use, such as "
"C<ext3> or C<ntfs>. This is rarely needed, but can be useful if multiple "
"drivers are valid for a filesystem (eg: C<ext2> and C<ext3>), or if "
"libguestfs misidentifies a filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Parametra ceturtā daļa ir izmantojamais failu sistēmas draiveris, piemēram, "
"C<ext3> vai C<ntfs>. Tas vajadzīgs reti, taču var noderēt, ja failu sistēmai "
"der vairāki draiveri (piem., C<ext2> un C<ext3>) vai ja libguestfs nepareizi "
"identificē failu sistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:332
msgid "Enable QEMU user networking in the guest."
msgstr "Iespējot QEMU lietotāja tīklošanu viesī."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:334
msgid "B<-N> [FILENAME=]TYPE"
msgstr "B<-N> [FILENAME=]TYPE"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:336
msgid "B<--new> [FILENAME=]TYPE"
msgstr "B<--new> [FILENAME=]TYPE"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:338
msgid "B<-N> B<help>"
msgstr "B<-N> B<help>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:340
msgid ""
"Prepare a fresh disk image formatted as C<TYPE>.  This is an alternative to "
"the I<-a> option: whereas I<-a> adds an existing disk, I<-N> creates a "
"preformatted disk with a filesystem and adds it.  See L</PREPARED DISK "
"IMAGES> below."
msgstr ""
"Sagatavot jaunu diska attēlu, formatētu kā C<TYPE>.  Tā ir alternatīva "
"opcijai I<-a>: kamēr I<-a> pievieno esošu disku, I<-N> izveido iepriekš "
"formatētu disku ar failu sistēmu un pievieno to.  Skatiet L</SAGATAVOTI "
"DISKU ATTĒLI> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:347 fuse/guestmount.pod:286
msgid "B<--no-sync>"
msgstr "B<--no-sync>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:349
msgid ""
"Disable autosync.  This is enabled by default.  See the discussion of "
"autosync in the L<guestfs(3)> manpage."
msgstr ""
"Atspējot automātisko sinhronizāciju.  Pēc noklusējuma tā ir iespējota.  "
"Skatiet automātiskās sinhronizācijas aplūkojumu L<guestfs(3)> rokasgrāmatas "
"lapā."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:352
msgid "B<--no-dest-paths>"
msgstr "B<--no-dest-paths>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:354
msgid ""
"Don’t tab-complete paths on the guest filesystem.  It is useful to be able "
"to hit the tab key to complete paths on the guest filesystem, but this "
"causes extra \"hidden\" guestfs calls to be made, so this option is here to "
"allow this feature to be disabled."
msgstr ""
"Nepabeigt ceļus ar tabulēšanu viesa failu sistēmā.  Ir noderīgi, ka ar "
"tabulēšanas taustiņu var pabeigt ceļus viesa failu sistēmā, taču tas izraisa "
"papildu „slēptus” guestfs izsaukumus, tāpēc šī opcija ļauj šo līdzekli "
"atspējot."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:359
msgid "B<--pipe-error>"
msgstr "B<--pipe-error>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:361
msgid ""
"If writes fail to pipe commands (see L</PIPES> below), then the command "
"returns an error."
msgstr ""
"Ja rakstīšana kanāla komandās neizdodas (skatiet L</KANĀLI> tālāk), komanda "
"atgriež kļūdu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:364
msgid "The default (also for historical reasons) is to ignore such errors so that:"
msgstr "Noklusējums (arī vēsturisku iemeslu dēļ) ir ignorēt šādas kļūdas, lai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:367
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> command_with_lots_of_output | head\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> command_with_lots_of_output | head\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:369
msgid "doesn't give an error."
msgstr "nedotu kļūdu."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:371
msgid "B<--progress-bars>"
msgstr "B<--progress-bars>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:373
msgid "Enable progress bars, even when guestfish is used non-interactively."
msgstr ""
"Iespējot progresa joslas pat tad, ja guestfish tiek izmantots neinteraktīvi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:375
msgid ""
"Progress bars are enabled by default when guestfish is used as an "
"interactive shell."
msgstr ""
"Progresa joslas pēc noklusējuma ir iespējotas, kad guestfish tiek izmantots "
"kā interaktīva čaula."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:378
msgid "B<--no-progress-bars>"
msgstr "B<--no-progress-bars>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:380
msgid "Disable progress bars."
msgstr "Atspējot progresa joslas."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:382
msgid "B<--remote>"
msgstr "B<--remote>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:384
msgid "B<--remote=>PID"
msgstr "B<--remote=>PID"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:386
msgid ""
"Send remote commands to C<$GUESTFISH_PID> or C<pid>.  See section L</REMOTE "
"CONTROL GUESTFISH OVER A SOCKET> below."
msgstr ""
"Sūtīt attālās komandas uz C<$GUESTFISH_PID> vai C<pid>.  Skatiet sadaļu L</"
"GUESTFISH TĀLVADĪBA CAUR LIGZDU> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:391 fuse/guestmount.pod:350 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:231
msgid "B<--ro>"
msgstr "B<--ro>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:393
msgid ""
"This changes the I<-a>, I<-d> and I<-m> options so that disks are added and "
"mounts are done read-only."
msgstr ""
"Tas maina opcijas I<-a>, I<-d> un I<-m>, lai diski tiktu pievienoti un "
"montējumi veikti tikai lasīšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:396 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:235
msgid ""
"The option must always be used if the disk image or virtual machine might be "
"running, and is generally recommended in cases where you don't need write "
"access to the disk."
msgstr ""
"Opcija vienmēr jāizmanto, ja diska attēls vai virtuālā mašīna var darboties, "
"un parasti tā ieteicama gadījumos, kad rakstīšanas piekļuve diskam nav "
"vajadzīga."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:400
msgid ""
"Note that prepared disk images created with I<-N> are not affected by this "
"option.  Also commands like C<add> are not affected - you have to specify "
"the C<readonly:true> option explicitly if you need it."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šī opcija neietekmē ar I<-N> izveidotos sagatavotos disku "
"attēlus.  Tāpat netiek ietekmētas tādas komandas kā C<add> — ja "
"nepieciešams, opcija C<readonly:true> jānorāda eksplicīti."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:404
msgid "See also L</OPENING DISKS FOR READ AND WRITE> below."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</DISKU ATVĒRŠANA LASĪŠANAI UN RAKSTĪŠANAI> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:406 fuse/guestmount.pod:362 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:253
msgid "B<--selinux>"
msgstr "B<--selinux>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:408 fuse/guestmount.pod:364 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:255
msgid "This option is provided for backwards compatibility and does nothing."
msgstr "Šī opcija nodrošināta atpakaļsaderībai un neko nedara."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:414
msgid ""
"Enable very verbose messages.  This is particularly useful if you find a "
"bug."
msgstr "Iespējot ļoti izvērstus ziņojumus.  Tas īpaši noder, ja atrodat kļūdu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:421
msgid "Display the guestfish / libguestfs version number and exit."
msgstr "Parādīt guestfish / libguestfs versijas numuru un iziet."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:423 fuse/guestmount.pod:378 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:283
msgid "B<-w>"
msgstr "B<-w>"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:425 fuse/guestmount.pod:380 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:285
msgid "B<--rw>"
msgstr "B<--rw>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:427 fuse/guestmount.pod:382 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:287
msgid ""
"This changes the I<-a>, I<-d> and I<-m> options so that disks are added and "
"mounts are done read-write."
msgstr ""
"Tas maina opcijas I<-a>, I<-d> un I<-m>, lai diski tiktu pievienoti un "
"montējumi veikti lasīšanai un rakstīšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:430
msgid "See L</OPENING DISKS FOR READ AND WRITE> below."
msgstr "Skatiet L</DISKU ATVĒRŠANA LASĪŠANAI UN RAKSTĪŠANAI> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:432 fuse/guestmount.pod:387 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:292
msgid "B<-x>"
msgstr "B<-x>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:434
msgid "Echo each command before executing it."
msgstr "Atbalsot katru komandu pirms tās izpildes."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:438
msgid "COMMANDS ON COMMAND LINE"
msgstr "KOMANDAS KOMANDRINDĀ"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:440
msgid "Any additional (non-option) arguments are treated as commands to execute."
msgstr ""
"Visi papildu (ne-opciju) argumenti tiek uzskatīti par izpildāmām komandām."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:443
msgid ""
"Commands to execute should be separated by a colon (C<:>), where the colon "
"is a separate parameter.  Thus:"
msgstr ""
"Izpildāmās komandas jāatdala ar kolu (C<:>), kur kols ir atsevišķs "
"parametrs.  Tādējādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:446
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish cmd [args...] : cmd [args...] : cmd [args...] ...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish cmd [args...] : cmd [args...] : cmd [args...] ...\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:448
msgid ""
"If there are no additional arguments, then we enter a shell, either an "
"interactive shell with a prompt (if the input is a terminal) or a "
"non-interactive shell."
msgstr ""
"Ja papildu argumentu nav, nonākam čaulā — vai nu interaktīvā čaulā ar "
"uzvedni (ja ievade ir terminālis), vai neinteraktīvā čaulā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:452
msgid ""
"In either command line mode or non-interactive shell, the first command that "
"gives an error causes the whole shell to exit.  In interactive mode (with a "
"prompt) if a command fails, you can continue to enter commands."
msgstr ""
"Gan komandrindas režīmā, gan neinteraktīvā čaulā pirmā komanda, kas dod "
"kļūdu, liek visai čaulai iziet.  Interaktīvajā režīmā (ar uzvedni), ja "
"komanda neizdodas, varat turpināt ievadīt komandas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:457
msgid ""
"Note that arguments of the commands will be considered as guestfish options "
"if they start with a dash (C<->): you can always separate the guestfish "
"options and the rest of the commands (with their arguments)  using a double "
"dash (C<-->).  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka komandu argumenti tiks uzskatīti par guestfish opcijām, ja "
"tie sākas ar domuzīmi (C<->): guestfish opcijas un pārējās komandas (ar to "
"argumentiem) vienmēr var atdalīt ar dubultu domuzīmi (C<-->).  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:462
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -- disk_create overlay.qcow2 qcow2 -1 backingfile:image.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -- disk_create overlay.qcow2 qcow2 -1 backingfile:image.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:464
msgid "USING launch (OR run)"
msgstr "LAUNCH (VAI RUN) IZMANTOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:466
msgid ""
"As with L<guestfs(3)>, you must first configure your guest by adding disks, "
"then launch it, then mount any disks you need, and finally issue "
"actions/commands.  So the general order of the day is:"
msgstr ""
"Tāpat kā L<guestfs(3)>, viesis vispirms jākonfigurē, pievienojot diskus, tad "
"jāpalaiž, tad jāmontē vajadzīgie diski un visbeidzot jāizdod darbības/"
"komandas.  Tātad vispārējā kārtība ir:"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:474
msgid "add or -a/--add"
msgstr "add vai -a/--add"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:478
msgid "launch (aka run)"
msgstr "launch (jeb run)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:482
msgid "mount or -m/--mount"
msgstr "mount vai -m/--mount"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:486
msgid "any other commands"
msgstr "jebkuras citas komandas"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:490
msgid ""
"C<run> is a synonym for C<launch>.  You must C<launch> (or C<run>)  your "
"guest before mounting or performing any other commands."
msgstr ""
"C<run> ir C<launch> sinonīms.  Pirms montēšanas vai jebkuru citu komandu "
"izpildes viesis jāpalaiž ar C<launch> (vai C<run>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:493
msgid ""
"The only exception is that if any of the I<-i>, I<-m>, I<--mount>, I<-N> or "
"I<--new> options were given then C<run> is done automatically, simply "
"because guestfish can't perform the action you asked for without doing this."
msgstr ""
"Vienīgais izņēmums ir, ja tika norādīta kāda no opcijām I<-i>, I<-m>, I<--"
"mount>, I<-N> vai I<--new>, tad C<run> tiek veikts automātiski, vienkārši "
"tāpēc, ka guestfish bez tā nevar veikt pieprasīto darbību."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:498
msgid "OPENING DISKS FOR READ AND WRITE"
msgstr "DISKU ATVĒRŠANA LASĪŠANAI UN RAKSTĪŠANAI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:500
msgid ""
"The guestfish, L<guestmount(1)> and L<virt-rescue(1)> options I<--ro> and "
"I<--rw> affect whether the other command line options I<-a>, I<-c>, I<-d>, "
"I<-i> and I<-m> open disk images read-only or for writing."
msgstr ""
"Guestfish, L<guestmount(1)> un L<virt-rescue(1)> opcijas I<--ro> un I<--rw> "
"ietekmē, vai citas komandrindas opcijas I<-a>, I<-c>, I<-d>, I<-i> un I<-m> "
"atver disku attēlus tikai lasīšanai vai rakstīšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:505
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<le> 1.10, guestfish, guestmount and virt-rescue defaulted to "
"opening disk images supplied on the command line for write.  To open a disk "
"image read-only you have to do I<-a image --ro>."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<le> 1.10 guestfish, guestmount un virt-rescue pēc noklusējuma "
"atvēra komandrindā norādītos disku attēlus rakstīšanai.  Lai atvērtu diska "
"attēlu tikai lasīšanai, jāizpilda I<-a image --ro>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:509
msgid ""
"This matters: If you accidentally open a live VM disk image writable then "
"you will cause irreversible disk corruption."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir svarīgi: ja nejauši atverat darbojošās VM diska attēlu rakstīšanai, "
"izraisīsiet neatgriezenisku diska bojājumu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:512
msgid ""
"In a future libguestfs we intend to change the default the other way.  Disk "
"images will be opened read-only.  You will have to either specify "
"I<guestfish --rw>, I<guestmount --rw>, I<virt-rescue --rw>, or change the "
"configuration file in order to get write access for disk images specified by "
"those other command line options."
msgstr ""
"Nākamajā libguestfs versijā plānojam mainīt noklusējumu uz pretējo.  Disku "
"attēli tiks atvērti tikai lasīšanai.  Lai iegūtu rakstīšanas piekļuvi ar šīm "
"citām komandrindas opcijām norādītajiem disku attēliem, būs jānorāda "
"I<guestfish --rw>, I<guestmount --rw>, I<virt-rescue --rw> vai jāmaina "
"konfigurācijas fails."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:518
msgid ""
"This version of guestfish, guestmount and virt-rescue has a I<--rw> option "
"which does nothing (it is already the default).  However it is highly "
"recommended that you use this option to indicate that you need write access, "
"and prepare your scripts for the day when this option will be required for "
"write access."
msgstr ""
"Šai guestfish, guestmount un virt-rescue versijai ir opcija I<--rw>, kas "
"neko nedara (tā jau ir noklusējums).  Tomēr ļoti ieteicams izmantot šo "
"opciju, lai norādītu, ka nepieciešama rakstīšanas piekļuve, un sagatavot "
"skriptus dienai, kad šī opcija būs obligāta rakstīšanas piekļuvei."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:524
msgid ""
"B<Note:> This does I<not> affect commands like L</add> and L</mount>, or any "
"other libguestfs program apart from guestfish and guestmount."
msgstr ""
"B<Piezīme:> tas I<neietekmē> tādas komandas kā L</add> un L</mount> vai "
"jebkuru citu libguestfs programmu, izņemot guestfish un guestmount."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:527
msgid "QUOTING"
msgstr "CITĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:529
msgid ""
"You can quote ordinary parameters using either single or double quotes.  For "
"example:"
msgstr "Parastos parametrus var likt vienpēdiņās vai dubultpēdiņās.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:532
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" add \"file with a space.img\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" add \"file with a space.img\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:534
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rm '/file name'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rm '/file name'\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:536
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rm '/\"'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rm '/\"'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:538
msgid ""
"A few commands require a list of strings to be passed.  For these, use a "
"whitespace-separated list, enclosed in quotes.  Strings containing "
"whitespace to be passed through must be enclosed in single quotes.  A "
"literal single quote must be escaped with a backslash."
msgstr ""
"Dažām komandām jānodod virkņu saraksts.  Tām izmantojiet ar atstarpēm "
"atdalītu sarakstu, kas ietverts pēdiņās.  Virknes ar atstarpēm, kas jānodod "
"tālāk, jāietver vienpēdiņās.  Burtiska vienpēdiņa jāatsoļo ar atpakaļvērsto "
"slīpsvītru."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:543
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgcreate VG \"/dev/sda1 /dev/sdb1\"\n"
" command \"/bin/echo 'foo      bar'\"\n"
" command \"/bin/echo \\'foo\\'\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgcreate VG \"/dev/sda1 /dev/sdb1\"\n"
" command \"/bin/echo 'foo      bar'\"\n"
" command \"/bin/echo \\'foo\\'\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:547
msgid "ESCAPE SEQUENCES IN DOUBLE QUOTED ARGUMENTS"
msgstr "ATSOĻA SECĪBAS DUBULTPĒDIŅĀS LIKTOS ARGUMENTOS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:549
msgid ""
"In double-quoted arguments (only) use backslash to insert special "
"characters:"
msgstr ""
"Dubultpēdiņu argumentos (tikai) izmantojiet atpakaļvērsto slīpsvītru īpašo "
"rakstzīmju ievietošanai:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:554
msgid "C<\\a>"
msgstr "C<\\a>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:556
msgid "Alert (bell) character."
msgstr "Brīdinājuma (zvana) rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:558
msgid "C<\\b>"
msgstr "C<\\b>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:560
msgid "Backspace character."
msgstr "Atpakaļatkāpes rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:562
msgid "C<\\f>"
msgstr "C<\\f>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:564
msgid "Form feed character."
msgstr "Lapas padeves rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:566
msgid "C<\\n>"
msgstr "C<\\n>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:568
msgid "Newline character."
msgstr "Jaunas rindas rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:570
msgid "C<\\r>"
msgstr "C<\\r>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:572
msgid "Carriage return character."
msgstr "Rakstatgriezes rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:574
msgid "C<\\t>"
msgstr "C<\\t>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:576
msgid "Horizontal tab character."
msgstr "Horizontālās tabulācijas rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:578
msgid "C<\\v>"
msgstr "C<\\v>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:580
msgid "Vertical tab character."
msgstr "Vertikālās tabulācijas rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:582
msgid "C<\\\">"
msgstr "C<\\\">"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:584
msgid "A literal double quote character."
msgstr "Burtiska dubultpēdiņas rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:586
msgid "C<\\ooo>"
msgstr "C<\\ooo>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:588
msgid ""
"A character with octal value I<ooo>.  There must be precisely 3 octal digits "
"(unlike C)."
msgstr ""
"Rakstzīme ar astoņnieku vērtību I<ooo>.  Jābūt tieši 3 astoņnieku cipariem "
"(atšķirībā no C)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:591
msgid "C<\\xhh>"
msgstr "C<\\xhh>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:593
msgid "A character with hex value I<hh>.  There must be precisely 2 hex digits."
msgstr ""
"Rakstzīme ar heksadecimālo vērtību I<hh>.  Jābūt tieši 2 heksadecimāliem "
"cipariem."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:596
msgid ""
"In the current implementation C<\\000> and C<\\x00> cannot be used in "
"strings."
msgstr "Pašreizējā realizācijā C<\\000> un C<\\x00> virknēs izmantot nevar."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:599
msgid "C<\\\\>"
msgstr "C<\\\\>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:601 fish/guestfish.pod:1275
msgid "A literal backslash character."
msgstr "Burtiska atpakaļvērstās slīpsvītras rakstzīme."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:605 java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:74
msgid "OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS"
msgstr "NEOBLIGĀTIE ARGUMENTI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:607
msgid ""
"Some commands take optional arguments.  These arguments appear in this "
"documentation as C<[argname:..]>.  You can use them as in these examples:"
msgstr ""
"Dažas komandas pieņem neobligātus argumentus.  Šajā dokumentācijā šie "
"argumenti parādās kā C<[argname:..]>.  Tos var izmantot kā šajos piemēros:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:611
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" add filename\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" add filename\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:613
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" add filename readonly:true\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" add filename readonly:true\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:615
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" add filename format:qcow2 readonly:false\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" add filename format:qcow2 readonly:false\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:617
msgid ""
"Each optional argument can appear at most once.  All optional arguments must "
"appear after the required ones."
msgstr ""
"Katrs neobligātais arguments var parādīties ne vairāk kā vienreiz.  Visiem "
"neobligātajiem argumentiem jāatrodas pēc obligātajiem."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:620
msgid "NUMBERS"
msgstr "SKAITĻI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:622
msgid "This section applies to all commands which can take integers as parameters."
msgstr ""
"Šī sadaļa attiecas uz visām komandām, kas kā parametrus var pieņemt veselus "
"skaitļus."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:625
msgid "SIZE SUFFIX"
msgstr "IZMĒRA PIEDĒKLIS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:627
msgid ""
"When the command takes a parameter measured in bytes, you can use one of the "
"following suffixes to specify kilobytes, megabytes and larger sizes:"
msgstr ""
"Ja komanda pieņem parametru, kas mērīts baitos, kilobaitu, megabaitu un "
"lielāku izmēru norādīšanai var izmantot vienu no šiem sufiksiem:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:633
msgid "B<k> or B<K> or B<KiB>"
msgstr "B<k> or B<K> or B<KiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:635
msgid "The size in kilobytes (multiplied by 1024)."
msgstr "Izmērs kilobaitos (reizināts ar 1024)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:637
msgid "B<KB>"
msgstr "B<KB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:639
msgid "The size in SI 1000 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 1000 baitu vienībās."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:641
msgid "B<M> or B<MiB>"
msgstr "B<M> vai B<MiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:643
msgid "The size in megabytes (multiplied by 1048576)."
msgstr "Izmērs megabaitos (reizināts ar 1048576)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:645
msgid "B<MB>"
msgstr "B<MB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:647
msgid "The size in SI 1000000 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 1000000 baitu vienībās."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:649
msgid "B<G> or B<GiB>"
msgstr "B<G> vai B<GiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:651
msgid "The size in gigabytes (multiplied by 2**30)."
msgstr "Izmērs gigabaitos (reizināts ar 2**30)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:653
msgid "B<GB>"
msgstr "B<GB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:655
msgid "The size in SI 10**9 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 10**9 baitu vienībās."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:657
msgid "B<T> or B<TiB>"
msgstr "B<T> vai B<TiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:659
msgid "The size in terabytes (multiplied by 2**40)."
msgstr "Izmērs terabaitos (reizināts ar 2**40)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:661
msgid "B<TB>"
msgstr "B<TB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:663
msgid "The size in SI 10**12 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 10**12 baitu vienībās."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:665
msgid "B<P> or B<PiB>"
msgstr "B<P> vai B<PiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:667
msgid "The size in petabytes (multiplied by 2**50)."
msgstr "Izmērs petabaitos (reizināts ar 2**50)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:669
msgid "B<PB>"
msgstr "B<PB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:671
msgid "The size in SI 10**15 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 10**15 baitu vienībās."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:673
msgid "B<E> or B<EiB>"
msgstr "B<E> vai B<EiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:675
msgid "The size in exabytes (multiplied by 2**60)."
msgstr "Izmērs eksabaitos (reizināts ar 2**60)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:677
msgid "B<EB>"
msgstr "B<EB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:679
msgid "The size in SI 10**18 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 10**18 baitu vienībās."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:681
msgid "B<Z> or B<ZiB>"
msgstr "B<Z> vai B<ZiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:683
msgid "The size in zettabytes (multiplied by 2**70)."
msgstr "Izmērs zetabaitos (reizināts ar 2**70)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:685
msgid "B<ZB>"
msgstr "B<ZB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:687
msgid "The size in SI 10**21 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 10**21 baitu vienībās."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:689
msgid "B<Y> or B<YiB>"
msgstr "B<Y> vai B<YiB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:691
msgid "The size in yottabytes (multiplied by 2**80)."
msgstr "Izmērs jotabaitos (reizināts ar 2**80)."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:693
msgid "B<YB>"
msgstr "B<YB>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:695
msgid "The size in SI 10**24 byte units."
msgstr "Izmērs SI 10**24 baitu vienībās."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:701
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" truncate-size /file 1G\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" truncate-size /file 1G\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:703
msgid "would truncate the file to 1 gigabyte."
msgstr "saīsinātu failu līdz 1 gigabaitam."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:705
msgid ""
"Be careful because a few commands take sizes in kilobytes or megabytes "
"(eg. the parameter to L</memsize> is specified in megabytes already).  "
"Adding a suffix will probably not do what you expect."
msgstr ""
"Esiet uzmanīgi, jo dažas komandas pieņem izmērus kilobaitos vai megabaitos "
"(piem., L</memsize> parametrs jau ir norādīts megabaitos).  Sufiksa "
"pievienošana, visticamāk, nedarīs to, ko gaidāt."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:709
msgid "OCTAL AND HEXADECIMAL NUMBERS"
msgstr "ASTOŅNIEKU UN SEŠPADSMITNIEKU SKAITĻI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:711
msgid ""
"For specifying the radix (base) use the C convention: C<0> to prefix an "
"octal number or C<0x> to prefix a hexadecimal number.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Bāzes norādīšanai izmantojiet C konvenciju: C<0> kā priedēkli astoņnieku "
"skaitlim vai C<0x> kā priedēkli heksadecimālam skaitlim.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:714
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" 1234      decimal number 1234\n"
" 02322     octal number, equivalent to decimal 1234\n"
" 0x4d2     hexadecimal number, equivalent to decimal 1234\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" 1234      decimal number 1234\n"
" 02322     octal number, equivalent to decimal 1234\n"
" 0x4d2     hexadecimal number, equivalent to decimal 1234\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:718
msgid ""
"When using the C<chmod> command, you almost always want to specify an octal "
"number for the mode, and you must prefix it with C<0> (unlike the Unix "
"L<chmod(1)> program):"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot komandu C<chmod>, režīmam gandrīz vienmēr jānorāda astoņnieku "
"skaitlis, un tam jāpievieno priedēklis C<0> (atšķirībā no Unix programmas "
"L<chmod(1)>):"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:722
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" chmod 0777 /public  # OK\n"
" chmod 777 /public   # WRONG! This is mode 777 decimal = 01411 octal.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" chmod 0777 /public  # OK\n"
" chmod 777 /public   # WRONG! This is mode 777 decimal = 01411 octal.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:725
msgid ""
"Commands that return numbers usually print them in decimal, but some "
"commands print numbers in other radices (eg. C<umask> prints the mode in "
"octal, preceded by C<0>)."
msgstr ""
"Komandas, kas atgriež skaitļus, parasti tos izdrukā decimāli, bet dažas "
"komandas izdrukā skaitļus citās bāzēs (piem., C<umask> izdrukā režīmu "
"astoņniekos ar priekšā esošu C<0>)."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:729
msgid "WILDCARDS AND GLOBBING"
msgstr "AIZSTĀJĒJZĪMES UN GLOBĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:731
msgid ""
"Neither guestfish nor the underlying guestfs API performs wildcard expansion "
"(globbing) by default.  So for example the following will not do what you "
"expect:"
msgstr ""
"Ne guestfish, ne pamatā esošā guestfs API pēc noklusējuma neveic "
"aizstājējzīmju izvēršanu (glob).  Tāpēc, piemēram, šis nedarīs to, ko gaidāt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:735
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rm-rf /home/*\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rm-rf /home/*\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:737
msgid ""
"Assuming you don’t have a directory called literally F</home/*> then the "
"above command will return an error."
msgstr ""
"Pieņemot, ka jums nav direktorijas ar burtisku nosaukumu F</home/*>, "
"iepriekšējā komanda atgriezīs kļūdu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:740
msgid "To perform wildcard expansion, use the C<glob> command."
msgstr "Lai veiktu aizstājējzīmju izvēršanu, izmantojiet komandu C<glob>."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:742
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" glob rm-rf /home/*\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" glob rm-rf /home/*\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:744
msgid ""
"runs C<rm-rf> on each path that matches (ie. potentially running the command "
"many times), equivalent to:"
msgstr ""
"izpilda C<rm-rf> katram atbilstošajam ceļam (t. i., iespējams, komandu "
"izpildot daudzas reizes), līdzvērtīgi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:747
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" rm-rf /home/jim\n"
" rm-rf /home/joe\n"
" rm-rf /home/mary\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" rm-rf /home/jim\n"
" rm-rf /home/joe\n"
" rm-rf /home/mary\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:751
msgid "C<glob> only works on simple guest paths and not on device names."
msgstr ""
"C<glob> darbojas tikai ar vienkāršiem viesa ceļiem, nevis ar ierīču "
"nosaukumiem."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:753
msgid ""
"If you have several parameters, each containing a wildcard, then glob will "
"perform a Cartesian product."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir vairāki parametri, katrs ar aizstājējzīmi, glob veiks Dekarta "
"reizinājumu."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:756
msgid "COMMENTS"
msgstr "KOMENTĀRI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:758
msgid ""
"Any line which starts with a I<#> character is treated as a comment and "
"ignored.  The I<#> can optionally be preceded by whitespace, but B<not> by a "
"command.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Jebkura rinda, kas sākas ar rakstzīmi I<#>, tiek uzskatīta par komentāru un "
"ignorēta.  Pirms I<#> pēc izvēles var būt atstarpes, bet B<ne> komanda.  "
"Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:762
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # this is a comment\n"
"         # this is a comment\n"
" foo # NOT a comment\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # this is a comment\n"
"         # this is a comment\n"
" foo # NOT a comment\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:766
msgid "Blank lines are also ignored."
msgstr "Tukšas rindas arī tiek ignorētas."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:768
msgid "RUNNING COMMANDS LOCALLY"
msgstr "KOMANDU IZPILDE LOKĀLI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:770
msgid ""
"Any line which starts with a I<!> character is treated as a command sent to "
"the local shell (F</bin/sh> or whatever L<system(3)> uses).  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Jebkura rinda, kas sākas ar rakstzīmi I<!>, tiek uzskatīta par komandu, kas "
"tiek nosūtīta lokālajai čaulai (F</bin/sh> vai tam, ko izmanto L<system(3)>)"
".  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:774
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" !mkdir local\n"
" tgz-out /remote local/remote-data.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" !mkdir local\n"
" tgz-out /remote local/remote-data.tar.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:777
msgid ""
"will create a directory C<local> on the host, and then export the contents "
"of F</remote> on the mounted filesystem to F<local/remote-data.tar.gz>.  "
"(See C<tgz-out>)."
msgstr ""
"izveidos resursdatorā direktoriju C<local> un pēc tam eksportēs F</remote> "
"saturu montētajā failu sistēmā uz F<local/remote-data.tar.gz>.  (Skatiet "
"C<tgz-out>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:781
msgid ""
"To change the local directory, use the C<lcd> command.  C<!cd> will have no "
"effect, due to the way that subprocesses work in Unix."
msgstr ""
"Lai mainītu lokālo direktoriju, izmantojiet komandu C<lcd>.  C<!cd> nebūs "
"ietekmes tā dēļ, kā Unix darbojas apakšprocesi."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:784
msgid "LOCAL COMMANDS WITH INLINE EXECUTION"
msgstr "LOKĀLAS KOMANDAS AR IEKĻAUTU IZPILDI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:786
msgid ""
"If a line starts with I<E<lt>!> then the shell command is executed (as for "
"I<!>), but subsequently any output (stdout) of the shell command is parsed "
"and executed as guestfish commands."
msgstr ""
"Ja rinda sākas ar I<E<lt>!>, čaulas komanda tiek izpildīta (kā I<!>), bet "
"pēc tam jebkura čaulas komandas izvade (stdout) tiek parsēta un izpildīta kā "
"guestfish komandas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:790
msgid ""
"Thus you can use shell script to construct arbitrary guestfish commands "
"which are then parsed by guestfish."
msgstr ""
"Tādējādi varat izmantot čaulas skriptu, lai izveidotu patvaļīgas guestfish "
"komandas, ko pēc tam parsē guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:793
msgid ""
"For example it is tedious to create a sequence of files (eg. F</foo.1> "
"through F</foo.100>) using guestfish commands alone.  However this is simple "
"if we use a shell script to create the guestfish commands for us:"
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, ir nogurdinoši izveidot failu secību (piem., no F</foo.1> līdz F</"
"foo.100>), izmantojot tikai guestfish komandas.  Tomēr tas ir vienkārši, ja "
"guestfish komandu izveidei izmantojam čaulas skriptu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:798
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <! for n in `seq 1 100`; do echo write /foo.$n $n; done\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <! for n in `seq 1 100`; do echo write /foo.$n $n; done\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:800
msgid "or with names like F</foo.001>:"
msgstr "vai ar tādiem nosaukumiem kā F</foo.001>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:802
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <! for n in `seq 1 100`; do printf \"write /foo.%03d %d\\n\" $n $n; done\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <! for n in `seq 1 100`; do printf \"write /foo.%03d %d\\n\" $n $n; done\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:804
msgid ""
"When using guestfish interactively it can be helpful to just run the shell "
"script first (ie. remove the initial C<E<lt>> character so it is just an "
"ordinary I<!> local command), see what guestfish commands it would run, and "
"when you are happy with those prepend the C<E<lt>> character to run the "
"guestfish commands for real."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot guestfish interaktīvi, var būt noderīgi vispirms vienkārši "
"izpildīt čaulas skriptu (t. i., noņemt sākuma rakstzīmi C<E<lt>>, lai tā "
"būtu tikai parasta I<!> lokālā komanda), apskatīt, kuras guestfish komandas "
"tā izpildītu, un, kad tās der, pievienot sākumā rakstzīmi C<E<lt>>, lai "
"guestfish komandas izpildītu pa īstam."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:810
msgid "PIPES"
msgstr "KANĀLI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:812
msgid ""
"Use C<command E<lt>spaceE<gt> | command> to pipe the output of the first "
"command (a guestfish command) to the second command (any host command).  For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet C<command E<lt>spaceE<gt> | command>, lai pirmās komandas "
"(guestfish komandas) izvadi novirzītu ar kanālu otrajai komandai (jebkurai "
"resursdatora komandai).  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:816
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" cat /etc/passwd | awk -F: '$3 == 0 { print }'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" cat /etc/passwd | awk -F: '$3 == 0 { print }'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:818
msgid ""
"(where C<cat> is the guestfish cat command, but C<awk> is the host awk "
"program).  The above command would list all accounts in the guest filesystem "
"which have UID 0, ie. root accounts including backdoors.  Other examples:"
msgstr ""
"(kur C<cat> ir guestfish komanda cat, bet C<awk> ir resursdatora programma "
"awk).  Iepriekšējā komanda uzskaitītu visus kontus viesa failu sistēmā ar "
"UID 0, t. i., root kontus, ieskaitot „sētas durvis”.  Citi piemēri:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:823
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" hexdump /bin/ls | head\n"
" list-devices | tail -1\n"
" tgz-out / - | tar ztf -\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" hexdump /bin/ls | head\n"
" list-devices | tail -1\n"
" tgz-out / - | tar ztf -\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:827
msgid ""
"The space before the pipe symbol is required, any space after the pipe "
"symbol is optional.  Everything after the pipe symbol is just passed "
"straight to the host shell, so it can contain redirections, globs and "
"anything else that makes sense on the host side."
msgstr ""
"Atstarpe pirms kanāla simbola ir obligāta, jebkura atstarpe pēc kanāla "
"simbola nav obligāta.  Viss aiz kanāla simbola tiek vienkārši nodots tieši "
"resursdatora čaulai, tāpēc tas var saturēt novirzīšanas, glob šablonus un "
"jebko citu, kam ir jēga resursdatora pusē."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:832
msgid ""
"To use a literal argument which begins with a pipe symbol, you have to quote "
"it, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izmantotu burtisku argumentu, kas sākas ar kanāla simbolu, tas jāliek "
"pēdiņās, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:835
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" echo \"|\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" echo \"|\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:837
msgid "HOME DIRECTORIES"
msgstr "MĀJAS DIREKTORIJAS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:839
msgid ""
"If a parameter starts with the character C<~> then the tilde may be expanded "
"as a home directory path (either C<~> for the current user's home directory, "
"or C<~user> for another user)."
msgstr ""
"Ja parametrs sākas ar rakstzīmi C<~>, tilde var tikt izvērsta kā mājas "
"direktorijas ceļš (vai nu C<~> pašreizējā lietotāja mājas direktorijai, vai "
"C<~user> citam lietotājam)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:843
msgid ""
"Note that home directory expansion happens for users known I<on the host>, "
"not in the guest filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka mājas direktorijas izvēršana notiek lietotājiem, kas zināmi "
"I<resursdatorā>, nevis viesa failu sistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:846
msgid ""
"To use a literal argument which begins with a tilde, you have to quote it, "
"eg:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izmantotu burtisku argumentu, kas sākas ar tildi, tas jāliek pēdiņās, "
"piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:849
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" echo \"~\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" echo \"~\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:851 lib/guestfs.pod:579
msgid "ENCRYPTED DISKS"
msgstr "ŠIFRĒTI DISKI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:853
msgid ""
"Libguestfs has some support for Linux guests encrypted according to the "
"Linux Unified Key Setup (LUKS) standard, which includes nearly all whole "
"disk encryption systems used by modern Linux guests, and Windows BitLocker."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs ir zināms atbalsts Linux viesiem, kas šifrēti saskaņā ar Linux "
"Unified Key Setup (LUKS) standartu, kas ietver gandrīz visas moderno Linux "
"viesu izmantotās pilna diska šifrēšanas sistēmas, un Windows BitLocker."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:858
msgid "Identify encrypted block devices and partitions using L</vfs-type>:"
msgstr ""
"Identificējiet šifrētās bloku ierīces un nodalījumus, izmantojot L</vfs-type>"
":"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:860
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> vfs-type /dev/sda2\n"
" crypto_LUKS\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> vfs-type /dev/sda2\n"
" crypto_LUKS\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:865
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> vfs-type /dev/sda2\n"
" BitLocker\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> vfs-type /dev/sda2\n"
" BitLocker\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:868
msgid ""
"Then open those devices using L</cryptsetup-open>.  This creates a "
"device-mapper device called F</dev/mapper/name>."
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam atveriet šīs ierīces ar L</cryptsetup-open>.  Tas izveido device-"
"mapper ierīci F</dev/mapper/name>."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:871
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> cryptsetup-open /dev/sda2 name\n"
" Enter key or passphrase (\"key\"): <enter the passphrase>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> cryptsetup-open /dev/sda2 name\n"
" Enter key or passphrase (\"key\"): <enter the passphrase>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:874
msgid ""
"For Linux guests you have to tell LVM to scan for volume groups on the newly "
"created mapper device:"
msgstr ""
"Linux viesiem LVM jāliek skenēt sējumu grupas jaunizveidotajā kartētāja "
"ierīcē:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:877
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vgscan\n"
" vg-activate-all true\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vgscan\n"
" vg-activate-all true\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:880
msgid "The filesystems or logical volumes can now be mounted in the usual way."
msgstr "Failu sistēmas vai loģiskos sējumus tagad var montēt parastajā veidā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:882
msgid ""
"Before closing an encrypted device you must unmount any logical volumes on "
"it and deactivate the volume groups by calling C<vg-activate false VG> on "
"each one.  Then you can close the mapper device:"
msgstr ""
"Pirms šifrētas ierīces aizvēršanas jānomontē visi tajā esošie loģiskie "
"sējumi un jādeaktivizē sējumu grupas, katrai izsaucot C<vg-activate false VG>"
".  Pēc tam kartētāja ierīci var aizvērt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:887
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" vg-activate false /dev/VG\n"
" cryptsetup-close /dev/mapper/name\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" vg-activate false /dev/VG\n"
" cryptsetup-close /dev/mapper/name\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:890
msgid "WINDOWS PATHS"
msgstr "WINDOWS CEĻI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:892
msgid ""
"If a path is prefixed with C<win:> then you can use Windows-style drive "
"letters and paths (with some limitations).  The following commands are "
"equivalent:"
msgstr ""
"Ja ceļam ir priedēklis C<win:>, varat izmantot Windows stila disku burtus un "
"ceļus (ar dažiem ierobežojumiem).  Šīs komandas ir līdzvērtīgas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:896
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" file /WINDOWS/system32/config/system.LOG\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" file /WINDOWS/system32/config/system.LOG\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:898
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" file win:\\windows\\system32\\config\\system.log\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" file win:\\windows\\system32\\config\\system.log\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:900
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" file WIN:C:\\Windows\\SYSTEM32\\CONFIG\\SYSTEM.LOG\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" file WIN:C:\\Windows\\SYSTEM32\\CONFIG\\SYSTEM.LOG\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:902
msgid ""
"The parameter is rewritten \"behind the scenes\" by looking up the position "
"where the drive is mounted, prepending that to the path, changing all "
"backslash characters to forward slash, then resolving the result using "
"L</case-sensitive-path>.  For example if the E: drive was mounted on F</e> "
"then the parameter might be rewritten like this:"
msgstr ""
"Parametrs tiek pārrakstīts „aizkulisēs”, meklējot pozīciju, kur disks ir "
"montēts, pievienojot to ceļa sākumā, mainot visas atpakaļvērstās slīpsvītras "
"uz parastajām un pēc tam atrisinot rezultātu ar L</case-sensitive-path>.  "
"Piemēram, ja disks E: tika montēts F</e>, parametrs varētu tikt pārrakstīts "
"šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:908
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" win:e:\\foo\\bar => /e/FOO/bar\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" win:e:\\foo\\bar => /e/FOO/bar\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:910
msgid "This only works in argument positions that expect a path."
msgstr "Tas darbojas tikai argumentu pozīcijās, kur tiek gaidīts ceļš."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:912
msgid "UPLOADING AND DOWNLOADING FILES"
msgstr "FAILU AUGŠUPIELĀDE UN LEJUPIELĀDE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:914
msgid ""
"For commands such as C<upload>, C<download>, C<tar-in>, C<tar-out> and "
"others which upload from or download to a local file, you can use the "
"special filename C<-> to mean \"from stdin\" or \"to stdout\".  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Tādām komandām kā C<upload>, C<download>, C<tar-in>, C<tar-out> un citām, "
"kas augšupielādē no lokāla faila vai lejupielādē uz to, varat izmantot īpašo "
"faila nosaukumu C<->, kas nozīmē „no stdin” vai „uz stdout”.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:918
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" upload - /foo\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" upload - /foo\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:920
msgid "reads stdin and creates from that a file F</foo> in the disk image, and:"
msgstr "nolasa stdin un no tā izveido failu F</foo> diska attēlā, un:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:923
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" tar-out /etc - | tar tf -\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" tar-out /etc - | tar tf -\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:925
msgid ""
"writes the tarball to stdout and then pipes that into the external \"tar\" "
"command (see L</PIPES>)."
msgstr ""
"ieraksta tar arhīvu uz stdout un tad ar kanālu nodod to ārējai komandai „tar"
"” (skatiet L</KANĀLI>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:928
msgid ""
"When using C<-> to read from stdin, the input is read up to the end of "
"stdin.  You can also use a special \"heredoc\"-like syntax to read up to "
"some arbitrary end marker:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot C<->, lai lasītu no stdin, ievade tiek lasīta līdz stdin beigām.  "
"Varat izmantot arī īpašu „heredoc” līdzīgu sintaksi, lai lasītu līdz kādam "
"patvaļīgam beigu marķierim:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:932
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" upload -<<END /foo\n"
" input line 1\n"
" input line 2\n"
" input line 3\n"
" END\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" upload -<<END /foo\n"
" input line 1\n"
" input line 2\n"
" input line 3\n"
" END\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:938
msgid ""
"Any string of characters can be used instead of C<END>.  The end marker must "
"appear on a line of its own, without any preceding or following characters "
"(not even spaces)."
msgstr ""
"C<END> vietā var izmantot jebkuru rakstzīmju virkni.  Beigu marķierim "
"jāatrodas atsevišķā rindā bez jebkādām rakstzīmēm pirms vai pēc tā (pat ne "
"atstarpēm)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:942
msgid ""
"Note that the C<-E<lt>E<lt>> syntax only applies to parameters used to "
"upload local files (so-called \"FileIn\" parameters in the generator)."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka sintakse C<-E<lt>E<lt>> attiecas tikai uz parametriem, ko "
"izmanto lokālu failu augšupielādei (ģeneratorā tā sauktajiem „FileIn” "
"parametriem)."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:945
msgid "EXIT ON ERROR BEHAVIOUR"
msgstr "IZIEŠANA KĻŪDAS GADĪJUMĀ"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:947
msgid ""
"By default, guestfish will ignore any errors when in interactive mode "
"(ie. taking commands from a human over a tty), and will exit on the first "
"error in non-interactive mode (scripts, commands given on the command line)."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma guestfish interaktīvajā režīmā (t. i., saņemot komandas no "
"cilvēka caur tty) ignorēs jebkuras kļūdas un neinteraktīvajā režīmā "
"(skripti, komandrindā norādītas komandas) izies pie pirmās kļūdas."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:952
msgid ""
"If you prefix a command with a I<-> character, then that command will not "
"cause guestfish to exit, even if that (one) command returns an error."
msgstr ""
"Ja komandai pievienojat priedēkli — rakstzīmi I<->, šī komanda neliks "
"guestfish iziet, pat ja šī (viena) komanda atgriež kļūdu."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:956
msgid "REMOTE CONTROL GUESTFISH OVER A SOCKET"
msgstr "GUESTFISH TĀLVADĪBA CAUR LIGZDU"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:958
msgid ""
"Guestfish can be remote-controlled over a socket.  This is useful "
"particularly in shell scripts where you want to make several different "
"changes to a filesystem, but you don't want the overhead of starting up a "
"guestfish process each time."
msgstr ""
"Guestfish var tālvadīt caur ligzdu.  Tas īpaši noder čaulas skriptos, kur "
"vēlaties veikt vairākas dažādas izmaiņas failu sistēmā, bet nevēlaties katru "
"reizi tērēt resursus guestfish procesa palaišanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:963
msgid "Start a guestfish server process using:"
msgstr "Palaidiet guestfish servera procesu ar:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:965
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:967
msgid "and then send it commands by doing:"
msgstr "un pēc tam sūtiet tam komandas šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:969
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --remote cmd [...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --remote cmd [...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:971
msgid "To cause the server to exit, send it the exit command:"
msgstr "Lai liktu serverim iziet, nosūtiet tam komandu exit:"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:975
msgid ""
"Note that the server will normally exit if there is an error in a command.  "
"You can change this in the usual way.  See section L</EXIT ON ERROR "
"BEHAVIOUR>."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka serveris parasti izies, ja komandā ir kļūda.  To var mainīt "
"parastajā veidā.  Skatiet sadaļu L</IZIEŠANA KĻŪDAS GADĪJUMĀ>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:979
msgid "CONTROLLING MULTIPLE GUESTFISH PROCESSES"
msgstr "VAIRĀKU GUESTFISH PROCESU VADĪBA"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:981
msgid ""
"The C<eval> statement sets the environment variable C<$GUESTFISH_PID>, which "
"is how the I<--remote> option knows where to send the commands.  You can "
"have several guestfish listener processes running using:"
msgstr ""
"Priekšraksts C<eval> iestata vides mainīgo C<$GUESTFISH_PID>, pēc kura "
"opcija I<--remote> zina, kur sūtīt komandas.  Varat darbināt vairākus "
"guestfish klausītāju procesus, izmantojot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:985
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
" pid1=$GUESTFISH_PID\n"
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
" pid2=$GUESTFISH_PID\n"
" ...\n"
" guestfish --remote=$pid1 cmd\n"
" guestfish --remote=$pid2 cmd\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
" pid1=$GUESTFISH_PID\n"
" eval \"`guestfish --listen`\"\n"
" pid2=$GUESTFISH_PID\n"
" ...\n"
" guestfish --remote=$pid1 cmd\n"
" guestfish --remote=$pid2 cmd\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:993
msgid "REMOTE CONTROL AND CSH"
msgstr "TĀLVADĪBA UN CSH"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:995
msgid ""
"When using csh-like shells (csh, tcsh etc) you have to add the I<--csh> "
"option:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot csh līdzīgas čaulas (csh, tcsh u. c.), jāpievieno opcija I<--csh>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:998
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen --csh`\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" eval \"`guestfish --listen --csh`\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1000
msgid "REMOTE CONTROL DETAILS"
msgstr "TĀLVADĪBAS SĪKĀKA INFORMĀCIJA"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1002
msgid ""
"Remote control happens over a Unix domain socket called "
"F</tmp/.guestfish-$UID/socket-$PID>, where C<$UID> is the effective user ID "
"of the process, and C<$PID> is the process ID of the server."
msgstr ""
"Tālvadība notiek caur Unix domēna ligzdu F</tmp/.guestfish-$UID/socket-$PID>"
", kur C<$UID> ir procesa efektīvais lietotāja ID un C<$PID> ir servera "
"procesa ID."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1006
msgid "Guestfish client and server versions must match exactly."
msgstr "Guestfish klienta un servera versijām jāsakrīt precīzi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1008
msgid ""
"Older versions of guestfish were vulnerable to CVE-2013-4419 (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/CVE-2013-4419>).  This is fixed in the current version."
msgstr ""
"Vecākas guestfish versijas bija ievainojamas pret CVE-2013-4419 (skatiet "
"L<guestfs(3)/CVE-2013-4419>).  Pašreizējā versijā tas ir izlabots."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1011
msgid "USING REMOTE CONTROL ROBUSTLY FROM SHELL SCRIPTS"
msgstr "DROŠA TĀLVADĪBAS IZMANTOŠANA NO ČAULAS SKRIPTIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1013
msgid ""
"From Bash, you can use the following code which creates a guestfish "
"instance, correctly quotes the command line, handles failure to start, and "
"cleans up guestfish when the script exits:"
msgstr ""
"No Bash varat izmantot šo kodu, kas izveido guestfish instanci, pareizi liek "
"komandrindu pēdiņās, apstrādā palaišanas neizdošanos un sakopj guestfish, "
"kad skripts iziet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1021
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish[0]=\"guestfish\"\n"
" guestfish[1]=\"--listen\"\n"
" guestfish[2]=\"--ro\"\n"
" guestfish[3]=\"-a\"\n"
" guestfish[4]=\"disk.img\"\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish[0]=\"guestfish\"\n"
" guestfish[1]=\"--listen\"\n"
" guestfish[2]=\"--ro\"\n"
" guestfish[3]=\"-a\"\n"
" guestfish[4]=\"disk.img\"\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1027
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" GUESTFISH_PID=\n"
" eval $(\"${guestfish[@]}\")\n"
" if [ -z \"$GUESTFISH_PID\" ]; then\n"
"     echo \"error: guestfish didn't start up, see error messages above\"\n"
"     exit 1\n"
" fi\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" GUESTFISH_PID=\n"
" eval $(\"${guestfish[@]}\")\n"
" if [ -z \"$GUESTFISH_PID\" ]; then\n"
"     echo \"error: guestfish didn't start up, see error messages above\"\n"
"     exit 1\n"
" fi\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1034
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" cleanup_guestfish ()\n"
" {\n"
"     guestfish --remote -- exit >/dev/null 2>&1 ||:\n"
" }\n"
" trap cleanup_guestfish EXIT ERR\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" cleanup_guestfish ()\n"
" {\n"
"     guestfish --remote -- exit >/dev/null 2>&1 ||:\n"
" }\n"
" trap cleanup_guestfish EXIT ERR\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1040
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --remote -- run\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --remote -- run\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1042
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # ...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # ...\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1044
msgid "REMOTE CONTROL DOES NOT WORK WITH I<-a> ETC. OPTIONS"
msgstr "TĀLVADĪBA NEDARBOJAS AR I<-a> U. C. OPCIJĀM"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1046
msgid ""
"Options such as I<-a>, I<--add>, I<-N>, I<--new> etc don’t interact properly "
"with remote support.  They are processed locally, and not sent through to "
"the remote guestfish.  In particular this won't do what you expect:"
msgstr ""
"Tādas opcijas kā I<-a>, I<--add>, I<-N>, I<--new> u. c. pareizi nesadarbojas "
"ar attālo atbalstu.  Tās tiek apstrādātas lokāli un netiek nosūtītas "
"attālajam guestfish.  It īpaši šis nedarīs to, ko gaidāt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1051
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --remote --add disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --remote --add disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1053
msgid "Don’t use these options.  Use the equivalent commands instead, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Neizmantojiet šīs opcijas.  Tā vietā izmantojiet līdzvērtīgas komandas, "
"piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1055
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --remote add-drive disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --remote add-drive disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1059
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --remote\n"
" ><fs> add disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --remote\n"
" ><fs> add disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1062
msgid "REMOTE CONTROL RUN COMMAND HANGING"
msgstr "TĀLVADĪBAS RUN KOMANDA UZKĀRAS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1064
msgid ""
"Using the C<run> (or C<launch>) command remotely in a command substitution "
"context hangs, ie. don't do (note the backquotes):"
msgstr ""
"Komandas C<run> (vai C<launch>) izmantošana attāli komandu aizstāšanas "
"kontekstā uzkaras, t. i., nedariet šādi (ņemiet vērā atpakaļpēdiņas):"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1067
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" a=`guestfish --remote run`\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" a=`guestfish --remote run`\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1069
msgid ""
"Since the C<run> command produces no output on stdout, this is not useful "
"anyway.  For further information see "
"L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=592910>."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā komanda C<run> neizvada neko uz stdout, tas tik un tā nav noderīgi.  "
"Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/"
"show_bug.cgi?id=592910>."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1073
msgid "PREPARED DISK IMAGES"
msgstr "SAGATAVOTI DISKU ATTĒLI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1075
msgid ""
"Use the I<-N [filename=]type> or I<--new [filename=]type> parameter to "
"select one of a set of preformatted disk images that guestfish can make for "
"you to save typing.  This is particularly useful for testing purposes.  This "
"option is used instead of the I<-a> option, and like I<-a> can appear "
"multiple times (and can be mixed with I<-a>)."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet parametru I<-N [filename=]type> vai I<--new [filename=]type>, "
"lai izvēlētos vienu no iepriekš formatētu disku attēlu kopas, ko guestfish "
"var izveidot jūsu vietā, lai ietaupītu rakstīšanu.  Tas īpaši noder "
"testēšanas nolūkiem.  Šī opcija tiek izmantota opcijas I<-a> vietā un, tāpat "
"kā I<-a>, var parādīties vairākas reizes (un to var jaukt ar I<-a>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1081
msgid ""
"The new disk is called F<test1.img> for the first I<-N>, F<test2.img> for "
"the second and so on.  Existing files in the current directory are "
"I<overwritten>.  You can use a different filename by specifying C<filename=> "
"before the type (see examples below)."
msgstr ""
"Jaunais disks pirmajai I<-N> tiek nosaukts F<test1.img>, otrajai "
"F<test2.img> un tā tālāk.  Esošie faili pašreizējā direktorijā tiek "
"I<pārrakstīti>.  Citu faila nosaukumu var izmantot, pirms tipa norādot "
"C<filename=> (skatiet piemērus tālāk)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1086
msgid ""
"The type briefly describes how the disk should be sized, partitioned, how "
"filesystem(s) should be created, and how content should be added.  "
"Optionally the type can be followed by extra parameters, separated by C<:> "
"(colon) characters.  For example, I<-N fs> creates a default 1G, "
"sparsely-allocated disk, containing a single partition, with the partition "
"formatted as ext2.  I<-N fs:ext4:2G> is the same, but for an ext4 filesystem "
"on a 2GB disk instead."
msgstr ""
"Tips īsi apraksta, kā diskam jānosaka izmērs, kā tas jānodala, kā jāizveido "
"failu sistēma(-s) un kā jāpievieno saturs.  Pēc izvēles tipam var sekot "
"papildu parametri, atdalīti ar rakstzīmēm C<:> (kols).  Piemēram, I<-N fs> "
"izveido noklusējuma 1G retināti piešķirtu disku ar vienu nodalījumu, kas "
"formatēts kā ext2.  I<-N fs:ext4:2G> ir tas pats, bet ext4 failu sistēmai "
"2GB diskā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1094
msgid ""
"Note that the prepared filesystem is not mounted.  You would usually have to "
"use the C<mount /dev/sda1 /> command or add the I<-m /dev/sda1> option."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka sagatavotā failu sistēma netiek montēta.  Parasti būtu "
"jāizmanto komanda C<mount /dev/sda1 /> vai jāpievieno opcija I<-m /dev/sda1>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1098
msgid ""
"If any I<-N> or I<--new> options are given, the libguestfs appliance is "
"automatically launched."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādītas jebkuras opcijas I<-N> vai I<--new>, libguestfs palīgsistēma "
"tiek palaista automātiski."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1103
msgid ""
"Create a 1G disk with an ext4-formatted partition, called F<test1.img> in "
"the current directory:"
msgstr ""
"Izveidot 1G disku ar ext4 formatētu nodalījumu, nosauktu F<test1.img> "
"pašreizējā direktorijā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -N fs:ext4\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -N fs:ext4\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1108
msgid "Create a 32MB disk with a VFAT-formatted partition, and mount it:"
msgstr "Izveidot 32MB disku ar VFAT formatētu nodalījumu un montēt to:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1110
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -N fs:vfat:32M -m /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -N fs:vfat:32M -m /dev/sda1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1112
msgid "Create a blank 200MB disk:"
msgstr "Izveidot tukšu 200MB disku:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -N disk:200M\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -N disk:200M\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1116
msgid "Create a blank 200MB disk called F<blankdisk.img> (instead of F<test1.img>):"
msgstr "Izveidot tukšu 200MB disku F<blankdisk.img> (nevis F<test1.img>):"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1119
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -N blankdisk.img=disk:200M\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -N blankdisk.img=disk:200M\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1121
msgid "__INCLUDE:guestfish-prepopts.pod__"
msgstr "__INCLUDE:guestfish-prepopts.pod__"

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1123
msgid "ADDING REMOTE STORAGE"
msgstr "ATTĀLĀS KRĀTUVES PIEVIENOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1125
msgid ""
"I<For API-level documentation on this topic, see "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts> and L<guestfs(3)/REMOTE STORAGE>>."
msgstr ""
"I<API līmeņa dokumentāciju par šo tēmu skatiet L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_add_drive_opts> un L<guestfs(3)/ATTĀLĀ KRĀTUVE>>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1129
msgid ""
"On the command line, you can use the I<-a> option to add network block "
"devices using a URI-style format, for example:"
msgstr ""
"Komandrindā varat izmantot opciju I<-a>, lai pievienotu tīkla bloku ierīces, "
"izmantojot URI stila formātu, piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1132
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -a ssh://root@example.com/disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -a ssh://root@example.com/disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1134
msgid ""
"URIs I<cannot> be used with the L</add> command.  The equivalent command "
"using the API directly is:"
msgstr ""
"URI I<nevar> izmantot ar komandu L</add>.  Līdzvērtīga komanda, tieši "
"izmantojot API, ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> add /disk.img protocol:ssh server:tcp:example.com username:root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> add /disk.img protocol:ssh server:tcp:example.com username:root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1139
msgid "The possible I<-a URI> formats are described below."
msgstr "Iespējamie I<-a URI> formāti aprakstīti tālāk."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1141
msgid "B<-a disk.img>"
msgstr "B<-a disk.img>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1143
msgid "B<-a file:///path/to/disk.img>"
msgstr "B<-a file:///path/to/disk.img>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1145
msgid "Add the local disk image (or device) called F<disk.img>."
msgstr "Pievienot lokālo diska attēlu (vai ierīci) F<disk.img>."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1147
msgid "B<-a ftp://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"
msgstr "B<-a ftp://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1149
msgid "B<-a ftps://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"
msgstr "B<-a ftps://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1151
msgid "B<-a http://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"
msgstr "B<-a http://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1153
msgid "B<-a https://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"
msgstr "B<-a https://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1155
msgid "Add a disk located on a remote FTP or HTTP server."
msgstr "Pievienot disku, kas atrodas attālā FTP vai HTTP serverī."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1157 fish/guestfish.pod:1165 fish/guestfish.pod:1199
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1209
msgid "The equivalent API command would be:"
msgstr "Līdzvērtīgā API komanda būtu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1159
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> add /disk.img protocol:(ftp|...) server:tcp:example.com\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> add /disk.img protocol:(ftp|...) server:tcp:example.com\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1161
msgid "B<-a iscsi://example.com[:port]/target-iqn-name[/lun]>"
msgstr "B<-a iscsi://example.com[:port]/target-iqn-name[/lun]>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1163
msgid "Add a disk located on an iSCSI server."
msgstr "Pievienot disku, kas atrodas iSCSI serverī."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1167
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> add target-iqn-name/lun protocol:iscsi server:tcp:example.com\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> add target-iqn-name/lun protocol:iscsi server:tcp:example.com\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1169
msgid "B<-a nbd://example.com[:port]>"
msgstr "B<-a nbd://example.com[:port]>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1171
msgid "B<-a nbd://example.com[:port]/exportname>"
msgstr "B<-a nbd://example.com[:port]/exportname>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1173
msgid "B<-a nbd://?socket=/socket>"
msgstr "B<-a nbd://?socket=/socket>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1175
msgid "B<-a nbd:///exportname?socket=/socket>"
msgstr "B<-a nbd:///exportname?socket=/socket>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1177
msgid "Add a disk located on Network Block Device (nbd) storage."
msgstr "Pievienot disku, kas atrodas Network Block Device (nbd) krātuvē."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1179
msgid ""
"The I<exportname> part of the URI specifies an NBD export name, but is "
"usually left empty."
msgstr ""
"URI daļa I<exportname> norāda NBD eksporta nosaukumu, bet parasti tiek "
"atstāta tukša."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1182
msgid ""
"The optional I<?socket> parameter can be used to specify a Unix domain "
"socket that we talk to the NBD server over.  Note that you cannot mix server "
"name (ie. TCP/IP) and socket path."
msgstr ""
"Neobligāto parametru I<?socket> var izmantot, lai norādītu Unix domēna "
"ligzdu, caur kuru sazināmies ar NBD serveri.  Ņemiet vērā, ka nevar jaukt "
"servera nosaukumu (t. i., TCP/IP) un ligzdas ceļu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1186
msgid "The equivalent API command would be (no export name):"
msgstr "Līdzvērtīgā API komanda būtu (bez eksporta nosaukuma):"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1188
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> add \"\" protocol:nbd server:[tcp:example.com|unix:/socket]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> add \"\" protocol:nbd server:[tcp:example.com|unix:/socket]\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1190
msgid "B<-a rbd:///pool/disk>"
msgstr "B<-a rbd:///pool/disk>"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1192
msgid "B<-a rbd://example.com[:port]/pool/disk>"
msgstr "B<-a rbd://example.com[:port]/pool/disk>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1194
msgid "Add a disk image located on a Ceph (RBD/librbd) storage volume."
msgstr "Pievienot diska attēlu, kas atrodas Ceph (RBD/librbd) krātuves sējumā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1196
msgid ""
"Although libguestfs and Ceph supports multiple servers, only a single server "
"can be specified when using this URI syntax."
msgstr ""
"Lai gan libguestfs un Ceph atbalsta vairākus serverus, izmantojot šo URI "
"sintaksi, var norādīt tikai vienu serveri."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1201
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> add pool/disk protocol:rbd server:tcp:example.com:port\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> add pool/disk protocol:rbd server:tcp:example.com:port\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1203
msgid "B<-a ssh://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"
msgstr "B<-a ssh://[user@]example.com[:port]/disk.img>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1205
msgid ""
"Add a disk image located on a remote server, accessed using the Secure Shell "
"(ssh) SFTP protocol.  SFTP is supported out of the box by all major SSH "
"servers."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot diska attēlu, kas atrodas attālā serverī un kam piekļūst, "
"izmantojot Secure Shell (ssh) SFTP protokolu.  SFTP uzreiz atbalsta visi "
"lielākie SSH serveri."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1211
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> add /disk protocol:ssh server:tcp:example.com [username:user]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> add /disk protocol:ssh server:tcp:example.com [username:user]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1213
msgid ""
"Note that the URIs follow the syntax of L<RFC "
"3986|https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986>: in particular, there are "
"restrictions on the allowed characters for the various components of the "
"URI.  Characters such as C<:>, C<@>, and C</> B<must> be percent-encoded:"
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka URI ievēro L<RFC 3986|https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986> "
"sintaksi: it īpaši ir ierobežojumi atļautajām rakstzīmēm dažādos URI "
"komponentos.  Tādas rakstzīmes kā C<:>, C<@> un C</> B<jākodē> ar procentu "
"kodējumu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1219
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ guestfish -a ssh://user:pass%40word@example.com/disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ guestfish -a ssh://user:pass%40word@example.com/disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1221
msgid "In this case, the password is C<pass@word>."
msgstr "Šajā gadījumā parole ir C<pass@word>."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1223
msgid "PROGRESS BARS"
msgstr "PROGRESA JOSLAS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1225
msgid ""
"Some (not all) long-running commands send progress notification messages as "
"they are running.  Guestfish turns these messages into progress bars."
msgstr ""
"Dažas (ne visas) ilgstošas komandas darbības laikā sūta progresa paziņojumu "
"ziņojumus.  Guestfish pārvērš šos ziņojumus progresa joslās."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1229
msgid ""
"When a command that supports progress bars takes longer than two seconds to "
"run, and if progress bars are enabled, then you will see one appearing below "
"the command:"
msgstr ""
"Ja komanda, kas atbalsta progresa joslas, izpildās ilgāk par divām sekundēm "
"un progresa joslas ir iespējotas, zem komandas parādīsies josla:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1233
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> copy-size /large-file /another-file 2048M\n"
" / 10% [#####-----------------------------------------] 00:30\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> copy-size /large-file /another-file 2048M\n"
" / 10% [#####-----------------------------------------] 00:30\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1236
msgid ""
"The spinner on the left hand side moves round once for every progress "
"notification received from the backend.  This is a (reasonably) golden "
"assurance that the command is \"doing something\" even if the progress bar "
"is not moving, because the command is able to send the progress "
"notifications.  When the bar reaches 100% and the command finishes, the "
"spinner disappears."
msgstr ""
"Griežamais indikators kreisajā pusē pagriežas vienreiz par katru no "
"aizmugursistēmas saņemto progresa paziņojumu.  Tā ir (diezgan) droša "
"garantija, ka komanda „kaut ko dara”, pat ja progresa josla nekustas, jo "
"komanda spēj sūtīt progresa paziņojumus.  Kad josla sasniedz 100% un komanda "
"beidzas, griežamais indikators pazūd."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1243
msgid ""
"Progress bars are enabled by default when guestfish is used interactively.  "
"You can enable them even for non-interactive modes using I<--progress-bars>, "
"and you can disable them completely using I<--no-progress-bars>."
msgstr ""
"Progresa joslas pēc noklusējuma ir iespējotas, kad guestfish tiek izmantots "
"interaktīvi.  Tās var iespējot arī neinteraktīvajos režīmos ar I<--progress-"
"bars> un pilnībā atspējot ar I<--no-progress-bars>."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1248
msgid "PROMPT"
msgstr "UZVEDNE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1250
msgid ""
"You can change or add colours to the default prompt (C<E<gt>E<lt>fsE<gt>>) "
"by setting the C<GUESTFISH_PS1> environment variable.  A second string "
"(C<GUESTFISH_OUTPUT>) is printed after the command has been entered and "
"before the output, allowing you to control the colour of the output.  A "
"third string (C<GUESTFISH_INIT>)  is printed before the welcome message, "
"allowing you to control the colour of that message.  A fourth string "
"(C<GUESTFISH_RESTORE>) is printed before guestfish exits."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma uzvednes (C<E<gt>E<lt>fsE<gt>>) krāsas var mainīt vai pievienot, "
"iestatot vides mainīgo C<GUESTFISH_PS1>.  Otra virkne (C<GUESTFISH_OUTPUT>) "
"tiek izdrukāta pēc komandas ievadīšanas un pirms izvades, ļaujot kontrolēt "
"izvades krāsu.  Trešā virkne (C<GUESTFISH_INIT>) tiek izdrukāta pirms "
"sveiciena ziņojuma, ļaujot kontrolēt šī ziņojuma krāsu.  Ceturtā virkne "
"(C<GUESTFISH_RESTORE>) tiek izdrukāta, pirms guestfish iziet."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1259
msgid ""
"A simple prompt can be set by setting C<GUESTFISH_PS1> to an alternate "
"string:"
msgstr ""
"Vienkāršu uzvedni var iestatīt, iestatot C<GUESTFISH_PS1> uz alternatīvu "
"virkni:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1262
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ GUESTFISH_PS1='(type a command) '\n"
" $ export GUESTFISH_PS1\n"
" $ guestfish\n"
" [...]\n"
" (type a command) ▂\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ GUESTFISH_PS1='(type a command) '\n"
" $ export GUESTFISH_PS1\n"
" $ guestfish\n"
" [...]\n"
" (type a command) ▂\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1268
msgid "You can also use special escape sequences, as described in the table below:"
msgstr "Varat izmantot arī īpašas atsoļa secības, kā aprakstīts tabulā tālāk:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1273
msgid "\\\\"
msgstr "\\\\"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1277
msgid "\\["
msgstr "\\["

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1279
msgid "\\]"
msgstr "\\]"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1281
msgid "(These should only be used in C<GUESTFISH_PS1>.)"
msgstr "(Tās jāizmanto tikai C<GUESTFISH_PS1>.)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1283
msgid ""
"Place non-printing characters (eg. terminal control codes for colours)  "
"between C<\\[...\\]>.  What this does it to tell the L<readline(3)> library "
"that it should treat this subsequence as zero-width, so that command-line "
"redisplay, editing etc works."
msgstr ""
"Nedrukājamās rakstzīmes (piem., termināļa vadības kodus krāsām) novietojiet "
"starp C<\\[...\\]>.  Tas norāda bibliotēkai L<readline(3)>, ka šī "
"apakšsecība jāuzskata par nulles platuma, lai komandrindas atkārtota "
"attēlošana, rediģēšana u. c. darbotos."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1288
msgid "\\a"
msgstr "\\a"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1290
msgid "A bell character."
msgstr "Zvana rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1292
msgid "\\e"
msgstr "\\e"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1294
msgid "An ASCII ESC (escape) character."
msgstr "ASCII ESC (atsoļa) rakstzīme."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1296
msgid "\\n"
msgstr "\\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1298
msgid "A newline."
msgstr "Jauna rinda."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1300
msgid "\\r"
msgstr "\\r"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1302
msgid "A carriage return."
msgstr "Rakstatgrieze."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1304
msgid "\\NNN"
msgstr "\\NNN"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1306
msgid "The ASCII character whose code is the octal value NNN."
msgstr "ASCII rakstzīme, kuras kods ir astoņnieku vērtība NNN."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1308
msgid "\\xNN"
msgstr "\\xNN"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1310
msgid "The ASCII character whose code is the hex value NN."
msgstr "ASCII rakstzīme, kuras kods ir heksadecimālā vērtība NN."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1314
msgid "EXAMPLES OF PROMPTS"
msgstr "UZVEDŅU PIEMĒRI"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1316
msgid "Note that these examples require a terminal that supports ANSI escape codes."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šiem piemēriem nepieciešams terminālis, kas atbalsta ANSI "
"atsoļa kodus."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1322
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" GUESTFISH_PS1='\\[\\e[1;30m\\]><fs>\\[\\e[0;30m\\] '\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" GUESTFISH_PS1='\\[\\e[1;30m\\]><fs>\\[\\e[0;30m\\] '\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1324
msgid "A bold black version of the ordinary prompt."
msgstr "Parastās uzvednes trekna melna versija."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1328
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" GUESTFISH_PS1='\\[\\e[1;32m\\]><fs>\\[\\e[0;31m\\] '\n"
" GUESTFISH_OUTPUT='\\e[0m'\n"
" GUESTFISH_RESTORE=\"$GUESTFISH_OUTPUT\"\n"
" GUESTFISH_INIT='\\e[1;34m'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" GUESTFISH_PS1='\\[\\e[1;32m\\]><fs>\\[\\e[0;31m\\] '\n"
" GUESTFISH_OUTPUT='\\e[0m'\n"
" GUESTFISH_RESTORE=\"$GUESTFISH_OUTPUT\"\n"
" GUESTFISH_INIT='\\e[1;34m'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1333
msgid "Blue welcome text, green prompt, red commands, black command output."
msgstr ""
"Zils sveiciena teksts, zaļa uzvedne, sarkanas komandas, melna komandu izvade."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1338
msgid "WINDOWS 8"
msgstr "WINDOWS 8"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1340
msgid ""
"Windows 8 \"fast startup\" can prevent guestfish from mounting NTFS "
"partitions.  See L<guestfs(3)/WINDOWS HIBERNATION AND WINDOWS 8 FAST "
"STARTUP>."
msgstr ""
"Windows 8 „ātrā palaišana” var neļaut guestfish montēt NTFS nodalījumus.  "
"Skatiet L<guestfs(3)/WINDOWS HIBERNĀCIJA UN WINDOWS 8 ĀTRĀ STARTĒŠANA>."

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1344
msgid "GUESTFISH COMMANDS"
msgstr "GUESTFISH KOMANDAS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1346
msgid ""
"The commands in this section are guestfish convenience commands, in other "
"words, they are not part of the L<guestfs(3)> API."
msgstr ""
"Šīs sadaļas komandas ir guestfish ērtības komandas, citiem vārdiem, tās nav "
"L<guestfs(3)> API daļa."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1349
msgid "help"
msgstr "help"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1351
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" help\n"
" help cmd\n"
" help -l|--list\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" help\n"
" help cmd\n"
" help -l|--list\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1355
msgid "Without any parameter, this provides general help."
msgstr "Bez parametra tas sniedz vispārīgu palīdzību."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1357
msgid "With a C<cmd> parameter, this displays detailed help for that command."
msgstr "Ar parametru C<cmd> tas parāda detalizētu palīdzību par šo komandu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1359
msgid "With I<-l> or I<--list>, this list all commands."
msgstr "Ar I<-l> vai I<--list> tas uzskaita visas komandas."

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1361
msgid "exit"
msgstr "exit"

#. type: =head2
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1363
msgid "quit"
msgstr "quit"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1365
msgid "This exits guestfish.  You can also use C<^D> key."
msgstr "Tas iziet no guestfish.  Varat izmantot arī taustiņu C<^D>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1367
msgid "__INCLUDE:guestfish-commands.pod__"
msgstr "__INCLUDE:guestfish-commands.pod__"

#. type: =head1
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1369
msgid "COMMANDS"
msgstr "KOMANDAS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1371
msgid "__INCLUDE:guestfish-actions.pod__"
msgstr "__INCLUDE:guestfish-actions.pod__"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1375
msgid ""
"guestfish returns 0 if the commands completed without error, or 1 if there "
"was an error."
msgstr ""
"guestfish atgriež 0, ja komandas pabeigtas bez kļūdām, vai 1, ja bija kļūda."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1382
msgid "EDITOR"
msgstr "EDITOR"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1384
msgid ""
"The C<edit> command uses C<$EDITOR> as the editor.  If not set, it uses "
"C<vi>."
msgstr ""
"Komanda C<edit> kā redaktoru izmanto C<$EDITOR>.  Ja nav iestatīts, tā "
"izmanto C<vi>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1387
msgid "GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE"
msgstr "GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1389
msgid ""
"The C<display> command uses C<$GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE> to display images.  "
"If not set, it uses L<display(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Komanda C<display> attēlu parādīšanai izmanto C<$GUESTFISH_DISPLAY_IMAGE>.  "
"Ja nav iestatīts, tā izmanto L<display(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1392
msgid "GUESTFISH_INIT"
msgstr "GUESTFISH_INIT"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1394
msgid "Printed when guestfish starts.  See L</PROMPT>."
msgstr "Izdrukā, kad guestfish startē.  Skatiet L</UZVEDNE>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1396
msgid "GUESTFISH_OUTPUT"
msgstr "GUESTFISH_OUTPUT"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1398
msgid "Printed before guestfish output.  See L</PROMPT>."
msgstr "Izdrukā pirms guestfish izvades.  Skatiet L</UZVEDNE>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1400
msgid "GUESTFISH_PID"
msgstr "GUESTFISH_PID"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1402
msgid ""
"Used with the I<--remote> option to specify the remote guestfish process to "
"control.  See section L</REMOTE CONTROL GUESTFISH OVER A SOCKET>."
msgstr ""
"Izmanto ar opciju I<--remote>, lai norādītu vadāmo attālo guestfish "
"procesu.  Skatiet sadaļu L</GUESTFISH TĀLVADĪBA CAUR LIGZDU>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1406
msgid "GUESTFISH_PS1"
msgstr "GUESTFISH_PS1"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1408
msgid "Set the command prompt.  See L</PROMPT>."
msgstr "Iestatīt komandu uzvedni.  Skatiet L</UZVEDNE>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1410
msgid "GUESTFISH_RESTORE"
msgstr "GUESTFISH_RESTORE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1412
msgid "Printed before guestfish exits.  See L</PROMPT>."
msgstr "Izdrukā, pirms guestfish iziet.  Skatiet L</UZVEDNE>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1414
msgid "HEXEDITOR"
msgstr "HEXEDITOR"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1416
msgid ""
"The L</hexedit> command uses C<$HEXEDITOR> as the external hex editor.  If "
"not specified, the external L<hexedit(1)> program is used."
msgstr ""
"Komanda L</hexedit> kā ārējo heksadecimālo redaktoru izmanto C<$HEXEDITOR>.  "
"Ja nav norādīts, tiek izmantota ārējā programma L<hexedit(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1420
msgid "HOME"
msgstr "HOME"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1422
msgid ""
"If compiled with GNU readline support, various files in the home directory "
"can be used.  See L</FILES>."
msgstr ""
"Ja kompilēts ar GNU readline atbalstu, var izmantot dažādus failus mājas "
"direktorijā.  Skatiet L</FAILI>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1425 lib/guestfs.pod:3105
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_APPEND"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_APPEND"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1427 lib/guestfs.pod:3107
msgid "Pass additional options to the guest kernel."
msgstr "Nodot viesa kodolam papildu opcijas."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1429 lib/guestfs.pod:3109
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_ATTACH_METHOD"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_ATTACH_METHOD"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1431 lib/guestfs.pod:3111
msgid "This is the old way to set C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND>."
msgstr "Šis ir vecais veids, kā iestatīt C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1433 lib/guestfs.pod:3113
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1435
msgid ""
"Choose the default way to create the appliance.  See "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_set_backend>."
msgstr ""
"Izvēlēties noklusējuma veidu palīgsistēmas izveidei.  Skatiet L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_set_backend>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1438 lib/guestfs.pod:3118
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1440
msgid ""
"A colon-separated list of backend-specific settings.  See "
"L<guestfs(3)/BACKEND>, L<guestfs(3)/BACKEND SETTINGS>."
msgstr ""
"Ar koliem atdalīts aizmugursistēmai specifisku iestatījumu saraksts.  "
"Skatiet L<guestfs(3)/AIZMUGURSISTĒMA>, L<guestfs(3)/AIZMUGURSISTĒMAS "
"IESTATĪJUMI>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1443 lib/guestfs.pod:3123
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1445 lib/guestfs.pod:3125
msgid ""
"The location where libguestfs will cache its appliance, when using a "
"supermin appliance.  The appliance is cached and shared between all handles "
"which have the same effective user ID."
msgstr ""
"Vieta, kur libguestfs kešos savu palīgsistēmu, izmantojot supermin "
"palīgsistēmu.  Palīgsistēma tiek kešota un koplietota starp visiem rokturiem "
"ar vienādu efektīvo lietotāja ID."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1449 lib/guestfs.pod:3129
msgid ""
"If C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> is not set, then C<TMPDIR> is used.  If C<TMPDIR> "
"is not set, then F</var/tmp> is used."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR> nav iestatīts, tiek izmantots C<TMPDIR>.  Ja "
"C<TMPDIR> nav iestatīts, tiek izmantots F</var/tmp>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1452
msgid "See also L</LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR>, L</set-cachedir>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR>, L</set-cachedir>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1454 lib/guestfs.pod:3134
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1456
msgid ""
"Set C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1> to enable verbose messages.  This has the same "
"effect as using the B<-v> option."
msgstr ""
"Iestatiet C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1>, lai iespējotu izvērstos ziņojumus.  Tam ir "
"tāda pati ietekme kā opcijas B<-v> izmantošanai."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1459 lib/guestfs.pod:3139
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_HV"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_HV"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1461 lib/guestfs.pod:3141
msgid ""
"Set the default hypervisor (usually qemu) binary that libguestfs uses.  If "
"not set, then the qemu which was found at compile time by the configure "
"script is used."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt noklusējuma hipervizora (parasti qemu) bināro failu, ko izmanto "
"libguestfs.  Ja nav iestatīts, tiek izmantots qemu, ko kompilēšanas laikā "
"atrada configure skripts."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1465 lib/guestfs.pod:3147
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_MEMSIZE"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_MEMSIZE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1467 lib/guestfs.pod:3149
msgid "Set the memory allocated to the qemu process, in megabytes.  For example:"
msgstr "Iestatīt qemu procesam piešķirto atmiņu megabaitos.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1470 lib/guestfs.pod:3152
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" LIBGUESTFS_MEMSIZE=700\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" LIBGUESTFS_MEMSIZE=700\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1472 lib/guestfs.pod:3154
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_PATH"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_PATH"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1474
msgid ""
"Set the path that guestfish uses to search for kernel and initrd.img.  See "
"the discussion of paths in L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt ceļu, kurā guestfish meklē kodolu un initrd.img.  Skatiet ceļu "
"aplūkojumu L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1477 lib/guestfs.pod:3159
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_QEMU"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_QEMU"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1479 lib/guestfs.pod:3161
msgid "This is the old way to set C<LIBGUESTFS_HV>."
msgstr "Šis ir vecais veids, kā iestatīt C<LIBGUESTFS_HV>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1481 lib/guestfs.pod:3163
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1483 lib/guestfs.pod:3165
msgid ""
"The location where libguestfs will store temporary files used by each "
"handle."
msgstr "Vieta, kur libguestfs glabās katra roktura izmantotos pagaidu failus."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1486 lib/guestfs.pod:3168
msgid ""
"If C<LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR> is not set, then C<TMPDIR> is used.  If C<TMPDIR> is "
"not set, then F</tmp> is used."
msgstr ""
"Ja C<LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR> nav iestatīts, tiek izmantots C<TMPDIR>.  Ja "
"C<TMPDIR> nav iestatīts, tiek izmantots F</tmp>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1489
msgid "See also L</LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>, L</set-tmpdir>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>, L</set-tmpdir>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1491 lib/guestfs.pod:3173
msgid "LIBGUESTFS_TRACE"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS_TRACE"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1493
msgid "Set C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1> to enable command traces."
msgstr "Iestatiet C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1>, lai iespējotu komandu izsekošanu."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1495
msgid "PAGER"
msgstr "PAGER"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1497
msgid ""
"The C<more> command uses C<$PAGER> as the pager.  If not set, it uses "
"C<more>."
msgstr ""
"Komanda C<more> kā lapotāju izmanto C<$PAGER>.  Ja nav iestatīts, tā izmanto "
"C<more>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1500 lib/guestfs.pod:1355 lib/guestfs.pod:3178
msgid "PATH"
msgstr "PATH"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1502
msgid ""
"Libguestfs and guestfish may run some external programs, and rely on "
"C<$PATH> being set to a reasonable value.  If using the libvirt backend, "
"libvirt will not work at all unless C<$PATH> contains the path of qemu/KVM."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs un guestfish var izpildīt dažas ārējas programmas un paļaujas, ka "
"C<$PATH> ir iestatīts uz saprātīgu vērtību.  Ja izmanto libvirt "
"aizmugursistēmu, libvirt nemaz nedarbosies, ja vien C<$PATH> nesatur qemu/"
"KVM ceļu."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1507 lib/guestfs.pod:3186
msgid "SUPERMIN_KERNEL"
msgstr "SUPERMIN_KERNEL"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1509 lib/guestfs.pod:3188
msgid "SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION"
msgstr "SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1511 lib/guestfs.pod:3190
msgid "SUPERMIN_MODULES"
msgstr "SUPERMIN_MODULES"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1513 lib/guestfs.pod:3192
msgid ""
"These three environment variables allow the kernel that libguestfs uses in "
"the appliance to be selected.  If C<$SUPERMIN_KERNEL> is not set, then the "
"most recent host kernel is chosen.  For more information about kernel "
"selection, see L<supermin(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Šie trīs vides mainīgie ļauj izvēlēties kodolu, ko libguestfs izmanto "
"palīgsistēmā.  Ja C<$SUPERMIN_KERNEL> nav iestatīts, tiek izvēlēts jaunākais "
"resursdatora kodols.  Plašāku informāciju par kodola izvēli skatiet "
"L<supermin(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1518 lib/guestfs.pod:3197
msgid "TMPDIR"
msgstr "TMPDIR"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1520 lib/guestfs.pod:3199
msgid "See L</LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>, L</LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR>."
msgstr "Skatiet L</LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>, L</LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1522 lib/guestfs.pod:3201
msgid "XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"
msgstr "XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1524 lib/guestfs.pod:3203
msgid ""
"This directory represents a user-specific directory for storing "
"non-essential runtime files."
msgstr ""
"Šī direktorija attēlo lietotājam specifisku direktoriju nebūtisku "
"izpildlaika failu glabāšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1527 lib/guestfs.pod:3206
msgid ""
"If it is set, then is used to store temporary sockets and PID files.  "
"Otherwise, F</tmp> is used."
msgstr ""
"Ja tā ir iestatīta, tā tiek izmantota pagaidu ligzdu un PID failu "
"glabāšanai.  Citādi tiek izmantots F</tmp>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1530
msgid ""
"See also L</get-sockdir>, "
"L<http://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Specifications/basedir-spec/>."
msgstr ""
"Skatīt arī L</get-sockdir>, L<http://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Specifications/"
"basedir-spec/>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1539 fuse/guestmount.pod:402 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:481
msgid "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf"
msgstr "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1541 fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:67
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:404 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:483
msgid "$HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc"
msgstr "$HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1543 fuse/guestmount.pod:406 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:485
msgid "$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf"
msgstr "$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1545 fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:77
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:408 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:487
msgid "/etc/libguestfs-tools.conf"
msgstr "/etc/libguestfs-tools.conf"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1547 fuse/guestmount.pod:410 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:489
msgid ""
"This configuration file controls the default read-only or read-write mode "
"(I<--ro> or I<--rw>)."
msgstr ""
"Šis konfigurācijas fails kontrolē noklusējuma tikai lasīšanas vai lasīšanas-"
"rakstīšanas režīmu (I<--ro> vai I<--rw>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1550 fuse/guestmount.pod:413 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:492
msgid "See L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>."
msgstr "Skatiet L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1552
msgid "$HOME/.guestfish"
msgstr "$HOME/.guestfish"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1554
msgid ""
"If compiled with GNU readline support, then the command history is saved in "
"this file."
msgstr ""
"Ja kompilēts ar GNU readline atbalstu, komandu vēsture tiek saglabāta šajā "
"failā."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1557
msgid "$HOME/.inputrc"
msgstr "$HOME/.inputrc"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1559
msgid "/etc/inputrc"
msgstr "/etc/inputrc"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1561
msgid ""
"If compiled with GNU readline support, then these files can be used to "
"configure readline.  For further information, please see "
"L<readline(3)/INITIALIZATION FILE>."
msgstr ""
"Ja kompilēts ar GNU readline atbalstu, šos failus var izmantot readline "
"konfigurēšanai.  Plašāku informāciju, lūdzu, skatiet L<readline(3)/"
"INITIALIZATION FILE>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1565
msgid "To write rules which only apply to guestfish, use:"
msgstr "Lai rakstītu kārtulas, kas attiecas tikai uz guestfish, izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1567
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $if guestfish\n"
" ...\n"
" $endif\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $if guestfish\n"
" ...\n"
" $endif\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1571
msgid ""
"Variables that you can set in inputrc that change the behaviour of guestfish "
"in useful ways include:"
msgstr ""
"Mainīgie, ko var iestatīt inputrc un kas noderīgi maina guestfish uzvedību, "
"ietver:"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1576
msgid "completion-ignore-case (default: on)"
msgstr "completion-ignore-case (noklusējums: on)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1578
msgid ""
"By default, guestfish will ignore case when tab-completing paths on the "
"disk.  Use:"
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma guestfish, pabeidzot ceļus diskā ar tabulēšanu, ignorēs "
"reģistru.  Izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1581
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" set completion-ignore-case off\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" set completion-ignore-case off\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1583
msgid "to make guestfish case sensitive."
msgstr "lai guestfish būtu reģistrjutīgs."

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1587
msgid "test1.img"
msgstr "test1.img"

#. type: =item
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1589
msgid "test2.img (etc)"
msgstr "test2.img (u. c.)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1591
msgid ""
"When using the I<-N> or I<--new> option, the prepared disk or filesystem "
"will be created in the file F<test1.img> in the current directory.  The "
"second use of I<-N> will use F<test2.img> and so on.  Any existing file with "
"the same name will be overwritten.  You can use a different filename by "
"using the C<filename=> prefix."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot opciju I<-N> vai I<--new>, sagatavotais disks vai failu sistēma "
"tiks izveidota failā F<test1.img> pašreizējā direktorijā.  Otrā I<-N> "
"izmantošana izmantos F<test2.img> un tā tālāk.  Jebkurš esošs fails ar tādu "
"pašu nosaukumu tiks pārrakstīts.  Citu faila nosaukumu var izmantot ar "
"priedēkli C<filename=>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/guestfish.pod:1601
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<virt-alignment-scan(1)>, "
"L<virt-builder(1)>, L<virt-builder-repository(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, "
"L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, L<virt-customize(1)>, "
"L<virt-df(1)>, L<virt-diff(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-filesystems(1)>, "
"L<virt-inspector(1)>, L<virt-list-filesystems(1)>, "
"L<virt-list-partitions(1)>, L<virt-log(1)>, L<virt-ls(1)>, "
"L<virt-make-fs(1)>, L<virt-p2v(1)>, L<virt-rescue(1)>, L<virt-resize(1)>, "
"L<virt-sparsify(1)>, L<virt-sysprep(1)>, L<virt-tail(1)>, L<virt-tar(1)>, "
"L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<virt-v2v(1)>, L<virt-win-reg(1)>, "
"L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>, L<display(1)>, L<hexedit(1)>, L<supermin(1)>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<virt-alignment-scan(1)>, L<virt-"
"builder(1)>, L<virt-builder-repository(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in"
"(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, L<virt-customize(1)>, L<virt-df(1)>, L<virt-diff"
"(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-inspector(1)>, L<virt-"
"list-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-list-partitions(1)>, L<virt-log(1)>, L<virt-ls"
"(1)>, L<virt-make-fs(1)>, L<virt-p2v(1)>, L<virt-rescue(1)>, L<virt-resize"
"(1)>, L<virt-sparsify(1)>, L<virt-sysprep(1)>, L<virt-tail(1)>, L<virt-tar"
"(1)>, L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<virt-v2v(1)>, L<virt-win-reg"
"(1)>, L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>, L<display(1)>, L<hexedit(1)>, L<supermin"
"(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:3
msgid ""
"libguestfs-tools.conf - configuration file for guestfish, guestmount, "
"virt-rescue"
msgstr ""
"libguestfs-tools.conf - guestfish, guestmount, virt-rescue konfigurācijas "
"fails"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /etc/libguestfs-tools.conf\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /etc/libguestfs-tools.conf\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:17
msgid ""
"F<libguestfs-tools.conf> (or F<$HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc>) changes the "
"defaults for the following programs only:"
msgstr ""
"F<libguestfs-tools.conf> (vai F<$HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc>) maina "
"noklusējumus tikai šīm programmām:"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:24
msgid "L<guestfish(1)>"
msgstr "L<guestfish(1)>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:28
msgid "L<guestmount(1)>"
msgstr "L<guestmount(1)>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:32
msgid "L<virt-rescue(1)>"
msgstr "L<virt-rescue(1)>"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:36
msgid ""
"There is currently only one setting which is controlled by this file.  "
"Adding (or uncommenting):"
msgstr ""
"Pašlaik ir tikai viens iestatījums, ko kontrolē šis fails.  Pievienojot (vai "
"atkomentējot):"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" read_only = true;\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" read_only = true;\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:41
msgid ""
"changes these programs so they act as if the I<--ro> flag was given on the "
"command line.  You can use this to make the programs safe against accidental "
"modification of a live guest (users would have to explicitly add the I<--rw> "
"flag to modify guests).  This is not the default because it is not backwards "
"compatible.  See also L<guestfish(1)/OPENING DISKS FOR READ AND WRITE>."
msgstr ""
"šīs programmas tiek mainītas, lai tās darbotos tā, it kā komandrindā būtu "
"norādīts karogs I<--ro>.  To var izmantot, lai programmas būtu drošas pret "
"nejaušu darbojoša viesa mainīšanu (lietotājiem būtu eksplicīti jāpievieno "
"karogs I<--rw>, lai mainītu viesus).  Tas nav noklusējums, jo tas nav "
"atpakaļsaderīgs.  Skatīt arī L<guestfish(1)/DISKU ATVĒRŠANA LASĪŠANAI UN "
"RAKSTĪŠANAI>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:48
msgid "Note that B<the semicolon is required>."
msgstr "Ņemiet vērā, ka B<semikols ir obligāts>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:50
msgid ""
"This file is parsed by the libconfig library.  For more information about "
"the format, see: "
"L<http://www.hyperrealm.com/libconfig/libconfig_manual.html>"
msgstr ""
"Šo failu parsē bibliotēka libconfig.  Plašāku informāciju par formātu "
"skatiet: L<http://www.hyperrealm.com/libconfig/libconfig_manual.html>"

#. type: =head1
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:54
msgid "FILE LOCATION"
msgstr "FAILA ATRAŠANĀS VIETA"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:56
msgid "The order of the configuration files being read is, by importance:"
msgstr "Konfigurācijas failu nolasīšanas secība pēc svarīguma ir:"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:62
msgid ""
"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf (C<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME> is "
"F<$HOME/.config> if not set)."
msgstr ""
"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf (C<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME> ir "
"F<$HOME/.config>, ja nav iestatīts)."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:71
msgid ""
"$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf (where C<$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS> "
"means any of the directories in that environment variable, or just "
"F</etc/xdg> if not set)"
msgstr ""
"$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf (kur C<$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS> "
"nozīmē jebkuru no direktorijām šajā vides mainīgajā vai tikai F</etc/xdg>, "
"ja nav iestatīts)"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:81
msgid ""
"This means local users can override the system configuration by copying the "
"configuration file (or creating it anew) into "
"F<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf>."
msgstr ""
"Tas nozīmē, ka lokālie lietotāji var ignorēt sistēmas konfigurāciju, "
"nokopējot konfigurācijas failu (vai izveidojot to no jauna) uz "
"F<$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/libguestfs/libguestfs-tools.conf>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:85
msgid ""
"F</etc/libguestfs-tools.conf> and F<$HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc> are the old "
"non-XDG paths which are read for compatibility."
msgstr ""
"F</etc/libguestfs-tools.conf> un F<$HOME/.libguestfs-tools.rc> ir vecie ne-"
"XDG ceļi, kas tiek nolasīti saderības dēļ."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/libguestfs-tools.conf.pod:90
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)/OPENING DISKS FOR READ AND WRITE>, L<guestmount(1)>, "
"L<virt-rescue(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, "
"L<http://standards.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/latest/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)/DISKU ATVĒRŠANA LASĪŠANAI UN RAKSTĪŠANAI>, L<guestmount(1)>, "
"L<virt-rescue(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://"
"standards.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/latest/>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:3
msgid "virt-copy-in - Copy files and directories into a virtual machine disk image."
msgstr ""
"virt-copy-in - failu un direktoriju iekopēšana virtuālās mašīnas diska "
"attēlā."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-in -a disk.img file|dir [file|dir ...] /destination\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-in -a disk.img file|dir [file|dir ...] /destination\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-in -d domain file|dir [file|dir ...] /destination\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-in -d domain file|dir [file|dir ...] /destination\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:13
msgid ""
"C<virt-copy-in> copies files and directories from the local disk into a "
"virtual machine disk image or named libvirt domain."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-copy-in> kopē failus un direktorijas no lokālā diska uz virtuālās "
"mašīnas diska attēlu vai nosauktu libvirt domēnu."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:16
msgid ""
"You can give one or more filenames and directories on the command line.  "
"Directories are copied in recursively.  The final parameter must be the "
"destination directory in the disk image which must be an absolute path "
"starting with a F</> character."
msgstr ""
"Komandrindā varat norādīt vienu vai vairākus failu nosaukumus un "
"direktorijas.  Direktorijas tiek iekopētas rekursīvi.  Pēdējam parametram "
"jābūt mērķa direktorijai diska attēlā, kurai jābūt absolūtam ceļam, kas "
"sākas ar rakstzīmi F</>."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-in -d MyGuest resolv.conf /etc\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-in -d MyGuest resolv.conf /etc\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:27 fish/virt-tar-in.pod:24
msgid "Upload a home directory to a guest:"
msgstr "Augšupielādēt mājas direktoriju viesī:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-in -d MyGuest skel /home\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-in -d MyGuest skel /home\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:31 fish/virt-copy-out.pod:26 fish/virt-tar-in.pod:28
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:28
msgid "JUST A SHELL SCRIPT WRAPPER AROUND GUESTFISH"
msgstr "TIKAI ČAULAS SKRIPTA IETINĒJS AP GUESTFISH"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:33
msgid ""
"This command is just a simple shell script wrapper around the "
"L<guestfish(1)> C<copy-in> command.  For anything more complex than a "
"trivial copy, you are probably better off using guestfish directly."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tikai vienkāršs čaulas skripta ietinējs ap L<guestfish(1)> "
"komandu C<copy-in>.  Jebkam sarežģītākam par triviālu kopēšanu, visticamāk, "
"labāk tieši izmantot guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:39 fish/virt-copy-out.pod:34 fish/virt-tar-in.pod:36
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:36
msgid ""
"Since the shell script just passes options straight to guestfish, read "
"L<guestfish(1)> to see the full list of options."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā čaulas skripts vienkārši nodod opcijas tieši guestfish, pilnu opciju "
"sarakstu skatiet L<guestfish(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-in.pod:44
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, "
"L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, "
"L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:3
msgid ""
"virt-copy-out - Copy files and directories out of a virtual machine disk "
"image."
msgstr ""
"virt-copy-out - failu un direktoriju izkopēšana no virtuālās mašīnas diska "
"attēla."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-out -a disk.img /file|dir [/file|dir ...] localdir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-out -a disk.img /file|dir [/file|dir ...] localdir\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-copy-out -d domain /file|dir [/file|dir ...] localdir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-copy-out -d domain /file|dir [/file|dir ...] localdir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:13
msgid ""
"C<virt-copy-out> copies files and directories out of a virtual machine disk "
"image or named libvirt domain."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-copy-out> kopē failus un direktorijas ārā no virtuālās mašīnas diska "
"attēla vai nosaukta libvirt domēna."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:16
msgid ""
"You can give one or more filenames and directories on the command line.  "
"Directories are copied out recursively."
msgstr ""
"Komandrindā varat norādīt vienu vai vairākus failu nosaukumus un "
"direktorijas.  Direktorijas tiek izkopētas rekursīvi."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:21
msgid "Download the home directories from a virtual machine:"
msgstr "Lejupielādēt mājas direktorijas no virtuālās mašīnas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mkdir homes\n"
" virt-copy-out -d MyGuest /home homes\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mkdir homes\n"
" virt-copy-out -d MyGuest /home homes\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:28
msgid ""
"This command is just a simple shell script wrapper around the "
"L<guestfish(1)> C<copy-out> command.  For anything more complex than a "
"trivial copy, you are probably better off using guestfish directly."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tikai vienkāršs čaulas skripta ietinējs ap L<guestfish(1)> "
"komandu C<copy-out>.  Jebkam sarežģītākam par triviālu kopēšanu, visticamāk, "
"labāk tieši izmantot guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-copy-out.pod:39
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, "
"L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-"
"tar-in(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:3
msgid "virt-tar-in - Unpack a tarball into a virtual machine disk image."
msgstr "virt-tar-in - tar arhīva izpakošana virtuālās mašīnas diska attēlā."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-in -a disk.img data.tar /destination\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-in -a disk.img data.tar /destination\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-in -d domain data.tar /destination\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-in -d domain data.tar /destination\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" zcat data.tar.gz | virt-tar-in -d domain - /destination\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" zcat data.tar.gz | virt-tar-in -d domain - /destination\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:15
msgid ""
"C<virt-tar-in> unpacks an uncompressed tarball into a virtual machine disk "
"image or named libvirt domain."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-tar-in> izpako nesaspiestu tar arhīvu virtuālās mašīnas diska attēlā "
"vai nosauktā libvirt domēnā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:18
msgid ""
"The first parameter is the tar file.  Use C<-> to read the tar file from "
"standard input.  The second parameter is the absolute target directory to "
"unpack into."
msgstr ""
"Pirmais parametrs ir tar fails.  Izmantojiet C<->, lai nolasītu tar failu no "
"standarta ievades.  Otrais parametrs ir absolūtā mērķa direktorija, kurā "
"izpakot."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-in -d MyGuest homes.tar /home\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-in -d MyGuest homes.tar /home\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:30
msgid ""
"This command is just a simple shell script wrapper around the "
"L<guestfish(1)> C<tar-in> command.  For anything more complex than a trivial "
"copy, you are probably better off using guestfish directly."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tikai vienkāršs čaulas skripta ietinējs ap L<guestfish(1)> "
"komandu C<tar-in>.  Jebkam sarežģītākam par triviālu kopēšanu, visticamāk, "
"labāk tieši izmantot guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-in.pod:41
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-make-fs(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-make-fs(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:3
msgid "virt-tar-out - Pack a virtual machine disk image directory into a tarball."
msgstr ""
"virt-tar-out - virtuālās mašīnas diska attēla direktorijas iepakošana tar "
"arhīvā."

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-out -a disk.img /dir files.tar\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-out -a disk.img /dir files.tar\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-out -d domain /dir files.tar\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-out -d domain /dir files.tar\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-out -d domain /dir - | gzip --best > files.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-out -d domain /dir - | gzip --best > files.tar.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:15
msgid "C<virt-tar-out> packs a virtual machine disk image directory into a tarball."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-tar-out> iepako virtuālās mašīnas diska attēla direktoriju tar arhīvā."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:18
msgid ""
"The first parameter is the absolute path of the virtual machine directory.  "
"The second parameter is the tar file to write.  Use C<-> to write to "
"standard output."
msgstr ""
"Pirmais parametrs ir virtuālās mašīnas direktorijas absolūtais ceļš.  Otrais "
"parametrs ir rakstāmais tar fails.  Izmantojiet C<->, lai rakstītu standarta "
"izvadē."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:24
msgid "Download the home directories from a guest:"
msgstr "Lejupielādēt mājas direktorijas no viesa:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-tar-out -d MyGuest /home - | gzip --best > homes.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-tar-out -d MyGuest /home - | gzip --best > homes.tar.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:30
msgid ""
"This command is just a simple shell script wrapper around the "
"L<guestfish(1)> C<tar-out> command.  For anything more complex than a "
"trivial copy, you are probably better off using guestfish directly."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda ir tikai vienkāršs čaulas skripta ietinējs ap L<guestfish(1)> "
"komandu C<tar-out>.  Jebkam sarežģītākam par triviālu kopēšanu, visticamāk, "
"labāk tieši izmantot guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: fish/virt-tar-out.pod:41
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:3
msgid "guestmount - Mount a guest filesystem on the host using FUSE and libguestfs"
msgstr ""
"guestmount - viesa failu sistēmas montēšana resursdatorā, izmantojot FUSE un "
"libguestfs"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount [--options] -a disk.img -m device [--ro] mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount [--options] -a disk.img -m device [--ro] mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount [--options] -a disk.img -i [--ro] mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount [--options] -a disk.img -i [--ro] mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount [--options] -d Guest -i [--ro] mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount [--options] -d Guest -i [--ro] mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:15
msgid ""
"The guestmount program can be used to mount virtual machine filesystems and "
"other disk images on the host.  It uses libguestfs for access to the guest "
"filesystem, and FUSE (the \"filesystem in userspace\") to make it appear as "
"a mountable device."
msgstr ""
"Programmu guestmount var izmantot virtuālo mašīnu failu sistēmu un citu "
"disku attēlu montēšanai resursdatorā.  Tā izmanto libguestfs piekļuvei viesa "
"failu sistēmai un FUSE („failu sistēma lietotāja telpā”), lai tā izskatītos "
"pēc montējamas ierīces."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:20
msgid ""
"Along with other options, you have to give at least one device (I<-a> "
"option) or libvirt domain (I<-d> option), and at least one mountpoint (I<-m> "
"option) or use the I<-i> inspection option.  How this works is better "
"explained in the L<guestfish(1)> manual page, or by looking at the examples "
"below."
msgstr ""
"Kopā ar citām opcijām jānorāda vismaz viena ierīce (opcija I<-a>) vai "
"libvirt domēns (opcija I<-d>) un vismaz viens montēšanas punkts (opcija I<-"
"m>), vai jāizmanto inspicēšanas opcija I<-i>.  Kā tas darbojas, labāk "
"izskaidrots L<guestfish(1)> rokasgrāmatas lapā vai apskatot tālāk dotos "
"piemērus."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:26
msgid ""
"FUSE lets you mount filesystems as non-root.  The mountpoint must be owned "
"by you.  The filesystem will not be visible to any other users unless you "
"make configuration changes, see L</NOTES> below."
msgstr ""
"FUSE ļauj montēt failu sistēmas ne kā root.  Montēšanas punktam jāpieder "
"jums.  Failu sistēma nebūs redzama citiem lietotājiem, ja vien neveicat "
"konfigurācijas izmaiņas, skatiet L</PIEZĪMES> tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:30
msgid "To unmount the filesystem, use the L<guestunmount(1)> command."
msgstr "Lai atmontētu failu sistēmu, izmantojiet komandu L<guestunmount(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:34
msgid ""
"For a typical Windows guest which has its main filesystem on the first "
"partition:"
msgstr ""
"Tipiskam Windows viesim, kura galvenā failu sistēma atrodas pirmajā "
"nodalījumā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount -a windows.img -m /dev/sda1 --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount -a windows.img -m /dev/sda1 --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:39
msgid ""
"For a typical Linux guest which has a /boot filesystem on the first "
"partition, and the root filesystem on a logical volume:"
msgstr ""
"Tipiskam Linux viesim, kuram /boot failu sistēma atrodas pirmajā nodalījumā "
"un saknes failu sistēma — loģiskajā sējumā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount -a linux.img -m /dev/VG/LV -m /dev/sda1:/boot --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount -a linux.img -m /dev/VG/LV -m /dev/sda1:/boot --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:44
msgid "To get libguestfs to detect guest mountpoints for you:"
msgstr "Lai libguestfs jūsu vietā noteiktu viesa montēšanas punktus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount -a guest.img -i --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount -a guest.img -i --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:48
msgid "For a libvirt guest called \"Guest\" you could do:"
msgstr "Libvirt viesim ar nosaukumu „Guest” varētu izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount -d Guest -i --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount -d Guest -i --ro /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:52
msgid ""
"If you don’t know what filesystems are contained in a guest or disk image, "
"use L<virt-filesystems(1)> first:"
msgstr ""
"Ja nezināt, kādas failu sistēmas ir viesī vai diska attēlā, vispirms "
"izmantojiet L<virt-filesystems(1)>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems -d MyGuest\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems -d MyGuest\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:57
msgid ""
"If you want to trace the libguestfs calls but without excessive debugging "
"information, we recommend:"
msgstr ""
"Ja vēlaties izsekot libguestfs izsaukumus, bet bez pārmērīgas atkļūdošanas "
"informācijas, iesakām:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount [...] --trace /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount [...] --trace /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:62
msgid "If you want to debug the program, we recommend:"
msgstr "Ja vēlaties atkļūdot programmu, iesakām:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount [...] --trace --verbose /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount [...] --trace --verbose /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:66
msgid "To unmount the filesystem after using it:"
msgstr "Lai atmontētu failu sistēmu pēc lietošanas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestunmount /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestunmount /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:70 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:66
msgid "NOTES"
msgstr "PIEZĪMES"

#. type: =head2
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:72
msgid "Other users cannot see the filesystem by default"
msgstr "Citi lietotāji pēc noklusējuma failu sistēmu neredz"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:74
msgid ""
"If you mount a filesystem as one user (eg. root), then other users will not "
"be able to see it by default.  The fix is to add the FUSE C<allow_other> "
"option when mounting:"
msgstr ""
"Ja montējat failu sistēmu kā viens lietotājs (piem., root), citi lietotāji "
"pēc noklusējuma to neredzēs.  Labojums ir montējot pievienot FUSE opciju "
"C<allow_other>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" sudo guestmount [...] -o allow_other /mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" sudo guestmount [...] -o allow_other /mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:80
msgid "B<and> to enable this option in F</etc/fuse.conf>."
msgstr "B<un> iespējot šo opciju failā F</etc/fuse.conf>."

#. type: =head2
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:82
msgid "Enabling FUSE"
msgstr "FUSE iespējošana"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:84
msgid ""
"On some distros, you may need to add yourself to a special group "
"(eg. C<fuse>) before you can use any FUSE filesystem.  This is necessary on "
"Debian and derivatives."
msgstr ""
"Dažās distribūcijās, pirms varat izmantot jebkuru FUSE failu sistēmu, sevi, "
"iespējams, jāpievieno īpašai grupai (piem., C<fuse>).  Tas ir nepieciešams "
"Debian un tā atvasinājumos."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:88
msgid ""
"On other distros, no special group is required.  It is not necessary on "
"Fedora or Red Hat Enterprise Linux."
msgstr ""
"Citās distribūcijās īpaša grupa nav nepieciešama.  Fedorā vai Red Hat "
"Enterprise Linux tas nav nepieciešams."

#. type: =head2
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:91
msgid "fusermount error: \"Device or resource busy\""
msgstr "fusermount kļūda: \"Device or resource busy\""

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:93
msgid ""
"You can see this error when another process on the system jumps into the "
"mountpoint you have just created, holding it open and preventing you from "
"unmounting it.  The usual culprits are various GUI \"indexing\" programs."
msgstr ""
"Šo kļūdu var redzēt, kad cits sistēmas process ielec tikko izveidotajā "
"montēšanas punktā, tur to atvērtu un neļauj to atmontēt.  Parastie "
"vaininieki ir dažādas GUI „indeksēšanas” programmas."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:98
msgid ""
"The popular workaround for this problem is to retry the C<fusermount -u> "
"command a few times until it works (L<guestunmount(1)> does this for you).  "
"Unfortunately this isn't a reliable fix if (for example)  the mounted "
"filesystem is particularly large and the intruding program particularly "
"persistent."
msgstr ""
"Populārā šīs problēmas apiešana ir atkārtot komandu C<fusermount -u> dažas "
"reizes, līdz tā izdodas (L<guestunmount(1)> to dara jūsu vietā).  Diemžēl "
"tas nav uzticams labojums, ja (piemēram) montētā failu sistēma ir īpaši "
"liela un traucējošā programma īpaši neatlaidīga."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:104
msgid ""
"A proper fix is to use a private mountpoint by creating a new mount "
"namespace using the Linux-specific L<clone(2)>/L<unshare(2)> flag "
"C<CLONE_NEWNS>.  Unfortunately at the moment this requires root and we would "
"also probably need to add it as a feature to guestmount."
msgstr ""
"Pareizs labojums ir izmantot privātu montēšanas punktu, izveidojot jaunu "
"montēšanas nosaukumtelpu ar Linux specifisko L<clone(2)>/L<unshare(2)> "
"karogu C<CLONE_NEWNS>.  Diemžēl pašlaik tam nepieciešams root, un, "
"visticamāk, mums tas būtu jāpievieno kā guestmount līdzeklis."

#. type: =head2
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:109
msgid "Race conditions possible when shutting down the connection"
msgstr "Iespējami sacensību stāvokļi, aizverot savienojumu"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:111
msgid ""
"When L<guestunmount(1)>/L<fusermount(1)> exits, guestmount may still be "
"running and cleaning up the mountpoint.  The disk image will not be fully "
"finalized."
msgstr ""
"Kad L<guestunmount(1)>/L<fusermount(1)> iziet, guestmount, iespējams, "
"joprojām darbojas un sakopj montēšanas punktu.  Diska attēls nebūs pilnībā "
"pabeigts."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:115
msgid "This means that scripts like the following have a nasty race condition:"
msgstr "Tas nozīmē, ka tādos skriptos kā šis ir nepatīkams sacensību stāvoklis:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:118
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount -a disk.img -i /mnt\n"
" # copy things into /mnt\n"
" guestunmount /mnt\n"
" # immediately try to use 'disk.img' ** UNSAFE **\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount -a disk.img -i /mnt\n"
" # copy things into /mnt\n"
" guestunmount /mnt\n"
" # immediately try to use 'disk.img' ** UNSAFE **\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:123
msgid ""
"The solution is to use the I<--pid-file> option to write the guestmount PID "
"to a file, then after guestunmount spin waiting for this PID to exit."
msgstr ""
"Risinājums ir izmantot opciju I<--pid-file>, lai ierakstītu guestmount PID "
"failā, un pēc guestunmount cilpā gaidīt, līdz šis PID iziet."

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:127
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount -a disk.img -i --pid-file guestmount.pid /mnt\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount -a disk.img -i --pid-file guestmount.pid /mnt\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # ...\n"
" # ...\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" # ...\n"
" # ...\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:132
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Save the PID of guestmount *before* calling guestunmount.\n"
" pid=\"$(cat guestmount.pid)\"\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" # Save the PID of guestmount *before* calling guestunmount.\n"
" pid=\"$(cat guestmount.pid)\"\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:135
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Unmount the filesystem.\n"
" guestunmount /mnt\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" # Unmount the filesystem.\n"
" guestunmount /mnt\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:138
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" timeout=10\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" timeout=10\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:140
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" count=$timeout\n"
" while kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null && [ $count -gt 0 ]; do\n"
"     sleep 1\n"
"     ((count--))\n"
" done\n"
" if [ $count -eq 0 ]; then\n"
"     echo \"$0: wait for guestmount to exit failed after $timeout "
"seconds\"\n"
"     exit 1\n"
" fi\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" count=$timeout\n"
" while kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null && [ $count -gt 0 ]; do\n"
"     sleep 1\n"
"     ((count--))\n"
" done\n"
" if [ $count -eq 0 ]; then\n"
"     echo \"$0: wait for guestmount to exit failed after $timeout seconds\"\n"
"     exit 1\n"
" fi\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Now it is safe to use the disk image.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # Now it is safe to use the disk image.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:152
msgid ""
"Note that if you use the C<guestfs_mount_local> API directly (see "
"L<guestfs(3)/MOUNT LOCAL>) then it is much easier to write a safe, race-free "
"program."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, ja tieši izmantojat API C<guestfs_mount_local> (skatiet "
"L<guestfs(3)/LOKĀLĀ MONTĒŠANA>), drošu programmu bez sacensību stāvokļiem "
"uzrakstīt ir daudz vieglāk."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:164
msgid "Add a block device or virtual machine image."
msgstr "Pievienot bloku ierīci vai virtuālās mašīnas attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:173 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:109
msgid "Add a remote disk.  See L<guestfish(1)/ADDING REMOTE STORAGE>."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot attālu disku.  Skatiet L<guestfish(1)/ATTĀLĀS KRĀTUVES "
"PIEVIENOŠANA>."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:195
msgid "B<--dir-cache-timeout> N"
msgstr "B<--dir-cache-timeout> N"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:197
msgid ""
"Set the readdir cache timeout to I<N> seconds, the default being 60 "
"seconds.  The readdir cache [actually, there are several semi-independent "
"caches] is populated after a readdir(2) call with the stat and extended "
"attributes of the files in the directory, in anticipation that they will be "
"requested soon after."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt readdir kešatmiņas noildzi uz I<N> sekundēm, noklusējums ir 60 "
"sekundes.  Readdir kešatmiņa [patiesībā ir vairākas daļēji neatkarīgas "
"kešatmiņas] pēc readdir(2) izsaukuma tiek aizpildīta ar direktorijas failu "
"stat un paplašinātajiem atribūtiem, paredzot, ka tie drīz tiks pieprasīti."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:203
msgid ""
"There is also a different attribute cache implemented by FUSE (see the FUSE "
"option I<-o attr_timeout>), but the FUSE cache does not anticipate future "
"requests, only cache existing ones."
msgstr ""
"Ir arī cita atribūtu kešatmiņa, ko realizē FUSE (skatiet FUSE opciju I<-o "
"attr_timeout>), taču FUSE kešatmiņa neparedz nākotnes pieprasījumus, tā "
"tikai kešo esošos."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:214
msgid "B<--fd=>FD"
msgstr "B<--fd=>FD"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:216
msgid ""
"Specify a pipe or eventfd file descriptor.  When the mountpoint is ready to "
"be used, guestmount writes a single byte to this file descriptor.  This can "
"be used in conjunction with I<--no-fork> in order to run guestmount captive "
"under another process."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt kanāla vai eventfd failu deskriptoru.  Kad montēšanas punkts ir "
"gatavs lietošanai, guestmount ieraksta šajā failu deskriptorā vienu baitu.  "
"To var izmantot kopā ar I<--no-fork>, lai izpildītu guestmount kā cita "
"procesa gūstekni."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:230
msgid ""
"If you have untrusted raw-format guest disk images, you should use this "
"option to specify the disk format.  This avoids a possible security problem "
"with malicious guests (CVE-2010-3851).  See also "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts>."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir neuzticami raw formāta viesa disku attēli, šī opcija jāizmanto "
"diska formāta norādīšanai.  Tas novērš iespējamu drošības problēmu ar "
"ļaunprātīgiem viesiem (CVE-2010-3851).  Skatīt arī L<guestfs(3)/"
"guestfs_add_drive_opts>."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:235
msgid "B<--fuse-help>"
msgstr "B<--fuse-help>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:237
msgid "Display help on special FUSE options (see I<-o> below)."
msgstr "Parādīt palīdzību par īpašajām FUSE opcijām (skatiet I<-o> tālāk)."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:241 fuse/guestunmount.pod:81
msgid "Display brief help and exit."
msgstr "Parādīt īsu palīdzību un iziet."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:255
msgid "B<-m> dev[:mountpoint[:options[:fstype]]"
msgstr "B<-m> dev[:mountpoint[:options[:fstype]]"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:259 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:202
msgid ""
"Mount the named partition or logical volume on the given mountpoint B<in the "
"guest> (this has nothing to do with mountpoints in the host)."
msgstr ""
"Montēt nosaukto nodalījumu vai loģisko sējumu dotajā montēšanas punktā "
"B<viesī> (tam nav nekāda sakara ar montēšanas punktiem resursdatorā)."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:262 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:205
msgid ""
"If the mountpoint is omitted, it defaults to F</>.  You have to mount "
"something on F</>."
msgstr ""
"Ja montēšanas punkts izlaists, noklusējums ir F</>.  Kaut kas jāmontē F</>."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:280
msgid "B<--no-fork>"
msgstr "B<--no-fork>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:282
msgid "Don’t daemonize (or fork into the background)."
msgstr "Nekļūt par dēmonu (nesazaroties fonā)."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:288
msgid ""
"By default, we attempt to sync the guest disk when the FUSE mountpoint is "
"unmounted.  If you specify this option, then we don't attempt to sync the "
"disk.  See the discussion of autosync in the L<guestfs(3)> manpage."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma mēģinām sinhronizēt viesa disku, kad FUSE montēšanas punkts "
"tiek atmontēts.  Ja norādāt šo opciju, disku nemēģinām sinhronizēt.  Skatiet "
"automātiskās sinhronizācijas aplūkojumu L<guestfs(3)> rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:293
msgid "B<-o> OPTION"
msgstr "B<-o> OPTION"

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:295
msgid "B<--option> OPTION"
msgstr "B<--option> OPTION"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:297
msgid "Pass extra options to FUSE."
msgstr "Nodot FUSE papildu opcijas."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:299
msgid ""
"To get a list of all the extra options supported by FUSE, use the command "
"below.  Note that only the FUSE I<-o> options can be passed, and only some "
"of them are a good idea."
msgstr ""
"Lai iegūtu visu FUSE atbalstīto papildu opciju sarakstu, izmantojiet tālāk "
"doto komandu.  Ņemiet vērā, ka var nodot tikai FUSE I<-o> opcijas, un tikai "
"dažas no tām ir laba doma."

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:303
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestmount --fuse-help\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestmount --fuse-help\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:305
msgid "Some potentially useful FUSE options:"
msgstr "Dažas potenciāli noderīgas FUSE opcijas:"

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:309
msgid "B<-o> B<allow_other>"
msgstr "B<-o> B<allow_other>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:311
msgid ""
"Allow other users to see the filesystem.  This option has no effect unless "
"you enable it globally in F</etc/fuse.conf>."
msgstr ""
"Ļaut citiem lietotājiem redzēt failu sistēmu.  Šai opcijai nav ietekmes, ja "
"vien neiespējojat to globāli failā F</etc/fuse.conf>."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:314
msgid "B<-o> B<attr_timeout=N>"
msgstr "B<-o> B<attr_timeout=N>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:316
msgid "Enable attribute caching by FUSE, and set the timeout to I<N> seconds."
msgstr "Iespējot FUSE atribūtu kešošanu un iestatīt noildzi uz I<N> sekundēm."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:318
msgid "B<-o> B<kernel_cache>"
msgstr "B<-o> B<kernel_cache>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:320
msgid ""
"Allow the kernel to cache files (reduces the number of reads that have to go "
"through the L<guestfs(3)> API).  This is generally a good idea if you can "
"afford the extra memory usage."
msgstr ""
"Ļaut kodolam kešot failus (samazina lasīšanu skaitu, kam jāiet caur L<guestfs"
"(3)> API).  Parasti tā ir laba doma, ja varat atļauties papildu atmiņas "
"lietojumu."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:324
msgid "B<-o> B<uid=N> B<-o> B<gid=N>"
msgstr "B<-o> B<uid=N> B<-o> B<gid=N>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:326
msgid ""
"Use these options to map all UIDs and GIDs inside the guest filesystem to "
"the chosen values."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet šīs opcijas, lai kartētu visus UID un GID viesa failu sistēmā uz "
"izvēlētajām vērtībām."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:329
msgid "B<-o> B<use_ino>"
msgstr "B<-o> B<use_ino>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:331
msgid "Preserve inode numbers from the underlying filesystem."
msgstr "Saglabāt pamatā esošās failu sistēmas inode numurus."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:333
msgid ""
"Without this option, FUSE makes up its own inode numbers.  The inode numbers "
"you see in L<stat(2)>, C<ls -i> etc aren't the inode numbers of the "
"underlying filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Bez šīs opcijas FUSE izdomā savus inode numurus.  Inode numuri, ko redzat "
"L<stat(2)>, C<ls -i> u. c., nav pamatā esošās failu sistēmas inode numuri."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:337
msgid ""
"B<Note> this option is potentially dangerous if the underlying filesystem "
"consists of multiple mountpoints, as you may see duplicate inode numbers "
"appearing through FUSE.  Use of this option can confuse some software."
msgstr ""
"B<Ņemiet vērā>, ka šī opcija ir potenciāli bīstama, ja pamatā esošā failu "
"sistēma sastāv no vairākiem montēšanas punktiem, jo caur FUSE var parādīties "
"dublēti inode numuri.  Šīs opcijas izmantošana var mulsināt dažu "
"programmatūru."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:344
msgid "B<--pid-file> FILENAME"
msgstr "B<--pid-file> FILENAME"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:346
msgid "Write the PID of the guestmount worker process to C<filename>."
msgstr "Ierakstīt guestmount darba procesa PID failā C<filename>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:352
msgid ""
"Add devices and mount everything read-only.  Also disallow writes and make "
"the disk appear read-only to FUSE."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot ierīces un montēt visu tikai lasīšanai.  Arī aizliegt rakstīšanu "
"un likt diskam FUSE izskatīties tikai lasāmam."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:355
msgid ""
"This is highly recommended if you are not going to edit the guest disk.  If "
"the guest is running and this option is I<not> supplied, then there is a "
"strong risk of disk corruption in the guest.  We try to prevent this from "
"happening, but it is not always possible."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir ļoti ieteicams, ja neplānojat rediģēt viesa disku.  Ja viesis "
"darbojas un šī opcija I<nav> norādīta, pastāv liels viesa diska bojājuma "
"risks.  Cenšamies to novērst, bet tas ne vienmēr ir iespējams."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:360 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:239
msgid "See also L<guestfish(1)/OPENING DISKS FOR READ AND WRITE>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<guestfish(1)/DISKU ATVĒRŠANA LASĪŠANAI UN RAKSTĪŠANAI>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:370
msgid "Enable verbose messages from underlying libguestfs."
msgstr "Iespējot pamatā esošās libguestfs izvērstos ziņojumus."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:376 fuse/guestunmount.pod:109
msgid "Display the program version and exit."
msgstr "Parādīt programmas versiju un iziet."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:385 rescue/virt-rescue.pod:290
msgid "See L<guestfish(1)/OPENING DISKS FOR READ AND WRITE>."
msgstr "Skatiet L<guestfish(1)/DISKU ATVĒRŠANA LASĪŠANAI UN RAKSTĪŠANAI>."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:389
msgid "B<--trace>"
msgstr "B<--trace>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:391
msgid "Trace libguestfs calls and entry into each FUSE function."
msgstr "Izsekot libguestfs izsaukumus un ieeju katrā FUSE funkcijā."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:393
msgid ""
"This also stops the daemon from forking into the background (see "
"I<--no-fork>)."
msgstr "Tas arī neļauj dēmonam sazaroties fonā (skatiet I<--no-fork>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestmount.pod:424
msgid ""
"L<guestunmount(1)>, L<fusermount(1)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-inspector(1)>, "
"L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-tar(1)>, "
"L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>, L<guestfs(3)/MOUNT LOCAL>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://fuse.sf.net/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestunmount(1)>, L<fusermount(1)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-inspector(1)>, "
"L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-tar(1)>, L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>"
", L<guestfs(3)/LOKĀLĀ MONTĒŠANA>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://"
"fuse.sf.net/>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:3
msgid "guestunmount - Unmount a guestmounted filesystem"
msgstr "guestunmount - ar guestmount montētas failu sistēmas atmontēšana"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:7 fuse/guestunmount.pod:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestunmount mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestunmount mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestunmount --fd=<FD> mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestunmount --fd=<FD> mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:13
msgid ""
"guestunmount is a utility to clean up mounted filesystems automatically.  "
"L<guestmount(1)> mounts filesystems using libguestfs.  This program unmounts "
"the filesystem when a program or script has finished with it."
msgstr ""
"guestunmount ir utilīta montētu failu sistēmu automātiskai sakopšanai.  "
"L<guestmount(1)> montē failu sistēmas, izmantojot libguestfs.  Šī programma "
"atmontē failu sistēmu, kad programma vai skripts ar to ir beidzis darbu."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:18
msgid ""
"guestunmount is a wrapper around the FUSE L<fusermount(1)> program, which "
"must exist on the current C<PATH>."
msgstr ""
"guestunmount ir ietinējs ap FUSE programmu L<fusermount(1)>, kurai jāeksistē "
"pašreizējā C<PATH>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:21
msgid "There are two ways to use guestunmount.  When called as:"
msgstr "Ir divi veidi, kā izmantot guestunmount.  Ja izsaukts kā:"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:25
msgid "it unmounts C<mountpoint> immediately."
msgstr "tas uzreiz atmontē C<mountpoint>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:27
msgid "When called as:"
msgstr "Ja izsaukts kā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:29 fuse/guestunmount.pod:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestunmount --fd=FD mountpoint\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestunmount --fd=FD mountpoint\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:31
msgid ""
"it waits until the pipe C<FD> is closed.  This can be used to monitor "
"another process and clean up its mountpoint when that process exits, as "
"described below."
msgstr ""
"tas gaida, līdz kanāls C<FD> tiek aizvērts.  To var izmantot, lai uzraudzītu "
"citu procesu un sakoptu tā montēšanas punktu, kad šis process iziet, kā "
"aprakstīts tālāk."

#. type: =head2
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:35
msgid "FROM PROGRAMS"
msgstr "NO PROGRAMMĀM"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:37
msgid ""
"You can just call C<guestunmount mountpoint> from the program, but a more "
"sophisticated way to use guestunmount is to have it monitor your program so "
"it can clean up the mount point if your program exits unexpectedly."
msgstr ""
"No programmas varat vienkārši izsaukt C<guestunmount mountpoint>, bet "
"sarežģītāks veids, kā izmantot guestunmount, ir likt tam uzraudzīt jūsu "
"programmu, lai tas varētu sakopt montēšanas punktu, ja programma negaidīti "
"iziet."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:42
msgid ""
"In the program, create a pipe (eg. by calling L<pipe(2)>).  Let C<FD> be the "
"file descriptor number of the read side of the pipe (ie. C<pipefd[0]>)."
msgstr ""
"Programmā izveidojiet kanālu (piem., izsaucot L<pipe(2)>).  Lai C<FD> ir "
"kanāla lasīšanas puses failu deskriptora numurs (t. i., C<pipefd[0]>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:46
msgid ""
"After mounting the filesystem with L<guestmount(1)> (on C<mountpoint>), fork "
"and run guestunmount like this:"
msgstr ""
"Pēc failu sistēmas montēšanas ar L<guestmount(1)> (uz C<mountpoint>) "
"sazarojiet un izpildiet guestunmount šādi:"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:51
msgid "Close the read side of the pipe in the parent process."
msgstr "Vecākprocesā aizveriet kanāla lasīšanas pusi."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:53
msgid ""
"Now, when the write side of the pipe (ie. C<pipefd[1]>) is closed for any "
"reason, either explicitly or because the parent process exits, guestunmount "
"notices and unmounts the mountpoint."
msgstr ""
"Tagad, kad kanāla rakstīšanas puse (t. i., C<pipefd[1]>) jebkāda iemesla dēļ "
"tiek aizvērta — vai nu eksplicīti, vai tāpēc, ka vecākprocess iziet —, "
"guestunmount to pamana un atmontē montēšanas punktu."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:57
msgid ""
"If your operating system supports it, you should set the C<FD_CLOEXEC> flag "
"on the write side of the pipe.  This is so that other child processes don't "
"inherit the file descriptor and keep it open."
msgstr ""
"Ja jūsu operētājsistēma to atbalsta, kanāla rakstīšanas pusei jāiestata "
"karogs C<FD_CLOEXEC>.  Tas ir tāpēc, lai citi bērnprocesi nemantotu failu "
"deskriptoru un neturētu to atvērtu."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:61
msgid "Guestunmount never daemonizes itself."
msgstr "Guestunmount nekad nekļūst par dēmonu."

#. type: =head2
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:63
msgid "FROM SHELL SCRIPTS"
msgstr "NO ČAULAS SKRIPTIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:65
msgid ""
"Since bash doesn't provide a way to create an unnamed pipe, use a trap to "
"call guestunmount on exit like this:"
msgstr ""
"Tā kā bash nenodrošina veidu, kā izveidot nenosauktu kanālu, izmantojiet "
"trap, lai iziešanas brīdī izsauktu guestunmount šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" trap \"guestunmount mountpoint\" EXIT INT QUIT TERM\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" trap \"guestunmount mountpoint\" EXIT INT QUIT TERM\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:74
msgid "B<--fd=FD>"
msgstr "B<--fd=FD>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:76
msgid ""
"Specify the pipe file descriptor to monitor, and delay cleanup until that "
"pipe is closed."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt uzraugāmā kanāla failu deskriptoru un aizkavēt sakopšanu, līdz šis "
"kanāls tiek aizvērts."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:83
msgid "B<-q>"
msgstr "B<-q>"

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:85
msgid "B<--quiet>"
msgstr "B<--quiet>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:87
msgid ""
"Don’t display error messages from fusermount.  The return status is still "
"set (see L</EXIT STATUS> below)."
msgstr ""
"Nerādīt fusermount kļūdu ziņojumus.  Atgriešanas statuss joprojām tiek "
"iestatīts (skatiet L</IZEJAS STATUSS> tālāk)."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:90
msgid "B<--no-retry>"
msgstr "B<--no-retry>"

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:92
msgid "B<--retry=N>"
msgstr "B<--retry=N>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:94
msgid ""
"By default, guestunmount will retry the fusermount operation up to S<5 "
"times> (that is, it will run it up to S<6 times> = S<1 try> + S<5 retries>)."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma guestunmount atkārtos fusermount darbību līdz S<5 reizēm> "
"(t. i., izpildīs to līdz S<6 reizēm> = S<1 mēģinājums> + S<5 atkārtojumi>)."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:98
msgid "Use I<--no-retry> to make guestunmount run fusermount only once."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet I<--no-retry>, lai guestunmount izpildītu fusermount tikai "
"vienreiz."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:100
msgid "Use I<--retry=N> to make guestunmount retry C<N> times instead of 5."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet I<--retry=N>, lai guestunmount atkārtotu C<N> reizes, nevis 5."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:102
msgid ""
"guestunmount performs an exponential back-off between retries, waiting S<1 "
"second>, S<2 seconds>, S<4 seconds>, etc before each retry."
msgstr ""
"guestunmount starp atkārtojumiem veic eksponenciālu atkāpšanos, pirms katra "
"atkārtojuma gaidot S<1 sekundi>, S<2 sekundes>, S<4 sekundes> u. c."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:117
msgid "C<PATH>"
msgstr "C<PATH>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:119
msgid ""
"The L<fusermount(1)> program (supplied by FUSE) must be available on the "
"current C<PATH>."
msgstr ""
"Programmai L<fusermount(1)> (ko nodrošina FUSE) jābūt pieejamai pašreizējā "
"C<PATH>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:126
msgid "This program returns 0 if successful, or one of the following error codes:"
msgstr ""
"Šī programma atgriež 0 veiksmes gadījumā vai vienu no šiem kļūdu kodiem:"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:133
msgid ""
"Program error, eg. could not allocate memory, could not run fusermount.  See "
"the error message printed for more information."
msgstr ""
"Programmas kļūda, piem., nevarēja piešķirt atmiņu, nevarēja izpildīt "
"fusermount.  Plašāku informāciju skatiet izdrukātajā kļūdas ziņojumā."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:136
msgid "C<2>"
msgstr "C<2>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:138
msgid ""
"The mount point could not be unmounted even after retrying.  See the error "
"message printed for the underlying fusermount error."
msgstr ""
"Montēšanas punktu nevarēja atmontēt pat pēc atkārtojumiem.  Pamatā esošo "
"fusermount kļūdu skatiet izdrukātajā kļūdas ziņojumā."

#. type: =item
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:141
msgid "C<3>"
msgstr "C<3>"

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:143
msgid "The mount point is not mounted."
msgstr "Montēšanas punkts nav montēts."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:149
msgid ""
"L<guestmount(1)>, L<fusermount(1)>, L<pipe(2)>, L<guestfs(3)/MOUNT LOCAL>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://fuse.sf.net/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestmount(1)>, L<fusermount(1)>, L<pipe(2)>, L<guestfs(3)/LOKĀLĀ "
"MONTĒŠANA>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://fuse.sf.net/>."

#. type: textblock
#: fuse/guestunmount.pod:162 golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:97
msgid "Copyright (C) 2013 Red Hat Inc."
msgstr "Copyright (C) 2013 Red Hat Inc."

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-golang - How to use libguestfs from Go"
msgstr "guestfs-golang - kā izmantot libguestfs no Go"

#. type: verbatim
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" import \"libguestfs.org/guestfs\"\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" import \"libguestfs.org/guestfs\"\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" g, errno := guestfs.Create ()\n"
" if errno != nil {\n"
"     panic (fmt.Sprintf (\"could not create handle: %s\", errno))\n"
" }\n"
" defer g.Close ()\n"
" if err := g.Add_drive (\"test.img\"); err != nil {\n"
"     panic (err)\n"
" }\n"
" if err := g.Launch (); err != nil {\n"
"     panic (err)\n"
" }\n"
" if err := g.Shutdown (); err != nil {\n"
"     panic (err)\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" g, errno := guestfs.Create ()\n"
" if errno != nil {\n"
"     panic (fmt.Sprintf (\"could not create handle: %s\", errno))\n"
" }\n"
" defer g.Close ()\n"
" if err := g.Add_drive (\"test.img\"); err != nil {\n"
"     panic (err)\n"
" }\n"
" if err := g.Launch (); err != nil {\n"
"     panic (err)\n"
" }\n"
" if err := g.Shutdown (); err != nil {\n"
"     panic (err)\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:26
msgid ""
"This manual page documents how to call libguestfs from the Go programming "
"language.  This page just documents the differences from the C API and gives "
"some examples.  If you are not familiar with using libguestfs, you also need "
"to read L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā dokumentēts, kā izsaukt libguestfs no programmēšanas "
"valodas Go.  Šajā lapā dokumentētas tikai atšķirības no C API un doti daži "
"piemēri.  Ja libguestfs izmantošana jums nav pazīstama, jāizlasa arī "
"L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:31
msgid "IMPORTING THE MODULE"
msgstr "MODUĻA IMPORTĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:33
msgid ""
"The module is called C<guestfs>.  The full package name to import is "
"C<libguestfs.org/guestfs>."
msgstr ""
"Moduļa nosaukums ir C<guestfs>.  Pilns importējamās pakotnes nosaukums ir "
"C<libguestfs.org/guestfs>."

#. type: =head2
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:36
msgid "CREATING AND CLOSING THE HANDLE"
msgstr "ROKTURA IZVEIDE UN AIZVĒRŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:38
msgid ""
"Use either C<guestfs.Create> or C<guestfs.Create_flags> to create the "
"handle.  The handle is closed implicitly if it is garbage collected.  "
"However it is probably a good idea to close it explicitly, either by calling "
"S<C<g.Close ()>> or by deferring the same."
msgstr ""
"Roktura izveidei izmantojiet C<guestfs.Create> vai C<guestfs.Create_flags>.  "
"Rokturis tiek aizvērts netieši, ja to savāc atkritumu savācējs.  Tomēr, "
"iespējams, ir laba doma to aizvērt eksplicīti, vai nu izsaucot S<C<g.Close "
"()>>, vai to atliekot (defer)."

#. type: =head2
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:43 lua/examples/guestfs-lua.pod:74
#: perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:25
msgid "ERRORS"
msgstr "KĻŪDAS"

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:45
msgid ""
"C<guestfs.Create> and C<guestfs.Create_flags> return a simple C<*error>, "
"which is really just a C C<errno> wrapped up in the appropriate golang "
"struct."
msgstr ""
"C<guestfs.Create> un C<guestfs.Create_flags> atgriež vienkāršu C<*error>, "
"kas patiesībā ir tikai C C<errno>, ietīts atbilstošā golang struktūrā."

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:49
msgid ""
"All other calls return a C<*GuestfsError> which (if non-nil) is a richer "
"struct that contains the error string from libguestfs, the errno (if "
"available) and the operation which failed.  This can also be converted to a "
"string for display."
msgstr ""
"Visi pārējie izsaukumi atgriež C<*GuestfsError>, kas (ja nav nil) ir "
"bagātāka struktūra, kas satur kļūdas virkni no libguestfs, errno (ja "
"pieejams) un neizdevušos darbību.  To var arī pārvērst virknē attēlošanai."

#. type: =head2
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:54
msgid "LIMITATIONS"
msgstr "IEROBEŽOJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:60
msgid "No support for events (see L<guestfs(3)/EVENTS>)."
msgstr "Nav notikumu atbalsta (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/NOTIKUMI>)."

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:64
msgid "UUIDs are not returned in structures."
msgstr "UUID netiek atgriezti struktūrās."

#. type: textblock
#: golang/examples/guestfs-golang.pod:78
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://www.golang.org/>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-java"
"(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-"
"python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://"
"www.golang.org/>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-java - How to use libguestfs from Java"
msgstr "guestfs-java - kā izmantot libguestfs no Java"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" import com.redhat.et.libguestfs.*;\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" import com.redhat.et.libguestfs.*;\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" GuestFS g = new GuestFS ();\n"
" g.add_drive (\"disk.img\",\n"
"              new HashMap<String,Object>() {\n"
"                {\n"
"                    put (\"readonly\", Boolean.TRUE);\n"
"                    put (\"format\", \"raw\");\n"
"                }\n"
"              });\n"
" g.launch ();\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" GuestFS g = new GuestFS ();\n"
" g.add_drive (\"disk.img\",\n"
"              new HashMap<String,Object>() {\n"
"                {\n"
"                    put (\"readonly\", Boolean.TRUE);\n"
"                    put (\"format\", \"raw\");\n"
"                }\n"
"              });\n"
" g.launch ();\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:21
msgid ""
"This manual page documents how to call libguestfs from the Java programming "
"language.  This page just documents the differences from the C API and gives "
"some examples.  If you are not familiar with using libguestfs, you also need "
"to read L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā dokumentēts, kā izsaukt libguestfs no programmēšanas "
"valodas Java.  Šajā lapā dokumentētas tikai atšķirības no C API un doti daži "
"piemēri.  Ja libguestfs izmantošana jums nav pazīstama, jāizlasa arī "
"L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:26 ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:51
msgid "CLOSING THE HANDLE"
msgstr "ROKTURA AIZVĒRŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:28
msgid ""
"The handle is closed when it is reaped by the garbage collector.  Because "
"libguestfs handles include a lot of state, it is also possible to close (and "
"hence free) them explicitly by calling the C<close> method."
msgstr ""
"Rokturis tiek aizvērts, kad to savāc atkritumu savācējs.  Tā kā libguestfs "
"rokturi ietver daudz stāvokļa, tos var arī aizvērt (un līdz ar to atbrīvot) "
"eksplicīti, izsaucot metodi C<close>."

#. type: =head2
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:33 ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:58
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:30 ruby/examples/guestfs-ruby.pod:20
msgid "EXCEPTIONS"
msgstr "IZŅĒMUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:35
msgid ""
"Errors from libguestfs functions are mapped into the C<LibGuestFSException> "
"exception.  This has a single parameter which is the error message (a "
"C<String>)."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas no libguestfs funkcijām tiek kartētas uz izņēmumu "
"C<LibGuestFSException>.  Tam ir viens parametrs, kas ir kļūdas ziņojums "
"(C<String>)."

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:39
msgid "Calling any method on a closed handle raises the same exception."
msgstr ""
"Jebkuras metodes izsaukšana aizvērtam rokturim izraisa to pašu izņēmumu."

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:41
msgid ""
"If L<malloc(3)> or some other allocation fails inside the bindings, the "
"C<LibGuestFSOutOfMemory> exception is thrown."
msgstr ""
"Ja L<malloc(3)> vai kāda cita piešķiršana saistījumos neizdodas, tiek "
"izmests izņēmums C<LibGuestFSOutOfMemory>."

#. type: =head2
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:44 lib/guestfs.pod:2251
#: lua/examples/guestfs-lua.pod:98
msgid "EVENTS"
msgstr "NOTIKUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:46
msgid ""
"The L<libguestfs event API|guestfs(3)/EVENTS> is fully supported from Java.  "
"Create a class which implements the C<EventCallback> interface, create an "
"instance of this class, and then call the C<GuestFS#set_event_callback> "
"method to register this instance.  The C<event> method of the class is "
"called when libguestfs generates an event."
msgstr ""
"L<libguestfs notikumu API|guestfs(3)/EVENTS> tiek pilnībā atbalstīta no "
"Java.  Izveidojiet klasi, kas realizē saskarni C<EventCallback>, izveidojiet "
"šīs klases instanci un tad izsauciet metodi C<GuestFS#set_event_callback>, "
"lai reģistrētu šo instanci.  Klases metode C<event> tiek izsaukta, kad "
"libguestfs ģenerē notikumu."

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:52
msgid "For example, this will print all trace events:"
msgstr "Piemēram, šis izdrukās visus izsekošanas notikumus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" GuestFS g = new GuestFS ();\n"
" g.set_trace (true);\n"
" g.set_event_callback (\n"
"   new EventCallback () {\n"
"     public void event (long event, int eh,\n"
"                        String buffer, long[] array) {\n"
"       System.out.println (GuestFS.eventToString (event) +\n"
"                           \": \" + buffer);\n"
"     }\n"
"   },\n"
"   GuestFS.EVENT_TRACE);\n"
" g.add_drive_ro (\"disk.img\");\n"
" // etc.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" GuestFS g = new GuestFS ();\n"
" g.set_trace (true);\n"
" g.set_event_callback (\n"
"   new EventCallback () {\n"
"     public void event (long event, int eh,\n"
"                        String buffer, long[] array) {\n"
"       System.out.println (GuestFS.eventToString (event) +\n"
"                           \": \" + buffer);\n"
"     }\n"
"   },\n"
"   GuestFS.EVENT_TRACE);\n"
" g.add_drive_ro (\"disk.img\");\n"
" // etc.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:68
msgid "The output looks similar to this:"
msgstr "Izvade izskatās līdzīgi šai:"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" EVENT_TRACE: add_drive_ro \"disk.img\"\n"
" EVENT_TRACE: add_drive_ro = 0\n"
" // etc.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" EVENT_TRACE: add_drive_ro \"disk.img\"\n"
" EVENT_TRACE: add_drive_ro = 0\n"
" // etc.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:76
msgid ""
"Some methods take an optional map of optional parameters.  An example of "
"this is C<g.add_drive> which can be called in one of two ways:"
msgstr ""
"Dažas metodes pieņem neobligātu neobligāto parametru karti.  Piemērs ir "
"C<g.add_drive>, ko var izsaukt vienā no diviem veidiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" g.add_drive (\"disk.img\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" g.add_drive (\"disk.img\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:81
msgid "or with optional arguments:"
msgstr "vai ar neobligātiem argumentiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Map<String, Object> optargs =\n"
"   new HashMap<String, Object>() {\n"
"   {\n"
"     put (\"readonly\", Boolean.TRUE);\n"
"     put (\"format\", \"raw\");\n"
"   }\n"
" };\n"
" g.add_drive (\"disk.img\", optargs);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Map<String, Object> optargs =\n"
"   new HashMap<String, Object>() {\n"
"   {\n"
"     put (\"readonly\", Boolean.TRUE);\n"
"     put (\"format\", \"raw\");\n"
"   }\n"
" };\n"
" g.add_drive (\"disk.img\", optargs);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:92
msgid ""
"For more information on this topic, see L<guestfs(3)/CALLS WITH OPTIONAL "
"ARGUMENTS>."
msgstr ""
"Plašāku informāciju par šo tēmu skatiet L<guestfs(3)/IZSAUKUMI AR "
"NEOBLIGĀTIEM ARGUMENTIEM>."

#. type: =head3
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:95
msgid "Optional handle parameters"
msgstr "Neobligātie roktura parametri"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:97
msgid "When creating the handle you can also pass a map of optional parameters:"
msgstr "Veidojot rokturi, var nodot arī neobligāto parametru karti:"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:100
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Map<String, Object> optargs =\n"
"   new HashMap<String, Object>() {\n"
"   {\n"
"     put (\"close_on_exit\", Boolean.FALSE);\n"
"     put (\"environment\", Boolean.TRUE);\n"
"   }\n"
" };\n"
" GuestFS g = new GuestFS (optargs);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Map<String, Object> optargs =\n"
"   new HashMap<String, Object>() {\n"
"   {\n"
"     put (\"close_on_exit\", Boolean.FALSE);\n"
"     put (\"environment\", Boolean.TRUE);\n"
"   }\n"
" };\n"
" GuestFS g = new GuestFS (optargs);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:109
msgid "For more information, see L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_create_flags>."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_create_flags>."

#. type: =head1
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:111
msgid "COMPILING AND RUNNING"
msgstr "KOMPILĒŠANA UN PALAIŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:113
msgid ""
"Libguestfs for Java is a Java Native Interface (JNI) extension, supplied in "
"three parts:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs Java valodai ir Java Native Interface (JNI) paplašinājums, kas "
"tiek piegādāts trīs daļās:"

#. type: =item
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:118
msgid "F<libguestfs.jar>"
msgstr "F<libguestfs.jar>"

#. type: =item
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:120
msgid "F<libguestfs-I<VERSION>.jar>"
msgstr "F<libguestfs-I<VERSION>.jar>"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:122
msgid ""
"The pure Java JAR file which contains several classes, the primary one being "
"C<com.redhat.et.libguestfs.GuestFS>.  Upstream, the JAR file contains a "
"version number in the filename, but some Linux distros may rename it without "
"the version number."
msgstr ""
"Tīrais Java JAR fails, kas satur vairākas klases, galvenā no tām ir "
"C<com.redhat.et.libguestfs.GuestFS>.  Augštecē JAR faila nosaukumā ir "
"versijas numurs, taču dažas Linux distribūcijas to var pārdēvēt bez versijas "
"numura."

#. type: =item
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:127
msgid "F<libguestfs_jni.so>"
msgstr "F<libguestfs_jni.so>"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:129
msgid ""
"The JNI code (written in C).  This contains private native functions that "
"interface between Java code and the regular libguestfs C library.  You "
"should B<not> call these directly."
msgstr ""
"JNI kods (rakstīts C valodā).  Tas satur privātas vietējās funkcijas, kas "
"nodrošina saskarni starp Java kodu un parasto libguestfs C bibliotēku.  Tās "
"B<nevajadzētu> izsaukt tieši."

#. type: =item
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:133
msgid "F<libguestfs.so>"
msgstr "F<libguestfs.so>"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:135
msgid "The regular libguestfs C library."
msgstr "Parastā libguestfs C bibliotēka."

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:139
msgid ""
"To compile your Java program, you need to locate the JAR file and add it to "
"the class path.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Lai kompilētu savu Java programmu, jāatrod JAR fails un jāpievieno tas klašu "
"ceļam.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:142
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export CLASSPATH=/usr/share/java/libguestfs.jar\n"
" javac MyProgram.java\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export CLASSPATH=/usr/share/java/libguestfs.jar\n"
" javac MyProgram.java\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:145
msgid ""
"To run your Java program, you also need to ensure that the JAR file is on "
"the class path, as well as the path of your program.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izpildītu savu Java programmu, arī jānodrošina, ka JAR fails ir klašu "
"ceļā, kā arī jūsu programmas ceļš.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export CLASSPATH=.:/usr/share/java/libguestfs.jar\n"
" java MyProgram\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export CLASSPATH=.:/usr/share/java/libguestfs.jar\n"
" java MyProgram\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: java/examples/guestfs-java.pod:161
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-golang(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://caml.inria.fr/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-golang"
"(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-"
"python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>, L<http://caml.inria.fr/>."

