#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6727
msgid ""
"This function is a helpful wrapper around C<guestfs_inotify_read> which just "
"returns a list of pathnames of objects that were touched.  The returned "
"pathnames are sorted and deduplicated."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija ir noderīgs ietinējs ap C<guestfs_inotify_read>, kas vienkārši "
"atgriež aizskarto objektu ceļu nosaukumu sarakstu.  Atgrieztie ceļu "
"nosaukumi ir sakārtoti un bez dublikātiem."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6740
msgid "guestfs_inotify_init"
msgstr "guestfs_inotify_init"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6742
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" guestfs_inotify_init (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                       int maxevents);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" guestfs_inotify_init (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                       int maxevents);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6750
msgid ""
"C<maxevents> is the maximum number of events which will be queued up between "
"calls to C<guestfs_inotify_read> or C<guestfs_inotify_files>.  If this is "
"passed as C<0>, then the kernel (or previously set)  default is used.  For "
"Linux 2.6.29 the default was 16384 events.  Beyond this limit, the kernel "
"throws away events, but records the fact that it threw them away by setting "
"a flag C<IN_Q_OVERFLOW> in the returned structure list (see "
"C<guestfs_inotify_read>)."
msgstr ""
"C<maxevents> ir maksimālais notikumu skaits, kas tiks ierindots starp "
"C<guestfs_inotify_read> vai C<guestfs_inotify_files> izsaukumiem.  Ja tas "
"nodots kā C<0>, tiek izmantots kodola (vai iepriekš iestatītais) "
"noklusējums.  Linux 2.6.29 noklusējums bija 16384 notikumi.  Pārsniedzot šo "
"ierobežojumu, kodols izmet notikumus, bet fiksē faktu, ka tos izmeta, "
"iestatot karogu C<IN_Q_OVERFLOW> atgrieztajā struktūru sarakstā (skatiet "
"C<guestfs_inotify_read>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6760
msgid ""
"Before any events are generated, you have to add some watches to the "
"internal watch list.  See: C<guestfs_inotify_add_watch> and "
"C<guestfs_inotify_rm_watch>."
msgstr ""
"Pirms tiek ģenerēti jebkādi notikumi, iekšējam vērošanas sarakstam "
"jāpievieno dažas vērošanas.  Skatiet: C<guestfs_inotify_add_watch> un "
"C<guestfs_inotify_rm_watch>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6764
msgid ""
"Queued up events should be read periodically by calling "
"C<guestfs_inotify_read> (or C<guestfs_inotify_files> which is just a helpful "
"wrapper around C<guestfs_inotify_read>).  If you don't read the events out "
"often enough then you risk the internal queue overflowing."
msgstr ""
"Ierindotie notikumi periodiski jānolasa, izsaucot C<guestfs_inotify_read> "
"(vai C<guestfs_inotify_files>, kas ir tikai noderīgs ietinējs ap "
"C<guestfs_inotify_read>).  Ja notikumus nenolasāt pietiekami bieži, riskējat "
"ar iekšējās rindas pārpildi."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:6771
msgid ""
"The handle should be closed after use by calling C<guestfs_inotify_close>.  "
"This also removes any watches automatically."
msgstr ""
"Pēc lietošanas rokturis jāaizver, izsaucot C<guestfs_inotify_close>.  Tas "
"arī automātiski noņem visas vērošanas."

