"                     char *const *names);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" struct guestfs_xattr_list *\n"
" guestfs_lxattrlist (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                     const char *path,\n"
"                     char *const *names);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10051
msgid ""
"On return you get a flat list of xattr structs which must be interpreted "
"sequentially.  The first xattr struct always has a zero-length C<attrname>.  "
"C<attrval> in this struct is zero-length to indicate there was an error "
"doing C<guestfs_lgetxattr> for this file, I<or> is a C string which is a "
"decimal number (the number of following attributes for this file, which "
"could be C<\"0\">).  Then after the first xattr struct are the zero or more "
"attributes for the first named file.  This repeats for the second and "
"subsequent files."
msgstr ""
"Atgriežot saņemat plakanu xattr struktūru sarakstu, kas jāinterpretē "
"secīgi.  Pirmajai xattr struktūrai vienmēr ir nulles garuma C<attrname>.  "
"C<attrval> šajā struktūrā ir nulles garuma, lai norādītu, ka šim failam, "
"veicot C<guestfs_lgetxattr>, radās kļūda, I<vai> ir C virkne, kas ir "
"decimāls skaitlis (sekojošo atribūtu skaits šim failam, kas var būt C<\"0\">)"
".  Pēc pirmās xattr struktūras seko nulle vai vairāk pirmā nosauktā faila "
"atribūtu.  Tas atkārtojas otrajam un nākamajiem failiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10061
msgid ""
"This call is intended for programs that want to efficiently list a directory "
"contents without making many round-trips.  See also C<guestfs_lstatlist> for "
"a similarly efficient call for getting standard stats."
msgstr ""
"Šis izsaukums paredzēts programmām, kas vēlas efektīvi uzskaitīt "
"direktorijas saturu bez daudzām turp-atpakaļ apmaiņām.  Skatīt arī "
"C<guestfs_lstatlist> līdzīgi efektīvam izsaukumam standarta stat iegūšanai."

