#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10860
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_mkmountpoint> and C<guestfs_rmmountpoint> are specialized calls "
"that can be used to create extra mountpoints before mounting the first "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""
"C<guestfs_mkmountpoint> un C<guestfs_rmmountpoint> ir specializēti "
"izsaukumi, ko var izmantot papildu montēšanas punktu izveidei pirms pirmās "
"failu sistēmas montēšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10884
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_mkmountpoint> is not compatible with C<guestfs_umount_all>.  You "
"may get unexpected errors if you try to mix these calls.  It is safest to "
"manually unmount filesystems and remove mountpoints after use."
msgstr ""
"C<guestfs_mkmountpoint> nav saderīgs ar C<guestfs_umount_all>.  Ja "
"mēģināsiet jaukt šos izsaukumus, varat saņemt negaidītas kļūdas.  Visdrošāk "
"ir pēc lietošanas manuāli atmontēt failu sistēmas un noņemt montēšanas "
"punktus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10888
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_umount_all> unmounts filesystems by sorting the paths longest "
"first, so for this to work for manual mountpoints, you must ensure that the "
"innermost mountpoints have the longest pathnames, as in the example code "
"above."
msgstr ""
"C<guestfs_umount_all> atmontē failu sistēmas, kārtojot ceļus no garākā, "
"tāpēc, lai tas darbotos ar manuāliem montēšanas punktiem, jānodrošina, ka "
"visdziļākajiem montēšanas punktiem ir garākie ceļu nosaukumi, kā iepriekšējā "
"koda piemērā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10895
msgid ""
"Autosync [see C<guestfs_set_autosync>, this is set by default on handles] "
"can cause C<guestfs_umount_all> to be called when the handle is closed which "
"can also trigger these issues."
msgstr ""
"Automātiskā sinhronizācija [skatiet C<guestfs_set_autosync>, rokturiem tā ir "
"iestatīta pēc noklusējuma] var izraisīt C<guestfs_umount_all> izsaukšanu, "
"kad rokturis tiek aizvērts, kas arī var izraisīt šīs problēmas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10901 lib/guestfs-actions.pod:11552
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:13218
msgid "(Added in 1.0.62)"
msgstr "(Pievienots versijā 1.0.62)"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10903
msgid "guestfs_mknod"
msgstr "guestfs_mknod"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10905
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int\n"
" guestfs_mknod (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                int mode,\n"
"                int devmajor,\n"
"                int devminor,\n"
"                const char *path);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int\n"
" guestfs_mknod (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                int mode,\n"
"                int devmajor,\n"
"                int devminor,\n"
"                const char *path);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs-actions.pod:10920
msgid ""
"Note that, just like L<mknod(2)>, the mode must be bitwise OR'd with "
"S_IFBLK, S_IFCHR, S_IFIFO or S_IFSOCK (otherwise this call just creates a "
"regular file).  These constants are available in the standard Linux header "
"files, or you can use C<guestfs_mknod_b>, C<guestfs_mknod_c> or "
"C<guestfs_mkfifo> which are wrappers around this command which bitwise OR in "
"the appropriate constant for you."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, tāpat kā L<mknod(2)>, režīms bitu līmenī jāapvieno ar OR ar "
"S_IFBLK, S_IFCHR, S_IFIFO vai S_IFSOCK (citādi šis izsaukums vienkārši "
"izveido parastu failu).  Šīs konstantes ir pieejamas standarta Linux "
"galvenes failos, vai varat izmantot C<guestfs_mknod_b>, C<guestfs_mknod_c> "
"vai C<guestfs_mkfifo>, kas ir ietinēji ap šo komandu un jūsu vietā bitu "
"līmenī pievieno ar OR atbilstošo konstanti."

