#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:80
msgid "API OVERVIEW"
msgstr "API PĀRSKATS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:82
msgid ""
"This section provides a gentler overview of the libguestfs API.  We also try "
"to group API calls together, where that may not be obvious from reading "
"about the individual calls in the main section of this manual."
msgstr ""
"Šī sadaļa sniedz saudzīgāku libguestfs API pārskatu.  Mēs arī cenšamies "
"grupēt API izsaukumus kopā, ja tas var nebūt acīmredzams, lasot par "
"atsevišķiem izsaukumiem šīs rokasgrāmatas galvenajā sadaļā."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:87
msgid "HANDLES"
msgstr "ROKTURI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:89
msgid ""
"Before you can use libguestfs calls, you have to create a handle.  Then you "
"must add at least one disk image to the handle, followed by launching the "
"handle, then performing whatever operations you want, and finally closing "
"the handle.  By convention we use the single letter C<g> for the name of the "
"handle variable, although of course you can use any name you want."
msgstr ""
"Pirms varat izmantot libguestfs izsaukumus, jāizveido rokturis.  Pēc tam "
"rokturim jāpievieno vismaz viens diska attēls, tad rokturis jāpalaiž, jāveic "
"vajadzīgās darbības un visbeidzot rokturis jāaizver.  Pēc vienošanās roktura "
"mainīgajam izmantojam vienu burtu C<g>, lai gan, protams, varat izmantot "
"jebkuru nosaukumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:96
msgid "The general structure of all libguestfs-using programs looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Visu libguestfs izmantojošo programmu vispārējā struktūra izskatās šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:99
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_h *g = guestfs_create ();\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_h *g = guestfs_create ();\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Call guestfs_add_drive additional times if there are\n"
"  * multiple disk images.\n"
"  */\n"
" guestfs_add_drive (g, \"guest.img\");\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* Call guestfs_add_drive additional times if there are\n"
"  * multiple disk images.\n"
"  */\n"
" guestfs_add_drive (g, \"guest.img\");\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Most manipulation calls won't work until you've launched\n"
"  * the handle 'g'.  You have to do this _after_ adding drives\n"
"  * and _before_ other commands.\n"
"  */\n"
" guestfs_launch (g);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* Most manipulation calls won't work until you've launched\n"
"  * the handle 'g'.  You have to do this _after_ adding drives\n"
"  * and _before_ other commands.\n"
"  */\n"
" guestfs_launch (g);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Either: examine what partitions, LVs etc are available: */\n"
" char **partitions = guestfs_list_partitions (g);\n"
" char **logvols = guestfs_lvs (g);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* Either: examine what partitions, LVs etc are available: */\n"
" char **partitions = guestfs_list_partitions (g);\n"
" char **logvols = guestfs_lvs (g);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:116
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Or: ask libguestfs to find filesystems for you: */\n"
" char **filesystems = guestfs_list_filesystems (g);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* Or: ask libguestfs to find filesystems for you: */\n"
" char **filesystems = guestfs_list_filesystems (g);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:119
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Or: use inspection (see INSPECTION section below). */\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* Or: use inspection (see INSPECTION section below). */\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* To access a filesystem in the image, you must mount it. */\n"
" guestfs_mount (g, \"/dev/sda1\", \"/\");\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* To access a filesystem in the image, you must mount it. */\n"
" guestfs_mount (g, \"/dev/sda1\", \"/\");\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Now you can perform filesystem actions on the guest\n"
"  * disk image.\n"
"  */\n"
" guestfs_touch (g, \"/hello\");\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* Now you can perform filesystem actions on the guest\n"
"  * disk image.\n"
"  */\n"
" guestfs_touch (g, \"/hello\");\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Synchronize the disk.  This is the opposite of guestfs_launch. */\n"
" guestfs_shutdown (g);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* Synchronize the disk.  This is the opposite of guestfs_launch. */\n"
" guestfs_shutdown (g);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:132
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* Close and free the handle 'g'. */\n"
" guestfs_close (g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /* Close and free the handle 'g'. */\n"
" guestfs_close (g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:135
msgid ""
"The code above doesn't include any error checking.  In real code you should "
"check return values carefully for errors.  In general all functions that "
"return integers return C<-1> on error, and all functions that return "
"pointers return C<NULL> on error.  See section L</ERROR HANDLING> below for "
"how to handle errors, and consult the documentation for each function call "
"below to see precisely how they return error indications."
msgstr ""
"Iepriekšējais kods neietver nekādu kļūdu pārbaudi.  Reālā kodā atgriešanas "
"vērtības rūpīgi jāpārbauda attiecībā uz kļūdām.  Parasti visas funkcijas, "
"kas atgriež veselus skaitļus, kļūdas gadījumā atgriež C<-1>, un visas "
"funkcijas, kas atgriež rādītājus, kļūdas gadījumā atgriež C<NULL>.  Kā "
"apstrādāt kļūdas, skatiet sadaļu L</KĻŪDU APSTRĀDE> tālāk, un, lai precīzi "
"uzzinātu, kā katrs funkcijas izsaukums norāda kļūdu, skatiet tā "
"dokumentāciju tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:143
msgid ""
"The code above does not L<free(3)> the strings and arrays returned from "
"functions.  Consult the documentation for each function to find out how to "
"free the return value."
msgstr ""
"Iepriekšējais kods neizpilda L<free(3)> no funkcijām atgrieztajām virknēm un "
"masīviem.  Kā atbrīvot atgriešanas vērtību, skatiet katras funkcijas "
"dokumentācijā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:147
msgid "See L<guestfs-examples(3)> for fully worked examples."
msgstr "Pilnībā izstrādātus piemērus skatiet L<guestfs-examples(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:149
msgid "DISK IMAGES"
msgstr "DISKU ATTĒLI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:151
msgid ""
"The image filename (C<\"guest.img\"> in the example above) could be a disk "
"image from a virtual machine, a L<dd(1)> copy of a physical hard disk, an "
"actual block device, or simply an empty file of zeroes that you have created "
"through L<posix_fallocate(3)>.  Libguestfs lets you do useful things to all "
"of these."
msgstr ""
"Attēla faila nosaukums (iepriekšējā piemērā C<\"guest.img\">) var būt "
"virtuālās mašīnas diska attēls, fiziska cietā diska L<dd(1)> kopija, īsta "
"bloku ierīce vai vienkārši tukšs nulļu fails, kas izveidots ar "
"L<posix_fallocate(3)>.  Libguestfs ļauj ar tiem visiem darīt noderīgas "
"lietas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:157
msgid ""
"The call you should use in modern code for adding drives is "
"L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>.  To add a disk image, allowing writes, and "
"specifying that the format is raw, do:"
msgstr ""
"Mūsdienu kodā disku pievienošanai jāizmanto izsaukums L</"
"guestfs_add_drive_opts>.  Lai pievienotu diska attēlu, atļaujot rakstīšanu, "
"un norādītu, ka formāts ir raw, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:165
msgid "You can add a disk read-only using:"
msgstr "Disku tikai lasīšanai var pievienot, izmantojot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:167
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_READONLY, 1,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_READONLY, 1,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:172
msgid ""
"or by calling the older function L</guestfs_add_drive_ro>.  If you use the "
"readonly flag, libguestfs won't modify the file.  (See also L</DISK IMAGE "
"FORMATS> below)."
msgstr ""
"vai izsaucot vecāko funkciju L</guestfs_add_drive_ro>.  Ja izmantojat karogu "
"readonly, libguestfs failu nemainīs.  (Skatīt arī L</DISKU ATTĒLU FORMĀTI> "
"tālāk.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:176
msgid ""
"Be extremely cautious if the disk image is in use, eg. if it is being used "
"by a virtual machine.  Adding it read-write will almost certainly cause disk "
"corruption, but adding it read-only is safe."
msgstr ""
"Esiet ārkārtīgi piesardzīgi, ja diska attēls tiek izmantots, piem., ja to "
"izmanto virtuālā mašīna.  Tā pievienošana lasīšanai un rakstīšanai gandrīz "
"noteikti izraisīs diska bojājumu, bet tā pievienošana tikai lasīšanai ir "
"droša."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:180
msgid ""
"You should usually add at least one disk image, and you may add multiple "
"disk images.  If adding multiple disk images, they usually have to be "
"\"related\", ie. from the same guest.  In the API, the disk images are "
"usually referred to as F</dev/sda> (for the first one you added), "
"F</dev/sdb> (for the second one you added), etc."
msgstr ""
"Parasti jāpievieno vismaz viens diska attēls, un var pievienot vairākus "
"disku attēlus.  Ja pievienojat vairākus disku attēlus, tiem parasti jābūt „"
"saistītiem”, t. i., no viena viesa.  API disku attēli parasti tiek apzīmēti "
"kā F</dev/sda> (pirmajam pievienotajam), F</dev/sdb> (otrajam pievienotajam) "
"u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:186
msgid ""
"Once L</guestfs_launch> has been called you cannot add any more images.  You "
"can call L</guestfs_list_devices> to get a list of the device names, in the "
"order that you added them.  See also L</BLOCK DEVICE NAMING> below."
msgstr ""
"Kad L</guestfs_launch> ir izsaukts, vairs nevar pievienot attēlus.  Varat "
"izsaukt L</guestfs_list_devices>, lai iegūtu ierīču nosaukumu sarakstu tādā "
"secībā, kādā tās pievienojāt.  Skatīt arī L</BLOKU IERĪČU NOSAUKUMI> tālāk."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:191
msgid "MOUNTING"
msgstr "MONTĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:193
msgid ""
"Before you can read or write files, create directories and so on in a disk "
"image that contains filesystems, you have to mount those filesystems using "
"L</guestfs_mount> or L</guestfs_mount_ro>.  If you already know that a disk "
"image contains (for example) one partition with a filesystem on that "
"partition, then you can mount it directly:"
msgstr ""
"Pirms varat lasīt vai rakstīt failus, izveidot direktorijas u. tml. diska "
"attēlā, kas satur failu sistēmas, šīs failu sistēmas jāmontē, izmantojot L</"
"guestfs_mount> vai L</guestfs_mount_ro>.  Ja jau zināt, ka diska attēlā ir "
"(piemēram) viens nodalījums ar failu sistēmu tajā, varat to montēt tieši:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:200
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_mount (g, \"/dev/sda1\", \"/\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_mount (g, \"/dev/sda1\", \"/\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:202
msgid ""
"where F</dev/sda1> means literally the first partition (C<1>) of the first "
"disk image that we added (F</dev/sda>).  If the disk contains Linux LVM2 "
"logical volumes you could refer to those instead (eg. F</dev/VG/LV>).  Note "
"that these are libguestfs virtual devices, and are nothing to do with host "
"devices."
msgstr ""
"kur F</dev/sda1> burtiski nozīmē pirmā pievienotā diska attēla (F</dev/sda>) "
"pirmo nodalījumu (C<1>).  Ja diskā ir Linux LVM2 loģiskie sējumi, varētu tā "
"vietā atsaukties uz tiem (piem., F</dev/VG/LV>).  Ņemiet vērā, ka tās ir "
"libguestfs virtuālās ierīces, un tām nav nekāda sakara ar resursdatora "
"ierīcēm."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:208
msgid ""
"If you are given a disk image and you don’t know what it contains then you "
"have to find out.  Libguestfs can do that too: use "
"L</guestfs_list_partitions> and L</guestfs_lvs> to list possible partitions "
"and LVs, and either try mounting each to see what is mountable, or else "
"examine them with L</guestfs_vfs_type> or L</guestfs_file>.  To list just "
"filesystems, use L</guestfs_list_filesystems>."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums dots diska attēls un nezināt, ko tas satur, tas jānoskaidro.  "
"Libguestfs to var izdarīt arī: izmantojiet L</guestfs_list_partitions> un L</"
"guestfs_lvs>, lai uzskaitītu iespējamos nodalījumus un LV, un vai nu "
"mēģiniet montēt katru, lai redzētu, kas ir montējams, vai pārbaudiet tos ar "
"L</guestfs_vfs_type> vai L</guestfs_file>.  Lai uzskaitītu tikai failu "
"sistēmas, izmantojiet L</guestfs_list_filesystems>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:216
msgid ""
"Libguestfs also has a set of APIs for inspection of unknown disk images (see "
"L</INSPECTION> below).  You might also want to look at higher level programs "
"built on top of libguestfs, in particular L<virt-inspector(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs ir arī API kopa nezināmu disku attēlu inspicēšanai (skatiet L</"
"INSPICĒŠANA> tālāk).  Varat arī apskatīt augstāka līmeņa programmas, kas "
"veidotas uz libguestfs, it īpaši L<virt-inspector(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:221
msgid ""
"To mount a filesystem read-only, use L</guestfs_mount_ro>.  There are "
"several other variations of the C<guestfs_mount_*> call."
msgstr ""
"Lai montētu failu sistēmu tikai lasīšanai, izmantojiet L</guestfs_mount_ro>"
".  Ir vairākas citas izsaukuma C<guestfs_mount_*> variācijas."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:224
msgid "FILESYSTEM ACCESS AND MODIFICATION"
msgstr "PIEKĻUVE FAILU SISTĒMĀM UN TO MAIŅA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:226
msgid ""
"The majority of the libguestfs API consists of fairly low-level calls for "
"accessing and modifying the files, directories, symlinks etc on mounted "
"filesystems.  There are over a hundred such calls which you can find listed "
"in detail below in this man page, and we don't even pretend to cover them "
"all in this overview."
msgstr ""
"Lielākā daļa libguestfs API sastāv no diezgan zema līmeņa izsaukumiem failu, "
"direktoriju, simbolisko saišu u. c. piekļuvei un mainīšanai montētās failu "
"sistēmās.  Šādu izsaukumu ir vairāk nekā simts, un tie ir sīki uzskaitīti "
"tālāk šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā, un mēs pat neizliekamies, ka aptveram tos "
"visus šajā pārskatā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:232
msgid ""
"Specify filenames as full paths, starting with C<\"/\"> and including the "
"mount point."
msgstr ""
"Norādiet failu nosaukumus kā pilnus ceļus, sākot ar C<\"/\"> un ieskaitot "
"montēšanas punktu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:235
msgid ""
"For example, if you mounted a filesystem at C<\"/\"> and you want to read "
"the file called C<\"etc/passwd\"> then you could do:"
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, ja montējāt failu sistēmu C<\"/\"> un vēlaties nolasīt failu "
"C<\"etc/passwd\">, varētu izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:238
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char *data = guestfs_cat (g, \"/etc/passwd\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char *data = guestfs_cat (g, \"/etc/passwd\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:240
msgid ""
"This would return C<data> as a newly allocated buffer containing the full "
"content of that file (with some conditions: see also L</DOWNLOADING> below), "
"or C<NULL> if there was an error."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgrieztu C<data> kā jaunpiešķirtu buferi ar visu šī faila saturu (ar "
"dažiem nosacījumiem: skatīt arī L</LEJUPIELĀDE> tālāk) vai C<NULL>, ja bija "
"kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:244
msgid ""
"As another example, to create a top-level directory on that filesystem "
"called C<\"var\"> you would do:"
msgstr ""
"Vēl viens piemērs: lai šajā failu sistēmā izveidotu augšējā līmeņa "
"direktoriju C<\"var\">, izpildītu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:247
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_mkdir (g, \"/var\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_mkdir (g, \"/var\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:249
msgid "To create a symlink you could do:"
msgstr "Lai izveidotu simbolisko saiti, varētu izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:251
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_ln_s (g, \"/etc/init.d/portmap\",\n"
"               \"/etc/rc3.d/S30portmap\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_ln_s (g, \"/etc/init.d/portmap\",\n"
"               \"/etc/rc3.d/S30portmap\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:254
msgid ""
"Libguestfs will reject attempts to use relative paths and there is no "
"concept of a current working directory."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs noraidīs mēģinājumus izmantot relatīvus ceļus, un pašreizējās "
"darba direktorijas jēdziena nav."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:257
msgid ""
"Libguestfs can return errors in many situations: for example if the "
"filesystem isn't writable, or if a file or directory that you requested "
"doesn't exist.  If you are using the C API (documented here)  you have to "
"check for those error conditions after each call.  (Other language bindings "
"turn these errors into exceptions)."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs var atgriezt kļūdas daudzās situācijās: piemēram, ja failu "
"sistēma nav rakstāma vai ja pieprasītais fails vai direktorija neeksistē.  "
"Ja izmantojat C API (dokumentēta šeit), pēc katra izsaukuma jāpārbauda šie "
"kļūdu nosacījumi.  (Citu valodu saistījumi pārvērš šīs kļūdas izņēmumos.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:263
msgid ""
"File writes are affected by the per-handle umask, set by calling "
"L</guestfs_umask> and defaulting to 022.  See L</UMASK>."
msgstr ""
"Failu rakstīšanu ietekmē katra roktura umask, kas iestatīts, izsaucot L</"
"guestfs_umask>, un pēc noklusējuma ir 022.  Skatiet L</UMASK>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:266
msgid ""
"Since libguestfs 1.18, it is possible to mount the libguestfs filesystem on "
"a local directory, subject to some restrictions.  See L</MOUNT LOCAL> below."
msgstr ""
"Kopš libguestfs 1.18 libguestfs failu sistēmu ir iespējams montēt lokālā "
"direktorijā ar dažiem ierobežojumiem.  Skatiet L</LOKĀLĀ MONTĒŠANA> tālāk."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:270
msgid "PARTITIONING"
msgstr "NODALĪŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:272
msgid ""
"Libguestfs contains API calls to read, create and modify partition tables on "
"disk images."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs satur API izsaukumus nodalījumu tabulu lasīšanai, izveidei un "
"mainīšanai disku attēlos."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:275
msgid ""
"In the common case where you want to create a single partition covering the "
"whole disk, you should use the L</guestfs_part_disk> call:"
msgstr ""
"Parastajā gadījumā, kad vēlaties izveidot vienu nodalījumu, kas aptver visu "
"disku, jāizmanto izsaukums L</guestfs_part_disk>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:279
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" const char *parttype = \"mbr\";\n"
" if (disk_is_larger_than_2TB)\n"
"   parttype = \"gpt\";\n"
" guestfs_part_disk (g, \"/dev/sda\", parttype);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" const char *parttype = \"mbr\";\n"
" if (disk_is_larger_than_2TB)\n"
"   parttype = \"gpt\";\n"
" guestfs_part_disk (g, \"/dev/sda\", parttype);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:284
msgid ""
"Obviously this effectively wipes anything that was on that disk image "
"before."
msgstr ""
"Acīmredzot tas faktiski izdzēš visu, kas iepriekš bija šajā diska attēlā."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:287
msgid "LVM2"
msgstr "LVM2"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:289
msgid ""
"Libguestfs provides access to a large part of the LVM2 API, such as "
"L</guestfs_lvcreate> and L</guestfs_vgremove>.  It won't make much sense "
"unless you familiarize yourself with the concepts of physical volumes, "
"volume groups and logical volumes."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs nodrošina piekļuvi lielai LVM2 API daļai, piemēram, L</"
"guestfs_lvcreate> un L</guestfs_vgremove>.  Tam nebūs lielas jēgas, ja "
"neiepazīsieties ar fizisko sējumu, sējumu grupu un loģisko sējumu jēdzieniem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:294
msgid ""
"This author strongly recommends reading the LVM HOWTO, online at "
"L<http://tldp.org/HOWTO/LVM-HOWTO/>."
msgstr ""
"Šī teksta autors stingri iesaka izlasīt LVM HOWTO, tiešsaistē L<http://"
"tldp.org/HOWTO/LVM-HOWTO/>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:297
msgid "DOWNLOADING"
msgstr "LEJUPIELĀDE"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:299
msgid ""
"Use L</guestfs_cat> to download small, text only files.  This call cannot "
"handle files containing any ASCII NUL (C<\\0>) characters.  However the API "
"is very simple to use."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L</guestfs_cat>, lai lejupielādētu mazus, tikai teksta failus.  "
"Šis izsaukums nevar apstrādāt failus ar jebkādām ASCII NUL (C<\\0>) "
"rakstzīmēm.  Tomēr API ir ļoti vienkārši lietojama."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:303
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_read_file> can be used to read files which contain arbitrary 8 "
"bit data, since it returns a (pointer, size) pair."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_read_file> var izmantot failu lasīšanai, kas satur patvaļīgus 8 "
"bitu datus, jo tas atgriež pāri (rādītājs, izmērs)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:306
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_download> can be used to download any file, with no limits on "
"content or size."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_download> var izmantot jebkura faila lejupielādei bez satura vai "
"izmēra ierobežojumiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:309
msgid "To download multiple files, see L</guestfs_tar_out> and L</guestfs_tgz_out>."
msgstr ""
"Lai lejupielādētu vairākus failus, skatiet L</guestfs_tar_out> un L</"
"guestfs_tgz_out>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:312
msgid "UPLOADING"
msgstr "AUGŠUPIELĀDE"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:314
msgid ""
"To write a small file with fixed content, use L</guestfs_write>.  To create "
"a file of all zeroes, use L</guestfs_truncate_size> (sparse) or "
"L</guestfs_fallocate64> (with all disk blocks allocated).  There are a "
"variety of other functions for creating test files, for example "
"L</guestfs_fill> and L</guestfs_fill_pattern>."
msgstr ""
"Lai ierakstītu mazu failu ar fiksētu saturu, izmantojiet L</guestfs_write>.  "
"Lai izveidotu failu tikai ar nullēm, izmantojiet L</guestfs_truncate_size> "
"(retināts) vai L</guestfs_fallocate64> (ar visiem piešķirtajiem diska "
"blokiem).  Ir dažādas citas funkcijas testa failu izveidei, piemēram, L</"
"guestfs_fill> un L</guestfs_fill_pattern>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:320
msgid ""
"To upload a single file, use L</guestfs_upload>.  This call has no limits on "
"file content or size."
msgstr ""
"Lai augšupielādētu vienu failu, izmantojiet L</guestfs_upload>.  Šim "
"izsaukumam nav faila satura vai izmēra ierobežojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:323
msgid "To upload multiple files, see L</guestfs_tar_in> and L</guestfs_tgz_in>."
msgstr ""
"Lai augšupielādētu vairākus failus, skatiet L</guestfs_tar_in> un L</"
"guestfs_tgz_in>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:325
msgid ""
"However the fastest way to upload I<large numbers of arbitrary files> is to "
"turn them into a squashfs or CD ISO (see L<mksquashfs(8)> and "
"L<mkisofs(8)>), then attach this using L</guestfs_add_drive_ro>.  If you add "
"the drive in a predictable way (eg. adding it last after all other drives) "
"then you can get the device name from L</guestfs_list_devices> and mount it "
"directly using L</guestfs_mount_ro>.  Note that squashfs images are "
"sometimes non-portable between kernel versions, and they don't support "
"labels or UUIDs.  If you want to pre-build an image or you need to mount it "
"using a label or UUID, use an ISO image instead."
msgstr ""
"Tomēr ātrākais veids, kā augšupielādēt I<lielu skaitu patvaļīgu failu>, ir "
"pārvērst tos squashfs vai CD ISO (skatiet L<mksquashfs(8)> un L<mkisofs(8)>) "
"un pēc tam pievienot to ar L</guestfs_add_drive_ro>.  Ja pievienojat disku "
"paredzamā veidā (piem., pievienojot to pēdējo pēc visiem pārējiem diskiem), "
"ierīces nosaukumu varat iegūt no L</guestfs_list_devices> un montēt to tieši "
"ar L</guestfs_mount_ro>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka squashfs attēli dažreiz nav "
"pārnesami starp kodola versijām, un tie neatbalsta etiķetes vai UUID.  Ja "
"vēlaties attēlu uzbūvēt iepriekš vai tas jāmontē, izmantojot etiķeti vai "
"UUID, tā vietā izmantojiet ISO attēlu."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:336
msgid "COPYING"
msgstr "KOPĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:338
msgid ""
"There are various different commands for copying between files and devices "
"and in and out of the guest filesystem.  These are summarised in the table "
"below."
msgstr ""
"Ir dažādas komandas kopēšanai starp failiem un ierīcēm un uz viesa failu "
"sistēmu un no tās.  Tās apkopotas tālāk dotajā tabulā."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:344
msgid "B<file> to B<file>"
msgstr "B<file> uz B<file>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:346
msgid ""
"Use L</guestfs_cp> to copy a single file, or L</guestfs_cp_a> to copy "
"directories recursively."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L</guestfs_cp>, lai kopētu vienu failu, vai L</guestfs_cp_a>, "
"lai rekursīvi kopētu direktorijas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:349
msgid "To copy part of a file (offset and size) use L</guestfs_copy_file_to_file>."
msgstr ""
"Lai kopētu faila daļu (nobīde un izmērs), izmantojiet L</"
"guestfs_copy_file_to_file>."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:352
msgid "B<file> to B<device>"
msgstr "B<file> uz B<device>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:354
msgid "B<device> to B<file>"
msgstr "B<device> uz B<file>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:356
msgid "B<device> to B<device>"
msgstr "B<device> uz B<device>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:358
msgid ""
"Use L</guestfs_copy_file_to_device>, L</guestfs_copy_device_to_file>, or "
"L</guestfs_copy_device_to_device>."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L</guestfs_copy_file_to_device>, L</guestfs_copy_device_to_file> "
"vai L</guestfs_copy_device_to_device>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:361
msgid "Example: duplicate the contents of an LV:"
msgstr "Piemērs: LV satura dublēšana:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:363
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_copy_device_to_device (g,\n"
"         \"/dev/VG/Original\", \"/dev/VG/Copy\",\n"
"         /* -1 marks the end of the list of optional parameters */\n"
"         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_copy_device_to_device (g,\n"
"         \"/dev/VG/Original\", \"/dev/VG/Copy\",\n"
"         /* -1 marks the end of the list of optional parameters */\n"
"         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:368
msgid ""
"The destination (F</dev/VG/Copy>) must be at least as large as the source "
"(F</dev/VG/Original>).  To copy less than the whole source device, use the "
"optional C<size> parameter:"
msgstr ""
"Mērķim (F</dev/VG/Copy>) jābūt vismaz tikpat lielam kā avotam (F</dev/VG/"
"Original>).  Lai kopētu mazāk par visu avota ierīci, izmantojiet neobligāto "
"parametru C<size>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:372
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_copy_device_to_device (g,\n"
"         \"/dev/VG/Original\", \"/dev/VG/Copy\",\n"
"         GUESTFS_COPY_DEVICE_TO_DEVICE_SIZE, 10000,\n"
"         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_copy_device_to_device (g,\n"
"         \"/dev/VG/Original\", \"/dev/VG/Copy\",\n"
"         GUESTFS_COPY_DEVICE_TO_DEVICE_SIZE, 10000,\n"
"         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:377
msgid "B<file on the host> to B<file or device>"
msgstr "B<file on the host> uz B<file or device>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:379
msgid "Use L</guestfs_upload>.  See L</UPLOADING> above."
msgstr "Izmantojiet L</guestfs_upload>.  Skatiet L</AUGŠUPIELĀDE> iepriekš."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:381
msgid "B<file or device> to B<file on the host>"
msgstr "B<file or device> uz B<file on the host>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:383
msgid "Use L</guestfs_download>.  See L</DOWNLOADING> above."
msgstr "Izmantojiet L</guestfs_download>.  Skatiet L</LEJUPIELĀDE> iepriekš."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:387
msgid "UPLOADING AND DOWNLOADING TO PIPES AND FILE DESCRIPTORS"
msgstr "AUGŠUPIELĀDE UN LEJUPIELĀDE KANĀLOS UN FAILU DESKRIPTOROS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:389
msgid ""
"Calls like L</guestfs_upload>, L</guestfs_download>, L</guestfs_tar_in>, "
"L</guestfs_tar_out> etc appear to only take filenames as arguments, so it "
"appears you can only upload and download to files.  However many Un*x-like "
"hosts let you use the special device files F</dev/stdin>, F</dev/stdout>, "
"F</dev/stderr> and F</dev/fd/N> to read and write from stdin, stdout, "
"stderr, and arbitrary file descriptor N."
msgstr ""
"Tādi izsaukumi kā L</guestfs_upload>, L</guestfs_download>, L</"
"guestfs_tar_in>, L</guestfs_tar_out> u. c. šķietami pieņem tikai failu "
"nosaukumus kā argumentus, tāpēc šķiet, ka var augšupielādēt un lejupielādēt "
"tikai failos.  Tomēr daudzi Un*x līdzīgi resursdatori ļauj izmantot īpašos "
"ierīču failus F</dev/stdin>, F</dev/stdout>, F</dev/stderr> un F</dev/fd/N>, "
"lai lasītu un rakstītu stdin, stdout, stderr un patvaļīgā failu deskriptorā "
"N."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:397
msgid "For example, L<virt-cat(1)> writes its output to stdout by doing:"
msgstr "Piemēram, L<virt-cat(1)> raksta savu izvadi uz stdout, izpildot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:400
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_download (g, filename, \"/dev/stdout\");\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_download (g, filename, \"/dev/stdout\");\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:402
msgid "and you can write tar output to a file descriptor C<fd> by doing:"
msgstr "un tar izvadi failu deskriptorā C<fd> var ierakstīt, izpildot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char devfd[64];\n"
" snprintf (devfd, sizeof devfd, \"/dev/fd/%d\", fd);\n"
" guestfs_tar_out (g, \"/\", devfd);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char devfd[64];\n"
" snprintf (devfd, sizeof devfd, \"/dev/fd/%d\", fd);\n"
" guestfs_tar_out (g, \"/\", devfd);\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:408
msgid "LISTING FILES"
msgstr "FAILU UZSKAITĪŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:410
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_ll> is just designed for humans to read (mainly when using the "
"L<guestfish(1)>-equivalent command C<ll>)."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_ll> ir paredzēts tikai cilvēkiem lasīšanai (galvenokārt, "
"izmantojot L<guestfish(1)> līdzvērtīgo komandu C<ll>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:413
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_ls> is a quick way to get a list of files in a directory from "
"programs, as a flat list of strings."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_ls> ir ātrs veids, kā no programmām iegūt direktorijas failu "
"sarakstu kā plakanu virkņu sarakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:416
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_readdir> is a programmatic way to get a list of files in a "
"directory, plus additional information about each one.  It is more "
"equivalent to using the L<readdir(3)> call on a local filesystem."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_readdir> ir programmatisks veids, kā iegūt direktorijas failu "
"sarakstu kopā ar papildu informāciju par katru no tiem.  Tas vairāk līdzinās "
"izsaukuma L<readdir(3)> izmantošanai lokālā failu sistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:420
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_find> and L</guestfs_find0> can be used to recursively list "
"files."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_find> un L</guestfs_find0> var izmantot rekursīvai failu "
"uzskaitīšanai."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:423
msgid "RUNNING COMMANDS"
msgstr "KOMANDU IZPILDE"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:425
msgid ""
"Although libguestfs is primarily an API for manipulating files inside guest "
"images, we also provide some limited facilities for running commands inside "
"guests."
msgstr ""
"Lai gan libguestfs galvenokārt ir API failu apstrādei viesu attēlos, "
"nodrošinām arī dažas ierobežotas iespējas komandu izpildei viesos."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:429
msgid "There are many limitations to this:"
msgstr "Tam ir daudz ierobežojumu:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:435
msgid ""
"The kernel version that the command runs under will be different from what "
"it expects."
msgstr ""
"Kodola versija, kurā komanda tiek izpildīta, atšķirsies no tās, ko tā gaida."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:440
msgid ""
"If the command needs to communicate with daemons, then most likely they "
"won't be running."
msgstr "Ja komandai jāsazinās ar dēmoniem, visticamāk, tie nedarbosies."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:445
msgid "The command will be running in limited memory."
msgstr "Komanda tiks izpildīta ierobežotā atmiņā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:449
msgid ""
"The network may not be available unless you enable it (see "
"L</guestfs_set_network>)."
msgstr ""
"Tīkls var nebūt pieejams, ja vien to neiespējojat (skatiet L</"
"guestfs_set_network>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:454
msgid "Only supports Linux guests (not Windows, BSD, etc)."
msgstr "Atbalsta tikai Linux viesus (ne Windows, BSD u. c.)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:458
msgid "Architecture limitations (eg. won’t work for a PPC guest on an X86 host)."
msgstr ""
"Arhitektūras ierobežojumi (piem., nedarbosies PPC viesim X86 resursdatorā)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:463
msgid ""
"For SELinux guests, you may need to relabel the guest after creating new "
"files.  See L</SELINUX> below."
msgstr ""
"SELinux viesiem pēc jaunu failu izveides, iespējams, viesim būs atkārtoti "
"jāpiešķir etiķetes.  Skatiet L</SELINUX> tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:468
msgid ""
"I<Security:> It is not safe to run commands from untrusted, possibly "
"malicious guests.  These commands may attempt to exploit your program by "
"sending unexpected output.  They could also try to exploit the Linux kernel "
"or qemu provided by the libguestfs appliance.  They could use the network "
"provided by the libguestfs appliance to bypass ordinary network partitions "
"and firewalls.  They could use the elevated privileges or different SELinux "
"context of your program to their advantage."
msgstr ""
"I<Drošība:> nav droši izpildīt komandas no neuzticamiem, iespējams, "
"ļaunprātīgiem viesiem.  Šīs komandas var mēģināt izmantot jūsu programmas "
"ievainojamības, sūtot negaidītu izvadi.  Tās var arī mēģināt izmantot "
"libguestfs palīgsistēmas nodrošinātā Linux kodola vai qemu ievainojamības.  "
"Tās var izmantot libguestfs palīgsistēmas nodrošināto tīklu, lai apietu "
"parastos tīkla nodalījumus un ugunsmūrus.  Tās var izmantot savā labā jūsu "
"programmas paaugstinātās privilēģijas vai atšķirīgo SELinux kontekstu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:477
msgid ""
"A secure alternative is to use libguestfs to install a \"firstboot\" script "
"(a script which runs when the guest next boots normally), and to have this "
"script run the commands you want in the normal context of the running guest, "
"network security and so on.  For information about other security issues, "
"see L<guestfs-security(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Droša alternatīva ir izmantot libguestfs, lai instalētu „pirmās sāknēšanas” "
"skriptu (skriptu, kas tiek izpildīts, kad viesis nākamreiz sāknējas normāli)"
", un likt šim skriptam izpildīt vajadzīgās komandas darbojošā viesa "
"parastajā kontekstā ar tīkla drošību u. tml.  Informāciju par citām drošības "
"problēmām skatiet L<guestfs-security(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:485
msgid ""
"The two main API calls to run commands are L</guestfs_command> and "
"L</guestfs_sh> (there are also variations)."
msgstr ""
"Divi galvenie API izsaukumi komandu izpildei ir L</guestfs_command> un L</"
"guestfs_sh> (ir arī variācijas)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:488
msgid ""
"The difference is that L</guestfs_sh> runs commands using the shell, so any "
"shell globs, redirections, etc will work."
msgstr ""
"Atšķirība ir tā, ka L</guestfs_sh> izpilda komandas, izmantojot čaulu, tāpēc "
"darbosies jebkuri čaulas glob šabloni, novirzīšanas u. c."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:491
msgid "CONFIGURATION FILES"
msgstr "KONFIGURĀCIJAS FAILI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:493
msgid ""
"To read and write configuration files in Linux guest filesystems, we "
"strongly recommend using Augeas.  For example, Augeas understands how to "
"read and write, say, a Linux shadow password file or X.org configuration "
"file, and so avoids you having to write that code."
msgstr ""
"Konfigurācijas failu lasīšanai un rakstīšanai Linux viesu failu sistēmās "
"stingri iesakām izmantot Augeas.  Piemēram, Augeas saprot, kā lasīt un "
"rakstīt, teiksim, Linux shadow paroļu failu vai X.org konfigurācijas failu, "
"tādējādi jums nav jāraksta šis kods."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:498
msgid ""
"The main Augeas calls are bound through the C<guestfs_aug_*> APIs.  We don't "
"document Augeas itself here because there is excellent documentation on the "
"L<http://augeas.net/> website."
msgstr ""
"Galvenie Augeas izsaukumi ir piesaistīti caur C<guestfs_aug_*> API.  Pašu "
"Augeas šeit nedokumentējam, jo tīmekļa vietnē L<http://augeas.net/> ir "
"lieliska dokumentācija."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:502
msgid ""
"If you don’t want to use Augeas (you fool!) then try calling "
"L</guestfs_read_lines> to get the file as a list of lines which you can "
"iterate over."
msgstr ""
"Ja nevēlaties izmantot Augeas (muļķis!), mēģiniet izsaukt L</"
"guestfs_read_lines>, lai iegūtu failu kā rindu sarakstu, ko var iterēt."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:506
msgid "SYSTEMD JOURNAL FILES"
msgstr "SYSTEMD ŽURNĀLA FAILI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:508
msgid ""
"To read the systemd journal from a Linux guest, use the C<guestfs_journal_*> "
"APIs starting with L</guestfs_journal_open>."
msgstr ""
"Lai nolasītu systemd žurnālu no Linux viesa, izmantojiet "
"C<guestfs_journal_*> API, sākot ar L</guestfs_journal_open>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:511
msgid ""
"Consult the journal documentation here: L<sd-journal(3)>, "
"L<sd_journal_open(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Skatiet žurnāla dokumentāciju šeit: L<sd-journal(3)>, L<sd_journal_open(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:514
msgid "SELINUX"
msgstr "SELINUX"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:516
msgid ""
"We support SELinux guests.  However it is not possible to load the SELinux "
"policy of the guest into the appliance kernel.  Therefore the strategy for "
"dealing with SELinux guests is to relabel them after making changes."
msgstr ""
"Mēs atbalstām SELinux viesus.  Tomēr viesa SELinux politiku nav iespējams "
"ielādēt palīgsistēmas kodolā.  Tāpēc stratēģija darbam ar SELinux viesiem ir "
"pēc izmaiņu veikšanas tiem atkārtoti piešķirt etiķetes."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:521
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.34 there is a new API, L</guestfs_setfiles>, which can "
"be used for this.  To properly use this API you have to parse the guest "
"SELinux configuration.  See the L<virt-customize(1)> module "
"F<customize/SELinux_relabel.ml> for how to do this."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.34 tam ir jauna API, L</guestfs_setfiles>.  Lai pareizi "
"izmantotu šo API, jāparsē viesa SELinux konfigurācija.  Kā to izdarīt, "
"skatiet L<virt-customize(1)> moduli F<customize/SELinux_relabel.ml>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:526
msgid ""
"A simpler but slower alternative is to touch F</.autorelabel> in the guest, "
"which means that the guest will relabel itself at next boot."
msgstr ""
"Vienkāršāka, bet lēnāka alternatīva ir izpildīt touch F</.autorelabel> "
"viesī, kas nozīmē, ka viesis nākamajā sāknēšanā pats sev atkārtoti piešķirs "
"etiķetes."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:529
msgid ""
"Libguestfs E<le> 1.32 had APIs C<guestfs_set_selinux>, "
"C<guestfs_get_selinux>, C<guestfs_setcon> and C<guestfs_getcon>.  These did "
"not work properly, are deprecated, and should not be used in new code."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<le> 1.32 bija API C<guestfs_set_selinux>, C<guestfs_get_selinux>"
", C<guestfs_setcon> un C<guestfs_getcon>.  Tās nedarbojās pareizi, ir "
"novecojušas, un tās nevajadzētu izmantot jaunā kodā."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:534
msgid "UMASK"
msgstr "UMASK"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:536
msgid ""
"Certain calls are affected by the current file mode creation mask (the "
"\"umask\").  In particular ones which create files or directories, such as "
"L</guestfs_touch>, L</guestfs_mknod> or L</guestfs_mkdir>.  This affects "
"either the default mode that the file is created with or modifies the mode "
"that you supply."
msgstr ""
"Dažus izsaukumus ietekmē pašreizējā failu režīma izveides maska („umask”).  "
"It īpaši tos, kas izveido failus vai direktorijas, piemēram, L</"
"guestfs_touch>, L</guestfs_mknod> vai L</guestfs_mkdir>.  Tas ietekmē vai nu "
"noklusējuma režīmu, ar kuru fails tiek izveidots, vai maina norādīto režīmu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:542
msgid ""
"The default umask is C<022>, so files are created with modes such as C<0644> "
"and directories with C<0755>."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma umask ir C<022>, tāpēc faili tiek izveidoti ar tādiem režīmiem "
"kā C<0644> un direktorijas ar C<0755>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:545
msgid ""
"There are two ways to avoid being affected by umask.  Either set umask to 0 "
"(call C<guestfs_umask (g, 0)> early after launching).  Or call "
"L</guestfs_chmod> after creating each file or directory."
msgstr ""
"Ir divi veidi, kā izvairīties no umask ietekmes.  Vai nu iestatiet umask uz "
"0 (izsauciet C<guestfs_umask (g, 0)> drīz pēc palaišanas).  Vai arī pēc "
"katra faila vai direktorijas izveides izsauciet L</guestfs_chmod>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:549
msgid "For more information about umask, see L<umask(2)>."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju par umask skatiet L<umask(2)>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:551
msgid "LABELS AND UUIDS"
msgstr "ETIĶETES UN UUID"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:553
msgid ""
"Many filesystems, devices and logical volumes support either labels (short "
"strings like \"BOOT\" which might not be unique) and/or UUIDs (globally "
"unique IDs)."
msgstr ""
"Daudzas failu sistēmas, ierīces un loģiskie sējumi atbalsta etiķetes (īsas "
"virknes, piemēram, „BOOT”, kas var nebūt unikālas) un/vai UUID (globāli "
"unikālus ID)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:557
msgid ""
"For filesystems, use L</guestfs_vfs_label> or L</guestfs_vfs_uuid> to read "
"the label or UUID.  Some filesystems let you call L</guestfs_set_label> or "
"L</guestfs_set_uuid> to change the label or UUID."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēmām izmantojiet L</guestfs_vfs_label> vai L</guestfs_vfs_uuid>, "
"lai nolasītu etiķeti vai UUID.  Dažas failu sistēmas ļauj izsaukt L</"
"guestfs_set_label> vai L</guestfs_set_uuid>, lai mainītu etiķeti vai UUID."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:562
msgid ""
"You can locate a filesystem by its label or UUID using "
"L</guestfs_findfs_label> or L</guestfs_findfs_uuid>."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēmu var atrast pēc tās etiķetes vai UUID, izmantojot L</"
"guestfs_findfs_label> vai L</guestfs_findfs_uuid>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:565
msgid ""
"For LVM2 (which supports only UUIDs), there is a rich set of APIs for "
"fetching UUIDs, fetching UUIDs of the contained objects, and changing "
"UUIDs.  See: L</guestfs_lvuuid>, L</guestfs_vguuid>, L</guestfs_pvuuid>, "
"L</guestfs_vglvuuids>, L</guestfs_vgpvuuids>, L</guestfs_vgchange_uuid>, "
"L</guestfs_vgchange_uuid_all>, L</guestfs_pvchange_uuid>, "
"L</guestfs_pvchange_uuid_all>."
msgstr ""
"LVM2 (kas atbalsta tikai UUID) ir bagātīga API kopa UUID iegūšanai, ietverto "
"objektu UUID iegūšanai un UUID maiņai.  Skatiet: L</guestfs_lvuuid>, L</"
"guestfs_vguuid>, L</guestfs_pvuuid>, L</guestfs_vglvuuids>, L</"
"guestfs_vgpvuuids>, L</guestfs_vgchange_uuid>, L</guestfs_vgchange_uuid_all>"
", L</guestfs_pvchange_uuid>, L</guestfs_pvchange_uuid_all>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:576
msgid ""
"Note when cloning a filesystem, device or whole guest, it is a good idea to "
"set new randomly generated UUIDs on the copy."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, klonējot failu sistēmu, ierīci vai visu viesi, kopijai "
"ieteicams iestatīt jaunus nejauši ģenerētus UUID."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:581
msgid ""
"Libguestfs allows you to access Linux guests which have been encrypted using "
"whole disk encryption that conforms to the Linux Unified Key Setup (LUKS) "
"standard.  This includes nearly all whole disk encryption systems used by "
"modern Linux guests.  Windows BitLocker is also supported."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs ļauj piekļūt Linux viesiem, kas šifrēti ar pilna diska šifrēšanu, "
"kura atbilst Linux Unified Key Setup (LUKS) standartam.  Tas ietver gandrīz "
"visas moderno Linux viesu izmantotās pilna diska šifrēšanas sistēmas.  Tiek "
"atbalstīts arī Windows BitLocker."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:587
msgid ""
"Use L</guestfs_vfs_type> to identify encrypted block devices.  For LUKS it "
"returns the string C<crypto_LUKS>.  For Windows BitLocker it returns "
"C<BitLocker>."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L</guestfs_vfs_type>, lai identificētu šifrētas bloku ierīces.  "
"LUKS gadījumā tas atgriež virkni C<crypto_LUKS>.  Windows BitLocker gadījumā "
"tas atgriež C<BitLocker>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:591
msgid ""
"Then open these devices by calling L</guestfs_cryptsetup_open>.  Obviously "
"you will require the passphrase!"
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam atveriet šīs ierīces, izsaucot L</guestfs_cryptsetup_open>.  "
"Acīmredzot būs vajadzīga paroles frāze!"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:594
msgid ""
"Passphrase-less unlocking is supported for LUKS (not BitLocker)  block "
"devices that have been encrypted with network-bound disk encryption (NBDE), "
"using Clevis on the Linux guest side, and Tang on a separate Linux server.  "
"Open such devices with L</guestfs_clevis_luks_unlock>.  The appliance will "
"need networking enabled (refer to L</guestfs_set_network>) and actual "
"connectivity to the Tang servers noted in the C<tang> Clevis pins that are "
"bound to the LUKS header.  (This includes the ability to resolve the names "
"of the Tang servers.)"
msgstr ""
"Atbloķēšana bez paroles frāzes tiek atbalstīta LUKS (ne BitLocker) bloku "
"ierīcēm, kas šifrētas ar tīklam piesaistītu diska šifrēšanu (NBDE), "
"izmantojot Clevis Linux viesa pusē un Tang atsevišķā Linux serverī.  Šādas "
"ierīces atveriet ar L</guestfs_clevis_luks_unlock>.  Palīgsistēmai būs "
"vajadzīga iespējota tīklošana (skatiet L</guestfs_set_network>) un faktiska "
"savienojamība ar Tang serveriem, kas norādīti LUKS galvenei piesaistītajās "
"C<tang> Clevis tapās.  (Tas ietver spēju atrisināt Tang serveru nosaukumus.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:604
msgid ""
"Opening an encrypted device creates a new device mapper device called "
"F</dev/mapper/mapname> (where C<mapname> is the string you supply to "
"L</guestfs_cryptsetup_open> or L</guestfs_clevis_luks_unlock>). Reads and "
"writes to this mapper device are decrypted from and encrypted to the "
"underlying block device respectively."
msgstr ""
"Šifrētas ierīces atvēršana izveido jaunu device mapper ierīci F</dev/mapper/"
"mapname> (kur C<mapname> ir virkne, ko nododat L</guestfs_cryptsetup_open> "
"vai L</guestfs_clevis_luks_unlock>). Lasīšana no šīs kartētāja ierīces un "
"rakstīšana tajā tiek attiecīgi atšifrēta no pamatā esošās bloku ierīces un "
"šifrēta uz to."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:611
msgid ""
"LVM volume groups on the device can be made visible by calling "
"L</guestfs_vgscan> followed by L</guestfs_vg_activate_all>.  The logical "
"volume(s) can now be mounted in the usual way."
msgstr ""
"Ierīcē esošās LVM sējumu grupas var padarīt redzamas, izsaucot L</"
"guestfs_vgscan> un pēc tam L</guestfs_vg_activate_all>.  Loģisko(-os) sējumu"
"(-us) tagad var montēt parastajā veidā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:615
msgid ""
"Use the reverse process to close an encrypted device.  Unmount any logical "
"volumes on it, deactivate the volume groups by calling C<guestfs_vg_activate "
"(g, 0, [\"/dev/VG\"])>.  Then close the mapper device by calling "
"L</guestfs_cryptsetup_close> on the F</dev/mapper/mapname> device (I<not> "
"the underlying encrypted block device)."
msgstr ""
"Lai aizvērtu šifrētu ierīci, izmantojiet apgriezto procesu.  Atmontējiet "
"visus tajā esošos loģiskos sējumus, deaktivizējiet sējumu grupas, izsaucot "
"C<guestfs_vg_activate (g, 0, [\"/dev/VG\"])>.  Pēc tam aizveriet kartētāja "
"ierīci, izsaucot L</guestfs_cryptsetup_close> ierīcei F</dev/mapper/mapname> "
"(I<nevis> pamatā esošajai šifrētajai bloku ierīcei)."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:622
msgid "MOUNT LOCAL"
msgstr "LOKĀLĀ MONTĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:624
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.18, it is possible to mount the libguestfs filesystem "
"on a local directory and access it using ordinary POSIX calls and programs."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.18 libguestfs failu sistēmu ir iespējams montēt lokālā "
"direktorijā un piekļūt tai, izmantojot parastus POSIX izsaukumus un "
"programmas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:628
msgid ""
"Availability of this is subject to a number of restrictions: it requires "
"FUSE (the Filesystem in USErspace), and libfuse must also have been "
"available when libguestfs was compiled.  FUSE may require that a kernel "
"module is loaded, and it may be necessary to add the current user to a "
"special C<fuse> group.  See the documentation for your distribution and "
"L<http://fuse.sf.net> for further information."
msgstr ""
"Tās pieejamībai ir vairāki ierobežojumi: tai nepieciešams FUSE (Filesystem "
"in USErspace), un libfuse arī jābūt bijušai pieejamai, kad libguestfs tika "
"kompilēta.  FUSE var pieprasīt, lai būtu ielādēts kodola modulis, un var būt "
"nepieciešams pievienot pašreizējo lietotāju īpašai grupai C<fuse>.  Plašāku "
"informāciju skatiet savas distribūcijas dokumentācijā un L<http://"
"fuse.sf.net>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:635
msgid ""
"The call to mount the libguestfs filesystem on a local directory is "
"L</guestfs_mount_local> (q.v.) followed by L</guestfs_mount_local_run>.  The "
"latter does not return until you unmount the filesystem.  The reason is that "
"the call enters the FUSE main loop and processes kernel requests, turning "
"them into libguestfs calls.  An alternative design would have been to create "
"a background thread to do this, but libguestfs doesn't require pthreads.  "
"This way is also more flexible: for example the user can create another "
"thread for L</guestfs_mount_local_run>."
msgstr ""
"Izsaukums libguestfs failu sistēmas montēšanai lokālā direktorijā ir L</"
"guestfs_mount_local> (skat. tur), kam seko L</guestfs_mount_local_run>.  "
"Pēdējais neatgriežas, kamēr nenomontējat failu sistēmu.  Iemesls ir tāds, ka "
"izsaukums ieiet FUSE galvenajā ciklā un apstrādā kodola pieprasījumus, "
"pārvēršot tos libguestfs izsaukumos.  Alternatīvs dizains būtu bijis "
"izveidot fona pavedienu, kas to darītu, bet libguestfs nav nepieciešami "
"pthreads.  Šis veids ir arī elastīgāks: piemēram, lietotājs var izveidot "
"citu pavedienu L</guestfs_mount_local_run>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:645
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_mount_local> needs a certain amount of time to set up the "
"mountpoint.  The mountpoint is not ready to use until the call returns.  At "
"this point, accesses to the filesystem will block until the main loop is "
"entered (ie. L</guestfs_mount_local_run>).  So if you need to start another "
"process to access the filesystem, put the fork between "
"L</guestfs_mount_local> and L</guestfs_mount_local_run>."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_mount_local> vajadzīgs zināms laiks montēšanas punkta "
"iestatīšanai.  Montēšanas punkts nav gatavs lietošanai, līdz izsaukums "
"atgriežas.  Šajā brīdī piekļuve failu sistēmai bloķēs, līdz tiks ieiets "
"galvenajā ciklā (t. i., L</guestfs_mount_local_run>).  Tāpēc, ja jāpalaiž "
"cits process piekļuvei failu sistēmai, novietojiet fork starp L</"
"guestfs_mount_local> un L</guestfs_mount_local_run>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:653
msgid "MOUNT LOCAL COMPATIBILITY"
msgstr "LOKĀLĀS MONTĒŠANAS SADERĪBA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:655
msgid ""
"Since local mounting was only added in libguestfs 1.18, and may not be "
"available even in these builds, you should consider writing code so that it "
"doesn't depend on this feature, and can fall back to using libguestfs file "
"system calls."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā lokālā montēšana tika pievienota tikai libguestfs 1.18 un var nebūt "
"pieejama pat šajās būvēs, jāapsver kods, kas nav atkarīgs no šī līdzekļa un "
"var pāriet uz libguestfs failu sistēmas izsaukumiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:660
msgid ""
"If libguestfs was compiled without support for L</guestfs_mount_local> then "
"calling it will return an error with errno set to C<ENOTSUP> (see "
"L</guestfs_last_errno>)."
msgstr ""
"Ja libguestfs tika kompilēta bez L</guestfs_mount_local> atbalsta, tās "
"izsaukšana atgriezīs kļūdu ar errno, kas iestatīts uz C<ENOTSUP> (skatiet L</"
"guestfs_last_errno>)."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:664
msgid "MOUNT LOCAL PERFORMANCE"
msgstr "LOKĀLĀS MONTĒŠANAS VEIKTSPĒJA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:666
msgid ""
"Libguestfs on top of FUSE performs quite poorly.  For best performance do "
"not use it.  Use ordinary libguestfs filesystem calls, upload, download "
"etc. instead."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs virs FUSE darbojas diezgan slikti.  Labākai veiktspējai "
"neizmantojiet to.  Tā vietā izmantojiet parastos libguestfs failu sistēmas "
"izsaukumus, upload, download u. c."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:670
msgid "REMOTE STORAGE"
msgstr "ATTĀLĀ KRĀTUVE"

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:672
msgid "CEPH"
msgstr "CEPH"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:674
msgid "Libguestfs can access Ceph (librbd/RBD) disks."
msgstr "Libguestfs var piekļūt Ceph (librbd/RBD) diskiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:676 lib/guestfs.pod:731 lib/guestfs.pod:775
msgid ""
"To do this, set the optional C<protocol> and C<server> parameters of "
"L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> like this:"
msgstr ""
"Lai to izdarītu, iestatiet L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> neobligātos parametrus "
"C<protocol> un C<server> šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:679
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char **servers = { \"ceph1.example.org:3000\", /* ... */, NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"pool/image\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"rbd\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, servers,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_USERNAME, \"rbduser\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SECRET, "
"\"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA==\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char **servers = { \"ceph1.example.org:3000\", /* ... */, NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"pool/image\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"rbd\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, servers,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_USERNAME, \"rbduser\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SECRET, "
"\"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA==\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:688
msgid ""
"C<servers> (the C<server> parameter) is a list of one or more Ceph servers.  "
"The server string is documented in L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>. The "
"C<username> and C<secret> parameters are also optional, and if not given, "
"then no authentication will be used."
msgstr ""
"C<servers> (parametrs C<server>) ir viena vai vairāku Ceph serveru "
"saraksts.  Servera virkne ir dokumentēta L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>. "
"Parametri C<username> un C<secret> arī ir neobligāti, un, ja tie nav "
"norādīti, autentifikācija netiks izmantota."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:693
msgid ""
"An encrypted RBD disk -- I<directly> opening which would require the "
"C<username> and C<secret> parameters -- cannot be accessed if the following "
"conditions all hold:"
msgstr ""
"Šifrētam RBD diskam — kura I<tiešai> atvēršanai būtu nepieciešami parametri "
"C<username> un C<secret> — nevar piekļūt, ja izpildās visi šie nosacījumi:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:701
msgid "the L<backend|/BACKEND> is libvirt,"
msgstr "L<aizmugursistēma|/AIZMUGURSISTĒMA> ir libvirt,"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:705
msgid ""
"the image specified by the C<filename> parameter is different from the "
"encrypted RBD disk,"
msgstr ""
"ar parametru C<filename> norādītais attēls atšķiras no šifrētā RBD diska,"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:710
msgid ""
"the image specified by the C<filename> parameter has L<qcow2 format|/COMMON "
"VIRTUAL DISK IMAGE FORMATS>,"
msgstr ""
"ar parametru C<filename> norādītajam attēlam ir L<qcow2 formāts|/IZPLATĪTI "
"VIRTUĀLO DISKU ATTĒLU FORMĀTI>,"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:715
msgid ""
"the encrypted RBD disk is specified as a backing file at some level in the "
"qcow2 backing chain."
msgstr ""
"šifrētais RBD disks ir norādīts kā pamatfails kādā qcow2 pamatķēdes līmenī."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:720
msgid ""
"This limitation is due to libvirt's (justified) separate handling of disks "
"vs. secrets.  When the RBD username and secret are provided inside a qcow2 "
"backing file specification, libvirt does not construct an ephemeral secret "
"object from those, for Ceph authentication.  Refer to "
"L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/2033247>."
msgstr ""
"Šis ierobežojums ir saistīts ar libvirt (pamatotu) atsevišķu disku un "
"noslēpumu apstrādi.  Ja RBD lietotājvārds un noslēpums ir norādīti qcow2 "
"pamatfaila specifikācijā, libvirt no tiem neizveido īslaicīgu noslēpuma "
"objektu Ceph autentifikācijai.  Skatiet L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/"
"2033247>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:726
msgid "FTP AND HTTP"
msgstr "FTP UN HTTP"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:728
msgid "Libguestfs can access remote disks over FTP, FTPS, HTTP or HTTPS protocols."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs var piekļūt attāliem diskiem caur protokoliem FTP, FTPS, HTTP vai "
"HTTPS."

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:734
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char **servers = { \"www.example.org\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"/disk.img\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"http\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, servers,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char **servers = { \"www.example.org\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"/disk.img\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"http\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, servers,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:741
msgid ""
"The C<protocol> can be one of C<\"ftp\">, C<\"ftps\">, C<\"http\">, or "
"C<\"https\">."
msgstr ""
"C<protocol> var būt viens no C<\"ftp\">, C<\"ftps\">, C<\"http\"> vai "
"C<\"https\">."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:744
msgid ""
"C<servers> (the C<server> parameter) is a list which must have a single "
"element.  The single element is a string defining the web or FTP server.  "
"The format of this string is documented in L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>."
msgstr ""
"C<servers> (parametrs C<server>) ir saraksts, kurā jābūt vienam elementam.  "
"Šis viens elements ir virkne, kas definē tīmekļa vai FTP serveri.  Šīs "
"virknes formāts ir dokumentēts L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:749
msgid "GLUSTER"
msgstr "GLUSTER"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:751
msgid "Glusterfs support was removed in libguestfs 1.54 (2024)."
msgstr "Glusterfs atbalsts tika noņemts libguestfs 1.54 (2024)."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:753
msgid "ISCSI"
msgstr "ISCSI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:755
msgid "Libguestfs can access iSCSI disks remotely."
msgstr "Libguestfs var attāli piekļūt iSCSI diskiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:757
msgid "To do this, set the optional C<protocol> and C<server> parameters like this:"
msgstr ""
"Lai to izdarītu, iestatiet neobligātos parametrus C<protocol> un C<server> "
"šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:760
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char **server = { \"iscsi.example.org:3000\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"target-iqn-name/lun\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"iscsi\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, server,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char **server = { \"iscsi.example.org:3000\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"target-iqn-name/lun\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"iscsi\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, server,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:767
msgid ""
"The C<server> parameter is a list which must have a single element.  The "
"single element is a string defining the iSCSI server.  The format of this "
"string is documented in L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<server> ir saraksts, kurā jābūt vienam elementam.  Šis viens "
"elements ir virkne, kas definē iSCSI serveri.  Šīs virknes formāts ir "
"dokumentēts L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:771
msgid "NETWORK BLOCK DEVICE"
msgstr "TĪKLA BLOKU IERĪCE"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:773
msgid "Libguestfs can access Network Block Device (NBD) disks remotely."
msgstr "Libguestfs var attāli piekļūt Network Block Device (NBD) diskiem."

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:778
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char **server = { \"nbd.example.org:3000\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"\" /* export name - see below */,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"nbd\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, server,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char **server = { \"nbd.example.org:3000\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"\" /* export name - see below */,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"nbd\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, server,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:791
msgid ""
"C<server> is in fact a list of servers.  For NBD you must always supply a "
"list with a single element.  (Other remote protocols require zero or more "
"than one server, hence the requirement for this parameter to be a list)."
msgstr ""
"C<server> patiesībā ir serveru saraksts.  NBD vienmēr jānodod saraksts ar "
"vienu elementu.  (Citiem attāliem protokoliem nepieciešami nulle vai vairāk "
"nekā viens serveris, tāpēc šim parametram jābūt sarakstam.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:798
msgid ""
"The C<server> string is documented in L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>.  To "
"connect to a local qemu-nbd instance over a Unix domain socket, use "
"C<\"unix:/path/to/socket\">."
msgstr ""
"Virkne C<server> ir dokumentēta L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>.  Lai savienotos "
"ar lokālu qemu-nbd instanci caur Unix domēna ligzdu, izmantojiet C<\"unix:/"
"path/to/socket\">."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:804
msgid ""
"The C<filename> parameter is the NBD export name.  Use an empty string to "
"mean the default export.  Many NBD servers, including qemu-nbd, do not "
"support export names."
msgstr ""
"Parametrs C<filename> ir NBD eksporta nosaukums.  Izmantojiet tukšu virkni, "
"lai norādītu noklusējuma eksportu.  Daudzi NBD serveri, ieskaitot qemu-nbd, "
"neatbalsta eksporta nosaukumus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:810
msgid ""
"If using qemu-nbd as your server, you should always specify the C<-t> "
"option.  The reason is that libguestfs may open several connections to the "
"server."
msgstr ""
"Ja kā serveri izmantojat qemu-nbd, vienmēr jānorāda opcija C<-t>.  Iemesls "
"ir tāds, ka libguestfs var atvērt vairākus savienojumus ar serveri."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:816
msgid ""
"The libvirt backend requires that you set the C<format> parameter of "
"L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> accurately when you use writable NBD disks."
msgstr ""
"Libvirt aizmugursistēma pieprasa, lai, izmantojot rakstāmus NBD diskus, "
"precīzi iestatītu L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> parametru C<format>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:821
msgid ""
"The libvirt backend has a bug that stops Unix domain socket connections from "
"working: L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=922888>"
msgstr ""
"Libvirt aizmugursistēmai ir kļūda, kas neļauj darboties Unix domēna ligzdu "
"savienojumiem: L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=922888>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:827
msgid ""
"The direct backend does not support readonly connections because of a bug in "
"qemu: L<https://bugs.launchpad.net/qemu/+bug/1155677>"
msgstr ""
"Tiešā aizmugursistēma neatbalsta tikai lasāmus savienojumus qemu kļūdas dēļ: "
"L<https://bugs.launchpad.net/qemu/+bug/1155677>"

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:833
msgid "SHEEPDOG"
msgstr "SHEEPDOG"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:835
msgid "Sheepdog support was removed in libguestfs 1.54 (2024)."
msgstr "Sheepdog atbalsts tika noņemts libguestfs 1.54 (2024)."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:837
msgid "SSH"
msgstr "SSH"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:839
msgid "Libguestfs can access disks over a Secure Shell (SSH) connection."
msgstr "Libguestfs var piekļūt diskiem caur Secure Shell (SSH) savienojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:841
msgid ""
"To do this, set the C<protocol> and C<server> and (optionally)  C<username> "
"parameters of L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> like this:"
msgstr ""
"Lai to izdarītu, iestatiet L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> parametrus C<protocol> "
"un C<server> un (pēc izvēles) C<username> šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:844
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char **server = { \"remote.example.com\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"/path/to/disk.img\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"ssh\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, server,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_USERNAME, \"remoteuser\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char **server = { \"remote.example.com\", NULL };\n"
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, \"/path/to/disk.img\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"raw\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_PROTOCOL, \"ssh\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_SERVER, server,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_USERNAME, \"remoteuser\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:852
msgid "The format of the server string is documented in L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>."
msgstr "Servera virknes formāts ir dokumentēts L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:855
msgid "INSPECTION"
msgstr "INSPICĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:857
msgid ""
"Libguestfs has APIs for inspecting an unknown disk image to find out if it "
"contains operating systems, an install CD or a live CD."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs ir API nezināma diska attēla inspicēšanai, lai noskaidrotu, vai "
"tajā ir operētājsistēmas, instalēšanas CD vai live CD."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:860
msgid ""
"Add all disks belonging to the unknown virtual machine and call "
"L</guestfs_launch> in the usual way."
msgstr ""
"Pievienojiet visus nezināmajai virtuālajai mašīnai piederošos diskus un "
"parastajā veidā izsauciet L</guestfs_launch>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:863
msgid ""
"Then call L</guestfs_inspect_os>.  This function uses other libguestfs calls "
"and certain heuristics, and returns a list of operating systems that were "
"found.  An empty list means none were found.  A single element is the root "
"filesystem of the operating system.  For dual- or multi-boot guests, "
"multiple roots can be returned, each one corresponding to a separate "
"operating system.  (Multi-boot virtual machines are extremely rare in the "
"world of virtualization, but since this scenario can happen, we have built "
"libguestfs to deal with it.)"
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam izsauciet L</guestfs_inspect_os>.  Šī funkcija izmanto citus "
"libguestfs izsaukumus un noteiktu heiristiku un atgriež atrasto "
"operētājsistēmu sarakstu.  Tukšs saraksts nozīmē, ka neviena netika "
"atrasta.  Viens elements ir operētājsistēmas saknes failu sistēma.  "
"Divsāknēšanas vai vairāksāknēšanas viesiem var tikt atgrieztas vairākas "
"saknes, katra atbilstoša atsevišķai operētājsistēmai.  (Vairāksāknēšanas "
"virtuālās mašīnas virtualizācijas pasaulē ir ārkārtīgi retas, bet, tā kā "
"šāds scenārijs var gadīties, esam uzbūvējuši libguestfs, lai to apstrādātu.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:872
msgid ""
"For each root, you can then call various C<guestfs_inspect_get_*> functions "
"to get additional details about that operating system.  For example, call "
"L</guestfs_inspect_get_type> to return the string C<windows> or C<linux> for "
"Windows and Linux-based operating systems respectively."
msgstr ""
"Katrai saknei pēc tam varat izsaukt dažādas C<guestfs_inspect_get_*> "
"funkcijas, lai iegūtu papildu informāciju par šo operētājsistēmu.  Piemēram, "
"izsauciet L</guestfs_inspect_get_type>, lai atgrieztu virkni C<windows> vai "
"C<linux> attiecīgi Windows un uz Linux balstītām operētājsistēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:878
msgid ""
"Un*x-like and Linux-based operating systems usually consist of several "
"filesystems which are mounted at boot time (for example, a separate boot "
"partition mounted on F</boot>).  The inspection rules are able to detect how "
"filesystems correspond to mount points.  Call "
"C<guestfs_inspect_get_mountpoints> to get this mapping.  It might return a "
"hash table like this example:"
msgstr ""
"Un*x līdzīgas un uz Linux balstītas operētājsistēmas parasti sastāv no "
"vairākām failu sistēmām, kas tiek montētas sāknēšanas laikā (piemēram, "
"atsevišķs sāknēšanas nodalījums, kas montēts F</boot>).  Inspicēšanas "
"kārtulas spēj noteikt, kā failu sistēmas atbilst montēšanas punktiem.  "
"Izsauciet C<guestfs_inspect_get_mountpoints>, lai iegūtu šo kartējumu.  Tas "
"var atgriezt jaucējtabulu kā šajā piemērā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:885
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /boot => /dev/sda1\n"
" /     => /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
" /usr  => /dev/vg_guest/lv_usr\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /boot => /dev/sda1\n"
" /     => /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
" /usr  => /dev/vg_guest/lv_usr\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:889
msgid ""
"The caller can then make calls to L</guestfs_mount> to mount the filesystems "
"as suggested."
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam izsaucējs var izsaukt L</guestfs_mount>, lai montētu failu sistēmas, "
"kā ieteikts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:892
msgid ""
"Be careful to mount filesystems in the right order (eg. F</> before "
"F</usr>).  Sorting the keys of the hash by length, shortest first, should "
"work."
msgstr ""
"Uzmanieties montēt failu sistēmas pareizā secībā (piem., F</> pirms F</usr>)"
".  Jaucējtabulas atslēgu kārtošanai pēc garuma, sākot ar īsāko, vajadzētu "
"darboties."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:896
msgid ""
"Inspection currently only works for some common operating systems.  "
"Contributors are welcome to send patches for other operating systems that we "
"currently cannot detect."
msgstr ""
"Inspicēšana pašlaik darbojas tikai dažām izplatītām operētājsistēmām.  "
"Ieguldītāji ir aicināti sūtīt ielāpus citām operētājsistēmām, kuras pašlaik "
"nevaram noteikt."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:900
msgid ""
"Encrypted disks must be opened before inspection.  See L</ENCRYPTED DISKS> "
"for more details.  The L</guestfs_inspect_os> function just ignores any "
"encrypted devices."
msgstr ""
"Šifrētie diski jāatver pirms inspicēšanas.  Sīkāk skatiet L</ŠIFRĒTI DISKI>"
".  Funkcija L</guestfs_inspect_os> vienkārši ignorē visas šifrētās ierīces."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:904
msgid ""
"A note on the implementation: The call L</guestfs_inspect_os> performs "
"inspection and caches the results in the guest handle.  Subsequent calls to "
"C<guestfs_inspect_get_*> return this cached information, but I<do not> "
"re-read the disks.  If you change the content of the guest disks, you can "
"redo inspection by calling L</guestfs_inspect_os> again.  "
"(L</guestfs_inspect_list_applications2> works a little differently from the "
"other calls and does read the disks.  See documentation for that function "
"for details)."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme par realizāciju: izsaukums L</guestfs_inspect_os> veic inspicēšanu "
"un kešo rezultātus viesa rokturī.  Nākamie C<guestfs_inspect_get_*> "
"izsaukumi atgriež šo kešoto informāciju, bet I<atkārtoti nenolasa> diskus.  "
"Ja maināt viesa disku saturu, inspicēšanu var veikt no jauna, vēlreiz "
"izsaucot L</guestfs_inspect_os>.  (L</guestfs_inspect_list_applications2> "
"darbojas nedaudz citādi nekā pārējie izsaukumi un nolasa diskus.  Sīkāk "
"skatiet šīs funkcijas dokumentāciju.)"

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:913
msgid "INSPECTING INSTALL DISKS"
msgstr "INSTALĒŠANAS DISKU INSPICĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:915
msgid ""
"Libguestfs (since 1.9.4) can detect some install disks, install CDs, live "
"CDs and more."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs (kopš 1.9.4) var noteikt dažus instalēšanas diskus, instalēšanas "
"CD, live CD u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:918
msgid ""
"Further information is available about the operating system that can be "
"installed using the regular inspection APIs like "
"L</guestfs_inspect_get_product_name>, L</guestfs_inspect_get_major_version> "
"etc."
msgstr ""
"Papildu informācija par operētājsistēmu, ko var instalēt, ir pieejama, "
"izmantojot parastās inspicēšanas API, piemēram, L</"
"guestfs_inspect_get_product_name>, L</guestfs_inspect_get_major_version> u. "
"c."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:923
msgid "SPECIAL CONSIDERATIONS FOR WINDOWS GUESTS"
msgstr "ĪPAŠI APSVĒRUMI WINDOWS VIESIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:925
msgid ""
"Libguestfs can mount NTFS partitions.  It does this using the "
"L<http://www.ntfs-3g.org/> driver."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs var montēt NTFS nodalījumus.  Tā to dara, izmantojot draiveri "
"L<http://www.ntfs-3g.org/>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:928
msgid "DRIVE LETTERS AND PATHS"
msgstr "DISKU BURTI UN CEĻI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:930
msgid ""
"DOS and Windows still use drive letters, and the filesystems are always "
"treated as case insensitive by Windows itself, and therefore you might find "
"a Windows configuration file referring to a path like "
"C<c:\\windows\\system32>.  When the filesystem is mounted in libguestfs, "
"that directory might be referred to as F</WINDOWS/System32>."
msgstr ""
"DOS un Windows joprojām izmanto disku burtus, un pats Windows failu sistēmas "
"vienmēr uzskata par reģistrnejutīgām, tāpēc varat atrast Windows "
"konfigurācijas failu, kas atsaucas uz tādu ceļu kā C<c:\\windows\\system32>"
".  Kad failu sistēma ir montēta libguestfs, uz šo direktoriju var atsaukties "
"kā F</WINDOWS/System32>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:936
msgid ""
"Drive letter mappings can be found using inspection (see L</INSPECTION> and "
"L</guestfs_inspect_get_drive_mappings>)"
msgstr ""
"Disku burtu kartējumus var atrast, izmantojot inspicēšanu (skatiet L</"
"INSPICĒŠANA> un L</guestfs_inspect_get_drive_mappings>)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:939
msgid ""
"Dealing with separator characters (backslash vs forward slash) is outside "
"the scope of libguestfs, but usually a simple character replacement will "
"work."
msgstr ""
"Darbs ar atdalītāju rakstzīmēm (atpakaļvērstā slīpsvītra pret parasto "
"slīpsvītru) ir ārpus libguestfs darbības jomas, bet parasti pietiek ar "
"vienkāršu rakstzīmju aizstāšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:943
msgid ""
"To resolve the case insensitivity of paths, call "
"L</guestfs_case_sensitive_path>."
msgstr ""
"Lai atrisinātu ceļu reģistrnejutīgumu, izsauciet L</"
"guestfs_case_sensitive_path>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:946
msgid "LONG FILENAMES ON NTFS"
msgstr "GARI FAILU NOSAUKUMI NTFS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:948
msgid ""
"NTFS supports filenames up to 255 characters long.  \"Character\" means a 2 "
"byte UTF-16 codepoint which can encode the most common Unicode codepoints."
msgstr ""
"NTFS atbalsta failu nosaukumus līdz 255 rakstzīmēm.  „Rakstzīme” nozīmē 2 "
"baitu UTF-16 koda punktu, kas var kodēt biežākos Unikoda koda punktus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:952
msgid ""
"Most Linux filesystems support filenames up to 255 I<bytes>.  This means you "
"may get an error:"
msgstr ""
"Lielākā daļa Linux failu sistēmu atbalsta failu nosaukumus līdz 255 "
"I<baitiem>.  Tas nozīmē, ka varat saņemt kļūdu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:955
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" File name too long\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" File name too long\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:957
msgid ""
"when you copy a file from NTFS to a Linux filesystem if the name, when "
"reencoded as UTF-8, would exceed 255 bytes in length."
msgstr ""
"kopējot failu no NTFS uz Linux failu sistēmu, ja nosaukums, pārkodēts UTF-8, "
"pārsniegtu 255 baitu garumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:960
msgid ""
"This will most often happen when using non-ASCII names that are longer than "
"~127 characters (eg. Greek, Cyrillic) or longer than ~85 characters (Asian "
"languages)."
msgstr ""
"Visbiežāk tas notiks, izmantojot ne-ASCII nosaukumus, kas garāki par ~127 "
"rakstzīmēm (piem., grieķu, kirilica) vai garāki par ~85 rakstzīmēm (Āzijas "
"valodas)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:964
msgid ""
"A workaround is not to try to store such long filenames on Linux native "
"filesystems.  Since the L<tar(1)> format can store unlimited length "
"filenames, keep the files in a tarball."
msgstr ""
"Apiešana ir nemēģināt glabāt tik garus failu nosaukumus Linux vietējās failu "
"sistēmās.  Tā kā formāts L<tar(1)> var glabāt neierobežota garuma failu "
"nosaukumus, glabājiet failus tar arhīvā."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:968
msgid "ACCESSING THE WINDOWS REGISTRY"
msgstr "PIEKĻUVE WINDOWS REĢISTRAM"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:970
msgid ""
"Libguestfs also provides some help for decoding Windows Registry \"hive\" "
"files, through a separate C library called L<hivex(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs arī sniedz zināmu palīdzību Windows reģistra „stropu” failu "
"atkodēšanā, izmantojot atsevišķu C bibliotēku L<hivex(3)>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:973
msgid ""
"Before libguestfs 1.19.35 you had to download the hive file, operate on it "
"locally using hivex, and upload it again.  Since this version, we have "
"included the major hivex APIs directly in the libguestfs API (see "
"L</guestfs_hivex_open>).  This means that if you have opened a Windows "
"guest, you can read and write the registry directly."
msgstr ""
"Pirms libguestfs 1.19.35 stropa fails bija jālejupielādē, ar to jāstrādā "
"lokāli, izmantojot hivex, un jāaugšupielādē atpakaļ.  Kopš šīs versijas "
"galvenās hivex API esam iekļāvuši tieši libguestfs API (skatiet L</"
"guestfs_hivex_open>).  Tas nozīmē, ka, ja Windows viesis ir atvērts, "
"reģistru varat lasīt un rakstīt tieši."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:979
msgid "See also L<virt-win-reg(1)>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<virt-win-reg(1)>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:981
msgid "SYMLINKS ON NTFS-3G FILESYSTEMS"
msgstr "SIMBOLISKĀS SAITES NTFS-3G FAILU SISTĒMĀS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:983
msgid ""
"Ntfs-3g tries to rewrite \"Junction Points\" and NTFS \"symbolic links\" to "
"provide something which looks like a Linux symlink.  The way it tries to do "
"the rewriting is described here:"
msgstr ""
"Ntfs-3g mēģina pārrakstīt „savienojuma punktus” (Junction Points) un NTFS „"
"simboliskās saites”, lai nodrošinātu kaut ko, kas izskatās pēc Linux "
"simboliskās saites.  Veids, kā tas mēģina veikt pārrakstīšanu, aprakstīts "
"šeit:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:987
msgid "L<https://github.com/tuxera/ntfs-3g/wiki/Junctions-Points,-Symbolic-Links-and-Reparse-Points>"
msgstr ""
"L<https://github.com/tuxera/ntfs-3g/wiki/Junctions-Points,-Symbolic-Links-"
"and-Reparse-Points>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:989
msgid ""
"The essential problem is that ntfs-3g simply does not have enough "
"information to do a correct job.  NTFS links can contain drive letters and "
"references to external device GUIDs that ntfs-3g has no way of resolving.  "
"It is almost certainly the case that libguestfs callers should ignore what "
"ntfs-3g does (ie. don't use L</guestfs_readlink> on NTFS volumes)."
msgstr ""
"Būtiskā problēma ir tā, ka ntfs-3g vienkārši nav pietiekami daudz "
"informācijas, lai darbu izdarītu pareizi.  NTFS saites var saturēt disku "
"burtus un atsauces uz ārējo ierīču GUID, kurus ntfs-3g nekādi nevar "
"atrisināt.  Gandrīz noteikti libguestfs izsaucējiem jāignorē tas, ko dara "
"ntfs-3g (t. i., neizmantojiet L</guestfs_readlink> NTFS sējumos)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:996
msgid ""
"Instead if you encounter a symbolic link on an ntfs-3g filesystem, use "
"L</guestfs_lgetxattr> to read the C<system.ntfs_reparse_data> extended "
"attribute, and read the raw reparse data from that (you can find the format "
"documented in various places around the web)."
msgstr ""
"Tā vietā, ja ntfs-3g failu sistēmā sastopat simbolisko saiti, izmantojiet L</"
"guestfs_lgetxattr>, lai nolasītu paplašināto atribūtu "
"C<system.ntfs_reparse_data>, un no tā nolasiet neapstrādātos reparse datus "
"(formāts ir dokumentēts dažādās vietās tīmeklī)."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1001
msgid "EXTENDED ATTRIBUTES ON NTFS-3G FILESYSTEMS"
msgstr "PAPLAŠINĀTIE ATRIBŪTI NTFS-3G FAILU SISTĒMĀS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1003
msgid ""
"There are other useful extended attributes that can be read from ntfs-3g "
"filesystems (using L</guestfs_getxattr>).  See:"
msgstr ""
"Ir arī citi noderīgi paplašinātie atribūti, ko var nolasīt no ntfs-3g failu "
"sistēmām (izmantojot L</guestfs_getxattr>).  Skatiet:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1006
msgid "L<https://github.com/tuxera/ntfs-3g/wiki/Using-Extended-Attributes>"
msgstr "L<https://github.com/tuxera/ntfs-3g/wiki/Using-Extended-Attributes>"

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1008
msgid "WINDOWS HIBERNATION AND WINDOWS 8 FAST STARTUP"
msgstr "WINDOWS HIBERNĀCIJA UN WINDOWS 8 ĀTRĀ STARTĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1010
msgid ""
"Windows guests which have been hibernated (instead of fully shut down)  "
"cannot be mounted.  This is a limitation of ntfs-3g.  You will see an error "
"like this:"
msgstr ""
"Windows viesus, kas ir hibernēti (nevis pilnībā izslēgti), nevar montēt.  "
"Tas ir ntfs-3g ierobežojums.  Redzēsiet šādu kļūdu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1014
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" The disk contains an unclean file system (0, 0).\n"
" Metadata kept in Windows cache, refused to mount.\n"
" Failed to mount '/dev/sda2': Operation not permitted\n"
" The NTFS partition is in an unsafe state. Please resume\n"
" and shutdown Windows fully (no hibernation or fast\n"
" restarting), or mount the volume read-only with the\n"
" 'ro' mount option.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" The disk contains an unclean file system (0, 0).\n"
" Metadata kept in Windows cache, refused to mount.\n"
" Failed to mount '/dev/sda2': Operation not permitted\n"
" The NTFS partition is in an unsafe state. Please resume\n"
" and shutdown Windows fully (no hibernation or fast\n"
" restarting), or mount the volume read-only with the\n"
" 'ro' mount option.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1022
msgid ""
"In Windows 8, the shutdown button does not shut down the guest at all.  "
"Instead it usually hibernates the guest.  This is known as \"fast startup\"."
msgstr ""
"Windows 8 izslēgšanas poga viesi vispār neizslēdz.  Tā vietā tā parasti "
"hibernē viesi.  To sauc par „ātro palaišanu”."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1026
msgid "Some suggested workarounds are:"
msgstr "Daži ieteiktie apiešanas veidi ir:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1032
msgid "Mount read-only (eg. L</guestfs_mount_ro>)."
msgstr "Montēt tikai lasīšanai (piem., L</guestfs_mount_ro>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1036
msgid ""
"On Windows 8, turn off fast startup.  It is in the Control Panel → Power "
"Options → Choose what the power buttons do → Change settings that are "
"currently unavailable → Turn on fast startup."
msgstr ""
"Windows 8 izslēdziet ātro palaišanu.  Tā atrodas: Control Panel → Power "
"Options → Choose what the power buttons do → Change settings that are "
"currently unavailable → Turn on fast startup."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1042
msgid ""
"On Windows 7 and earlier, shut the guest off properly instead of hibernating "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Windows 7 un vecākās versijās viesi izslēdziet pareizi, nevis hibernējiet."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1047
msgid "RESIZE2FS ERRORS"
msgstr "RESIZE2FS KĻŪDAS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1049
msgid ""
"The L</guestfs_resize2fs>, L</guestfs_resize2fs_size> and "
"L</guestfs_resize2fs_M> calls are used to resize ext2/3/4 filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Izsaukumi L</guestfs_resize2fs>, L</guestfs_resize2fs_size> un L</"
"guestfs_resize2fs_M> tiek izmantoti ext2/3/4 failu sistēmu izmēra maiņai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1052
msgid ""
"The underlying program (L<resize2fs(8)>) requires that the filesystem is "
"clean and recently fsck'd before you can resize it.  Also, if the resize "
"operation fails for some reason, then you had to call fsck the filesystem "
"again to fix it."
msgstr ""
"Pamatā esošā programma (L<resize2fs(8)>) pieprasa, lai pirms izmēra maiņas "
"failu sistēma būtu tīra un nesen pārbaudīta ar fsck.  Turklāt, ja izmēra "
"maiņas darbība kāda iemesla dēļ neizdodas, failu sistēmai atkal bija "
"jāizsauc fsck, lai to izlabotu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1057
msgid ""
"In libguestfs C<lt> 1.17.14, you usually had to call L</guestfs_e2fsck_f> "
"before the resize.  However, in C<ge> 1.17.14, L<e2fsck(8)> is called "
"automatically before the resize, so you no longer need to do this."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs C<lt> 1.17.14 pirms izmēra maiņas parasti bija jāizsauc L</"
"guestfs_e2fsck_f>.  Tomēr C<ge> 1.17.14 pirms izmēra maiņas automātiski tiek "
"izsaukts L<e2fsck(8)>, tāpēc tas vairs nav jādara."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1062
msgid ""
"The L<resize2fs(8)> program can still fail, in which case it prints an error "
"message similar to:"
msgstr ""
"Programma L<resize2fs(8)> joprojām var neizdoties, tādā gadījumā tā izdrukā "
"kļūdas ziņojumu, līdzīgu šim:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1065
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Please run 'e2fsck -fy <device>' to fix the filesystem\n"
" after the aborted resize operation.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Please run 'e2fsck -fy <device>' to fix the filesystem\n"
" after the aborted resize operation.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1068
msgid ""
"You can do this by calling L</guestfs_e2fsck> with the C<forceall> option.  "
"However in the context of disk images, it is usually better to avoid this "
"situation, eg. by rolling back to an earlier snapshot, or by copying and "
"resizing and on failure going back to the original."
msgstr ""
"To var izdarīt, izsaucot L</guestfs_e2fsck> ar opciju C<forceall>.  Tomēr "
"disku attēlu kontekstā parasti labāk izvairīties no šādas situācijas, piem., "
"atritinot uz agrāku momentuzņēmumu vai kopējot un mainot izmēru un "
"neveiksmes gadījumā atgriežoties pie oriģināla."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1073
msgid "USING LIBGUESTFS WITH OTHER PROGRAMMING LANGUAGES"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS IZMANTOŠANA AR CITĀM PROGRAMMĒŠANAS VALODĀM"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1075
msgid ""
"Although we don’t want to discourage you from using the C API, we will "
"mention here that the same API is also available in other languages."
msgstr ""
"Lai gan nevēlamies jūs atrunāt no C API izmantošanas, šeit pieminēsim, ka tā "
"pati API ir pieejama arī citās valodās."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1078
msgid ""
"The API is broadly identical in all supported languages.  This means that "
"the C call C<guestfs_add_drive_ro(g,file)> is C<$g-E<gt>add_drive_ro($file)> "
"in Perl, C<g.add_drive_ro(file)> in Python, and C<g#add_drive_ro file> in "
"OCaml.  In other words, a straightforward, predictable isomorphism between "
"each language."
msgstr ""
"API visās atbalstītajās valodās ir būtībā identiska.  Tas nozīmē, ka C "
"izsaukums C<guestfs_add_drive_ro(g,file)> Perl ir C<$g-E<gt>add_drive_ro"
"($file)>, Python C<g.add_drive_ro(file)> un OCaml C<g#add_drive_ro file>.  "
"Citiem vārdiem, vienkāršs, paredzams izomorfisms starp katru valodu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1084
msgid ""
"Error messages are automatically transformed into exceptions if the language "
"supports it."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdu ziņojumi tiek automātiski pārveidoti izņēmumos, ja valoda to atbalsta."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1087
msgid ""
"We don’t try to \"object orientify\" parts of the API in OO languages, "
"although contributors are welcome to write higher level APIs above what we "
"provide in their favourite languages if they wish."
msgstr ""
"OO valodās nemēģinām „objektorientēt” API daļas, lai gan ieguldītāji ir "
"aicināti, ja vēlas, savās iecienītajās valodās rakstīt augstāka līmeņa API "
"virs tā, ko nodrošinām."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1093
msgid "B<C++>"
msgstr "B<C++>"

#. type: textblock
