msgstr "Skatiet L<guestfish(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1195
msgid "LIBGUESTFS GOTCHAS"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS SLAZDI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1197
msgid ""
"L<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotcha_(programming)>: \"A feature of a "
"system [...] that works in the way it is documented but is counterintuitive "
"and almost invites mistakes.\""
msgstr ""
"L<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotcha_(programming)>: „Sistēmas līdzeklis "
"[...], kas darbojas tā, kā dokumentēts, bet ir pretintuitīvs un gandrīz "
"aicina kļūdīties.”"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1201
msgid ""
"Since we developed libguestfs and the associated tools, there are several "
"things we would have designed differently, but are now stuck with for "
"backwards compatibility or other reasons.  If there is ever a libguestfs 2.0 "
"release, you can expect these to change.  Beware of them."
msgstr ""
"Kopš izstrādājām libguestfs un saistītos rīkus, ir vairākas lietas, ko būtu "
"izstrādājuši citādi, bet ar kurām tagad esam saistīti atpakaļsaderības vai "
"citu iemeslu dēļ.  Ja kādreiz būs libguestfs 2.0 laidiens, varat sagaidīt, "
"ka tās mainīsies.  Uzmanieties no tām."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1209
msgid "Read-only should be the default."
msgstr "Noklusējumam jābūt tikai lasīšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1211
msgid ""
"In L<guestfish(3)>, I<--ro> should be the default, and you should have to "
"specify I<--rw> if you want to make changes to the image."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(3)> noklusējumam jābūt I<--ro>, un, ja vēlaties veikt izmaiņas "
"attēlā, būtu jānorāda I<--rw>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1214
msgid "This would reduce the potential to corrupt live VM images."
msgstr "Tas samazinātu iespēju sabojāt darbojošos VM attēlus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1216
msgid ""
"Note that many filesystems change the disk when you just mount and unmount, "
"even if you didn't perform any writes.  You need to use "
"L</guestfs_add_drive_ro> to guarantee that the disk is not changed."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka daudzas failu sistēmas maina disku, jau vienkārši montējot "
"un atmontējot, pat ja neveicāt nekādu rakstīšanu.  Lai garantētu, ka disks "
"netiek mainīts, jāizmanto L</guestfs_add_drive_ro>."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1220
msgid "guestfish command line is hard to use."
msgstr "guestfish komandrinda ir grūti lietojama."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1222
msgid ""
"F<guestfish disk.img> doesn't do what people expect (open F<disk.img> for "
"examination).  It tries to run a guestfish command F<disk.img> which doesn't "
"exist, so it fails.  In earlier versions of guestfish the error message was "
"also unintuitive, but we have corrected this since.  Like the Bourne shell, "
"we should have used C<guestfish -c command> to run commands."
msgstr ""
"F<guestfish disk.img> nedara to, ko cilvēki gaida (atvērt F<disk.img> "
"pārbaudei).  Tas mēģina izpildīt guestfish komandu F<disk.img>, kas "
"neeksistē, tāpēc tas neizdodas.  Agrākās guestfish versijās arī kļūdas "
"ziņojums bija neintuitīvs, bet kopš tā laika esam to izlabojuši.  Tāpat kā "
"Bourne čaulā, komandu izpildei vajadzēja izmantot C<guestfish -c command>."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1229
msgid "guestfish megabyte modifiers don’t work right on all commands"
msgstr "guestfish megabaitu modifikatori nedarbojas pareizi visās komandās"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1231
msgid ""
"In recent guestfish you can use C<1M> to mean 1 megabyte (and similarly for "
"other modifiers).  What guestfish actually does is to multiply the number "
"part by the modifier part and pass the result to the C API.  However this "
"doesn't work for a few APIs which aren't expecting bytes, but are already "
"expecting some other unit (eg. megabytes)."
msgstr ""
"Jaunākajā guestfish varat izmantot C<1M>, lai apzīmētu 1 megabaitu (un "
"līdzīgi citiem modifikatoriem).  Tas, ko guestfish faktiski dara, ir reizina "
"skaitļa daļu ar modifikatora daļu un nodod rezultātu C API.  Tomēr tas "
"nedarbojas dažām API, kas negaida baitus, bet jau gaida kādu citu vienību "
"(piem., megabaitus)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1238
msgid "The most common is L</guestfs_lvcreate>.  The guestfish command:"
msgstr "Visizplatītākā ir L</guestfs_lvcreate>.  Guestfish komanda:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1240
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" lvcreate LV VG 100M\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" lvcreate LV VG 100M\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1242
msgid ""
"does not do what you might expect.  Instead because L</guestfs_lvcreate> is "
"already expecting megabytes, this tries to create a 100 I<terabyte> (100 "
"megabytes * megabytes) logical volume.  The error message you get from this "
"is also a little obscure."
msgstr ""
"nedara to, ko varētu gaidīt.  Tā vietā, tā kā L</guestfs_lvcreate> jau gaida "
"megabaitus, tā mēģina izveidot 100 I<terabaitu> (100 megabaiti * megabaiti) "
"loģisko sējumu.  Kļūdas ziņojums, ko par to saņemat, arī ir nedaudz "
"neskaidrs."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1247
msgid ""
"This could be fixed in the generator by specially marking parameters and "
"return values which take bytes or other units."
msgstr ""
"To varētu izlabot ģeneratorā, īpaši atzīmējot parametrus un atgriešanas "
"vērtības, kas pieņem baitus vai citas vienības."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1250
msgid "Ambiguity between devices and paths"
msgstr "Neviennozīmība starp ierīcēm un ceļiem"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1252
msgid ""
"There is a subtle ambiguity in the API between a device name "
"(eg. F</dev/sdb2>) and a similar pathname.  A file might just happen to be "
"called C<sdb2> in the directory F</dev> (consider some non-Unix VM image)."
msgstr ""
"API ir smalka neviennozīmība starp ierīces nosaukumu (piem., F</dev/sdb2>) "
"un līdzīgu ceļa nosaukumu.  Fails direktorijā F</dev> var gadīties ar "
"nosaukumu C<sdb2> (iedomājieties kādu ne-Unix VM attēlu)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1257
msgid ""
"In the current API we usually resolve this ambiguity by having two separate "
"calls, for example L</guestfs_checksum> and L</guestfs_checksum_device>.  "
"Some API calls are ambiguous and (incorrectly) resolve the problem by "
"detecting if the path supplied begins with F</dev/>."
msgstr ""
"Pašreizējā API šo neviennozīmību parasti atrisinām, izmantojot divus "
"atsevišķus izsaukumus, piemēram, L</guestfs_checksum> un L</"
"guestfs_checksum_device>.  Daži API izsaukumi ir neviennozīmīgi un "
"(nepareizi) atrisina problēmu, nosakot, vai norādītais ceļš sākas ar F</dev/>"
"."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1263
msgid ""
"To avoid both the ambiguity and the need to duplicate some calls, we could "
"make paths/devices into structured names.  One way to do this would be to "
"use a notation like grub (C<hd(0,0)>), although nobody really likes this "
"aspect of grub.  Another way would be to use a structured type, equivalent "
"to this OCaml type:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izvairītos gan no neviennozīmības, gan no nepieciešamības dublēt dažus "
"izsaukumus, ceļus/ierīces varētu padarīt par strukturētiem nosaukumiem.  "
"Viens veids būtu izmantot grub līdzīgu notāciju (C<hd(0,0)>), lai gan šis "
"grub aspekts īsti nevienam nepatīk.  Cits veids būtu izmantot strukturētu "
"tipu, līdzvērtīgu šim OCaml tipam:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1269
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" type path = Path of string | Device of int | Partition of int * int\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" type path = Path of string | Device of int | Partition of int * int\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1271
msgid "which would allow you to pass arguments like:"
msgstr "kas ļautu nodot tādus argumentus kā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1273
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Path \"/foo/bar\"\n"
" Device 1            (* /dev/sdb, or perhaps /dev/sda *)\n"
" Partition (1, 2)    (* /dev/sdb2 (or is it /dev/sda2 or /dev/sdb3?) *)\n"
" Path \"/dev/sdb2\"    (* not a device *)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Path \"/foo/bar\"\n"
" Device 1            (* /dev/sdb, or perhaps /dev/sda *)\n"
" Partition (1, 2)    (* /dev/sdb2 (or is it /dev/sda2 or /dev/sdb3?) *)\n"
" Path \"/dev/sdb2\"    (* not a device *)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1278
msgid ""
"As you can see there are still problems to resolve even with this "
"representation.  Also consider how it might work in guestfish."
msgstr ""
"Kā redzams, pat ar šo attēlojumu joprojām ir atrisināmas problēmas.  "
"Padomājiet arī, kā tas varētu darboties guestfish."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1283
msgid "KEYS AND PASSPHRASES"
msgstr "ATSLĒGAS UN PAROĻFRĀZES"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1285
msgid ""
"Certain libguestfs calls take a parameter that contains sensitive key "
"material, passed in as a C string."
msgstr ""
"Daži libguestfs izsaukumi pieņem parametru, kas satur sensitīvu atslēgas "
"materiālu, nodotu kā C virkni."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1288
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.60 you can pass in 8 bit binary key data (allowing "
"C<'\\n'> or C<'\\0'>) by prefixing the string with:"
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.60 var nodot 8 bitu bināros atslēgas datus (atļaujot C<'\\"
"n'> vai C<'\\0'>), pievienojot virknei priedēkli:"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1293
msgid "C<base64:...>"
msgstr "C<base64:...>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1295
msgid "Pass in base64-encoded key data.  This supports 8 bit binary key data."
msgstr ""
"Nodot base64 kodētus atslēgas datus.  Tas atbalsta 8 bitu bināros atslēgas "
"datus."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1298
msgid "C<text:...>"
msgstr "C<text:...>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1300
msgid ""
"Pass in regular text passphrase.  This does not support 8 bit binary key "
"data."
msgstr ""
"Nodot parastu teksta paroles frāzi.  Tas neatbalsta 8 bitu bināros atslēgas "
"datus."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1303
msgid "Unprefixed"
msgstr "Bez priedēkļa"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1305
msgid ""
"For backwards compatibility with libguestfs E<le> 1.58, a text passphrase "
"can be passed in unprefixed.  However this does not support 8 bit binary key "
"data."
msgstr ""
"Atpakaļsaderībai ar libguestfs E<le> 1.58 teksta paroles frāzi var nodot bez "
"priedēkļa.  Tomēr tas neatbalsta 8 bitu bināros atslēgas datus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1311
msgid ""
"In the future we would hope to change the libguestfs implementation so that "
"keys are L<mlock(2)>-ed into physical RAM, and thus can never end up in "
"swap.  However this is I<not> done at the moment, because of the complexity "
"of such an implementation."
msgstr ""
"Nākotnē ceram mainīt libguestfs realizāciju, lai atslēgas tiktu fiksētas "
"fiziskajā RAM ar L<mlock(2)> un tādējādi nekad nevarētu nonākt maiņatmiņā.  "
"Tomēr pašlaik tas I<netiek> darīts šādas realizācijas sarežģītības dēļ."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1316
msgid ""
"Therefore you should be aware that any key parameter you pass to libguestfs "
"might end up being written out to the swap partition.  If this is a concern, "
"scrub the swap partition or don't use libguestfs on encrypted devices."
msgstr ""
"Tāpēc jāņem vērā, ka jebkurš atslēgas parametrs, ko nododat libguestfs, var "
"tikt izrakstīts maiņatmiņas nodalījumā.  Ja tas rada bažas, attīriet "
"maiņatmiņas nodalījumu vai neizmantojiet libguestfs šifrētās ierīcēs."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1321
msgid "MULTIPLE HANDLES AND MULTIPLE THREADS"
msgstr "VAIRĀKI ROKTURI UN VAIRĀKI PAVEDIENI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1323
msgid ""
"All high-level libguestfs actions are synchronous.  If you want to use "
"libguestfs asynchronously then you must create a thread."
msgstr ""
"Visas augsta līmeņa libguestfs darbības ir sinhronas.  Ja vēlaties izmantot "
"libguestfs asinhroni, jāizveido pavediens."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1326
msgid "Threads in libguestfs E<ge> 1.38"
msgstr "Pavedieni libguestfs E<ge> 1.38"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1328
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.38, each handle (C<guestfs_h>) contains a lock which "
"is acquired automatically when you call a libguestfs function.  The "
"practical effect of this is you can call libguestfs functions with the same "
"handle from multiple threads without needing to do any locking."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.38 katrs rokturis (C<guestfs_h>) satur slēdzeni, kas tiek "
"automātiski iegūta, kad izsaucat libguestfs funkciju.  Praktiskā ietekme ir "
"tāda, ka libguestfs funkcijas ar vienu un to pašu rokturi var izsaukt no "
"vairākiem pavedieniem bez jebkādas bloķēšanas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1334
msgid ""
"Also in libguestfs E<ge> 1.38, the last error on the handle "
"(L</guestfs_last_error>, L</guestfs_last_errno>) is stored in thread-local "
"storage, so it is safe to write code like:"
msgstr ""
"Arī libguestfs E<ge> 1.38 pēdējā roktura kļūda (L</guestfs_last_error>, L</"
"guestfs_last_errno>) tiek glabāta pavedienam lokālā krātuvē, tāpēc ir droši "
"rakstīt tādu kodu kā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1338
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" if (guestfs_add_drive_ro (g, drive) == -1)\n"
"   fprintf (stderr, \"error was: %s\\n\", guestfs_last_error (g));\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" if (guestfs_add_drive_ro (g, drive) == -1)\n"
"   fprintf (stderr, \"error was: %s\\n\", guestfs_last_error (g));\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1341
msgid "even when other threads may be concurrently using the same handle C<g>."
msgstr ""
"pat tad, ja citi pavedieni vienlaikus var izmantot to pašu rokturi C<g>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1343
msgid "Threads in libguestfs E<lt> 1.38"
msgstr "Pavedieni libguestfs E<lt> 1.38"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1345
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<lt> 1.38, you must use the handle only from a single "
"thread.  Either use the handle exclusively from one thread, or provide your "
"own mutex so that two threads cannot issue calls on the same handle at the "
"same time.  Even apparently innocent functions like L</guestfs_get_trace> "
"are I<not> safe to be called from multiple threads without a mutex in "
"libguestfs E<lt> 1.38."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<lt> 1.38 rokturis jāizmanto tikai no viena pavediena.  Vai nu "
"izmantojiet rokturi tikai no viena pavediena, vai nodrošiniet savu mutex, "
"lai divi pavedieni nevarētu vienlaikus izdot izsaukumus vienam rokturim.  "
"Pat šķietami nevainīgas funkcijas, piemēram, L</guestfs_get_trace>, "
"libguestfs E<lt> 1.38 I<nav> droši izsaukt no vairākiem pavedieniem bez "
"mutex."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1352
msgid ""
"Use L</guestfs_set_identifier> to make it simpler to identify threads in "
"trace output."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L</guestfs_set_identifier>, lai atvieglotu pavedienu "
"identificēšanu izsekošanas izvadē."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1357
msgid ""
"Libguestfs needs a supermin appliance, which it finds by looking along an "
"internal path."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs nepieciešama supermin palīgsistēma, ko tā atrod, meklējot iekšējā "
"ceļā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1360
msgid ""
"By default it looks for these in the directory C<$libdir/guestfs> "
"(eg. F</usr/local/lib/guestfs> or F</usr/lib64/guestfs>)."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma tā tās meklē direktorijā C<$libdir/guestfs> (piem., F</usr/"
"local/lib/guestfs> vai F</usr/lib64/guestfs>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1363
msgid ""
"Use L</guestfs_set_path> or set the environment variable L</LIBGUESTFS_PATH> "
"to change the directories that libguestfs will search in.  The value is a "
"colon-separated list of paths.  The current directory is I<not> searched "
"unless the path contains an empty element or C<.>.  For example "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH=:/usr/lib/guestfs> would search the current directory and "
"then F</usr/lib/guestfs>."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L</guestfs_set_path> vai iestatiet vides mainīgo L</"
"LIBGUESTFS_PATH>, lai mainītu direktorijas, kurās libguestfs meklēs.  "
"Vērtība ir ar koliem atdalīts ceļu saraksts.  Pašreizējā direktorija "
"I<netiek> pārmeklēta, ja vien ceļā nav tukša elementa vai C<.>.  Piemēram, "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_PATH=:/usr/lib/guestfs> pārmeklētu pašreizējo direktoriju un "
"pēc tam F</usr/lib/guestfs>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1370
msgid "QEMU WRAPPERS"
msgstr "QEMU IETINĒJI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1372
msgid ""
"If you want to compile your own qemu, run qemu from a non-standard location, "
"or pass extra arguments to qemu, then you can write a shell-script wrapper "
"around qemu."
msgstr ""
"Ja vēlaties kompilēt savu qemu, izpildīt qemu no nestandarta vietas vai "
"nodot qemu papildu argumentus, varat uzrakstīt čaulas skripta ietinēju ap "
"qemu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1376
msgid ""
"There is one important rule to remember: you I<must C<exec qemu>> as the "
"last command in the shell script (so that qemu replaces the shell and "
"becomes the direct child of the libguestfs-using program).  If you don't do "
"this, then the qemu process won't be cleaned up correctly."
msgstr ""
"Jāatceras viena svarīga kārtula: čaulas skripta pēdējai komandai I<jābūt "
"C<exec qemu>> (lai qemu aizstātu čaulu un kļūtu par libguestfs izmantojošās "
"programmas tiešo bērnu).  Ja to nedarāt, qemu process netiks pareizi sakopts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1381
msgid ""
"Here is an example of a wrapper, where I have built my own copy of qemu from "
"source:"
msgstr "Lūk, ietinēja piemērs, kur esmu uzbūvējis savu qemu kopiju no pirmkoda:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1384
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #!/bin/sh -\n"
" qemudir=/home/rjones/d/qemu\n"
" exec $qemudir/x86_64-softmmu/qemu-system-x86_64 -L $qemudir/pc-bios "
"\"$@\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #!/bin/sh -\n"
" qemudir=/home/rjones/d/qemu\n"
" exec $qemudir/x86_64-softmmu/qemu-system-x86_64 -L $qemudir/pc-bios \"$@\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1388
msgid ""
"Save this script as F</tmp/qemu.wrapper> (or wherever), C<chmod +x>, and "
"then use it by setting the LIBGUESTFS_HV environment variable.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Saglabājiet šo skriptu kā F</tmp/qemu.wrapper> (vai jebkur), izpildiet "
"C<chmod +x> un pēc tam izmantojiet to, iestatot vides mainīgo "
"LIBGUESTFS_HV.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1392
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" LIBGUESTFS_HV=/tmp/qemu.wrapper guestfish\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" LIBGUESTFS_HV=/tmp/qemu.wrapper guestfish\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1394
msgid ""
"Note that libguestfs also calls qemu with the -help and -version options in "
"order to determine features."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka libguestfs izsauc qemu arī ar opcijām -help un -version, lai "
"noteiktu līdzekļus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1397
msgid ""
"Wrappers can also be used to edit the options passed to qemu.  In the "
"following example, the C<-machine ...> option (C<-machine> and the following "
"argument) are removed from the command line and replaced with C<-machine "
"pc,accel=tcg>.  The while loop iterates over the options until it finds the "
"right one to remove, putting the remaining options into the C<args> array."
msgstr ""
"Ietinējus var izmantot arī qemu nodoto opciju rediģēšanai.  Šajā piemērā "
"opcija C<-machine ...> (C<-machine> un sekojošais arguments) tiek noņemta no "
"komandrindas un aizstāta ar C<-machine pc,accel=tcg>.  While cikls iterē "
"pāri opcijām, līdz atrod noņemamo, ievietojot atlikušās opcijas masīvā "
"C<args>."

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1406
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" i=0\n"
" while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do\n"
"     case \"$1\" in\n"
"     -machine)\n"
"         shift 2;;\n"
"     *)\n"
"         args[i]=\"$1\"\n"
"         (( i++ ))\n"
"         shift ;;\n"
"     esac\n"
" done\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" i=0\n"
" while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do\n"
"     case \"$1\" in\n"
"     -machine)\n"
"         shift 2;;\n"
"     *)\n"
"         args[i]=\"$1\"\n"
"         (( i++ ))\n"
"         shift ;;\n"
"     esac\n"
" done\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1418
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" exec qemu-kvm -machine pc,accel=tcg \"${args[@]}\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" exec qemu-kvm -machine pc,accel=tcg \"${args[@]}\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1422
msgid "<!-- old anchor for the next section --> <a name=\"attach-method\"/>"
msgstr "<!-- old anchor for the next section --> <a name=\"attach-method\"/>"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1427
msgid "BACKEND"
msgstr "AIZMUGURSISTĒMA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1429
msgid ""
"The backend (previously known as the \"attach method\") controls how "
"libguestfs creates and/or connects to the backend daemon, eg. by starting "
"qemu directly, or using libvirt to manage an appliance, running User-Mode "
"Linux, or connecting to an already running daemon."
msgstr ""
"Aizmugursistēma (agrāk saukta par „pievienošanas metodi”) kontrolē, kā "
"libguestfs izveido aizmugursistēmas dēmonu un/vai savienojas ar to, piem., "
"tieši palaižot qemu vai izmantojot libvirt palīgsistēmas pārvaldībai, "
"izpildot User-Mode Linux vai savienojoties ar jau darbojošos dēmonu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1434
msgid ""
"You can set the backend by calling L</guestfs_set_backend>, or by setting "
"the environment variable C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND>."
msgstr ""
"Aizmugursistēmu var iestatīt, izsaucot L</guestfs_set_backend> vai iestatot "
"vides mainīgo C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1437
msgid "Possible backends are described below:"
msgstr "Iespējamās aizmugursistēmas aprakstītas tālāk:"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1441
msgid "C<direct>"
msgstr "C<direct>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1443
msgid "C<appliance>"
msgstr "C<appliance>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1445
msgid "Run qemu directly to launch an appliance."
msgstr "Palīgsistēmas palaišanai tieši izpildīt qemu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1447
msgid "C<direct> and C<appliance> are synonyms."
msgstr "C<direct> un C<appliance> ir sinonīmi."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1449
msgid ""
"This is the ordinary method and normally the default, but see the note "
"below."
msgstr "Šī ir parastā metode un parasti noklusējums, bet skatiet piezīmi tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1452
msgid "C<libvirt>"
msgstr "C<libvirt>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1454
msgid "C<libvirt:null>"
msgstr "C<libvirt:null>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1456
msgid "C<libvirt:I<URI>>"
msgstr "C<libvirt:I<URI>>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1458
msgid "Use libvirt to launch and manage the appliance."
msgstr "Izmantot libvirt palīgsistēmas palaišanai un pārvaldībai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1460
msgid ""
"C<libvirt> causes libguestfs to choose a suitable URI for creating session "
"guests.  If using the libvirt backend, you almost always should use this."
msgstr ""
"C<libvirt> liek libguestfs izvēlēties piemērotu URI sesijas viesu izveidei.  "
"Ja izmantojat libvirt aizmugursistēmu, gandrīz vienmēr jāizmanto šis."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1464
msgid ""
"C<libvirt:null> causes libguestfs to use the C<NULL> connection URI, which "
"causes libvirt to try to guess what the user meant.  You probably don't want "
"to use this."
msgstr ""
"C<libvirt:null> liek libguestfs izmantot savienojuma URI C<NULL>, kas liek "
"libvirt mēģināt uzminēt, ko lietotājs domāja.  Visticamāk, nevēlaties to "
"izmantot."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1468
msgid ""
"C<libvirt:I<URI>> uses I<URI> as the libvirt connection URI (see "
"L<http://libvirt.org/uri.html>).  The typical libvirt backend with a URI "
"would be C<libvirt:qemu:///session>"
msgstr ""
"C<libvirt:I<URI>> izmanto I<URI> kā libvirt savienojuma URI (skatiet "
"L<http://libvirt.org/uri.html>).  Tipiskā libvirt aizmugursistēma ar URI "
"būtu C<libvirt:qemu:///session>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1472
msgid "The libvirt backend supports more features, including sVirt."
msgstr "Libvirt aizmugursistēma atbalsta vairāk līdzekļu, ieskaitot sVirt."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1476
msgid ""
"C<direct> is usually the default backend.  However since libguestfs E<ge> "
"1.19.24, libguestfs can be built with a different default by doing:"
msgstr ""
"C<direct> parasti ir noklusējuma aizmugursistēma.  Tomēr kopš libguestfs "
"E<ge> 1.19.24 libguestfs var būvēt ar citu noklusējumu šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1480
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ./configure --with-default-backend=...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ./configure --with-default-backend=...\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1482
msgid "To find out if libguestfs was compiled with a different default backend, do:"
msgstr ""
"Lai noskaidrotu, vai libguestfs tika kompilēta ar citu noklusējuma "
"aizmugursistēmu, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1485 test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:93
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:114
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" unset LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND\n"
" guestfish get-backend\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" unset LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND\n"
" guestfish get-backend\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1488
msgid "BACKEND SETTINGS"
msgstr "AIZMUGURSISTĒMAS IESTATĪJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1490
msgid ""
"Each backend can be configured by passing a list of strings.  You can either "
"call L</guestfs_set_backend_settings> with a list of strings, or set the "
"C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS> environment variable to a colon-separated "
"list of strings (before creating the handle)."
msgstr ""
"Katru aizmugursistēmu var konfigurēt, nododot virkņu sarakstu.  Varat vai nu "
"izsaukt L</guestfs_set_backend_settings> ar virkņu sarakstu, vai iestatīt "
"vides mainīgo C<LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS> uz ar koliem atdalītu virkņu "
"sarakstu (pirms roktura izveides)."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1495
msgid "force_tcg"
msgstr "force_tcg"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1497 lib/guestfs.pod:1506
msgid "Using:"
msgstr "Izmantojot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1499
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS=force_tcg\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS=force_tcg\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1501
msgid ""
"will force the direct and libvirt backends to use TCG (software emulation) "
"instead of KVM (hardware accelerated virtualization)."
msgstr ""
"piespiedīs direct un libvirt aizmugursistēmas izmantot TCG (programmatūras "
"emulāciju), nevis KVM (aparatūras paātrinātu virtualizāciju)."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1504
msgid "force_kvm"
msgstr "force_kvm"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1508
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS=force_kvm\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS=force_kvm\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1510
msgid ""
"will force the direct and libvirt backends to use KVM (hardware accelerated "
"virtualization) instead of TCG (software emulation)."
msgstr ""
"piespiedīs direct un libvirt aizmugursistēmas izmantot KVM (aparatūras "
"paātrinātu virtualizāciju), nevis TCG (programmatūras emulāciju)."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1513
msgid "gdb"
msgstr "gdb"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1515
msgid "The direct backend supports:"
msgstr "Tiešā aizmugursistēma atbalsta:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1517
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS=gdb\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND_SETTINGS=gdb\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1519
msgid ""
"When this is set, qemu will not start running the appliance immediately.  It "
"will wait for you to connect to it using gdb:"
msgstr ""
"Ja tas iestatīts, qemu nesāks izpildīt palīgsistēmu uzreiz.  Tas gaidīs, "
"kamēr pievienosieties tam ar gdb:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1522
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ gdb\n"
" (gdb) symbol-file /path/to/vmlinux\n"
" (gdb) target remote tcp::1234\n"
" (gdb) cont\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ gdb\n"
" (gdb) symbol-file /path/to/vmlinux\n"
" (gdb) target remote tcp::1234\n"
" (gdb) cont\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1527
msgid ""
"You can then debug the appliance kernel, which is useful to debug boot "
"failures (especially ones where there are no debug messages printed - tip: "
"look in the kernel C<log_buf>)."
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam varat atkļūdot palīgsistēmas kodolu, kas noder sāknēšanas kļūmju "
"atkļūdošanai (it īpaši, ja netiek izdrukāti atkļūdošanas ziņojumi — padoms: "
"skatieties kodola C<log_buf>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1531
msgid ""
"On Fedora, install C<kernel-debuginfo> for the C<vmlinux> file (containing "
"symbols).  Make sure the symbols precisely match the kernel being used."
msgstr ""
"Fedorā instalējiet C<kernel-debuginfo>, lai iegūtu failu C<vmlinux> (ar "
"simboliem).  Pārliecinieties, ka simboli precīzi atbilst izmantotajam "
"kodolam."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1535
msgid "ABI GUARANTEE"
msgstr "ABI GARANTIJA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1537
msgid ""
"We guarantee the libguestfs ABI (binary interface), for public, high-level "
"actions as outlined in this section.  Although we will deprecate some "
"actions, for example if they get replaced by newer calls, we will keep the "
"old actions forever.  This allows you the developer to program in confidence "
"against the libguestfs API."
msgstr ""
"Mēs garantējam libguestfs ABI (bināro saskarni) publiskajām, augsta līmeņa "
"darbībām, kā izklāstīts šajā sadaļā.  Lai gan dažas darbības atzīsim par "
"novecojušām, piemēram, ja tās tiks aizstātas ar jaunākiem izsaukumiem, vecās "
"darbības paturēsim uz visiem laikiem.  Tas ļauj jums kā izstrādātājam droši "
"programmēt pret libguestfs API."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1543
msgid "BLOCK DEVICE NAMING"
msgstr "BLOKU IERĪČU NOSAUKUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1545
msgid ""
"Libguestfs defines F</dev/sd*> as the I<standard naming scheme> for devices "
"passed to API calls.  So F</dev/sda> means \"the first device added by "
"L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>\", and F</dev/sdb3> means \"the third partition "
"on the second device\"."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs definē F</dev/sd*> kā API izsaukumiem nodoto ierīču I<standarta "
"nosaukšanas shēmu>.  Tātad F</dev/sda> nozīmē „pirmā ierīce, ko pievienojis "
"L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>”, un F</dev/sdb3> nozīmē „trešais nodalījums "
"otrajā ierīcē”."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1550
msgid ""
"Internally device names are sometimes translated, but this should not be "
"visible at the API level."
msgstr ""
"Iekšēji ierīču nosaukumi dažreiz tiek tulkoti, bet tam nevajadzētu būt "
"redzamam API līmenī."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1553
msgid "DISK LABELS"
msgstr "DISKU ETIĶETES"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1555
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.20, you can give a label to a disk when you add it, "
"using the optional C<label> parameter to L</guestfs_add_drive_opts>.  (Note "
"that disk labels are different from and not related to filesystem labels)."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.20 diskam, to pievienojot, var piešķirt etiķeti, "
"izmantojot L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> neobligāto parametru C<label>.  "
"(Ņemiet vērā, ka disku etiķetes atšķiras no failu sistēmu etiķetēm un nav ar "
"tām saistītas.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1560
msgid ""
"Not all versions of libguestfs support setting a disk label, and when it is "
"supported, it is limited to 20 ASCII characters C<[a-zA-Z]>."
msgstr ""
"Ne visas libguestfs versijas atbalsta diska etiķetes iestatīšanu, un, ja tā "
"tiek atbalstīta, tā ir ierobežota līdz 20 ASCII rakstzīmēm C<[a-zA-Z]>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1563
msgid ""
"When you add a disk with a label, it can either be addressed using "
"F</dev/sd*>, or using F</dev/disk/guestfs/I<label>>.  Partitions on the disk "
"can be addressed using F</dev/disk/guestfs/I<label>I<partnum>>."
msgstr ""
"Kad pievienojat disku ar etiķeti, uz to var atsaukties, izmantojot F</dev/"
"sd*> vai F</dev/disk/guestfs/I<label>>.  Uz diska nodalījumiem var "
"atsaukties, izmantojot F</dev/disk/guestfs/I<label>I<partnum>>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1568
msgid ""
"Listing devices (L</guestfs_list_devices>) and partitions "
"(L</guestfs_list_partitions>) returns the block device names.  However you "
"can use L</guestfs_list_disk_labels> to map disk labels to block device and "
"partition names."
msgstr ""
"Ierīču (L</guestfs_list_devices>) un nodalījumu (L</"
"guestfs_list_partitions>) uzskaitīšana atgriež bloku ierīču nosaukumus.  "
"Tomēr varat izmantot L</guestfs_list_disk_labels>, lai kartētu disku "
"etiķetes uz bloku ierīču un nodalījumu nosaukumiem."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1573
msgid "NULL DISKS"
msgstr "NULL DISKI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1575
msgid ""
"When adding a disk using, eg., L</guestfs_add_drive>, you can set the "
"filename to C<\"/dev/null\">.  This string is treated specially by "
"libguestfs, causing it to add a \"null disk\"."
msgstr ""
"Pievienojot disku, izmantojot, piem., L</guestfs_add_drive>, faila nosaukumu "
"var iestatīt uz C<\"/dev/null\">.  Libguestfs šo virkni apstrādā īpaši, "
"liekot tai pievienot „null disku”."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1579
msgid "A null disk has the following properties:"
msgstr "Null diskam ir šādas īpašības:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1585
msgid ""
"A null disk will appear as a normal device, eg. in calls to "
"L</guestfs_list_devices>."
msgstr ""
"Null disks parādīsies kā parasta ierīce, piem., L</guestfs_list_devices> "
"izsaukumos."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1590
msgid "You may add C<\"/dev/null\"> multiple times."
msgstr "C<\"/dev/null\"> var pievienot vairākas reizes."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1594
msgid ""
"You should not try to access a null disk in any way.  For example, you "
"shouldn't try to read it or mount it."
msgstr ""
"Nevajadzētu mēģināt piekļūt null diskam nekādā veidā.  Piemēram, nevajadzētu "
"mēģināt to lasīt vai montēt."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1599
msgid "Null disks are used for three main purposes:"
msgstr "Null diskus izmanto trim galvenajiem mērķiem:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1605
msgid "Performance testing of libguestfs (see L<guestfs-performance(1)>)."
msgstr "Libguestfs veiktspējas testēšanai (skatiet L<guestfs-performance(1)>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1609
msgid "The internal test suite."
msgstr "Iekšējam testu komplektam."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1613
msgid ""
"If you want to use libguestfs APIs that don’t refer to disks, since "
"libguestfs requires that at least one disk is added, you should add a null "
"disk."
msgstr ""
"Ja vēlaties izmantot libguestfs API, kas neattiecas uz diskiem, — tā kā "
"libguestfs pieprasa, lai būtu pievienots vismaz viens disks, jāpievieno null "
"disks."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1617
msgid "For example, to test if a feature is available, use code like this:"
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, lai pārbaudītu, vai līdzeklis ir pieejams, izmantojiet šādu kodu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1619
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_h *g;\n"
" char **groups = [ \"btrfs\", NULL ];\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_h *g;\n"
" char **groups = [ \"btrfs\", NULL ];\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1622
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" g = guestfs_create ();\n"
" guestfs_add_drive (g, \"/dev/null\");\n"
" guestfs_launch (g);\n"
" if (guestfs_available (g, groups) == 0) {\n"
"   // group(s) are available\n"
" } else {\n"
"   // group(s) are not available\n"
" }\n"
" guestfs_close (g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" g = guestfs_create ();\n"
" guestfs_add_drive (g, \"/dev/null\");\n"
" guestfs_launch (g);\n"
" if (guestfs_available (g, groups) == 0) {\n"
"   // group(s) are available\n"
" } else {\n"
"   // group(s) are not available\n"
" }\n"
" guestfs_close (g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1634
msgid "DISK IMAGE FORMATS"
msgstr "DISKU ATTĒLU FORMĀTI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1636
msgid ""
"Virtual disks come in a variety of formats.  Some common formats are listed "
"below."
msgstr ""
"Virtuālie diski ir dažādos formātos.  Daži izplatītākie formāti uzskaitīti "
"tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1639
msgid ""
"Note that libguestfs itself is not responsible for handling the disk format: "
"this is done using L<qemu(1)>.  If support for a particular format is "
"missing or broken, this has to be fixed in qemu."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka pati libguestfs nav atbildīga par diska formāta apstrādi: to "
"dara L<qemu(1)>.  Ja konkrēta formāta atbalsts trūkst vai ir bojāts, tas "
"jālabo qemu."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1643
msgid "COMMON VIRTUAL DISK IMAGE FORMATS"
msgstr "IZPLATĪTI VIRTUĀLO DISKU ATTĒLU FORMĀTI"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1647
msgid "I<raw>"
msgstr "I<raw>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1649
msgid ""
"Raw format is simply a dump of the sequential bytes of the virtual hard "
"disk.  There is no header, container, compression or processing of any sort."
msgstr ""
"Raw formāts ir vienkārši virtuālā cietā diska secīgo baitu izmešana.  Nav "
"galvenes, konteinera, saspiešanas vai jebkādas apstrādes."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1653
msgid ""
"Since raw format requires no translation to read or write, it is both fast "
"and very well supported by qemu and all other hypervisors.  You can consider "
"it to be a universal format that any hypervisor can access."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā raw formātam lasīšanai vai rakstīšanai nav vajadzīga tulkošana, tas ir "
"gan ātrs, gan ļoti labi atbalstīts qemu un visos citos hipervizoros.  To var "
"uzskatīt par universālu formātu, kuram var piekļūt jebkurš hipervizors."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1658
msgid ""
"Raw format files are not compressed and so take up the full space of the "
"original disk image even when they are empty.  A variation (on Linux/Unix at "
"least) is to not store ranges of all-zero bytes by storing the file as a "
"sparse file.  This \"variant format\" is sometimes called I<raw sparse>.  "
"Many utilities, including L<virt-sparsify(1)>, can make raw disk images "
"sparse."
msgstr ""
"Raw formāta faili nav saspiesti, tāpēc aizņem visu oriģinālā diska attēla "
"vietu, pat ja ir tukši.  Variācija (vismaz Linux/Unix) ir neglabāt "
"diapazonus tikai ar nulles baitiem, glabājot failu kā retinātu failu.  Šo „"
"variantu formātu” dažreiz sauc par I<raw sparse>.  Daudzas utilītas, "
"ieskaitot L<virt-sparsify(1)>, var padarīt raw disku attēlus retinātus."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1665
msgid "I<qcow2>"
msgstr "I<qcow2>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1667
msgid ""
"Qcow2 is the native disk image format used by qemu.  Internally it uses a "
"two-level directory structure so that only blocks containing data are stored "
"in the file.  It also has many other features such as compression, snapshots "
"and backing files."
msgstr ""
"Qcow2 ir qemu izmantotais vietējais disku attēlu formāts.  Iekšēji tas "
"izmanto divlīmeņu direktoriju struktūru, lai failā tiktu glabāti tikai bloki "
"ar datiem.  Tam ir arī daudz citu līdzekļu, piemēram, saspiešana, "
"momentuzņēmumi un pamatfaili."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1672
msgid ""
"There are at least two distinct variants of this format, although qemu (and "
"hence libguestfs) handles both transparently to the user."
msgstr ""
"Šim formātam ir vismaz divi atšķirīgi varianti, lai gan qemu (un līdz ar to "
"libguestfs) abus apstrādā lietotājam caurspīdīgi."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1675
msgid "I<vmdk>"
msgstr "I<vmdk>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1677
msgid ""
"VMDK is VMware’s native disk image format.  There are many variations.  "
"Modern qemu (hence libguestfs) supports most variations, but you should be "
"aware that older versions of qemu had some very bad data-corrupting bugs in "
"this area."
msgstr ""
"VMDK ir VMware vietējais disku attēlu formāts.  Ir daudz variāciju.  "
"Mūsdienu qemu (un līdz ar to libguestfs) atbalsta lielāko daļu variāciju, "
"taču jāņem vērā, ka vecākām qemu versijām šajā jomā bija dažas ļoti sliktas "
"datu bojāšanas kļūdas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1682
msgid ""
"Note that VMware ESX exposes files with the name F<guest-flat.vmdk>.  These "
"are not VMDK.  They are raw format files which happen to have a C<.vmdk> "
"extension."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka VMware ESX atklāj failus ar nosaukumu F<guest-flat.vmdk>.  "
"Tie nav VMDK.  Tie ir raw formāta faili, kuriem gadās paplašinājums C<.vmdk>."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1686
msgid "I<vdi>"
msgstr "I<vdi>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1688
msgid ""
"VDI is VirtualBox’s native disk image format.  Qemu (hence libguestfs)  has "
"generally good support for this."
msgstr ""
"VDI ir VirtualBox vietējais disku attēlu formāts.  Qemu (un līdz ar to "
"libguestfs) to parasti labi atbalsta."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1691
msgid "I<vpc>"
msgstr "I<vpc>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1693
msgid "I<vhd>"
msgstr "I<vhd>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1695
msgid ""
"VPC (old) and VHD (modern) are the native disk image format of Microsoft "
"(and previously, Connectix) Virtual PC and Hyper-V."
msgstr ""
"VPC (vecais) un VHD (modernais) ir Microsoft (un iepriekš Connectix) Virtual "
"PC un Hyper-V vietējais disku attēlu formāts."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1698
msgid "Obsolete formats"
msgstr "Novecojuši formāti"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1700
msgid ""
"The following formats are obsolete and should not be used: I<qcow> (aka "
"I<qcow1>), I<cow>, I<bochs>."
msgstr ""
"Šie formāti ir novecojuši, un tos nevajadzētu izmantot: I<qcow> (jeb "
"I<qcow1>), I<cow>, I<bochs>."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1705
msgid "DETECTING THE FORMAT OF A DISK IMAGE"
msgstr "DISKA ATTĒLA FORMĀTA NOTEIKŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1707
msgid ""
"Firstly note there is a security issue with auto-detecting the format of a "
"disk image.  It may or may not apply in your use case.  Read "
"L</CVE-2010-3851> below."
msgstr ""
"Vispirms ņemiet vērā, ka ar diska attēla formāta automātisku noteikšanu ir "
"saistīta drošības problēma.  Tā var attiekties vai neattiekties uz jūsu "
"gadījumu.  Lasiet L</CVE-2010-3851> tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1711
msgid ""
"Libguestfs offers an API to get the format of a disk image "
"(L</guestfs_disk_format>), and it is safest to use this."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs piedāvā API diska attēla formāta iegūšanai (L</"
"guestfs_disk_format>), un visdrošāk ir izmantot to."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1714
msgid ""
"I<Don’t> be tempted to try parsing the text / human-readable output of "
"C<qemu-img> since it cannot be parsed reliably and securely.  Also do not "
"use the C<file> command since the output of that changes over time."
msgstr ""
"I<Nevajag> kārdināties mēģināt parsēt C<qemu-img> teksta / cilvēkam lasāmo "
"izvadi, jo to nevar uzticami un droši parsēt.  Tāpat neizmantojiet komandu "
"C<file>, jo tās izvade laika gaitā mainās."

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1719
msgid "CONNECTION MANAGEMENT"
msgstr "SAVIENOJUMU PĀRVALDĪBA"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1721
msgid "guestfs_h *"
msgstr "guestfs_h *"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1723
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_h> is the opaque type representing a connection handle.  Create a "
"handle by calling L</guestfs_create> or L</guestfs_create_flags>.  Call "
"L</guestfs_close> to free the handle and release all resources used."
msgstr ""
"C<guestfs_h> ir necaurredzams tips, kas attēlo savienojuma rokturi.  "
"Izveidojiet rokturi, izsaucot L</guestfs_create> vai L</guestfs_create_flags>"
".  Izsauciet L</guestfs_close>, lai atbrīvotu rokturi un visus izmantotos "
"resursus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1728
msgid ""
"For information on using multiple handles and threads, see the section "
"L</MULTIPLE HANDLES AND MULTIPLE THREADS> above."
msgstr ""
"Informāciju par vairāku rokturu un pavedienu izmantošanu skatiet sadaļā L</"
"VAIRĀKI ROKTURI UN VAIRĀKI PAVEDIENI> iepriekš."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1731
msgid "guestfs_create"
msgstr "guestfs_create"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1733
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_h *guestfs_create (void);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_h *guestfs_create (void);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1735
msgid "Create a connection handle."
msgstr "Izveidot savienojuma rokturi."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1737 lib/guestfs.pod:1756
msgid ""
"On success this returns a non-NULL pointer to a handle.  On error it returns "
"NULL."
msgstr ""
"Veiksmes gadījumā tas atgriež ne-NULL rādītāju uz rokturi.  Kļūdas gadījumā "
"tas atgriež NULL."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1740
msgid ""
"You have to \"configure\" the handle after creating it.  This includes "
"calling L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> (or one of the equivalent calls) on the "
"handle at least once."
msgstr ""
"Pēc izveides rokturis „jākonfigurē”.  Tas ietver vismaz vienreiz izsaukt "
"rokturim L</guestfs_add_drive_opts> (vai kādu no līdzvērtīgiem izsaukumiem)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1744
msgid "After configuring the handle, you have to call L</guestfs_launch>."
msgstr "Pēc roktura konfigurēšanas jāizsauc L</guestfs_launch>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1746
msgid ""
"You may also want to configure error handling for the handle.  See the "
"L</ERROR HANDLING> section below."
msgstr ""
"Iespējams, vēlēsieties arī konfigurēt roktura kļūdu apstrādi.  Skatiet "
"sadaļu L</KĻŪDU APSTRĀDE> tālāk."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1749
msgid "guestfs_create_flags"
msgstr "guestfs_create_flags"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1751
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_h *guestfs_create_flags (unsigned flags [, ...]);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_h *guestfs_create_flags (unsigned flags [, ...]);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1753
msgid ""
"Create a connection handle, supplying extra flags and extra arguments to "
"control how the handle is created."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot savienojuma rokturi, nododot papildu karogus un papildu argumentus, "
"lai kontrolētu, kā rokturis tiek izveidots."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1759
msgid "L</guestfs_create> is equivalent to calling C<guestfs_create_flags(0)>."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_create> ir līdzvērtīgs C<guestfs_create_flags(0)> izsaukšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1761
msgid ""
"The following flags may be logically ORed together.  (Currently no extra "
"arguments are used)."
msgstr ""
"Šos karogus var apvienot ar loģisko OR.  (Pašlaik papildu argumenti netiek "
"izmantoti.)"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1766
msgid "C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT>"
msgstr "C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1768
msgid "Don’t parse any environment variables (such as C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG> etc)."
msgstr "Neparsēt nekādus vides mainīgos (piemēram, C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG> u. c.)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1770
msgid ""
"You can call L</guestfs_parse_environment> or "
"L</guestfs_parse_environment_list> afterwards to parse environment "
"variables.  Alternately, I<don't> call these functions if you want the "
"handle to be unaffected by environment variables.  See the example below."
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam varat izsaukt L</guestfs_parse_environment> vai L</"
"guestfs_parse_environment_list>, lai parsētu vides mainīgos.  Vai arī "
"I<neizsauciet> šīs funkcijas, ja vēlaties, lai vides mainīgie rokturi "
"neietekmētu.  Skatiet piemēru tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1775
msgid ""
"The default (if this flag is not given) is to implicitly call "
"L</guestfs_parse_environment>."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums (ja šis karogs nav norādīts) ir netieši izsaukt L</"
"guestfs_parse_environment>."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1778
msgid "C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_CLOSE_ON_EXIT>"
msgstr "C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_CLOSE_ON_EXIT>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1780
msgid ""
"Don’t try to close the handle in an L<atexit(3)> handler if the program "
"exits without explicitly closing the handle."
msgstr ""
"Nemēģināt aizvērt rokturi L<atexit(3)> apstrādātājā, ja programma iziet, "
"eksplicīti neaizverot rokturi."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1783
msgid ""
"The default (if this flag is not given) is to install such an atexit "
"handler."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums (ja šis karogs nav norādīts) ir instalēt šādu atexit "
"apstrādātāju."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1788
msgid "USING C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT>"
msgstr "C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT> IZMANTOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1790
msgid ""
"You might use C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT> and an explicit call to "
"L</guestfs_parse_environment> like this:"
msgstr ""
"C<GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT> un eksplicītu L</guestfs_parse_environment> "
"izsaukumu varētu izmantot šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1793
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_h *g;\n"
" int r;\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_h *g;\n"
" int r;\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1796
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" g = guestfs_create_flags (GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT);\n"
" if (!g) {\n"
"   perror (\"guestfs_create_flags\");\n"
"   exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" }\n"
" r = guestfs_parse_environment (g);\n"
" if (r == -1)\n"
"   exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" g = guestfs_create_flags (GUESTFS_CREATE_NO_ENVIRONMENT);\n"
" if (!g) {\n"
"   perror (\"guestfs_create_flags\");\n"
"   exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" }\n"
" r = guestfs_parse_environment (g);\n"
" if (r == -1)\n"
"   exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1805
msgid ""
"Or to create a handle which is unaffected by environment variables, omit the "
"call to C<guestfs_parse_environment> from the above code."
msgstr ""
"Vai, lai izveidotu rokturi, ko neietekmē vides mainīgie, izlaidiet no "
"iepriekšējā koda C<guestfs_parse_environment> izsaukumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1808
msgid ""
"The above code has another advantage which is that any errors from parsing "
"the environment are passed through the error handler, whereas "
"C<guestfs_create> prints errors on stderr and ignores them."
msgstr ""
"Iepriekšējam kodam ir vēl viena priekšrocība — jebkuras vides parsēšanas "
"kļūdas tiek nodotas kļūdu apstrādātājam, turpretī C<guestfs_create> izdrukā "
"kļūdas uz stderr un tās ignorē."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1812
msgid "guestfs_close"
msgstr "guestfs_close"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1814
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void guestfs_close (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void guestfs_close (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1816
msgid ""
"This closes the connection handle and frees up all resources used.  If a "
"close callback was set on the handle, then it is called."
msgstr ""
"Tas aizver savienojuma rokturi un atbrīvo visus izmantotos resursus.  Ja "
"rokturim bija iestatīts aizvēršanas atzvans, tas tiek izsaukts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1819
msgid "The correct way to close the handle is:"
msgstr "Pareizais veids, kā aizvērt rokturi, ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1821
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" if (guestfs_shutdown (g) == -1) {\n"
"   /* handle write errors here */\n"
" }\n"
" guestfs_close (g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" if (guestfs_shutdown (g) == -1) {\n"
"   /* handle write errors here */\n"
" }\n"
" guestfs_close (g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1826
msgid "L</guestfs_shutdown> is only needed if B<all> of the following are true:"
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_shutdown> ir vajadzīgs tikai tad, ja izpildās B<visi> šie "
"nosacījumi:"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1830
msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1832
msgid "one or more disks were added in read-write mode, I<and>"
msgstr "lasīšanai un rakstīšanai tika pievienots viens vai vairāki diski, I<un>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1834
msgid "2"
msgstr "2"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1836
msgid "guestfs_launch was called, I<and>"
msgstr "tika izsaukts guestfs_launch, I<un>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1838
msgid "3"
msgstr "3"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1840
msgid "you made some changes, I<and>"
msgstr "veicāt dažas izmaiņas, I<un>"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1842
msgid "4"
msgstr "4"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1844
msgid ""
"you have a way to handle write errors (eg. by exiting with an error code or "
"reporting something to the user)."
msgstr ""
"jums ir veids, kā apstrādāt rakstīšanas kļūdas (piem., izejot ar kļūdas kodu "
"vai ziņojot lietotājam)."

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1849
msgid "ERROR HANDLING"
msgstr "KĻŪDU APSTRĀDE"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1851
msgid ""
"API functions can return errors.  For example, almost all functions that "
"return C<int> will return C<-1> to indicate an error."
msgstr ""
"API funkcijas var atgriezt kļūdas.  Piemēram, gandrīz visas funkcijas, kas "
"atgriež C<int>, atgriezīs C<-1>, lai norādītu kļūdu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1854
msgid ""
"Additional information is available for errors: an error message string and "
"optionally an error number (errno) if the thing that failed was a system "
"call."
msgstr ""
"Par kļūdām ir pieejama papildu informācija: kļūdas ziņojuma virkne un pēc "
"izvēles kļūdas numurs (errno), ja neizdevās sistēmas izsaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1858
msgid ""
"You can get at the additional information about the last error on the handle "
"by calling L</guestfs_last_error>, L</guestfs_last_errno>, and/or by setting "
"up an error handler with L</guestfs_set_error_handler>."
msgstr ""
"Papildu informāciju par pēdējo roktura kļūdu varat iegūt, izsaucot L</"
"guestfs_last_error>, L</guestfs_last_errno> un/vai iestatot kļūdu "
"apstrādātāju ar L</guestfs_set_error_handler>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1863
msgid ""
"When the handle is created, a default error handler is installed which "
"prints the error message string to C<stderr>.  For small short-running "
"command line programs it is sufficient to do:"
msgstr ""
"Kad rokturis tiek izveidots, tiek instalēts noklusējuma kļūdu apstrādātājs, "
"kas izdrukā kļūdas ziņojuma virkni uz C<stderr>.  Mazām, īsi darbojošām "
"komandrindas programmām pietiek ar:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1867
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" if (guestfs_launch (g) == -1)\n"
"   exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" if (guestfs_launch (g) == -1)\n"
"   exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1870
msgid ""
"since the default error handler will ensure that an error message has been "
"printed to C<stderr> before the program exits."
msgstr ""
"jo noklusējuma kļūdu apstrādātājs nodrošinās, ka pirms programmas iziešanas "
"kļūdas ziņojums ir izdrukāts uz C<stderr>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1873
msgid ""
"For other programs the caller will almost certainly want to install an "
"alternate error handler or do error handling in-line as in the example "
"below.  The non-C language bindings all install NULL error handlers and turn "
"errors into exceptions using code similar to this:"
msgstr ""
"Citām programmām izsaucējs gandrīz noteikti vēlēsies instalēt alternatīvu "
"kļūdu apstrādātāju vai apstrādāt kļūdas uz vietas, kā tālāk dotajā piemērā.  "
"Visi ne-C valodu saistījumi instalē NULL kļūdu apstrādātājus un pārvērš "
"kļūdas izņēmumos, izmantojot kodu, līdzīgu šim:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1878
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" const char *msg;\n"
" int errnum;\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" const char *msg;\n"
" int errnum;\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1881
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /* This disables the default behaviour of printing errors\n"
"    on stderr. */\n"
" guestfs_set_error_handler (g, NULL, NULL);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" /* This disables the default behaviour of printing errors\n"
"    on stderr. */\n"
" guestfs_set_error_handler (g, NULL, NULL);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1885
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" if (guestfs_launch (g) == -1) {\n"
"   /* Examine the error message and print it, throw it,\n"
"      etc. */\n"
"   msg = guestfs_last_error (g);\n"
"   errnum = guestfs_last_errno (g);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" if (guestfs_launch (g) == -1) {\n"
"   /* Examine the error message and print it, throw it,\n"
"      etc. */\n"
"   msg = guestfs_last_error (g);\n"
"   errnum = guestfs_last_errno (g);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1891
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   fprintf (stderr, \"%s\", msg);\n"
"   if (errnum != 0)\n"
"     fprintf (stderr, \": %s\", strerror (errnum));\n"
"   fprintf (stderr, \"\\n\");\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   fprintf (stderr, \"%s\", msg);\n"
"   if (errnum != 0)\n"
"     fprintf (stderr, \": %s\", strerror (errnum));\n"
"   fprintf (stderr, \"\\n\");\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1896
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   /* ... */\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"   /* ... */\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1899
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_create> returns C<NULL> if the handle cannot be created, and "
"because there is no handle if this happens there is no way to get additional "
"error information.  Since libguestfs E<ge> 1.20, you can use "
"L</guestfs_create_flags> to properly deal with errors during handle "
"creation, although the vast majority of programs can continue to use "
"L</guestfs_create> and not worry about this situation."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_create> atgriež C<NULL>, ja rokturi nevar izveidot, un, tā kā "
"tādā gadījumā roktura nav, nav veida, kā iegūt papildu kļūdas informāciju.  "
"Kopš libguestfs E<ge> 1.20 varat izmantot L</guestfs_create_flags>, lai "
"pareizi apstrādātu kļūdas roktura izveides laikā, lai gan lielākā daļa "
"programmu var turpināt izmantot L</guestfs_create> un neuztraukties par šo "
"situāciju."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1906
msgid ""
"Out of memory errors are handled differently.  The default action is to call "
"L<abort(3)>.  If this is undesirable, then you can set a handler using "
"L</guestfs_set_out_of_memory_handler>."
msgstr ""
"Atmiņas trūkuma kļūdas tiek apstrādātas citādi.  Noklusējuma darbība ir "
"izsaukt L<abort(3)>.  Ja tas nav vēlams, varat iestatīt apstrādātāju ar L</"
"guestfs_set_out_of_memory_handler>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1910
msgid "guestfs_last_error"
msgstr "guestfs_last_error"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1912
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" const char *guestfs_last_error (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" const char *guestfs_last_error (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1914
msgid ""
"This returns the last error message that happened on C<g>.  If there has not "
"been an error since the handle was created, then this returns C<NULL>."
msgstr ""
"Tas atgriež pēdējo kļūdas ziņojumu, kas radās rokturī C<g>.  Ja kopš roktura "
"izveides nav bijis kļūdas, tas atgriež C<NULL>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1918
msgid ""
"Note the returned string does I<not> have a newline character at the end.  "
"Most error messages are single lines.  Some are split over multiple lines "
"and contain C<\\n> characters within the string but not at the end."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka atgrieztās virknes beigās I<nav> jaunas rindas rakstzīmes.  "
"Lielākā daļa kļūdu ziņojumu ir vienā rindā.  Daži ir sadalīti vairākās "
"rindās un satur rakstzīmes C<\\n> virknes iekšpusē, bet ne beigās."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1923
msgid ""
"The lifetime of the returned string is until the next error occurs on the "
"same handle, or L</guestfs_close> is called.  If you need to keep it longer, "
"copy it."
msgstr ""
"Atgrieztā virkne ir derīga, līdz tajā pašā rokturī notiek nākamā kļūda vai "
"tiek izsaukts L</guestfs_close>.  Ja tā jāpatur ilgāk, nokopējiet to."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1927
msgid "guestfs_last_errno"
msgstr "guestfs_last_errno"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1929
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int guestfs_last_errno (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int guestfs_last_errno (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1931
msgid "This returns the last error number (errno) that happened on C<g>."
msgstr "Tas atgriež pēdējo kļūdas numuru (errno), kas radās rokturī C<g>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1933
msgid "If successful, an errno integer not equal to zero is returned."
msgstr "Veiksmes gadījumā tiek atgriezts errno vesels skaitlis, kas nav nulle."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1935
msgid ""
"In many cases the special errno C<ENOTSUP> is returned if you tried to call "
"a function or use a feature which is not supported."
msgstr ""
"Daudzos gadījumos tiek atgriezts īpašais errno C<ENOTSUP>, ja mēģinājāt "
"izsaukt funkciju vai izmantot līdzekli, kas netiek atbalstīts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1938
msgid ""
"If no error number is available, this returns 0.  This call can return 0 in "
"three situations:"
msgstr ""
"Ja kļūdas numurs nav pieejams, tas atgriež 0.  Šis izsaukums var atgriezt 0 "
"trīs situācijās:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1945
msgid "There has not been any error on the handle."
msgstr "Rokturī nav bijis nevienas kļūdas."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1949
msgid ""
"There has been an error but the errno was meaningless.  This corresponds to "
"the case where the error did not come from a failed system call, but for "
"some other reason."
msgstr ""
"Ir bijusi kļūda, bet errno bija bezjēdzīgs.  Tas atbilst gadījumam, kad "
"kļūda neradās no neizdevušos sistēmas izsaukuma, bet kāda cita iemesla dēļ."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1955
msgid ""
"There was an error from a failed system call, but for some reason the errno "
"was not captured and returned.  This usually indicates a bug in libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Bija kļūda no neizdevušos sistēmas izsaukuma, bet kāda iemesla dēļ errno "
"netika tverts un atgriezts.  Parasti tas norāda uz kļūdu libguestfs."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1961
msgid ""
"Libguestfs tries to convert the errno from inside the appliance into a "
"corresponding errno for the caller (not entirely trivial: the appliance "
"might be running a completely different operating system from the library "
"and error numbers are not standardized across Un*xen).  If this could not be "
"done, then the error is translated to C<EINVAL>.  In practice this should "
"only happen in very rare circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs mēģina pārvērst errno no palīgsistēmas iekšienes atbilstošā errno "
"izsaucējam (ne gluži triviāli: palīgsistēmā var darboties pilnīgi cita "
"operētājsistēma nekā bibliotēkai, un kļūdu numuri nav standartizēti starp "
"Un*x sistēmām).  Ja to nevarēja izdarīt, kļūda tiek pārvērsta par C<EINVAL>"
".  Praksē tam vajadzētu notikt tikai ļoti retos apstākļos."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1969
msgid "guestfs_set_error_handler"
msgstr "guestfs_set_error_handler"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1971
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" typedef void (*guestfs_error_handler_cb) (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                           void *opaque,\n"
"                                           const char *msg);\n"
" void guestfs_set_error_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                 guestfs_error_handler_cb cb,\n"
"                                 void *opaque);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" typedef void (*guestfs_error_handler_cb) (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                           void *opaque,\n"
"                                           const char *msg);\n"
" void guestfs_set_error_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                 guestfs_error_handler_cb cb,\n"
"                                 void *opaque);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1978
msgid ""
"The callback C<cb> will be called if there is an error.  The parameters "
"passed to the callback are an opaque data pointer and the error message "
"string."
msgstr ""
"Atzvans C<cb> tiks izsaukts, ja ir kļūda.  Atzvanam nodotie parametri ir "
"necaurredzams datu rādītājs un kļūdas ziņojuma virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1982
msgid ""
"C<errno> is not passed to the callback.  To get that the callback must call "
"L</guestfs_last_errno>."
msgstr ""
"C<errno> atzvanam netiek nodots.  Lai to iegūtu, atzvanam jāizsauc L</"
"guestfs_last_errno>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1985
msgid ""
"Note that the message string C<msg> is freed as soon as the callback "
"function returns, so if you want to stash it somewhere you must make your "
"own copy."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka ziņojuma virkne C<msg> tiek atbrīvota, tiklīdz atzvana "
"funkcija atgriežas, tāpēc, ja vēlaties to kaut kur saglabāt, jāizveido sava "
"kopija."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1989
msgid "The default handler prints messages on C<stderr>."
msgstr "Noklusējuma apstrādātājs izdrukā ziņojumus uz C<stderr>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1991
msgid "If you set C<cb> to C<NULL> then I<no> handler is called."
msgstr "Ja iestatāt C<cb> uz C<NULL>, I<netiek> izsaukts neviens apstrādātājs."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1993
msgid "guestfs_get_error_handler"
msgstr "guestfs_get_error_handler"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1995
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_error_handler_cb guestfs_get_error_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                                     void **opaque_rtn);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_error_handler_cb guestfs_get_error_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                                     void **opaque_rtn);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:1998
msgid "Returns the current error handler callback."
msgstr "Atgriež pašreizējo kļūdu apstrādātāja atzvanu."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2000
msgid "guestfs_push_error_handler"
msgstr "guestfs_push_error_handler"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2002
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void guestfs_push_error_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                  guestfs_error_handler_cb cb,\n"
"                                  void *opaque);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void guestfs_push_error_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                  guestfs_error_handler_cb cb,\n"
"                                  void *opaque);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2006
msgid ""
"This is the same as L</guestfs_set_error_handler>, except that the old error "
"handler is stashed away in a stack inside the handle.  You can restore the "
"previous error handler by calling L</guestfs_pop_error_handler>."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas L</guestfs_set_error_handler>, izņemot to, ka vecais "
"kļūdu apstrādātājs tiek noglabāts stekā roktura iekšienē.  Iepriekšējo kļūdu "
"apstrādātāju var atjaunot, izsaucot L</guestfs_pop_error_handler>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2011
msgid "Use the following code to temporarily disable errors around a function:"
msgstr "Izmantojiet šo kodu, lai īslaicīgi atspējotu kļūdas ap funkciju:"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2017
msgid "guestfs_pop_error_handler"
msgstr "guestfs_pop_error_handler"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2019
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void guestfs_pop_error_handler (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void guestfs_pop_error_handler (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2021
msgid "Restore the previous error handler (see L</guestfs_push_error_handler>)."
msgstr ""
"Atjaunot iepriekšējo kļūdu apstrādātāju (skatiet L</"
"guestfs_push_error_handler>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2023
msgid ""
"If you pop the stack too many times, then the default error handler is "
"restored."
msgstr ""
"Ja steku izņemat pārāk daudz reižu, tiek atjaunots noklusējuma kļūdu "
"apstrādātājs."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2026
msgid "guestfs_set_out_of_memory_handler"
msgstr "guestfs_set_out_of_memory_handler"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2028
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" typedef void (*guestfs_abort_cb) (void);\n"
" void guestfs_set_out_of_memory_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                         guestfs_abort_cb);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" typedef void (*guestfs_abort_cb) (void);\n"
" void guestfs_set_out_of_memory_handler (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                         guestfs_abort_cb);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2032
msgid ""
"The callback C<cb> will be called if there is an out of memory situation.  "
"I<Note this callback must not return>."
msgstr ""
"Atzvans C<cb> tiks izsaukts, ja radīsies atmiņas trūkuma situācija.  "
"I<Ņemiet vērā, ka šis atzvans nedrīkst atgriezties>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2035
msgid "The default is to call L<abort(3)>."
msgstr "Noklusējums ir izsaukt L<abort(3)>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2037
msgid "You cannot set C<cb> to C<NULL>.  You can’t ignore out of memory situations."
msgstr ""
"C<cb> nevar iestatīt uz C<NULL>.  Atmiņas trūkuma situācijas nevar ignorēt."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2040
msgid "guestfs_get_out_of_memory_handler"
msgstr "guestfs_get_out_of_memory_handler"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2042
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_abort_fn guestfs_get_out_of_memory_handler (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_abort_fn guestfs_get_out_of_memory_handler (guestfs_h *g);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2044
msgid "This returns the current out of memory handler."
msgstr "Tas atgriež pašreizējo atmiņas trūkuma apstrādātāju."

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2046
msgid "API CALLS"
msgstr "API IZSAUKUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2048
msgid "__ACTIONS__"
msgstr "__ACTIONS__"

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2050
msgid "STRUCTURES"
msgstr "STRUKTŪRAS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2052
msgid "__STRUCTS__"
msgstr "__STRUCTS__"

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2054
msgid "AVAILABILITY"
msgstr "PIEEJAMĪBA"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2056
msgid "GROUPS OF FUNCTIONALITY IN THE APPLIANCE"
msgstr "FUNKCIONALITĀTES GRUPAS PALĪGSISTĒMĀ"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2058
msgid ""
"Using L</guestfs_available> you can test availability of the following "
"groups of functions.  This test queries the appliance to see if the "
"appliance you are currently using supports the functionality."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot L</guestfs_available>, varat pārbaudīt šādu funkciju grupu "
"pieejamību.  Šis tests vaicā palīgsistēmai, vai pašlaik izmantotā "
"palīgsistēma atbalsta šo funkcionalitāti."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2063
msgid "__AVAILABILITY__"
msgstr "__AVAILABILITY__"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2065
msgid "FILESYSTEM AVAILABLE"
msgstr "PIEEJAMĀ FAILU SISTĒMA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2067
msgid ""
"The L</guestfs_filesystem_available> call tests whether a filesystem type is "
"supported by the appliance kernel."
msgstr ""
"Izsaukums L</guestfs_filesystem_available> pārbauda, vai palīgsistēmas "
"kodols atbalsta failu sistēmas tipu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2070
msgid ""
"This is mainly useful as a negative test.  If this returns true, it doesn't "
"mean that a particular filesystem can be mounted, since filesystems can fail "
"for other reasons such as it being a later version of the filesystem, or "
"having incompatible features."
msgstr ""
"Tas galvenokārt noder kā negatīvs tests.  Ja tas atgriež true, tas nenozīmē, "
"ka konkrēto failu sistēmu var montēt, jo failu sistēmas var neizdoties citu "
"iemeslu dēļ, piemēram, ja tā ir jaunāka failu sistēmas versija vai tai ir "
"nesaderīgi līdzekļi."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2075
msgid "GUESTFISH supported COMMAND"
msgstr "GUESTFISH KOMANDA supported"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2077
msgid ""
"In L<guestfish(3)> there is a handy interactive command C<supported> which "
"prints out the available groups and whether they are supported by this build "
"of libguestfs.  Note however that you have to do C<run> first."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(3)> ir ērta interaktīva komanda C<supported>, kas izdrukā "
"pieejamās grupas un to, vai šī libguestfs būve tās atbalsta.  Tomēr ņemiet "
"vērā, ka vispirms jāizpilda C<run>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2082
msgid "SINGLE CALLS AT COMPILE TIME"
msgstr "ATSEVIŠĶI IZSAUKUMI KOMPILĒŠANAS LAIKĀ"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2084
msgid ""
"Since version 1.5.8, C<E<lt>guestfs.hE<gt>> defines symbols for each C API "
"function, such as:"
msgstr ""
"Kopš versijas 1.5.8 C<E<lt>guestfs.hE<gt>> definē simbolus katrai C API "
"funkcijai, piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2087
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #define GUESTFS_HAVE_DD 1\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" #define GUESTFS_HAVE_DD 1\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2089
msgid "if L</guestfs_dd> is available."
msgstr "ja L</guestfs_dd> ir pieejams."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2091
msgid ""
"Before version 1.5.8, if you needed to test whether a single libguestfs "
"function is available at compile time, we recommended using build tools such "
"as autoconf or cmake.  For example in autotools you could use:"
msgstr ""
"Pirms versijas 1.5.8, ja vajadzēja pārbaudīt, vai viena libguestfs funkcija "
"ir pieejama kompilēšanas laikā, ieteicām izmantot tādus būvēšanas rīkus kā "
"autoconf vai cmake.  Piemēram, autotools varētu izmantot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2096
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" AC_CHECK_LIB([guestfs],[guestfs_create])\n"
" AC_CHECK_FUNCS([guestfs_dd])\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" AC_CHECK_LIB([guestfs],[guestfs_create])\n"
" AC_CHECK_FUNCS([guestfs_dd])\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2099
msgid ""
"which would result in C<HAVE_GUESTFS_DD> being either defined or not defined "
"in your program."
msgstr ""
"kā rezultātā jūsu programmā C<HAVE_GUESTFS_DD> būtu vai nu definēts, vai "
"nedefinēts."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2102
msgid "SINGLE CALLS AT RUN TIME"
msgstr "ATSEVIŠĶI IZSAUKUMI IZPILDLAIKĀ"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2104
msgid ""
"Testing at compile time doesn't guarantee that a function really exists in "
"the library.  The reason is that you might be dynamically linked against a "
"previous I<libguestfs.so> (dynamic library)  which doesn't have the call.  "
"This situation unfortunately results in a segmentation fault, which is a "
"shortcoming of the C dynamic linking system itself."
msgstr ""
"Pārbaude kompilēšanas laikā negarantē, ka funkcija tiešām eksistē "
"bibliotēkā.  Iemesls ir tāds, ka programma var būt dinamiski saistīta ar "
"iepriekšēju I<libguestfs.so> (dinamisko bibliotēku), kurā šī izsaukuma nav.  "
"Diemžēl šī situācija izraisa segmentācijas kļūdu, kas ir pašas C dinamiskās "
"saistīšanas sistēmas trūkums."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2111
msgid ""
"You can use L<dlopen(3)> to test if a function is available at run time, as "
"in this example program (note that you still need the compile time check as "
"well):"
msgstr ""
"Lai pārbaudītu, vai funkcija ir pieejama izpildes laikā, varat izmantot "
"L<dlopen(3)>, kā šajā programmas piemērā (ņemiet vērā, ka joprojām vajadzīga "
"arī pārbaude kompilēšanas laikā):"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" #include <stdio.h>\n"
" #include <stdlib.h>\n"
" #include <unistd.h>\n"
" #include <dlfcn.h>\n"
" #include <guestfs.h>\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" #include <stdio.h>\n"
" #include <stdlib.h>\n"
" #include <unistd.h>\n"
" #include <dlfcn.h>\n"
" #include <guestfs.h>\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" main ()\n"
" {\n"
" #ifdef GUESTFS_HAVE_DD\n"
"   void *dl;\n"
"   int has_function;\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" main ()\n"
" {\n"
" #ifdef GUESTFS_HAVE_DD\n"
"   void *dl;\n"
"   int has_function;\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2127
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   /* Test if the function guestfs_dd is really available. */\n"
"   dl = dlopen (NULL, RTLD_LAZY);\n"
"   if (!dl) {\n"
"     fprintf (stderr, \"dlopen: %s\\n\", dlerror ());\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"   }\n"
"   has_function = dlsym (dl, \"guestfs_dd\") != NULL;\n"
"   dlclose (dl);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   /* Test if the function guestfs_dd is really available. */\n"
"   dl = dlopen (NULL, RTLD_LAZY);\n"
"   if (!dl) {\n"
"     fprintf (stderr, \"dlopen: %s\\n\", dlerror ());\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"   }\n"
"   has_function = dlsym (dl, \"guestfs_dd\") != NULL;\n"
"   dlclose (dl);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   if (!has_function)\n"
"     printf (\"this libguestfs.so does NOT have guestfs_dd function\\n\");\n"
"   else {\n"
"     printf (\"this libguestfs.so has guestfs_dd function\\n\");\n"
"     /* Now it's safe to call\n"
"     guestfs_dd (g, \"foo\", \"bar\");\n"
"     */\n"
"   }\n"
" #else\n"
"   printf (\"guestfs_dd function was not found at compile time\\n\");\n"
" #endif\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"   if (!has_function)\n"
"     printf (\"this libguestfs.so does NOT have guestfs_dd function\\n\");\n"
"   else {\n"
"     printf (\"this libguestfs.so has guestfs_dd function\\n\");\n"
"     /* Now it's safe to call\n"
"     guestfs_dd (g, \"foo\", \"bar\");\n"
"     */\n"
"   }\n"
" #else\n"
"   printf (\"guestfs_dd function was not found at compile time\\n\");\n"
" #endif\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2149
msgid ""
"You may think the above is an awful lot of hassle, and it is.  There are "
"other ways outside of the C linking system to ensure that this kind of "
"incompatibility never arises, such as using package versioning:"
msgstr ""
"Varbūt domājat, ka iepriekšējais ir šausmīgi daudz pūļu, un tā tas arī ir.  "
"Ir citi veidi ārpus C saistīšanas sistēmas, kā nodrošināt, ka šāda "
"nesaderība nekad nerodas, piemēram, izmantojot pakotņu versijas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2154
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Requires: libguestfs >= 1.0.80\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" Requires: libguestfs >= 1.0.80\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2156
msgid "CALLS WITH OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS"
msgstr "IZSAUKUMI AR NEOBLIGĀTIEM ARGUMENTIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2158
msgid ""
"A recent feature of the API is the introduction of calls which take optional "
"arguments.  In C these are declared 3 ways.  The main way is as a call which "
"takes variable arguments (ie. C<...>), as in this example:"
msgstr ""
"Nesens API līdzeklis ir izsaukumi, kas pieņem neobligātus argumentus.  C "
"valodā tie tiek deklarēti 3 veidos.  Galvenais veids ir kā izsaukums, kas "
"pieņem mainīgu argumentu skaitu (t. i., C<...>), kā šajā piemērā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2163
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int guestfs_add_drive_opts (guestfs_h *g, const char *filename, ...);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int guestfs_add_drive_opts (guestfs_h *g, const char *filename, ...);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2165
msgid ""
"Call this with a list of optional arguments, terminated by C<-1>.  So to "
"call with no optional arguments specified:"
msgstr ""
"Izsauciet to ar neobligāto argumentu sarakstu, kas noslēgts ar C<-1>.  "
"Tātad, lai izsauktu bez neobligātiem argumentiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2168
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename, -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename, -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2170
msgid "With a single optional argument:"
msgstr "Ar vienu neobligātu argumentu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2172
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"qcow2\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"qcow2\",\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2176
msgid "With two:"
msgstr "Ar diviem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2178
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"qcow2\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_READONLY, 1,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts (g, filename,\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT, \"qcow2\",\n"
"                         GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_READONLY, 1,\n"
"                         -1);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2183
msgid ""
"and so forth.  Don’t forget the terminating C<-1> otherwise Bad Things will "
"happen!"
msgstr ""
"un tā tālāk.  Neaizmirstiet noslēdzošo C<-1>, citādi notiks Sliktas Lietas!"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2186
msgid "USING va_list FOR OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS"
msgstr "va_list IZMANTOŠANA NEOBLIGĀTIEM ARGUMENTIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2188
msgid ""
"The second variant has the same name with the suffix C<_va>, which works the "
"same way but takes a C<va_list>.  See the C manual for details.  For the "
"example function, this is declared:"
msgstr ""
"Otrajam variantam ir tas pats nosaukums ar sufiksu C<_va>, kas darbojas "
"tāpat, bet pieņem C<va_list>.  Sīkāk skatiet C rokasgrāmatā.  Piemēra "
"funkcijai tas ir deklarēts šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2192
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int guestfs_add_drive_opts_va (guestfs_h *g, const char *filename,\n"
"                                va_list args);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int guestfs_add_drive_opts_va (guestfs_h *g, const char *filename,\n"
"                                va_list args);\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2195
msgid "CONSTRUCTING OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS"
msgstr "NEOBLIGĀTO ARGUMENTU VEIDOŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2197
msgid ""
"The third variant is useful where you need to construct these calls.  You "
"pass in a structure where you fill in the optional fields.  The structure "
"has a bitmask as the first element which you must set to indicate which "
"fields you have filled in.  For our example function the structure and call "
"are declared:"
msgstr ""
"Trešais variants noder, ja šie izsaukumi jākonstruē.  Jūs nododat struktūru, "
"kurā aizpildāt neobligātos laukus.  Struktūras pirmais elements ir bitu "
"maska, kas jāiestata, lai norādītu, kuri lauki aizpildīti.  Mūsu piemēra "
"funkcijai struktūra un izsaukums ir deklarēti šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2203
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" struct guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv {\n"
"   uint64_t bitmask;\n"
"   int readonly;\n"
"   const char *format;\n"
"   /* ... */\n"
" };\n"
" int guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv (guestfs_h *g, const char *filename,\n"
"              const struct guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv *optargs);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" struct guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv {\n"
"   uint64_t bitmask;\n"
"   int readonly;\n"
"   const char *format;\n"
"   /* ... */\n"
" };\n"
" int guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv (guestfs_h *g, const char *filename,\n"
"              const struct guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv *optargs);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2212
msgid "You could call it like this:"
msgstr "To varētu izsaukt šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2214
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" struct guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv optargs = {\n"
"   .bitmask = GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_READONLY_BITMASK |\n"
"              GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT_BITMASK,\n"
"   .readonly = 1,\n"
"   .format = \"qcow2\"\n"
" };\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" struct guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv optargs = {\n"
"   .bitmask = GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_READONLY_BITMASK |\n"
"              GUESTFS_ADD_DRIVE_OPTS_FORMAT_BITMASK,\n"
"   .readonly = 1,\n"
"   .format = \"qcow2\"\n"
" };\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2221
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv (g, filename, &optargs);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_add_drive_opts_argv (g, filename, &optargs);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2229
msgid "The C<_BITMASK> suffix on each option name when specifying the bitmask."
msgstr "Sufikss C<_BITMASK> pie katras opcijas nosaukuma, norādot bitu masku."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2234
msgid "You do not need to fill in all fields of the structure."
msgstr "Visi struktūras lauki nav jāaizpilda."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2238
msgid ""
"There must be a one-to-one correspondence between fields of the structure "
"that are filled in, and bits set in the bitmask."
msgstr ""
"Starp aizpildītajiem struktūras laukiem un bitu maskā iestatītajiem bitiem "
"jābūt atbilstībai viens pret vienu."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2243
msgid "OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS IN OTHER LANGUAGES"
msgstr "NEOBLIGĀTIE ARGUMENTI CITĀS VALODĀS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2245
msgid ""
"In other languages, optional arguments are expressed in the way that is "
"natural for that language.  We refer you to the language-specific "
"documentation for more details on that."
msgstr ""
"Citās valodās neobligātie argumenti tiek izteikti šai valodai dabiskā "
"veidā.  Sīkāk skatiet konkrētās valodas dokumentāciju."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2249
msgid "For guestfish, see L<guestfish(1)/OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS>."
msgstr "Guestfish skatiet L<guestfish(1)/NEOBLIGĀTIE ARGUMENTI>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2253
msgid "SETTING CALLBACKS TO HANDLE EVENTS"
msgstr "ATZVANU IESTATĪŠANA NOTIKUMU APSTRĀDEI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2255
msgid ""
"B<Note:> This section documents the generic event mechanism introduced in "
"libguestfs 1.10, which you should use in new code if possible.  The old "
"functions C<guestfs_set_log_message_callback>, "
"C<guestfs_set_subprocess_quit_callback>, "
"C<guestfs_set_launch_done_callback>, C<guestfs_set_close_callback> and "
"C<guestfs_set_progress_callback> are no longer documented in this manual "
"page.  Because of the ABI guarantee, the old functions continue to work."
msgstr ""
"B<Piezīme:> šajā sadaļā dokumentēts vispārīgais notikumu mehānisms, kas "
"ieviests libguestfs 1.10 un kas, ja iespējams, jāizmanto jaunā kodā.  Vecās "
"funkcijas C<guestfs_set_log_message_callback>, "
"C<guestfs_set_subprocess_quit_callback>, C<guestfs_set_launch_done_callback>"
", C<guestfs_set_close_callback> un C<guestfs_set_progress_callback> šajā "
"rokasgrāmatas lapā vairs netiek dokumentētas.  ABI garantijas dēļ vecās "
"funkcijas turpina darboties."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2264
msgid ""
"Handles generate events when certain things happen, such as log messages "
"being generated, progress messages during long-running operations, or the "
"handle being closed.  The API calls described below let you register a "
"callback to be called when events happen.  You can register multiple "
"callbacks (for the same, different or overlapping sets of events), and "
"individually remove callbacks.  If callbacks are not removed, then they "
"remain in force until the handle is closed."
msgstr ""
"Rokturi ģenerē notikumus, kad notiek noteiktas lietas, piemēram, tiek "
"ģenerēti žurnāla ziņojumi, progresa ziņojumi ilgstošu darbību laikā vai "
"rokturis tiek aizvērts.  Tālāk aprakstītie API izsaukumi ļauj reģistrēt "
"atzvanu, kas tiks izsaukts, kad notiek notikumi.  Var reģistrēt vairākus "
"atzvanus (tām pašām, dažādām vai pārklājošām notikumu kopām) un atsevišķi "
"noņemt atzvanus.  Ja atzvani netiek noņemti, tie paliek spēkā, līdz rokturis "
"tiek aizvērts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2272
msgid ""
"In the current implementation, events are only generated synchronously: that "
"means that events (and hence callbacks) can only happen while you are in the "
"middle of making another libguestfs call.  The callback is called in the "
"same thread."
msgstr ""
"Pašreizējā realizācijā notikumi tiek ģenerēti tikai sinhroni: tas nozīmē, ka "
"notikumi (un līdz ar to atzvani) var notikt tikai tad, kad esat cita "
"libguestfs izsaukuma vidū.  Atzvans tiek izsaukts tajā pašā pavedienā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2277
msgid ""
"Events may contain a payload, usually nothing (void), an array of 64 bit "
"unsigned integers, or a message buffer.  Payloads are discussed later on."
msgstr ""
"Notikumiem var būt slodze — parasti nekas (void), 64 bitu neparakstītu "
"veselu skaitļu masīvs vai ziņojuma buferis.  Slodzes aplūkotas vēlāk."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2281
msgid "CLASSES OF EVENTS"
msgstr "NOTIKUMU KLASES"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2285
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_CLOSE (payload type: void)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_CLOSE (slodzes tips: void)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2288
msgid ""
"The callback function will be called while the handle is being closed "
"(synchronously from L</guestfs_close>)."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiks izsaukta roktura aizvēršanas laikā (sinhroni no L</"
"guestfs_close>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2291
msgid ""
"Note that libguestfs installs an L<atexit(3)> handler to try to clean up "
"handles that are open when the program exits.  This means that this callback "
"might be called indirectly from L<exit(3)>, which can cause unexpected "
"problems in higher-level languages (eg. if your HLL interpreter has already "
"been cleaned up by the time this is called, and if your callback then jumps "
"into some HLL function)."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka libguestfs instalē L<atexit(3)> apstrādātāju, lai mēģinātu "
"sakopt rokturus, kas ir atvērti, programmai izejot.  Tas nozīmē, ka šo "
"atzvanu var netieši izsaukt no L<exit(3)>, kas var radīt negaidītas "
"problēmas augstāka līmeņa valodās (piem., ja jūsu HLL interpretators jau ir "
"sakopts brīdī, kad tas tiek izsaukts, un jūsu atzvans pēc tam pārlec uz kādu "
"HLL funkciju)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2298
msgid ""
"If no callback is registered: the handle is closed without any callback "
"being invoked."
msgstr ""
"Ja atzvans nav reģistrēts: rokturis tiek aizvērts, neizsaucot nevienu "
"atzvanu."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2301
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_SUBPROCESS_QUIT (payload type: void)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_SUBPROCESS_QUIT (slodzes tips: void)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2304
msgid ""
"The callback function will be called when the child process quits, either "
"asynchronously or if killed by L</guestfs_kill_subprocess>.  (This "
"corresponds to a transition from any state to the CONFIG state)."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiks izsaukta, kad bērnprocess iziet, vai nu asinhroni, vai "
"ja to nobeidz L</guestfs_kill_subprocess>.  (Tas atbilst pārejai no jebkura "
"stāvokļa uz stāvokli CONFIG.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2308 lib/guestfs.pod:2317 lib/guestfs.pod:2444
msgid "If no callback is registered: the event is ignored."
msgstr "Ja atzvans nav reģistrēts: notikums tiek ignorēts."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2310
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_LAUNCH_DONE (payload type: void)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_LAUNCH_DONE (slodzes tips: void)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2313
msgid ""
"The callback function will be called when the child process becomes ready "
"first time after it has been launched.  (This corresponds to a transition "
"from LAUNCHING to the READY state)."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiks izsaukta, kad bērnprocess pirmo reizi pēc palaišanas "
"kļūst gatavs.  (Tas atbilst pārejai no LAUNCHING uz stāvokli READY.)"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2319
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_PROGRESS (payload type: array of 4 x uint64_t)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_PROGRESS (slodzes tips: 4 x uint64_t masīvs)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2322
msgid ""
"Some long-running operations can generate progress messages.  If this "
"callback is registered, then it will be called each time a progress message "
"is generated (usually two seconds after the operation started, and three "
"times per second thereafter until it completes, although the frequency may "
"change in future versions)."
msgstr ""
"Dažas ilgstošas darbības var ģenerēt progresa ziņojumus.  Ja šis atzvans ir "
"reģistrēts, tas tiks izsaukts katru reizi, kad tiek ģenerēts progresa "
"ziņojums (parasti divas sekundes pēc darbības sākuma un pēc tam trīs reizes "
"sekundē, līdz tā beidzas, lai gan biežums nākamajās versijās var mainīties)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2328
msgid ""
"The callback receives in the payload four unsigned 64 bit numbers which are "
"(in order): C<proc_nr>, C<serial>, C<position>, C<total>."
msgstr ""
"Atzvans slodzē saņem četrus neparakstītus 64 bitu skaitļus, kas ir (šādā "
"secībā): C<proc_nr>, C<serial>, C<position>, C<total>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2331
msgid ""
"The units of C<total> are not defined, although for some operations C<total> "
"may relate in some way to the amount of data to be transferred (eg. in bytes "
"or megabytes), and C<position> may be the portion which has been "
"transferred."
msgstr ""
"C<total> vienības nav definētas, lai gan dažām darbībām C<total> var būt "
"kaut kā saistīts ar pārsūtāmo datu apjomu (piem., baitos vai megabaitos), un "
"C<position> var būt jau pārsūtītā daļa."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2336
msgid "The only defined and stable parts of the API are:"
msgstr "Vienīgās definētās un stabilās API daļas ir:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2342
msgid ""
"The callback can display to the user some type of progress bar or indicator "
"which shows the ratio of C<position>:C<total>."
msgstr ""
"Atzvans var lietotājam parādīt kāda veida progresa joslu vai indikatoru, kas "
"rāda attiecību C<position>:C<total>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2347
msgid "0 E<lt>= C<position> E<lt>= C<total>"
msgstr "0 E<lt>= C<position> E<lt>= C<total>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2351
msgid ""
"If any progress notification is sent during a call, then a final progress "
"notification is always sent when C<position> = C<total> (I<unless> the call "
"fails with an error)."
msgstr ""
"Ja izsaukuma laikā tiek nosūtīts jebkāds progresa paziņojums, vienmēr tiek "
"nosūtīts arī pēdējais progresa paziņojums, kad C<position> = C<total> (I<ja "
"vien> izsaukums neizdodas ar kļūdu)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2355
msgid ""
"This is to simplify caller code, so callers can easily set the progress "
"indicator to \"100%\" at the end of the operation, without requiring special "
"code to detect this case."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir, lai vienkāršotu izsaucēja kodu, lai izsaucēji darbības beigās varētu "
"viegli iestatīt progresa indikatoru uz „100%”, bez īpaša koda šī gadījuma "
"noteikšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2361
msgid ""
"For some calls we are unable to estimate the progress of the call, but we "
"can still generate progress messages to indicate activity.  This is known as "
"\"pulse mode\", and is directly supported by certain progress bar "
"implementations (eg. GtkProgressBar)."
msgstr ""
"Dažiem izsaukumiem nevaram novērtēt izsaukuma progresu, bet joprojām varam "
"ģenerēt progresa ziņojumus, lai norādītu aktivitāti.  To sauc par „pulsa "
"režīmu”, un to tieši atbalsta dažas progresa joslu realizācijas (piem., "
"GtkProgressBar)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2366
msgid ""
"For these calls, zero or more progress messages are generated with "
"C<position = 0> and C<total = 1>, followed by a final message with "
"C<position = total = 1>."
msgstr ""
"Šiem izsaukumiem tiek ģenerēti nulle vai vairāk progresa ziņojumu ar "
"C<position = 0> un C<total = 1>, kam seko pēdējais ziņojums ar C<position = "
"total = 1>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2370
msgid ""
"As noted above, if the call fails with an error then the final message may "
"not be generated."
msgstr ""
"Kā minēts iepriekš, ja izsaukums neizdodas ar kļūdu, pēdējais ziņojums var "
"netikt ģenerēts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2375
msgid ""
"The callback also receives the procedure number (C<proc_nr>) and serial "
"number (C<serial>) of the call.  These are only useful for debugging "
"protocol issues, and the callback can normally ignore them.  The callback "
"may want to print these numbers in error messages or debugging messages."
msgstr ""
"Atzvans saņem arī izsaukuma procedūras numuru (C<proc_nr>) un sērijas numuru "
"(C<serial>).  Tie noder tikai protokola problēmu atkļūdošanai, un atzvans "
"parasti var tos ignorēt.  Atzvans var vēlēties tos izdrukāt kļūdu vai "
"atkļūdošanas ziņojumos."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2381
msgid "If no callback is registered: progress messages are discarded."
msgstr "Ja atzvans nav reģistrēts: progresa ziņojumi tiek atmesti."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2383
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE (payload type: message buffer)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE (slodzes tips: ziņojuma buferis)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2386
msgid ""
"The callback function is called whenever a log message is generated by qemu, "
"the appliance kernel, guestfsd (daemon), or utility programs."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiek izsaukta katru reizi, kad qemu, palīgsistēmas kodols, "
"guestfsd (dēmons) vai utilītprogrammas ģenerē žurnāla ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2389
msgid ""
"If the verbose flag (L</guestfs_set_verbose>) is set before launch "
"(L</guestfs_launch>) then additional debug messages are generated."
msgstr ""
"Ja pirms palaišanas (L</guestfs_launch>) ir iestatīts izvērstās izvades "
"karogs (L</guestfs_set_verbose>), tiek ģenerēti papildu atkļūdošanas "
"ziņojumi."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2392 lib/guestfs.pod:2406
msgid ""
"If no callback is registered: the messages are discarded unless the verbose "
"flag is set in which case they are sent to stderr.  You can override the "
"printing of verbose messages to stderr by setting up a callback."
msgstr ""
"Ja atzvans nav reģistrēts: ziņojumi tiek atmesti, ja vien nav iestatīts "
"izvērstās izvades karogs — tādā gadījumā tie tiek sūtīti uz stderr.  "
"Izvērsto ziņojumu drukāšanu uz stderr varat ignorēt, iestatot atzvanu."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2397
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY (payload type: message buffer)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY (slodzes tips: ziņojuma buferis)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2400
msgid ""
"The callback function is called whenever a log message is generated by the "
"library part of libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiek izsaukta katru reizi, kad libguestfs bibliotēkas daļa "
"ģenerē žurnāla ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2403
msgid ""
"If the verbose flag (L</guestfs_set_verbose>) is set then additional debug "
"messages are generated."
msgstr ""
"Ja ir iestatīts izvērstās izvades karogs (L</guestfs_set_verbose>), tiek "
"ģenerēti papildu atkļūdošanas ziņojumi."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2411
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING (payload type: message buffer)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING (slodzes tips: ziņojuma buferis)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2414
msgid ""
"The callback function is called whenever a warning message is generated by "
"the library part of libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiek izsaukta katru reizi, kad libguestfs bibliotēkas daļa "
"ģenerē brīdinājuma ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2417
msgid ""
"If no callback is registered: the messages are printed to stderr.  You can "
"override the printing of warning messages to stderr by setting up a "
"callback."
msgstr ""
"Ja atzvans nav reģistrēts: ziņojumi tiek izdrukāti uz stderr.  Brīdinājuma "
"ziņojumu drukāšanu uz stderr varat ignorēt, iestatot atzvanu."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2421
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_TRACE (payload type: message buffer)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_TRACE (slodzes tips: ziņojuma buferis)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2424
msgid ""
"The callback function is called whenever a trace message is generated.  This "
"only applies if the trace flag (L</guestfs_set_trace>) is set."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiek izsaukta katru reizi, kad tiek ģenerēts izsekošanas "
"ziņojums.  Tas attiecas tikai tad, ja ir iestatīts izsekošanas karogs (L</"
"guestfs_set_trace>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2427
msgid ""
"If no callback is registered: the messages are sent to stderr.  You can "
"override the printing of trace messages to stderr by setting up a callback."
msgstr ""
"Ja atzvans nav reģistrēts: ziņojumi tiek sūtīti uz stderr.  Izsekošanas "
"ziņojumu drukāšanu uz stderr varat ignorēt, iestatot atzvanu."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2431
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_ENTER (payload type: function name)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_ENTER (slodzes tips: funkcijas nosaukums)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2434
msgid "The callback function is called whenever a libguestfs function is entered."
msgstr ""
"Atzvana funkcija tiek izsaukta katru reizi, kad tiek ieiets libguestfs "
"funkcijā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2437
msgid ""
"The payload is a string which contains the name of the function that we are "
"entering (not including C<guestfs_> prefix)."
msgstr ""
"Slodze ir virkne, kas satur funkcijas nosaukumu, kurā ieejam (neietverot "
"priedēkli C<guestfs_>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2440
msgid ""
"Note that libguestfs functions can call themselves, so you may see many "
"events from a single call.  A few libguestfs functions do not generate this "
"event."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka libguestfs funkcijas var izsaukt pašas sevi, tāpēc no viena "
"izsaukuma var redzēt daudz notikumu.  Dažas libguestfs funkcijas šo notikumu "
"neģenerē."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2446
msgid "GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH (payload type: libvirt URI)"
msgstr "GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH (slodzes tips: libvirt URI)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2449
msgid ""
"For any API function that opens a libvirt connection, this event may be "
"generated to indicate that libvirt demands authentication information.  See "
"L</LIBVIRT AUTHENTICATION> below."
msgstr ""
"Jebkurai API funkcijai, kas atver libvirt savienojumu, šis notikums var tikt "
"ģenerēts, lai norādītu, ka libvirt pieprasa autentifikācijas informāciju.  "
"Skatiet L</LIBVIRT AUTENTIFIKĀCIJA> tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2453
msgid ""
"If no callback is registered: C<virConnectAuthPtrDefault> is used (suitable "
"for command-line programs only)."
msgstr ""
"Ja atzvans nav reģistrēts: tiek izmantots C<virConnectAuthPtrDefault> "
"(piemērots tikai komandrindas programmām)."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2458
msgid "EVENT API"
msgstr "NOTIKUMU API"

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2460
msgid "guestfs_set_event_callback"
msgstr "guestfs_set_event_callback"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2462
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int guestfs_set_event_callback (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                 guestfs_event_callback cb,\n"
"                                 uint64_t event_bitmask,\n"
"                                 int flags,\n"
"                                 void *opaque);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int guestfs_set_event_callback (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                                 guestfs_event_callback cb,\n"
"                                 uint64_t event_bitmask,\n"
"                                 int flags,\n"
"                                 void *opaque);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2468
msgid ""
"This function registers a callback (C<cb>) for all event classes in the "
"C<event_bitmask>."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija reģistrē atzvanu (C<cb>) visām notikumu klasēm C<event_bitmask>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2471
msgid ""
"For example, to register for all log message events, you could call this "
"function with the bitmask "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE|GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY|GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING>.  To "
"register a single callback for all possible classes of events, use "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_ALL>."
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, lai reģistrētos visiem žurnāla ziņojumu notikumiem, šo funkciju "
"varētu izsaukt ar bitu masku "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE|GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY|GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING>.  Lai "
"reģistrētu vienu atzvanu visām iespējamajām notikumu klasēm, izmantojiet "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_ALL>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2477
msgid "C<flags> should always be passed as 0."
msgstr "C<flags> vienmēr jānodod kā 0."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2479
msgid ""
"C<opaque> is an opaque pointer which is passed to the callback.  You can use "
"it for any purpose."
msgstr ""
"C<opaque> ir necaurredzams rādītājs, kas tiek nodots atzvanam.  To var "
"izmantot jebkuram nolūkam."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2482
msgid ""
"The return value is the event handle (an integer) which you can use to "
"delete the callback (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Atgriešanas vērtība ir notikuma rokturis (vesels skaitlis), ko var izmantot "
"atzvana dzēšanai (skatiet tālāk)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2485
msgid ""
"If there is an error, this function returns C<-1>, and sets the error in the "
"handle in the usual way (see L</guestfs_last_error> etc.)"
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas gadījumā šī funkcija atgriež C<-1> un parastajā veidā iestata kļūdu "
"rokturī (skatiet L</guestfs_last_error> u. c.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2488
msgid ""
"Callbacks remain in effect until they are deleted, or until the handle is "
"closed."
msgstr ""
"Atzvani paliek spēkā, līdz tie tiek dzēsti vai līdz rokturis tiek aizvērts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2491
msgid ""
"In the case where multiple callbacks are registered for a particular event "
"class, all of the callbacks are called.  The order in which multiple "
"callbacks are called is not defined."
msgstr ""
"Ja konkrētai notikumu klasei reģistrēti vairāki atzvani, tiek izsaukti visi "
"atzvani.  Vairāku atzvanu izsaukšanas secība nav definēta."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2495
msgid "guestfs_delete_event_callback"
msgstr "guestfs_delete_event_callback"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2497
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void guestfs_delete_event_callback (guestfs_h *g, int event_handle);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void guestfs_delete_event_callback (guestfs_h *g, int event_handle);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2499
msgid ""
"Delete a callback that was previously registered.  C<event_handle> should be "
"the integer that was returned by a previous call to "
"C<guestfs_set_event_callback> on the same handle."
msgstr ""
"Dzēst iepriekš reģistrētu atzvanu.  C<event_handle> jābūt veselam skaitlim, "
"ko atgriezis iepriekšējs C<guestfs_set_event_callback> izsaukums tam pašam "
"rokturim."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2503
msgid "guestfs_event_to_string"
msgstr "guestfs_event_to_string"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2505
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" char *guestfs_event_to_string (uint64_t event);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" char *guestfs_event_to_string (uint64_t event);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2507
msgid ""
"C<event> is either a single event or a bitmask of events.  This returns a "
"string representation (useful for debugging or printing events)."
msgstr ""
"C<event> ir vai nu viens notikums, vai notikumu bitu maska.  Tas atgriež "
"virknes attēlojumu (noderīgu atkļūdošanai vai notikumu izdrukāšanai)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2511
msgid "A single event is returned as the name in lower case, eg. C<\"close\">."
msgstr ""
"Viens notikums tiek atgriezts kā nosaukums mazajiem burtiem, piem., "
"C<\"close\">."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2513
msgid ""
"A bitmask of several events is returned as a comma-separated list, "
"eg. C<\"close,progress\">."
msgstr ""
"Vairāku notikumu bitu maska tiek atgriezta kā ar komatiem atdalīts saraksts, "
"piem., C<\"close,progress\">."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2516
msgid "If zero is passed, then the empty string C<\"\"> is returned."
msgstr "Ja tiek nodota nulle, tiek atgriezta tukša virkne C<\"\">."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2518
msgid ""
"On success this returns a string.  On error it returns NULL and sets "
"C<errno>."
msgstr ""
"Veiksmes gadījumā tas atgriež virkni.  Kļūdas gadījumā tas atgriež NULL un "
"iestata C<errno>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2521
msgid "The returned string must be freed by the caller."
msgstr "Atgrieztā virkne izsaucējam jāatbrīvo."

#. type: =head3
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2523
msgid "guestfs_event_callback"
msgstr "guestfs_event_callback"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2525
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" typedef void (*guestfs_event_callback) (\n"
"                  guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                  void *opaque,\n"
"                  uint64_t event,\n"
"                  int event_handle,\n"
"                  int flags,\n"
"                  const char *buf, size_t buf_len,\n"
"                  const uint64_t *array, size_t array_len);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" typedef void (*guestfs_event_callback) (\n"
"                  guestfs_h *g,\n"
"                  void *opaque,\n"
"                  uint64_t event,\n"
"                  int event_handle,\n"
"                  int flags,\n"
"                  const char *buf, size_t buf_len,\n"
"                  const uint64_t *array, size_t array_len);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2534
msgid "This is the type of the event callback function that you have to provide."
msgstr "Šis ir notikuma atzvana funkcijas tips, kas jums jānodrošina."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2537
msgid ""
"The basic parameters are: the handle (C<g>), the opaque user pointer "
"(C<opaque>), the event class (eg. C<GUESTFS_EVENT_PROGRESS>), the event "
"handle, and C<flags> which in the current API you should ignore."
msgstr ""
"Pamata parametri ir: rokturis (C<g>), necaurredzamais lietotāja rādītājs "
"(C<opaque>), notikuma klase (piem., C<GUESTFS_EVENT_PROGRESS>), notikuma "
"rokturis un C<flags>, kas pašreizējā API jāignorē."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2541
msgid ""
"The remaining parameters contain the event payload (if any).  Each event may "
"contain a payload, which usually relates to the event class, but for future "
"proofing your code should be written to handle any payload for any event "
"class."
msgstr ""
"Atlikušie parametri satur notikuma slodzi (ja tāda ir).  Katram notikumam "
"var būt slodze, kas parasti attiecas uz notikuma klasi, bet nākotnes "
"drošības labad jūsu kodam jāspēj apstrādāt jebkuru slodzi jebkurai notikumu "
"klasei."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2546
msgid ""
"C<buf> and C<buf_len> contain a message buffer (if C<buf_len == 0>, then "
"there is no message buffer).  Note that this message buffer can contain "
"arbitrary 8 bit data, including NUL bytes."
msgstr ""
"C<buf> un C<buf_len> satur ziņojuma buferi (ja C<buf_len == 0>, ziņojuma "
"bufera nav).  Ņemiet vērā, ka šis ziņojuma buferis var saturēt patvaļīgus 8 "
"bitu datus, ieskaitot NUL baitus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2550
msgid ""
"C<array> and C<array_len> is an array of 64 bit unsigned integers.  At the "
"moment this is only used for progress messages."
msgstr ""
"C<array> un C<array_len> ir 64 bitu neparakstītu veselu skaitļu masīvs.  "
"Pašlaik to izmanto tikai progresa ziņojumiem."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2553
msgid "EXAMPLE: CAPTURING LOG MESSAGES"
msgstr "PIEMĒRS: ŽURNĀLA ZIŅOJUMU TVERŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2555
msgid ""
"A working program demonstrating this can be found in "
"F<examples/debug-logging.c> in the source of libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Strādājošu programmu, kas to demonstrē, var atrast libguestfs pirmkodā failā "
"F<examples/debug-logging.c>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2558
msgid ""
"One motivation for the generic event API was to allow GUI programs to "
"capture debug and other messages.  In libguestfs E<le> 1.8 these were sent "
"unconditionally to C<stderr>."
msgstr ""
"Viens no vispārīgās notikumu API motīviem bija ļaut GUI programmām tvert "
"atkļūdošanas un citus ziņojumus.  Libguestfs E<le> 1.8 tie tika bez "
"nosacījumiem sūtīti uz C<stderr>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2562
msgid ""
"Events associated with log messages are: C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY>, "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE>, C<GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING> and "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_TRACE>.  (Note that error messages are not events; you must "
"capture error messages separately)."
msgstr ""
"Ar žurnāla ziņojumiem saistītie notikumi ir: C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY>, "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE>, C<GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING> un "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_TRACE>.  (Ņemiet vērā, ka kļūdu ziņojumi nav notikumi; kļūdu "
"ziņojumi jātver atsevišķi.)"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2567
msgid ""
"Programs have to set up a callback to capture the classes of events of "
"interest:"
msgstr "Programmām jāiestata atzvans, lai tvertu interesējošās notikumu klases:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2570
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int eh =\n"
"   guestfs_set_event_callback\n"
"     (g, message_callback,\n"
"      GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY | GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE |\n"
"      GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING | GUESTFS_EVENT_TRACE,\n"
"      0, NULL) == -1)\n"
" if (eh == -1) {\n"
"   // handle error in the usual way\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int eh =\n"
"   guestfs_set_event_callback\n"
"     (g, message_callback,\n"
"      GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBRARY | GUESTFS_EVENT_APPLIANCE |\n"
"      GUESTFS_EVENT_WARNING | GUESTFS_EVENT_TRACE,\n"
"      0, NULL) == -1)\n"
" if (eh == -1) {\n"
"   // handle error in the usual way\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2580
msgid ""
"The callback can then direct messages to the appropriate place.  In this "
"example, messages are directed to syslog:"
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam atzvans var novirzīt ziņojumus uz piemērotu vietu.  Šajā piemērā "
"ziņojumi tiek novirzīti uz syslog:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2583
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" static void\n"
" message_callback (\n"
"         guestfs_h *g,\n"
"         void *opaque,\n"
"         uint64_t event,\n"
"         int event_handle,\n"
"         int flags,\n"
"         const char *buf, size_t buf_len,\n"
"         const uint64_t *array, size_t array_len)\n"
" {\n"
"   const int priority = LOG_USER|LOG_INFO;\n"
"   if (buf_len > 0)\n"
"     syslog (priority, \"event 0x%lx: %s\", event, buf);\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" static void\n"
" message_callback (\n"
"         guestfs_h *g,\n"
"         void *opaque,\n"
"         uint64_t event,\n"
"         int event_handle,\n"
"         int flags,\n"
"         const char *buf, size_t buf_len,\n"
"         const uint64_t *array, size_t array_len)\n"
" {\n"
"   const int priority = LOG_USER|LOG_INFO;\n"
"   if (buf_len > 0)\n"
"     syslog (priority, \"event 0x%lx: %s\", event, buf);\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2598
msgid "LIBVIRT AUTHENTICATION"
msgstr "LIBVIRT AUTENTIFIKĀCIJA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2600
msgid ""
"Some libguestfs API calls can open libvirt connections.  Currently the only "
"ones are L</guestfs_add_domain>; and L</guestfs_launch> if the libvirt "
"backend has been selected.  Libvirt connections may require authentication, "
"for example if they need to access a remote server or to access root "
"services from non-root.  Libvirt authentication happens via a callback "
"mechanism, see "
"L<http://libvirt.org/guide/html/Application_Development_Guide-Connections.html>"
msgstr ""
"Daži libguestfs API izsaukumi var atvērt libvirt savienojumus.  Pašlaik "
"vienīgie ir L</guestfs_add_domain> un L</guestfs_launch>, ja izvēlēta "
"libvirt aizmugursistēma.  Libvirt savienojumiem var būt nepieciešama "
"autentifikācija, piemēram, ja tiem jāpiekļūst attālam serverim vai "
"jāpiekļūst root pakalpojumiem no ne-root.  Libvirt autentifikācija notiek "
"caur atzvanu mehānismu, skatiet L<http://libvirt.org/guide/html/"
"Application_Development_Guide-Connections.html>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2608
msgid ""
"You may provide libvirt authentication data by registering a callback for "
"events of type C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH>."
msgstr ""
"Libvirt autentifikācijas datus varat nodrošināt, reģistrējot atzvanu "
"notikumiem ar tipu C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2611
msgid ""
"If no such event is registered, then libguestfs uses a libvirt function that "
"provides command-line prompts (C<virConnectAuthPtrDefault>).  This is only "
"suitable for command-line libguestfs programs."
msgstr ""
"Ja šāds notikums nav reģistrēts, libguestfs izmanto libvirt funkciju, kas "
"nodrošina komandrindas uzvednes (C<virConnectAuthPtrDefault>).  Tas ir "
"piemērots tikai komandrindas libguestfs programmām."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2616
msgid ""
"To provide authentication, first call "
"L</guestfs_set_libvirt_supported_credentials> with the list of credentials "
"your program knows how to provide.  Second, register a callback for the "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH> event.  The event handler will be called when "
"libvirt is requesting authentication information."
msgstr ""
"Lai nodrošinātu autentifikāciju, vispirms izsauciet L</"
"guestfs_set_libvirt_supported_credentials> ar akreditācijas datu sarakstu, "
"ko jūsu programma prot nodrošināt.  Otrkārt, reģistrējiet atzvanu notikumam "
"C<GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH>.  Notikumu apstrādātājs tiks izsaukts, kad "
"libvirt pieprasīs autentifikācijas informāciju."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2623
msgid ""
"In the event handler, call L</guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credentials> to "
"get a list of the credentials that libvirt is asking for.  You then need to "
"ask (eg. the user) for each credential, and call "
"L</guestfs_set_libvirt_requested_credential> with the answer.  Note that for "
"each credential, additional information may be available via the calls "
"L</guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_prompt>, "
"L</guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_challenge> or "
"L</guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_defresult>."
msgstr ""
"Notikumu apstrādātājā izsauciet L</guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credentials>"
", lai iegūtu sarakstu ar akreditācijas datiem, ko libvirt pieprasa.  Pēc tam "
"katrs akreditācijas datu vienums jāpieprasa (piem., lietotājam) un jāizsauc "
"L</guestfs_set_libvirt_requested_credential> ar atbildi.  Ņemiet vērā, ka "
"katram akreditācijas datu vienumam papildu informācija var būt pieejama caur "
"izsaukumiem L</guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_prompt>, L</"
"guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_challenge> vai L</"
"guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_defresult>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2634
msgid "The example program below should make this clearer."
msgstr "Tālāk dotajai programmas piemērs to jāpadara skaidrāk."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2636
msgid ""
"There is also a more substantial working example program supplied with the "
"libguestfs sources, called F<libvirt-auth.c>."
msgstr ""
"Ar libguestfs pirmkodu tiek piegādāta arī apjomīgāka strādājoša piemēra "
"programma F<libvirt-auth.c>."

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2639
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" main ()\n"
" {\n"
"   guestfs_h *g;\n"
"   char *creds[] = { \"authname\", \"passphrase\", NULL };\n"
"   int r, eh;\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" main ()\n"
" {\n"
"   guestfs_h *g;\n"
"   char *creds[] = { \"authname\", \"passphrase\", NULL };\n"
"   int r, eh;\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2645
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   g = guestfs_create ();\n"
"   if (!g) exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   g = guestfs_create ();\n"
"   if (!g) exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2648
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   /* Tell libvirt what credentials the program supports. */\n"
"   r = guestfs_set_libvirt_supported_credentials (g, creds);\n"
"   if (r == -1)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   /* Tell libvirt what credentials the program supports. */\n"
"   r = guestfs_set_libvirt_supported_credentials (g, creds);\n"
"   if (r == -1)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2653
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   /* Set up the event handler. */\n"
"   eh = guestfs_set_event_callback (\n"
"       g, do_auth,\n"
"       GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH, 0, NULL);\n"
"   if (eh == -1)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   /* Set up the event handler. */\n"
"   eh = guestfs_set_event_callback (\n"
"       g, do_auth,\n"
"       GUESTFS_EVENT_LIBVIRT_AUTH, 0, NULL);\n"
"   if (eh == -1)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2660
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   /* An example of a call that may ask for credentials. */\n"
"   r = guestfs_add_domain (\n"
"       g, \"dom\",\n"
"       GUESTFS_ADD_DOMAIN_LIBVIRTURI, \"qemu:///system\",\n"
"       -1);\n"
"   if (r == -1)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   /* An example of a call that may ask for credentials. */\n"
"   r = guestfs_add_domain (\n"
"       g, \"dom\",\n"
"       GUESTFS_ADD_DOMAIN_LIBVIRTURI, \"qemu:///system\",\n"
"       -1);\n"
"   if (r == -1)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2668
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   exit (EXIT_SUCCESS);\n"
" }\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   exit (EXIT_SUCCESS);\n"
" }\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2671
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" static void\n"
" do_auth (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"          void *opaque,\n"
"          uint64_t event,\n"
"          int event_handle,\n"
"          int flags,\n"
"          const char *buf, size_t buf_len,\n"
"          const uint64_t *array, size_t array_len)\n"
" {\n"
"   char **creds;\n"
"   size_t i;\n"
"   char *prompt;\n"
"   char *reply;\n"
"   size_t replylen;\n"
"   int r;\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" static void\n"
" do_auth (guestfs_h *g,\n"
"          void *opaque,\n"
"          uint64_t event,\n"
"          int event_handle,\n"
"          int flags,\n"
"          const char *buf, size_t buf_len,\n"
"          const uint64_t *array, size_t array_len)\n"
" {\n"
"   char **creds;\n"
"   size_t i;\n"
"   char *prompt;\n"
"   char *reply;\n"
"   size_t replylen;\n"
"   int r;\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2687
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   // buf will be the libvirt URI.  buf_len may be ignored.\n"
"   printf (\"Authentication required for libvirt conn '%s'\\n\",\n"
"           buf);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   // buf will be the libvirt URI.  buf_len may be ignored.\n"
"   printf (\"Authentication required for libvirt conn '%s'\\n\",\n"
"           buf);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2691
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   // Ask libguestfs what credentials libvirt is demanding.\n"
"   creds = guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credentials (g);\n"
"   if (creds == NULL)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   // Ask libguestfs what credentials libvirt is demanding.\n"
"   creds = guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credentials (g);\n"
"   if (creds == NULL)\n"
"     exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2696
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   // Now ask the user for answers.\n"
"   for (i = 0; creds[i] != NULL; ++i)\n"
"   {\n"
"     if (strcmp (creds[i], \"authname\") == 0 ||\n"
"         strcmp (creds[i], \"passphrase\") == 0)\n"
"     {\n"
"       prompt =\n"
"         guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_prompt (g, i);\n"
"       if (prompt && strcmp (prompt, \"\") != 0)\n"
"         printf (\"%s: \", prompt);\n"
"       free (prompt);\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"   // Now ask the user for answers.\n"
"   for (i = 0; creds[i] != NULL; ++i)\n"
"   {\n"
"     if (strcmp (creds[i], \"authname\") == 0 ||\n"
"         strcmp (creds[i], \"passphrase\") == 0)\n"
"     {\n"
"       prompt =\n"
"         guestfs_get_libvirt_requested_credential_prompt (g, i);\n"
"       if (prompt && strcmp (prompt, \"\") != 0)\n"
"         printf (\"%s: \", prompt);\n"
"       free (prompt);\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2708
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"       // Some code here to ask for the credential.\n"
"       // ...\n"
"       // Put the reply in 'reply', length 'replylen' (bytes).\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"       // Some code here to ask for the credential.\n"
"       // ...\n"
"       // Put the reply in 'reply', length 'replylen' (bytes).\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2712
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      r = guestfs_set_libvirt_requested_credential (g, i,\n"
"          reply, replylen);\n"
"      if (r == -1)\n"
"        exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"     }\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"      r = guestfs_set_libvirt_requested_credential (g, i,\n"
"          reply, replylen);\n"
"      if (r == -1)\n"
"        exit (EXIT_FAILURE);\n"
"     }\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2718
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     free (creds[i]);\n"
"   }\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
"     free (creds[i]);\n"
"   }\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2721
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   free (creds);\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"   free (creds);\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2724
msgid "CANCELLING LONG TRANSFERS"
msgstr "ILGU PĀRSŪTĪŠANU ATCELŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2726
msgid ""
"Some operations can be cancelled by the caller while they are in progress.  "
"Currently only operations that involve uploading or downloading data can be "
"cancelled (technically: operations that have C<FileIn> or C<FileOut> "
"parameters in the generator)."
msgstr ""
"Dažas darbības izsaucējs var atcelt to izpildes laikā.  Pašlaik var atcelt "
"tikai darbības, kas ietver datu augšupielādi vai lejupielādi (tehniski: "
"darbības, kurām ģeneratorā ir C<FileIn> vai C<FileOut> parametri)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2731
msgid ""
"To cancel the transfer, call L</guestfs_user_cancel>.  For more information, "
"read the description of L</guestfs_user_cancel>."
msgstr ""
"Lai atceltu pārsūtīšanu, izsauciet L</guestfs_user_cancel>.  Plašāku "
"informāciju lasiet L</guestfs_user_cancel> aprakstā."

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2734
msgid "PRIVATE DATA AREA"
msgstr "PRIVĀTO DATU APGABALS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2736
msgid ""
"You can attach named pieces of private data to the libguestfs handle, fetch "
"them by name, and walk over them, for the lifetime of the handle.  This is "
"called the private data area and is only available from the C API."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs rokturim var piesaistīt nosauktus privātu datu gabalus, iegūt tos "
"pēc nosaukuma un iziet tiem cauri visu roktura dzīves laiku.  To sauc par "
"privāto datu apgabalu, un tas ir pieejams tikai no C API."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2741
msgid "To attach a named piece of data, use the following call:"
msgstr "Lai piesaistītu nosauktu datu gabalu, izmantojiet šo izsaukumu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2743
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void guestfs_set_private (guestfs_h *g, const char *key, void *data);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void guestfs_set_private (guestfs_h *g, const char *key, void *data);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2745
msgid ""
"C<key> is the name to associate with this data, and C<data> is an arbitrary "
"pointer (which can be C<NULL>).  Any previous item with the same key is "
"overwritten."
msgstr ""
"C<key> ir nosaukums, ko saistīt ar šiem datiem, un C<data> ir patvaļīgs "
"rādītājs (kas var būt C<NULL>).  Jebkurš iepriekšējs vienums ar tādu pašu "
"atslēgu tiek pārrakstīts."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2749
msgid ""
"You can use any C<key> string you want, but avoid keys beginning with an "
"underscore character (libguestfs uses those for its own internal purposes, "
"such as implementing language bindings).  It is recommended that you prefix "
"the key with some unique string to avoid collisions with other users."
msgstr ""
"Varat izmantot jebkuru vēlamo C<key> virkni, bet izvairieties no atslēgām, "
"kas sākas ar pasvītru (libguestfs tās izmanto saviem iekšējiem mērķiem, "
"piemēram, valodu saistījumu realizēšanai).  Ieteicams atslēgai pievienot "
"kādu unikālu priedēkli, lai izvairītos no sadursmēm ar citiem lietotājiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2755
msgid "To retrieve the pointer, use:"
msgstr "Lai iegūtu rādītāju, izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2757
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void *guestfs_get_private (guestfs_h *g, const char *key);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void *guestfs_get_private (guestfs_h *g, const char *key);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2759
msgid ""
"This function returns C<NULL> if either no data is found associated with "
"C<key>, or if the user previously set the C<key>’s C<data> pointer to "
"C<NULL>."
msgstr ""
"Šī funkcija atgriež C<NULL>, ja vai nu ar C<key> nav saistītu datu, vai "
"lietotājs iepriekš iestatīja C<key> rādītāju C<data> uz C<NULL>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2763
msgid ""
"Libguestfs does not try to look at or interpret the C<data> pointer in any "
"way.  As far as libguestfs is concerned, it need not be a valid pointer at "
"all.  In particular, libguestfs does I<not> try to free the data when the "
"handle is closed.  If the data must be freed, then the caller must either "
"free it before calling L</guestfs_close> or must set up a close callback to "
"do it (see L</GUESTFS_EVENT_CLOSE>)."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs nekādā veidā nemēģina aplūkot vai interpretēt rādītāju C<data>.  "
"Libguestfs skatījumā tam vispār nav jābūt derīgam rādītājam.  It īpaši, "
"libguestfs I<nemēģina> atbrīvot datus, kad rokturis tiek aizvērts.  Ja dati "
"jāatbrīvo, izsaucējam tie vai nu jāatbrīvo pirms L</guestfs_close> "
"izsaukšanas, vai jāiestata aizvēršanas atzvans, kas to izdara (skatiet L</"
"GUESTFS_EVENT_CLOSE>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2770
msgid "To walk over all entries, use these two functions:"
msgstr "Lai izietu cauri visiem ierakstiem, izmantojiet šīs divas funkcijas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2772
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void *guestfs_first_private (guestfs_h *g, const char **key_rtn);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void *guestfs_first_private (guestfs_h *g, const char **key_rtn);\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2774
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" void *guestfs_next_private (guestfs_h *g, const char **key_rtn);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" void *guestfs_next_private (guestfs_h *g, const char **key_rtn);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2776
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_first_private> returns the first key, pointer pair (\"first\" does "
"not have any particular meaning -- keys are not returned in any defined "
"order).  A pointer to the key is returned in C<*key_rtn> and the "
"corresponding data pointer is returned from the function.  C<NULL> is "
"returned if there are no keys stored in the handle."
msgstr ""
"C<guestfs_first_private> atgriež pirmo atslēgas, rādītāja pāri („pirmais” "
"nenozīmē neko īpašu — atslēgas netiek atgrieztas nekādā definētā secībā).  "
"Rādītājs uz atslēgu tiek atgriezts C<*key_rtn>, un atbilstošais datu "
"rādītājs tiek atgriezts no funkcijas.  Ja rokturī nav glabātu atslēgu, tiek "
"atgriezts C<NULL>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2782
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_next_private> returns the next key, pointer pair.  The return "
"value of this function is C<NULL> if there are no further entries to return."
msgstr ""
"C<guestfs_next_private> atgriež nākamo atslēgas, rādītāja pāri.  Šīs "
"funkcijas atgriešanas vērtība ir C<NULL>, ja vairs nav atgriežamu ierakstu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2786
msgid "Notes about walking over entries:"
msgstr "Piezīmes par iešanu cauri ierakstiem:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2792
msgid "You must not call C<guestfs_set_private> while walking over the entries."
msgstr "Ejot cauri ierakstiem, nedrīkst izsaukt C<guestfs_set_private>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2797
msgid ""
"The handle maintains an internal iterator which is reset when you call "
"C<guestfs_first_private>.  This internal iterator is invalidated when you "
"call C<guestfs_set_private>."
msgstr ""
"Rokturis uztur iekšēju iteratoru, kas tiek atiestatīts, izsaucot "
"C<guestfs_first_private>.  Šis iekšējais iterators kļūst nederīgs, izsaucot "
"C<guestfs_set_private>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2803
msgid "If you have set the data pointer associated with a key to C<NULL>, ie:"
msgstr "Ja ar atslēgu saistītais datu rādītājs ir iestatīts uz C<NULL>, t. i.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2805
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfs_set_private (g, key, NULL);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfs_set_private (g, key, NULL);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2807
msgid "then that C<key> is not returned when walking."
msgstr "tad šī C<key> ejot cauri netiek atgriezta."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2811
msgid ""
"C<*key_rtn> is only valid until the next call to C<guestfs_first_private>, "
"C<guestfs_next_private> or C<guestfs_set_private>."
msgstr ""
"C<*key_rtn> ir derīgs tikai līdz nākamajam C<guestfs_first_private>, "
"C<guestfs_next_private> vai C<guestfs_set_private> izsaukumam."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2817
msgid ""
"The following example code shows how to print all keys and data pointers "
"that are associated with the handle C<g>:"
msgstr ""
"Šis koda piemērs parāda, kā izdrukāt visas atslēgas un datu rādītājus, kas "
"saistīti ar rokturi C<g>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2820
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" const char *key;\n"
" void *data = guestfs_first_private (g, &key);\n"
" while (data != NULL)\n"
"   {\n"
"     printf (\"key = %s, data = %p\\n\", key, data);\n"
"     data = guestfs_next_private (g, &key);\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" const char *key;\n"
" void *data = guestfs_first_private (g, &key);\n"
" while (data != NULL)\n"
"   {\n"
"     printf (\"key = %s, data = %p\\n\", key, data);\n"
"     data = guestfs_next_private (g, &key);\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2828
msgid ""
"More commonly you are only interested in keys that begin with an "
"application-specific prefix C<foo_>.  Modify the loop like so:"
msgstr ""
"Biežāk interesē tikai atslēgas, kas sākas ar lietotnei specifisku priedēkli "
"C<foo_>.  Mainiet ciklu šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2831
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" const char *key;\n"
" void *data = guestfs_first_private (g, &key);\n"
" while (data != NULL)\n"
"   {\n"
"     if (strncmp (key, \"foo_\", strlen (\"foo_\")) == 0)\n"
"       printf (\"key = %s, data = %p\\n\", key, data);\n"
"     data = guestfs_next_private (g, &key);\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" const char *key;\n"
" void *data = guestfs_first_private (g, &key);\n"
" while (data != NULL)\n"
"   {\n"
"     if (strncmp (key, \"foo_\", strlen (\"foo_\")) == 0)\n"
"       printf (\"key = %s, data = %p\\n\", key, data);\n"
"     data = guestfs_next_private (g, &key);\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2840
msgid ""
"If you need to modify keys while walking, then you have to jump back to the "
"beginning of the loop.  For example, to delete all keys prefixed with "
"C<foo_>:"
msgstr ""
"Ja ejot cauri jāmaina atslēgas, jāpārlec atpakaļ uz cikla sākumu.  Piemēram, "
"lai dzēstu visas atslēgas ar priedēkli C<foo_>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2844
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  const char *key;\n"
"  void *data;\n"
" again:\n"
"  data = guestfs_first_private (g, &key);\n"
"  while (data != NULL)\n"
"    {\n"
"      if (strncmp (key, \"foo_\", strlen (\"foo_\")) == 0)\n"
"        {\n"
"          guestfs_set_private (g, key, NULL);\n"
"          /* note that 'key' pointer is now invalid, and so is\n"
"             the internal iterator */\n"
"          goto again;\n"
"        }\n"
"      data = guestfs_next_private (g, &key);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  const char *key;\n"
"  void *data;\n"
" again:\n"
"  data = guestfs_first_private (g, &key);\n"
"  while (data != NULL)\n"
"    {\n"
"      if (strncmp (key, \"foo_\", strlen (\"foo_\")) == 0)\n"
"        {\n"
"          guestfs_set_private (g, key, NULL);\n"
"          /* note that 'key' pointer is now invalid, and so is\n"
"             the internal iterator */\n"
"          goto again;\n"
"        }\n"
"      data = guestfs_next_private (g, &key);\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2860
msgid ""
"Note that the above loop is guaranteed to terminate because the keys are "
"being deleted, but other manipulations of keys within the loop might not "
"terminate unless you also maintain an indication of which keys have been "
"visited."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka iepriekšējā cikls garantēti beigsies, jo atslēgas tiek "
"dzēstas, bet citas atslēgu manipulācijas ciklā var nebeigties, ja vien "
"neuzturat arī norādi par to, kuras atslēgas jau apmeklētas."

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2865
msgid "LIBGUESTFS VERSION NUMBERS"
msgstr "LIBGUESTFS VERSIJU NUMURI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2867
msgid ""
"Since April 2010, libguestfs has started to make separate development and "
"stable releases, along with corresponding branches in our git repository.  "
"These separate releases can be identified by version number:"
msgstr ""
"Kopš 2010. gada aprīļa libguestfs sāka veidot atsevišķus izstrādes un "
"stabilos laidienus kopā ar atbilstošiem zariem mūsu git repozitorijā.  Šos "
"atsevišķos laidienus var identificēt pēc versijas numura:"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2872
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                 even numbers for stable: 1.2.x, 1.4.x, ...\n"
"       .-------- odd numbers for development: 1.3.x, 1.5.x, ...\n"
"       |\n"
"       v\n"
" 1  .  3  .  5\n"
" ^           ^\n"
" |           |\n"
" |           `-------- sub-version\n"
" |\n"
" `------ always '1' because we don't change the ABI\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"                 even numbers for stable: 1.2.x, 1.4.x, ...\n"
"       .-------- odd numbers for development: 1.3.x, 1.5.x, ...\n"
"       |\n"
"       v\n"
" 1  .  3  .  5\n"
" ^           ^\n"
" |           |\n"
" |           `-------- sub-version\n"
" |\n"
" `------ always '1' because we don't change the ABI\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2883
msgid "Thus \"1.3.5\" is the 5th update to the development branch \"1.3\"."
msgstr "Tādējādi „1.3.5” ir izstrādes zara „1.3” 5. atjauninājums."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2885
msgid ""
"As time passes we cherry pick fixes from the development branch and backport "
"those into the stable branch, the effect being that the stable branch should "
"get more stable and less buggy over time.  So the stable releases are ideal "
"for people who don't need new features but would just like the software to "
"work."
msgstr ""
"Laikam ejot, mēs atlasām labojumus no izstrādes zara un pārnesam tos uz "
"stabilo zaru, kā rezultātā stabilajam zaram laika gaitā vajadzētu kļūt "
"stabilākam un ar mazāk kļūdām.  Tāpēc stabilie laidieni ir ideāli cilvēkiem, "
"kuriem nav vajadzīgi jauni līdzekļi, bet vienkārši vēlas, lai programmatūra "
"darbotos."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2891
msgid "Our criteria for backporting changes are:"
msgstr "Mūsu izmaiņu pārnešanas kritēriji ir:"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2897
msgid ""
"Documentation changes which don’t affect any code are backported unless the "
"documentation refers to a future feature which is not in stable."
msgstr ""
"Dokumentācijas izmaiņas, kas neietekmē kodu, tiek pārnestas, ja vien "
"dokumentācija neattiecas uz nākotnes līdzekli, kura nav stabilajā zarā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2903
msgid ""
"Bug fixes which are not controversial, fix obvious problems, and have been "
"well tested are backported."
msgstr ""
"Tiek pārnesti kļūdu labojumi, kas nav pretrunīgi, labo acīmredzamas "
"problēmas un ir labi pārbaudīti."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2908
msgid ""
"Simple rearrangements of code which shouldn't affect how it works get "
"backported.  This is so that the code in the two branches doesn't get too "
"far out of step, allowing us to backport future fixes more easily."
msgstr ""
"Tiek pārnesti vienkārši koda pārkārtojumi, kam nevajadzētu ietekmēt "
"darbību.  Tas ir tāpēc, lai abu zaru kods pārāk neatšķirtos, ļaujot vieglāk "
"pārnest nākamos labojumus."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2914
msgid ""
"We I<don’t> backport new features, new APIs, new tools etc, except in one "
"exceptional case: the new feature is required in order to implement an "
"important bug fix."
msgstr ""
"Mēs I<nepārnesam> jaunus līdzekļus, jaunas API, jaunus rīkus u. c., izņemot "
"vienu izņēmuma gadījumu: jaunais līdzeklis ir nepieciešams, lai realizētu "
"svarīgu kļūdas labojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2920
msgid ""
"A new stable branch starts when we think the new features in development are "
"substantial and compelling enough over the current stable branch to warrant "
"it.  When that happens we create new stable and development versions 1.N.0 "
"and 1.(N+1).0 [N is even].  The new dot-oh release won't necessarily be so "
"stable at this point, but by backporting fixes from development, that branch "
"will stabilize over time."
msgstr ""
"Jauns stabilais zars sākas, kad uzskatām, ka jaunie līdzekļi izstrādē ir "
"pietiekami būtiski un pārliecinoši salīdzinājumā ar pašreizējo stabilo "
"zaru.  Tad izveidojam jaunas stabilās un izstrādes versijas 1.N.0 un 1.(N+1)"
".0 [N ir pāra skaitlis].  Jaunais .0 laidiens šajā brīdī ne vienmēr būs tik "
"stabils, bet, pārnesot labojumus no izstrādes, šis zars laika gaitā "
"stabilizēsies."

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2928
msgid "LIMITS"
msgstr "LIMITI"

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2930
msgid "PROTOCOL LIMITS"
msgstr "PROTOKOLA IEROBEŽOJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2932
msgid ""
"Internally libguestfs uses a message-based protocol to pass API calls and "
"their responses to and from a small \"appliance\" (see "
"L<guestfs-internals(1)> for plenty more detail about this).  The maximum "
"message size used by the protocol is slightly less than 4 MB.  For some API "
"calls you may need to be aware of this limit.  The API calls which may be "
"affected are individually documented, with a link back to this section of "
"the documentation."
msgstr ""
"Iekšēji libguestfs izmanto ziņojumu protokolu, lai nodotu API izsaukumus un "
"to atbildes uz nelielu „palīgsistēmu” un no tās (sīkāk skatiet L<guestfs-"
"internals(1)>).  Protokola izmantotais maksimālais ziņojuma izmērs ir "
"nedaudz mazāks par 4 MB.  Dažiem API izsaukumiem, iespējams, jāņem vērā šis "
"ierobežojums.  API izsaukumi, kurus tas var ietekmēt, ir dokumentēti "
"atsevišķi ar saiti atpakaļ uz šo dokumentācijas sadaļu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2940
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<lt> 1.19.32, several calls had to encode either their entire "
"argument list or their entire return value (or sometimes both)  in a single "
"protocol message, and this gave them an arbitrary limitation on how much "
"data they could handle.  For example, L</guestfs_cat> could only download a "
"file if it was less than around 4 MB in size.  In later versions of "
"libguestfs, some of these limits have been removed.  The APIs which were "
"previously limited but are now unlimited (except perhaps by available "
"memory) are listed below.  To find out if a specific API is subject to "
"protocol limits, check for the warning in the API documentation which links "
"to this section, and remember to check the version of the documentation that "
"matches the version of libguestfs you are using."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<lt> 1.19.32 vairākiem izsaukumiem vienā protokola ziņojumā bija "
"jākodē vai nu viss argumentu saraksts, vai visa atgriešanas vērtība (vai "
"dažreiz abi), un tas tiem radīja patvaļīgu ierobežojumu, cik daudz datu tie "
"var apstrādāt.  Piemēram, L</guestfs_cat> varēja lejupielādēt failu tikai "
"tad, ja tas bija mazāks par aptuveni 4 MB.  Vēlākās libguestfs versijās daži "
"no šiem ierobežojumiem ir noņemti.  API, kas iepriekš bija ierobežotas, bet "
"tagad ir neierobežotas (izņemot, iespējams, ar pieejamo atmiņu), ir "
"uzskaitītas tālāk.  Lai noskaidrotu, vai konkrētu API ierobežo protokols, "
"API dokumentācijā meklējiet brīdinājumu ar saiti uz šo sadaļu un "
"neaizmirstiet pārbaudīt dokumentācijas versiju, kas atbilst izmantotajai "
"libguestfs versijai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2953
msgid ""
"L</guestfs_cat>, L</guestfs_find>, L</guestfs_read_file>, "
"L</guestfs_read_lines>, L</guestfs_write>, L</guestfs_write_append>, "
"L</guestfs_lstatlist>, L</guestfs_lxattrlist>, L</guestfs_readlinklist>, "
"L</guestfs_ls>."
msgstr ""
"L</guestfs_cat>, L</guestfs_find>, L</guestfs_read_file>, L</"
"guestfs_read_lines>, L</guestfs_write>, L</guestfs_write_append>, L</"
"guestfs_lstatlist>, L</guestfs_lxattrlist>, L</guestfs_readlinklist>, L</"
"guestfs_ls>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2958
msgid ""
"See also L</UPLOADING> and L</DOWNLOADING> for further information about "
"copying large amounts of data into or out of a filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Plašāku informāciju par lielu datu apjomu kopēšanu failu sistēmā vai no tās "
"skatīt arī L</AUGŠUPIELĀDE> un L</LEJUPIELĀDE>."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2961
msgid "MAXIMUM NUMBER OF DISKS"
msgstr "MAKSIMĀLAIS DISKU SKAITS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2963
msgid ""
"In libguestfs E<ge> 1.19.7, you can query the maximum number of disks that "
"may be added by calling L</guestfs_max_disks>.  In earlier versions of "
"libguestfs (ie. where this call is not available) you should assume the "
"maximum is 25."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs E<ge> 1.19.7 maksimālo pievienojamo disku skaitu var vaicāt, "
"izsaucot L</guestfs_max_disks>.  Vecākās libguestfs versijās (t. i., kur šis "
"izsaukums nav pieejams) jāpieņem, ka maksimums ir 25."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2968
msgid ""
"The rest of this section covers implementation details, which could change "
"in future."
msgstr ""
"Atlikusī šīs sadaļas daļa aptver realizācijas detaļas, kas nākotnē var "
"mainīties."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2971
msgid ""
"When using virtio-scsi disks (the default if available in qemu) the current "
"limit is B<255> disks.  When using virtio-blk (the old default) the limit is "
"around B<27> disks, but may vary according to implementation details and "
"whether the network is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot virtio-scsi diskus (noklusējums, ja pieejams qemu), pašreizējais "
"ierobežojums ir B<255> diski.  Izmantojot virtio-blk (vecais noklusējums), "
"ierobežojums ir aptuveni B<27> diski, bet tas var atšķirties atkarībā no "
"realizācijas detaļām un tā, vai tīkls ir iespējots."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2976
msgid ""
"Virtio-scsi as used by libguestfs is configured to use one target per disk, "
"and 256 targets are available."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs izmantotais virtio-scsi ir konfigurēts izmantot vienu mērķi "
"katram diskam, un pieejami 256 mērķi."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2979
msgid ""
"Virtio-blk consumes 1 virtual PCI slot per disk, and PCI is limited to 31 "
"slots, but some of these are used for other purposes."
msgstr ""
"Virtio-blk katram diskam patērē 1 virtuālo PCI slotu, un PCI ir ierobežots "
"līdz 31 slotam, bet daži no tiem tiek izmantoti citiem mērķiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2982
msgid "One virtual disk is used by libguestfs internally."
msgstr "Vienu virtuālo disku libguestfs izmanto iekšēji."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2984
msgid ""
"Before libguestfs 1.19.7, disk names had to be a single character "
"(eg. F</dev/sda> through F</dev/sdz>), and since one disk is reserved, that "
"meant the limit was 25.  This has been fixed in more recent versions."
msgstr ""
"Pirms libguestfs 1.19.7 disku nosaukumiem bija jābūt vienai rakstzīmei "
"(piem., no F</dev/sda> līdz F</dev/sdz>), un, tā kā viens disks ir "
"rezervēts, tas nozīmēja, ka ierobežojums bija 25.  Jaunākās versijās tas ir "
"izlabots."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2989
msgid "MAXIMUM NUMBER OF PARTITIONS PER DISK"
msgstr "MAKSIMĀLAIS NODALĪJUMU SKAITS DISKĀ"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2991
msgid "Virtio limits the maximum number of partitions per disk to B<15>."
msgstr "Virtio ierobežo maksimālo nodalījumu skaitu diskā līdz B<15>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2993
msgid ""
"This is because it reserves 4 bits for the minor device number (thus "
"F</dev/vda>, and F</dev/vda1> through F</dev/vda15>)."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tāpēc, ka tas rezervē 4 bitus mazākajam ierīces numuram (tādējādi F</"
"dev/vda> un no F</dev/vda1> līdz F</dev/vda15>)."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2996
msgid ""
"If you attach a disk with more than 15 partitions, the extra partitions are "
"ignored by libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Ja pievienojat disku ar vairāk nekā 15 nodalījumiem, libguestfs papildu "
"nodalījumus ignorē."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:2999
msgid "MAXIMUM SIZE OF A DISK"
msgstr "MAKSIMĀLAIS DISKA IZMĒRS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3001
msgid "Probably the limit is between 2**63-1 and 2**64-1 bytes."
msgstr "Visticamāk, ierobežojums ir starp 2**63-1 un 2**64-1 baitiem."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3003
msgid ""
"We have tested block devices up to 1 exabyte (2**60 or "
"1,152,921,504,606,846,976 bytes) using sparse files backed by an XFS host "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Esam testējuši bloku ierīces līdz 1 eksabaitam (2**60 jeb 1 152 921 504 606 "
"846 976 baiti), izmantojot retinātus failus resursdatora XFS failu sistēmā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3007
msgid ""
"Although libguestfs probably does not impose any limit, the underlying host "
"storage will.  If you store disk images on a host ext4 filesystem, then the "
"maximum size will be limited by the maximum ext4 file size (currently 16 "
"TB).  If you store disk images as host logical volumes then you are limited "
"by the maximum size of an LV."
msgstr ""
"Lai gan libguestfs, visticamāk, neuzliek nekādu ierobežojumu, pamatā esošā "
"resursdatora krātuve to darīs.  Ja disku attēlus glabājat resursdatora ext4 "
"failu sistēmā, maksimālo izmēru ierobežos maksimālais ext4 faila izmērs "
"(pašlaik 16 TB).  Ja disku attēlus glabājat kā resursdatora loģiskos "
"sējumus, jūs ierobežo LV maksimālais izmērs."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3013
msgid ""
"For the hugest disk image files, we recommend using XFS on the host for "
"storage."
msgstr ""
"Vislielākajiem disku attēlu failiem iesakām krātuvei resursdatorā izmantot "
"XFS."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3016
msgid "MAXIMUM SIZE OF A PARTITION"
msgstr "MAKSIMĀLAIS NODALĪJUMA IZMĒRS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3018
msgid ""
"The MBR (ie. classic MS-DOS) partitioning scheme uses 32 bit sector "
"numbers.  Assuming a 512 byte sector size, this means that MBR cannot "
"address a partition located beyond 2 TB on the disk."
msgstr ""
"MBR (t. i., klasiskā MS-DOS) nodalīšanas shēma izmanto 32 bitu sektoru "
"numurus.  Pieņemot 512 baitu sektora izmēru, tas nozīmē, ka MBR nevar "
"adresēt nodalījumu, kas atrodas tālāk par 2 TB diskā."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3022
msgid ""
"It is recommended that you use GPT partitions on disks which are larger than "
"this size.  GPT uses 64 bit sector numbers and so can address partitions "
"which are theoretically larger than the largest disk we could support."
msgstr ""
"Diskos, kas lielāki par šo izmēru, ieteicams izmantot GPT nodalījumus.  GPT "
"izmanto 64 bitu sektoru numurus, tāpēc var adresēt nodalījumus, kas "
"teorētiski ir lielāki par lielāko disku, ko varētu atbalstīt."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3027
msgid "MAXIMUM SIZE OF A FILESYSTEM, FILES, DIRECTORIES"
msgstr "MAKSIMĀLAIS FAILU SISTĒMAS, FAILU, DIREKTORIJU IZMĒRS"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3029
msgid ""
"This depends on the filesystem type.  libguestfs itself does not impose any "
"known limit.  Consult Wikipedia or the filesystem documentation to find out "
"what these limits are."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir atkarīgs no failu sistēmas tipa.  Pati libguestfs neuzliek nekādu "
"zināmu ierobežojumu.  Lai noskaidrotu šos ierobežojumus, skatiet Wikipedia "
"vai failu sistēmas dokumentāciju."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3033
msgid "MAXIMUM UPLOAD AND DOWNLOAD"
msgstr "MAKSIMĀLĀ AUGŠUPIELĀDE UN LEJUPIELĀDE"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3035
msgid ""
"The API functions L</guestfs_upload>, L</guestfs_download>, "
"L</guestfs_tar_in>, L</guestfs_tar_out> and the like allow unlimited sized "
"uploads and downloads."
msgstr ""
"API funkcijas L</guestfs_upload>, L</guestfs_download>, L</guestfs_tar_in>, "
"L</guestfs_tar_out> u. tml. ļauj neierobežota izmēra augšupielādes un "
"lejupielādes."

#. type: =head2
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3039
msgid "INSPECTION LIMITS"
msgstr "INSPICĒŠANAS IEROBEŽOJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3041
msgid ""
"The inspection code has several arbitrary limits on things like the size of "
"Windows Registry hive it will read, and the length of product name.  These "
"are intended to stop a malicious guest from consuming arbitrary amounts of "
"memory and disk space on the host, and should not be reached in practice.  "
"See the source code for more information."
msgstr ""
"Inspicēšanas kodam ir vairāki patvaļīgi ierobežojumi tādām lietām kā "
"nolasāmā Windows reģistra stropa izmērs un produkta nosaukuma garums.  Tie "
"paredzēti, lai neļautu ļaunprātīgam viesim patērēt patvaļīgu atmiņas un "
"diska vietas apjomu resursdatorā, un praksē tos nevajadzētu sasniegt.  "
"Plašāku informāciju skatiet pirmkodā."

#. type: =head1
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3047
msgid "ADVANCED MACHINE READABLE OUTPUT"
msgstr "PAPLAŠINĀTA MAŠĪNLASĀMA IZVADE"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3049
msgid ""
"Some of the tools support a I<--machine-readable> option, which is generally "
"used to make the output more machine friendly, for easier parsing for "
"example.  By default, this output goes to stdout."
msgstr ""
"Daži rīki atbalsta opciju I<--machine-readable>, ko parasti izmanto, lai "
"padarītu izvadi mašīnai draudzīgāku, piemēram, vieglākai parsēšanai.  Pēc "
"noklusējuma šī izvade nonāk stdout."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3053
msgid ""
"When using the I<--machine-readable> option, the progress, information, "
"warning, and error messages are also printed in JSON format for easier log "
"tracking.  Thus, it is highly recommended to redirect the machine-readable "
"output to a different stream.  The format of these JSON messages is like the "
"following (actually printed within a single line, below it is indented for "
"readability):"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot opciju I<--machine-readable>, progresa, informācijas, brīdinājumu "
"un kļūdu ziņojumi tiek izdrukāti arī JSON formātā vieglākai žurnālu "
"izsekošanai.  Tāpēc ļoti ieteicams mašīnlasāmo izvadi novirzīt uz citu "
"straumi.  Šo JSON ziņojumu formāts ir šāds (faktiski izdrukāts vienā rindā, "
"tālāk tas ir ar atkāpēm lasāmības labad):"

#. type: verbatim
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3060
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" {\n"
"   \"message\": \"Finishing off\",\n"
"   \"timestamp\": \"2019-03-22T14:46:49.067294446+01:00\",\n"
"   \"type\": \"message\"\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" {\n"
"   \"message\": \"Finishing off\",\n"
"   \"timestamp\": \"2019-03-22T14:46:49.067294446+01:00\",\n"
"   \"type\": \"message\"\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3066
msgid ""
"C<type> can be: C<message> for progress messages, C<info> for information "
"messages, C<warning> for warning messages, and C<error> for error message.  "
"C<timestamp> is the L<RFC 3339|https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt> "
"timestamp of the message."
msgstr ""
"C<type> var būt: C<message> progresa ziņojumiem, C<info> informācijas "
"ziņojumiem, C<warning> brīdinājumu ziņojumiem un C<error> kļūdu ziņojumiem.  "
"C<timestamp> ir ziņojuma L<RFC 3339|https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt> "
"laikspiedols."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3072
msgid ""
"In addition to that, a subset of these tools support an extra string passed "
"to the I<--machine-readable> option: this string specifies where the "
"machine-readable output will go."
msgstr ""
"Turklāt daļa šo rīku atbalsta papildu virkni, kas nodota opcijai I<--machine-"
"readable>: šī virkne norāda, kur nonāks mašīnlasāmā izvade."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3076
msgid "The possible values are:"
msgstr "Iespējamās vērtības ir:"

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3080
msgid "B<fd:>I<fd>"
msgstr "B<fd:>I<fd>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3082
msgid ""
"The output goes to the specified I<fd>, which is a file descriptor already "
"opened for writing."
msgstr ""
"Izvade nonāk norādītajā I<fd>, kas ir jau rakstīšanai atvērts failu "
"deskriptors."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3085
msgid "B<file:>F<filename>"
msgstr "B<file:>F<filename>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3087
msgid "The output goes to the specified F<filename>."
msgstr "Izvade nonāk norādītajā F<filename>."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3089
msgid "B<stream:stdout>"
msgstr "B<stream:stdout>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3091
msgid ""
"The output goes to stdout.  This is basically the same as the default "
"behaviour of I<--machine-readable> with no parameter, although stdout as "
"output is specified explicitly."
msgstr ""
"Izvade nonāk stdout.  Tas būtībā ir tas pats, kas I<--machine-readable> "
"noklusējuma uzvedība bez parametra, lai gan stdout kā izvade ir norādīts "
"eksplicīti."

#. type: =item
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3095
msgid "B<stream:stderr>"
msgstr "B<stream:stderr>"

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3097
msgid "The output goes to stderr."
msgstr "Izvade nonāk stderr."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3115
msgid ""
"Choose the default way to create the appliance.  See L</guestfs_set_backend> "
"and L</BACKEND>."
msgstr ""
"Izvēlēties noklusējuma veidu palīgsistēmas izveidei.  Skatiet L</"
"guestfs_set_backend> un L</AIZMUGURSISTĒMA>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3120
msgid ""
"A colon-separated list of backend-specific settings.  See L</BACKEND>, "
"L</BACKEND SETTINGS>."
msgstr ""
"Ar koliem atdalīts aizmugursistēmai specifisku iestatījumu saraksts.  "
"Skatiet L</AIZMUGURSISTĒMA>, L</AIZMUGURSISTĒMAS IESTATĪJUMI>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3132
msgid "See also L</LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR>, L</guestfs_set_cachedir>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</LIBGUESTFS_TMPDIR>, L</guestfs_set_cachedir>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3136
msgid ""
"Set C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1> to enable verbose messages.  This has the same "
"effect as calling C<guestfs_set_verbose (g, 1)>."
msgstr ""
"Iestatiet C<LIBGUESTFS_DEBUG=1>, lai iespējotu izvērstos ziņojumus.  Tam ir "
"tāda pati ietekme kā C<guestfs_set_verbose (g, 1)> izsaukšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3145
msgid "See also L</QEMU WRAPPERS> above."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</QEMU IETINĒJI> iepriekš."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3156
msgid ""
"Set the path that libguestfs uses to search for a supermin appliance.  See "
"the discussion of paths in section L</PATH> above."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt ceļu, kurā libguestfs meklē supermin palīgsistēmu.  Skatiet ceļu "
"aplūkojumu sadaļā L</PATH> iepriekš."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3171
msgid "See also L</LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>, L</guestfs_set_tmpdir>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L</LIBGUESTFS_CACHEDIR>, L</guestfs_set_tmpdir>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3175
msgid ""
"Set C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1> to enable command traces.  This has the same "
"effect as calling C<guestfs_set_trace (g, 1)>."
msgstr ""
"Iestatiet C<LIBGUESTFS_TRACE=1>, lai iespējotu komandu izsekošanu.  Tam ir "
"tāda pati ietekme kā C<guestfs_set_trace (g, 1)> izsaukšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3180
msgid ""
"Libguestfs may run some external programs, and relies on C<$PATH> being set "
"to a reasonable value.  If using the libvirt backend, libvirt will not work "
"at all unless C<$PATH> contains the path of qemu/KVM.  Note that PHP by "
"default removes C<$PATH> from the environment which tends to break "
"everything."
msgstr ""
"Libguestfs var izpildīt dažas ārējas programmas un paļaujas, ka C<$PATH> ir "
"iestatīts uz saprātīgu vērtību.  Ja izmanto libvirt aizmugursistēmu, libvirt "
"nemaz nedarbosies, ja vien C<$PATH> nesatur qemu/KVM ceļu.  Ņemiet vērā, ka "
"PHP pēc noklusējuma noņem C<$PATH> no vides, kas mēdz sabojāt visu."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3209
msgid ""
"See also L</guestfs_get_sockdir>, "
"L<http://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Specifications/basedir-spec/>."
msgstr ""
"Skatīt arī L</guestfs_get_sockdir>, L<http://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/"
"Specifications/basedir-spec/>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3216
msgid "Examples written in C: L<guestfs-examples(3)>."
msgstr "C valodā rakstīti piemēri: L<guestfs-examples(3)>."

#. type: textblock
#: lib/guestfs.pod:3219
msgid ""
"Language bindings: L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-golang(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Valodu saistījumi: L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-golang(3)>, L<guestfs-java"
"(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-"
"python(3)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>."

#. type: textblock
