#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-ocaml - How to use libguestfs from OCaml"
msgstr "guestfs-ocaml - kā izmantot libguestfs no OCaml"

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:7
msgid "Module style:"
msgstr "Moduļa stils:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" let g = Guestfs.create () in\n"
" Guestfs.add_drive_opts g ~format:\"raw\" ~readonly:true \"disk.img\";\n"
" Guestfs.launch g;\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" let g = Guestfs.create () in\n"
" Guestfs.add_drive_opts g ~format:\"raw\" ~readonly:true \"disk.img\";\n"
" Guestfs.launch g;\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:13
msgid "Object-oriented style:"
msgstr "Objektorientētais stils:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" let g = new Guestfs.guestfs () in\n"
" g#add_drive_opts ~format:\"raw\" ~readonly:true \"disk.img\";\n"
" g#launch ();\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" let g = new Guestfs.guestfs () in\n"
" g#add_drive_opts ~format:\"raw\" ~readonly:true \"disk.img\";\n"
" g#launch ();\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ocamlfind opt prog.ml -package guestfs -linkpkg -o prog\n"
"or:\n"
" ocamlopt -I +guestfs mlguestfs.cmxa prog.ml -o prog\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ocamlfind opt prog.ml -package guestfs -linkpkg -o prog\n"
"or:\n"
" ocamlopt -I +guestfs mlguestfs.cmxa prog.ml -o prog\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:25
msgid ""
"This manual page documents how to call libguestfs from the OCaml programming "
"language.  This page just documents the differences from the C API and gives "
"some examples.  If you are not familiar with using libguestfs, you also need "
"to read L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā dokumentēts, kā izsaukt libguestfs no programmēšanas "
"valodas OCaml.  Šajā lapā dokumentētas tikai atšķirības no C API un doti "
"daži piemēri.  Ja libguestfs izmantošana jums nav pazīstama, jāizlasa arī "
"L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:30
msgid "PROGRAMMING STYLES"
msgstr "PROGRAMMĒŠANAS STILI"

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:32
msgid ""
"There are two different programming styles supported by the OCaml bindings.  "
"You can use a module style, with each C function mapped to an OCaml "
"function:"
msgstr ""
"OCaml saistījumi atbalsta divus dažādus programmēšanas stilus.  Varat "
"izmantot moduļa stilu, kur katra C funkcija kartēta uz OCaml funkciju:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" int guestfs_set_verbose (guestfs_h *g, int flag);\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" int guestfs_set_verbose (guestfs_h *g, int flag);\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:38
msgid "becomes:"
msgstr "becomes:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" val Guestfs.set_verbose : Guestfs.t -> bool -> unit\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" val Guestfs.set_verbose : Guestfs.t -> bool -> unit\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:42
msgid ""
"Alternately you can use an object-oriented style, calling methods on the "
"class C<Guestfs.guestfs>:"
msgstr ""
"Vai arī varat izmantot objektorientēto stilu, izsaucot klases "
"C<Guestfs.guestfs> metodes:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" method set_verbose : bool -> unit\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" method set_verbose : bool -> unit\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:47
msgid ""
"The object-oriented style is usually briefer, and the minor performance "
"penalty isn't noticeable in the general overhead of performing libguestfs "
"functions."
msgstr ""
"Objektorientētais stils parasti ir īsāks, un nelielais veiktspējas sods nav "
"pamanāms vispārējās libguestfs funkciju izpildes papildizmaksās."

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:53
msgid ""
"The handle is closed when it is reaped by the garbage collector.  Because "
"libguestfs handles include a lot of state, it is also possible to close (and "
"hence free) them explicitly by calling C<Guestfs.close> or the C<#close> "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Rokturis tiek aizvērts, kad to savāc atkritumu savācējs.  Tā kā libguestfs "
"rokturi ietver daudz stāvokļa, tos var arī aizvērt (un līdz ar to atbrīvot) "
"eksplicīti, izsaucot C<Guestfs.close> vai metodi C<#close>."

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:60
msgid ""
"Errors from libguestfs functions are mapped into the C<Guestfs.Error> "
"exception.  This has a single parameter which is the error message (a "
"string)."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas no libguestfs funkcijām tiek kartētas uz izņēmumu C<Guestfs.Error>.  "
"Tam ir viens parametrs, kas ir kļūdas ziņojums (virkne)."

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:64
msgid ""
"Calling any function/method on a closed handle raises "
"C<Guestfs.Handle_closed>.  The single parameter is the name of the function "
"that you called."
msgstr ""
"Jebkuras funkcijas/metodes izsaukšana aizvērtam rokturim izraisa "
"C<Guestfs.Handle_closed>.  Vienīgais parametrs ir izsauktās funkcijas "
"nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: ocaml/examples/guestfs-ocaml.pod:82
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-golang(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://caml.inria.fr/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-golang"
"(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-"
"python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>, L<http://caml.inria.fr/>."

#. type: textblock
#: perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-perl - How to use libguestfs from Perl"
msgstr "guestfs-perl - kā izmantot libguestfs no Perl"

#. type: verbatim
#: perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" use Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" use Sys::Guestfs;\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" my $g = Sys::Guestfs->new ();\n"
" $g->add_drive_opts ('guest.img', format => 'raw');\n"
" $g->launch ();\n"
" $g->mount ('/dev/sda1', '/');\n"
" $g->touch ('/hello');\n"
" $g->shutdown ();\n"
" $g->close ();\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" my $g = Sys::Guestfs->new ();\n"
" $g->add_drive_opts ('guest.img', format => 'raw');\n"
" $g->launch ();\n"
" $g->mount ('/dev/sda1', '/');\n"
" $g->touch ('/hello');\n"
" $g->shutdown ();\n"
" $g->close ();\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:19
msgid ""
"This manual page documents how to call libguestfs from the Perl programming "
"language.  This page just documents the differences from the C API and gives "
"some examples.  If you are not familiar with using libguestfs, you also need "
"to read L<guestfs(3)>.  To read the full Perl API, see L<Sys::Guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā dokumentēts, kā izsaukt libguestfs no programmēšanas "
"valodas Perl.  Šajā lapā dokumentētas tikai atšķirības no C API un doti daži "
"piemēri.  Ja libguestfs izmantošana jums nav pazīstama, jāizlasa arī "
"L<guestfs(3)>.  Pilnu Perl API skatiet L<Sys::Guestfs(3)>."

#. type: textblock
#: perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:27
msgid ""
"Errors from libguestfs functions turn into calls to C<croak> (see "
"L<Carp(3)>)."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas no libguestfs funkcijām pārvēršas C<croak> izsaukumos (skatiet L<Carp"
"(3)>)."

#. type: textblock
#: perl/examples/guestfs-perl.pod:40
msgid ""
"L<Sys::Guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-golang(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<Sys::Guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang"
"(3)>, L<guestfs-golang(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-"
"ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-python - How to use libguestfs from Python"
msgstr "guestfs-python - kā izmantot libguestfs no Python"

#. type: verbatim
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" import guestfs\n"
" g = guestfs.GuestFS(python_return_dict=True)\n"
" g.add_drive_opts(\"disk.img\", format=\"raw\", readonly=1)\n"
" g.launch()\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" import guestfs\n"
" g = guestfs.GuestFS(python_return_dict=True)\n"
" g.add_drive_opts(\"disk.img\", format=\"raw\", readonly=1)\n"
" g.launch()\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:14
msgid ""
"This manual page documents how to call libguestfs from the Python "
"programming language.  This page just documents the differences from the C "
"API and gives some examples.  If you are not familiar with using libguestfs, "
"you also need to read L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā dokumentēts, kā izsaukt libguestfs no programmēšanas "
"valodas Python.  Šajā lapā dokumentētas tikai atšķirības no C API un doti "
"daži piemēri.  Ja libguestfs izmantošana jums nav pazīstama, jāizlasa arī "
"L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: =head2
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:19
msgid "python_return_dict=True"
msgstr "python_return_dict=True"

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:21
msgid "All new code should construct the handle using:"
msgstr "Visam jaunajam kodam rokturis jāizveido, izmantojot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" g = guestfs.GuestFS(python_return_dict=True)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" g = guestfs.GuestFS(python_return_dict=True)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:25
msgid ""
"This indicates that your program wants to receive Python dicts for methods "
"in the API that return hashtables."
msgstr ""
"Tas norāda, ka jūsu programma vēlas saņemt Python vārdnīcas API metodēm, kas "
"atgriež jaucējtabulas."

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:28
msgid "In a future version of libguestfs, this will become the default."
msgstr "Nākamajā libguestfs versijā tas kļūs par noklusējumu."

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:32
msgid ""
"Errors from libguestfs functions are mapped into C<RuntimeError> with a "
"single string argument which is the error message."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas no libguestfs funkcijām tiek kartētas uz C<RuntimeError> ar vienu "
"virknes argumentu, kas ir kļūdas ziņojums."

#. type: =head2
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:35
msgid "MORE DOCUMENTATION"
msgstr "PAPILDU DOKUMENTĀCIJA"

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:37
msgid "Type:"
msgstr "Tips:"

#. type: verbatim
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ python\n"
" >>> import guestfs\n"
" >>> help(guestfs)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ python\n"
" >>> import guestfs\n"
" >>> help(guestfs)\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:43
msgid "USING PYTHON BINDINGS IN A VIRTUALENV"
msgstr "PYTHON SAISTĪJUMU IZMANTOŠANA VIRTUALENV"

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:45
msgid ""
"These bindings are I<not> available in pypi owing to a licensing problem.  "
"See L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/1075594> for current status."
msgstr ""
"Šie saistījumi licencēšanas problēmas dēļ I<nav> pieejami pypi.  Pašreizējo "
"statusu skatiet L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/1075594>."

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:49
msgid ""
"However we do publish a Python distribution for selected stable versions of "
"libguestfs in L<http://libguestfs.org/download/python>.  You can use it like "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"Tomēr izvēlētām libguestfs stabilajām versijām publicējam Python "
"distribūciju L<http://libguestfs.org/download/python>.  To var izmantot šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" pip install http://libguestfs.org/download/python/guestfs-1.XX.YY.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" pip install http://libguestfs.org/download/python/guestfs-1.XX.YY.tar.gz\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: python/examples/guestfs-python.pod:65
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-golang(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, "
"L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-golang"
"(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-"
"perl(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<guestfs-ruby(3)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:3
msgid "virt-rescue - Run a rescue shell on a virtual machine"
msgstr "virt-rescue - glābšanas čaulas izpilde virtuālajā mašīnā"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...] [-i]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...] [-i]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:11
msgid "Old style:"
msgstr "Vecais stils:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue [--options] domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue [--options] domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue [--options] disk.img [disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue [--options] disk.img [disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:19
msgid ""
"virt-rescue is like a Rescue CD, but for virtual machines, and without the "
"need for a CD.  virt-rescue gives you a rescue shell and some simple "
"recovery tools which you can use to examine or rescue a virtual machine or "
"disk image."
msgstr ""
"virt-rescue ir kā glābšanas CD, bet virtuālajām mašīnām un bez "
"nepieciešamības pēc CD.  virt-rescue dod jums glābšanas čaulu un dažus "
"vienkāršus atkopšanas rīkus, ar kuriem var pārbaudīt vai glābt virtuālo "
"mašīnu vai diska attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:24
msgid ""
"You can run virt-rescue on any virtual machine known to libvirt, or directly "
"on disk image(s):"
msgstr ""
"virt-rescue var izpildīt jebkurai libvirt zināmai virtuālajai mašīnai vai "
"tieši disku attēliem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue -d GuestName -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue -d GuestName -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue --ro -a /path/to/disk.img -i\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue --ro -a /path/to/disk.img -i\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue -a /dev/sdc\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue -a /dev/sdc\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:33
msgid "For live VMs you I<must> use the I<--ro> option."
msgstr "Darbojošām VM I<jāizmanto> opcija I<--ro>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:35
msgid ""
"When you run virt-rescue on a virtual machine or disk image, you are placed "
"in an interactive bash shell where you can use many ordinary Linux "
"commands.  What you see in F</> (F</bin>, F</lib> etc) is the rescue "
"appliance.  You must mount the virtual machine’s filesystems.  There is an "
"empty directory called F</sysroot> where you can mount filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Kad izpildāt virt-rescue virtuālajai mašīnai vai diska attēlam, nonākat "
"interaktīvā bash čaulā, kur varat izmantot daudzas parastas Linux komandas.  "
"Tas, ko redzat F</> (F</bin>, F</lib> u. c.), ir glābšanas palīgsistēma.  "
"Virtuālās mašīnas failu sistēmas jāmontē.  Ir tukša direktorija F</sysroot>, "
"kur var montēt failu sistēmas."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:42
msgid ""
"To automatically mount the virtual machine’s filesystems under F</sysroot> "
"use the I<-i> option.  This uses libguestfs inspection to find the "
"filesystems and mount them in the right place.  You can also mount "
"filesystems individually using the I<-m> option."
msgstr ""
"Lai automātiski montētu virtuālās mašīnas failu sistēmas zem F</sysroot>, "
"izmantojiet opciju I<-i>.  Tā izmanto libguestfs inspicēšanu, lai atrastu "
"failu sistēmas un montētu tās pareizajā vietā.  Failu sistēmas var montēt "
"arī atsevišķi, izmantojot opciju I<-m>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:47
msgid ""
"Another way is to list the logical volumes (with L<lvs(8)>) and partitions "
"(with L<parted(8)>) and mount them by hand:"
msgstr ""
"Cits veids ir uzskaitīt loģiskos sējumus (ar L<lvs(8)>) un nodalījumus (ar "
"L<parted(8)>) un montēt tos ar roku:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><rescue> lvs\n"
" LV      VG        Attr   LSize   Origin Snap%  Move Log Copy%  Convert\n"
" lv_root vg_f15x32 -wi-a-   8.83G\n"
" lv_swap vg_f15x32 -wi-a- 992.00M\n"
" ><rescue> mount /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root /sysroot\n"
" ><rescue> mount /dev/vda1 /sysroot/boot\n"
" ><rescue> ls /sysroot\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><rescue> lvs\n"
" LV      VG        Attr   LSize   Origin Snap%  Move Log Copy%  Convert\n"
" lv_root vg_f15x32 -wi-a-   8.83G\n"
" lv_swap vg_f15x32 -wi-a- 992.00M\n"
" ><rescue> mount /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root /sysroot\n"
" ><rescue> mount /dev/vda1 /sysroot/boot\n"
" ><rescue> ls /sysroot\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:58
msgid "Another command to list available filesystems is L<virt-filesystems(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Vēl viena komanda pieejamo failu sistēmu uzskaitīšanai ir L<virt-filesystems"
"(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:61
msgid ""
"To run commands in a Linux guest (for example, grub), you should chroot into "
"the /sysroot directory first:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izpildītu komandas Linux viesī (piemēram, grub), vispirms jāveic chroot "
"direktorijā /sysroot:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><rescue> chroot /sysroot\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><rescue> chroot /sysroot\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:68
msgid ""
"Virt-rescue can be used on I<any> disk image file or device, not just a "
"virtual machine.  For example you can use it on a blank file if you want to "
"partition that file (although we would recommend using L<guestfish(1)> "
"instead as it is more suitable for this purpose).  You can even use "
"virt-rescue on things like USB drives, SD cards and hard disks."
msgstr ""
"Virt-rescue var izmantot ar I<jebkuru> diska attēla failu vai ierīci, ne "
"tikai virtuālo mašīnu.  Piemēram, to var izmantot tukšam failam, ja vēlaties "
"šo failu nodalīt (lai gan iesakām tā vietā izmantot L<guestfish(1)>, jo tas "
"šim nolūkam ir piemērotāks).  Virt-rescue var izmantot pat tādām lietām kā "
"USB diski, SD kartes un cietie diski."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:75
msgid ""
"You can get virt-rescue to give you scratch disk(s) to play with.  This is "
"useful for testing out Linux utilities (see I<--scratch>)."
msgstr ""
"Varat likt virt-rescue nodrošināt jums melnraksta disku(-s) eksperimentiem.  "
"Tas noder Linux utilītu testēšanai (skatiet I<--scratch>)."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:78
msgid ""
"Virt-rescue does not require root.  You only need to run it as root if you "
"need root to open the disk image."
msgstr ""
"Virt-rescue nav nepieciešams root.  To kā root jāizpilda tikai tad, ja root "
"ir vajadzīgs diska attēla atvēršanai."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:81
msgid ""
"This tool is just designed for quick interactive hacking on a virtual "
"machine.  For more structured access to a virtual machine disk image, you "
"should use L<guestfs(3)>.  To get a structured shell that you can use to "
"make scripted changes to guests, use L<guestfish(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Šis rīks ir paredzēts tikai ātrai interaktīvai virtuālās mašīnas "
"rediģēšanai.  Strukturētākai piekļuvei virtuālās mašīnas diska attēlam "
"jāizmanto L<guestfs(3)>.  Lai iegūtu strukturētu čaulu, ar kuru veikt "
"skriptētas izmaiņas viesos, izmantojiet L<guestfish(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:94
msgid "B<-a> FILE"
msgstr "B<-a> FILE"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:96
msgid "B<--add> FILE"
msgstr "B<--add> FILE"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:98
msgid ""
"Add C<FILE> which should be a disk image from a virtual machine.  If the "
"virtual machine has multiple block devices, you must supply all of them with "
"separate I<-a> options."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot C<FILE>, kam jābūt virtuālās mašīnas diska attēlam.  Ja "
"virtuālajai mašīnai ir vairākas bloku ierīces, visas jānorāda ar atsevišķām "
"opcijām I<-a>."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:111
msgid "B<--append> KERNELOPTS"
msgstr "B<--append> KERNELOPTS"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:113
msgid "Pass additional options to the rescue kernel."
msgstr "Nodot glābšanas kodolam papildu opcijas."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:121
msgid ""
"If using libvirt, connect to the given I<URI>.  If omitted, then we connect "
"to the default libvirt hypervisor."
msgstr ""
"Ja tiek izmantots libvirt, savienoties ar norādīto I<URI>.  Ja izlaists, "
"tiek savienots ar noklusējuma libvirt hipervizoru."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:124
msgid ""
"If you specify guest block devices directly (I<-a>), then libvirt is not "
"used at all."
msgstr ""
"Ja viesa bloku ierīces norādāt tieši (I<-a>), libvirt netiek izmantots "
"vispār."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:127
msgid "B<-d> guest"
msgstr "B<-d> guest"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:129
msgid "B<--domain> guest"
msgstr "B<--domain> guest"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:131
msgid ""
"Add all the disks from the named libvirt guest.  Domain UUIDs can be used "
"instead of names."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot visus diskus no nosauktā libvirt viesa.  Nosaukumu vietā var "
"izmantot domēnu UUID."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:134
msgid "B<-e none>"
msgstr "B<-e none>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:136
msgid "Disable the escape key."
msgstr "Atspējot atsoļa taustiņu."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:138
msgid "B<-e> KEY"
msgstr "B<-e> KEY"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:140
msgid ""
"Set the escape key to the given key sequence.  The default is C<^]>.  To "
"specify the escape key you can use:"
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt atsoļa taustiņu uz doto taustiņu secību.  Noklusējums ir C<^]>.  "
"Atsoļa taustiņa norādīšanai var izmantot:"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:145
msgid "C<^x>"
msgstr "C<^x>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:147
msgid "Control key + C<x> key."
msgstr "Control taustiņš + taustiņš C<x>."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:149
msgid "C<none>"
msgstr "C<none>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:151
msgid "I<-e none> means there is no escape key, escapes are disabled."
msgstr ""
"I<-e none> nozīmē, ka atsoļa taustiņa nav, atsoļa secības ir atspējotas."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:155
msgid "See L</ESCAPE KEY> below for further information."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju skatiet L</ATSOĻA TAUSTIŅŠ> tālāk."

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:168
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:172
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:177
msgid ""
"If you have untrusted raw-format guest disk images, you should use this "
"option to specify the disk format.  This avoids a possible security problem "
"with malicious guests (CVE-2010-3851)."
msgstr ""
"Ja jums ir neuzticami raw formāta viesu disku attēli, izmantojiet šo opciju, "
"lai norādītu diska formātu.  Tas novērš iespējamu drošības problēmu ar "
"ļaunprātīgiem viesiem (CVE-2010-3851)."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:189
msgid "The filesystems are mounted on F</sysroot> in the rescue environment."
msgstr "Failu sistēmas tiek montētas F</sysroot> glābšanas vidē."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:191
msgid "B<--memsize> MB"
msgstr "B<--memsize> MB"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:193
msgid ""
"Change the amount of memory allocated to the rescue system.  The default is "
"set by libguestfs and is small but adequate for running system tools.  The "
"occasional program might need more memory.  The parameter is specified in "
"megabytes."
msgstr ""
"Mainīt glābšanas sistēmai piešķirtās atmiņas apjomu.  Noklusējumu iestata "
"libguestfs, un tas ir mazs, bet pietiekams sistēmas rīku izpildei.  Dažreiz "
"kādai programmai var būt vajadzīgs vairāk atmiņas.  Parametrs tiek norādīts "
"megabaitos."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:208
msgid "The filesystems are mounted under F</sysroot> in the rescue environment."
msgstr "Failu sistēmas tiek montētas zem F</sysroot> glābšanas vidē."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:227
msgid "Enable QEMU user networking in the guest.  See L</NETWORK>."
msgstr "Iespējot QEMU lietotāja tīklošanu viesī.  Skatiet L</TĪKLS>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:233
msgid "Open the image read-only."
msgstr "Atvērt attēlu tikai lasīšanai."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:241
msgid "B<--scratch>"
msgstr "B<--scratch>"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:243
msgid "B<--scratch=N>"
msgstr "B<--scratch=N>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:245
msgid ""
"The I<--scratch> option adds a large scratch disk to the rescue appliance.  "
"I<--scratch=N> adds C<N> scratch disks.  The scratch disk(s) are deleted "
"automatically when virt-rescue exits."
msgstr ""
"Opcija I<--scratch> pievieno glābšanas palīgsistēmai lielu melnraksta "
"disku.  I<--scratch=N> pievieno C<N> melnraksta diskus.  Melnraksta disks(-"
"i) tiek automātiski dzēsts(-i), kad virt-rescue iziet."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:249
msgid ""
"You can also mix I<-a>, I<-d> and I<--scratch> options.  The scratch disk(s) "
"are added to the appliance in the order they appear on the command line."
msgstr ""
"Varat arī jaukt opcijas I<-a>, I<-d> un I<--scratch>.  Melnraksta disks(-i) "
"tiek pievienots(-i) palīgsistēmai secībā, kādā tie parādās komandrindā."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:257
msgid "B<--smp> N"
msgstr "B<--smp> N"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:259
msgid "Enable N E<ge> 2 virtual CPUs in the rescue appliance."
msgstr "Iespējot N E<ge> 2 virtuālos CPU glābšanas palīgsistēmā."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:261
msgid "B<--suggest>"
msgstr "B<--suggest>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:263
msgid ""
"This option was used in older versions of virt-rescue to suggest what "
"commands you could use to mount filesystems under F</sysroot>.  For the "
"current version of virt-rescue, it is easier to use the I<-i> option "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Šo opciju vecākās virt-rescue versijās izmantoja, lai ieteiktu, kādas "
"komandas varētu izmantot failu sistēmu montēšanai zem F</sysroot>.  "
"Pašreizējā virt-rescue versijā vieglāk ir tā vietā izmantot opciju I<-i>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:268
msgid ""
"This option implies I<--ro> and is safe to use even if the guest is up or if "
"another virt-rescue is running."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija ietver I<--ro> un to ir droši izmantot pat tad, ja viesis darbojas "
"vai ja darbojas cits virt-rescue."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:281
msgid "Display version number and exit."
msgstr "Parādīt versijas numuru un iziet."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:294
msgid "Enable tracing of libguestfs API calls."
msgstr "Iespējot libguestfs API izsaukumu izsekošanu."

#. type: =head1
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:298
msgid "OLD-STYLE COMMAND LINE ARGUMENTS"
msgstr "VECĀ STILA KOMANDRINDAS ARGUMENTI"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:300
msgid "Previous versions of virt-rescue allowed you to write either:"
msgstr "Iepriekšējās virt-rescue versijas ļāva rakstīt vai nu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:302
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue disk.img [disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue disk.img [disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:304
msgid "or"
msgstr "or"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:306
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue guestname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue guestname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:308
msgid ""
"whereas in this version you should use I<-a> or I<-d> respectively to avoid "
"the confusing case where a disk image might have the same name as a guest."
msgstr ""
"bet šajā versijā attiecīgi jāizmanto I<-a> vai I<-d>, lai izvairītos no "
"mulsinoša gadījuma, kad diska attēlam varētu būt tāds pats nosaukums kā "
"viesim."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:312
msgid "For compatibility the old style is still supported."
msgstr "Saderības labad vecais stils joprojām tiek atbalstīts."

#. type: =head1
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:314
msgid "NETWORK"
msgstr "TĪKLS"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:316
msgid ""
"Adding the I<--network> option enables QEMU user networking in the rescue "
"appliance.  There are some differences between user networking and ordinary "
"networking:"
msgstr ""
"Opcijas I<--network> pievienošana iespējo QEMU lietotāja tīklošanu glābšanas "
"palīgsistēmā.  Starp lietotāja tīklošanu un parasto tīklošanu ir dažas "
"atšķirības:"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:322
msgid "ping does not work"
msgstr "ping nedarbojas"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:324
msgid ""
"Because the ICMP ECHO_REQUEST protocol generally requires root in order to "
"send the ping packets, and because virt-rescue must be able to run as "
"non-root, QEMU user networking is not able to emulate the L<ping(8)> "
"command.  The ping command will appear to resolve addresses but will not be "
"able to send or receive any packets.  This does not mean that the network is "
"not working."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā ICMP ECHO_REQUEST protokolam ping pakešu sūtīšanai parasti "
"nepieciešams root un tā kā virt-rescue jāspēj darboties kā ne-root, QEMU "
"lietotāja tīklošana nespēj emulēt komandu L<ping(8)>.  Komanda ping šķietami "
"atrisinās adreses, bet nespēs sūtīt vai saņemt nekādas paketes.  Tas "
"nenozīmē, ka tīkls nedarbojas."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:331
msgid "cannot receive connections"
msgstr "nevar saņemt savienojumus"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:333
msgid "QEMU user networking cannot receive incoming connections."
msgstr "QEMU lietotāja tīklošana nevar saņemt ienākošos savienojumus."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:335
msgid "making TCP connections"
msgstr "TCP savienojumu veidošana"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:337
msgid ""
"The virt-rescue appliance needs to be small and so does not include many "
"network tools.  In particular there is no L<telnet(1)> command.  You can "
"make TCP connections from the shell using the magical "
"F</dev/tcp/E<lt>hostnameE<gt>/E<lt>portE<gt>> syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Virt-rescue palīgsistēmai jābūt mazai, tāpēc tā neietver daudz tīkla rīku.  "
"It īpaši nav komandas L<telnet(1)>.  TCP savienojumus no čaulas var veidot, "
"izmantojot maģisko sintaksi F</dev/tcp/E<lt>hostnameE<gt>/E<lt>portE<gt>>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:342
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" exec 3<>/dev/tcp/redhat.com/80\n"
" echo \"GET /\" >&3\n"
" cat <&3\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" exec 3<>/dev/tcp/redhat.com/80\n"
" echo \"GET /\" >&3\n"
" cat <&3\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:346
msgid "See L<bash(1)> for more details."
msgstr "Sīkāk skatiet L<bash(1)>."

#. type: =head1
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:350
msgid "ESCAPE KEY"
msgstr "ATSOĻA TAUSTIŅŠ"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:352
msgid ""
"Virt-rescue supports various keyboard escape sequences which are entered by "
"pressing C<^]> (Control key + C<]> key)."
msgstr ""
"Virt-rescue atbalsta dažādas tastatūras atsoļa secības, ko ievada, nospiežot "
"C<^]> (Control taustiņš + taustiņš C<]>)."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:355
msgid ""
"You can change the escape key using the I<-e> option on the command line "
"(see above), and you can disable escapes completely using I<-e none>.  The "
"rest of this section assumes the default escape key."
msgstr ""
"Atsoļa taustiņu var mainīt ar komandrindas opciju I<-e> (skatiet iepriekš), "
"un atsoļa secības var pilnībā atspējot ar I<-e none>.  Pārējā šīs sadaļas "
"daļa pieņem noklusējuma atsoļa taustiņu."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:359
msgid "The following escapes can be used:"
msgstr "Var izmantot šādas atsoļa secības:"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:363
msgid "C<^] ?>"
msgstr "C<^] ?>"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:365
msgid "C<^] h>"
msgstr "C<^] h>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:367
msgid "Prints a brief help text about escape sequences."
msgstr "Izdrukā īsu palīdzības tekstu par atsoļa secībām."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:369
msgid "C<^] i>"
msgstr "C<^] i>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:371
msgid ""
"Prints brief libguestfs inspection information for the guest.  This only "
"works if you used I<-i> on the virt-rescue command line."
msgstr ""
"Izdrukā īsu libguestfs inspicēšanas informāciju par viesi.  Tas darbojas "
"tikai tad, ja virt-rescue komandrindā izmantojāt I<-i>."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:374
msgid "C<^] q>"
msgstr "C<^] q>"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:376
msgid "C<^] x>"
msgstr "C<^] x>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:378
msgid "Quits virt-rescue immediately."
msgstr "Uzreiz iziet no virt-rescue."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:380
msgid "C<^] s>"
msgstr "C<^] s>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:382
msgid "Synchronize the filesystems (sync)."
msgstr "Sinhronizēt failu sistēmas (sync)."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:384
msgid "C<^] u>"
msgstr "C<^] u>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:386
msgid "Unmounts all the filesystems, except for the root (appliance)  filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Atmontē visas failu sistēmas, izņemot saknes (palīgsistēmas) failu sistēmas."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:389
msgid "C<^] z>"
msgstr "C<^] z>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:391
msgid ""
"Suspend virt-rescue (like pressing C<^Z> except that it affects virt-rescue "
"rather than the program inside the rescue shell)."
msgstr ""
"Apturēt virt-rescue (līdzīgi C<^Z> nospiešanai, izņemot to, ka tas ietekmē "
"virt-rescue, nevis programmu glābšanas čaulā)."

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:394
msgid "C<^] ^]>"
msgstr "C<^] ^]>"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:396
msgid "Sends the literal character C<^]> (ASCII 0x1d) through to the rescue shell."
msgstr "Nosūta glābšanas čaulai burtisku rakstzīmi C<^]> (ASCII 0x1d)."

#. type: =head1
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:401
msgid "CAPTURING CORE DUMPS"
msgstr "KODOLA IZMEŠU TVERŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:403
msgid ""
"If you are testing a tool inside virt-rescue and the tool (B<not> "
"virt-rescue) segfaults, it can be tricky to capture the core dump outside "
"virt-rescue for later analysis.  This section describes one way to do this."
msgstr ""
"Ja testējat rīku virt-rescue iekšienē un rīks (B<ne> virt-rescue) izraisa "
"segmentācijas kļūdu, var būt grūti tvert kodola izmeti ārpus virt-rescue "
"vēlākai analīzei.  Šajā sadaļā aprakstīts viens veids, kā to izdarīt."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:412
msgid "Create a scratch disk for core dumps:"
msgstr "Izveidojiet melnraksta disku kodola izmetēm:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:414
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" truncate -s 4G /tmp/corefiles\n"
" virt-format --partition=mbr --filesystem=ext2 -a /tmp/corefiles\n"
" virt-filesystems -a /tmp/corefiles --all --long -h\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" truncate -s 4G /tmp/corefiles\n"
" virt-format --partition=mbr --filesystem=ext2 -a /tmp/corefiles\n"
" virt-filesystems -a /tmp/corefiles --all --long -h\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:420
msgid "When starting virt-rescue, attach the core files disk last:"
msgstr "Palaižot virt-rescue, kodola failu disku pievienojiet pēdējo:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:422
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-rescue --rw [-a ...] -a /tmp/corefiles\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-rescue --rw [-a ...] -a /tmp/corefiles\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:424
msgid ""
"B<NB.> If you use the I<--ro> option, then virt-rescue will silently not "
"write any core files to F</tmp/corefiles>."
msgstr ""
"B<Piezīme.> Ja izmantojat opciju I<--ro>, virt-rescue klusi neierakstīs "
"nekādus kodola failus F</tmp/corefiles>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:429
msgid ""
"Inside virt-rescue, mount the core files disk.  Note replace F</dev/sdb1> "
"with the last disk index.  For example if the core files disk is the last of "
"four disks, you would use F</dev/sdd1>."
msgstr ""
"Virt-rescue iekšienē montējiet kodola failu disku.  Ņemiet vērā: aizstājiet "
"F</dev/sdb1> ar pēdējā diska indeksu.  Piemēram, ja kodola failu disks ir "
"pēdējais no četriem diskiem, izmantotu F</dev/sdd1>."

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:433
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><rescue> mkdir /tmp/mnt\n"
" ><rescue> mount /dev/sdb1 /tmp/mnt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><rescue> mkdir /tmp/mnt\n"
" ><rescue> mount /dev/sdb1 /tmp/mnt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:438
msgid "Enable core dumps in the rescue kernel:"
msgstr "Iespējojiet kodola izmetes glābšanas kodolā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:440
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><rescue> echo '/tmp/mnt/core.%p' > /proc/sys/kernel/core_pattern\n"
" ><rescue> ulimit -Hc unlimited\n"
" ><rescue> ulimit -Sc unlimited\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><rescue> echo '/tmp/mnt/core.%p' > /proc/sys/kernel/core_pattern\n"
" ><rescue> ulimit -Hc unlimited\n"
" ><rescue> ulimit -Sc unlimited\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:446
msgid ""
"Run the tool that caused the core dump.  The core dump will be written to "
"F</tmp/mnt/core.I<PID>>."
msgstr ""
"Izpildiet rīku, kas izraisīja kodola izmeti.  Kodola izmete tiks ierakstīta "
"F</tmp/mnt/core.I<PID>>."

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:449
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><rescue> ls -l /tmp/mnt\n"
" total 1628\n"
" -rw------- 1 root root 1941504 Dec  7 13:13 core.130\n"
" drwx------ 2 root root   16384 Dec  7 13:00 lost+found\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><rescue> ls -l /tmp/mnt\n"
" total 1628\n"
" -rw------- 1 root root 1941504 Dec  7 13:13 core.130\n"
" drwx------ 2 root root   16384 Dec  7 13:00 lost+found\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:456
msgid "Before exiting virt-rescue, unmount (or at least sync) the disks:"
msgstr ""
"Pirms iziešanas no virt-rescue atmontējiet (vai vismaz sinhronizējiet) "
"diskus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:458
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><rescue> umount /tmp/mnt\n"
" ><rescue> exit\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><rescue> umount /tmp/mnt\n"
" ><rescue> exit\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:461
msgid "7."
msgstr "7."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:463
msgid ""
"Outside virt-rescue, the core dump(s) can be removed from the disk using "
"L<guestfish(1)>.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Ārpus virt-rescue kodola izmeti(-es) no diska var izņemt, izmantojot "
"L<guestfish(1)>.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:466
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --ro -a /tmp/corefiles -m /dev/sda1\n"
" ><fs> ll /\n"
" ><fs> download /core.NNN /tmp/core.NNN\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --ro -a /tmp/corefiles -m /dev/sda1\n"
" ><fs> ll /\n"
" ><fs> download /core.NNN /tmp/core.NNN\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:474
msgid ""
"Several environment variables affect virt-rescue.  See "
"L<guestfs(3)/ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES> for the complete list."
msgstr ""
"Virt-rescue ietekmē vairāki vides mainīgie.  Pilnu sarakstu skatiet L<guestfs"
"(3)/VIDES MAINĪGIE>."

#. type: textblock
#: rescue/virt-rescue.pod:498
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, "
"L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-edit(1)>, L<virt-"
"filesystems(1)>, L<libguestfs-tools.conf(5)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: ruby/examples/guestfs-ruby.pod:3
msgid "guestfs-ruby - How to use libguestfs from Ruby"
msgstr "guestfs-ruby - kā izmantot libguestfs no Ruby"

#. type: verbatim
#: ruby/examples/guestfs-ruby.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" require 'guestfs'\n"
" g = Guestfs::Guestfs.new()\n"
" g.add_drive_opts(\"disk.img\",\n"
"                  :readonly => true, :format => \"raw\")\n"
" g.launch()\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" require 'guestfs'\n"
" g = Guestfs::Guestfs.new()\n"
" g.add_drive_opts(\"disk.img\",\n"
"                  :readonly => true, :format => \"raw\")\n"
" g.launch()\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ruby/examples/guestfs-ruby.pod:15
msgid ""
"This manual page documents how to call libguestfs from the Ruby programming "
"language.  This page just documents the differences from the C API and gives "
"some examples.  If you are not familiar with using libguestfs, you also need "
"to read L<guestfs(3)>."
msgstr ""
"Šajā rokasgrāmatas lapā dokumentēts, kā izsaukt libguestfs no programmēšanas "
"valodas Ruby.  Šajā lapā dokumentētas tikai atšķirības no C API un doti daži "
"piemēri.  Ja libguestfs izmantošana jums nav pazīstama, jāizlasa arī "
"L<guestfs(3)>."

#. type: textblock
#: ruby/examples/guestfs-ruby.pod:22
msgid ""
"Errors from libguestfs functions are mapped into the C<Error> exception.  "
"This has a single parameter which is the error message (a string)."
msgstr ""
"Kļūdas no libguestfs funkcijām tiek kartētas uz izņēmumu C<Error>.  Tam ir "
"viens parametrs, kas ir kļūdas ziņojums (virkne)."

#. type: textblock
#: ruby/examples/guestfs-ruby.pod:36
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-golang(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-perl(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, "
"L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfs-examples(3)>, L<guestfs-erlang(3)>, L<guestfs-golang"
"(3)>, L<guestfs-java(3)>, L<guestfs-lua(3)>, L<guestfs-ocaml(3)>, L<guestfs-"
"perl(3)>, L<guestfs-python(3)>, L<guestfs-recipes(1)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:3
msgid "libguestfs-test-tool - Diagnostics for libguestfs"
msgstr "libguestfs-test-tool - libguestfs diagnostika"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" libguestfs-test-tool [--options]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" libguestfs-test-tool [--options]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:11
msgid ""
"libguestfs-test-tool is a test program shipped with libguestfs to allow you "
"to check basic libguestfs functionality is working.  This is needed because "
"libguestfs occasionally breaks for reasons beyond our control: usually "
"because of changes in the underlying qemu or kernel packages, or the host "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"libguestfs-test-tool ir testa programma, kas tiek piegādāta ar libguestfs, "
"lai varētu pārbaudīt, vai libguestfs pamata funkcionalitāte darbojas.  Tas "
"ir vajadzīgs, jo libguestfs dažreiz salūst iemeslu dēļ, ko nevaram "
"kontrolēt: parasti pamatā esošo qemu vai kodola pakotņu vai resursdatora "
"vides izmaiņu dēļ."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:17
msgid "If you suspect a problem in libguestfs, then just run:"
msgstr "Ja jums ir aizdomas par problēmu libguestfs, vienkārši izpildiet:"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:21
msgid "It will print lots of diagnostic messages."
msgstr "Tas izdrukās daudz diagnostikas ziņojumu."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:23
msgid "If it runs to completion successfully, you will see this near the end:"
msgstr "Ja tas veiksmīgi izpildīsies līdz galam, beigu tuvumā redzēsiet šo:"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ===== TEST FINISHED OK =====\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ===== TEST FINISHED OK =====\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:27
msgid "and the test tool will exit with code 0."
msgstr "un testa rīks izies ar kodu 0."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:29
msgid ""
"If it fails (and/or exits with non-zero error code), please paste the "
"I<complete, unedited> output of the test tool into a bug report.  More "
"information about reporting bugs can be found on the "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/> website."
msgstr ""
"Ja tas neizdodas (un/vai iziet ar kļūdas kodu, kas nav nulle), lūdzu, "
"ielīmējiet testa rīka I<pilnu, nerediģētu> izvadi kļūdas ziņojumā.  Plašāka "
"informācija par kļūdu ziņošanu atrodama tīmekļa vietnē L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: =item
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:42
msgid "B<--qemu> qemu_binary"
msgstr "B<--qemu> qemu_binary"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:44
msgid ""
"If you have downloaded another qemu binary, point this option at the full "
"path of the binary to try it."
msgstr ""
"Ja lejupielādēts cits qemu binārais fails, norādiet ar šo opciju pilnu ceļu "
"uz bināro failu, lai to izmēģinātu."

#. type: =item
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:47
msgid "B<--qemudir> qemu_source_dir"
msgstr "B<--qemudir> qemu_source_dir"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:49
msgid ""
"If you have compiled qemu from source, point this option at the source "
"directory to try it."
msgstr ""
"Ja qemu kompilēts no pirmkoda, norādiet ar šo opciju pirmkoda direktoriju, "
"lai to izmēģinātu."

#. type: =item
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:52
msgid "B<-t> N"
msgstr "B<-t> N"

#. type: =item
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:54
msgid "B<--timeout> N"
msgstr "B<--timeout> N"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:56
msgid ""
"Set the launch timeout to C<N> seconds.  The default is 600 seconds (10 "
"minutes) which does not usually need to be adjusted."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt palaišanas noildzi uz C<N> sekundēm.  Noklusējums ir 600 sekundes "
"(10 minūtes), un to parasti nav jāpielāgo."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:63
msgid "Display the libguestfs version number and exit."
msgstr "Parādīt libguestfs versijas numuru un iziet."

#. type: =head1
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:67
msgid "TRYING OUT A DIFFERENT VERSION OF QEMU"
msgstr "CITAS QEMU VERSIJAS IZMĒĢINĀŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:69
msgid ""
"If you have compiled another version of qemu from source and would like to "
"try that, then you can use the I<--qemudir> option to point to the qemu "
"source directory."
msgstr ""
"Ja no pirmkoda kompilēta cita qemu versija un vēlaties to izmēģināt, varat "
"izmantot opciju I<--qemudir>, lai norādītu qemu pirmkoda direktoriju."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:73
msgid ""
"If you have downloaded a qemu binary from somewhere, use the I<--qemu> "
"option to point to the binary."
msgstr ""
"Ja qemu binārais fails lejupielādēts no kaut kurienes, izmantojiet opciju "
"I<--qemu>, lai norādītu uz bināro failu."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:76
msgid ""
"Note when using these options, you can ignore the business of qemu wrapper "
"scripts (L<guestfs(3)/QEMU WRAPPERS>), since libguestfs-test-tool writes a "
"wrapper script for you if one is needed."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka, izmantojot šīs opcijas, varat ignorēt jautājumu par qemu "
"ietinēju skriptiem (L<guestfs(3)/QEMU IETINĒJI>), jo libguestfs-test-tool, "
"ja nepieciešams, uzraksta ietinēja skriptu jūsu vietā."

#. type: =head1
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:80
msgid "TRYING OUT A DIFFERENT KERNEL"
msgstr "CITA KODOLA IZMĒĢINĀŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:82
msgid ""
"You can tell supermin to try a different kernel.  You do this by setting the "
"environment variables C<SUPERMIN_KERNEL>, C<SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION> and/or "
"C<SUPERMIN_MODULES>."
msgstr ""
"Varat likt supermin izmēģināt citu kodolu.  To dara, iestatot vides mainīgos "
"C<SUPERMIN_KERNEL>, C<SUPERMIN_KERNEL_VERSION> un/vai C<SUPERMIN_MODULES>."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:86
msgid "Refer to L<supermin(1)/ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES> for further information."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju skatiet L<supermin(1)/VIDES MAINĪGIE>."

#. type: =head1
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:88
msgid "TRYING OUT A DIFFERENT VERSION OF LIBVIRT"
msgstr "CITAS LIBVIRT VERSIJAS IZMĒĢINĀŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:90 test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:111
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:134
msgid "To find out which backend is the default in your libguestfs package, do:"
msgstr ""
"Lai noskaidrotu, kura aizmugursistēma ir noklusējums jūsu libguestfs "
"pakotnē, izpildiet:"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:96
msgid ""
"If you are using the libvirt backend, then you can try out a different "
"(eg. upstream) version of libvirt by running these commands (I<not> as "
"root):"
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat libvirt aizmugursistēmu, varat izmēģināt citu (piem., "
"augšteces) libvirt versiju, izpildot šīs komandas (I<ne> kā root):"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:100
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" killall libvirtd lt-libvirtd\n"
" ~/path/to/libvirt/run libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" killall libvirtd lt-libvirtd\n"
" ~/path/to/libvirt/run libguestfs-test-tool\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:103
msgid ""
"The first command kills any session C<libvirtd> process(es) that may be "
"running on the machine.  The second command uses libvirt’s C<run> script (in "
"the top-level libvirt build directory) to set some environment variables so "
"that the alternate version of libvirt is used to run the program."
msgstr ""
"Pirmā komanda nobeidz visus sesijas C<libvirtd> procesus, kas varētu "
"darboties datorā.  Otrā komanda izmanto libvirt skriptu C<run> (libvirt "
"būvēšanas augšējā līmeņa direktorijā), lai iestatītu dažus vides mainīgos, "
"lai programmas izpildei tiktu izmantota alternatīvā libvirt versija."

#. type: =head1
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:109
msgid "TRYING OUT WITH / WITHOUT LIBVIRT"
msgstr "IZMĒĢINĀŠANA AR / BEZ LIBVIRT"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:117
msgid ""
"If you are using the libvirt backend, you can try without (ie. libguestfs "
"directly launching qemu) by doing:"
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat libvirt aizmugursistēmu, varat izmēģināt bez tās (t. i., "
"libguestfs tieši palaiž qemu), izpildot:"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:122
msgid "Or if you are using the default (direct) backend, then you can try libvirt:"
msgstr ""
"Vai, ja izmantojat noklusējuma (direct) aizmugursistēmu, varat izmēģināt "
"libvirt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=libvirt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=libvirt\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:127
msgid "or with libvirt and a specific L<libvirt URI|http://libvirt.org/uri.html>:"
msgstr "vai ar libvirt un konkrētu L<libvirt URI|http://libvirt.org/uri.html>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:130
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=libvirt:qemu:///session\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" export LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=libvirt:qemu:///session\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:132
msgid "TRYING OUT DIFFERENT SELINUX SETTINGS"
msgstr "CITU SELINUX IESTATĪJUMU IZMĒĢINĀŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:140
msgid "To find out if SELinux is being used, do:"
msgstr "Lai noskaidrotu, vai tiek izmantots SELinux, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:142
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" getenforce\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" getenforce\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:144
msgid ""
"If you are using libvirt, SELinux and sVirt, then you can try to see if "
"changing SELinux to \"permissive\" mode makes any difference.  Use this "
"command as root:"
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat libvirt, SELinux un sVirt, varat mēģināt noskaidrot, vai "
"SELinux pārslēgšana uz „permissive” režīmu kaut ko maina.  Izmantojiet šo "
"komandu kā root:"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" setenforce Permissive\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" setenforce Permissive\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:150
msgid ""
"If this makes a difference, look in the audit logs for recent failures "
"(\"AVCs\"):"
msgstr "Ja tas kaut ko maina, meklējiet audita žurnālos nesenas kļūmes („AVC”):"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:153
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ausearch -m avc -ts recent\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ausearch -m avc -ts recent\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:155
msgid ""
"You can convert AVCs into suggested SELinux policy rules using tools like "
"L<audit2allow(1)>.  For more information, see the \"Security Enhanced Linux "
"User Guide\"."
msgstr ""
"AVC var pārvērst ieteiktās SELinux politikas kārtulās, izmantojot tādus "
"rīkus kā L<audit2allow(1)>.  Plašāku informāciju skatiet „Security Enhanced "
"Linux User Guide”."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:159
msgid "To re-enable SELinux and sVirt, do:"
msgstr "Lai atkārtoti iespējotu SELinux un sVirt, izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" setenforce Enforcing\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" setenforce Enforcing\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:163
msgid "SELF-DIAGNOSIS"
msgstr "PAŠDIAGNOSTIKA"

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:165
msgid ""
"Refer to L<guestfs(3)/APPLIANCE BOOT PROCESS> to understand the messages "
"produced by libguestfs-test-tool and/or possible errors."
msgstr ""
"Lai saprastu libguestfs-test-tool radītos ziņojumus un/vai iespējamās "
"kļūdas, skatiet L<guestfs(3)/PALĪGSISTĒMAS SĀKNĒŠANAS PROCESS>."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:170
msgid ""
"libguestfs-test-tool returns I<0> if the tests completed without error, or "
"I<1> if there was an error."
msgstr ""
"libguestfs-test-tool atgriež I<0>, ja testi pabeigti bez kļūdām, vai I<1>, "
"ja bija kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: test-tool/libguestfs-test-tool.pod:180
msgid "L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://qemu.org/>."
msgstr "L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<http://qemu.org/>."
